{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection","id":779860,"title":"Siren: The Surfacing (nWoD Abandoned Fangame Resurrection)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-04T09:06:34-08:00","id":779860,"title":"Siren: The Surfacing (nWoD Abandoned Fangame Resurrection)","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hello</span> everyone, I've been lurking on these forums and the RPG.net forums abit and loved how ideas for fangames were blossoming at these places, so if it's ok, I've been hoping to bring an idea up that's not entirely my own. Kind of going with the other thread I've made about continuing abandoned fanmade games, I've gotten the &quot;oks&quot; from the three closest creators of this fangame.<br /> <br /> Simply put, this fangame had alot of work put into it, and yet it suddenly cut off in 2014. There's just so much work in this that it'd be a waste to not finish it. That, and perhaps how other people might like the ideas this could bring. So I present to you all, Siren the Surfacing. I'll post the thread here, and there's a round up post of ideas as the second to last post in the thread, but for those not wanting to read all that, I'll post a shortened version after the link.<br /> <br /> I must note that Theme and Mood are the impressions I got from it and that I added abit of extra text purely for appearance, but everything is as it appeared in the thread. Siren is based off of mermaid mythos and stories,and as far as I know of the thread, your mermaid form doesn't have to have a fish tail. You can be like Octodad in that form if you want. :3<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?678032-nWoD-Siren-The-Surfacing-(Fan-Game-Brainstorm\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...ame-Brainstorm</a>)<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Siren the Drowning</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Do you remember the day you heard that beautiful noise? You\u2019ve never recalled from where you\u2019ve heard it, but it always had that twinge of nostalgia to it, like it was there your whole life and just now you\u2019re hearing it. Night after night, you hear it at the same time. 8PM sharp. And each night you can swear that you can begin to hear where it\u2019s coming from. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">However, since the new factory has moved in and polluting the river, the song has become abit twisted. It added a pitch of sorrow of where there was joy. A twinge of pain where there was bliss. The song has become corrupted, like nails on a chalkboard, but still you hear it. It calls you to the lake. Just walk right in. Become one with the music. Dive your head underwater and breathe for the first time. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You are now another voice within the Song, that treads the boundaries of civilization and nature, that tries to unite them in harmony in spite that the harmony can never be. Welcome to the world of Sirens. It\u2019s better down where it\u2019s wetter indeed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Theme: Irreconcilable Balance</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The world is just one great big ecosystem where everything gives to another to thrive, no matter how someone else put it. However, mankind has made many advances which set them apart from nature, with the power to tear it away as well. Nature just as well is untamable, and can tear apart what mankind creates with a simple natural disaster. Just as land and sea remain separate and tear into each other equally, so to do civilization and nature tear into each other. This is simply the natural order of things, as boundaries between the two must be upheld. Those that don\u2019t uphold either wish to destroy nature, help nature reclaim itself, or simply drown it all down under the Deluge to truly become one...and annihlate all life as w<span style=\"font-family:arial\">e kno</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">wit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mood: Survival</span></b></span> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">The life of a Siren is usually a fight to survive, to continue being able to exist as they do. For most Sirens, they fight to keep a peace of mind, to cling to their relationships alive and keep up their connections between Civilization and Nature. Even the Abyssal Currents cling to some notion of the above to keep themselves sane. And a Siren who wishes to avoid the encompassing future of the Deluge must work against that to keep everything they love alive. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Keeping the old alive isn\u2019t the only meaning of Survival for a Siren. A Siren can also adapt and change. She may make new connections of her own, and to replace the old where they don\u2019t apply anymore. A Siren who fails to adapt and survive falls into sterility and decay, eventually becoming a Banshee who can only vocalize woe and despair.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Inherent Axis: Waters</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Each Siren embraces an archetype close to their nature that embodies how they\u2019ll become. When they surface in the Deluge, the prospective Siren finds herself within the <b>Waters </b>that the Archetype she fits best in and thus points out the Opuses she's capable of working.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Polaria:</b> The Waters of Frozen Hearts. They\u2019re associated with the dark and unexplored depths and the succubi whose icy song lead sailors to their doom. They have affinity for the Opuses of Darkness, Death and Freeze.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Vaporia:</b> The Waters of Formless Auroras. These Sirens embody the ideals akin to a wandering troubadour, those who appear in lives to help or hinder before disappearing like the breeze. They have affinity for the Opuses of Wind, Sky and Pressure.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Tropicana: </b>The Waters of Bright Passions. They are the Sirens who are celebrants of life, giving power and love and working to gain them in turn. They have affinity for the Opuses of Light, Passion and Temper. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Gardenia:</b> The Waters of Tectonic Movements. Tempered like the Monsoon season, these Sirens seek to keep the waters flowing and the earth turning, upholding natural law as they should. They have affinity for the Opuses of Earth, Animal and Growth.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Freshwater: </b>The Waters of Sapient Breaths. All fresh water in the world attributes to this Water, and it being the water closest to humanity, so too are these sirens equally close. They have affinity for the Opuses of Technology, Human and Fate.<br /> <b>Discordia: </b>The Waters of Brewing Ruin. These waters drew in the damaged of humanity, be they those that hurt others or those wracked by the despair of their life. They're more drawn to the Abyssal Currents and they have affinity for the Opuses of Blood, Taint and Chaos.<br /> <br /> A group of Sirens working together could be known as Shoals, like Changeling Motleys or Vampire Coteries.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Outside Axis: Currents</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">If the Ocean is what a Siren is a part of, then it\u2019s the Current that declares what she follows. The Celestial Oceans are as such.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Conflict: </b>The Raging Current that fights for the oceans of the world.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Harmony:</b> The Current of Goodwill seeks to enact harmony where she may, bringing land and sea together without destroying them in the process.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Healing: </b>The Healing Waters heals man and beast alike.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Wisdom: </b>The Drops of Knowledge seek to find such wherever they look.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Buoyancy</b>: The Winding Current bobs all over the place, seeking to act through deceit and trickery.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Although the Five Currents are common for Sirens, the ocean still heralds untold depths. And like the depths, some things should be kept in them. These are known as the Abyssal Currents, and the Sirens that follow them are known as Abyssal Sirens.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Acheron</b>: The Current of the Void decided that it's time for everything to end. They believe it's best that nature and humanity should die and fade away.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Cocytus:</b> The Current of Dark Wisdom is like it\u2019s counterpart, but it searches deeper and darker than the Current of Wisdom would search. The Current of Dark Secrets searches for taboos, things heresy to harmony and occult secrets all others fear to touch.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Lethe:</b> The Current of Mankind's Victory believes that Mankind is in the right, that petty boundaries of harmony and nature shouldn\u2019t keep humanity\u2019s ambition shackled. They seek to destroy nature under a wave of pollution.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Phelegethon:</b> The Current of Dark Passions seek to indulge in their darker passions. Rage, hate, fear, despair, anything that gives power to a destructive impulse.</span></span><br /> <b>Styx: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Current of Primordial Darkness believes that mankind\u2019s time has passed, and that it\u2019s better for nature to gather itself up and reclaim itself before it\u2019s torn apart by the mud monkeys.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Morality Stat: Lucidity</b><br /> Lucidity (once known as Serenity) had been argued that it should represent harmony, the boundary between civilization and nature or to represent irreconsilable opposites (absolutes would be loved by Sirens), but the round up post explains it best, that it should be some mixture of the three. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Supernatural Advantage: Akashic Record</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">As far as I've looked, nothing wholesomely covers what Akasha can do, but from snippets on the thread ideas are that it governs how much Breath you can have, how long you can remain in mermaid/human form, how drawbacks on 6 dots and up can include requiring to stay in water for an amount of time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Fuel Stat: Pneuma</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Sirens are known to attract many a sailor in myth, as well as stealing voices or souls because they lack their own. Pneuma is what Sirens use to power their Verses, their abilities to transform themselves and the like. A Siren regains Pneuma from a human by either stealing his voice or killing to regain all breath (this covers a Succubi trope as well as Siren). It has been talked about to regain Breath through transforming when you desperately need it, at the cost of feeling your siren nature take over. Pneuma may also be regained by partaking in a type of love. What it is, it doesn't matter, so long as the Siren can at least see some significant manner of it, she can regain Pneuma. For Pneuma is the Breath of Life.<br /> <br /> The Siren nature taking over part has been discussed. It is known as <b>Maelstrom. </b>When a Siren partakes in a love she has, she endangers it by the level of intensity she can love it. It's more than just love. It's obsession. It's a reason why Sirens are enamoured with humanity and keep themselves away from it, because one night she might grow obsessed enough to take their beloved and drown them in the nearest lake until the bubbles stop coming...</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Powers: Verses</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Powered by Pneuma, the Sirens form their powers on the basis of song. Verses are what Sirens use for powers to affect certain parameters. How much they target is decided by the <b>Introduction</b> of the Verse. What they're affecting or targeting is decided by the <b>Opus </b>of the Verse. How they're affecting it is decided by the <b>Conclusion</b> of the Verse. Introductions include <b>Self, Object, Target, Group and Area. </b>Opuses include <b>Water, Sound, Beauty, and all Opuses the Waters favor. </b>Conclusions include <b>Protect, Restore, Calm, Travel, Sense, Disturb, Transform, Control, Invoke, </b>and <b>Destroy.</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Antagonists: </b>The Abyssal Sirens serve as one, even against each other. But even darker things exist in the depths\u2026<br /> <br /> Within the Deeps of the Deluge lies a great sunken ruin. Many Sirens live here, darkened and deadened. They speak in quiet snippets of song while monstrous things follow them, heeling and playing like dogs. All of these are Echidna\u2019s children. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Nobody is sure of what the great <b>Echidna </b>is or came from. Some say she is a Siren whose lost all Serenity, or something altogether stranger. Whatever the case is, she seeks sea creature and human alike to tear and splice apart their DNA to breed a new monster to bring more people down to her. Those who follow her speak in quiet tones, praising her as a god while dragging everything screaming to her until they too are changed\u2026</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Why is she doing this? It\u2019s out of love. She says she\u2019s breeding a new race out of humanity. She says that it will survive the apocalypse. </span></span><br /> <br /> Other than Echidna, there are also the <b>Flensers </b>and the <b>Furies</b>. <b>Flensers</b> are made up of mortal fishermen and women who have knowledge of a dirty secret....of how Sirens flesh can sustain their youth. They also embody mankind's ambition to transgress all boundaries no matter what the harm can be caused. They know what they do makes more Siren surface....so they do it to hunt them down to keep up their immortality. On the other hand, <b>Furies </b>are filled with Nature's rage at it's own defilement, they seek to let nature recover from mankind's intrusions and when too much has been invited onto an area, they, along with whatever else they command (mostly beasts) seek to destroy all that enters save nature, at least until their rage cools.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Deluge:</b> This is where all Sirens see upon surfacing. It holds every possible future, every timeline....and it's also the end of time and where Echidna resides. This is a future that is preventable however, but it'll take alot of work to do so...<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: Links to Google Documents now available! People may comment as they wish on development. Abuse of commenting (as in derogatory comments) will result in revoking commenting.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Link to all of the Documents: </b></span></span>https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0Bwda1WVb-LLcYVMyYl95MDAxa0U&amp;usp=sharing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 09-14-2017, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T13:01:06-08:00","id":780074,"title":"","content":"It all started so simple..<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://media0dk-a.akamaihd.net/54/59/2153e5c79e40afd5081d24f7cea0aac9-wtf-anime-fish.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://media0dk-a.akamaihd.net/54/59/2153e5c79e40afd5081d24f7cea0aac9-wtf-anime-fish.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://media0dk-a.akamaihd.net/54/59/2153e5c79e40afd5081d24f7cea0aac9-wtf-anime-fish.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://media0dk-a.akamaihd.net/54/59/2153e5c79e40afd5081d24f7cea0aac9-wtf-anime-fish.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> And now here we are. Carry on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:05:26-08:00","id":781232,"title":"","content":"The First time I saw this I had only one thing in mind: The Deluge is the Future. The Earth is doomed to be destroyed by the seas, and the Sirens can tap (Time Travel even) to a dimension where the World is Drowned, a future where the only inhabitants of the world are the Abyssal form that grew to conquer the World. As I see, The Deluge is the Future, the unstopabble end.<br /> <br /> \u200bP.S: at least that was my thougth<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T12:52:06-08:00","id":781276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=781232#post781232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First time I saw this I had only one thing in mind: The Deluge is the Future. The Earth is doomed to be destroyed by the seas, and the Sirens can tap (Time Travel even) to a dimension where the World is Drowned, a future where the only inhabitants of the world are the Abyssal form that grew to conquer the World. As I see, The Deluge is the Future, the unstopabble end.<br /> <br /> \u200bP.S: at least that was my thougth</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it was discussed abit in the forum thread that the Deluge could both be what everything once was and what everything could be. It was also said that, with the Deluge looking like everything covered in water that it takes the theme of Harmony abit further. The Deluge is what would be if you wanted to bring things together but it would only end in ruin. So yes, it fits the &quot;once past and maybe future&quot; part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If it further helps, the darker and deeper parts of the Deluge would be called &quot;The Deep&quot;, which is supposedly where Echidna resides and could be an exploratory part of the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T13:13:38-08:00","id":781289,"title":"","content":"I liked the Idea of Time Travelling Sirens, I'd buy that... With the Idea of Current and Tides making refenrece to oceanic aspects as much as Time aspects. Harmony is harder to achieve when you realize the future is fucked up. So, you need to work hard enough to prevent that future.<br /> \u200b<br /> Also, Echidna/The Dark Mother living in the depths of the Deluge would be such a nice thing. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T14:14:19-08:00","id":781314,"title":"","content":"Have there been any concrete rules for Streams? Because I have a semi-sorta idea for how you could do a &quot;keep them balanced&quot; thing with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T14:57:18-08:00","id":781329,"title":"","content":"Hrm. I'm sorry if I'm sounding bad and not getting the point you're trying to make (Sirens being tied to Time as well as the Oceans because most of the WoD lines (Fangames included) have some basis for the powers based on real life stories/myths on the creature, but there's almost nothing on Sirens and a connection to Time. Almost.), but I've gotten an idea from it after abit of looking up. To make this not TL;DR, I'm going to put them into spoiler boxes.<br /> <br /> This idea is abit based off of the idea of Aphrodite's birth in the sea, which came when Khronos/Saturn (the Greek God/Titan of Time) cut off Ouranos/Uranus's reproductive parts and from the blood dripping into the sea came Aphrodite.<br /> <br /> <b>Ideas on the Deluge being a &quot;Cut off Future&quot;:</b> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> What if the Deluge was a cut off future? What if it's a &quot;What if&quot; scenario when it comes to everything being mashed together, being exactly what the Sirens (at least, all of the sane ones) would want to avoid? It's essentially what the world would look like before the end and if drowned, hence why Echidna wants to create a new race of beings/sirens is to survive it.This fits the &quot;Cut off by Time&quot; theme. I don't know how to explain it further, or if it needs explaining, especially since one great theme to go along with oceans would be &quot;Mystery&quot;. I still kind of like the one idea of &quot;Sirens version of the Astral Plane&quot;.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Idea on Deluge being how Sirens see the Astral Plane: </b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Actually, that could also be explainable. The Astral Plane doesn't translate at the same time that the real world does, and with the three examples I mentioned, the plane differs depending on the supernatural looking at it. Princesses see it as where everything is connected and changes on a second to second basis (for those who don't know, Magical Girls in the WoD). Mages see it in three-five different sections and everything connected only by symbology. Changelings see it as interconnecting threads between both human dreams (meaning in Mage terms that they go between Oneiros alot). Perhaps one theme that remains constant is that the Astral is the soul of humanity and every thought, dream, idea, and part of it, and that it changes depending on the splat looking at it. Perhaps more importantly, it also deals with how the splat in question relates to humanity.<br /> <br /> The idea here is that, bringing the idea of &quot;cut off from time&quot; and stuff, what if the Deluge is how the Sirens view the Astral, except it's much more heavy into the &quot;Anima Mundi&quot; part, which emphasizes the world's soul as a whole (humanity's impact on the earth? The Deluge shows the world, everyone and everything as being drowned underneath loads of water because it's dealing with the world as a whole rather than individually, and as such is actually showing the damages it's suffering. It still fits with the &quot;Cut off from time&quot; theme, if due to it not running at the same time as earth time does. Perhaps it also still fits with the &quot;bad future&quot; idea too, since as the world as a whole percieves it, this could be how the world's soul percieves that it's gonna end up: Drowning under it's own filth and waste. It also adds some emphasis to Echidna's desire to help humanity survive.<br /> <br /> Suddenly new idea. The Deluge has sections. The Surface is the top of the Deluge with an endless sky filled where human thoughts come up to like bubbles rising up. The Reef is where the lines of human history lie like stories or books, each reef growing as history goes on, and all kinds of material can make it up. The Twilight Zone is where the light above begins to die, as well as where a Siren usually enters the Deluge. And finally, the Deep/Depths/Abyssal Zone, where Echidna holds some provinces and the Abyssal sirens retreat to. I think the Surface and Reef themes fit well if in connecting to Humanity as well as &quot;The Little Mermaid&quot; story.</div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> <b>Idea on Echidna fitting into all of this:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> So about the cutoff by time theme. It's not ultimately said or explained what Echidna is at all, just that she's connected to Sirens and creates monsters by mashing together fish and human DNA. Here's something I would find fitting as an idea for Echidna. She's the Ouranos in the story above, and whomever is patron/matron to the Sirens is the Aphrodite. It's said in the forum that Echidna only takes the people she's captured and fish and puts them together, often into different combonations to see what would result. In other words, she can rearrange and change, but she cannot truly <i>create new things. </i>Like Ouranos in the story, she might've been rendered unable to reproduce. <br /> <br /> Perhaps I shouldn't say anything on her due to lack of a proper backstory on Sirens, but ideas I have currently are based around the &quot;Khronos(???) usurps Ouranos(Echidna) and makes him unable to reproduce, the last remains of his ability to do so becoming Aphrodite (Sirens). Any further thoughts?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>As for Streams. </b>There's no official powers or rules made for Streams really, only generic guidelines. Perhaps the closest to any powers comes the Antedeluvian Symphony, in which the very last post on the first thread for Sirens only has a generic outline of what each power level would do. Perhaps to note, like with all gamelines, the powers needs to be fitting for the splat to have. For example, nowhere will anyone see any powers dealing with fire for Sirens as no material on them has them being able to do that. Other than that, feel free to shoot your ideas up. :3<br /> <br /> I'm so sorry if I'm doing bad in responding, this is my first time bringing up ideas and leading a fansplat, so please tell me if I'm doing something wrong at all. <br /> <br /> And I should totally be studying for finals but I got ideas after seeing the messages being posted. And studying is soul sucking. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:23:05-08:00","id":781342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=781329#post781329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm. I'm sorry if I'm sounding bad and not getting the point you're trying to make (Sirens being tied to Time as well as the Oceans because most of the WoD lines (Fangames included) have some basis for the powers based on real life stories/myths on the creature, but there's almost nothing on Sirens and a connection to Time. Almost.), but I've gotten an idea from it after abit of looking up. To make this not TL;DR, I'm going to put them into spoiler boxes..</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it, maybe i'm the one that am going too far. I like to make connections between the gamelines and something that is completely new to the creature, not originaly related, (Prometheans and Alchemy, for example). Now, the Sirens try to bring Harmonia to the world, a little bit like the Werewolves, but differently. I thought that, their connection to the water and Currents, alongside with a little extra (Currents of Time) and the World being Drowned by the Deluge, they could access this time in History (Drowned Future) by their connection to the water currents and the Time River (just references). For me, Water and Time can be related, like suggest some philosophies and such.<br /> <br /> As for the Idea of the Deluge being the Astral Plane: I don't believe that one is exclusive to the other. The Deluge IS an/the Astral Plane hence it still did not Happened, but it MAY be a representation of the Future. The Sirens may be sure that it is the Future and that they need to stop it, which may or may not be the truth.<br /> <br /> Echidna as an Antagonist and Her Creations being a deformed version of a Siren (Cacophonies) is a idea that's been around my mind,<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I'm also new at this, but you're doing great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-06-2015, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:54:56-08:00","id":781356,"title":"","content":"AH. Now I see from the comparison of Prometheans and Alchemy. It would also make much more sense with the Siren's power stat being named Akasha, whose definition is an etheric field where past events are recorded. Alright, I can see your reasoning and it working, sorry for the confusion on my part.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Cacophonies serve the same function as most antagonist splats (Pandorans, Darkened, Clockstoppers) do? Hrm...if I may suggest as an idea, what if Cacophonies is the name of their powers and Vodianoi are the name of the children proper? The name &quot;Vodianoi&quot; comes from the name of Slavic water spirits who lived in palaces of sunken ships, were covered with hair, scales and slime and hated the boldness of humans to which they'd drown them and keep a few as slaves.<br /> <br /> And yes, there's a tad bit of overlap with Werewolf the Forsaken, as they both somewhat deal with conservation themes. I believe the difference brought up was that Sirens ultimately deal with mundane concerns over the spiritual ones that all Werewolves deal with. Another idea was the idea that not all Sirens had an &quot;Aquatic Form&quot; like wolves do with their forms. I don't like the latter idea to be abit honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:12:23-08:00","id":781368,"title":"","content":"Good, I like the Vodianoi idea! Still thinking a way we coul use banshees.<br /> <br /> I believe that every Siren would need a mashup with some other form of oceanic life. And I believe they should have a Aquatic form, but that they could only manifest under water or in the Deluge, or with a proper Cacophonie.<br /> <br /> \u200bI Was wondering, do Sirens start off as humans and find out their origin after, like a lineage? or they are born inside the Culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-06-2015, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:09:18-08:00","id":781396,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the said mashup, I've been thinking on that. Given that the Inherent and Social/External Axises were posted as they were written, I was toying with the idea that maybe Oceans should serve as the Internal Axis and Currents could be the Social Axis. Sirens could take features of animals most known for living in said oceans (like Arctica Sirens having some natural antifreeze like fishes do down in the Antarctic Ocean that makes them immune to cold environmental factors). Not to mention since Social Axises can be changed, it just sounds better to have Currents be them, since Currents are known for moving about and exchanging etc etc. The only problem then becomes the Abyssal Currents and what to do with them. Perhaps renaming them to &quot;Abyssal Rivers/Oceans&quot; and rename them after mythical rivers/oceans? I can imagine them being named after the Greek Rivers of Hades.:<br /> <br /> Dark Passions: Phelegethon, the River of Boiling Blood - As emotions boil the blood of others, these sirens seek to make the vessels burst forth in destruction.<br /> Dark Secrets: Cocytus, the River of Lamentation - The gain of knowledge is a loss of innocence, and these sirens seek to lose it all in search of their secrets.<br /> Mankind's Victory: Lethe, the River of Forgetfulness - Just as mankind forgot about nature after the Industrial Revolution, so too do these sirens believe they must forget nature and wipe it all out.<br /> Primordial Darkness: Styx, the River of Hate - These sirens have boiled to hatred of all civilized society, and in turn they seek to wipe it all away so nature may cleanse itself.<br /> <br /> It's not quite clear how Sirens come to be. What I do get is that Sirens hear &quot;The Song&quot; which calls them to their nature. In a sense, it might be somewhat like how Werewolves experience the first change, but not as violent? I don't have any ideas for this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Perhaps the most obvious thing that all Sirens have is the ability to breath underwater indefinitely. And after reading the one thread, I got an idea for a Stream. Perhaps it should be a Stream the Current of Dark Passions recieves.<br /> <br /> Stream of Dead Tales: The Sirens ability to command the dead and force them to cough up their bounty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 12-06-2015, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:42:01-08:00","id":781421,"title":"","content":"Here comes my two cents and overral critics of what I find of the Splat (know that first I read all the discussion on the other thread):<br /> <br /> <b>Theme: Irreconcilable Balance</b><br /> I Like it. Lots.<br /> <br /> <b>Mood: Tempting Absolutes.</b><br /> I believe it needs Work, the Absolutes may truly be tempting, but they would not define the urge to stop the &quot;may be&quot; future that is the Deluge, I believe that it this aspect could be worked on as we progress.<br /> <br /> <b>Inherent Axis: Oceans </b><br /> Didn't like the names and at first they didn't sound that Inherent to me. I mean, nature rarely changes, but sometimes you take a diferente approach on your objective. I don't know, maybe i'm being silly. I Mean, an Atlantic Siren may be a Warrior already, so the Conflict Current becomes redundant. I Suppose people are BORN Sirens, they just don't know, therefore, they have ancestrals that were Siren. What if the Inherent Axis would be Ancestrality? Like, What Clan, Subrace, Species of Siren do you descend from? that way we could give real inherent differences because of the &quot;genetics&quot;. Don't know, just an idea. So if your ancestral Family comes from the Artic, you have Aspect from the marine fauna from there, and so it goes on...<br /> <br /> <b>Social Axis: Currents</b><br /> Liked, they seem very good, would work on the Names, tough. hehehehe.<br /> <br /> <b>Morality Stat: Serenity</b><br /> I would go further, Why not have Harmony as morality?<br /> <br /> <b>Supernatural Stat: Akasha</b><br /> Yes, that's what I mean, although none of the guys went with the Time Travel, Time River thing. As we could work Sirens are creatures inherently connected to the Time River (The Khronos in our Story), and swim trough it. Akasha coul represent the connection to the Past and Future, or something like this.<br /> <br /> <b>Fuel: Breath</b><br /> I don't have an opinion about it yet.<br /> <br /> <b>Powers: Streams</b><br /> Actually, I would divide the powers in two sets, one: The Streams are the powers that range from 1 to 5 and need to be bought progressively. The other set of powers is like the Demon form in D:tD. You buy a group of aspects to be your Aquatic Form or True Form: Tentacles, Eletric pulse, Bioluminescence, etc...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Antagonists:</b> Vodianoi, for now.<br /> <br /> <b>The Deluge</b>: I'm preparing a big document on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-06-2015, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:48:45-08:00","id":781424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=781396#post781396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the said mashup, I've been thinking on that. Given that the Inherent and Social/External Axises were posted as they were written, I was toying with the idea that maybe Oceans should serve as the Internal Axis and Currents could be the Social Axis. Sirens could take features of animals most known for living in said oceans (like Arctica Sirens having some natural antifreeze like fishes do down in the Antarctic Ocean that makes them immune to cold environmental factors). Not to mention since Social Axises can be changed, it just sounds better to have Currents be them, since Currents are known for moving about and exchanging etc etc. The only problem then becomes the Abyssal Currents and what to do with them. Perhaps renaming them to &quot;Abyssal Rivers/Oceans&quot; and rename them after mythical rivers/oceans? I can imagine them being named after the Greek Rivers of Hades.:<br /> <br /> Dark Passions: Phelegethon, the River of Boiling Blood - As emotions boil the blood of others, these sirens seek to make the vessels burst forth in destruction.<br /> Dark Secrets: Cocytus, the River of Lamentation - The gain of knowledge is a loss of innocence, and these sirens seek to lose it all in search of their secrets.<br /> Mankind's Victory: Lethe, the River of Forgetfulness - Just as mankind forgot about nature after the Industrial Revolution, so too do these sirens believe they must forget nature and wipe it all out.<br /> Primordial Darkness: Styx, the River of Hate - These sirens have boiled to hatred of all civilized society, and in turn they seek to wipe it all away so nature may cleanse itself.<br /> <br /> It's not quite clear how Sirens come to be. What I do get is that Sirens hear &quot;The Song&quot; which calls them to their nature. In a sense, it might be somewhat like how Werewolves experience the first change, but not as violent? I don't have any ideas for this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Perhaps the most obvious thing that all Sirens have is the ability to breath underwater indefinitely. And after reading the one thread, I got an idea for a Stream. Perhaps it should be a Stream the Current of Dark Passions recieves.<br /> <br /> Stream of Dead Tales: The Sirens ability to command the dead and force them to cough up their bounty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damm, one second too late. Was reworking the Abyssals and saw your post. Also nice touch with the Greek names. I'm bought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:07:35-08:00","id":781441,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Also, my rework of Streams, critics needed.<br /> <br /> Stream of the Sunken Ship:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s Song. The ability to control human minds and Desires, Emotions.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Underwater Senses:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s Sight. The ability to enhance perceptions of the World for herself and others.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Rusted Iron:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s ties to Time, the ability of aging Human tech and Rusting Iron to easily destroy objects.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Breaking Waves: </span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Siren\u2019s Arsenal. Turn the wrath of the sea onto your enemies.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Choleric Sky:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s Ability to command weather and Storms.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Raging Earth:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Sirens influence on the movement of the earth.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Healing Waters:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s ability to Heal itself using any body of water</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Flood:</span></b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The Siren\u2019s ability to interact with the Deluge from reality.<br /> <br /> Mostly name changes, but some core changes that I thougth would fit... also, for the new Abyssal Rivers:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dark Passions: Stream of the Boiling Blood:</b> Blood is a lot of Water, of course we can control it.<br /> <b>Dark Secrets: Stream of the Sunken Body:</b> Control Emotions is never as powerful as controling the Deep Fears<br /> <b>Mankind's Victory: Stream of the Ironborn:</b> Polluting is the solution.<br /> <b>Primordial Darkness: Stream of the Raging Nature:</b> Floods, Tsunamis, even Drought. Humans had their time, Let the Deluge come.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-06-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:52:12-08:00","id":781468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=781441#post781441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Also, my rework of Streams, critics needed.<br /> <br /> Stream of the Sunken Ship:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s Song. The ability to control human minds and Desires, Emotions.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Underwater Senses:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s Sight. The ability to enhance perceptions of the World for herself and others.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Rusted Iron:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s ties to Time, the ability of aging Human tech and Rusting Iron to easily destroy objects.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Breaking Waves: </span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Siren\u2019s Arsenal. Turn the wrath of the sea onto your enemies.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Choleric Sky:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s Ability to command weather and Storms.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Raging Earth:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Sirens influence on the movement of the earth.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Healing Waters:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Siren\u2019s ability to Heal itself using any body of water</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stream of the Flood:</span></b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The Siren\u2019s ability to interact with the Deluge from reality.<br /> <br /> Mostly name changes, but some core changes that I thougth would fit... also, for the new Abyssal Rivers:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dark Passions: Stream of the Boiling Blood:</b> Blood is a lot of Water, of course we can control it.<br /> <b>Dark Secrets: Stream of the Sunken Body:</b> Control Emotions is never as powerful as controling the Deep Fears<br /> <b>Mankind's Victory: Stream of the Ironborn:</b> Polluting is the solution.<br /> <b>Primordial Darkness: Stream of the Raging Nature:</b> Floods, Tsunamis, even Drought. Humans had their time, Let the Deluge come.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hrm, I know that a few of these are renames of some of the current streams, but to be honest, I sort of liked the older names abit better. Also, there's fewer Streams than the ones posted.<br /> <b>Sunken Ship: </b>I liked the name of &quot;Sunken Melody&quot; abit better, if because it does show the connection between Sirens and song. The name is abit misleading, implying that it has to do more with capsizing ships than controlling human minds and emotions.<br /> <b>Rusted Iron: </b>I believe that originally this was meant to be something having to do with controlling technology and the like. It would be amazingly useful if not only your song lead to sailors coming towards you, but also using this to make their ship change course without any input from the sailors to you. I also believe that the Time aspect could be made into it's own stream. <br /> <b>Breaking Waves: </b>I don't have any complaints, the name change is better I feel.<br /> <b>Choleric Sky and Raging Earth: </b>Renames to Indefatigable Cycles and Geological Schism. On one hand, I like the old names, but on the other it may be annoying to spell out &quot;Indefatigable&quot; for some people. <br /> <b>Healing Waters: </b>I take it that it's a redo of the Stream of Submergence? Perhaps the only problem I have is that it can affect less than it once could. Although then again I can see making a separate Stream dealing with &quot;Submerging&quot; aspects of things, even bringing people along.<br /> <b>Flood: </b>Antedeluvian Symphony. Sort of the same issue with Choleric Sky and Raging Earth.<br /> <br /> I think I'll make a Google Doc for the supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:00:53-08:00","id":781474,"title":"","content":"Exactly my thougth on changing the names. I accept that Sunken Melody was better, so Agreed on returning to Sunken Melody. Also, the name changes in the other ones were exactly because I thougth it was too complex and wanted to simplify. The Stream of Submergence (Didn't like the name, too. Damm, I'm such a brag), but yes I wanted to separate the ability to heal from the ability to Merge with bodies of water.<br /> <br /> \u200bRusted Iron, also, is something that is quite annoying to me. I mean, as much as i understand, this streams also control other Tech, and I don't like that. I mean, technology like computer being controlled by Sirens seems a little bit off for me. But I guess it's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-06-2015, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:02:30-08:00","id":781476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=781421#post781421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps on Tempting Absolutes As for the Oceans, as said most of them were reposted directly from the thread linked. Although redundancy may be an issue, it depends on how it's played. For example, in Princess the Hopeful you could play as a Champion Calling Princess (they focus on fighting and solving problems) and be in the Court of Storms (They do LOADS of fighting the Darkness). It may be redundant, but with how it's done it still works. As for becoming a Siren or the like, it might be simpler with Oceans rather than genetics or family. Don't want to step on Leviathan's toes either.<br /> <br /> As for why not using Harmony, don't want to step too much on Werewolf's toes or make Siren TOO similar to Werewolves. As for the idea on group aspects, I'm not too well read on DtD. Would it be like Changeling's Court Mantle or the like? Thats how I sort of get the picture of it. Finally, as for Antagonists, it's the Vodianoi, Abyssal Sirens and Echidna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 12-06-2015, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T19:15:15-08:00","id":781482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=781476#post781476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps on Tempting Absolutes As for the Oceans, as said most of them were reposted directly from the thread linked. Although redundancy may be an issue, it depends on how it's played. For example, in Princess the Hopeful you could play as a Champion Calling Princess (they focus on fighting and solving problems) and be in the Court of Storms (They do LOADS of fighting the Darkness). It may be redundant, but with how it's done it still works. As for becoming a Siren or the like, it might be simpler with Oceans rather than genetics or family. Don't want to step on Leviathan's toes either.<br /> <br /> As for why not using Harmony, don't want to step too much on Werewolf's toes or make Siren TOO similar to Werewolves. As for the idea on group aspects, I'm not too well read on DtD. Would it be like Changeling's Court Mantle or the like? Thats how I sort of get the picture of it. Finally, as for Antagonists, it's the Vodianoi, Abyssal Sirens and Echidna.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> \u200bHmmm, I see. Agreed with the majority of the arguments, just still am feeling that Oceans seems a little bit subjective. Transformed in the Waters of X Ocean seems strange, but maybe I am being just Stubborn and I grow to like it. Until I have something else to argument I'll just go along with Oceans.<br /> <br /> As for I understand the Demonic Form in D:tD Works like the construction of Halfbreed Form in Changing Breeds. There's a List of Options that represent diverses aspects of the Body and you have a number of points to create the creature. Each aspect gives and advantage to the player.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T04:13:11-08:00","id":781643,"title":"","content":"So it's essentially like building a character in a classic RPG where you choose traits? Or for those familiar with DtF; Visages where you can pick the traits rather than having them pre-picked for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T06:45:30-08:00","id":781682,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is The way I understood it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T13:43:04-08:00","id":781824,"title":"","content":"I see. As far as I can see it, there's a few things that need to be conceptualized before anything else is done.<br /> <b>Alterations</b><br /> -What innate forms or &quot;Transfigurations/Mutations/Alterations&quot; that a Siren can access<br /> -What their limits are, like using Higher Akasha = Can have more Alterations at one time<br /> -How or by what means they're accessed or bought. I would like to suggest that there's some that are innate to Oceans and can be bought off the bat, whereas other mutations not of the Oceans own (perhaps even ones that only Echidna can provide) cost more to buy<br /> -Perhaps at Higher Akasha, as a drawback, some of your mutations show on human form and give penalties to social rolls because of it. <br /> <br /> <b>Aquatic Form</b><br /> -What it entails. I imagine for now that you gain 9 Again for Athletics rolls in the water, can breathe indefinitely underwater and perhaps some other forms or bonuses.<br /> -Sirens are known for killing sailors, leading them to their doom and etc etc. How do we show that exactly? Do they feel some primordial rage at the world's defilement and it comes out to rip apart or drown the person closest to the Siren? Imagine how screwed the person is if the Siren has Antediluvian Symphony. <br /> <br /> <b>Backstory</b><br /> -What is the backstory of Sirens? How did they form their place in the world and if they're like most other WoD gamelines, did they have some primordial paradise that got torn to shreds or something?<br /> <br /> <b>Miscellaneous</b><br /> -The Time motif. I'm sorry for bringing this up, I may be refusing to give up some ideas I have on other things, but how exactly does Time fit with Sirens? I can see why the Prometheans and Alchemy go hand in hand due to stories of golems made of stone being animated and the like or animation being an alchemical purview. I think the biggest reason is that there's literally no myths or stories of Sirens being connected to time, and the story I pulled of Khronos, Ouranos and Aphrodite was really pulling at straws and not even connected to Sirens or the like. I'm sorry for bringing this up, I'm just skeptical of how it could fit because there's little basis of it fitting for Sirens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:27:41-08:00","id":781882,"title":"","content":"So, i'm not anywhere near a PC to properly answer, but I understand your skepticism. As I ser, Sirena as basic mythology is very shallow, nor even close as deep as the other gamelines of the WoD, I mean, werewolves weren't much know for their connetions to spirits before. The time aspect would be a way of creating a concrete and deep mythos around the creature. I knoe sirens are not famous to their relation to time, but water, a important aspect of the Siren Mythos is, phillosophically speaking. Also is Atlantis, by the way. Time is not a common theme on the WoD, nor is Time Travel and such, the Time theme could serve as a light cast of the surface of the game, making it interesting and new. <br /> <br /> <br /> But I undertand your skepticism. When I get to my computer I'll give a longer explanation and argumentation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T19:03:39-08:00","id":782013,"title":"","content":"Now that i'm Home and with my computer, let's see:<br /> <br /> Why did I came up with the Time as theme? If we would take the original Myth of the Sirens, back with the Greeks, we would have a Winged ladies that sang so beautifuly that made men drown so they could eat. Mermaids have interesting stories that are centered in their beauty, but that is, they are mainly demons, spirits, or ephemeral entities Sirens have truly no greater mythos or stories that could be worked to create a deep and interesting setting that can walk on it's own legs, or fins, without receiving commentaries like: &quot;The temathics is a little bt like Werewolf&quot; or: &quot;This could be accomplished with a Beast Hack&quot; or even &quot;Sirens are so much Changeling&quot;, at lest that's how I see It. (Don't thake it personally, I know that you don't want it either, I'm just trying to clarify why I'm eager to take Sirens this way.)<br /> <br /> The famous Werewolves were never asociated with Spirits, nor Mages with Five Towers in Astral Planes, nor Frankestein's Monster with Alchemic Abilities or Mummies with Memory (with a Capital &quot;M&quot;). those aspects of the game were there only superficialy after lots of thinking and exploring minor aspects of particular stories, I.E: The Golems and Alchemy. Mostly, they represent an exploration of a philosophical aspect made pratical (promethean's goal is their transformation from monsters to the natural order, so Alchemy truly fits). So I went with this aspect. Also, never a gameline fan or officialy made has taken on the subject of time, so it's new, intriguing and full of possibilities.<br /> <br /> Heraclitus, greek phillosopher, is believed to have said: &quot;Everything flows, nothing stands stills. You cannot step a same river twice, for is never the same water that touchs your skin&quot;. So is the time, you can never regain a second, for every second passed is a second wasted, and the past will never come back again. The River of Time only flows onwards, want you or not. Next, Thales, another greek philosopher, went <a href=\"http://www.iep.utm.edu/thales/#H3\" target=\"_blank\">with a theory that was very accepted at the time</a> with this assertion: Water is the base element for every matter in the world, everything came from water (and might as well get back to it with the Deluge). For the Tibetans Water was the element of Cohesion connected with phenomena related to Time, Space and other subjective aspects. (May as well remember that Akasha was one of the Five elements for the Hindi, along with water, fire, air and Earth, representing, as you said, a place were memories were kept, all humans memories. So, water has Always been a subject in modern and ancient philosophy, and can sometimes be seem as a representation of time. I tryied to construct the Time theme around the theories of Thales of Miletus so the splat could have a deeper meaning. <br /> <br /> Another aspect that I wanted to ecplore was: Why would the Sirens fight agains human pollution? Isn't a little bit Clich\u00e8 and Obvious that they would have conflict with pollution and predatory hunt? But, what if they knew something? They knew that something is happening and the only way is to stop it would sistematically stop with agressive actions toward Earth? Even worse, what if, in their Paradise (that I'll call Atlantis for now), they lived it? Imagine: Atlantis Sank, but Elder Sirens managed to save a few citizens and transported them to a Place with no Time, above the time river, where they could prevent future destruction of their home. (Here i'm accepting that Atlanteans and Sirens are related, but is just My own fan wish, nothing that I truly believe would work), but it was no deal, Their Paradise also Sank, reflecting the retunr of all matter to Water as a warning for the Deluge, staying forever lost in time underwater. .<br /> <br /> Other thing that I was in mind was that in interested in filling the Mages Arcana with Gamelines. A few gamelines can be comparised with Mages Arcana like: Changeling = Fate, Werewolf = Spirit, Geist = Death, etc... and nothing stands for time, hehehehe.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm feeling that I'm not being clear enough yet, but it's the best I can do with my poor English. If you're not interested yet, I can move on, as I'm here merely trying to give a hand in creating something new and exciting. Will continue helping, altough I'll need to wait for you answer to continue working on the Deluge, as I was creating it as a timeless Astral Plane where all that is gone and all that will be gone lies in the Reefs. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:34:07-08:00","id":782348,"title":"","content":"On the first paragraph. When it comes to stories concerning Sirens and Mermaids and them being depicted as &quot;Spirits, Demons etc&quot;, that's pretty much cultural variation rather than gameline differences. For example, Vampires were once categorized as Demons in folklore, yet they bear enough differences to make their own gamelines. As for &quot;Sirens have abit of the same things as other gamelines do&quot;, the things you've listed were purely in cosmetics. Gangrel vampires appear like werewolves, Leechfinger Changelings could be mistaken for vampires etc.<br /> <br /> And when it comes to that certain concepts not existing before until the WoD put them that way, I must note that they actually did exist before then, and the WoD only conceptualized them afterwards. Mage Towers are basically the concept of the witch stories of them following paths of magic or the like (Left Hand Path (not the supplement) was once a term for evil magicdoers). As for Werewolves, there have been stories of Werewolves being men channeling/being possessed by wolf spirits, dealing with familiars or even being commanded to be into a wolf form for their sins. As for Mummies, Egyptians had a thing called a Cartouche. They're basically a hieroglyph depicting a person's name that was put with them after death, and if the person's Cartouche was destroyed, it was believed that the person would then die forever in the afterlife, aka cessitation of existence. Even though they weren't in the &quot;one way&quot; the (n)WoD puts them, they still existed as concepts for them before then.<br /> <br /> As for the Time and Water Aspects, there's only one glaring flaw I can see. The logic I get is &quot;everything changes and nothing remains the same&quot;. By that logic, that would mean that Sirens wouldn't/shouldn't be able to Time travel at all because they can't return to how things were before. I can see what/where you mean to go with the Time motif, but in my opinion it would fit better in the sense of &quot;History&quot;. It would keep the Time motif more in the sense of that you can change the future rather than changing the past. If I may go a step further, the &quot;Deluge = Astral Realm&quot; idea (sorry for not giving this idea up) fits with this, because the Astral Realm (mostly in Tenemos and Anima Mundi) contains the history of all of humanity and nature within it. You can't change the past, but you can see how it was and make a better future to where it won't happen again. Perhaps that's even the flaw of the Abyssal Sirens, that they didn't read their history, and as such are doomed to repeat it (aka the Deluge, there's been more than one story of a primordial flood wiping out life before it began again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). Perhaps as a final note on Time, Genius and Mage both cover it (especially Genius), so the idea of Time Travelling might not be good with Sirens. I do agree though that there should be more to Sirens than just &quot;Ecowarriors&quot; because then it would be kind of like Werewolf the Apocalypse, minus the &quot;Technology is evullll&quot; part.<br /> <br /> As for why Sirens should be fighting pollution, there's a very good reason why that the History motif covers actually. Let's go with the &quot;Nothing remains the same&quot; stance, because this is the best arguement for why they would fight against pollution. Nature's very nature (English at it's finest ladies and gents <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) is to adapt and survive. Pollution and radiation change nature to adapt to this life, and become the new way nature forms. Sure, many things may die, but Nature doesn't. It simply changes to something else, even if how it adapts is very negative to the people living there. There's nothing worked out for Siren's paradise, although on part of the thread calls it &quot;Babylon&quot;, which by now I'm very sure that Leviathan has as their &quot;Paradise&quot;. We should probably take a name of another paradise, preferably separate from Atlantis since most nWoD games can easily be crossed over as easily as they can be played alone.<br /> <br /> As for Mage arcana fittingness, there doesn't have to be a gameline for every Arcana. Sometimes things in the depths should remain in the depths...although the Mage shouldn't whine about not being warned when his eyes are gouged out by whatever was in the Depths. (Just to note, that was meant to be a joke, not anything else. D: Ack sorry)<br /> <br /> Finally, as a person living in the US, your english is much better than 50-95% of people living here. :3 Don't worry, I got your point. I simply offer my counterarguments, and I did get really interested with the &quot;time as history&quot; idea I got that came from the arguments you brought up (I'm sorry for that, and before it's said I apologize alot out of fear of offending someone else). And I see on the Deluge being like the Astral Plane part, I know I bring it up alot. &gt;&gt; If it helps, as far as I know the Astral Planes are connected to humanity and nature as a whole, and therefore can be called Timeless by extension. And don't you mean the Depths? The Reefs were an idea I had for how Sirens viewed the Tenemos. D:<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 12-08-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T10:07:50-08:00","id":782365,"title":"","content":"Oh, i guess we were not understanding each other...! Firt: thanks a lot, I'm very insecure about my English, Second: I'm definitely not ofended but thrilled to be constructing something with you.<br /> <br /> \u200bI wasn't meaning that the time motif would be proeminent like Time traveling every session and creating alternating timelines. No, very far from that. Acually, we were thinking the same, the past can't be changes because it already passed. What I truly meant was that the Sirens had a better understanding of the Time based on a backstory that would create an intimacy with the Deluge, that would be the Unstoppable force that destroyed everything and brings all back to the original matter: Water. So, in the Deluge, as a Timeless place, we could find newspapers from 1975 and 2025, but we would never be able to stop that destruction that we are seeing. The Angst would be that their fight looks lost, for the Deluge already destroyed all the Earth (in the future). The Time motif would be connected to thei backstore, a mythos, not a concrete mechanics that would throw them in the 70s so they could stop a calamity, but a philosophical background that could give a meaning to their fight. They know nature changes and even worse, that it throws back at us sometimes, thay know that it is changing right now, because that's what they are taught by their currents, how to deal/adapt/stop that changes.<br /> <br /> As for the Mages Arcana, it was just a joke, actually <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> wasn't talking serious.<br /> <br /> Going to the Deluge, they would be able to access Sirenuse (Another possible name, taken from Greek Mythology), where all their History past, presente and future would be stocked, alongside with the whole world and nature. Entire cities, submerged, from all times. Better than Time as Motif, as you said: History as Motif. Do not Forget, Always Remenber the time of Our Death (The Subjective Future or the True Death, when their Paradise was lost).<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, loved the Astral Realm Idea and yes, I means the Depths, sorry. The Reefs was just a imagery (Cities as Reefs)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-08-2015, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T13:21:00-08:00","id":782462,"title":"","content":"OH. Okies then, we were understanding each other and all, sorry for confusion on my part.<br /> <br /> Yes, I can see that. Perhaps as a small idea (or perhaps you can clarify if you're meaning for this to be how they see the future), instead of being able to see the absolute future, what if the Deluge held only the most visible future from the perspective of itself? For example, there's this town where this new plant moved to but it causes pollution. There's not enough people who care enough to do something about it and the department of sanitation was bribed to keep quiet. In the Deluge, newspaper stands instead of having their print in the normal world would have leaking ink stating how unlivable the area has become within ten years. The print would describe by general terms so that at least the future isn't directly seen. It would be the future that humanity and nature can envision happening, but not the exact human timeline that would actually occur. It won't tell how the place got bankrupted by the wealthy Sirens who bought them out.<br /> <br /> The reason for this is because the Deluge/Astral reflects humanity and nature's thoughts on things. If there's nobody doing anything and really bad stuff is going on, then it will certainly reflect in the Deluge's premonitions. Perhaps Serenia (Cantre'r Gwaelod, Kitezh, Llys Helig, Dilmun and Ys are all names of mythological lost kingdoms under the waves) is the only place that holds any meaning of the Siren's history, only now ruled by or distorted into Echidna's view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 12-08-2015, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T14:43:01-08:00","id":782511,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Truly liked the Idea of the uncertainty and that Echidna has taking their Paradise for herself. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Alterations</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">- Well, let's see, I suppose they should have only two forms: Human and Halfsiren, with half their bodies resembling a marine animal and all.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">- They could be able to access their alterations to a certain extent, like, you have bioluminescence you can use it paying Breath/Willpower and rolling stamina + proper skill (this way we emulate that they are bringing up an aspect of their interior. How many alterations they can use at the same time is still debatable, but akasha sure have to intervene in this.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">- Yes, i agree that some Alterations should be Ocean exclusive, and a few should be given only to the children of Echidna.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">- Also liked it, but I have been wondering, Higher Akasha means a bigger connection to their History and the World itself, so they could maybe even access Ancient Alterations, like Size of ancient marine Creatures.<br /> <br /> <b>Aquatic Form</b><br /> - Animal Ken could receive a bonus, also.<br /> - Never liked the killing part, it makes the creature bound to losing Serenity or going all uratha and destroying everything. But right now I don't have a better idea.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Backstory</b><br /> - We agreed that they have a Paradise that was lost in the Deluge and now could be taken by Echidna, that controls all the History of the Sirens. What can Echidna do with it, and why she is trying to mimic the Sirens, giving birth to the Vodianoi? I liked your Idea that maybe Echidna has given like to the Sirens in first place but then her ability of doing it again was destroyed and now she tries to redo the formula. Now, who were the Sirens Before their World fell apart and why their world fell apart?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T15:18:05-08:00","id":782531,"title":"","content":"Suggestion: let's change the &quot;The Surfacing&quot; surname, I suppose it no longer defines the game. I guess &quot;The Deluge&quot; maybe fit better. I Would like to hear what you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T16:23:27-08:00","id":782545,"title":"","content":"Other thing: Why, more than physical earthly Oceans, the Innate splat refer to Deluge's Oceans? We could create a few Oceans and backstories to support it. They could represent the moment the Siren Emerges in the Deluge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T17:06:43-08:00","id":782558,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, did you read my google doc on Siren? I haven't posted it at all and yet I set the mood of the game as &quot;Uncertainty&quot;. XD I can post what I put down for it if you want.<br /> <br /> <b>Alterations</b><br /> -I'm willing to go the Mage route and say that they can only have Akasha + 3 Alterations in general and that they're either always on (when in Aquatic form) or if they're things that can be turned on and off (I believe that bioluminescence is an example of something that can be turned on and off by the animals possessing them) you simply need to either pay Breath as normal (in normal form) or have a simple Akasha + Serenity roll to activate it (if in Aquatic form).<br /> -I'm willing to agree to that as long as it means something akin to &quot;dinosaur&quot; like Alterations. I mean, if they're practically Cthulhu-like Alterations then that'd be stepping on Leviathan's toes.<br /> <br /> <b>Aquatic Form</b><br /> -How about just a free specialty to Animal Ken and the specialty applies to whatever animal looks closest to your form? Or a free specialty in Intimidating (if you looked like a shark and wanted to get some trout or salmon to work to clog up some pipe with algae or something for example)? Any free specialty that has to do with your form's appearance.<br /> -Losing Serenity is going to be a part of the game regardless sadly, without it then all Sirens would be like Echidna. Not to mention the &quot;drowning sailors/leading people to their doom&quot; trope needs to be played out somehow, as that's a major part of mermaid lore. <br /> <br /> <b>Backstory</b><br /> Respectively, here are the answers to the questions.<br /> -What can Echidna do with it?: The history of the Sirens or the lost Paradise? For one, I imagine that she would have anything the paradise held at her disposal, which would be prolly priceless treasures she could supply the Sirens who side with her or.her footsoldiers. As for the lost Paradise, it's bound to be guarded heavily enough to make Fort Knox jealous. <br /> -Why is she mimicking the Sirens/Giving birth to Vodianoi?: For now I'm sticking with the idea that she truly does want to create a race of people to survive the apocalypse that humanity will surely give rise to. From the thread's wording, she's basically an example of when humanity discovered evolution and all of the practices of Eugenics that followed for little to no reason. To her, there's no difference between a human and their DNA. <br /> -Who were Sirens before the world fell apart and why did it fall apart?: I have no idea how to answer this without it sounding alot like Werewolf the Forsaken. I would like to imagine that it has to do with the &quot;Song&quot; that turns people into Sirens and it being tampered with in a way that destroyed Siren society Don't take this answer as an answer, it's just my thoughts and I'll make a complete one after skimming the thread once more.<br /> -Though not a question, Abyssal Sirens are meant to be social enemies to normal Sirens with some morally dubious actions that get results. Think &quot;Mage the Ascension Technocracy&quot;, but then split it up into four groups and make them Sirens. <br /> <br /> As for renaming, I think &quot;The Flooding&quot; or &quot;The Drowning&quot; might fit.<br /> <br /> I can't help but feel like we need more people commenting on this or giving criticisms. If anyone's looking at this thread, please feel free to give your two cents or ideas, it would be appreciated. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T17:29:54-08:00","id":782564,"title":"","content":"Completely Agree, we need more criticism and Ideas, if there's anyone reading this, you are not alone, please halp!<br /> <br /> I like &quot;the Drowning&quot; more than &quot;the Flooding&quot;<br /> <br /> We could work out that &quot;Song&quot;, maybe entering a more classical view of Atlantis and &quot;Singing Crystals&quot; or at least take that concept and work something<br /> Also in my head the reasoning of a Abyssal would be something along the line of: We need to Speed up the Deluge, so the Humans Pay and the Uncertainty ends.<br /> <br /> Yes, i want to read your doc alot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-08-2015, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T06:20:14-08:00","id":782756,"title":"","content":"Perhaps that's what we could call it when people become Sirens. &quot;The Drowning&quot; is someone becoming a Siren. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for Abyssals, it depends on the Current actually. Primordial Darkness might want to flood the world, but Mankind's Victory would want to wipe nature away.<br /> <br /> I've noticed that we've focused more on the nature aspects of Sirens than the human aspects as of late, and I've been thinking of how to implement the &quot;human&quot; side of things. I believe that when it comes to dealing with Humans, Sirens as a whole would probably believe that humanity isn't bad or evil nor is technology. I believe that in dealing with humanity, the one thing that Sirens believe that humanity has forgotten is that humanity is as much of the great ecosystem that is nature as everything else is. That if nature goes down, humanity goes down too. In a sense, this means that civilization is as much nature as well. In this sense, it sort of gives an option for Sirens outside of &quot;Ecowarrior&quot; or something, I still need to flesh it out completely. However I do think that this theory gives a path for Dark Passions, who use Humanity's darker impulses for their own use. They could even fit perfectly in for Sirens &quot;Dark Temptress/Seductress&quot; trope too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have pretty much nothing when it comes to things being written. Finals are draining my soul for this week sadly so I don't have much more.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T07:16:09-08:00","id":784149,"title":"","content":"Finals are finally over with, I can write more for the project. At least while break persists and before Spring Semester.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking. This game has mostly been conceptualized before GMC came out. I was thinking that if we continue on this, it would probably be best to write both a Pre-GMC along with a GMC version.<br /> <br /> I've also been thinking on Streams and the like, and how GMC tries to make powers really customizable and the like, what if we tried something along those lines for Streams? I have no idea of where I'm going with this idea, but so far it sounds like (to me) that it would be like Mage arcana and magic, which shouldn't probably be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T07:39:34-08:00","id":784157,"title":"","content":"Stupid question: are all the sirens female?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T10:37:19-08:00","id":784240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784157#post784157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stupid question: are all the sirens female?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, as theres been tales about mermen<br /> <br /> I agree with The streams Idea, I just know nothing about GMC (I'm going to read the update now that my finals are ending).<br /> <br /> I'm sorry for the silence. Have been busy last week and this one with work + college","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-11-2015, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T11:15:20-08:00","id":784251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784157#post784157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stupid question: are all the sirens female?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Yads said. Not all Sirens are female. :3<br /> <br /> And it's fine, it's been the same for me. I should probably read up on GMC too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T11:18:38-08:00","id":784254,"title":"","content":"What if their powers are modular? They select target, effect and other aspects to create a new music. Like selecting notes to create a partiture. I.e: &quot;Single target + invoke + lightning&quot; or &quot;Area + Invoke + Rain&quot;.<br /> <br /> May be a little complex, and all would be musics, like each effect is a different note. All caracthers would need to sing and/or play a instrument. Different instruments could give bonuses to tests based on wich instrument the person was focusing when creating the music","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 12-11-2015, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T11:45:40-08:00","id":784266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784254#post784254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if their powers are modular? They select target, effect and other aspects to create a new music. Like selecting notes to create a partiture. I.e: &quot;Single target + invoke + lightning&quot; or &quot;Area + Invoke + Rain&quot;.<br /> <br /> May be a little complex, and all would be musics, like each effect is a different note. All caracthers would need to sing and/or play a instrument. Different instruments could give bonuses to tests based on wich instrument the person was focusing when creating the music</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That reminds me ALOT of Skyrim and how Dragon Shouts worked. Which I love. This idea sounds like it'll be a good one. Perhaps though there should be something like &quot;if you put two notes that don't work well together, it creates Dissonance and might wreck what you're trying to do with it.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T17:51:39-08:00","id":784442,"title":"","content":"So, let me explain better what I was thinking; There would be three steps in creating a new Music (Now that we like the Idea of powers coming form music we should rename Streams to something else, I would go along with Partiture, Musics, and so On).<br /> <br /> \u200b1 - Choose a Target (Single target, Multi Target or Area), each would have a diferente cost in Breath and XP to buy. something like: Single cost 2 XP, Multi cost 4 and Area 6 (1 XP extra to widen the \u00e1rea)<br /> <br /> 2 - Choose a Propertie (Sense, Control, Transform, Invoke, Destroy), Each also costing differently: Sense = 2, Control = 4, Tranform = 4, Invoke = 6, Destroy = 6<br /> <br /> 3 - Choose a Factor (Rain, Ice, Lightining, Sound, Fear, etc.. The ST would be in charge of deciding if a Factor is valid), the cost of these should be an agr\u00e9ment between the player and the ST. But, let's say Lightining is a 6 at cost.<br /> <br /> EXTRA = The character may spend more XP to &quot;Refine&quot; the music with an Instrument, meaning they receive bonuses if they use the chosen Instrument to play the music (Didn't thought about the costs yet, but for more bonus the character would pay more maybe 1 = 1 to a max of 3?)<br /> <br /> So we would have: A music that invokes a lightning to damage a Single target would cost = 14 XP, but if I want to do that while a play a Violin that gives me +3 in a test it would be 14 + 3 = 17 XP<br /> <br /> I still need to think how to stipulate the cost in Breath and the Rolls, but that's what I have in mind.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T17:57:05-08:00","id":784448,"title":"","content":"Also, thought about a Plot. A group of Sirens find a Old-Like-Hell papyrus with a partiture written. They don't know yet but an Abyssal a Thousand years ago unlocked a way to speed up the Deluge and now they have it, but a Music so Strong touches the heart of every Siren, and the Abyssal already know whats going on, So does Echidna. While they try to unlock the secrets of the Papyrus, the life in Coast City may start to feel a little worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T20:55:18-08:00","id":784522,"title":"","content":"I'm loving the way you put them immensely. The one thing that I can't help but feel is that you shouldn't have to pay a high exp cost to learn new songs to use from words you already know. What if instead, you had to pay exp to learn them separately rather than all at once? I'm sorry, my reasoning for this is because GMC has lowered the cost for most exp prices, but in exchange you need to get loads of beats to get exp. For example what I imagine in GMC terms:<br /> <br /> 1: Single, Multi or Area Target costs 7 Exp to learn each. (Idea: If we're using musical terminology to describe things, how about calling this the &quot;introduction&quot;?)<br /> 2: Properties cost 5 exp to learn each, which increases by 1 exp for each Property the Siren already knows. (This could be called &quot;Verse&quot;)<br /> 3: Factors cost a flat rate of 3 exp apiece. (This could be called &quot;Conclusion&quot;)<br /> 4: To make them into a Lyric (a better version of a song so to speak), it would cost the combined experience that it cost to make the song (like you mentioned?).<br /> <br /> It would be possible to make a song/power to do something if you know the words to them. I have an idea. What if the difference between using the words you know and them being codified into a song (like you suggested) was the same difference between a generic Mage Arcana Spell (Gnosis + Arcana (in this case Akasha + ???)) and a Rote (Attribute + Skill + Arcana (Attribute + Skill + Akasha for Sirens). I have another idea. Doing it without it being codified would be known as &quot;A Capella&quot;, whereas codified songs are known as &quot;Lyrics&quot;?<br /> <br /> Like &quot;Area-Control-Rain&quot; would create a rainstorm regardless. A capella would be &quot;Area-Control-Rain&quot;, but if a Siren codified it into being a Lyric for herself, it becomes &quot;Crying Sky Blues&quot; (or whatever the Siren decides to name it)? Just a suggestion. As for how Breath is used, perhaps the cost depends on both Verses and Introduction? <br /> <br /> Perhaps as another thing, joining an Ocean or Current gives a free Conclusion or Verse upon joining that you may only recieve at Character creation. But a Siren can learn Verses and Conclusions from other Sirens as well. For example, Polaria, the Ocean of Perishing, could give a free Conclusion of &quot;Death&quot;. <br /> <br /> As for the plot, it sounds like a neat story idea. And you reminded me, we need to pick a town for Sirens to base off of. Somewhere in the US since it seems most home cities for splats are based off of a town here. And preferably one that uses Siren themes, so some level of enviornmental disaster (on a managable level to note) and human problems. I imagine New York could fit.I'm sorry if I'm not giving enough ideas of my own or just working off of the ones others make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T23:42:16-08:00","id":784572,"title":"","content":"I actually didn't expect for <b><i>Siren</i></b> to be one of the resurrected fansplats, but I have to say that I am pretty hopeful that it works through.<br /> <br /> My main concern is that there is enough reference material to build up the idea of the Sirens.Granted, the game is about mermaids and there is quite a bit of lore that is available <i>(the main one I see being used is the Greek origins of the Siren [which are more harpy-esque than fish-like but that's more of a matter of what is currently associated with sirens])</i> but, at least in the original forums for <b><i>Siren</i></b>, things were much more touch-and-go &quot;Wouldn't it be cool if&quot; brainstorming; the cosmic axis was scrapped for a philosophy axis based on water and such. <br /> <br /> As for references to build up the Siren repertoire, I'd like to establish some:<br /> <br /> <b>MANGA:</b> <i>School Mermaid (or School Ningyo)</i> is about a journal that reveals a spell that summons mermaids to your school <i>(the setting is set around a middle/high school)</i>. If you kill a mermaid and eat its flesh, you will be able to make the person you are attracted to fall in love with you unconditionally. The mermaids themselves are girls that wear swimsuits with a letter on the chest and are able to phase through solid materials as if everything were composed of water. You need to match the letter with the first letter of the last name of the person you want and you need to do it before sunrise. Spoilers in the box below.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If you fail to consume the flesh of a mermaid before sunrise, the mermaids will them come after you and forcibly &quot;drown&quot; you in the walls of the school, tearing off your clothes and skin to reveal a swimsuit. They have turned you into a mermaid, forced to be hunted down by those who wish to gain love. If the person you are attracted to already loves you, the mermaids become filled with jealousy and will transform, gaining bulging fish eyes, piranha-like teeth, and scales. They will then hunt you down for having the gall to hunt them.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>VIDEO GAME:</b> <i>Mermaid Swamp</i> features a legend about a mermaid and the man who fell in love with her. The legend goes that the man was so enamored by the mermaid's beauty, he built a fish tank large enough to support her and brought her to his mountain home to be with. However, because the water in the tank was swamp water, the mermaid became ill and her beauty faded. Her melodious voice became howls of pain and she eventually died, cursing the man's mountain home so that young women would disappear. The main characters in the story have ended up stuck on the mountain and are haunted by dreams of being drowned and seeing horrifying, bloated creatures. The game also mentions the Shakespearean drama <i>Hamlet</i>, specifically the character Ophelia, who dies by drowning herself. Spoilers below.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In all actuality, the reality behind the mermaid legend is much more horrifying. The main characters speculate that the story goes more like this: a man falls in love with a beautiful woman, most-likely a diver, and kidnaps her. Because he is so attracted to her beauty underwater, he forces her to live in a large tank full of water until she eventually dies from health complications and bloats up. The man grew to love this form as well and he, along with his male descendants, began to forcibly transform and preserve young women as bloated corpses.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>FAIRY TALE:</b><i> The Little Mermaid</i> is basically the precursor to all mermaids of modern times. However, this is not the Disney interpretation. The Hans Christian Anderson tale follows the titular Little Mermaid as she falls in love with a man from the mainland who she saves from drowning. However, her grandmother warns against this as the humans live shorter lives and will go on to Heaven when they die as opposed to the merfolk, whose life lasts three times as long and will dissolve into sea foam when they die. The Little Mermaid longs to be with the man and makes a deal with the Sea Witch by cutting out her tongue <i>(and thus removing her beautiful voice)</i> in exchange for a pair of legs. Of course, the new appendages cause her to feel constant pain and the mermaid-now-human still lacks a soul, which she can only gain if she makes the man fall in love with her. In short, he doesn't and she dissolves into foam. What a shame.<br /> <br /> <b>FOLKLORE</b> <i>Iara</i> of Brazilian mythology is a beautiful woman-spirit who sits in a river and sings an enchanting song that attracts men. When she finds a man coming for her, she brings him underwater where either A) she drowns them with impunity, or B) she makes them one of her lovers for the rest of their life. The rusalka, a river-spirit of Slavic mythology, are said to be the ghosts of young women who commit suicide by drowning and, similar to Iara, would drown men who were attracted to them. The nokken, male river-spirits of Scandinavian mythology, also follow the same modus operandi, although they tend to target women and attract them by playing the violin. Continuously similarly are the morgens of Welsh mythology.<br /> <br /> <b>TOYS:</b> At the risk of stretching this too far, there is the Mattel toy line of Monster High dolls, which feature a surprising amount of horror and mythological creatures as described as teenagers in a monster high school. Yeah. Of the selection of creatures, Monster High notably divides Merfolk and Sirens as two distinct creatures. The merfolk are unmistakably fish-based, as the character Finnegan Wake demonstrates by having a tailed bottom, requiring him to sit in a wheelchair when he is on land. The sirens are allegedly bird-based, though the character Madison Fear features two finned legs and no discernible bird-like traits. There is also the half-mermaid, half-ghost character Sirena Von Boo who can pass through solid objects and floats as if she is swimming in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T09:11:01-08:00","id":784785,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the examples. We really appreciate it. I'll take a look at these for sure, but from a glance it seems that so far some of the Siren stories have a resemblance to Vampire ones (lethal attraction that is). As for what you said on the original forums of Siren, just to ask for criticism, are we doing it justice? I know that there was discussion of throwing out the cosmological and doing philosophical things instead, but are we doing the same here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T10:13:41-08:00","id":784831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784785#post784785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the examples. We really appreciate it. I'll take a look at these for sure, but from a glance it seems that so far some of the Siren stories have a resemblance to Vampire ones (lethal attraction that is). As for what you said on the original forums of Siren, just to ask for criticism, are we doing it justice? I know that there was discussion of throwing out the cosmological and doing philosophical things instead, but are we doing the same here?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Men live, men die; change is good.&quot; -Illaoi, the Kraken Priestess</i><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, it's not in my right to judge. There are a few points that I feel should be expanded upon and developed before going all-in on crunch and mechanics, but there is conversation about the splat and everyone wants to contribute. That is good.<br /> <br /> For suggestions pertaining to <b><i>Siren</i></b>, there was mention of the idea of Time being integrated. Given that the Theme is meant to be about man overstepping the boundaries that were created for them and taking away from nature more than they give back, I feel that Time could work in albeit with a slight change. Perhaps the <b><i>Sirens</i></b> are heralds and harbingers, having seen the many outcomes that branch out from one decision. The many tales of merfolk and river spirits appearing before humans are really an attempt to convince them to change their ways before it id too late to turn back. If the human in question is too far on their path, then the drownings that occur are the only way to keep the future safe. It's really roundabout and may alter the core of <b><i>Siren</i></b>, but I feel that it may work. <br /> <br /> And in terms of questions, I do want to ask: Do Banshees count as Sirens? Do the half-bird creatures that were the Greek Sirens count as Sirens? I know someone mentioned banshees but I don't believe it was addressed. The entire basis for the fansplat is Merfolk so I am unsure how these brothers and sisters factor in. Do they get mentioned? Are they subsets of Sirens that are now completely different? Can they be based on different aspects of marine life <i>(the half-bird sirens are the gulls that subsist off of the atolls of the sea, the banshees are the dragonflies and spiders that make their nest near riverbanks)</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T12:20:47-08:00","id":784901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784831#post784831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all seriousness, it's not in my right to judge. There are a few points that I feel should be expanded upon and developed before going all-in on crunch and mechanics, but there is conversation about the splat and everyone wants to contribute. That is good.<br /> <br /> For suggestions pertaining to <b><i>Siren</i></b>, there was mention of the idea of Time being integrated. Given that the Theme is meant to be about man overstepping the boundaries that were created for them and taking away from nature more than they give back, I feel that Time could work in albeit with a slight change. Perhaps the <b><i>Sirens</i></b> are heralds and harbingers, having seen the many outcomes that branch out from one decision. The many tales of merfolk and river spirits appearing before humans are really an attempt to convince them to change their ways before it id too late to turn back. If the human in question is too far on their path, then the drownings that occur are the only way to keep the future safe. It's really roundabout and may alter the core of <b><i>Siren</i></b>, but I feel that it may work.<br /> <br /> And in terms of questions, I do want to ask: Do Banshees count as Sirens? Do the half-bird creatures that were the Greek Sirens count as Sirens? I know someone mentioned banshees but I don't believe it was addressed. The entire basis for the fansplat is Merfolk so I am unsure how these brothers and sisters factor in. Do they get mentioned? Are they subsets of Sirens that are now completely different? Can they be based on different aspects of marine life <i>(the half-bird sirens are the gulls that subsist off of the atolls of the sea, the banshees are the dragonflies and spiders that make their nest near riverbanks)</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. That's really fitting. Especially with the mention of Banshees and their mythology of them being spirits forwarning of human death and as &quot;messengers of another world&quot;. The idea you posted in the first paragraph I feel could actually be integrated without much trouble or much changing (at least to how I see Siren coming as). <br /> <br /> As for Banshees and the like, the mentions I recalled were from the thread for a Stream using noise to harm people known as &quot;The Banshees Wails&quot; and one reference from Yads. I think that banshees can be used as inspiration for Siren, especially with the Wikipedia entry saying that Mermaid and Banshees have been confused with each other before. I think one thing that also needs to be done is resolving the issues you pointed up, the &quot;Siren/Harpie-Mermaid-Banshee&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Do Banshees count as Sirens? - </b>I believe that Banshees would/should be a subsplat to Sirens, like Ghouls are to Vampires. They can hear the Song and manipulate it to a small extent, but not to the grand extent that Sirens do. Their wailing could be attributed to some form of night terrors or something a Banshee suffers when a negative event happens in man or nature, they get these (very vague might I add) prophecies of doom from their connection to the Deluge.<br /> <br /> <b>Do the half-bird creatures that were Greek Sirens count as Sirens? - </b>I feel the need to play on this is present, but I don't have any ideas. The closest I get is an inspiration. In Legend of Zelda: The Wind Waker, before Hyrule was flooded the Zoras (fish people) went to the top of a mountain and they instead transformed into a race of bird people known as the Rito. Very tribal like and even acting as messenger (in the form of mailmen that is, easy to traverse the sea by flying over it).<br /> <br /> <b>Do they get mentioned? Are they subsets of Sirens that are now completely different? - </b>On one hand, I feel this could be stepping on Werewolf's/Changing Breeds toes. On another, I think it's fine. I think that it could be possible for Sirens of that nature to look like other kinds of marine life (especially the Freshwater Ocean, because those are mainly inland ponds/rivers), but then the only problem becomes &quot;how will the Deluge look to them&quot;? The Deluge looking like a flooded world to Sirens. It would mean that at least as a whole, the birds/insects that live around water that Sirens could get features from would need to be capable of swimming underwater, if nothing else and even for a short time if it comes down to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T12:45:31-08:00","id":784920,"title":"","content":"Heh, wasn't alone in the Time aspect. But I like the place we are, and I find what Reaper suggested fitting with what we were working on, Nice!<br /> <br /> \u200bDo Banshee count as Siren?<br /> I say yes. Banshees could be either part of a Rework in the Inherent Axis or, as Saulotthe said, they could be a minor splat of Sirens, Humans affected by the Deluge, prophecies and such. As I said in a post earlier I thought that maybe if the Inherent Axis represented Aspects of where the Siren Drowned in the Deluge, maybe we could work diferente aspects of diferente mythologies (Harpy-like Sirens Drowned in the surface, near the top of the highest mountains that now are nothing but tips of rocks above the water. So diferente mythologies could be embraced in diferente axis. Don't know, I'm not truly fond of this Idea, but maybe you guys can work something out of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T13:18:06-08:00","id":784941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784901#post784901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Do Banshees count as Sirens? - </b>I believe that Banshees would/should be a subsplat to Sirens, like Ghouls are to Vampires. They can hear the Song and manipulate it to a small extent, but not to the grand extent that Sirens do. Their wailing could be attributed to some form of night terrors or something a Banshee suffers when a negative event happens in man or nature, they get these (very vague might I add) prophecies of doom from their connection to the Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can definitely see Ghoul-types or even Blood Doll-types that were driven mad by the Song. Maybe they see the world as a mixture of reality and the Deluge simultaneously and they are incredibly sensitive to the misdeeds of humanity. They live in constant terror and pain and can only get respite by calling out the death of another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Do the half-bird creatures that were Greek Sirens count as Sirens? - </b>I feel the need to play on this is present, but I don't have any ideas. The closest I get is an inspiration. In Legend of Zelda: The Wind Waker, before Hyrule was flooded the Zoras (fish people) went to the top of a mountain and they instead transformed into a race of bird people known as the Rito. Very tribal like and even acting as messenger (in the form of mailmen that is, easy to traverse the sea by flying over it). </div> </div> </div>Ironically, I am a gamer and I am not necessarily familiar with the Legend of Zelda series, but the Zora/Rito connection is incredibly brilliant. I know a <i><b>Supernatural </b></i>episode that features a sea-creature-esque siren that enchants men into killing or destroying the thing that they love most. I believe most incarnations of Harpies that also have them lure their prey using their voice would work as well. Both <b><i>The Odyssey</i></b> and <b><i>Jason and the Argonauts</i></b> include sirens as bird women who lure ships into jagged rocks and feast upon the sailors on board. There's also Talon from <b><i>Static Shock</i></b> who was mutated by the Big Bang to look like a harpy and has a sonic scream.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Do they get mentioned? Are they subsets of Sirens that are now completely different? - </b>On one hand, I feel this could be stepping on Werewolf's/Changing Breeds toes. On another, I think it's fine. I think that it could be possible for Sirens of that nature to look like other kinds of marine life (especially the Freshwater Ocean, because those are mainly inland ponds/rivers), but then the only problem becomes &quot;how will the Deluge look to them&quot;? The Deluge looking like a flooded world to Sirens. It would mean that at least as a whole, the birds/insects that live around water that Sirens could get features from would need to be capable of swimming underwater, if nothing else and even for a short time if it comes down to it. </div> </div> </div>I think that fleshing out the visuals of The Deluge would be something. Like, because the mermaid-Sirens are entirely fish-like, perhaps they see The Deluge as a flooded world but from the open waters, never having to weave through the submerged canyons and the roots of great trees. In Japan, there is a creature called the sazae-oni which are demons of sea snails that would entice sailors to have sex with them only to cut off their testicles when they were done. Perhaps these &quot;mollusk-Sirens&quot; are closer to the bottom of the flooded world and do not see the world as much as the mermaid-Sirens. And the more mammalian Sirens based of of the Selkie <i>(human-looking creatures that become seals by wearing a special skin)</i> are found closer to the surface of The Deluge, unable to sink deep enough in the water before having to breach the surface while the harpy-Sirens are firmly above the surface and rest on the remains of the solid earth.<br /> <br /> As a side-note, I've noticed that a lot of the morals behind the folklore of river people/mermaids/sirens is a warning not to be entranced by beauty. Would &quot;do not disturb the beauty of the natural world&quot; also work as one of the themes for <b><i>Siren</i></b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T15:14:48-08:00","id":785013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784941#post784941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can definitely see Ghoul-types or even Blood Doll-types that were driven mad by the Song. Maybe they see the world as a mixture of reality and the Deluge simultaneously and they are incredibly sensitive to the misdeeds of humanity. They live in constant terror and pain and can only get respite by calling out the death of another.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, on the forum a question was asked that there should be two subsplats to things. Like the Ghoul and Blood doll types like you said. What if the Ghoul Type are Banshees, and the Blood Doll type are called &quot;The Mute&quot;? People who resist the call out of fear of it, but the extra breath they have in their system makes them easy feeding targets for Sirens?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784941#post784941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically, I am a gamer and I am not necessarily familiar with the Legend of Zelda series, but the Zora/Rito connection is incredibly brilliant. I know a <i><b>Supernatural </b></i>episode that features a sea-creature-esque siren that enchants men into killing or destroying the thing that they love most. I believe most incarnations of Harpies that also have them lure their prey using their voice would work as well. Both <b><i>The Odyssey</i></b> and <b><i>Jason and the Argonauts</i></b> include sirens as bird women who lure ships into jagged rocks and feast upon the sailors on board. There's also Talon from <b><i>Static Shock</i></b> who was mutated by the Big Bang to look like a harpy and has a sonic scream.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Glad to see that Wind Waker isn't the first example of this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784941#post784941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that fleshing out the visuals of The Deluge would be something. Like, because the mermaid-Sirens are entirely fish-like, perhaps they see The Deluge as a flooded world but from the open waters, never having to weave through the submerged canyons and the roots of great trees. In Japan, there is a creature called the sazae-oni which are demons of sea snails that would entice sailors to have sex with them only to cut off their testicles when they were done. Perhaps these &quot;mollusk-Sirens&quot; are closer to the bottom of the flooded world and do not see the world as much as the mermaid-Sirens. And the more mammalian Sirens based of of the Selkie <i>(human-looking creatures that become seals by wearing a special skin)</i> are found closer to the surface of The Deluge, unable to sink deep enough in the water before having to breach the surface while the harpy-Sirens are firmly above the surface and rest on the remains of the solid earth.<br /> <br /> As a side-note, I've noticed that a lot of the morals behind the folklore of river people/mermaids/sirens is a warning not to be entranced by beauty. Would &quot;do not disturb the beauty of the natural world&quot; also work as one of the themes for <b><i>Siren</i></b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem is that the form of a Siren can be altered and changed. It's possible for Sirens to appear like other animals without needing to be a kind of &quot;strain&quot; so to speak. My only suggestion is that the Deluge would appear differently depending on where in the world you're at rather than &quot;what kind of person or strain of Siren you are&quot;. Kind of like how the Shadow and Underworld remains the same to Werewolves and Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> As for the folklore, I would say that &quot;do not disturb the beauty of the natural world&quot; works and is abit covered by the &quot;do not overstep your boundaries&quot; that Sirens hold for both civilization and nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T17:34:48-08:00","id":785083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785013#post785013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> IIRC, on the forum a question was asked that there should be two subsplats to things. Like the Ghoul and Blood doll types like you said. What if the Ghoul Type are Banshees, and the Blood Doll type are called &quot;The Mute&quot;? People who resist the call out of fear of it, but the extra breath they have in their system makes them easy feeding targets for Sirens?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would work. Maybe there's a way to divorce it from being too similar to Blood Dolls. Maybe Sirens find people who are Breathless and use them as a sort of lure to find people who do have Breath. Kind of a dark mirror of fishermen. <i>(Granted, this idea is me assuming that Breath is interpreted to be a breath of life and people who are Breathless have long-since become numb to the world around them, thus lacking the breath of life.)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only problem is that the form of a Siren can be altered and changed. It's possible for Sirens to appear like other animals without needing to be a kind of &quot;strain&quot; so to speak. My only suggestion is that the Deluge would appear differently depending on where in the world you're at rather than &quot;what kind of person or strain of Siren you are&quot;. Kind of like how the Shadow and Underworld remains the same to Werewolves and Sin-Eaters. </div> </div> </div>Ah. I misinterpreted your words earlier. So a Siren's aquatic form can be changed as in they can, at-will, morph parts of their body so they gain a lobster's claw or is it a cosmetic thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the folklore, I would say that &quot;do not disturb the beauty of the natural world&quot; works and is abit covered by the &quot;do not overstep your boundaries&quot; that Sirens hold for both civilization and nature. </div> </div> </div>I see, I think a question for this is &quot;What gives Sirens the right to travel both the natural world and the civilized world?&quot; That's sort of a balancing act that make Sirens seem rather...odd, especially if the idea of the &quot;harbinger&quot; is fully incorporated. Perhaps the Sirens cannot enforce change themselves? There was a bit in the original post about Sirens that are more-aligned to humanity or more-aligned to nature which seems rather dissonant if Sirens come between the two. Perhaps Sirens are the mediators attempting to temper civilization with nature, reducing humanity's claim on nature but also preventing nature from invoking its wrath on humanity <i>(such as how the Little Mermaid rescues the sailor from drowning)</i>. Sirens themselves want to save humanity from its darker side while taming the world's forces as to not take vengeance on the ones who have wronged it. <br /> <br /> As side-notes about the way that the Currents and Oceans are handled, I enjoy the Currents and feel that they work but I am skeptical about the Oceans due to the fact that they are a little too literal in what they are describing. <b>Polaria </b>and <b>Fresh </b>sound perfect and make sense, but name-dropping the Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian Oceans are too on-the-nose. Of course, I believe that is due to them being artifacts from the previous thread, especially as one of the ideas in the original post stated that the Oceans were more symbolic of what archetype the Siren calls upon when she Surfaces.<br /> <br /> Is there another way to refer to this splat so it isn't as confusing to refer to the Atlantic Ocean in terms of the game and in reality? Is it possible to change it so it refers to something different? This was the main reason I posited having sections of The Deluge relate to the harpy-Sirens and mermaid-Sirens and such. It would be difficult as the Sirens are supposed to &quot;Surface&quot;, but can <i><b>Depth </b></i>play a part as a splat, where the distance the Siren travels in order to Surface affects her in the ways that the Oceans do?<br /> <br /> <i>(Such as this: there are five Depths that a Siren may see The Deluge and it changes how long it takes for them to Surface. Sirens that are closer to the top see the depth of The Deluge as a dark place and Surface faster, giving them the outlook of the Fresh Ocean. Sirens that are at the lowest point experience The Deluge in full force and take the longest to Surface, giving them the outlook of the Polaria Ocean.)</i><br /> <br /> Also as a side-note, there is a fifth river in Hades that could be added as an Abyssal Current: <i><b>Acheron. the River of Woe</b></i>. Perhaps this relates to grief, pain, and catharsis where Sirens believe that the only way to lash out until others learn to regret.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T18:30:46-08:00","id":785105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785083#post785083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That would work. Maybe there's a way to divorce it from being too similar to Blood Dolls. Maybe Sirens find people who are Breathless and use them as a sort of lure to find people who do have Breath. Kind of a dark mirror of fishermen. <i>(Granted, this idea is me assuming that Breath is interpreted to be a breath of life and people who are Breathless have long-since become numb to the world around them, thus lacking the breath of life.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. In the original forum since Sirens had the &quot;beauty&quot; theme (in mythology, it's optional to play on it in game), &quot;Breath&quot; was suggested to be the Sirens fuel stat. They feed off of the breath of life, aka the Human Soul. They don't eat souls to note, but it's been an idea that killing a human (taking the breath of life like you said) could replenish the Sirens entire Breath pool while other ways to gain breath could include stealing someone's voice (like in the little mermaid) or the like could replenish some.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785083#post785083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah. I misinterpreted your words earlier. So a Siren's aquatic form can be changed as in they can, at-will, morph parts of their body so they gain a lobster's claw or is it a cosmetic thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea I had for this was that Sirens could choose how their Aquatic form appears to some extent, and they gain mechanical bonuses to things depending on what it is. They're often a trait found on some aquatic animal in nature, and I've suggested that it's best to have three kinds of Alterations (what these morphs are known as). General (any siren can get), Oceanic (Exclusive only to Oceans and based on the animals that live in the Ocean the most (like Polaria Sirens getting natural antifreeze that most fishes in Ant/Arctic oceans have which would make said Sirens with said Alteration immune to cold penalties or weather)) and Echidna/Abyssal ones (Exclusive to Abyssal Currents and followers of Echidna).<br /> <br /> If it helps to note, Alterations WILL be limited and that it's possible to use them outside of Aquatic form, but only with the expendature of Breath. In Aquatic form though, the Alterations apply for free and are usually the type of things that are &quot;always on&quot;. For example, a Siren who instead of having a fish tail on her bottom half has octopus tentacles instead which are very good at grabbing things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785083#post785083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see, I think a question for this is &quot;What gives Sirens the right to travel both the natural world and the civilized world?&quot; That's sort of a balancing act that make Sirens seem rather...odd, especially if the idea of the &quot;harbinger&quot; is fully incorporated. Perhaps the Sirens cannot enforce change themselves? There was a bit in the original post about Sirens that are more-aligned to humanity or more-aligned to nature which seems rather dissonant if Sirens come between the two. Perhaps Sirens are the mediators attempting to temper civilization with nature, reducing humanity's claim on nature but also preventing nature from invoking its wrath on humanity <i>(such as how the Little Mermaid rescues the sailor from drowning)</i>. Sirens themselves want to save humanity from its darker side while taming the world's forces as to not take vengeance on the ones who have wronged it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the right is as you said. Sirens are mediators between man and nature. Keeping the boundaries while ensuring they don't fall the same way. If it helps for more conceptualization, Abyssal Currents have philosophies on siding with one and abandoning their duty (Mankind's Victory and Primordial Darkness) or those far more interested in darker, more compromising solutions (Dark Passions and Wisdom)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785083#post785083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As side-notes about the way that the Currents and Oceans are handled, I enjoy the Currents and feel that they work but I am skeptical about the Oceans due to the fact that they are a little too literal in what they are describing. <b>Polaria </b>and <b>Fresh </b>sound perfect and make sense, but name-dropping the Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian Oceans are too on-the-nose. Of course, I believe that is due to them being artifacts from the previous thread, especially as one of the ideas in the original post stated that the Oceans were more symbolic of what archetype the Siren calls upon when she Surfaces.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are indeed artifacts. The best reason I can see why Oceans should remain the X-Splat name and theme is the same reason why some Alterations are exclusive to Oceans. The animals most living in the Ocean are what make the Ocean Alterations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785083#post785083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is there another way to refer to this splat so it isn't as confusing to refer to the Atlantic Ocean in terms of the game and in reality? Is it possible to change it so it refers to something different? This was the main reason I posited having sections of The Deluge relate to the harpy-Sirens and mermaid-Sirens and such. It would be difficult as the Sirens are supposed to &quot;Surface&quot;, but can <i><b>Depth </b></i>play a part as a splat, where the distance the Siren travels in order to Surface affects her in the ways that the Oceans do?<br /> <br /> <i>(Such as this: there are five Depths that a Siren may see The Deluge and it changes how long it takes for them to Surface. Sirens that are closer to the top see the depth of The Deluge as a dark place and Surface faster, giving them the outlook of the Fresh Ocean. Sirens that are at the lowest point experience The Deluge in full force and take the longest to Surface, giving them the outlook of the Polaria Ocean.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. In that case, would it seem abit better to rename the X-Splat to &quot;Depth&quot; and name the Oceans after Oceanic Zones based off of depth? We can still use the &quot;Ocean Alterations based on animals that live the most in said oceans&quot;, but apply them to Depth. Honestly I don't know which we should go with, they both sound like good ideas. I still favor Ocean abit because there are some animals that exclusively live in said zones and would be easier to base Alterations off of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785083#post785083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also as a side-note, there is a fifth river in Hades that could be added as an Abyssal Current: <i><b>Acheron. the River of Woe</b></i>. Perhaps this relates to grief, pain, and catharsis where Sirens believe that the only way to lash out until others learn to regret.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know of this. How does this sound? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Current of the Void AKA Acheron, the River of Woe:</b> Fuck nature. Fuck civilization. Fuck it all under a world ending tidal wave and give in to the sweet serenity of nothingness.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, this could be the current that followers of Echidna subscribe to, to make a new race out of humanity to survive the apocalypse it'll eventually bring unto itself (a manmade apocalypse made by WW3 is just as plausible as a biblical one afterall). It could alternatively be named <b>Current of Echidna, </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 12-12-2015, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T18:48:53-08:00","id":785118,"title":"","content":"All the discussions are pretty nice, I'm loving it, wish I had a better english base so I could discuss with you guys. But so far I'm loving how are you handling it all. The &quot;Depths&quot; Idea is neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T20:52:01-08:00","id":785157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785105#post785105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of. In the original forum since Sirens had the &quot;beauty&quot; theme (in mythology, it's optional to play on it in game), &quot;Breath&quot; was suggested to be the Sirens fuel stat. They feed off of the breath of life, aka the Human Soul. They don't eat souls to note, but it's been an idea that killing a human (taking the breath of life like you said) could replenish the Sirens entire Breath pool while other ways to gain breath could include stealing someone's voice (like in the little mermaid) or the like could replenish some.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a baseline, I feel that the most basic way to gain Breath is to kiss a willing mortal <i>(and, in effect, stealing their breath away) </i>while the most powerful way is to, not just kill, but drown a mortal <i>(forcibly stealing all their breath). </i>Other ways that vary in how much Breath it offers is stealing someone's voice <i>(I don't know how a Siren would do this literally, but perhaps figuratively stealing their voice by impersonating them)</i>, impressing them through spectacular feats <i>(and having them breathless [pun])</i>, and scaring them <i>(and forcing them to gasp out their breath)</i>. Perhaps, linking into the idea of &quot;the breath of life&quot;, Sirens can help someone out of a depressive state by expending their Breath or can steal even more Breath away by dashing their hopes. Of course, the latter action may end up costing the Siren some of her Serenity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea I had for this was that Sirens could choose how their Aquatic form appears to some extent, and they gain mechanical bonuses to things depending on what it is. They're often a trait found on some aquatic animal in nature, and I've suggested that it's best to have three kinds of Alterations (what these morphs are known as). General (any siren can get), Oceanic (Exclusive only to Oceans and based on the animals that live in the Ocean the most (like Polaria Sirens getting natural antifreeze that most fishes in Ant/Arctic oceans have which would make said Sirens with said Alteration immune to cold penalties or weather)) and Echidna/Abyssal ones (Exclusive to Abyssal Currents and followers of Echidna).<br /> <br /> If it helps to note, Alterations WILL be limited and that it's possible to use them outside of Aquatic form, but only with the expendature of Breath. In Aquatic form though, the Alterations apply for free and are usually the type of things that are &quot;always on&quot;. For example, a Siren who instead of having a fish tail on her bottom half has octopus tentacles instead which are very good at grabbing things. </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. In a way to mirror things, will Abyssal Alterations <i>(That is the set-in-stone name, right?)</i> allow Sirens to take on unnatural forms as opposed to the natural Oceanic forms? Like, Sirens that follow the Current of Dark Secrets gain features akin to those of the <i>Deep Ones</i> as opposed to the sleek body of an Oceanic dolphin?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are indeed artifacts. The best reason I can see why Oceans should remain the X-Splat name and theme is the same reason why some Alterations are exclusive to Oceans. The animals most living in the Ocean are what make the Ocean Alterations.<br /> <br /> <b>[...]</b><br /> <br /> Hrm. In that case, would it seem abit better to rename the X-Splat to &quot;Depth&quot; and name the Oceans after Oceanic Zones based off of depth? We can still use the &quot;Ocean Alterations based on animals that live the most in said oceans&quot;, but apply them to Depth. Honestly I don't know which we should go with, they both sound like good ideas. I still favor Ocean abit because there are some animals that exclusively live in said zones and would be easier to base Alterations off of. </div> </div> </div>There are categories of zones based on the factors of Depth and sunlight that define areas where marine life may exist. The Oceans <i>(literal oceans of the Earth)</i> are actually divided into zones based of depth known as the Pelagic zones. These zones are divided based on the amount of sunlight that can penetrate through into the waters, which affects the amount of plant life available and what creatures are able to live in the regions. <br /> <br /> The <b>Littoral Zone</b> is the area where sea and land are the closest together, the area in which there is a notable ebb and flow of the tide. Most of the creatures that can live in this area are various types of shellfish and mollusks such as crabs, shrimp, bivalves, barnacles, whelks, sea stars, and the occasional fish.<br /> <br /> The <b>Neritic Zone</b> describes an area or body of water in which sunlight fully penetrates the water's surface and reaches the bottom of the body. Areas such as these support most types of coastal fish, coral reefs, otters, seals, turtles, and seahorses. <br /> <br /> The <b>Photic/Epipalegic Zone</b> has the most amount of sunlight, strong enough to allow the plant life within to undergo photosynthesis. This is also the area where most sea life resides and contains creatures such as jellyfish, dolphins, turtles, and sharks. Other smaller fish such as barracuda and tuna as well as plankton live in this area as well.<br /> <br /> The <b>Mesopalegic Zone</b> still has some sunlight but only enough to be considered twilight. In this area, photosynthesis is impossible, so the creatures that live here either have better gills to breathe or have minimized their use of movement. Such creatures include swordfish and squid; creatures within this area are also capable of biolumination, color-based camouflage, and ambush predation.<br /> <br /> The <b>Bathyal/Bathypalegic Zone</b> only has enough light to be considered midnight. At this point, most creatures that are considered fish cannot survive, meaning that giant squids, whales, octopus anglerfish, and creatures coated with a layer of slime can survive. Because of how deep the zone is and how hard it is to live in such conditions, most food comes from the remains floating down to the zone. <br /> <br /> The <b>Abyssal/Abyssopalegic Zone</b> is covered in almost entirely pure darkness. Pressure is at its highest and only creatures such as sea cucumbers, sea squirts, snails, starfish, sea urchins, sea spiders, and creatures that can survive on the sea bed can survive. Most of these creatures have no eyes due to the lack of light. <br /> <br /> Beyond that is the <b>Hadal/Hadopalegic/Trench Zone</b>, named after Hades. At this point, there is not information on what kinds of creature can exist. Most of these creatures subsist on whatever trickles down and from the heat vents in the ocean floor. <br /> <br /> If <b>Depths</b> is used as an axis, the playable Sirens should be found between the Littorial and Bathyal Zone, while Sirens that are found within the Abyssal Zone and below have been overcome by the visions of The Deluge and become warped.<br /> <br /> For <b><i>Siren</i></b><i>, </i>perhaps the Siren find themselves drowning, either metaphorically or literally, and see visions of The Deluge. Some have been dragged down into the deep sea; some have been left on the coast of what remains of once-great mountain tops. The Song is an echoing noise that allow the Sirens to look upwards towards the surface and find the light that is shining down upon them, calling to them with its haunting tune. The Surfacing is the moment in which the Sirens decide to fight rather than being carried down and they swim upwards to find air and to feel the warmth of the light on their skin. For some, it feels like a process that last years; for others, it is a fleeting moment. Time within The Deluge is not always constant. Once the Siren reaches the Surface, she lets out a gasp for air, gaining her first Breath in the world of The Deluge. She realizes the struggle with the sea that was drowning her was just a single possibility and that she worked to break through that reality and create her own. She looks back at the waters and sees all of the other Sirens struggling with The Deluge. Some are gasping for air long before they reach the surface, some are being dragged down further, beyond the depths into the great unknown. When the Siren awakens in the real world, she is gifted with the knowledge of The Deluge being a possible future that will claim all of humanity if they continue their ways. She knows she needs to avert this future and, with her experiences in traversing through the Depths, knows how she will go about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know of this. How does this sound? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Current of the Void AKA Acheron, the River of Woe:</b> Fuck nature. Fuck civilization. Fuck it all under a world ending tidal wave and give in to the sweet serenity of nothingness.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, this could be the current that followers of Echidna subscribe to, to make a new race out of humanity to survive the apocalypse it'll eventually bring unto itself (a manmade apocalypse made by WW3 is just as plausible as a biblical one afterall). It could alternatively be named <b>Current of Echidna, </b> </div> </div> </div>Neat. And this Abyssal Current is named as the Current of the Void? Will the other Currents receive a similar treatment or are they going to be &quot;the Current of Dark Secrets&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T08:04:46-08:00","id":785393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785157#post785157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-ico