n effect, stealing their breath away) </i>while the most powerful way is to, not just kill, but drown a mortal <i>(forcibly stealing all their breath). </i>Other ways that vary in how much Breath it offers is stealing someone's voice <i>(I don't know how a Siren would do this literally, but perhaps figuratively stealing their voice by impersonating them)</i>, impressing them through spectacular feats <i>(and having them breathless [pun])</i>, and scaring them <i>(and forcing them to gasp out their breath)</i>. Perhaps, linking into the idea of &quot;the breath of life&quot;, Sirens can help someone out of a depressive state by expending their Breath or can steal even more Breath away by dashing their hopes. Of course, the latter action may end up costing the Siren some of her Serenity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just a fantastic pun storm. XD Yes, these are all really good ideas! Especially the last one, which I imagine would be a regular gameplay (or downtime) way for Sirens to replenish their Breath by getting people to act. I also imagine it being the most popular way for Abyssal Sirens to gain Breath (by dashing hopes).<br /> <br /> One idea for Abyssals that I recall from the original forum is the idea of an Abyssal Siren Cheerleader. She seduces most of the boys she meets and at the end of every relationship, she reveals it was all a lie and breaks their hearts, leaving them hollow versions of themselves. But when he said &quot;I love you&quot; to each of them, she actually meant it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785157#post785157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense. In a way to mirror things, will Abyssal Alterations <i>(That is the set-in-stone name, right?)</i> allow Sirens to take on unnatural forms as opposed to the natural Oceanic forms? Like, Sirens that follow the Current of Dark Secrets gain features akin to those of the <i>Deep Ones</i> as opposed to the sleek body of an Oceanic dolphin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. The only thing that's a small problem is that there's still a difference between Abyssals and Echidna followers. Abyssals have dubious and probably Serenity reducing solutions, but they get stuff done and the Abyssal Difference from the normal Currents is simply philosophical. Echidna mixes fish and human together for flimsy and evil reasons and joining up with her (as far as I've read on the original forums) it doesn't seem entirely possible to leave her side once you're on it. Another idea I had which is why I put a difference between Abyssal and Echidnal Alterations was that Echidna could give special Alterations that were more potent than normal Alterations and weren't subject to the limits of Sirens Alteration limit. However, Echidna Alterations are still present <b>even on human form </b>to level the cost.<br /> <br /> I would say that the &quot;Deep Ones&quot; should be kept with Echidna, because if Sirens were able to <i>naturally </i>get those Alterations, then it would be stepping on Leviathan the Tempest's toes. However, because Echidnal Alterations are unnatural by definition, it would be finer because then it wouldn't step on Leviathan as much as it would be if they were natural. I also sort of imagined that Abyssal Sirens would get Alterations based on animals in the Abyssopalegic Zone as noted in your next paragraph. Deep black squid, Angler fish, various other things that make most people &quot;nope&quot; out of the ocean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785157#post785157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are categories of zones based on the factors of Depth and sunlight that define areas where marine life may exist. The Oceans <i>(literal oceans of the Earth)</i> are actually divided into zones based of depth known as the Pelagic zones. These zones are divided based on the amount of sunlight that can penetrate through into the waters, which affects the amount of plant life available and what creatures are able to live in the regions.<br /> <b>...</b><br /> If <b>Depths</b> is used as an axis, the playable Sirens should be found between the Littorial and Bathyal Zone, while Sirens that are found within the Abyssal Zone and below have been overcome by the visions of The Deluge and become warped.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is nice. To ask, Abyssal zone has no connection to the Abyssal Currents? The reason I ask is because Abyssals aren't an inherent splat (or at least, weren't meant to be inherent splats at all). Or are Sirens who Surface part of the Sirens who surface as absolute monsters? Kind of like how some Mages awake to being some of the Mad?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm sold on this by the way, <b>Depths </b>should be the X Splat. Is there any objections? :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785157#post785157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b><i>Siren</i></b><i>, </i>perhaps the Siren find themselves drowning, either metaphorically or literally, and see visions of The Deluge. Some have been dragged down into the deep sea; some have been left on the coast of what remains of once-great mountain tops. The Song is an echoing noise that allow the Sirens to look upwards towards the surface and find the light that is shining down upon them, calling to them with its haunting tune. The Surfacing is the moment in which the Sirens decide to fight rather than being carried down and they swim upwards to find air and to feel the warmth of the light on their skin. For some, it feels like a process that last years; for others, it is a fleeting moment. Time within The Deluge is not always constant. Once the Siren reaches the Surface, she lets out a gasp for air, gaining her first Breath in the world of The Deluge. She realizes the struggle with the sea that was drowning her was just a single possibility and that she worked to break through that reality and create her own. She looks back at the waters and sees all of the other Sirens struggling with The Deluge. Some are gasping for air long before they reach the surface, some are being dragged down further, beyond the depths into the great unknown. When the Siren awakens in the real world, she is gifted with the knowledge of The Deluge being a possible future that will claim all of humanity if they continue their ways. She knows she needs to avert this future and, with her experiences in traversing through the Depths, knows how she will go about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Perhaps fittingly, this reminds me of Princess the Hopeful, but played differently. When Princesses Blossom, they are stuck in a really stressful situation where if they picked an option that wasn't &quot;the right thing&quot; they wouldn't have been able to forgive themselves otherwise. After which, usually when they fall asleep they recall bits of pieces of their previous incarnations/past lives, all the way back to the time of the Kingdoms in which were the ultimate pinnacle of good. When they blossom, they know that it was possible to make the Kingdom once, and therefore possible to create it once more.<br /> <br /> This story for Sirens is the backwards (or is it forwards?) version of that. It's where they're trapped by nearly drowning into despair, but despite all odds cling to and act for hope. When they Surface, they become Sirens and know the truth of the Deluge. It's the recorded past and forseeable future that everything and everyone will eventually sink to become. I take it that the &quot;She knows she needs to avert this future and how she will go about it&quot; was referring to joining Social Axises? Speaking of which, I forgot to mention that in the thread, Sirens who aren't a part of a social axis are known as &quot;Castaways&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me, this story of Surfacing actually makes this gameline a nice successor to Werewolf the Apocalypse in a sense. Instead of fighting against an opponent already present and a completely unavoidable apocalypse however, Sirens faces antagonists only when it threatens to overstep boundaries and that the apocalyptic scenario is both known of and avoidable if enough help is given to Sirens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785157#post785157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat. And this Abyssal Current is named as the Current of the Void? Will the other Currents receive a similar treatment or are they going to be &quot;the Current of Dark Secrets&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking, there'll be five Abyssal Currents as it seems. Dark Passions, Dark Wisdom, Mankind's Victory, Primordial Darkness and Void. The first four are artifacts from the thread, but the Rivers of Hades were suggested to be alternate names for them (or renames because at the time of those posts, that's what was being discussed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T13:05:57-08:00","id":785526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785394#post785394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably. The only thing that's a small problem is that there's still a difference between Abyssals and Echidna followers. Abyssals have dubious and probably Serenity reducing solutions, but they get stuff done and the Abyssal Difference from the normal Currents is simply philosophical. Echidna mixes fish and human together for flimsy and evil reasons and joining up with her (as far as I've read on the original forums) it doesn't seem entirely possible to leave her side once you're on it. Another idea I had which is why I put a difference between Abyssal and Echidnal Alterations was that Echidna could give special Alterations that were more potent than normal Alterations and weren't subject to the limits of Sirens Alteration limit. However, Echidna Alterations are still present <b>even on human form </b>to level the cost.<br /> <br /> I would say that the &quot;Deep Ones&quot; should be kept with Echidna, because if Sirens were able to <i>naturally </i>get those Alterations, then it would be stepping on Leviathan the Tempest's toes. However, because Echidnal Alterations are unnatural by definition, it would be finer because then it wouldn't step on Leviathan as much as it would be if they were natural. I also sort of imagined that Abyssal Sirens would get Alterations based on animals in the Abyssopalegic Zone as noted in your next paragraph. Deep black squid, Angler fish, various other things that make most people &quot;nope&quot; out of the ocean.<br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> This is nice. To ask, Abyssal zone has no connection to the Abyssal Currents? The reason I ask is because Abyssals aren't an inherent splat (or at least, weren't meant to be inherent splats at all). Or are Sirens who Surface part of the Sirens who surface as absolute monsters? Kind of like how some Mages awake to being some of the Mad?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm sold on this by the way, <b>Depths </b>should be the X Splat. Is there any objections? :3</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So Echidnal Alterations are a more permanent blend of creature and human. Alright. Could it be possible that creatures that are obviously less humanoid than Sirens follow Echidna, such as the part-horse Kelpie or the Kappa?<br /> <br /> And with the Abyssal Zone, maybe Sirens who have seen the Abyssal Zone are more-inclined to take up the Abyssal Currents, like how the Zeka from <b><i>Promethean</i></b> find it easier to practice and harder to escape from Centimanus. They were taken too deep into The Deluge and were bathed in pure darkness. Their Surfacing wasn't because they were able to each the light above; their Surfacing was a blind search, swimming in every direction until they found an alcove with a pocket of air and took a Breath of the stagnant air. They became Sirens, but they cannot see the full picture. Their suffering within The Deluge drove them to madness and fury, allowing them to follow the Abyssal Currents with no trouble.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nice. Perhaps fittingly, this reminds me of Princess the Hopeful, but played differently. When Princesses Blossom, they are stuck in a really stressful situation where if they picked an option that wasn't &quot;the right thing&quot; they wouldn't have been able to forgive themselves otherwise. After which, usually when they fall asleep they recall bits of pieces of their previous incarnations/past lives, all the way back to the time of the Kingdoms in which were the ultimate pinnacle of good. When they blossom, they know that it was possible to make the Kingdom once, and therefore possible to create it once more.<br /> <br /> This story for Sirens is the backwards (or is it forwards?) version of that. It's where they're trapped by nearly drowning into despair, but despite all odds cling to and act for hope. When they Surface, they become Sirens and know the truth of the Deluge. It's the recorded past and forseeable future that everything and everyone will eventually sink to become. I take it that the &quot;She knows she needs to avert this future and how she will go about it&quot; was referring to joining Social Axises? Speaking of which, I forgot to mention that in the thread, Sirens who aren't a part of a social axis are known as &quot;Castaways&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me, this story of Surfacing actually makes this gameline a nice successor to Werewolf the Apocalypse in a sense. Instead of fighting against an opponent already present and a completely unavoidable apocalypse however, Sirens faces antagonists only when it threatens to overstep boundaries and that the apocalyptic scenario is both known of and avoidable if enough help is given to Sirens. </div> </div> </div>I completely forgot about Princesses and Blossoming. I think with Princesses and Sirens, Princesses are focused on nostalgia while Sirens are focused on change. Princesses have memories and want to fix everything by keeping things the same and bringing them back to the &quot;Golden Era&quot;. Sirens have visions and want to fix everything by preventing things from staying the same. <br /> <br /> And I didn't realize Sirens also mirror <i><b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse. </b></i>Perhaps the Sirens have a sort of temporal empathy where they can feel when someone's actions will lead to a disastrous outcome. It might be something rather small and comparatively trivial, like having visions of a couple attempting to mend their relationship, or it could be something dramatic and that affects a community, like a child's kidnapping. The world is somehow affected by these occurrences and by interrupting these events or preventing them from occurring, The Siren feels as if the water of The Deluge has been affected.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another side-note: The Deluge is a natural occurrence that will happen once humanity has completely overstepped its boundary. In some way, humanity has also contributed to The Deluge by falling into despair. At some moment in the future, humanity had accepted its fate of being swallowed by the seas. Scientists had given up, families were holding each other as they said goodbye. The hopeless began to dig graves to allow those who wished for death a proper burial. The Deluge grew in size, not just because nature was going to reclaim the world, but because humanity gave it their tears. Every moment of sorrow, every sob that was choked out gave The Deluge its strength to take back humanity. The waves grew larger and larger, wiping out coastlines and swallowing cities into its torrential maw. Every child taken let their tears fall as they lost their grip on their mother's hands. Every lover screamed out in pain as their other half was swept away from them. The last few of humanity climbed up mountaintops, unable to allow themselves the cold embrace of the sea. It was the end of humanity.<br /> <br /> And then, someone began to sing.<br /> <br /> It was a morose, hollow tune that came from the last survivors, a mournful dirge as a reminder of humanity's folly. But it was...beautiful, ethereal. For a moment, everything stopped. The wind that whipped against the waves stood still. The tide that raged against the remains of the mountains stilled, cowing to the Song. The last of humanity dried their tears as they listed to the Song, taking in every note that came from the singer's mouth. It was supposed to be their funeral song, the final thing they could hear before the waves took them, but it was strange. It was strange how powerful the voice was as it broke against the crashing tides. It was strange how calming the Song was despite the destruction that laid beneath it. It was strange how...uplifting it was. It was something that humanity had forgotten long ago. It was something that only those who were never exposed to the harshness of humanity could experience. It was hope. It was peace.<br /> <br /> It was the pure joy of life. <br /> <br /> And that is when the rest felt themselves compelled to sing. The remaining people, the tired, the weary, the hopeless, began to sing the Song in harmony. It was no longer a painful, ironic tune for the death of humanity. It was a Song that resonated within everyone. It was a reflective melody, an anthem that screamed out in solidarity. Humanity cried out a Song of hope out into the empty skies, letting every emotion escape from their heart. One by one, they felt themselves being lifted up into the air, reaching toward the last bit of sunlight that could pierce through the storm clouds. They let their voice call out into the sea as they took to the air, feeling themselves float through the wind. They were calling out to those who had been drowned, to those who were lost to the waters, wishing them to hear their call. They wished to share their Song to those who had been taken.<br /> <br /> And the drowned had heard them. <br /> <br /> One by one, the surface of The Deluge broke as humanity rose above the water. Those submerged for so long desperately gasped for a Breath of air, taking in the light that was cast down upon them and finally hearing the Song in full form. They looked upon themselves and realized that they were different. Though their core being was still human, they saw their changes in the light. Fins that stretched out from their arms, a strong carapace that wrapped around them like a suit of armor, a soft tail that propelled them through the waters. They weren't only humans forced to stay within their own boundaries, they were a gestalt. The refinement of civilization crossed with the beauty of the natural world. They were a new being formed from an old society and an even older wilderness. They were given a second chance, not as individuals who have done wrong, but as a species who must do right. No one must suffer from the crushing despair. No one must experience such a pain. No one must be taken by The Deluge.<br /> <br /> The individual finds themselves huddled down against the ground. What was it that played through their mind? An ocean of despair? An overwhelming force that dragged them down? Was it all just a hallucination? Was it a forewarning? The individual contemplates this as they head into the nearest restroom to wipe their brow. Maybe it is a warning. Maybe there is something that needs to be done. Maybe they are a second chance for humanity.<br /> <br /> As they wet their hands in the restroom sink, they see the scales that pepper their hands through the water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T15:45:53-08:00","id":785612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785526#post785526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. So Echidnal Alterations are a more permanent blend of creature and human. Alright. Could it be possible that creatures that are obviously less humanoid than Sirens follow Echidna, such as the part-horse Kelpie or the Kappa?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least that's what I have for ideas on them. And yes, it should be completely possible to be less humanoid, or even be completely incapable of being mistaken for human. As for Kelpies or Kappa, we so far have &quot;Vodianoi&quot; being the name for Echidna's children, her monstrous experiments in the attempt to make a race to survive the apocalypse. It's been suggested on the original forum that Echidna cannot procreate at all, but it's been agreed on that she she takes the DNA of man and fish, puts them into the blender of her body, spits them back out and sends them out to see how they'll do for survival. Or lets Sirens allied with her use them as they see fit. One or the other. Here's what I have on them by the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Malformations are just an idea I had for what Echidna's Alterations could be called, but I got borked before I could make anything else. I think though that if Echindal Alterations/Malformations are able to be taken by Sirens, then Vodianoi should be able to have some other special power that only they can access. Like the Cacophonies that Yads suggested earlier.We might have to wait until we get to writing up how Songs (Their version of Disciplines, Contracts, Gifts, etc) are first though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785526#post785526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And with the Abyssal Zone, maybe Sirens who have seen the Abyssal Zone are more-inclined to take up the Abyssal Currents, like how the Zeka from <b><i>Promethean</i></b> find it easier to practice and harder to escape from Centimanus. They were taken too deep into The Deluge and were bathed in pure darkness. Their Surfacing wasn't because they were able to each the light above; their Surfacing was a blind search, swimming in every direction until they found an alcove with a pocket of air and took a Breath of the stagnant air. They became Sirens, but they cannot see the full picture. Their suffering within The Deluge drove them to madness and fury, allowing them to follow the Abyssal Currents with no trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. :3<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785526#post785526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely forgot about Princesses and Blossoming. I think with Princesses and Sirens, Princesses are focused on nostalgia while Sirens are focused on change. Princesses have memories and want to fix everything by keeping things the same and bringing them back to the &quot;Golden Era&quot;. Sirens have visions and want to fix everything by preventing things from staying the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone whose helped abit PtH and is on the threads alot, I would say that Princesses are focused on change while Sirens are focused on inspiration. The reason I say this is why the heck would Princesses want to keep the World of Darkness like it is? Corruption lurks around every corner and if a Princess wants to recreate a bastion of Light like the Kingdoms were, then she's going to have to inevitably change things or require change in order to make that better world. After all, it's the Light's nature to create and renew, and the Dark's to stagnate and corrupt. Although the Court of Tears IS keen on keeping things the way they are (more in Alhambra, the one thing they'd want to change on Earth is to claim it in Alhambra's name).<br /> <br /> For Sirens, the reason I say protection is that, considering this being the World of Darkness, there's many people who are either all too happy to plunder nature's bounties and many more who simply don't care what happens. The most of the minority of people who do want to change stuff and protect wildlife and nature are easily brushed off by the said people plundering natures bounty, and those who can actually make a difference to protect things are quietly taken care of. In the past paragraph, I've been speaking in a strictly mortal sense. Sirens, unlike mortals, will considerably be able to rally mortals who do care and not be one of the people who can make a difference who gets shot down. They'll be able to inspire mortals who don't care to act up and make them see what'll happen if things continue the way they are (not in the &quot;look at the Deluge&quot; sense, it's completely possible to show it in a mundane sense).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785526#post785526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I didn't realize Sirens also mirror <i><b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse. </b></i>Perhaps the Sirens have a sort of temporal empathy where they can feel when someone's actions will lead to a disastrous outcome. It might be something rather small and comparatively trivial, like having visions of a couple attempting to mend their relationship, or it could be something dramatic and that affects a community, like a child's kidnapping. The world is somehow affected by these occurrences and by interrupting these events or preventing them from occurring, The Siren feels as if the water of The Deluge has been affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, there's a few pitfalls of Werewolf the Apocalypse that I don't want Siren the Drowning to fall into.<br /> To make this as clear as possible for anyone reading:<br /> <br /> <b>1: </b>I don't want any implications that Civilization and all of it's fruits (technology, religion, etc) are evil. This can go a few ways. One is the Technological side. Technology isn't inherently evil. If there's disasters, then it's better to clean up the mess, fix the problem on the equipment so it doesn't happen again. Another way is &quot;civilization in general&quot;, people thinking it's better to get back to nature and live in caves. If nothing else, the best thing I can put is that civilization IS NOT inherently evil and that civilization is as much of nature as nature is part of civilization and it doesn't matter if there will be a freak accident oil spill or a tornado that kills an entire city, <b>there will always be problems that simply cannot be fixed or will reappear no matter what and killing off one side doesn't solve the problems in the other.</b><br /> <br /> <b>2: </b>I don't want to force anyone playing this into one single role or into only one single way to play things, which in both this case and in WtA is Ecowarriorism. It's fine that people want to save the Earth and all, and that's cool. But if that's all that Sirens do, then it'll quickly kill off interest for people wanting to do some other role. The main point of this is that it should be possible to play almost any role the player wants to do as long as the main point of the splat is there. For example, Princesses are generally hopebringers or Werewolves are Spirit Police. It's fine if it's generally done, but if it's shoved down the throat of the players in a &quot;but thou must&quot; fashion (as in you can only ever be a hopebringer or a Spirit Cop) then it loses any allure to playing. For Sirens, I believe that their general role would be as &quot;Mediator&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if sounding bad or if getting anything wrong, I just wanted to point out those pitfalls so that they may be avoided. If it sounds like a rant, it's not meant to be, I'm just greatly fearful of this game falling into said pitfalls and wanting to state my desire of avoiding those pitfalls at all costs.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785526#post785526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *snip story of the Deluge*</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span>This would be a really great beginning story/paragraph to the corebook when we make one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yads, you can still contribute to the discussion if you want to. Don't worry about any bad english. Just do your best, it's all anyone can ask you to do. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T18:10:33-08:00","id":785660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785612#post785612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least that's what I have for ideas on them. And yes, it should be completely possible to be less humanoid, or even be completely incapable of being mistaken for human. As for Kelpies or Kappa, we so far have &quot;Vodianoi&quot; being the name for Echidna's children, her monstrous experiments in the attempt to make a race to survive the apocalypse. It's been suggested on the original forum that Echidna cannot procreate at all, but it's been agreed on that she she takes the DNA of man and fish, puts them into the blender of her body, spits them back out and sends them out to see how they'll do for survival. Or lets Sirens allied with her use them as they see fit. One or the other. Here's what I have on them by the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Malformations are just an idea I had for what Echidna's Alterations could be called, but I got borked before I could make anything else. I think though that if Echindal Alterations/Malformations are able to be taken by Sirens, then Vodianoi should be able to have some other special power that only they can access. Like the Cacophonies that Yads suggested earlier.We might have to wait until we get to writing up how Songs (Their version of Disciplines, Contracts, Gifts, etc) are first though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building a base for the Songs <i>(probably change this so that it doesn't conflict with the plot-important Song. Maybe Sirens can impart a section of the Song into the abilities they cast, effectively constructing a Verse?) </i>would be best. So far, these Verses are modular and feature a prelude that describes who/what is being targeted, what the Verse is supposed to do, and the quality that affects the Verse. So, a Verse that goes [Single Target] [Protect] [Water] causes a purification affect that washes someone or detoxifies them and a Verse that goes [Area] [Transformation] [Fear] causes the Siren to sing in an infrasonic level, causing those who are affected to suffer from hallucinations. Constructing these Verses off-hand means that the Siren is working A Capella, testing out the effects of creating a Verse without fully understanding what the outcome may be. When a Siren successfully constructs a Verse to her intent, she can memorize the effect of the Verse by codifying it and creating a Stanza. Like what you stated before, singing Area-Control-Rain is a Verse that creates a rainstorm; however, singing a memorized Stanza that is named &quot;Crying Sky Blues&quot; allows for a more refined version of a rainstorm. As an extrapolation, a different Siren may compose an Area-Control-Rain Verse that, instead of creating a rainstorm, is meant to ease the effects of natural weather like heavy sunlight, flooding, or fog. The Siren adds her own emotions into the Verse and creates the &quot;Aria of Tranquil Sky&quot; Stanza. A third Siren who knows the &quot;Area&quot;, &quot;Control&quot;, and &quot;Rain&quot; parts might even be able to learn the two different Stanzas from the other Sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking as someone whose helped abit PtH and is on the threads alot, I would say that Princesses are focused on change while Sirens are focused on inspiration. The reason I say this is why the heck would Princesses want to keep the World of Darkness like it is? Corruption lurks around every corner and if a Princess wants to recreate a bastion of Light like the Kingdoms were, then she's going to have to inevitably change things or require change in order to make that better world. After all, it's the Light's nature to create and renew, and the Dark's to stagnate and corrupt. Although the Court of Tears IS keen on keeping things the way they are (more in Alhambra, the one thing they'd want to change on Earth is to claim it in Alhambra's name).<br /> <br /> For Sirens, the reason I say protection is that, considering this being the World of Darkness, there's many people who are either all too happy to plunder nature's bounties and many more who simply don't care what happens. The most of the minority of people who do want to change stuff and protect wildlife and nature are easily brushed off by the said people plundering natures bounty, and those who can actually make a difference to protect things are quietly taken care of. In the past paragraph, I've been speaking in a strictly mortal sense. Sirens, unlike mortals, will considerably be able to rally mortals who do care and not be one of the people who can make a difference who gets shot down. They'll be able to inspire mortals who don't care to act up and make them see what'll happen if things continue the way they are (not in the &quot;look at the Deluge&quot; sense, it's completely possible to show it in a mundane sense).<br /> <br /> <b><i>[+]</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>2: </b>I don't want to force anyone playing this into one single role or into only one single way to play things, which in both this case and in WtA is Ecowarriorism. It's fine that people want to save the Earth and all, and that's cool. But if that's all that Sirens do, then it'll quickly kill off interest for people wanting to do some other role. The main point of this is that it should be possible to play almost any role the player wants to do as long as the main point of the splat is there. For example, Princesses are generally hopebringers or Werewolves are Spirit Police. It's fine if it's generally done, but if it's shoved down the throat of the players in a &quot;but thou must&quot; fashion (as in you can only ever be a hopebringer or a Spirit Cop) then it loses any allure to playing. For Sirens, I believe that their general role would be as &quot;Mediator&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Hmm...perhaps there is a way to capitalize on the &quot;Mediator&quot; idea and further incorporate the &quot;inspiration&quot; focus. They cannot live purely with humanity and they cannot live purely within the wild, so they have become accustomed to living a life in which they are frequently popping in and popping out. The Sirens seek out humans who have the potential to change the fate of the world and attempt to push them to make these changes without revealing why they need to. The Sirens also need to look after nature, which is slowly attempting to take back the Earth. There are beings of the primal Earth that hunger for the time to destroy humanity or to expand their reach against the civilized world. Thorny briers and kudzu-like vines overgrow cities, wildfires break out in areas that do not make sense, lakes and oceans pulsate as they swallow ships whole. <i><b>[In effect, think SCP-1100, which causes plants to explode near humans and forces domestic animals to go feral on their owners]</b></i> Sirens whisper to humanity to change their ways while taming the fury before it grows out of control. They may appear to humanity as Mysterious Waifs, subtly pointing individuals towards change. They may hide in the wild to calm the angered world, protecting others from feeding into nature's wrath. They may take to being iconic faces in society, inspiring others to keep from losing themselves to the drowning sensation of modern life. They may even just seek to make others happy, allowing them to partake in the Breath of life and keeping The Deluge from claiming their tears. <br /> <br /> Although the overall message still leans towards &quot;Environmentalism&quot;, it also has notes about &quot;Fighting against Complacency&quot;, &quot;Eliminating the Toxic Influences in Your Life&quot;, &quot;Preventing the Preventable&quot;, and &quot;Experiencing Life in All Its Splendor&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T19:43:11-08:00","id":785708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785660#post785660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building a base for the Songs <i>(probably change this so that it doesn't conflict with the plot-important Song. Maybe Sirens can impart a section of the Song into the abilities they cast, effectively constructing a Verse?) </i>would be best. So far, these Verses are modular and feature a prelude that describes who/what is being targeted, what the Verse is supposed to do, and the quality that affects the Verse. So, a Verse that goes [Single Target] [Protect] [Water] causes a purification affect that washes someone or detoxifies them and a Verse that goes [Area] [Transformation] [Fear] causes the Siren to sing in an infrasonic level, causing those who are affected to suffer from hallucinations. Constructing these Verses off-hand means that the Siren is working A Capella, testing out the effects of creating a Verse without fully understanding what the outcome may be. When a Siren successfully constructs a Verse to her intent, she can memorize the effect of the Verse by codifying it and creating a Stanza. Like what you stated before, singing Area-Control-Rain is a Verse that creates a rainstorm; however, singing a memorized Stanza that is named &quot;Crying Sky Blues&quot; allows for a more refined version of a rainstorm. As an extrapolation, a different Siren may compose an Area-Control-Rain Verse that, instead of creating a rainstorm, is meant to ease the effects of natural weather like heavy sunlight, flooding, or fog. The Siren adds her own emotions into the Verse and creates the &quot;Aria of Tranquil Sky&quot; Stanza. A third Siren who knows the &quot;Area&quot;, &quot;Control&quot;, and &quot;Rain&quot; parts might even be able to learn the two different Stanzas from the other Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now all we need is some magical language merit that most other Supernaturals have (High Speech, Royal Tongue, First Tongue) for bonuses and we're set. XD<br /> <br /> On a serious note, I do like how these are coming up. I should make a Doc for a Lexicon for Siren Terminology.<br /> <br /> I'm also mulling over the possibility of being able to put in multiple Conclusions to the Verses (Such as &quot;Area-Control-Weather-Water&quot; could create a rainstorm with &quot;Weather + Water&quot; being the Conclusions). Or perhaps that the Conclusion and the middle word could switch places (as it seems the middle word (Control, Transform, Invoke, etc) is telling what you're going to do with it). What do you think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785526#post785526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...perhaps there is a way to capitalize on the &quot;Mediator&quot; idea and further incorporate the &quot;inspiration&quot; focus. They cannot live purely with humanity and they cannot live purely within the wild, so they have become accustomed to living a life in which they are frequently popping in and popping out. The Sirens seek out humans who have the potential to change the fate of the world and attempt to push them to make these changes without revealing why they need to. The Sirens also need to look after nature, which is slowly attempting to take back the Earth. There are beings of the primal Earth that hunger for the time to destroy humanity or to expand their reach against the civilized world. Thorny briers and kudzu-like vines overgrow cities, wildfires break out in areas that do not make sense, lakes and oceans pulsate as they swallow ships whole. <i><b>[In effect, think SCP-1100, which causes plants to explode near humans and forces domestic animals to go feral on their owners]</b></i> Sirens whisper to humanity to change their ways while taming the fury before it grows out of control. They may appear to humanity as Mysterious Waifs, subtly pointing individuals towards change. They may hide in the wild to calm the angered world, protecting others from feeding into nature's wrath. They may take to being iconic faces in society, inspiring others to keep from losing themselves to the drowning sensation of modern life. They may even just seek to make others happy, allowing them to partake in the Breath of life and keeping The Deluge from claiming their tears.<br /> <br /> Although the overall message still leans towards &quot;Environmentalism&quot;, it also has notes about &quot;Fighting against Complacency&quot;, &quot;Eliminating the Toxic Influences in Your Life&quot;, &quot;Preventing the Preventable&quot;, and &quot;Experiencing Life in All Its Splendor&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silly me, I just realized how in the post I made I didn't change &quot;protector&quot; in the second paragraph to &quot;inspirator&quot; or something. Anyways, your ideas basically cover it. Thank you so much, I'm sorry if overrelying or sounding bad on the post of pitfalls, I'm not angry, just not wanting the same pitfalls to happen.<br /> <br /> Perhaps just one last question when it comes to X Splat. You mentioned Depth being used instead of Ocean. I do like the idea, but just to be really clear, are they intended to replace Oceans or are they a way to explain how a Siren Surfaces with the outlook she has?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T20:21:16-08:00","id":785714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785708#post785708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now all we need is some magical language merit that most other Supernaturals have (High Speech, Royal Tongue, First Tongue) for bonuses and we're set. XD<br /> <br /> On a serious note, I do like how these are coming up. I should make a Doc for a Lexicon for Siren Terminology.<br /> <br /> I'm also mulling over the possibility of being able to put in multiple Conclusions to the Verses (Such as &quot;Area-Control-Weather-Water&quot; could create a rainstorm with &quot;Weather + Water&quot; being the Conclusions). Or perhaps that the Conclusion and the middle word could switch places (as it seems the middle word (Control, Transform, Invoke, etc) is telling what you're going to do with it). What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Conclusion, it could work as if you are attempting to mash two words together to create a very specific word. Sort of like German. Like, the word &quot;Sky&quot; and the word &quot;Water&quot; exist as Conclusions by themselves, but combining them allows you to specify that you are attempting to invoke &quot;Sky-Water&quot; AKA rain. Or combining &quot;Light&quot; and &quot;Pain&quot; to make &quot;Light-Pain&quot; which could be lightning or fire. By combining words, it allows the Siren to achieve a more specific goal but it may cause it to backfire. &quot;Stone-Water&quot; may refer to sand or it could refer to ice. &quot;Pain-Water&quot; could mean blood or it could mean poison. And combining words that are fundamentally different, like trying to sing &quot;Sky-Stone&quot; for a meteorite or comet, may cause a Dissonance in the Verse and cause some effect.<br /> <br /> I also don't understand what you mean when you ask about switching the middle and Conclusion. Do you mean grammatically so it goes [Area of Effect] [Quality of Verse] [Effect of Verse]?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Silly me, I just realized how in the post I made I didn't change &quot;protector&quot; in the second paragraph to &quot;inspirator&quot; or something. Anyways, your ideas basically cover it. Thank you so much, I'm sorry if overrelying or sounding bad on the post of pitfalls, I'm not angry, just not wanting the same pitfalls to happen. </div> </div> </div>No worries. If there's a point of contention, that just means the original post had something that was unclear or seemed to lean towards some area. Calling attention helps create discussion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps just one last question when it comes to X Splat. You mentioned Depth being used instead of Ocean. I do like the idea, but just to be really clear, are they intended to replace Oceans or are they a way to explain how a Siren Surfaces with the outlook she has? </div> </div> </div>I think the Depths are to replace Ocean. Depth is where a Siren started off before she managed to Surface; it gives her a sense of what is around her and where she comes from. She may be close to the Surface and was exposed to what remains of the world after The Deluge. She may come incredibly far within The Deluge and struggles with the pressure and darkness that hold her down. Depth would be more of a &quot;How was your childhood?&quot; Currents would be more of the outlook, sort of like &quot;What made everything change?&quot;. The Depth is where the Siren was in The Deluge and The Current is how she managed to Surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T20:48:40-08:00","id":785726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785714#post785714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For the Conclusion, it could work as if you are attempting to mash two words together to create a very specific word. Sort of like German. Like, the word &quot;Sky&quot; and the word &quot;Water&quot; exist as Conclusions by themselves, but combining them allows you to specify that you are attempting to invoke &quot;Sky-Water&quot; AKA rain. Or combining &quot;Light&quot; and &quot;Pain&quot; to make &quot;Light-Pain&quot; which could be lightning or fire. By combining words, it allows the Siren to achieve a more specific goal but it may cause it to backfire. &quot;Stone-Water&quot; may refer to sand or it could refer to ice. &quot;Pain-Water&quot; could mean blood or it could mean poison. And combining words that are fundamentally different, like trying to sing &quot;Sky-Stone&quot; for a meteorite or comet, may cause a Dissonance in the Verse and cause some effect.<br /> <br /> I also don't understand what you mean when you ask about switching the middle and Conclusion. Do you mean grammatically so it goes [Area of Effect] [Quality of Verse] [Effect of Verse]?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And in my original post in naming the Song's different sections, I mentioned that<br /> Introduction - First Word used that refers to what it's affecting (Single/Multi target and Area of Effect)<br /> Verse/Opus (the word I used for naming the Second Word rather than how you used it. I'll rename it to Opus) - Second Word involving what the Siren wants to do (Transform, Invoke, Control, etcetc)<br /> Conclusion - The Third Word that is what the Siren wants to effect (Ice, Water, Fear, Sky, etc)<br /> <br /> When I spoke of &quot;switching them around', I was thinking that it might be better to have Opus and Conclusion switch definition with each other. Opus would hold what the Siren wanted to affect (Sky, Water, Fear etc) and Conclusion would have what the Siren wanted to do with it (Control, Invoke etc). Just purely for the sake of &quot;Conclusion&quot; being a case of &quot;what it says on the tin can&quot;, in this case being &quot;to what <b>end </b>the Siren wants the <i>opus subject </i>to do. So it would be like &quot;Area-Rain-Invoke&quot; to bring about a rainfall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785714#post785714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Depths are to replace Ocean. Depth is where a Siren started off before she managed to Surface; it gives her a sense of what is around her and where she comes from. She may be close to the Surface and was exposed to what remains of the world after The Deluge. She may come incredibly far within The Deluge and struggles with the pressure and darkness that hold her down. Depth would be more of a &quot;How was your childhood?&quot; Currents would be more of the outlook, sort of like &quot;What made everything change?&quot;. The Depth is where the Siren was in The Deluge and The Current is how she managed to Surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I'm sorry for being that person who clings to ideas until there's no use in holding to them, but I have some reasons/arguments for why Oceans should be kept.<br /> <br /> For one, the Deluge is a possible bad end future and it literally and figuratively encompasses all Oceans equally. In the perspective of the Deluge, it could refer to where the Siren comes to when she surfaces (Such as a Polaria Siren surfacing where the air is cold and icebergs float about with the corpses of those who cried out the Song are still frozen atop of them) and could be explained accordingly. For another, while the Depths idea does make the pool for Alterations greater for each Depth, it takes out any possibility of General Alterations existing. On the other hand, Oceans would have a lesser pool for Alterations, but it would be greater emphasized how they're belonging only to that ocean. Finally, the only reasoning I have left is that Oceans could be tied to the Mythology of the Merfolk of the Ocean it's based on, kind of like how Vampire Clans are based on Vampire Genres/famous tellings of Vampires or how they acted in stories.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry for bringing these thoughts up. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":".  Little Edit about Songs 12-14-2015, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:41:26-08:00","id":785747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785726#post785726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. And in my original post, I mentioned that<br /> Introduction - First Word used that refers to what it's affecting (Single/Multi target and Area of Effect)<br /> Verse/Opus (the word I used for naming the Second Word rather than how you used it. I'll rename it to Opus) - Second Word involving what the Siren wants to do (Transform, Invoke, Control, etcetc)<br /> Conclusion - The Third Word that is what the Siren wants to effect (Ice, Water, Fear, Sky, etc)<br /> <br /> When I spoke of &quot;switching them around', I was thinking that it might be better to have Opus and Conclusion switch definition with each other. Opus would hold what the Siren wanted to affect (Sky, Water, Fear etc) and Conclusion would have what the Siren wanted to do with it (Control, Invoke etc). Just purely for the sake of &quot;Conclusion&quot; being a case of &quot;what it says on the tin can&quot;, in this case being &quot;to what <b>end </b>the Siren wants the <i>opus subject </i>to do. So it would be like &quot;Area-Rain-Invoke&quot; to bring about a rainfall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. That would make sense. And it adds more emphasis on the Opus. I figure that the Introduction would consist of a few words [Single, Multi, Area, Touch, etc.] and that the Conclusion would have at least a set. The Opus words are probably going to have the greatest variety.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. I'm sorry for being that person who clings to ideas until there's no use in holding to them, but I have some reasons/arguments for why Oceans should be kept.<br /> <br /> For one, the Deluge is a possible bad end future and it literally and figuratively encompasses all Oceans equally. In the perspective of the Deluge, it could refer to where the Siren comes to when she surfaces (Such as a Polaria Siren surfacing where the air is cold and icebergs float about with the corpses of those who cried out the Song are still frozen atop of them) and could be explained accordingly. For another, while the Depths idea does make the pool for Alterations greater for each Depth, it takes out any possibility of General Alterations existing. On the other hand, Oceans would have a lesser pool for Alterations, but it would be greater emphasized how they're belonging only to that ocean. Finally, the only reasoning I have left is that Oceans could be tied to the Mythology of the Merfolk of the Ocean it's based on, kind of like how Vampire Clans are based on Vampire Genres/famous tellings of Vampires or how they acted in stories.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry for bringing these thoughts up. D: </div> </div> </div>I understand. My reasons for disagreeing with the original Oceans was based on semantics. For the most part, the Axises for the other Splats aren't as specific as &quot;This person comes from the Indian Ocean&quot; and are more &quot;This person is based on this version of the myth but it spans pretty far&quot;. Depths could be moved into the Z-axis, like how <b><i>Mage</i></b> as the Order, the Path, and the Legacy. <br /> <br /> Of the original Oceans, I prefer Polaria and Fresh over Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian. Maybe instead of Oceans, they are more based on the Quality of the Water that the Sirens come from. <b>Polaria</b> refers to the arctic waters and gives an overall Death-motif while <b>Fresh</b> refers to any source of freshwater and gives an overall Birth-motif. Maybe there's an Ocean that's dedicated to warm waters called <b>Tropicana</b>. Rather than being cold and pained or refreshing and lively, Sirens from Tropicana are filled with the joy of life and want to partake in it with others. It could overtake the Pacific Ocean splat. The Indian Ocean, being that it's themed towards preservation, could be something related to flood plains, marshes, or swamps where nature and humanity exist without disturbing one another. That could be named something like Arcadia<b>, </b>but not Arcadia because it has been used. <b>Gardenia</b>, as a reference to the Garden of Eden being a place that is supposed to be pure and paradise-like? And the Atlantic Ocean, which is more volatile and conflict-based, might not work with the idea of Mediation that is currently considered for Sirens. Perhaps they are the Sirens that would choose to follow the Abyssal Currents and come from an ocean of <b>Discordia</b>. Maybe a Siren that are based off of foggy or misty oceans; their thing is that they feel they should just come and go, only coming in to push things into place before allowing things to take their course. They could be <b>Vapor</b>. Sorry. Running out of thematic words that fit. Perhaps, instead of Oceans, they could be <b>Waters</b>.<br /> <br /> It could work into how the Sirens enjoy their water and can regain Breath or transform into their Aquatic form. Fresh Sirens need pure or at least drinkable water, preferably from a river but can make do with a fountain in the middle of a park. Polaria Sirens need cold water or even snow or ice. Tropicana Sirens need hot water or water that is exposed to sunlight. Gardenia Sirens need stagnant water or water that contains dirt or soil. Vapor Sirens need aerated water like mist or steam or even rainfall. Discordia Sirens need tainted water, touched by blood or oil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T22:44:10-08:00","id":785783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785747#post785747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand. My reasons for disagreeing with the original Oceans was based on semantics. For the most part, the Axises for the other Splats aren't as specific as &quot;This person comes from the Indian Ocean&quot; and are more &quot;This person is based on this version of the myth but it spans pretty far&quot;. Depths could be moved into the Z-axis, like how <b><i>Mage</i></b> as the Order, the Path, and the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Of the original Oceans, I prefer Polaria and Fresh over Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian. Maybe instead of Oceans, they are more based on the Quality of the Water that the Sirens come from. <b>Polaria</b> refers to the arctic waters and gives an overall Death-motif while <b>Fresh</b> refers to any source of freshwater and gives an overall Birth-motif. Maybe there's an Ocean that's dedicated to warm waters called <b>Tropicana</b>. Rather than being cold and pained or refreshing and lively, Sirens from Tropicana are filled with the joy of life and want to partake in it with others. It could overtake the Pacific Ocean splat. The Indian Ocean, being that it's themed towards preservation, could be something related to flood plains, marshes, or swamps where nature and humanity exist without disturbing one another. That could be named something like Arcadia<b>, </b>but not Arcadia because it has been used. <b>Gardenia</b>, as a reference to the Garden of Eden being a place that is supposed to be pure and paradise-like? And the Atlantic Ocean, which is more volatile and conflict-based, might not work with the idea of Mediation that is currently considered for Sirens. Perhaps they are the Sirens that would choose to follow the Abyssal Currents and come from an ocean of <b>Discordia</b>. Maybe a Siren that are based off of foggy or misty oceans; their thing is that they feel they should just come and go, only coming in to push things into place before allowing things to take their course. They could be <b>Vapor</b>. Sorry. Running out of thematic words that fit. Perhaps, instead of Oceans, they could be <b>Waters</b>.<br /> <br /> It could work into how the Sirens enjoy their water and can regain Breath or transform into their Aquatic form. Fresh Sirens need pure or at least drinkable water, preferably from a river but can make do with a fountain in the middle of a park. Polaria Sirens need cold water or even snow or ice. Tropicana Sirens need hot water or water that is exposed to sunlight. Gardenia Sirens need stagnant water or water that contains dirt or soil. Vapor Sirens need aerated water like mist or steam or even rainfall. Discordia Sirens need tainted water, touched by blood or oil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. This is fitting. I think this change is fine, thank you for listening. As for conflict, unpredictability is definitely a part of the Ocean. One day it may look serene and calm, and the next it's threatening to crash your boat onto the rocks, but I do agree that it doesn't fit well with the Mediator theme. And the way to regain breath sounds good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which now brings to another thought. In almost every myth Sirens have been known to drown people or be generically yandereish. The idea is, do Siren's have their own kind of &quot;Frenzy&quot; or &quot;Death Rage&quot;? Given the stories on Sirens, I imagine that it's triggered by whatever the Siren cares for the most (like a light crush becoming a deranged obsession in this mode) to which she goes into a rage if anything she doesn't like happens to it. Perhaps fitting the mediation theme, it's why they can't get too close to something. Because they'll eventually end up hurting it or themselves. I can't help but feel like it really fits &quot;the Little Mermaid&quot; schtick.<br /> <br /> And also, I recalled something else. Remember the one part in this thread where we talked about how water beings have became air beings to see if the &quot;bird folk&quot; trope could be played with Siren as well? Well, I've just recalled that Hans Christian Andersen wrote an alternate ending to the Little Mermaid. When she becomes sea foam, instead of cessitation of existence for her, she becomes a &quot;daughter of the air&quot; from which her selflessness and striving for an immortal soul has given her a chance to get one if she does 300 years worth of good deeds. It might be something? Perhaps it's a form of Siren ascendancy in which they truly become part of the Song?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T23:50:29-08:00","id":785800,"title":"","content":"Just a note:<br /> <br /> One of the Greek words for soul, pneuma, <i>more directly</i> translates to &quot;breath&quot;.<br /> <br /> Drink dem delicious souls, Sirens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T23:58:50-08:00","id":785802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785783#post785783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. This is fitting. I think this change is fine, thank you for listening. As for conflict, unpredictability is definitely a part of the Ocean. One day it may look serene and calm, and the next it's threatening to crash your boat onto the rocks, but I do agree that it doesn't fit well with the Mediator theme. And the way to regain breath sounds good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, maybe it revolves around deliberately trying to cause trouble in order to mediate. Being a Gadfly, something that is unceasingly persistent in pestering and bringing things up until it gets resolved. These Sirens might be someone who would push for someone to confront something that they are trying to repress or they might be digging up information that needs to be known. They aren't just a Mediator; they are an Activist that wants change and wants it now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which now brings to another thought. In almost every myth Sirens have been known to drown people or be generically yandereish. The idea is, do Siren's have their own kind of &quot;Frenzy&quot; or &quot;Death Rage&quot;? Given the stories on Sirens, I imagine that it's triggered by whatever the Siren cares for the most (like a light crush becoming a deranged obsession in this mode) to which she goes into a rage if anything she doesn't like happens to it. Perhaps fitting the mediation theme, it's why they can't get too close to something. Because they'll eventually end up hurting it or themselves. I can't help but feel like it really fits &quot;the Little Mermaid&quot; schtick. </div> </div> </div>In some folk tales, a river spirit may become attached to a person and become their devoted lover. Once their lover passes, they become overcome with loss and commit suicide. I think that Sirens, by nature, want to be with others. They long to share experiences with others and listen to whatever tales they come by. However, this eventually grows into an obsession. Their experiences with another is like the sweetest taste of life-water the Siren can ever dream of. It is like the first Breath she took when she Surfaced. It is pure joy and elation. And it is the only thing that keeps her mind off of The Deluge. The waters are always dragging her down, no matter what she does or where she goes. She needs those fleeting moments with those others. It's like a struggle to pull oneself onto land as the waves attempt to swallow one whole. Eventually, this leads to a situation where the Siren feels that &quot;If she can't have you, no one will&quot;. She reaches for the one that gave her such elation. And she holds their head under water until the bubbles stop. <br /> <br /> It isn't just love. It's anyone who listens to the Siren's call and allows her into their life. It's a madness that plagues them and warns them not to become attached to humanity. <br /> <br /> If anything, I feel that the Siren's Frenzy-equivalent ties into their experience being alone in The Deluge and the fear of being alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And also, I recalled something else. Remember the one part in this thread where we talked about how water beings have became air beings to see if the &quot;bird folk&quot; trope could be played with Siren as well? Well, I've just recalled that Hans Christian Andersen wrote an alternate ending to the Little Mermaid. When she becomes sea foam, instead of cessitation of existence for her, she becomes a &quot;daughter of the air&quot; from which her selflessness and striving for an immortal soul has given her a chance to get one if she does 300 years worth of good deeds. It might be something? Perhaps it's a form of Siren ascendancy in which they truly become part of the Song? </div> </div> </div>I touched on it a little bit when I wrote the snippet about the Deluge and the Song. I implied that the Song is something that is uplifting and that the remaining humans that were graced by the Song were transformed into the winged Sirens because they were able to hear the Song firsthand. Sirens that need to Surface are only exposed to the Song secondhand and through the medium of water, which is why they are not winged. The Verses that Sirens sing are actually snippets of the Song that Sirens try to string together. There are legends about Sirens being able to sing the Song fully and seeing visions of The Deluge from the sky. There may be a process where Sirens that know every Introduction, Opus, and Conclusion meditate within The Deluge before Resurfacing and ascending.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T02:12:28-08:00","id":785836,"title":"","content":"I'm Back!<br /> <br /> \u200bLots to catch up, let's see:<br /> <br /> As for the X-splat.<br /> I like the Depths concept, although I understand why Ocenas may be abit more fitting, The Depth concept, as I understand, is connected directly with how a Siren experiences de Deluge, how they understand and see the Deluge for the first time, and how the Song reaches them. They realize the Deluge as a Future and that is a Significant aspect of how they will deal with it. My suggestion would be to make Depth the main X-Splat and Ocean become a Z-Splat, like Changeling Kiths, they refer less to how you understand it bou more ho you experimente it, how your senses are connected to the deluge in a more physical way, less than the subjective aspect of the Depths. So, firts two Cents: Depths (X -Splat) How they understand it. Ocean (Z-Splat) where and how they experience it.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;Songs?&quot;<br /> Sorry, didn't catch the new name of their powers, but loved how the idea is being worked. Yay! I like the More-Than-One-Verse Idea, just think we need rules to not let the verses become too broad, like, someones buys Rain + Lightining to create a Lightining Storm while someone Else buys Lighning Storm already and does the same effect with less exp. EDIT: Oh, wait, Just realized that someone that has more than one verse has a far broader action pallete while the guy who has only Lighning Storm with be attatched to playing only a few set. Nevermind this paragraph. Also, wanted to ask, is possible to create an Symphony by playing alongside other Sirens or a Maelstrom when you olay against them? I mean, the clash of two song should produce a terrifiying effect.<br /> <br /> Pneuma as the Fuel Stat<br /> hmmmmmm.... it fits. I like.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sirens &quot;Ascencion&quot;<br /> It sounds like that would be they ultimate experience on the Deluge, Seeing it from above, relizing not everything is lost (so far I imagine that maybe something still lives and is just adrift. But: thats an endgame thing? It's the callling of the Sing that lifts them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T08:51:49-08:00","id":786006,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785800#post785800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Greek words for soul, pneuma, <i>more directly</i> translates to &quot;breath&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I know of this. For some stupid reason I thought that Djinn the Binding had that for a fuel stat, but after checking and seeing it doesn't, let's change it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785802#post785802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In some folk tales, a river spirit may become attached to a person and become their devoted lover. Once their lover passes, they become overcome with loss and commit suicide. I think that Sirens, by nature, want to be with others. They long to share experiences with others and listen to whatever tales they come by. However, this eventually grows into an obsession. Their experiences with another is like the sweetest taste of life-water the Siren can ever dream of. It is like the first Breath she took when she Surfaced. It is pure joy and elation. And it is the only thing that keeps her mind off of The Deluge. The waters are always dragging her down, no matter what she does or where she goes. She needs those fleeting moments with those others. It's like a struggle to pull oneself onto land as the waves attempt to swallow one whole. Eventually, this leads to a situation where the Siren feels that &quot;If she can't have you, no one will&quot;. She reaches for the one that gave her such elation. And she holds their head under water until the bubbles stop.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It isn't just love. It's anyone who listens to the Siren's call and allows her into their life. It's a madness that plagues them and warns them not to become attached to humanity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If anything, I feel that the Siren's Frenzy-equivalent ties into their experience being alone in The Deluge and the fear of being alone.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is very fitting. :3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785802#post785802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I touched on it a little bit when I wrote the snippet about the Deluge and the Song. I implied that the Song is something that is uplifting and that the remaining humans that were graced by the Song were transformed into the winged Sirens because they were able to hear the Song firsthand. Sirens that need to Surface are only exposed to the Song secondhand and through the medium of water, which is why they are not winged. The Verses that Sirens sing are actually snippets of the Song that Sirens try to string together. There are legends about Sirens being able to sing the Song fully and seeing visions of The Deluge from the sky. There may be a process where Sirens that know every Introduction, Opus, and Conclusion meditate within The Deluge before Resurfacing and ascending.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I see. I take it that a requirement for this is also only attainable from Akasha 6 and up? :3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And also some other ideas and questions. Are there some added benefits to being a Siren other than &quot;can live and breathe underwater&quot;? I was thinking that longevity (even to the point of immortality if they manage to ascend) would be a factor for them. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785836#post785836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the X-splat. I like the Depths concept, although I understand why Ocenas may be abit more fitting, The Depth concept, as I understand, is connected directly with how a Siren experiences de Deluge, how they understand and see the Deluge for the first time, and how the Song reaches them. They realize the Deluge as a Future and that is a Significant aspect of how they will deal with it. My suggestion would be to make Depth the main X-Splat and Ocean become a Z-Splat, like Changeling Kiths, they refer less to how you understand it bou more ho you experimente it, how your senses are connected to the deluge in a more physical way, less than the subjective aspect of the Depths. So, firts two Cents: Depths (X -Splat) How they understand it. Ocean (Z-Splat) where and how they experience it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a counterpoint, I would like to suggest that regardless, a Siren is going to drown first before she surfaces. The one reason against Depth that I have is that a drowning person wouldn't care about how deep they are, the only thing that matters for the person is getting up to the surface as fast as possible, and after that they'd care about where they've ended up after they surfaced. You can't choose where you surface when coming back up. <br /> <br /> A reason though that Depth would fit as a Z-Splat after a Siren surfaces is that a Siren could take time to see and examine how life is like at each depth, viewing what life and ecosystem lives at the Depth and choosing to make it a part of her life, fitting for Z-Splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785836#post785836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the &quot;Songs?&quot;<br /> Sorry, didn't catch the new name of their powers, but loved how the idea is being worked. Yay! I like the More-Than-One-Verse Idea, just think we need rules to not let the verses become too broad, like, someones buys Rain + Lightining to create a Lightining Storm while someone Else buys Lighning Storm already and does the same effect with less exp. EDIT: Oh, wait, Just realized that someone that has more than one verse has a far broader action pallete while the guy who has only Lighning Storm with be attatched to playing only a few set. Nevermind this paragraph. Also, wanted to ask, is possible to create an Symphony by playing alongside other Sirens or a Maelstrom when you olay against them? I mean, the clash of two song should produce a terrifiying effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new name is &quot;Verses&quot;, them codified (like Mage Rotes) is &quot;Stanzas&quot;. I think a suggestion that could fix this (more than one verse idea) is to make the ability to have multiple Opuses (Like having &quot;Weather&quot; and &quot;Water&quot; instead of flatly &quot;Rain&quot; to create Rain) added to a Verse, but of course these can be limited (Akasha limit?). <br /> <br /> Even though I didn't ignore the paragraph before the Edit, technically speaking wouldn't they still need to know the words in order to make the song in the first place? Because then everyone would be using Stanzas instead of Verses without knowing the power behind the words or knowing what gives them power (think of it as a Mage using a Rote to an Arcana he doesn't know of, it doesn't make much sense). Although I do love the idea that personal definition can change the meaning of a Verse, like the example where two Sirens put together &quot;Area-Rain-Invoke&quot; separately, one puts her emotions into making a song that creates rain whereas the other creates one that clears it up. As for Sirens working together on a Verse, I was imagining that it could be called a &quot;Concert&quot; and ones where Sirens are invoking powers against each other are known as &quot;Concerto Grosso&quot; (Musical term for when two Concerts are playing against each other). <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=785836#post785836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sirens &quot;Ascencion&quot;<br /> It sounds like that would be they ultimate experience on the Deluge, Seeing it from above, relizing not everything is lost (so far I imagine that maybe something still lives and is just adrift. But: thats an endgame thing? It's the callling of the Sing that lifts them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would most likely be endgame stuff indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:31:25-08:00","id":786035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=786006#post786006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The new name is &quot;Verses&quot;, them codified (like Mage Rotes) is &quot;Stanzas&quot;. I think a suggestion that could fix this (more than one verse idea) is to make the ability to have multiple Opuses (Like having &quot;Weather&quot; and &quot;Water&quot; instead of flatly &quot;Rain&quot; to create Rain) added to a Verse, but of course these can be limited (Akasha limit?).<br /> <br /> Even though I didn't ignore the paragraph before the Edit, technically speaking wouldn't they still need to know the words in order to make the song in the first place? Because then everyone would be using Stanzas instead of Verses without knowing the power behind the words or knowing what gives them power (think of it as a Mage using a Rote to an Arcana he doesn't know of, it doesn't make much sense). Although I do love the idea that personal definition can change the meaning of a Verse, like the example where two Sirens put together &quot;Area-Rain-Invoke&quot; separately, one puts her emotions into making a song that creates rain whereas the other creates one that clears it up. As for Sirens working together on a Verse, I was imagining that it could be called a &quot;Concert&quot; and ones where Sirens are invoking powers against each other are known as &quot;Concerto Grosso&quot; (Musical term for when two Concerts are playing against each other).<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> I see. For example: at akasha 1 your connection to the Song is so thin that you can add only one Opus to a Verse (Touch + Water + Control), at akasha 3 you can add 2 Opus to a verse (Area + Water + Weather + Invoke) and so on? If that's it I believe it is balanced enough and thus I like. Was afraid of PCs going all &quot;5 Opus in a verse&quot; and bringing down whole Veneza mid game.<br /> <br /> Personal definition is a very good addition, I just feel that maybe is too subjective to a Mechanical part of the game, and need to be further clarified. But it's nice, the Song touches Sirens in a diferente way.<br /> <br /> I suppose Concerts work like Hunter's Tactics, If everyone knows the same Verses they add bonuses to a certain Roll regarding the taks. As for Concerto Grosse I believe that it should cause some kind of disaster or disgrace. The Song wasn't made for nonsense conflicts, so it would retaliate, Nothing at Fukushima level, of course, but something big enough to stop the conflict.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T14:28:53-08:00","id":786249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=786035#post786035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. For example: at akasha 1 your connection to the Song is so thin that you can add only one Opus to a Verse (Touch + Water + Control), at akasha 3 you can add 2 Opus to a verse (Area + Water + Weather + Invoke) and so on? If that's it I believe it is balanced enough and thus I like. Was afraid of PCs going all &quot;5 Opus in a verse&quot; and bringing down whole Veneza mid game.<br /> <br /> Personal definition is a very good addition, I just feel that maybe is too subjective to a Mechanical part of the game, and need to be further clarified. But it's nice, the Song touches Sirens in a diferente way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume that when creating Opuses, there is going to be a glossary of possible interpretations and a list of denied interpretations. Like, 'Light&quot; may refer to sunlight, fire, or electricity but cannot refer to stars <i>(they are too far away to be called upon using &quot;Light&quot;), </i>nuclear energy <i>(considering that radiation has tainted the Pacific Ocean as well as scarring multiple tracts of land), </i>and quantity <i>(as in lightening a load)</i>. Combining &quot;Light&quot; with &quot;Sky&quot; can create sudden sunlight, call down a firestorm or lightning, or send an orb of light upwards to act as a beacon. It also depends on other factors like the Introduction or Conclusion, so [Area][Light-Sky][Create] summons a beacon while [Target][Light-Sky][Transform] may cause the target to reveal their true form when they are exposed to sunlight. The most basic Verse allows a Siren to impart intent while a Verse with extra Opuses allows the Siren to establish specific conditions. Just [Target][Light][Transform] is vague enough that the magic of the Verse may interpret &quot;Light&quot; as fire, which is significantly harder to find unless the Siren brings a can of kerosene and a match.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose Concerts work like Hunter's Tactics, If everyone knows the same Verses they add bonuses to a certain Roll regarding the taks. As for Concerto Grosse I believe that it should cause some kind of disaster or disgrace. The Song wasn't made for nonsense conflicts, so it would retaliate, Nothing at Fukushima level, of course, but something big enough to stop the conflict. </div> </div> </div>That sounds both dangerous and awesome at the same time. Perhaps if a Concerto Grosso isn't resolved within a certain amount of time, the Song lashes out, causing the raw energy of the Opuses used to be released. Maybe the Bloop that occurs every now and then in the ocean is actually the resolution of an age-old grudge match between two ancient Shoals of Sirens trying to out-do the other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=786006#post786006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. I take it that a requirement for this is also only attainable from Akasha 6 and up? :3<br /> <br /> And also some other ideas and questions. Are there some added benefits to being a Siren other than &quot;can live and breathe underwater&quot;? I was thinking that longevity (even to the point of immortality if they manage to ascend) would be a factor for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sirens are incredibly healthy creatures; there are even legends of hunters searching for mermaids just so they can consume their flesh and gain immortality. The truth is that, while Sirens can live significantly longer than humans, it isn't necessarily immortality. The longest time that any Siren has been ever able to live is close to 300 years. Most Sirens never even come close to that age before they are hunted down or die from complications. Of course, that's not to say that Sirens are weak creatures.<br /> <br /> While Sirens do not have a regenerative power outside of their Verses, they are notoriously difficult to pin down. As long as a Siren still has Pneuma <i>(Breath)</i>, she will not suffer from her pain. If her rightmost Health box is marked with bashing damage while she still has at least one point of Pneuma, she does not need to roll Stamina to remain conscious; the breath of life within her, the will to fight and survive The Deluge, allows her to push through her pain. If her rightmost Health box is marked with lethal Damage while she still has at least three points of Pneuma, she does not take an additional point of damage each minute; the pain of bleeding out cannot compare to the suffering felt within The Deluge. However, once she drops down to no Pneuma or two Pneuma respectively, reality ensues and she must make a Stamina roll or receive a point of Damage each minute until she regains Pneuma or is exposed to her Waters <i>(still pushing for Oceans to be called Waters)</i>. <br /> <br /> Because Sirens have a connection to The Deluge, they have the ability to Trace events back to the source, akin to following a river to its source. In their minds, visions of rushing water flows through like a movie reel rewound. The Siren can see the moment in which a lonely child loses hope in finding a friend. The Siren can see the moment in which a murder victim is taken away by the killer. It is a vivid scene that plays in her mind, telling the secrets that have been hidden, forgotten, or untold. In game, a Siren may spend a point of Pneuma to trace through an object or person's experiences, similar to the Psychometry Merit. Unlike the Merit, a Siren asks a question before she Traces her object or person and attempts to find experiences that would answer her question. <i>For example, a Siren wants to trace the events before an arson occurred. Her question is &quot;Who was the person that started the fire?&quot; She spends a point of Pneuma and begins to see visions throughout time. As she's passing through, she sees several people in the area before and during the fire, including a man leaving the house before the fire started and a woman throwing garbage over the house's fence moments before smoke begins to appear. The vision stops. She doesn't necessarily know the exact person that committed the arson, but she has two possible suspects. She may recall the vision if she needs to, but she cannot refine it until she finds the people in the vision and attempts to Trace them. She may also attempt to Trace the scene of the arson again to get a different question answered, such as &quot;How long did the fire burn?&quot; or &quot;Who was in the house before it burned?&quot; Her Traces need to be specific to the object or person she is Tracing.</i><br /> <br /> Sirens are also capable of calling to another Siren, akin to the way that whales call out to other whales. It isn't necessarily a conscious act, however; the Song that resonates within each Siren continues to sing, even if a Siren is not singing a Verse. Depending on a Siren's Akasha, the Siren is able to feel the presence of the Song within others. It may be another Siren in the city. It may be a Banshee, howling in pain. The Siren may also be able to hear the lack of Song within others, finding people who are Breathless. The Siren may also increase how far her Song travels by singing a Verse or by simply spending a point of Pneuma to release a quick wave of the Song, like a flare that can only be heard by the Sirens.<br /> <br /> Sirens do have things that work against them, however. Because a Siren is a product of both civilization and nature, she feels profound pain when she is affected by unnatural toxins. Chemicals such as bleach or various pesticides are utterly toxic to Sirens and deal aggravated damage to a Siren. The exposure to the chemicals also cause their ability to resist pain to go out of wack. When a Siren is exposed to chemicals while she has damage in her rightmost Health box, her ability to ignore its effects is temporarily lifted until she can remove the points of aggravated damage. And while Sirens can survive pain, it only really works as long as her body is connected to her lungs. If a Siren is ever to lose a body part while she is in her human form, she must find medical help immediately before the lost part dissolves into sea foam. Flesh cut off the Siren's body will only last for 1 hour when exposed to the air before it dissolves. If a Siren is decapitated, it's a done deal; the Siren's head dissolves into sea foam while the body is fresh for an hour. If the body part is placed on ice, however, it may last for several months. Some hunters that know of this capture Sirens and force them to live in a tank as they systematically cut off pieces of her body in order to steal away some of her longevity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T14:49:03-08:00","id":786273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=786035#post786035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. For example: at akasha 1 your connection to the Song is so thin that you can add only one Opus to a Verse (Touch + Water + Control), at akasha 3 you can add 2 Opus to a verse (Area + Water + Weather + Invoke) and so on? If that's it I believe it is balanced enough and thus I like. Was afraid of PCs going all &quot;5 Opus in a verse&quot; and bringing down whole Veneza mid game.<br /> <br /> Personal definition is a very good addition, I just feel that maybe is too subjective to a Mechanical part of the game, and need to be further clarified. But it's nice, the Song touches Sirens in a diferente way.<br /> <br /> I suppose Concerts work like Hunter's Tactics, If everyone knows the same Verses they add bonuses to a certain Roll regarding the taks. As for Concerto Grosse I believe that it should cause some kind of disaster or disgrace. The Song wasn't made for nonsense conflicts, so it would retaliate, Nothing at Fukushima level, of course, but something big enough to stop the conflict</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. there's definitely going to be limits. Now the only question is &quot;How much Pneuma does a Verse cost&quot;? I'm willing to say that it costs as much Pneuma equal to how many Conclusions are in it. &quot;Area-Invoke-Water-Weather&quot; would cost a minimum of 2 Pneuma. <br /> <br /> As it comes to personal definition, it might be abit too subjective, but I have no ideas on how to explain. You two might do better. D:<br /> <br /> Finally, I'm unable to reach my source for Hunters tactics, but could you explain them to me? Actually, from what I recall from PtH and a Troupe Magic Merit, is a concert basically like a teamwork action for Sirens in pulling off a power? EDIT: Nevermind, I read over what you said and I'm basically repeating it. Anyhow, I would say though that Concerto Grossos can and should be allowed, Imagine if a few Sirens from Mankind's Victory wanted to use the Verse &quot;Area-Invoke-Weather-Water-Acid&quot; to make Acid rain destroy a city, but then some other Sirens make a counterpoint &quot;Area-Invoke-Weather-Clear&quot; to combat the Verse of the Mankind's Victory Sirens. It should be allowed at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T15:03:31-08:00","id":786281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=786249#post786249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume that when creating Opuses, there is going to be a glossary of possible interpretations and a list of denied interpretations. Like, 'Light&quot; may refer to sunlight, fire, or electricity but cannot refer to stars <i>(they are too far away to be called upon using &quot;Light&quot;), </i>nuclear energy <i>(considering that radiation has tainted the Pacific Ocean as well as scarring multiple tracts of land), </i>and quantity <i>(as in lightening a load)</i>. Combining &quot;Light&quot; with &quot;Sky&quot; can create sudden sunlight, call down a firestorm or lightning, or send an orb of light upwards to act as a beacon. It also depends on other factors like the Introduction or Conclusion, so [Area][Light-Sky][Create] summons a beacon while [Target][Light-Sky][Transform] may cause the target to reveal their true form when they are exposed to sunlight. The most basic Verse allows a Siren to impart intent while a Verse with extra Opuses allows the Siren to establish specific conditions. Just [Target][Light][Transform] is vague enough that the magic of the Verse may interpret &quot;Light&quot; as fire, which is significantly harder to find unless the Siren brings a can of kerosene and a match.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for double post, but this is what I meant by &quot;better wording than I can&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=786249#post786249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds both dangerous and awesome at the same time. Perhaps if a Concerto Grosso isn't resolved within a certain amount of time, the Song lashes out, causing the raw energy of the Opuses used to be released. Maybe the Bloop that occurs every now and then in the ocean is actually the resolution of an age-old grudge match between two ancient Shoals of Sirens trying to out-do the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was talked about using the Bloop on the original thread actually. Except the thing is that they've used it for why normal oceans popped up and that until the normal Waters/Bloop happened, there were only Abyssal Sirens out and about up to then. Here's the text from the forum describing it. We of course can change it however we want to note. D:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><i>For the longest time-since the Industrial Revolution onwards, in fact-humans simply forgot about nature. This isn't actually an indictment-for all the eons before then, nature was a source of terror and fear, and engendered a kind of respect because of that. As technology and society began to outpace nature however, nature lost its awfulness, and thus its awe. The woods were no longer a dark place where witches dwelled, where beasts roamed looking for the young of man-they were simply houses that weren't built yet, paper needing mills. Because of this, only those with truly extreme personalities-those who despised technology for daring to exist, and those with a genuine hatred of the natural environment-heard the Song, and so only Abyssal Sirens were Called.<br /> <br /> The 1990s changed that. That decade saw the rise of advanced ecological sciences, of the growing recognition that humanity had become an unintentional mass extinction event out of a combination of sheer intellect and appalling (in retrospect) naivety. Thus, in an astronomically short period of time compared to previous eras, the Calling began to be heard by the relatively normal once more-and given humanity's size and populace, on a similarly massively large in comparison level. <br /> <br /> Massive enough, as it was, to actually be heard on a physical as well as spiritual level. Ever heard of the Bloop? Or the Slow Down?<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: Yes, Those Are Real Things</b> [Text about the actual Bloop and Slow Down here, as well as a note that most of the scientists who discovered them are still mortal and do not have the mortal ally template, although they strange and recurring-though not unpleasant-dreams about the ocean. A large minority of the non-scientific staff and the college interns however, have grown withdrawn and secretive, assuming they didn't vanish altogether with the last eyewitness reports seeing them disappear, nude, into large bodies of water.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=786249#post786249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *snip Siren passives*</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span>I love all of this, especially the last paragraph as it introduces some more horror to living as a Siren. Which reminds me, there were some stuff on there being Fishermen like Hunters being antagonists for Sirens as well, something I'll get to work on soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:30:13-08:00","id":786898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry for triple posting, but if anyone's interested, I've started writing up on the Waters. Polaria is completely done and Freshwater I've just started on. Any thoughts or feelings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T16:14:12-08:00","id":787012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=786898#post786898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Sorry for triple posting, but if anyone's interested, I've started writing up on the Waters. Polaria is completely done and Freshwater I've just started on. Any thoughts or feelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do like how each type of Water ties into a style of song, with the Sirens of Polaria being Dirges and the write-up being about a death while the Sirens of Freshwater are Preludes and talk about a birth. <br /> <br /> I presume we're having 6 types of Waters, with Discordia effectively being the Zeka-types of Sirens? I also feel that &quot;Vapor&quot; should be renamed &quot;Vaporia&quot; to match the whole &quot;ending with -a&quot; style that the majority of the Waters have. <br /> <br /> So the Sirens of Polaria have Conclusions rather than Opuses or do all Waters give a Conclusion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T17:33:41-08:00","id":787053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787012#post787012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I do like how each type of Water ties into a style of song, with the Sirens of Polaria being Dirges and the write-up being about a death while the Sirens of Freshwater are Preludes and talk about a birth.<br /> <br /> I presume we're having 6 types of Waters, with Discordia effectively being the Zeka-types of Sirens? I also feel that &quot;Vapor&quot; should be renamed &quot;Vaporia&quot; to match the whole &quot;ending with -a&quot; style that the majority of the Waters have.<br /> <br /> So the Sirens of Polaria have Conclusions rather than Opuses or do all Waters give a Conclusion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Yes, I imagined taking different song styles to fit what each Water was about. More than abit Inspired by The Legend of Zelda Ocarina of Time and all of the Warp songs being named after a song type (best example is the &quot;Prelude to Light&quot;). Yes, we are having 6 types of waters, although I feel a tiny bit iffy on Vapor/ia. Are there any oceans or bodies of water that are misty all the time?<br /> <br /> As for Conclusions/Opuses, I was under the impression that my idea of making Conclusions all the &quot;Death, Darkness, Decay etc&quot; type words and Opus being the &quot;Invoke,Transform etc&quot; type words was accepted. If it's not (please tell me if it's not) then it's just a simple name change to fix the section.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I now realize I didn't answer your question. I imagined that all Oceans gave three free words that their sirens gain upon character creation, kind of like how most X Splats give free powers and stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 12-15-2015, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T18:03:30-08:00","id":787065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787053#post787053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. Yes, I imagined taking different song styles to fit what each Water was about. More than abit Inspired by The Legend of Zelda Ocarina of Time and all of the Warp songs being named after a song type (best example is the &quot;Prelude to Light&quot;). Yes, we are having 6 types of waters, although I feel a tiny bit iffy on Vapor/ia. Are there any oceans or bodies of water that are misty all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also The Legend of Zelda: Oracle of Ages which also has the music and time motif revolving around Naryu. <br /> <br /> Basically, the entirety of the UK. On a more serious note, hot springs and areas near volcanic activity tend to have a lot of steam due to the temperature. There's an area in Newfoundland in Canada that is known to the the foggiest area in the world and the Bay Area in California is known for its fogginess. Basically, anywhere where cold and warm air meet over an area with a large amount of water. In places that are close to the ocean, there's also sea fog due to the salt in the ocean. It would also fit the elemental motif that is running with Polaria (cold), Tropicana (warmth and sunlight), Gardenia (earthy or verdant life), and Vaporia <i>(Aurora instead?)</i> (wind currents) with Freshwater being order and Discordia being chaos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Conclusions/Opuses, I was under the impression that my idea of making Conclusions all the &quot;Death, Darkness, Decay etc&quot; type words and Opus being the &quot;Invoke,Transform etc&quot; type words was accepted. If it's not (please tell me if it's not) then it's just a simple name change to fix the section.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I now realize I didn't answer your question. I imagined that all Oceans gave three free words that their sirens gain upon character creation, kind of like how most X Splats give free powers and stuff </div> </div> </div>I thought that the definitions of Conclusion and Opus was changed given this post: <br /> <br /> <i>Indeed. And in my original post in naming the Song's different sections, I mentioned that<br /> Introduction - First Word used that refers to what it's affecting (Single/Multi target and Area of Effect)<br /> Verse/Opus (the word I used for naming the Second Word rather than how you used it. I'll rename it to Opus) - Second Word involving what the Siren wants to do (Transform, Invoke, Control, etcetc)<br /> Conclusion - The Third Word that is what the Siren wants to effect (Ice, Water, Fear, Sky, etc)<br /> <br /> When I spoke of &quot;switching them around', I was thinking that it might be better to have Opus and Conclusion switch definition with each other. Opus would hold what the Siren wanted to affect (Sky, Water, Fear etc) and Conclusion would have what the Siren wanted to do with it (Control, Invoke etc). Just purely for the sake of &quot;Conclusion&quot; being a case of &quot;what it says on the tin can&quot;, in this case being &quot;to what <b>end </b>the Siren wants the <i>opus subject </i>to do. So it would be like &quot;Area-Rain-Invoke&quot; to bring about a rainfall.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T18:22:44-08:00","id":787068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787065#post787065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's also The Legend of Zelda: Oracle of Ages which also has the music and time motif revolving around Naryu.<br /> <br /> Basically, the entirety of the UK. On a more serious note, hot springs and areas near volcanic activity tend to have a lot of steam due to the temperature. There's an area in Newfoundland in Canada that is known to the the foggiest area in the world and the Bay Area in California is known for its fogginess. Basically, anywhere where cold and warm air meet over an area with a large amount of water. In places that are close to the ocean, there's also sea fog due to the salt in the ocean. It would also fit the elemental motif that is running with Polaria (cold), Tropicana (warmth and sunlight), Gardenia (earthy or verdant life), and Vaporia <i>(Aurora instead?)</i> (wind currents) with Freshwater being order and Discordia being chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I sort of like the implication for Sirens (that I imagine at least) that they use &quot;Sunlight&quot; instead of &quot;Fire&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think Vaporia would be best with the Air motif, Freshwater would have perhaps just plain water (perhaps?). Seems like a cop out for just one of the Siren splats to hold control over water. We could take the PtH route and split &quot;Earth&quot; and &quot;Plant&quot; apart and have Freshwater take up the plant motif while Gardenia keeps the Earth motif or vice versa. As for Discordia, I imagine that they would have &quot;the dark art' when it comes to controlling water: Blood (perhaps as a tiny shout out to Avatar the Last Airbender, which actually does have the mediation motif that Siren has).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787065#post787065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that the definitions of Conclusion and Opus was changed given this post:</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Pardon my confusion. No changes then. As for the Conclusions for Waters, it's my fault for thinking ahead without explaining myself. I was thinking that on Character creation, Sirens gained the &quot;Self/One target&quot; Introduction automatically, could pick one Opus out which they also automatically gained, and they would recieve three free Conclusions depending on which Water they were part of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T19:21:56-08:00","id":787088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787068#post787068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. I sort of like the implication for Sirens (that I imagine at least) that they use &quot;Sunlight&quot; instead of &quot;Fire&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think Vaporia would be best with the Air motif, Freshwater would have perhaps just plain water (perhaps?). Seems like a cop out for just one of the Siren splats to hold control over water. We could take the PtH route and split &quot;Earth&quot; and &quot;Plant&quot; apart and have Freshwater take up the plant motif while Gardenia keeps the Earth motif or vice versa. As for Discordia, I imagine that they would have &quot;the dark art' when it comes to controlling water: Blood (perhaps as a tiny shout out to Avatar the Last Airbender, which actually does have the mediation motif that Siren has).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that, mentally, I was attaching specific environments to each Water. <b>Tropicana</b> and <b>Polaria</b> are obviously supposed to represent the tropics and the arctic poles, respectively. <b>Gardenia</b> leaned more towards the &quot;Louisianan Bayou&quot; and &quot;Mangroves of Asia&quot; type feel to them with the idea that the areas would be swampy and overgrown with life. <b>Vaporia</b>, in contrast, was mentally within sea ports and cities like Washington or the marshes of Scotland where the fog is thick and it rains all the time. <b>Freshwater</b> was more undisturbed, like a hidden lagoon or a koi pond while <b>Discordia</b> was placed in the middle of the ocean where storms come in and the currents draw flotsam and jetsam into a garbage pile. Freshwater could work for plant-life or life in general while keeping with the themes.<br /> <br /> I also remember writing something about the Sirens of Discordia thriving on tainted water. Water diluted with blood was one of those sorts of tainted water that I was thinking of, actually. That, and rust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, I see. Pardon my confusion. No changes then. As for the Conclusions for Waters, it's my fault for thinking ahead without explaining myself. I was thinking that on Character creation, Sirens gained the &quot;Self/One target&quot; Introduction automatically, could pick one Opus out which they also automatically gained, and they would recieve three free Conclusions depending on which Water they were part of. </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay. So each Water has its selection of Conclusions while each Siren, regardless of Water, gains a free Introduction and Opus. I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T20:55:52-08:00","id":787134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787088#post787088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that, mentally, I was attaching specific environments to each Water. <b>Tropicana</b> and <b>Polaria</b> are obviously supposed to represent the tropics and the arctic poles, respectively. <b>Gardenia</b> leaned more towards the &quot;Louisianan Bayou&quot; and &quot;Mangroves of Asia&quot; type feel to them with the idea that the areas would be swampy and overgrown with life. <b>Vaporia</b>, in contrast, was mentally within sea ports and cities like Washington or the marshes of Scotland where the fog is thick and it rains all the time. <b>Freshwater</b> was more undisturbed, like a hidden lagoon or a koi pond while <b>Discordia</b> was placed in the middle of the ocean where storms come in and the currents draw flotsam and jetsam into a garbage pile. Freshwater could work for plant-life or life in general while keeping with the themes.<br /> <br /> I also remember writing something about the Sirens of Discordia thriving on tainted water. Water diluted with blood was one of those sorts of tainted water that I was thinking of, actually. That, and rust.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I believe that Freshwater (at least how it was originally written) also refers to &quot;Fresh Water&quot;, the kind of water that basically occurs anywhere there isn't ocean, like rivers, bogs, ponds/lakes and groundwater. The closest to humanity since it's the type of water that is mostly within land.<br /> <br /> Also yes, you did bring up the idea of Discordian Sirens regaining Pneuma through tainted water (my only question is was it by drinking it or by swimming in it?). I just thought that &quot;Blood&quot; as a Conclusion for Discordian Sirens was just me thinking &quot;this would be cool&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787088#post787088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, okay. So each Water has its selection of Conclusions while each Siren, regardless of Water, gains a free Introduction and Opus. I understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any thoughts or concerns if I may ask? My only fear is that Sirens could be able to get alot of powers from the get go (despite being basically capable of only doing three Verses at the get go). Or I could just be needlessly paranoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T21:22:57-08:00","id":787147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787134#post787134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. I believe that Freshwater (at least how it was originally written) also refers to &quot;Fresh Water&quot;, the kind of water that basically occurs anywhere there isn't ocean, like rivers, bogs, ponds/lakes and groundwater. The closest to humanity since it's the type of water that is mostly within land.<br /> <br /> Also yes, you did bring up the idea of Discordian Sirens regaining Pneuma through tainted water (my only question is was it by drinking it or by swimming in it?). I just thought that &quot;Blood&quot; as a Conclusion for Discordian Sirens was just me thinking &quot;this would be cool&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I can go either way on the Freshwater Sirens. Rivers, lakes, and groundwater make sense because they are sources of fairly clean water. I would lump bogs in with the Gardenian Sirens because they usually consist of dead plant material that can be used to fertilize land. Not necessarily the best to drink from.<br /> <br /> And with the ability to regain Pneuma, I assume that, once per scene, a Siren may consume her favorite Water to regain a point of Pneuma or, again once per scene, submerge herself within the water of her choice to regain a set amount of her Pneuma, probably tying in with her Akasha as she attempts to become one with the water. Discordian Sirens would mix blood into water or possibly even swim through sewage <i>(that mental image is both scarring and disgusting and I probably shouldn't have suggested it).</i> I was also thinking about the Blood idea because it would at least allow Sirens to work with the idea of healing by keying &quot;Blood&quot; with &quot;flesh, body, or health&quot; when it comes to Verses.<br /> <br /> Should probably also say that Verses that create Water or any other form of water does not allow a Siren to regain Pneuma, though there are probably ways to affect Water using Verses in order to create the Siren's favorite Water. Maybe. I'm on the fence with this idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any thoughts or concerns if I may ask? My only fear is that Sirens could be able to get alot of powers from the get go (despite being basically capable of only doing three Verses at the get go). Or I could just be needlessly paranoid. </div> </div> </div>It is pretty strange how many permutations Sirens can go through when creating Verses. I assume that at least establishing how many per Introduction, Opus, and Conclusion will at least limit it. I think that, for the most part, the Opus and the Conclusion are the most important parts in a Verse, as they define what is happening with what. The Introduction controls the vastness of the power, so it's pretty limited on how much or how far it can go. Plus, the Verses will still have Pneuma costs. Presumably, increasing the number of targets beyond the Siren herself would increase the Pneuma cost and various Conclusions <i>(I thought Conclusions were the &quot;what it does&quot; part and Opuses were the &quot;what is it&quot; part)</i> have a fixed cost. [Sense] would be maybe 1 Pneuma because it's more of a utility while [Destroy] or [Create] are closer to 3 or 4 Pneuma because they are significantly more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T03:44:45-08:00","id":787257,"title":"","content":"Just a quick question- how many Conclusions and Opuses do you think would be needed? Figuring in to that, how 'generic' (for lack of a better word) do you envision them being? For example, would Sunlight encompass fire and light? What about more poetic things, like using Sunlight to heal or inspire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T06:37:30-08:00","id":787322,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787147#post787147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Sense] would be maybe 1 Pneuma because it's more of a utility while [Destroy] or [Create] are closer to 3 or 4 Pneuma because they are significantly more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, but we would need to have a few examples of each cost so players could understand what &quot;Utility&quot; means, in this case. Also, the cost in EXP would differ? or every conclusion would have a fixed cost? Anyway I believe we shoul make a small list of what we think Works as Clonclusions, Opuses and Introductions, when I suggested this mechanics (yay, so happy it was useful!) I had a few words in mind for introduction (Single Target, Multi, Area, Self and Conduction, where conduction would be more or Less a Touch introduction, but it could work by touching something that touches the target), and a large list for Opuses that could be broken down to units (i.e: instead of Storm there should be Wind + Water).<br /> <br /> As for Waters' Opuses and Conclusions, well I don't know. Each could start with A Conclusion but would need to pay the cost in EXP for the Opus, afterall, in character creation, they will receive dots to buy Opus, Conclusions and Introduction (which I believe should be limited to a Starting core, with more powerful Verses being a little more costly)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just wanted to say that I'm loving everything else, this gameline has a Huge potential.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: Is Bono Vox a Siren?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T12:22:02-08:00","id":787556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787147#post787147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. I can go either way on the Freshwater Sirens. Rivers, lakes, and groundwater make sense because they are sources of fairly clean water. I would lump bogs in with the Gardenian Sirens because they usually consist of dead plant material that can be used to fertilize land. Not necessarily the best to drink from.<br /> <br /> And with the ability to regain Pneuma, I assume that, once per scene, a Siren may consume her favorite Water to regain a point of Pneuma or, again once per scene, submerge herself within the water of her choice to regain a set amount of her Pneuma, probably tying in with her Akasha as she attempts to become one with the water. Discordian Sirens would mix blood into water or possibly even swim through sewage <i>(that mental image is both scarring and disgusting and I probably shouldn't have suggested it).</i> I was also thinking about the Blood idea because it would at least allow Sirens to work with the idea of healing by keying &quot;Blood&quot; with &quot;flesh, body, or health&quot; when it comes to Verses.<br /> <br /> Should probably also say that Verses that create Water or any other form of water does not allow a Siren to regain Pneuma, though there are probably ways to affect Water using Verses in order to create the Siren's favorite Water. Maybe. I'm on the fence with this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. These are good ideas, I was actually thinking of the submerging idea, thanks for putting your thought out first though. :3 As for swimming through sewage, why not just replace it with &quot;Stormy&quot; waters, as in swimming when there's a storm outside or the like? Although I don't mind the image of swimming through sewage, at least as long as it's just for Discordian Sirens.<br /> <br /> I would also say that the Water should be &quot;natural&quot; to apply for the Siren regaining Pneuma. I have an idea for a rule. If a Siren creates water befitting her Waters and it remains the way she's made it for a lunar cycle (so a month), then it is considered natural water and may be used for regaining Pneuma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787147#post787147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is pretty strange how many permutations Sirens can go through when creating Verses. I assume that at least establishing how many per Introduction, Opus, and Conclusion will at least limit it. I think that, for the most part, the Opus and the Conclusion are the most important parts in a Verse, as they define what is happening with what. The Introduction controls the vastness of the power, so it's pretty limited on how much or how far it can go. Plus, the Verses will still have Pneuma costs. Presumably, increasing the number of targets beyond the Siren herself would increase the Pneuma cost and various Conclusions <i>(I thought Conclusions were the &quot;what it does&quot; part and Opuses were the &quot;what is it&quot; part)</i> have a fixed cost. [Sense] would be maybe 1 Pneuma because it's more of a utility while [Destroy] or [Create] are closer to 3 or 4 Pneuma because they are significantly more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conclusions: &quot;What it does&quot;<br /> Opus: &quot;What is it&quot;<br /> <br /> Should we switch the definitions back around? I feel like it was stupid idea on my part. If nothing else, I do like the customization idea. I had a concern but it literally slipped my mind, I'll post it later if it comes up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787257#post787257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick question- how many Conclusions and Opuses do you think would be needed? Figuring in to that, how 'generic' (for lack of a better word) do you envision them being? For example, would Sunlight encompass fire and light? What about more poetic things, like using Sunlight to heal or inspire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whichever uses &quot;Dark, Death, Freeze&quot; kind words will have much more words in them than the one that uses &quot;Invoke, Destroy, Create&quot; kind words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787322#post787322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, but we would need to have a few examples of each cost so players could understand what &quot;Utility&quot; means, in this case. Also, the cost in EXP would differ? or every conclusion would have a fixed cost? Anyway I believe we shoul make a small list of what we think Works as Clonclusions, Opuses and Introductions, when I suggested this mechanics (yay, so happy it was useful!) I had a few words in mind for introduction (Single Target, Multi, Area, Self and Conduction, where conduction would be more or Less a Touch introduction, but it could work by touching something that touches the target), and a large list for Opuses that could be broken down to units (i.e: instead of Storm there should be Wind + Water).<br /> <br /> As for Waters' Opuses and Conclusions, well I don't know. Each could start with A Conclusion but would need to pay the cost in EXP for the Opus, afterall, in character creation, they will receive dots to buy Opus, Conclusions and Introduction (which I believe should be limited to a Starting core, with more powerful Verses being a little more costly</div> </div> </div> </div>Introduction, Opus and Conclusion should all have differing EXP costs. Will explain more after a confirmation on to switch back the Opus (From &quot;Invoke, Create, Destroy etc&quot; to &quot;Death, Darkness, Decay etc&quot;) and Conclusion (From &quot;Death Darkness Decay&quot; to &quot;Invoke Create Destroy&quot;) or keep them as they are now..<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if I'm seeming so difficult at all. &gt;&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 12-16-2015, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T14:49:42-08:00","id":787645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787257#post787257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick question- how many Conclusions and Opuses do you think would be needed? Figuring in to that, how 'generic' (for lack of a better word) do you envision them being? For example, would Sunlight encompass fire and light? What about more poetic things, like using Sunlight to heal or inspire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the Opuses <i>(the What It Is part)</i>would be fairly literal in their interpretation but they would be rather expansive in what they can do. With the Polaria Sirens that have &quot;Darkness&quot;, &quot;Death&quot;, and &quot;Freeze&quot; as Opuses, here's what is written up by SaulottheGentle:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Death</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, the word that connects to dead bodies and wandering ghosts with equal power.</span></span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Darkness</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, the ability to manipulate shadows that can equally conceal as much as they can illuminate, depending on whether they\u2019re covering up with darkness or removing the shadows so light shines.</span></span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Freeze, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">the word that stops progress as much as it turns water to ice. </span></span></span></i><br /> <br /> I would presume that &quot;Death&quot;, while it refers to dead bodies and ghosts, would not be able to suddenly strike people dead nor would it work on things that are more based on symbolism, like a plastic skeleton that hangs in biology labs or a depiction of the grim reaper. With the Conclusions and Introductions, the &quot;Death&quot; Opus might be able to remove dead flesh or necrosis from a Siren or it could possibly allow the Siren to feign death or summon an Anchor <i>(not literally)</i> for ghosts and spirits to manifest around. With Light, which encompasses Sunlight, Fire, and Lightning and possibly light in general, it may be able to be used as a sudden burst of light or fire that may be able to cauterize wounds but wouldn't necessarily heal. With clever use, a Siren may be able to create a Verse that allows the Light to be used as a laser and partake in eye surgery, but that would require a <i>very</i> specific set of skills to use. <br /> <br /> Given that there are six types of Waters that Sirens belong to and assuming that the Opuses are not crossed over, that would make a set of 18 unique Opuses with the possibility of more. If the Waters have some sort of cross-over with other Waters, that would mean that there are 8 shared Opuses, three each. I believe we are probably going for 18 unique Opuses and some along with the Conclusions, which could make upwards of 90 combinations of unique Verses, not including Introductions. Of course, because things are based on an interpretation-based system, that may mean that things will be less set-in-stone and more up-in-the-air. <br /> <br /> Hoo boy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787322#post787322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, but we would need to have a few examples of each cost so players could understand what &quot;Utility&quot; means, in this case. Also, the cost in EXP would differ? or every conclusion would have a fixed cost? Anyway I believe we shoul make a small list of what we think Works as Clonclusions, Opuses and Introductions, when I suggested this mechanics (yay, so happy it was useful!) I had a few words in mind for introduction (Single Target, Multi, Area, Self and Conduction, where conduction would be more or Less a Touch introduction, but it could work by touching something that touches the target), and a large list for Opuses that could be broken down to units (i.e: instead of Storm there should be Wind + Water).<br /> <br /> As for Waters' Opuses and Conclusions, well I don't know. Each could start with A Conclusion but would need to pay the cost in EXP for the Opus, afterall, in character creation, they will receive dots to buy Opus, Conclusions and Introduction (which I believe should be limited to a Starting core, with more powerful Verses being a little more costly)</div> </div> </div> </div>When I referred to [Sense] as a utility, I meant that it doesn't necessarily have an offensive or defensive use. Sensing a type of material or element like sensing a source of water or sensing a nearby dead body only offers so much information before a Siren actually goes to investigate the source. A different Conclusion that would possibly have a slightly higher cost than [Sense] may be [Travel], which allows a Siren to move from point A to point B through a medium based on the Opus as if it were water, like [Stone][Travel], which allows a Siren to phase through concrete material. <br /> <br /> I believe that, say, Introductions cost 2 EXP, Favored Opuses cost 3 EXP while Unfavored Opuses cost 5 EXP, and Conclusions cost 3 EXP. Given that a starting Siren has 1 dot of Akasha, the power stat, she would have a maximum of 10 points of Pneuma. [Sense] would probably give +0 Pneuma cost to a Verse while [Travel] might be around +1 Pneuma cost. A single Opus would probably give +0 Pneuma cost to a Verse while each additional Opus adds +1 Pneuma cost. This would mean that [Death][Sense] would be +0 Pneuma cost overall while [Sky][Light][Travel] would be +2 Pneuma cost. The Introduction, which shapes who or what is being affected will probably change the cost as well. [Self] would most-likely be +0 Cost while [Area] would be +2 or possibly even more. So [Self][Pain][Sense] would allow the Siren to sense what or where is causing her body pain for no Pneuma while [Area][Stone][Travel] would allow Sirens or other individuals to pass through concrete buildings as long as they hear the Siren using the Verse and chose to utilize the Verse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT2: Is Bono Vox a Siren? </div> </div> </div>...I hope he isn't but it could be a possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787556#post787556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. These are good ideas, I was actually thinking of the submerging idea, thanks for putting your thought out first though. :3 As for swimming through sewage, why not just replace it with &quot;Stormy&quot; waters, as in swimming when there's a storm outside or the like? Although I don't mind the image of swimming through sewage, at least as long as it's just for Discordian Sirens.<br /> <br /> I would also say that the Water should be &quot;natural&quot; to apply for the Siren regaining Pneuma. I have an idea for a rule. If a Siren creates water befitting her Waters and it remains the way she's made it for a lunar cycle (so a month), then it is considered natural water and may be used for regaining Pneuma.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for the Discordian Sirens, &quot;Stormy&quot; waters is a little too dependent on factors outside of her control. Polarian Sirens can make an ice bath while Tropican Sirens can swim in water warmed by sunlight. Freshwater Sirens are slightly restricted in that the water needs to be pure, but they can circumvent this by buying bottles of water in bulk. Vaporian Sirens can stay in a sauna and absorb the vapors or maybe even use a humidifier. Gardenian Sirens can take a mud bath or consume clay, mud, or silt. They are all relatively less dependent on outside forces, which is why I feel that the sewage or blood options would work better and that rain may work better for Freshwater or Vaporians.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of creating water that lasts for the lunar cycle being considered natural. It's also a good way to work in the moon, considering that the moon controls the tides and we haven't really touched on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conclusions: &quot;What it does&quot;<br /> Opus: &quot;What is it&quot;<br /> <br /> Should we switch the definitions back around? I feel like it was stupid idea on my part. If nothing else, I do like the customization idea. I had a concern but it literally slipped my mind, I'll post it later if it comes up.<br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> Whichever uses &quot;Dark, Death, Freeze&quot; kind words will have much more words in them than the one that uses &quot;Invoke, Destroy, Create&quot; kind words. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dark, Death, Freeze&quot; are Opuses, &quot;Invoke, Destroy, Create&quot; are Conclusions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Introduction, Opus and Conclusion should all have differing EXP costs. Will explain more after a confirmation on to switch back the Opus (From &quot;Invoke, Create, Destroy etc&quot; to &quot;Death, Darkness, Decay etc&quot;) and Conclusion (From &quot;Death Darkness Decay&quot; to &quot;Invoke Create Destroy&quot;) or keep them as they are now..<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if I'm seeming so difficult at all. &gt;&gt; </div> </div> </div>I did a little explanation up there. :V","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T17:27:02-08:00","id":787724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787645#post787645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would presume that &quot;Death&quot;, while it refers to dead bodies and ghosts, would not be able to suddenly strike people dead nor would it work on things that are more based on symbolism, like a plastic skeleton that hangs in biology labs or a depiction of the grim reaper. With the Conclusions and Introductions, the &quot;Death&quot; Opus might be able to remove dead flesh or necrosis from a Siren or it could possibly allow the Siren to feign death or summon an Anchor <i>(not literally)</i> for ghosts and spirits to manifest around. With Light, which encompasses Sunlight, Fire, and Lightning and possibly light in general, it may be able to be used as a sudden burst of light or fire that may be able to cauterize wounds but wouldn't necessarily heal. With clever use, a Siren may be able to create a Verse that allows the Light to be used as a laser and partake in eye surgery, but that would require a <i>very</i> specific set of skills to use.<br /> <br /> Given that there are six types of Waters that Sirens belong to and assuming that the Opuses are not crossed over, that would make a set of 18 unique Opuses with the possibility of more. If the Waters have some sort of cross-over with other Waters, that would mean that there are 8 shared Opuses, three each. I believe we are probably going for 18 unique Opuses and some along with the Conclusions, which could make upwards of 90 combinations of unique Verses, not including Introductions. Of course, because things are based on an interpretation-based system, that may mean that things will be less set-in-stone and more up-in-the-air.<br /> <br /> Hoo boy.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the first rules of Tabletop Games: No instant death buttons. :3<br /> <br /> Although to put it in a sense and as an addendum to what Reaper said, I would say that an Opus has as much power in it as much as the Siren's imagination for how it could be used. Wordplay and double meanings is perhaps the greatest weapon any author (or in this case <i>songwriter</i>) can have. Take for example a man who calls Mother Teresa a whore. She obviously wasn't a &quot;whore&quot; in that she's a prostitute or had sex. Whores are known for seeing lots of people and interacting with them, which Mother Teresa did. I don't know if I'm breaking any forum rules and if I am, I apologize, it was just an example I've pulled up for the use of double meanings.<br /> <br /> Another thing though is that an Opus has no power if you don't have an Introduction or a Conclusion, the three need to be stringed together to form a Verse to affect anything. In this case, if a Siren uses &quot;Target-Death-Destroy&quot; as a Verse, she'd be rolling Akasha + ??? for damaging whatever she's targeting. &quot;Death&quot; could refer to &quot;Decay&quot; as well if we chose to make it so.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I don't think we've came up with a dice pool for Verses (at least, a default one). To start up ideas on this, my idea is that the base dicepool for it is the Siren's Akasha rating, followed by a system of Bonuses/Penalties to raise/lower the pool. One idea for a bonus is knowing the target's name, or being close to what an Opus depicts. Wordplay here is very useful, has to be in the Siren's immediate vicinity and she has to know it occurred if it's something situational. In said case of situationalism, it's possible to use the Trace ability to pick up the bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787645#post787645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that, say, Introductions cost 2 EXP, Favored Opuses cost 3 EXP while Unfavored Opuses cost 5 EXP, and Conclusions cost 3 EXP. Given that a starting Siren has 1 dot of Akasha, the power stat, she would have a maximum of 10 points of Pneuma. [Sense] would probably give +0 Pneuma cost to a Verse while [Travel] might be around +1 Pneuma cost. A single Opus would probably give +0 Pneuma cost to a Verse while each additional Opus adds +1 Pneuma cost. This would mean that [Death][Sense] would be +0 Pneuma cost overall while [Sky][Light][Travel] would be +2 Pneuma cost. The Introduction, which shapes who or what is being affected will probably change the cost as well. [Self] would most-likely be +0 Cost while [Area] would be +2 or possibly even more. So [Self][Pain][Sense] would allow the Siren to sense what or where is causing her body pain for no Pneuma while [Area][Stone][Travel] would allow Sirens or other individuals to pass through concrete buildings as long as they hear the Siren using the Verse and chose to utilize the Verse.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll probably need some kind of idea or ruling for how much the Introductions and Conclusions add to cost (or availability if we don't deal with cost) just so that there isn't a case of &quot;I've just started playing this game and I can't use any Verses because the ones I have cost 2+ Pneuma and I can only spend 1 per turn&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787645#post787645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for the Discordian Sirens, &quot;Stormy&quot; waters is a little too dependent on factors outside of her control. Polarian Sirens can make an ice bath while Tropican Sirens can swim in water warmed by sunlight. Freshwater Sirens are slightly restricted in that the water needs to be pure, but they can circumvent this by buying bottles of water in bulk. Vaporian Sirens can stay in a sauna and absorb the vapors or maybe even use a humidifier. Gardenian Sirens can take a mud bath or consume clay, mud, or silt. They are all relatively less dependent on outside forces, which is why I feel that the sewage or blood options would work better and that rain may work better for Freshwater or Vaporians.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of creating water that lasts for the lunar cycle being considered natural. It's also a good way to work in the moon, considering that the moon controls the tides and we haven't really touched on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ice Bucket Challenge is literally a way for Polarian Sirens to regain Pneuma. XD<br /> <br /> Sorry, had to say that. Anyways, I would suggest that given a huge motif with water is that it eventually runs everywhere or becomes almost anything at all, perhaps the way it can be regained is more open. For example, there's a river inland that's cold due to the winter and known for being intermixed with dirt. Because it's a fresh water river, a Freshwater Siren can use it for Pneuma. Because it's icy cold, a Polarian Siren can use it. Because it's dirty water, a Gardenia Siren can use it.<br /> <br /> In exchange for this &quot;more options/less restrictiveness&quot; on water quality, it would give less Pneuma (a minimum of 1 Pneuma) or gives an Akasha + Her-Specific-Waters Alterations Pneuma that can only be done once per day. Perhaps only while the moon is out to boot (the phase doesn't matter).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787645#post787645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dark, Death, Freeze&quot; are Opuses, &quot;Invoke, Destroy, Create&quot; are Conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it. Thank you. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787645#post787645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a little explanation up there. :V</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty then, lets use it. I forgot my idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T20:16:11-08:00","id":787802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787724#post787724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the first rules of Tabletop Games: No instant death buttons. :3<br /> <br /> Although to put it in a sense and as an addendum to what Reaper said, I would say that an Opus has as much power in it as much as the Siren's imagination for how it could be used. Wordplay and double meanings is perhaps the greatest weapon any author (or in this case <i>songwriter</i>) can have. Take for example a man who calls Mother Teresa a whore. She obviously wasn't a &quot;whore&quot; in that she's a prostitute or had sex. Whores are known for seeing lots of people and interacting with them, which Mother Teresa did. I don't know if I'm breaking any forum rules and if I am, I apologize, it was just an example I've pulled up for the use of double meanings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that, as long as you don't make anything incredibly explicit or use a term in an incredibly derogatory term, you should be safe. But that's my thought so it's up to the mods to figure that one out.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Opuses, we are going to add a list of possible interpretations and a list of denied interpretations <i>(my example of [Light] referring to sunlight and not &quot;lightening the load&quot;)</i> so I assume anything that falls in between might add difficulty in creating the Verse, but it is still possible to be created.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing though is that an Opus has no power if you don't have an Introduction or a Conclusion, the three need to be stringed together to form a Verse to affect anything. In this case, if a Siren uses &quot;Target-Death-Destroy&quot; as a Verse, she'd be rolling Akasha + ??? for damaging whatever she's targeting. &quot;Death&quot; could refer to &quot;Decay&quot; as well if we chose to make it so.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I don't think we've came up with a dice pool for Verses (at least, a default one). To start up ideas on this, my idea is that the base dicepool for it is the Siren's Akasha rating, followed by a system of Bonuses/Penalties to raise/lower the pool. One idea for a bonus is knowing the target's name, or being close to what an Opus depicts. Wordplay here is very useful, has to be in the Siren's immediate vicinity and she has to know it occurred if it's something situational. In said case of situationalism, it's possible to use the Trace ability to pick up the bonus. </div> </div> </div>I think that the Dice Pool may be Akasha + a Statistic that relates to what the Conclusion relates to <i>([Travel], being movement-based, is Akasha + Dexterity, possibly) +/- </i>whatever various bonuses are available while Alterations are passives that are based on Statistics + Skill. Mainly so that Sirens can invest in both Verse-building and Alterations without feeling like they are spending points to increase their skills which aren't as mechanically impressive as the Verses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We'll probably need some kind of idea or ruling for how much the Introductions and Conclusions add to cost (or availability if we don't deal with cost) just so that there isn't a case of &quot;I've just started playing this game and I can't use any Verses because the ones I have cost 2+ Pneuma and I can only spend 1 per turn&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I completely forgot about the &quot;Fuel Per Turn&quot; rule that all of the splats have. Maybe negative cost based on how many are being targeted? So [Self] is -1 Pneuma Cost, which allows beginning Sirens to invest in +2 Pneuma Cost Conclusions as long as they build for [Self] or maybe [Object], with [Object] referring to any inanimate, non-living object that is equal to or smaller than the Siren's Size. Verses will be able to go down to 0 Pneuma Cost but going into negative Pneuma Cost doesn't mean that the Siren regains Pneuma; the Verse is just at a free cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ice Bucket Challenge is literally a way for Polarian Sirens to regain Pneuma. XD<br /> <br /> Sorry, had to say that. Anyways, I would suggest that given a huge motif with water is that it eventually runs everywhere or becomes almost anything at all, perhaps the way it can be regained is more open. For example, there's a river inland that's cold due to the winter and known for being intermixed with dirt. Because it's a fresh water river, a Freshwater Siren can use it for Pneuma. Because it's icy cold, a Polarian Siren can use it. Because it's dirty water, a Gardenia Siren can use it.<br /> <br /> In exchange for this &quot;more options/less restrictiveness&quot; on water quality, it would give less Pneuma (a minimum of 1 Pneuma) or gives an Akasha + Her-Specific-Waters Alterations Pneuma that can only be done once per day. Perhaps only while the moon is out to boot (the phase doesn't matter). </div> </div> </div>I think that's a pretty good idea for mixed-source Waters, though it would add contention between the opposing Sirens <i>(Tropicana vs. Polaria, Gardenia vs. Vaporia, Freshwater vs. Discordia)</i>. Actually, that might still fit because it works in the whole &quot;Mediator&quot; idea by showing that, sometimes, the sides are pushed over to one bias. <br /> <br /> And now I just realized that the Waters have contrasting personalities. I'm really slow on the uptake. <br /> [/QUOTE]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T21:14:36-08:00","id":787834,"title":"","content":"All I have to add to this topic is that I can't wait for the Mermaider supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T21:38:47-08:00","id":787844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787802#post787802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of the Opuses, we are going to add a list of possible interpretations and a list of denied interpretations <i>(my example of [Light] referring to sunlight and not &quot;lightening the load&quot;)</i> so I assume anything that falls in between might add difficulty in creating the Verse, but it is still possible to be created.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Perhaps we should also add in that the words have a default way of being interpreted, but when combined with other words they can have a new meaning. Like &quot;Light+Gravity&quot; does mean lighter weight? If this idea is bad, we can take it out. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787802#post787802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Dice Pool may be Akasha + a Statistic that relates to what the Conclusion relates to <i>([Travel], being movement-based, is Akasha + Dexterity, possibly) +/- </i>whatever various bonuses are available while Alterations are passives that are based on Statistics + Skill. Mainly so that Sirens can invest in both Verse-building and Alterations without feeling like they are spending points to increase their skills which aren't as mechanically impressive as the Verses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Loving this idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So just as a thought, the Conclusions could perhaps be based off of Attributes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787802#post787802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely forgot about the &quot;Fuel Per Turn&quot; rule that all of the splats have. Maybe negative cost based on how many are being targeted? So [Self] is -1 Pneuma Cost, which allows beginning Sirens to invest in +2 Pneuma Cost Conclusions as long as they build for [Self] or maybe [Object], with [Object] referring to any inanimate, non-living object that is equal to or smaller than the Siren's Size. Verses will be able to go down to 0 Pneuma Cost but going into negative Pneuma Cost doesn't mean that the Siren regains Pneuma; the Verse is just at a free cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least concerning the Supernatural Advantage, to which here would be Akasha. Yes, cost negation sounds well enough and adding &quot;Object&quot; to the list of Introductions sounds good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787802#post787802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's a pretty good idea for mixed-source Waters, though it would add contention between the opposing Sirens <i>(Tropicana vs. Polaria, Gardenia vs. Vaporia, Freshwater vs. Discordia)</i>. Actually, that might still fit because it works in the whole &quot;Mediator&quot; idea by showing that, sometimes, the sides are pushed over to one bias.<br /> <br /> And now I just realized that the Waters have contrasting personalities. I'm really slow on the uptake.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tendencies of X-Splats. It does help with the themes. :3 Although I wouldn't think that most Sirens (at least the normal Currents and thus non-Abyssal ones) would mind that much over some territory dispute on water. Nature is nature, the Tropicana can have the waters during the summer and use hot tubs in the winter. Of course, location counts too. I would imagine though that more than a few Sirens would get sore if there was a Siren actively trying to keep the water about being to her Waters liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T07:06:03-08:00","id":788064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787834#post787834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I have to add to this topic is that I can't wait for the Mermaider supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Dethlok reference, right? Metalopocalypse? I kinda want to give it a cursory glace because it could actually work.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me, Rikuo from <i>Darkstalkers </i>could work as inspiration for Alterations considering that he can instantly change part of his form to gain aspects of a marine creature when he fights, like morphing crab claws to do a stronger punch or gaining a pufferfish's quills to block attacks. Corrin from his introduction in <i>Super Smash Brothers for Wii U/3DS </i>might also serve as inspiration, despite him being a dragon. Apparently, he can transform one of his arms into a dragon's mouth and bite using his mouth hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=787844#post787844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Indeed. Perhaps we should also add in that the words have a default way of being interpreted, but when combined with other words they can have a new meaning. Like &quot;Light+Gravity&quot; does mean lighter weight? If this idea is bad, we can take it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm partially skeptical on this idea because there are so many combinations of Opuses that would just absolutely fill the splatbook. I think the &quot;Absolute Yes, Absolute No&quot; definitions would allow for a broad spectrum of interpretations. [Gravity] by itself could be taken to mean weight going in either direction and kinda fits the idea of &quot;lighter/heavier weight&quot; already, so I assume that [Light][Gravity] would be more literal or creative, like using fire to lighten yourself to the point where you can fly or using a sunbeam with so much weight that it is effectively a laser beam of devastation. We could possibly have a few examples, but it would be rather difficult to create a meaning for each and every Opus combination.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. Loving this idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So just as a thought, the Conclusions could perhaps be based off of Attributes? </div> </div> </div>I completely forgot the word for Attributes when I was typing. Yes. If there is a possibility to get 9 unique Conclusions or at least a multiple of 3, then we would be able to split up the Conclusions to relate to an Attribute. <b>[Travel]</b> is definitely <b>Dexterity </b>while<b> [Sense]</b> could be <b>Intelligence</b>. <b>[Destroy]</b> feels like it leans towards <b>Strength</b>. I referred to one of the Conclusions as <b>[Create]</b> but I believe Yads Dom suggested <b>[Invoke]</b> in the post that actually started the idea of making modular powers, so <b>[Invoke]</b> could be used as <b>Presence</b>. <b>[Transform]</b> may be <b>Wits </b>while<b> [Control]</b> is more <b>Wits</b>. That would leave 3 more Conclusions for Stamina, Resolve, and Composure. Perhaps something like [Protect] or [Restore]?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The tendencies of X-Splats. It does help with the themes. :3 Although I wouldn't think that most Sirens (at least the normal Currents and thus non-Abyssal ones) would mind that much over some territory dispute on water. Nature is nature, the Tropicana can have the waters during the summer and use hot tubs in the winter. Of course, location counts too. I would imagine though that more than a few Sirens would get sore if there was a Siren actively trying to keep the water about being to her Waters liking. </div> </div> </div>I would err on the side of caution when it comes to territory disputes over water. Kinda crossing into something that is almost entirely Werewolf-y. Honestly, I think it would be more &quot;Migration&quot; and &quot;Big Fish, Little Pond&quot; type scenario, where Sirens that enjoy the warm water in the summer have to find somewhere else for the Winter and that Sirens that attempt to &quot;stake a claim&quot; in a location of water will soon become acclimated to the water and not receive as strong of a benefit. Kinda like building a tolerance to alcohol and needing more and more just to get a little tipsy. I'm not saying that the Sirens being miffed over another Siren keeping her waters the way she likes. That's actually a pretty good idea to bring up for inter-team disputes. But I think that it would be too same-y with Werewolf unless something was changed or added to keep it unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":". 12-17-2015, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T09:00:04-08:00","id":788140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788064#post788064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm partially skeptical on this idea because there are so many combinations of Opuses that would just absolutely fill the splatbook. I think the &quot;Absolute Yes, Absolute No&quot; definitions would allow for a broad spectrum of interpretations. [Gravity] by itself could be taken to mean weight going in either direction and kinda fits the idea of &quot;lighter/heavier weight&quot; already, so I assume that [Light][Gravity] would be more literal or creative, like using fire to lighten yourself to the point where you can fly or using a sunbeam with so much weight that it is effectively a laser beam of devastation. We could possibly have a few examples, but it would be rather difficult to create a meaning for each and every Opus combination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. One way I can think of to allieviate some requirement for explanation is to put in a note somewhere that it's up to the ST to dictate whether things can be pulled out to whatever extreme they're pulled at?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788064#post788064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely forgot the word for Attributes when I was typing. Yes. If there is a possibility to get 9 unique Conclusions or at least a multiple of 3, then we would be able to split up the Conclusions to relate to an Attribute. <b>[Travel]</b> is definitely <b>Dexterity </b>while<b> [Sense]</b> could be <b>Intelligence</b>. <b>[Destroy]</b> feels like it leans towards <b>Strength</b>. I referred to one of the Conclusions as <b>[Create]</b> but I believe Yads Dom suggested <b>[Invoke]</b> in the post that actually started the idea of making modular powers, so <b>[Invoke]</b> could be used as <b>Presence</b>. <b>[Transform]</b> may be <b>Wits </b>while<b> [Control]</b> is more <b>Wits</b>. That would leave 3 more Conclusions for Stamina, Resolve, and Composure. Perhaps something like [Protect] or [Restore]?</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot Manipulation, or you meant it when you said &quot;Control is more Wits&quot; with the second Wits supposing to be &quot;Manipulation&quot;? If nothing else, I'm liking these, one thing we should keep in mind though is that the Conclusions should not be able to majorly cover the same ground that other Conclusions can do. Just as a note is all.<br /> <br /> Stamina:<b> Protect</b><br /> Resolve: <b>Restore</b><br /> Composure: <b>Calm </b>(Kind of the opposite of Presence's <b>Invoke</b>? Such as the previous &quot;Area-Weather-Water-Invoke&quot; example being cancelled out by a &quot;Area-Weather-Water-Calm&quot;?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788064#post788064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would err on the side of caution when it comes to territory disputes over water. Kinda crossing into something that is almost entirely Werewolf-y. Honestly, I think it would be more &quot;Migration&quot; and &quot;Big Fish, Little Pond&quot; type scenario, where Sirens that enjoy the warm water in the summer have to find somewhere else for the Winter and that Sirens that attempt to &quot;stake a claim&quot; in a location of water will soon become acclimated to the water and not receive as strong of a benefit. Kinda like building a tolerance to alcohol and needing more and more just to get a little tipsy. I'm not saying that the Sirens being miffed over another Siren keeping her waters the way she likes. That's actually a pretty good idea to bring up for inter-team disputes. But I think that it would be too same-y with Werewolf unless something was changed or added to keep it unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ack, the &quot;Would&quot; in that paragraph was supposed to be a &quot;Wouldn't&quot;. &gt;&gt; I meant it more in the sense of that I didn't think that Sirens would have territory disputes over water or even get riled up over the type of water present unless if someone was actively making it more &quot;theirs&quot; to the point that it disrupted natural order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T09:37:55-08:00","id":788157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788140#post788140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alrighties then. One way I can think of to allieviate some requirement for explanation is to put in a note somewhere that it's up to the ST to dictate whether things can be pulled out to whatever extreme they're pulled at?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that there should basically be a preface in the powers chapter that explicitly says &quot;While there is a set of possible accepted and denied interpretations as written in the splatbook, the final call is always up to the Storyteller's discretion. Using an Opus or Conclusion to a definition not defined as accepted or denied will be considered case-by-case by the Storyteller, but it is recommended that as-written acceptable interpretations should be able to go through.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You forgot Manipulation, or you meant it when you said &quot;Control is more Wits&quot; with the second Wits supposing to be &quot;Manipulation&quot;? If nothing else, I'm liking these, one thing we should keep in mind though is that the Conclusions should not be able to majorly cover the same ground that other Conclusions can do. Just as a note is all.<br /> <br /> Stamina:<b> Protect</b><br /> Resolve: <b>Restore</b><br /> Composure: <b>Calm </b>(Kind of the opposite of Presence's <b>Invoke</b>? Such as the previous &quot;Area-Weather-Water-Invoke&quot; example being cancelled out by a &quot;Area-Weather-Water-Calm&quot;?) </div> </div> </div>The second Wits is supposed to be Manipulation. It was 7 in the morning for me when I last wrote that, so I was a little tired. :V<br /> <br /> I would definitely agree that the Conclusions at least should try not to overlap. I would say that [Control] would have to be more creative and based on rearranging whatever is being targeted instead of controlling its form. Sort of like playing with clay. [Weather-Water][Calm] would ease the strength of the storm while [Weather-Water][Control] would allow the storm to be moved somewhere else or formed so that it only rains on one side of a city.<br /> <br /> I am also liking Protect, Restore, and Calm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ack, the &quot;Would&quot; in that paragraph was supposed to be a &quot;Wouldn't&quot;. &gt;&gt; I meant it more in the sense of that I didn't think that Sirens would have territory disputes over water or even get riled up over the type of water present unless if someone was actively making it more &quot;theirs&quot; to the point that it disrupted natural order. </div> </div> </div>Ah. Okay. So Sirens aren't going to be thinking in terms of &quot;This is Mine&quot; but more in a sense of &quot;This is Ours, as Sirens and as Nature&quot;, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T10:28:14-08:00","id":788195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788157#post788157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that there should basically be a preface in the powers chapter that explicitly says &quot;While there is a set of possible accepted and denied interpretations as written in the splatbook, the final call is always up to the Storyteller's discretion. Using an Opus or Conclusion to a definition not defined as accepted or denied will be considered case-by-case by the Storyteller, but it is recommended that as-written acceptable interpretations should be able to go through.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. :3 As a note, I'm finally beginning to stop being lazy and beginning to list these all in Google docs. Pardon me if I take awhile, before I post these, as sloth is my master.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788157#post788157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second Wits is supposed to be Manipulation. It was 7 in the morning for me when I last wrote that, so I was a little tired. :V<br /> <br /> I would definitely agree that the Conclusions at least should try not to overlap. I would say that [Control] would have to be more creative and based on rearranging whatever is being targeted instead of controlling its form. Sort of like playing with clay. [Weather-Water][Calm] would ease the strength of the storm while [Weather-Water][Control] would allow the storm to be moved somewhere else or formed so that it only rains on one side of a city.<br /> <br /> I am also liking Protect, Restore, and Calm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. What's next for Verses? I'm probably getting ahead of myself as I haven't finished up the Waters yet (working on the Siren Lexicon). Listing out all of the words (Introduction, Opus and Conclusion wise) and defining them as much as possible? If it helps, here's the ideas I have for Waters Opuses are (listing from your ideas as well as mine). <br /> <br /> Polaria: Dark, Death, Freeze.<br /> Freshwater: Human, Fate, Technology<br /> Tropicana: Light, Sear (the opposite of Polaria's &quot;Freeze&quot; or meant to be, something like &quot;Catalyze&quot; may work better), ??? <br /> Gardenia: Plant, Earth, Animal<br /> Vaporia: Wind, Weather, ???<br /> Discordia: Blood, Insanity, ???<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788157#post788157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. Okay. So Sirens aren't going to be thinking in terms of &quot;This is Mine&quot; but more in a sense of &quot;This is Ours, as Sirens and as Nature&quot;, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I imagine this to be actually a thing where Werewolves and Sirens wouldn't get along in crossovers. Sirens (at least most of them) don't mind sharing waters to regain Pneuma, whereas Werewolves always have some territory devoted to themselves. If Werewolves tried pushing Sirens away, I don't think that Sirens would sit down to take it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T11:19:43-08:00","id":788226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788195#post788195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Alrighties then. :3 As a note, I'm finally beginning to stop being lazy and beginning to list these all in Google docs. Pardon me if I take awhile, before I post these, as sloth is my master.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. I know how it feels, considering that I'm sitting on three splats of my own that I haven't touched or a month.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand. What's next for Verses? I'm probably getting ahead of myself as I haven't finished up the Waters yet (working on the Siren Lexicon). Listing out all of the words (Introduction, Opus and Conclusion wise) and defining them as much as possible? If it helps, here's the ideas I have for Waters Opuses are (listing from your ideas as well as mine). </div> </div> </div>Polaria: Dark, Death, Freeze.<br /> Freshwater: Human, Fate, Technology<br /> Tropicana: Light, Sear (the opposite of Polaria's &quot;Freeze&quot; or meant to be, something like &quot;Catalyze&quot; may work better), ???<br /> Gardenia: Plant, Earth, Animal<br /> Vaporia: Wind, Weather, ???<br /> Discordia: Blood, Insanity, ???[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> For Tropicana, Light for fire/sunlight, maybe Temper or Boil for the Sear/Catalyze aspect as you are effectively heating something up to prepare, and Warmth as in comfort and pleasure.<br /> <br /> For Gardenia, possibly switch Plant to Growth as in literal and figurative Growth? It would allow each Water to have an Opus that is more figurative, along the lines of Freeze and Temper/Boil.<br /> <br /> For Vaporia, Wind, Weather or Sky, and maybe Pressure in a sense of a feeling of metaphorical weight or meaning <i>(considering that the Vaporian Sirens are waif-like and are more-likely to appear to a mortal, tell them that they have a hard decision to make, and disappear without another word).</i><br /> <br /> For Discordia, Blood, Insanity or Chaos, and maybe Taint as in impurities or damage like rust or mold?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I think that we may have to do something to the Opuses as some can be more literal while others are more metaphorical. Considering that [Travel] is one of the Conclusions, it would be odd to try to use [Freeze][Travel] to...stop movement? To travel through things that have been stopped? Or having to [Travel] through [Temper/Boil]? <br /> <br /> Dark, Death, Human, Technology, Light, Plant, Earth, Animal, Wind, Blood, and maybe Taint are fairly literal and would make sense to be [Travel]ed, [Restore]ed, or [Destroy]ed. <br /> <br /> Freeze, Fate, Sear/Temper/Boil, Warmth, Pressure, and Insanity/Chaos seem more metaphorical and wouldn't necessarily work with [Travel], [Protect] or even [Sense]. Because of this, I feel that I should go back on my idea to keep everything literal and instead have both literal and figurative interpretations?<br /> <br /> Take Freeze for example. When it was written in the document for the Polarians, it was stated that it stopped progress like it froze water into ice, which to me made it seem like it was more of a metaphorical type. Plus, the fact that it is called &quot;Freeze&quot; which is more of a verb makes it seem more like a Conclusion. Maybe renaming it to Frost and having the interpretation also include ice and snow. Or it could be a Conclusion that is exclusive to the Polarians?<br /> <br /> It would significantly lighten the amount of Opuses and even out the total between Opuses and Conclusions to have the Waters provide a choice between two Opuses and granting a free Conclusion. While [Calm] does allow for the chosen Opus to be released, it doesn't necessarily stop it dead in its tracks, which could tie into the fact that Sirens are from a different time and are able to slightly affect the way that time flows through special Conclusions.<br /> <br /> At least, it will make it so that Opuses aren't incredibly brain-busting to work through and allow for a greater pool for what the Verses would be capable of. <br /> <br /> If the idea does fly, then the Polarians would be able to [Freeze] things in time, Tropicans could [Temper] things and cause them to escalate, Gardenians could [Nourish] things by allowing them to be undisturbed, Vaporians could [Push] things by allowing them to be noticed immediately, Freshwaters could [Refine] things by allowing progress to move through them, and Discordians could [Disturb] things by causing them to experience a temporally displaced version of The Deluge. Then the Waters would look something like this:<br /> <br /> Polaria: [Freeze] Darkness or Death<br /> Tropicana: [Temper] Light or Warmth<br /> Gardenia: [Nourish] Earth or Animal<br /> Vaporia: [Push] Wind or Weather<br /> Freshwater: [Refine] Human or Technology<br /> Discordia: [Disturb] Blood or Insanity/Chaos <i>(Chaos interpretations would include junk piles and crowds of people, basically things that are considered chaotic)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed. I imagine this to be actually a thing where Werewolves and Sirens wouldn't get along in crossovers. Sirens (at least most of them) don't mind sharing waters to regain Pneuma, whereas Werewolves always have some territory devoted to themselves. If Werewolves tried pushing Sirens away, I don't think that Sirens would sit down to take it though. </div> </div> </div>I doubt that Sirens would leave anything to their own devices unless the Sirens were sure that nothing bad would happen. Sirens and Werewolves would probably have a tentative peace-like agreement that gets strained whenever a Werewolf feels like they need to establish dominance or protect their territory or whenever a Siren attempts to play peacekeeper or attract the attention of humanity. The two would definitely be sick of each other, but almost at the level of bureaucratic disagreements that would slowly lead into grudges and eventual murder attempts.<br /> <br /> I also feel like we need to start discussing how the Currents would factor in, considering that we have done a lot of talk about the Oceans which are now Waters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T12:38:47-08:00","id":788276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788226#post788226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Tropicana, Light for fire/sunlight, maybe Temper or Boil for the Sear/Catalyze aspect as you are effectively heating something up to prepare, and Warmth as in comfort and pleasure.<br /> <br /> For Gardenia, possibly switch Plant to Growth as in literal and figurative Growth? It would allow each Water to have an Opus that is more figurative, along the lines of Freeze and Temper/Boil.<br /> <br /> For Vaporia, Wind, Weather or Sky, and maybe Pressure in a sense of a feeling of metaphorical weight or meaning <i>(considering that the Vaporian Sirens are waif-like and are more-likely to appear to a mortal, tell them that they have a hard decision to make, and disappear without another word).</i><br /> <br /> For Discordia, Blood, Insanity or Chaos, and maybe Taint as in impurities or damage like rust or mold?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think these are fine. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788226#post788226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that we may have to do something to the Opuses as some can be more literal while others are more metaphorical. Considering that [Travel] is one of the Conclusions, it would be odd to try to use [Freeze][Travel] to...stop movement? To travel through things that have been stopped? Or having to [Travel] through [Temper/Boil]?<br /> <br /> Dark, Death, Human, Technology, Light, Plant, Earth, Animal, Wind, Blood, and maybe Taint are fairly literal and would make sense to be [Travel]ed, [Restore]ed, or [Destroy]ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Target-Freeze-Travel&quot; would be IMMENSELY useful in a chase scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I would imagine that there should be something saying &quot;The Verse needs to make sense in order to work&quot;. It does sort of take out clarifying things, but it also gives some additional freedom to players making use of the Verses. Maybe instead of changing Opuses to work for Conclusions, maybe we should add some things to Conclusions to make them work for Opuses? For example, the <b>Travel </b>Opus could refer to both being able to travel through things, or to be able to affect things from a far away distance. This could also bring in the idea of being able to compile Conclusions as well as Opuses. <b>Destroy</b> could be taken as the Verse being used to damage the item or thing in question. Such as &quot;Target-Light-Destroy&quot; begins damaging light fixtures around the Siren. <br /> <br /> I do imagine there to be a few cases of &quot;this verse doesn't work&quot;, and I know this'll sound bad but I'm fine with that so long as it's a few cases..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788226#post788226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freeze, Fate, Sear/Temper/Boil, Warmth, Pressure, and Insanity/Chaos seem more metaphorical and wouldn't necessarily work with [Travel], [Protect] or even [Sense]. Because of this, I feel that I should go back on my idea to keep everything literal and instead have both literal and figurative interpretations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate-Sense would sense good or bad fortune or be able to acutely pick up on Changelings, Insanity-Protect could keep the target (or Siren herself) from acquiring derangements/negative conditions, Death-Travel or Fate-Travel could even perhaps allow travelling into Twilight, Underworld or even Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788226#post788226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take Freeze for example. When it was written in the document for the Polarians, it was stated that it stopped progress like it froze water into ice, which to me made it seem like it was more of a metaphorical type. Plus, the fact that it is called &quot;Freeze&quot; which is more of a verb makes it seem more like a Conclusion. Maybe renaming it to Frost and having the interpretation also include ice and snow. Or it could be a Conclusion that is exclusive to the Polarians?<br /> <br /> It would significantly lighten the amount of Opuses and even out the total between Opuses and Conclusions to have the Waters provide a choice between two Opuses and granting a free Conclusion. While [Calm] does allow for the chosen Opus to be released, it doesn't necessarily stop it dead in its tracks, which could tie into the fact that Sirens are from a different time and are able to slightly affect the way that time flows through special Conclusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm....I'm a tiny bit skeptical on this idea. For one, I would imagine that the Currents could give Conclusions to buy (leaving most of the Opuses with the Waters). For another, I believe that the Opuses could be kept as they are, the demand for abit of creativity in using the powers is perhaps fitting for powers based around songs and the like. If not, it can be taken out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788226#post788226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the idea does fly, then the Polarians would be able to [Freeze] things in time, Tropicans could [Temper] things and cause them to escalate, Gardenians could [Nourish] things by allowing them to be undisturbed, Vaporians could [Push] things by allowing them to be noticed immediately, Freshwaters could [Refine] things by allowing progress to move through them, and Discordians could [Disturb] things by causing them to experience a temporally displaced version of The Deluge. Then the Waters would look something like this:<br /> <br /> Polaria: [Freeze] Darkness or Death<br /> Tropicana: [Temper] Light or Warmth<br /> Gardenia: [Nourish] Earth or Animal<br /> Vaporia: [Push] Wind or Weather<br /> Freshwater: [Refine] Human or Technology<br /> Discordia: [Disturb] Blood or Insanity/Chaos <i>(Chaos interpretations would include junk piles and crowds of people, basically things that are considered chaotic)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem is that <b>Temper </b>and <b>Nourish</b> are practically the same thing that affect different targets (Temper on objects and items, Nourish on people and living things) and <b>Refine</b> is/can be a synonym to Temper. And I'm sorry to point out that the &quot;More Conclusions&quot; idea has more of the same problems that you pointed out with some Conclusions being incompatible with Opuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788226#post788226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that Sirens would leave anything to their own devices unless the Sirens were sure that nothing bad would happen. Sirens and Werewolves would probably have a tentative peace-like agreement that gets strained whenever a Werewolf feels like they need to establish dominance or protect their territory or whenever a Siren attempts to play peacekeeper or attract the attention of humanity. The two would definitely be sick of each other, but almost at the level of bureaucratic disagreements that would slowly lead into grudges and eventual murder attempts.<br /> <br /> I also feel like we need to start discussing how the Currents would factor in, considering that we have done a lot of talk about the Oceans which are now Waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, as for Currents it seems simple enough but I think that we have enough on the plate for now. If not, then is there any thoughts on the Currents? They seem to be more duty/job based, even the Abyssal ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T13:21:52-08:00","id":788303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788276#post788276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Target-Freeze-Travel&quot; would be IMMENSELY useful in a chase scene. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I would imagine that there should be something saying &quot;The Verse needs to make sense in order to work&quot;. It does sort of take out clarifying things, but it also gives some additional freedom to players making use of the Verses. Maybe instead of changing Opuses to work for Conclusions, maybe we should add some things to Conclusions to make them work for Opuses? For example, the <b>Travel </b>Opus could refer to both being able to travel through things, or to be able to affect things from a far away distance. This could also bring in the idea of being able to compile Conclusions as well as Opuses. <b>Destroy</b> could be taken as the Verse being used to damage the item or thing in question. Such as &quot;Target-Light-Destroy&quot; begins damaging light fixtures around the Siren.<br /> <br /> I do imagine there to be a few cases of &quot;this verse doesn't work&quot;, and I know this'll sound bad but I'm fine with that so long as it's a few cases..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be more of an issue of how the grammatical structure of the Verse would work. From what I took from the Verses, the first part, the Introduction which refers to a [Target], defines the area in which the Verse affects, whether it is self-based, based off of an object at a set amount of distance away, or a general field area. The second part, the [Opus] refers to what is being sought after in the [Target] area, like finding all the [Light] within an [Area] of a room. The third word, the Conclusion, would affect the [Opus] within the [Target], so [Area][Light][Destroy] would snuff out candle light, bust out the light bulbs, or put a block within a city into a black out, as you said. Having the Conclusion [Travel] would make it so that the Siren or those who could hear the Verse constructed by the Siren could pass through the chosen [Opus].<br /> <br /> If we were going for the [Target][Freeze][Travel] example, I feel like it would be read as being able to [Travel] via objects that are cold [Freeze] and granting that power to the target [Target]. I feel like it should be worded as [Target][Human][Freeze] or even [Area][Human][Freeze], so that within the area [Area] or specified as that person [Target], any human [Human] caught by the Verse would be temporarily stopped [Freeze]. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fate-Sense would sense good or bad fortune or be able to acutely pick up on Changelings, Insanity-Protect could keep the target (or Siren herself) from acquiring derangements/negative conditions, Death-Travel or Fate-Travel could even perhaps allow travelling into Twilight, Underworld or even Arcadia. </div> </div> </div>I'll give it to you for coming up with [Death][Travel] and [Fate][Travel] allowing you to move through realms, but I almost feel as if giving Death and Fate exclusively to the Polarians and Freshwater, respectively, would limit the other Sirens' usefulness. Then again, the Discordians can work with [Blood] and I presume that the Tropicans might be able to manipulate Azoth using [Light].<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hrm....I'm a tiny bit skeptical on this idea. For one, I would imagine that the Currents could give Conclusions to buy (leaving most of the Opuses with the Waters). For another, I believe that the Opuses could be kept as they are, the demand for abit of creativity in using the powers is perhaps fitting for powers based around songs and the like. If not, it can be taken out.<br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> The only problem is that <b>Temper </b>and <b>Nourish</b> are practically the same thing that affect different targets (Temper on objects and items, Nourish on people and living things) and <b>Refine</b> is/can be a synonym to Temper. And I'm sorry to point out that the &quot;More Conclusions&quot; idea has more of the same problems that you pointed out with some Conclusions being incompatible with Opuses.<br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> Sounds good, as for Currents it seems simple enough but I think that we have enough on the plate for now. If not, then is there any thoughts on the Currents? They seem to be more duty/job based, even the Abyssal ones. </div> </div> </div>Alright. I feel that it would make sense to move the Conclusions to the Currents, then. That would make for 10 Conclusions that need to be written up unless we should add the already-created Conclusions to the Currents. <br /> <br /> I will say that I still want to push for the Opuses to not be actions and to be based around the object that the Verse is meant to control/create/etc. [Freeze] being used to stop things doesn't make much sense if everything else refers to a concept that would tangibly exist. I feel that [Freeze] works better as a definition for things that are cold or have gone into cool-down, like a stopped car. Let me type up what I think the Opuses should feel like:<br /> <br /> <b>Polaria</b>: [Darkness] for shadows and the absence of light or even nightmares, [Death] for dead bodies and ghosts, and [Freeze/Frost] for things that are literally cold or are on &quot;cool-down&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Tropicana</b>: [Light] for sunlight or light sources and fire, [Passion] for emotions and love, and [Temper] for things that are hot or are being heated up like a debate<br /> <br /> <b>Gardenia</b>: [Earth] for soil or stones and unrefined metals, [Animal] for creatures that aren't capable of free will, and [Growth] for vegetation or things that are capable of growing like mold or a movement<br /> <br /> <b>Vaporia</b>: [Wind] for air currents and breezes, [Weather/Sky] for things that are naturally occurring events like sandstorms or rain, and [Pressure] for air pressure or things that have a heavy metaphorical weight like decisions or guilt<br /> <br /> <b>Freshwater</b>: [Human] for mortals untouched by the supernatural, [Technology] for electronics or devices created out of refined metal such as cars, and [Fate] for fortune or things that are related to the idea of destiny<br /> <br /> <b>Discordia</b>: [Blood] as in blood or possibly even flesh, [Taint] for impurities or decay like rust or oil spills, and [Chaos] for junk piles or situations that can be described as chaotic<br /> <br /> I figure that, if we're going with the idea that &quot;Some Verses contain conflicting or vague ideas that will cause them to fail&quot; route, we could have a Tag system where Conclusions like [Travel] need Opuses that have the (Material) Tag so that there is something that the Siren can [Travel] through. Like, [Passion] isn't necessarily material, so a Siren can't create a [Passion][Travel] Verse but she is free to create [Darkness/Light/Human][Travel] Verses because those are material objects and have the (Material) Tag.<br /> <br /> I presume that these Opuses are not exclusive to the Waters; they are just Favored by the Waters and Sirens of that Water are able to buy these Opuses for cheaper. I would also presume that there are Opuses that are automatically favored or unfavored like [Water], [Sound], [Beauty], and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T16:07:54-08:00","id":788376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788303#post788303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that would be more of an issue of how the grammatical structure of the Verse would work. From what I took from the Verses, the first part, the Introduction which refers to a [Target], defines the area in which the Verse affects, whether it is self-based, based off of an object at a set amount of distance away, or a general field area. The second part, the [Opus] refers to what is being sought after in the [Target] area, like finding all the [Light] within an [Area] of a room. The third word, the Conclusion, would affect the [Opus] within the [Target], so [Area][Light][Destroy] would snuff out candle light, bust out the light bulbs, or put a block within a city into a black out, as you said. Having the Conclusion [Travel] would make it so that the Siren or those who could hear the Verse constructed by the Siren could pass through the chosen [Opus].<br /> <br /> If we were going for the [Target][Freeze][Travel] example, I feel like it would be read as being able to [Travel] via objects that are cold [Freeze] and granting that power to the target [Target]. I feel like it should be worded as [Target][Human][Freeze] or even [Area][Human][Freeze], so that within the area [Area] or specified as that person [Target], any human [Human] caught by the Verse would be temporarily stopped [Freeze].</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. So it's more of a grammatical manner in that case? In which case, I can see using Freeze for that. What I was thinking when putting Freeze in was that Opuses could be slightly malleable in a contextual fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788303#post788303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll give it to you for coming up with [Death][Travel] and [Fate][Travel] allowing you to move through realms, but I almost feel as if giving Death and Fate exclusively to the Polarians and Freshwater, respectively, would limit the other Sirens' usefulness. Then again, the Discordians can work with [Blood] and I presume that the Tropicans might be able to manipulate Azoth using [Light].</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, I do want to make something clear. Sirens are only as good as using powers that's normally the hat of other splats as well as the other splats are at using other splat stuff. For example, Vampires have limited means of dealing with Spirits and Ghosts, but otherwise they remain limited and not up at the same level as Werewolves or Sin-Eaters deal with them. The most I can imagine Sirens interacting with other Supernatural splats would be to be able to enter their domain and interact with the residents a tiny bit (only in the case of Spirits and Ghosts, everything forbid actually dealing with a True Fae), but nothing else. One thing that can be noted is that the usefulness of powers really depends on whether or not the game is played with additional elements. Fate doesn't have any Changeling connotations if &quot;Siren the Drowning&quot; is played without &quot;Changeling the Lost&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788303#post788303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. I feel that it would make sense to move the Conclusions to the Currents, then. That would make for 10 Conclusions that need to be written up unless we should add the already-created Conclusions to the Currents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the easiest option, since it feels like the 9 Conclusions we have now about covers it. However, I do believe that we do have a tenth Conclusion we can use that you've made. &quot;Taint&quot;. How does this look? As a note, I don't believe that these should be freely given on Character Creation. I would say that they're favoured by the Current, but they're not freely given on character creation (although a character will be able to pick out a free Conclusion on character creation, it doesn't have to be the same as the current she's a part of). <br /> Conflict: <b>Protect (Stamina)</b><br /> Healing: <b>Restore (Resolve)</b><br /> Harmony: <b>Calm (Composure)</b><br /> Buoyancy: <b>Travel (Dexterity)</b><br /> Wisdom: <b>Sense (Intelligence)</b><br /> <br /> Acheron (Void): <b>Taint (Let's say 10-Serenity bonus to Verse Rolls)</b><br /> Cocytus (Dark Wisdom): <b>Transform (Presence)</b><br /> Lethe (Mankind's Victory): <b>Control (Manipulation)</b><br /> Phelegethon (Dark Passions): <b>Invoke (Wits)</b><br /> Styx (Primordial Darkness): <b>Destroy (Strength)</b><br /> <br /> Now I also wonder, when it comes to Opuses and Conclusions, we're kind away from the &quot;5 dot hierarchy&quot; that most WoD games have. Should there be any similar hierarchy to Opuses? Otherwise, it'd be pretty easy to get all the words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788303#post788303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that I still want to push for the Opuses to not be actions and to be based around the object that the Verse is meant to control/create/etc. [Freeze] being used to stop things doesn't make much sense if everything else refers to a concept that would tangibly exist. I feel that [Freeze] works better as a definition for things that are cold or have gone into cool-down, like a stopped car. Let me type up what I think the Opuses should feel like<br /> <b>snip</b></div> </div> </div> </div>These are good. :3 We can replace the Taint idea for Acheron and put in something else if it helps Discordian Sirens. D:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788303#post788303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure that, if we're going with the idea that &quot;Some Verses contain conflicting or vague ideas that will cause them to fail&quot; route, we could have a Tag system where Conclusions like [Travel] need Opuses that have the (Material) Tag so that there is something that the Siren can [Travel] through. Like, [Passion] isn't necessarily material, so a Siren can't create a [Passion][Travel] Verse but she is free to create [Darkness/Light/Human][Travel] Verses because those are material objects and have the (Material) Tag.<br /> <br /> I presume that these Opuses are not exclusive to the Waters; they are just Favored by the Waters and Sirens of that Water are able to buy these Opuses for cheaper. I would also presume that there are Opuses that are automatically favored or unfavored like [Water], [Sound], [Beauty], and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably best for a system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T17:11:53-08:00","id":788409,"title":"","content":"Guys, I was thinking today: Does Silencing a Siren through a Power stops their ability to use Verses? If a Siren is playing a instrument to use the verse, does silencing na \u00e1rea with a Mage Spell, for example, stops the verse already in course?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T17:47:32-08:00","id":788419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788376#post788376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. So it's more of a grammatical manner in that case? In which case, I can see using Freeze for that. What I was thinking when putting Freeze in was that Opuses could be slightly malleable in a contextual fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that we should divorce the Opuses from the Conclusions as much as we can so that we don't have to do more work with making Opuses that can double as Conclusions depending on what needs to go where. That having been said, there could be a Conclusion that functions as a stop called something like [Pause] that works the way that [Freeze] would've worked as a Conclusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If nothing else, I do want to make something clear. Sirens are only as good as using powers that's normally the hat of other splats as well as the other splats are at using other splat stuff. For example, Vampires have limited means of dealing with Spirits and Ghosts, but otherwise they remain limited and not up at the same level as Werewolves or Sin-Eaters deal with them. The most I can imagine Sirens interacting with other Supernatural splats would be to be able to enter their domain and interact with the residents a tiny bit (only in the case of Spirits and Ghosts, everything forbid actually dealing with a True Fae), but nothing else. One thing that can be noted is that the usefulness of powers really depends on whether or not the game is played with additional elements. Fate doesn't have any Changeling connotations if &quot;Siren the Drowning&quot; is played without &quot;Changeling the Lost&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Ahh. I would say that [Travel] with [Death] or [Fate] should have some sort of default interpretation with a sidebar that mentions traveling into the Twilight/Underworld/Arcadia/etc, rather than stating it outright. I feel that those realms are definitely something that would not come up that often when playing Siren but that it would be an option for the Storyteller and players to explore. With [Travel][Death] I assumed that the Sirens would be able to corpse-jump by swimming into one dead body and arrive at a different location through another dead body or perhaps swimming as if they were ghosts and could float through the air as ephemeral beings. With [Travel][Fate], I'm kinda stumped. Maybe a stronger version of the Trace where the Siren swims through the timeline to be mentally placed in the period that she's trying to Trace but forces her to make her own interpretations rather than providing an answer to a question?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would be the easiest option, since it feels like the 9 Conclusions we have now about covers it. However, I do believe that we do have a tenth Conclusion we can use that you've made. &quot;Taint&quot;. How does this look? As a note, I don't believe that these should be freely given on Character Creation. I would say that they're favoured by the Current, but they're not freely given on character creation (although a character will be able to pick out a free Conclusion on character creation, it doesn't have to be the same as the current she's a part of).<br /> Conflict: <b>Protect (Stamina)</b><br /> Healing: <b>Restore (Resolve)</b><br /> Harmony: <b>Calm (Composure)</b><br /> Buoyancy: <b>Travel (Dexterity)</b><br /> Wisdom: <b>Sense (Intelligence)</b><br /> <br /> Acheron (Void): <b>Taint (Let's say 10-Serenity bonus to Verse Rolls)</b><br /> Cocytus (Dark Wisdom): <b>Transform (Presence)</b><br /> Lethe (Mankind's Victory): <b>Control (Manipulation)</b><br /> Phelegethon (Dark Passions): <b>Invoke (Wits)</b><br /> Styx (Primordial Darkness): <b>Destroy (Strength)</b><br /> <br /> Now I also wonder, when it comes to Opuses and Conclusions, we're kind away from the &quot;5 dot hierarchy&quot; that most WoD games have. Should there be any similar hierarchy to Opuses? Otherwise, it'd be pretty easy to get all the words. </div> </div> </div>I presume that Acheron's Conclusion could be the [Disturb] Conclusion that I pitched before, where [Disturb] can cause things to go out of wack, like [Disturb][Light] causes a flux in the power grid or [Disturb][Death] causes the ghost of the recently deceased to arise?<br /> <br /> I do have to say that it's interesting that the normal Currents have the more &quot;defensive, less cost&quot; Conclusions while the Abyssal Currents have the &quot;destructive, more cost&quot; Conclusions.<br /> <br /> As for the 5-Dot Hierarchy, I believe that <i><b>Demon: the Descent</b></i> doesn't have any powers that work off of a 5-Dot system and <b><i>Mummy: the Curse</i></b> only has it for the Pillars, although that does play in to the Utterances technically. We could work it into the Alterations somehow, but I think we're probably going to discuss those at a later time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are good. :3 We can replace the Taint idea for Acheron and put in something else if it helps Discordian Sirens. D:<br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> That's probably best for a system. </div> </div> </div>I presume that the tags would be (Material) for Opuses that influence things that are tangibly real like the metal of a car or a flickering flame, (Concept) for Opuses that deal with things that aren't necessarily tangible but exist on a different level like emotions or movements. Or there could be interpretations that allow Opuses to be used in a literal way, in a conceptual way, and in a symbolic way.<br /> <br /> Like, with [Light], the most-literal way for [Light] to be used is as sunlight or flames. Conceptually, [Light] would extend to anything that gives off light, including florescent lamps, lightning, and bioluminescent creatures. Symbolically, [Light] could represent the &quot;good&quot; side or the side of &quot;order&quot;. With [Growth], literally it applies to plants and molds because they grow and don't necessarily stop until they need to. Conceptually, [Growth] extends to things that have naturally grown other things like the spread of viruses or even cancerous cells. Symbolically, [Growth] could represent things that have aged or improve gradually. Combining the two into [Growth-Light] may mean that the interpretation refers to a plant that is considered to be &quot;good&quot; or helpful, such as medicinal plants, or light that grows in intensity, like a wildfire. It would also allow a wider array of Verses that could be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T06:14:19-08:00","id":788705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or there could be interpretations that allow Opuses to be used in a literal way, in a conceptual way, and in a symbolic way. </div> </div> </div>Having literal and conceptual interpretations sounds good, but I feel like the symbolic ones might create overlap and make certain Opuses much more useful. Maybe apply a progressive dice penalty to them as they get less literal?<br /> As for the five dot thing, I feel like that's not as strictly clung to now- Werewolf dropped it for 2e too.. It might not fit, especially if Siren's alternate form is going to be built like a demon's. But that's just my onion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T07:48:41-08:00","id":788744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788409#post788409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, I was thinking today: Does Silencing a Siren through a Power stops their ability to use Verses? If a Siren is playing a instrument to use the verse, does silencing na \u00e1rea with a Mage Spell, for example, stops the verse already in course?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Sirens should still be able to use Verses even if she's Silenced, but her ability to actually carry it out is VERY much diminished. Perhaps this way of doing verses without making a sound is called &quot;Lip Syncing&quot;?<br /> <br /> Oh, as another thought, what if when Sirens use Verses and they do use sounds, then even deaf people can hear them? This is because Verses don't discriminate based on &quot;who can hear it&quot;, it affects anyone who can hear it. :3 Maybe it's also a thing for Siren Hunters/Fletchers. Some of them are deaf or keep an eye on deaf people to tell if Sirens are around. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788419#post788419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that we should divorce the Opuses from the Conclusions as much as we can so that we don't have to do more work with making Opuses that can double as Conclusions depending on what needs to go where. That having been said, there could be a Conclusion that functions as a stop called something like [Pause] that works the way that [Freeze] would've worked as a Conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think of it, how about we mix Freeze/Pause's effects into Calm? They're pretty much close to the same thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788419#post788419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh. I would say that [Travel] with [Death] or [Fate] should have some sort of default interpretation with a sidebar that mentions traveling into the Twilight/Underworld/Arcadia/etc, rather than stating it outright. I feel that those realms are definitely something that would not come up that often when playing Siren but that it would be an option for the Storyteller and players to explore. With [Travel][Death] I assumed that the Sirens would be able to corpse-jump by swimming into one dead body and arrive at a different location through another dead body or perhaps swimming as if they were ghosts and could float through the air as ephemeral beings. With [Travel][Fate], I'm kinda stumped. Maybe a stronger version of the Trace where the Siren swims through the timeline to be mentally placed in the period that she's trying to Trace but forces her to make her own interpretations rather than providing an answer to a question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death-Travel could also make a dead body move to a location and Fate-Travel could also take successes from the future, but then the Siren would have to pay up on a later roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788419#post788419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume that Acheron's Conclusion could be the [Disturb] Conclusion that I pitched before, where [Disturb] can cause things to go out of wack, like [Disturb][Light] causes a flux in the power grid or [Disturb][Death] causes the ghost of the recently deceased to arise?<br /> <br /> I do have to say that it's interesting that the normal Currents have the more &quot;defensive, less cost&quot; Conclusions while the Abyssal Currents have the &quot;destructive, more cost&quot; Conclusions.<br /> <br /> As for the 5-Dot Hierarchy, I believe that <i><b>Demon: the Descent</b></i> doesn't have any powers that work off of a 5-Dot system and <b><i>Mummy: the Curse</i></b> only has it for the Pillars, although that does play in to the Utterances technically. We could work it into the Alterations somehow, but I think we're probably going to discuss those at a later time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Would probably be fitting. And yes, I thought that out because it would be fitting. :3 <br /> <br /> I'm sorry about asking on the 5 Dot hierarchy, still having trouble moving to GMC. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788419#post788419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume that the tags would be (Material) for Opuses that influence things that are tangibly real like the metal of a car or a flickering flame, (Concept) for Opuses that deal with things that aren't necessarily tangible but exist on a different level like emotions or movements. Or there could be interpretations that allow Opuses to be used in a literal way, in a conceptual way, and in a symbolic way.<br /> <br /> Like, with [Light], the most-literal way for [Light] to be used is as sunlight or flames. Conceptually, [Light] would extend to anything that gives off light, including florescent lamps, lightning, and bioluminescent creatures. Symbolically, [Light] could represent the &quot;good&quot; side or the side of &quot;order&quot;. With [Growth], literally it applies to plants and molds because they grow and don't necessarily stop until they need to. Conceptually, [Growth] extends to things that have naturally grown other things like the spread of viruses or even cancerous cells. Symbolically, [Growth] could represent things that have aged or improve gradually. Combining the two into [Growth-Light] may mean that the interpretation refers to a plant that is considered to be &quot;good&quot; or helpful, such as medicinal plants, or light that grows in intensity, like a wildfire. It would also allow a wider array of Verses that could be possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. This is very good too and it would make it easier to categorize the words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788705#post788705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having literal and conceptual interpretations sounds good, but I feel like the symbolic ones might create overlap and make certain Opuses much more useful. Maybe apply a progressive dice penalty to them as they get less literal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T12:04:47-08:00","id":788900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788409#post788409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, I was thinking today: Does Silencing a Siren through a Power stops their ability to use Verses? If a Siren is playing a instrument to use the verse, does silencing na \u00e1rea with a Mage Spell, for example, stops the verse already in course?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...I think that silencing a Siren while she's in the middle of the Verse would stop it through sheer shock but a Siren would still have the ability to play Verses via instruments or rhythmic noises made by tapping on the walls. It would definitely be more difficult for her to do so, however. Perhaps it could be made easier through a Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788705#post788705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having literal and conceptual interpretations sounds good, but I feel like the symbolic ones might create overlap and make certain Opuses much more useful. Maybe apply a progressive dice penalty to them as they get less literal?<br /> As for the five dot thing, I feel like that's not as strictly clung to now- Werewolf dropped it for 2e too.. It might not fit, especially if Siren's alternate form is going to be built like a demon's. But that's just my onion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. The Opuses are the strongest when they are referred to literally and the meaning of the word slowly bleeds out as Sirens try to stretch the definition.<br /> <br /> The Alterations might work like how a Demon's form is. I think how they work is that Sirens buy Alterations that all go into her Aquatic form and the amount of Alterations is limited by her level of Akasha. Sirens can't necessarily reveal her Aquatic form at will; she only fully reveals it in all its glory when she treads water. She can, however, spend Pneuma to temporarily allow an Alteration to appear while she's on dry land. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788744#post788744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Sirens should still be able to use Verses even if she's Silenced, but her ability to actually carry it out is VERY much diminished. Perhaps this way of doing verses without making a sound is called &quot;Lip Syncing&quot;?<br /> <br /> Oh, as another thought, what if when Sirens use Verses and they do use sounds, then even deaf people can hear them? This is because Verses don't discriminate based on &quot;who can hear it&quot;, it affects anyone who can hear it. :3 Maybe it's also a thing for Siren Hunters/Fletchers. Some of them are deaf or keep an eye on deaf people to tell if Sirens are around.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lip-Syncing idea might work, but the name sounds like it is going to be rendered as something visual instead. Maybe the Siren is playing Acoustic or Instrumental?<br /> <br /> And the Fletchers sound interesting. Is there a quick snippet about who they are?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now that I think of it, how about we mix Freeze/Pause's effects into Calm? They're pretty much close to the same thing? </div> </div> </div>It could work. Maybe [Calm] allows Sirens to either gradually slow down something until it stops or temporarily stop it in a moment of time. Granted, the object would continue doing whatever it was doing after it is unpaused, but it would allow a temporarily immediate solution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Death-Travel could also make a dead body move to a location and Fate-Travel could also take successes from the future, but then the Siren would have to pay up on a later roll. </div> </div> </div>[Death][Travel] could work if we allow [Travel] to warp objects, but I'm kinda iffy on [Fate][Travel]. I presume that there could be a Condition that causes the Siren to gain a pool of Successes that, once used up, means that she needs to spend the same amount of Successes on her next immediate rolls. Is there a power from another Splat that allows them to do something like this?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sorry about asking on the 5 Dot hierarchy, still having trouble moving to GMC. &gt;&gt; </div> </div> </div>No problem. Most splats have a system and foundation that works for them so it would make sense to wonder if a 5-Dot system would work with <b><i>Siren</i></b>. Kinda why there's 5 &quot;normal&quot; Waters, 1 &quot;rogue&quot; Water, 5 &quot;normal&quot; Currents, and 5 Abyssal Currents. Most X-axes and Y-axes are based on 5s with some variation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T13:29:29-08:00","id":788943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788900#post788900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...I think that silencing a Siren while she's in the middle of the Verse would stop it through sheer shock but a Siren would still have the ability to play Verses via instruments or rhythmic noises made by tapping on the walls. It would definitely be more difficult for her to do so, however. Perhaps it could be made easier through a Merit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Lip-Syncing idea might work, but the name sounds like it is going to be rendered as something visual instead. Maybe the Siren is playing Acoustic or Instrumental?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And the Fletchers sound interesting. Is there a quick snippet about who they are?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How about &quot;rhythmic&quot;? Because you can make a Rhythm without music, but you can't make music without a Rhythm. Not to mention it gives loads more methods to play out Verses without needing to sing it out and thus make it easier for Sirens to do Verses in public without basically going &quot;I'm a Supernatural&quot; to the muggles.<br /> <br /> Ooh, another idea popped up. Fitting the Time theme, what if Sirens paid the cost of a Verse in advance and played it out, but instead of unleashing it at that moment, she holds it back until she desires to unleash it? This form of unleashing Verses could be called &quot;Rehearsal&quot;? This idea is mostly if the Rhythmic idea doesn't go through.<br /> <br /> Also I was mistaken. It's NOT Fletchers, the people who make arrows. It's Flensers, the people on whaling ships who cut off the blubber and put it into storage. Anyways, the ideas behind the Flensers were to be the &quot;Human Progress Should Not Be Stopped&quot; Extreme that Sirens face compared to Echidna's &quot;Primordial Ways And Survival Mean Everything&quot;. They're the human antagonists who don't believe at all in restraint of progress and that ambition for more power (that they do not understand) is a good thing. I remember you posting something on Sirens bodies being edible if kept on ice and being able to be used to live longer? I imagine as a point for these guys, they'd definitely do that. Perhaps even more grotesquely I imagine that <b>Lethe </b>Current Sirens would join them, they're all about wiping out the natural world afterall.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788900#post788900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could work. Maybe [Calm] allows Sirens to either gradually slow down something until it stops or temporarily stop it in a moment of time. Granted, the object would continue doing whatever it was doing after it is unpaused, but it would allow a temporarily immediate solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that, at least in the case of a Clash of Wills when Supernatural powers going against each other (which I can imagine Calm being the most invoked Conclusion for doing that), that if the Siren(s) using Calm would be able to cancel out the powers effect. More permanent things (like a Vampiric blood bond) would only be cancelled temporarily though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788900#post788900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Death][Travel] could work if we allow [Travel] to warp objects, but I'm kinda iffy on [Fate][Travel]. I presume that there could be a Condition that causes the Siren to gain a pool of Successes that, once used up, means that she needs to spend the same amount of Successes on her next immediate rolls. Is there a power from another Splat that allows them to do something like this?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Mage the Awakening 1e</b> Time 3: &quot;Borrow from the Future&quot; spell and <b>Princess the Hopeful's </b>Embassy to Fortune's Consul Privilege &quot;It Will Be&quot; and Ambassador Privilege &quot;It Must Be&quot;. A Link for the latter two.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/Embassy:Fortune\" target=\"_blank\">http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/Embassy:Fortune</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T15:48:29-08:00","id":788993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788943#post788943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about &quot;rhythmic&quot;? Because you can make a Rhythm without music, but you can't make music without a Rhythm. Not to mention it gives loads more methods to play out Verses without needing to sing it out and thus make it easier for Sirens to do Verses in public without basically going &quot;I'm a Supernatural&quot; to the muggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be very intriguing. I can think of a plot point where a rival Siren moonlights as a DJ and draws a crowd, gingerly influencing the listeners to make vast changes in their lives, some of which lead to unfortunate immediate events but are meant to push towards a unified, greater future.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ooh, another idea popped up. Fitting the Time theme, what if Sirens paid the cost of a Verse in advance and played it out, but instead of unleashing it at that moment, she holds it back until she desires to unleash it? This form of unleashing Verses could be called &quot;Rehearsal&quot;? This idea is mostly if the Rhythmic idea doesn't go through. </div> </div> </div>This is definitely worth exploring. If we have a codex with all the terminology, we should definitely give it a mention while we actually build all the mechanics that go into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I was mistaken. It's NOT Fletchers, the people who make arrows. It's Flensers, the people on whaling ships who cut off the blubber and put it into storage. Anyways, the ideas behind the Flensers were to be the &quot;Human Progress Should Not Be Stopped&quot; Extreme that Sirens face compared to Echidna's &quot;Primordial Ways And Survival Mean Everything&quot;. They're the human antagonists who don't believe at all in restraint of progress and that ambition for more power (that they do not understand) is a good thing. I remember you posting something on Sirens bodies being edible if kept on ice and being able to be used to live longer? I imagine as a point for these guys, they'd definitely do that. Perhaps even more grotesquely I imagine that <b>Lethe </b>Current Sirens would join them, they're all about wiping out the natural world afterall. </div> </div> </div>I can totally imaging the Flensers being humans who have lived beyond their natural life by systematically eating the flesh of Sirens and want to push for The Deluge because it would mean that more Sirens would Surface <i>(they probably don't know what The Deluge is but they probably have an understanding that &quot;terrible things = more Sirens = more Siren flesh = eternal life for me&quot;.)</i> They would definitely make for very threatening Antagonists who have their fingers in many pies. I also kinda feel that the Flensers have Sirens of Lethe as allies because A) Abyssal Sirens taste horrible and B) the Sirens of Lethe feel that if the fight is inevitable and humanity has control, they might as well being it sooner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would think that, at least in the case of a Clash of Wills when Supernatural powers going against each other (which I can imagine Calm being the most invoked Conclusion for doing that), that if the Siren(s) using Calm would be able to cancel out the powers effect. More permanent things (like a Vampiric blood bond) would only be cancelled temporarily though. </div> </div> </div>So Sirens have the ability to Counterspell? Jokes, but I think that the Verse that uses [Calm] would instead lessen the impact than outright cancelling. Maybe it would cancel things like Mind-Control or Illusions, but I feel that it would be able to cancel the effects after the effects go into play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mage the Awakening 1e</b> Time 3: &quot;Borrow from the Future&quot; spell and <b>Princess the Hopeful's </b>Embassy to Fortune's Consul Privilege &quot;It Will Be&quot; and Ambassador Privilege &quot;It Must Be&quot;. A Link for the latter two.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/Embassy:Fortune\" target=\"_blank\">http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/Embassy:Fortune</a> </div> </div> </div>Oh, neat. [Fate][Travel] would definitely be more akin to &quot;It Will Be&quot;.<br /> <br /> On a Side-Note: Echidna and the relationship between Beasts and Sirens. I'm bringing this up because Echidna, as of now, plays a pretty important part when it comes to the lore of the Sirens, as does the Dark Mother in the lore of the Beasts. Obviously, Beasts would find the Sirens to be kin, but I was doing some quick research about Echidna and discovered something <i>really</i> interesting.<br /> <br /> If you track the family line of the Greek Gods and Goddesses, you would eventually come to Echidna, the mother of monsters and one of the names for the Dark Mother who is the progenitor of all Beasts. However, the Greek poet Hesoid stated that Echidna was born from Ceto, the primordial personification of the ocean. Of Ceto's children, there are Echidna, the Gorgons, the sea monster Scylla, and all other sea monsters. This also includes the Sirens of mythology. <br /> <br /> This is all speculative lore that can be changed at any time, but here's what I think the relationship between the Beasts and the Sirens would be like:<br /> <br /> Beasts consider Sirens to be an offset of creatures born from the Dark Mother or even Makaras who have deviated so far along the path that they are their own creatures and not Beasts. Sirens, however, see themselves as creatures born from the primordial waters and that, some time ago, an ancient Siren known as Echidna performed an act so horrible that the primordial water rejected her kind. Because of this slight, Echidna took it upon herself to be a creature who could form life, much like the primordial water, as a mockery. The creatures she created are seen by Sirens to be pitiable creatures that, although they are the merging of mankind and nature, are perverse and should not be. Sirens that find themselves aligned wit the thinking of Echidna are known as Abyssal Sirens. Sirens also feel that most Beasts are just the creations of Echidna and look down upon them.<br /> <br /> Another Side-Note, would Echidna create chimeric creatures like the manticore or sphinx and just unleash it upon humanity? It would give Sirens another type of Antagonist beyond the Flensers and Abyssal Sirens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T16:17:03-08:00","id":789002,"title":"","content":"A few more general mechanical questions:<br /> <br /> \u200bDo a Siren has to continuously play a Verse to it be Active? I mean: Area + Weather + Water + Invoke would bring a Rain for as long as the Siren Sings?<br /> <br /> if yes: While a Siren Sings can she make other actions? While they Sings, can they fight? Or any action that is not Singing would stop the verse right away?<br /> <br /> I'm loving everything around here, especially the Flensers. Awesome. My work is taking my time, so I don't have time to actively write lots of things, but I'm Always around reading what you guys are creating.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T20:52:31-08:00","id":789100,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a complete list of Song Bits? At least, those so far?<br /> <br /> I kinda like [Madness] better than [Chaos], if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> I also kinda like Songs primarily requiring your voice. Maybe an Instrument merit that lets you play Songs through it rather than singing?<br /> <br /> It ties into an idea I had concerning [Area]: namely, it should affect anything able to hear you. At Akasha 1, it only extends to how far your voice can go naturally (which can be <i>quite far</i> in water with some Alterations); at higher dots it goes further, pierces soundproofing, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 12-19-2015, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T02:10:22-08:00","id":789167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789002#post789002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bDo a Siren has to continuously play a Verse to it be Active? I mean: Area + Weather + Water + Invoke would bring a Rain for as long as the Siren Sings?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Things like that might work better as extended roles, that need say, five successes, with the effect lasting a scene. I'm not sure how long each roll should represent, but werewolf uses this kind of system for the weather gifts and each roll is one minute.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It ties into an idea I had concerning [Area]: namely, it should affect anything able to hear you. At Akasha 1, it only extends to how far your voice can go naturally (which can be <i>quite far</i> in water with some Alterations); at higher dots it goes further, pierces soundproofing, etc, etc.</span><br /> </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> That sounds like a pretty cool idea. I was going to pitch an idea for Akasha affecting how far your voice carries but that sounds better, especially once you factor in alterations.<br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T11:51:48-08:00","id":789342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788993#post788993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be very intriguing. I can think of a plot point where a rival Siren moonlights as a DJ and draws a crowd, gingerly influencing the listeners to make vast changes in their lives, some of which lead to unfortunate immediate events but are meant to push towards a unified, greater future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Or an Abyssal Cheerleader drawing a crowd to go madly in love with her before she starts breaking each and every one of their hearts later to have sources of Pneuma to draw on at any time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788993#post788993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is definitely worth exploring. If we have a codex with all the terminology, we should definitely give it a mention while we actually build all the mechanics that go into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I present the Siren Lexicon. This is as much as I've gotten so far and I've made it so that people can comment on it if they wish. If I forgot anything, please feel free to point it out in the document. I also apologize if some of these aren't well documented or have weird descriptions, I've been working while having migranes and therefore wasn't thinking much. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aDfvgZKcEUyieGuDiAK5I7xE776xqjjlyW7GdrS_5i0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aDfvgZKcEUyieGuDiAK5I7xE776xqjjlyW7GdrS_5i0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aDfvgZKcEUyieGuDiAK5I7xE776xqjjlyW7GdrS_5i0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aDfvgZKcEUyieGuDiAK5I7xE776xqjjlyW7GdrS_5i0/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788993#post788993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can totally imaging the Flensers being humans who have lived beyond their natural life by systematically eating the flesh of Sirens and want to push for The Deluge because it would mean that more Sirens would Surface <i>(they probably don't know what The Deluge is but they probably have an understanding that &quot;terrible things = more Sirens = more Siren flesh = eternal life for me&quot;.)</i> They would definitely make for very threatening Antagonists who have their fingers in many pies. I also kinda feel that the Flensers have Sirens of Lethe as allies because A) Abyssal Sirens taste horrible and B) the Sirens of Lethe feel that if the fight is inevitable and humanity has control, they might as well being it sooner.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least the higher up Flensers, I don't think it'd be allowed to be common knowledge to Flensers. Or at least, the newly hired Flensers aren't allowed into the kitchens where the food is cooked. ;3<br /> Perhaps as another thing, I also imagine that if a person constantly relies on Siren flesh to survive for an unnatural lifespan, without it they quickly begin to age faster back to their original age if they haven't aged for over a LONG period of time. This is sort of like what happens to Ghouls when they're cut off from Vampire Vitae.<br /> <br /> As a random question, why would Abyssal Sirens taste awful? They're social splats and in physicality aren't that different from normal Sirens. Sirens that serve Echidna though? I'd bet they'd taste absolutely despicable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788993#post788993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Sirens have the ability to Counterspell? Jokes, but I think that the Verse that uses [Calm] would instead lessen the impact than outright cancelling. Maybe it would cancel things like Mind-Control or Illusions, but I feel that it would be able to cancel the effects after the effects go into play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, that's acceptable. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788993#post788993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a Side-Note: Echidna and the relationship between Beasts and Sirens. I'm bringing this up because Echidna, as of now, plays a pretty important part when it comes to the lore of the Sirens, as does the Dark Mother in the lore of the Beasts. Obviously, Beasts would find the Sirens to be kin, but I was doing some quick research about Echidna and discovered something <i>really</i> interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sort of figured that Beast would pop up sooner or later since they use Echidna as an official entity. We can change out Echidna if wanted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788993#post788993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you track the family line of the Greek Gods and Goddesses, you would eventually come to Echidna, the mother of monsters and one of the names for the Dark Mother who is the progenitor of all Beasts. However, the Greek poet Hesoid stated that Echidna was born from Ceto, the primordial personification of the ocean. Of Ceto's children, there are Echidna, the Gorgons, the sea monster Scylla, and all other sea monsters. This also includes the Sirens of mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh, I can smell a Siren backstory brewing up. :3 What if Ceto is the progenitor of the song/SIrens and gave her life to form the 5 Waters that aren't Discordia?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=788993#post788993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all speculative lore that can be changed at any time, but here's what I think the relationship between the Beasts and the Sirens would be like:<br /> <br /> Beasts consider Sirens to be an offset of creatures born from the Dark Mother or even Makaras who have deviated so far along the path that they are their own creatures and not Beasts. Sirens, however, see themselves as creatures born from the primordial waters and that, some time ago, an ancient Siren known as Echidna performed an act so horrible that the primordial water rejected her kind. Because of this slight, Echidna took it upon herself to be a creature who could form life, much like the primordial water, as a mockery. The creatures she created are seen by Sirens to be pitiable creatures that, although they are the merging of mankind and nature, are perverse and should not be. Sirens that find themselves aligned wit the thinking of Echidna are known as Abyssal Sirens. Sirens also feel that most Beasts are just the creations of Echidna and look down upon them.<br /> <br /> Another Side-Note, would Echidna create chimeric creatures like the manticore or sphinx and just unleash it upon humanity? It would give Sirens another type of Antagonist beyond the Flensers and Abyssal Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, I was going to say that Sirens at least should be about equally kin to Beasts as Werewolves and/or Vampires are. :3 I should note though that I know next to nothing on Beast other than the horrific amount of backlash that occurred when it first came out. <br /> <br /> Anyways, as for Echidna creating other monsters, I believe that Abyssal Sirens (not all are Allied to Echidna, but that can be a stereotype the normal currents hold on Abyssals), Echidna and her Sirens and Vodianoi, and Flensers provide enough antagonists for the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789002#post789002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few more general mechanical questions: \u200bDo a Siren has to continuously play a Verse to it be Active? I mean: Area + Weather + Water + Invoke would bring a Rain for as long as the Siren Sings?<br /> <br /> I'm loving everything around here, especially the Flensers. Awesome. My work is taking my time, so I don't have time to actively write lots of things, but I'm Always around reading what you guys are creating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say what Beauty said. Continued singing would be extended rolls and perhaps if she wanted an effect to last longer. And don't worry about work, any amount of contribution is appreciated. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789167#post789167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a pretty cool idea. I was going to pitch an idea for Akasha affecting how far your voice carries but that sounds better, especially once you factor in alterations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T12:59:21-08:00","id":789389,"title":"","content":"Are there concrete rules for rolls for Verses yet? I'm assuming that Acapella Verses use an Akasha + Attribute, but what about Stanzas? I feel like each current could have favoured abilities, but I forget how Mage did it-being able to pick any fitting ability might fit better.<br /> I'm also thinking about an xp cost for Stanzas equal to twice the number of factors in the Stanza- so [Introduction][Opus][Opus][Conclusion] would cost 8xp. Then again, going for just the factors might be better (so that would be 4xp). Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T14:44:07-08:00","id":789434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789389#post789389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there concrete rules for rolls for Verses yet? I'm assuming that Acapella Verses use an Akasha + Attribute, but what about Stanzas? I feel like each current could have favoured abilities, but I forget how Mage did it-being able to pick any fitting ability might fit better.<br /> I'm also thinking about an xp cost for Stanzas equal to twice the number of factors in the Stanza- so [Introduction][Opus][Opus][Conclusion] would cost 8xp. Then again, going for just the factors might be better (so that would be 4xp). Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest to concrete that we have so far are these things.<br /> <br /> Conclusions are attached to an Attribute's dots.<br /> <br /> Strength, Dexterity and Stamina: <b>Destroy, Travel and Protect </b>respectively.<br /> Intelligence, Wits and Resolve: <b>Sense, Transform and Restore</b> respectively.<br /> Presence, Manipulation and Composure: <b>Invoke, Control and Calm</b> respectively.<br /> <br /> <b>Disturb</b> is a special case in that it's addition to rolls is graded by Serenity - 10. <br /> <br /> So for example, if a Siren wanted to Travel to the Underworld, she could use &quot;Self-Death-Travel&quot; and roll Akasha + Dexterity for it when doing it A capella.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what to do for Stanzas, but I believe that it would be like casting a Mage Rote (Attribute + Skill + Akasha), although in this case the Attribute MUST be the attribute used by the Conclusion (So in this case Dexterity + Skill + Akasha) and the skill could perhaps be anything the Siren wanted it to be? For example, if &quot;Self-Death-Travel&quot; was to go to the underworld, then logically &quot;Occult&quot; would be a skill for that. If she wanted to use it to make a dead body move to a location, then it would perhaps be the &quot;Athletics&quot; skill being used instead. In short, depending on what the Siren wants to do with the Stanza would dictate what Skill she wanted to use.<br /> <br /> I don't know whether we should use the &quot;Rote skills&quot; that Mage uses. What do you all think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T15:52:02-08:00","id":789452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789434#post789434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what to do for Stanzas, but I believe that it would be like casting a Mage Rote (Attribute + Skill + Akasha), although in this case the Attribute MUST be the attribute used by the Conclusion (So in this case Dexterity + Skill + Akasha) and the skill could perhaps be anything the Siren wanted it to be? For example, if &quot;Self-Death-Travel&quot; was to go to the underworld, then logically &quot;Occult&quot; would be a skill for that. If she wanted to use it to make a dead body move to a location, then it would perhaps be the &quot;Athletics&quot; skill being used instead. In short, depending on what the Siren wants to do with the Stanza would dictate what Skill she wanted to use.<br /> <br /> I don't know whether we should use the &quot;Rote skills&quot; that Mage uses. What do you all think?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI like the Rotes Idea, it's a nice way to make a Siren write down a Stanza, which remenbers me:<br /> <br /> Does Stanzas need to have a physical representation, like a Musical Score? Can Sirens find Codified Stanzas of a long time ago like in the plot hook I suggested? If yes, what implications do this Codified physical representations have in a game?. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T16:00:31-08:00","id":789458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789100#post789100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a complete list of Song Bits? At least, those so far?<br /> <br /> I kinda like [Madness] better than [Chaos], if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, boy. By complete, I assume that you mean &quot;complete with each definition&quot;. I think we have a working list, at least. I'm gonna try to add definitions on the fly.<br /> <br /> <b>[Introductions]</b><br /> These parts of the Verses dictate what the Verse is targeting. <br /> <br /> <b>[Self]</b> targets the Siren's self and body while <b>[Object]</b> targets an inanimate object with a Size that is equal or less than the Siren's Size. Because this Introductions have a supremely limited scope on what they may affect, they add a <b>-1 Pneuma</b> modifier on the overall cost of the Verse<br /> <br /> <b>[Target] </b>targets a specific creature that is within the range of the Siren's Verse as determined by the value of her Akasha. This Introduction has a cost modifier of <b>+0 Pneuma</b> due to how subjective the Verse may be in affecting the Target. This Introduction will also be affected by Supernatural Tolerance if the [Target] is supernatural.<br /> <br /> <b>[Location]</b> targets a location with defined boundaries, such as a park lined with a fence or a piece of property. This Introduction has a cost modifier <b>+1 Pneuma</b> due to the fact that the Verse only affects the location itself, not the creatures within the location's boundaries.<br /> <br /> <b>[Area]</b> targets creatures with a location defined by the range of the Siren's Verse as determined by the value of her Akasha. This Introduction has a cost modifier of <b>+2 Pneuma</b> as it allows the Verse to become innately ingrained into a location for a set amount of time. When a creature enters the [Area], they are affected by the Verse as if the Siren targeted them using the [Target] Introduction.<br /> <br /> <b>[Global]</b> targets an area that extends beyond the feasible range of the Siren's Akasha but may still be considered a region, such as an entire city or the expanse of a river or even an underground cavern. Because of the nature, this Introduction has a cost modifier of <b>+4 Pneuma</b>; the sheer scale of this Introduction covers a great amount of targets,<br /> <br /> <b>[Opuses]</b><br /> Opuses are the elements that the Verse is attempting to affect or contact in context within the <b>[Introduction]</b>. Each type of Water provides selection of Favored Opuses that the Sirens of said Waters are able to obtain at a discount. Each Opus has a selection of interpretations that would affect what the Verse is capable of affecting in relation to the Opus. Literal interpretations of the Opus will allow the Verse to behave at its strongest and without question. Conceptual interpretations stretch the definition of the Opus but could be feasibly related to the literal interpretation. Opuses used as their conceptual interpretation provide a penalty to the Verse roll, as the Sirens are attempting to wrap the Verse around a stretch, kind of like creating a metaphor that could be taken in a different way. Symbolic interpretations relate to the connotative implications of the Opus rather than the denotative definition. Because some Opuses are based on elements that are not always corporeal, some of them would need to rely on a symbolic interpretation in order for the Verse to make sense. Like with conceptual interpretations, symbolic interpretations also provide a penalty to the Verse roll as the connotative implications of the Opuses may range depending on language or culture. <br /> <br /> Opuses may also be used in conjunction with one another to specify what element is being affected, sort of like a Venn Diagram that focuses on what overlaps. However, additional Opuses add <b>+1 Pneuma cost</b> for each additional Opus used beyond the first Opus.<br /> <br /> Of the Opuses that are not favored by any Waters, there is <b>[Water]</b> itself, <b>[Sound] </b>due to a Siren's connection with The Song, and <b>[Beauty]</b> due to the association between water spirits and attractiveness in most myths and folk tales.<br /> <br /> <b>The Water of Polaria </b><b>favors</b>:<b> [Darkness]</b> for shadows and the absence of light or even nightmares,<b> [Death] </b>for dead bodies and ghosts, and <b>[Freeze/Frost] </b>for things that are literally cold or are on &quot;cool-down&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>The Water of Tropicana favors </b>: <b>[Light]</b> for sunlight or light sources and fire, <b>[Passion]</b> for emotions and love, and <b>[Temper] </b>for things that are hot or are being heated up like a debate<br /> <br /> <b>The Water of Gardenia favors</b>: <b>[Earth]</b> for soil or stones and unrefined metals, <b>[Animal] </b>for creatures that aren't capable of free will, and <b>[Growth]</b> for vegetation or things that are capable of growing like mold or a movement<br /> <br /> <b>The Water of Vaporia favors</b>:<b> [Wind]</b> for air currents and breezes, <b>[Weather/Sky] </b>for things that are naturally occurring events like sandstorms or rain, and <b>[Pressure] </b>for air pressure or things that have a heavy metaphorical weight like decisions or guilt<br /> <br /> <b>The Water of Freshwater favors</b>:<b> [Human] </b>for mortals untouched by the supernatural, <b>[Technology]</b> for electronics or devices created out of refined metal such as cars, and <b>[Fate]</b> for fortune or things that are related to the idea of destiny<br /> <br /> <b>The Water of Discordia favors</b>: <b>[Blood]</b> as in blood or possibly even flesh, <b>[Taint] </b>for impurities or decay like rust or oil spills, and<b> [Chaos]</b> for junk piles or situations that can be described as chaotic<br /> <br /> <b>[Conclusions]</b><br /> Conclusions define to what extent the Siren is able to manipulate the chosen<b> [Opus]</b>. Each Current provides a Conclusion for the Siren to utilize. The Pneuma cost of each Conclusion varies depending on what the Conclusion is meant to do. The Conclusions also provide the other half of the Dice Pool for the Verse.<br /> <br /> <b>Conflict: [</b><b>Protect] (Stamina) </b>allows the Siren to preemptively <b>[Protect] </b>the chosen <b>[Opus]</b> from being affected by outside sources, keeping the<b> [Opus]</b> in the state that is was when the Siren sang the Verse. The protective capabilities of this Conclusion provides a <b>+2 Pneuma Cost</b>. <br /> <br /> <b>Healing: [</b><b>Restore] (Resolve) </b>allows the Siren to <b>[Restore]</b> the chosen<b> [Opus] </b>to a previous state in which the <b>[Opus]</b> was not damaged, polluted, or otherwise affected by outside sources. It may also refine or purify the chosen<b> [Opus]</b>. The ability to restore what was broken provides this Conclusion with a <b>+1 Pneuma cost.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Harmony: [</b><b>Calm] (Composure) </b>allows the Siren to gradually slow the chosen<b> [Opus] </b>until it comes to a rest. It may also temporarily stop the<b> [Opus]</b> for a duration before allowing it to continue. While the abilities of this Conclusion are predominantly for utility or defensive purposes, the ability to stop certain events means that this Conclusion provides a <b>+2 Pneuma cost.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Buoyancy:</b> <b>[</b><b>Travel] (Dexterity) </b>allows the Siren or whoever she targets to freely move through the chosen <b>[Opus]</b> as if it were water. In terms of using a Verse upon a <b>[Location]</b>, it connects instances of the<b> [Opus]</b> like portals within the <b>[Location]</b>. This Conclusion's abilities would provide a <b>+1 Pneuma cost.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom: [</b><b>Sense] (Intelligence) </b>allows the Siren to<b> [Sense]</b> an instance of her chosen <b>[Opus]</b> within the area she targets. The utility of this Conclusion and the lack of an offensive/defensive application means that it provides a <b>+0 Pneuma cost.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Acheron (Void):</b> <b>[</b><b>Disturb] (10-Serenity bonus to Verse Rolls) </b>allows the Siren to affect the chosen <b>[Opus] </b>by jostling its stability, causing it to react violently and chaotically. While this definition is vague, it allows for a variety of events to occur simply because of one chaotic event, providing a <b>+2 Pneuma cost. </b><br /> <br /> <b>Cocytus (Dark Wisdom): [</b><b>Transform] (Presence) </b>allows the Siren to change and manipulate the appearance of the chosen <b>[Opus]</b>. The components and aspects of the <b>[Opus] </b>become malleable and bend to the Siren's command like clay. The illusive nature of the Conclusion provides a <b>+1 Pneuma cost.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Lethe (Mankind's Victory):</b> <b>[</b><b>Control] (Manipulation) </b>allows the Siren to direct the chosen <b>[Opus]</b> and influence it on a localized level. The <b>[Opus] </b>moves under the Siren's commands and flow in a way that would defy logic. The range of command provides a <b>+3 Pneuma cost.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Phlegethon (Dark Passions):</b> <b>[</b><b>Invoke] (Wits)</b> allows the Siren to summon the chosen<b> [Opus]</b> into the area, even if it is not present or would logically not exist in the area. It is a Conclusion that causes things to appear at an instant and within the Siren's command, providing it a <b>+3 Pneuma cost</b>. <br /> <br /> <b>Styx (Primordial Darkness):</b> <b>[</b><b>Destroy] (Strength) </b>allows the Siren to command the destruction of the chosen <b>[Opus]</b>, causing utter devastation in its wake. The level of destruction does vary depending on the<b> [Introduction]</b> and<b> [Opus]</b> but it is a swift action, akin to a sudden revelation. The sheer power of this Conclusion provides a <b>+4 Pneuma cost.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789389#post789389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there concrete rules for rolls for Verses yet? I'm assuming that Acapella Verses use an Akasha + Attribute, but what about Stanzas? I feel like each current could have favoured abilities, but I forget how Mage did it-being able to pick any fitting ability might fit better.</div> </div> </div> </div>What SaulottheGentile said. Akasha + Attribute for A Capella Verses. For Stanzas, the Rote Skill would probably make sense, as Stanzas are memorized Verses that are meant to do a very specific action. I would also say that a Siren would be able to share the knowledge of a specific Stanza, so a written score would make sense. An in-person lesson from the Siren who created the Stanza would allow Sirens to understand with no trouble. The further down it goes through the grape vine, however, would degrade the quality of the Stanza until it becomes a forgotten melody that only few know and even fewer know how to perform properly. <br /> <br /> Now then, excuse me as I rest my hands after typing that brick of a response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T19:18:38-08:00","id":789567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789452#post789452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI like the Rotes Idea, it's a nice way to make a Siren write down a Stanza, which remenbers me:<br /> <br /> Does Stanzas need to have a physical representation, like a Musical Score? Can Sirens find Codified Stanzas of a long time ago like in the plot hook I suggested? If yes, what implications do this Codified physical representations have in a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, I see. That would be nice, it actually reminds me alot of the Zelda games where you learn a song from other people or off of walls and the like. <br /> <br /> This gives me an idea. The Song itself can be best understood as a language of music and it's written in stylized (and perhaps abit more complicated) musical notes. I don't know what it should be called, but <i>Basso Continuo </i>(a musical term that means the bass in the music continues going) or <i>Bel Canto </i>(&quot;Beautiful Voice&quot; in italian, fine singing used in operas from the 18th-19th century) sound like good words to name it. <br /> <br /> It would be a two dot merit (or however many dots Supernatural languages are supposed to be). One dot shows that you're fluent speaking wise and that you can say it (although there's almost no difference between &quot;speaking&quot; and &quot;singing&quot;). Sirens, Banshees, Breathless and Vodianoi can understand it even if they don't know the language, call it them remembering what the Song sounded like. To everyone else it simply sounds like pure singing that evokes awe, hopefulness or heartbreak (the song was sung by dying people afterall). The second dot in the merit is when the Siren is capable of writing the language, to which the way it's written out is in the form of extremely stylized musical score and notes. The best comparison I can give is that it could look like the Witch Runes of Octavia Von Seckendorff in Puella Magi Madoka Magica. VERY fitting because she's a Mermaid Witch. If you haven't watched the show but plan on doing so, DON'T look up Octavia or else you'll spoil yourself on it. Those who've watched it though already know what I mean).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.puella-magi.net/Deciphering_the_runes\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.puella-magi.net/thumb/4/41/Episode_15_doppels.jpg/250px-Episode_15_doppels.jpg?v=b81tq975z28k9j0qgcgbg02j07nm1mt\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.puella-magi.net/Deciphering_the_runes\" target=\"_blank\"> Witch Runes/Deciphering - Puella Magi Wiki </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.puella-magi.net/Deciphering_the_runes\" target=\"_blank\"> http://wiki.puella-magi.net/Deciphering_the_runes </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Look underneath &quot;Table of Runes&quot; and underneath the &quot;Musical&quot; ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789458#post789458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Snip on the Huge Post describing Verses</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be fine if to use this as writing for the section of the corebook describing verses? To note, in making this corebook, everyone whose contributed ideas will be credited for their hand in making this, including the people who've originated the ideas on the rpg.net forums.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789458#post789458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What SaulottheGentile said. Akasha + Attribute for A Capella Verses. For Stanzas, the Rote Skill would probably make sense, as Stanzas are memorized Verses that are meant to do a very specific action. I would also say that a Siren would be able to share the knowledge of a specific Stanza, so a written score would make sense. An in-person lesson from the Siren who created the Stanza would allow Sirens to understand with no trouble. The further down it goes through the grape vine, however, would degrade the quality of the Stanza until it becomes a forgotten melody that only few know and even fewer know how to perform properly.<br /> <br /> Now then, excuse me as I rest my hands after typing that brick of a response.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. How would these work for Stanza specialties?<br /> <br /> <b>Conflict: </b>Brawl, Firearms and Weaponry.<br /> <b>Buoyancy:</b> Expression, Subterfuge, Athletics.<br /> <b>Harmony:</b> Animal Ken, Persuasion and Socialize.<br /> <b>Healing: </b>Empathy, Medicine, and Survival.<br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>Academics, Investigation, Science<br /> <br /> <b>Acheron: </b> Intimidation, Survival, Stealth<br /> <b>Cocytus: </b>Occult, Crafts, Stealth<br /> <b>Lethe: </b>Politics, Computer, Drive<br /> <b>Phelegethon: </b>Persuasion, Empathy, Intimidation<br /> <b>Styx: </b>Animal Ken, Survival, Brawl","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T21:19:26-08:00","id":789600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789567#post789567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gives me an idea. The Song itself can be best understood as a language of music and it's written in stylized (and perhaps abit more complicated) musical notes. I don't know what it should be called, but <i>Basso Continuo </i>(a musical term that means the bass in the music continues going) or <i>Bel Canto </i>(&quot;Beautiful Voice&quot; in italian, fine singing used in operas from the 18th-19th century) sound like good words to name it.<br /> <br /> It would be a two dot merit (or however many dots Supernatural languages are supposed to be). One dot shows that you're fluent speaking wise and that you can say it (although there's almost no difference between &quot;speaking&quot; and &quot;singing&quot;). Sirens, Banshees, Breathless and Vodianoi can understand it even if they don't know the language, call it them remembering what the Song sounded like. To everyone else it simply sounds like pure singing that evokes awe, hopefulness or heartbreak (the song was sung by dying people afterall). The second dot in the merit is when the Siren is capable of writing the language, to which the way it's written out is in the form of extremely stylized musical score and notes. The best comparison I can give is that it could look like the Witch Runes of Octavia Von Seckendorff in Puella Magi Madoka Magica. VERY fitting because she's a Mermaid Witch. If you haven't watched the show but plan on doing so, DON'T look up Octavia or else you'll spoil yourself on it. Those who've watched it though already know what I mean).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.puella-magi.net/Deciphering_the_runes\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.puella-magi.net/thumb/4/41/Episode_15_doppels.jpg/250px-Episode_15_doppels.jpg?v=b81tq975z28k9j0qgcgbg02j07nm1mt\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.puella-magi.net/Deciphering_the_runes\" target=\"_blank\"> Witch Runes/Deciphering - Puella Magi Wiki </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wiki.puella-magi.net/Deciphering_the_runes\" target=\"_blank\"> http://wiki.puella-magi.net/Deciphering_the_runes </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Look underneath &quot;Table of Runes&quot; and underneath the &quot;Musical&quot; ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go for Bel Canto as it's pretty literal in what it's referring to.<br /> <br /> Also, it's interesting to see PMMM being brought up, at least in a more aesthetics-based reference. .<br /> <br /> In terms of magical languages, there's also the Old Tongue in <i>Fire Emblem: Path of Radiance</i> and <i>Fire Emblem: Radiant Dawn.</i> Visually, it's just really fancy calligraphy-style writing but it is the core to a lyrical form of magic called Galdrar which is used by a group of animal-people called Herons. Link below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://fireemblemwiki.org/wiki/Ancient_language\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.fireemblemwiki.org/4/4b/SS_fe09_leanne_speaking_ancient_language.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fireemblemwiki.org/wiki/Ancient_language\" target=\"_blank\"> Ancient language </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://fireemblemwiki.org/wiki/Ancient_language\" target=\"_blank\"> http://fireemblemwiki.org/wiki/Ancient_language </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Not to be confused with the Ancient Letters of Valentia and Ylisse or the Ancient Texts of Fates. The ancient language (Japanese: \u53e4\u4ee3\u8a9e ancient language), also known occasionally as the Old Tongue, is one of two languages native to the continent of Tellius as seen in Fire Emblem: Path of Radiance and... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it be fine if to use this as writing for the section of the corebook describing verses? To note, in making this corebook, everyone whose contributed ideas will be credited for their hand in making this, including the people who've originated the ideas on the rpg.net forums. </div> </div> </div>Feel free to add it. Keep in mind that it's still not entirely finished so eventually it needs to be approached again. Still, it should be enough for a proof of concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. How would these work for Stanza specialties?<br /> <br /> <b>Conflict: </b>Brawl, Firearms and Weaponry.<br /> <b>Buoyancy:</b> Expression, Subterfuge, Athletics.<br /> <b>Harmony:</b> Animal Ken, Persuasion and Socialize.<br /> <b>Healing: </b>Empathy, Medicine, and Survival.<br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>Academics, Investigation, Science<br /> <br /> <b>Acheron: </b> Intimidation, Survival, Stealth<br /> <b>Cocytus: </b>Occult, Crafts, Stealth<br /> <b>Lethe: </b>Politics, Computer, Drive<br /> <b>Phelegethon: </b>Persuasion, Empathy, Intimidation<br /> <b>Styx: </b>Animal Ken, Survival, Brawl </div> </div> </div>Hmm...I think we would have to actually go through each [Conclusion] and review what would work as specialties. By Currents, these sound fine, but putting them into the Conclusions sound rather off. While I get that the main 3 fighting skills would fit into the mindset of &quot;Conflict&quot;, I don't necessarily understand how they would amplify the [Protect] Conclusion that goes with it unless the [Protect] Conclusion also offers some sort of reflective damage. I feel that Survival would work better as one of the three skills because [Protect] seems to be more about keeping something from being harmed. Likewise, I feel that Brawl, Firearms, and Weaponry would work better for [Invoke] or [Destroy] as they are both more about some form of powerful demonstration that may be used for violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T22:41:58-08:00","id":789618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789600#post789600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...I think we would have to actually go through each [Conclusion] and review what would work as specialties. By Currents, these sound fine, but putting them into the Conclusions sound rather off. While I get that the main 3 fighting skills would fit into the mindset of &quot;Conflict&quot;, I don't necessarily understand how they would amplify the [Protect] Conclusion that goes with it unless the [Protect] Conclusion also offers some sort of reflective damage. I feel that Survival would work better as one of the three skills because [Protect] seems to be more about keeping something from being harmed. Likewise, I feel that Brawl, Firearms, and Weaponry would work better for [Invoke] or [Destroy] as they are both more about some form of powerful demonstration that may be used for violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was working more off of how they'd act duty wise rather than by how their Conclusion would fit in. Just in my own view, given that the Currents are Social Splats, them having a favored Conclusion doesn't necessarily mean that they'd get it as an innate power (if anything, Y-Splats are anything but innate). More that they'd favor it because they find the most use for it. It's kind of the same thing with the Stanza specialties I listed. Although I do see your point in how the Conclusion and Stanza specialties should fit together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T00:24:54-08:00","id":789637,"title":"","content":"I think that basing the Stanza skills on the Current and not the Conclusion might fit better if you consider that you can make a Stanza with Conclusions other than the one favoured by your Current. I do think that we should at least bear their conclusion in mind though.<br /> Also, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations</a>. I did my best, but I imagine that they might need to be balanced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","user":"SquamousBeauty","date":". 12-20-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T23:40:12-08:00","id":790121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789618#post789618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was working more off of how they'd act duty wise rather than by how their Conclusion would fit in. Just in my own view, given that the Currents are Social Splats, them having a favored Conclusion doesn't necessarily mean that they'd get it as an innate power (if anything, Y-Splats are anything but innate). More that they'd favor it because they find the most use for it. It's kind of the same thing with the Stanza specialties I listed. Although I do see your point in how the Conclusion and Stanza specialties should fit together.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789637#post789637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that basing the Stanza skills on the Current and not the Conclusion might fit better if you consider that you can make a Stanza with Conclusions other than the one favoured by your Current. I do think that we should at least bear their conclusion in mind though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the internal logic is that &quot;Sirens of a specific Current are more likely to use [These Skills] when codifying a Stanza&quot;, it would make sense for there to be a selection of skills for them. However, I think the way that Stanzas work would make it so that it is more necessary to apply a skill on a case-by-case basis. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations</a>. I did my best, but I imagine that they might need to be balanced </div> </div> </div>Neat. <br /> <br /> Camouflage and Anti-Freeze work pretty well, in my opinion, and they would make sense. I'm not familiar if there are actual rules for diving or water-based chronicles, but Pressure Resistance sounds like it could come in handy, although we should probably define &quot;pressure damage&quot;. Fur Pelt works, though I feel that it should reiterate that points the points in Armor also take away from Dexterity-based rolls. I think the only one that I find to be very awkward would be Tail Fluke. Does the Tail Fluke develop as a protrusion from the Siren's rear or does it cause her legs to merge into a whale's tail? Both have certain issues with them and I feel that those issues would be unavoidable.<br /> <br /> Let's keep those examples, but I feel that we need to approach how Alterations work. I assume that, technically, all Alterations can be used by a Siren at the same time but the number of Alterations a Siren may call upon is limited to the Siren's Akasha. So a Siren could have two Alterations that would technically affect the same body part simultaneously. For example, one Alteration allows a Siren to change her arm so that it resembles a Pistol Shrimp's claw. Another Alteration allows a Siren to develop venomous spines along her extremities like a Lion Fish. The Siren could have both Alterations active on her body and have spiny, venomous Pistol Shrimp claws. However, Alterations that are favored by Waters cannot be purchased by Sirens that are not from the Water, so a Tropican Siren cannot develop amphibious skin that Gardenian Sirens can. However, there is a pool of basic Alterations that any Siren may have.<br /> <br /> In contrast to the Verses that are at least somewhat subtle, Alterations are probably going to be utterly obvious and would probably reveal the nature of a Siren to mortals should they be able to see her. I assume there is something that allows Sirens to partially reveal her Alterations without alerting the Flensers about a Siren in the neighborhood. Like an illusion that makes it seem like the Siren isn't suddenly developing scales all over her body? It could be called Refraction <i>(the bending of light when it travels through water at an angle)</i> and allow a Siren to hide the true nature of her Alterations when she uses them out of water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T02:33:33-08:00","id":790167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Tail Fluke develop as a protrusion from the Siren's rear or does it cause her legs to merge into a whale's tail? Both have certain issues with them and I feel that those issues would be unavoidable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was definitely to have her legs to merge into a whale's tail. I was going to give each Water some sort of 'tail' option, with the default mer-tail being a Common Alteration. I was working with the assumption that Sirens were going to have a definitive 'other' form, like a demon. If it doesn't fit, I included an alternate option in the doc. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the number of Alterations a Siren may call upon is limited to the Siren's Akasha.</div> </div> </div> </div>I reckon that's a pretty good idea. The only thing I'm wondering about is if Siren's still have the 'aquatic' form with all their Alterations that was mentioned earlier. If not, that means the Common Alterations are gonna have to include to abilities I'd assumed would be folded into it.<br /> As for the Refractions, maybe have it as a roll when she manifests the Alteration to see if she can keep it hidden. Or, to take a leaf from Beast's book, maybe the practise of manifesting an Alteration is called Refraction. The practise could be similar to Atavisms- the Siren is drawing on her 'true form' or the truth of the Deluge or something similar, so even if it isn't visible it's still effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:44:16-08:00","id":790348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=789637#post789637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that basing the Stanza skills on the Current and not the Conclusion might fit better if you consider that you can make a Stanza with Conclusions other than the one favoured by your Current. I do think that we should at least bear their conclusion in mind though.<br /> Also, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations</a>. I did my best, but I imagine that they might need to be balanced</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed and me gusta! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I need to at least finish up Freshwater splat, I imagine a definite alteration for them would be that they're able to have humanoid legs (Think <a href=\"http://www.zeldadungeon.net/wiki/images/f/fd/Hyrule_Warriors_Artwork_Ruto_Zora_Scale.png\" target=\"_blank\">something like these legs</a>) that allows them to walk on land in their Aquatic Form, unlike most Sirens. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790121#post790121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the internal logic is that &quot;Sirens of a specific Current are more likely to use [These Skills] when codifying a Stanza&quot;, it would make sense for there to be a selection of skills for them. However, I think the way that Stanzas work would make it so that it is more necessary to apply a skill on a case-by-case basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. If it further helps, since the closest thing Stanzas can be compared to is mage Rotes, not all Order Specific Rotes use the skills that the Order uses. There's waaay too many examples to note of it, but they do exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790121#post790121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's keep those examples, but I feel that we need to approach how Alterations work. I assume that, technically, all Alterations can be used by a Siren at the same time but the number of Alterations a Siren may call upon is limited to the Siren's Akasha. So a Siren could have two Alterations that would technically affect the same body part simultaneously. For example, one Alteration allows a Siren to change her arm so that it resembles a Pistol Shrimp's claw. Another Alteration allows a Siren to develop venomous spines along her extremities like a Lion Fish. The Siren could have both Alterations active on her body and have spiny, venomous Pistol Shrimp claws. However, Alterations that are favored by Waters cannot be purchased by Sirens that are not from the Water, so a Tropican Siren cannot develop amphibious skin that Gardenian Sirens can. However, there is a pool of basic Alterations that any Siren may have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sirens can have a maximum amount of Alterations on herself equal to her Akasha + 3, and it costs 1 Pneuma per Alteration to manifest them on a Siren's Human form to which manifesting them is a reflexive action. They remain on during a Scene and cannot be removed unless the Siren goes into her Aquatic Form and back to normal or if she spends another point of Pneuma to make a single Alteration go away as a reflexive action. How does that sound?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790121#post790121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In contrast to the Verses that are at least somewhat subtle, Alterations are probably going to be utterly obvious and would probably reveal the nature of a Siren to mortals should they be able to see her. I assume there is something that allows Sirens to partially reveal her Alterations without alerting the Flensers about a Siren in the neighborhood. Like an illusion that makes it seem like the Siren isn't suddenly developing scales all over her body? It could be called Refraction <i>(the bending of light when it travels through water at an angle)</i> and allow a Siren to hide the true nature of her Alterations when she uses them out of water.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790167#post790167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reckon that's a pretty good idea. The only thing I'm wondering about is if Siren's still have the 'aquatic' form with all their Alterations that was mentioned earlier. If not, that means the Common Alterations are gonna have to include to abilities I'd assumed would be folded into it.<br /> As for the Refractions, maybe have it as a roll when she manifests the Alteration to see if she can keep it hidden. Or, to take a leaf from Beast's book, maybe the practise of manifesting an Alteration is called Refraction. The practise could be similar to Atavisms- the Siren is drawing on her 'true form' or the truth of the Deluge or something similar, so even if it isn't visible it's still effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is best, I'm sorry I can't really help in developing Refraction because I have no idea on Beast mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:29:06-08:00","id":790451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saulotthegentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sirens can have a maximum amount of Alterations on herself equal to her Akasha + 3, and it costs 1 Pneuma per Alteration to manifest them</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Akasha +3 might be too many- a low Akasha Siren might not even have very many Alterations, so the aquatic form become somewhat redundant. Akasha or Akasha +1 would seem to work better. On that, how many Alterations does a starting Siren get?<br /> As for Refraction, maybe allow a roll to allow people to notice the Sirens inhuman features when they're used, if only for a second. Like seeing the light glint off scales as she shrugs off a blow or the subtle flash of lamprey teeth as she smiles. I'm not sure if that's particularly practical though- any thoughts?<br /> On a side note, if anyone has any ideas or innate abilities of the aquatic form then now's the time, cause I'm aiming to get 7 common alterations done soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","user":"SquamousBeauty","date":". 12-21-2015, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:42:31-08:00","id":790460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790348#post790348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed and me gusta! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I need to at least finish up Freshwater splat, I imagine a definite alteration for them would be that they're able to have humanoid legs (Think <a href=\"http://www.zeldadungeon.net/wiki/images/f/fd/Hyrule_Warriors_Artwork_Ruto_Zora_Scale.png\" target=\"_blank\">something like these legs</a>) that allows them to walk on land in their Aquatic Form, unlike most Sirens.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe some amphibious legs, <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/f5/c7/71/f5c771e9255bf83d62b04bddbface5e0.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">like this</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T14:40:31-08:00","id":790499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790460#post790460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe some amphibious legs, <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/f5/c7/71/f5c771e9255bf83d62b04bddbface5e0.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">like this</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both? Inclusivity for Sirens. On a serious note, the particular aesthetics of an Alteration should always be flexible, much like Beast's atavisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T17:15:06-08:00","id":790570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790451#post790451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Akasha +3 might be too many- a low Akasha Siren might not even have very many Alterations, so the aquatic form become somewhat redundant. Akasha or Akasha +1 would seem to work better. On that, how many Alterations does a starting Siren get?<br /> As for Refraction, maybe allow a roll to allow people to notice the Sirens inhuman features when they're used, if only for a second. Like seeing the light glint off scales as she shrugs off a blow or the subtle flash of lamprey teeth as she smiles. I'm not sure if that's particularly practical though- any thoughts?<br /> On a side note, if anyone has any ideas or innate abilities of the aquatic form then now's the time, cause I'm aiming to get 7 common alterations done soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be a good idea to look at <b><i>Demon's </i></b>Demonic Form, considering that most of the mechanics would work similarly. Effectively, a Siren's Aquatic Form is akin to the <b><i>Demon's</i></b> Demonic Form in that it allows them to use all of their Alterations. However, a Siren can partially transform her body and only use some of her Alterations. For Demons, they have Modifications, Technologies, Propulsions, and Processes. They gain a fixed number when they are created and gradually develop more once they hit a certain amount of Primum. They may also lose and gain an amount of abilities when they gain Primum.<br /> <br /> However, most to all of the Siren's Alterations are passive with some allowing the Siren to perform special actions tied into her Alterations, like an ink pouch that allows the Siren to fire out smoky clouds of ink into the air. In this instance, the Alterations are more like <b><i>Beast's </i></b>Atavisms as they are something that is fundamental to the Siren. I feel that the main difference is that while supernatural creatures can see a glimpse of the Beast's true form when they activate their Atavism, the Siren's true form is only present when she becomes submerged in water. Another difference is that while a Beast's Atavisms are free action-based abilities that are free to use unless the Beast wants to enhance them using their Satiety, a Siren's Alterations are ingrained trait-based abilities that she may awaken with her Pneuma and keep awakened for a period of time.<br /> <br /> However, the longer a Siren has her Alteration active, the weaker the Refraction that protects the Siren from being exposed grows. A few minutes of having her Alteration up is no issue; allowing her Alteration to last for hours causes her true nature to rise up every now and then, with scales causing her skin to reflect in the sun or her teeth sharpening to that of piranhas. I would say that every scene beyond the scene the Siren activates her Alteration necessitates a roll by the Siren to keep a hold of the Refraction effect, with a penalty per scene equal to the amount of Alteration the Siren has active and allowing the penalty to be cumulative and gradually growing the longer the Siren has the Alterations active.<br /> <br /> As for what her Aquatic Form allows the Siren to have, the most-obvious abilities would be to have the Siren breathe underwater and swim, possibly at twice her Speed. She would also have all her Alterations active and able to be used. The Siren's vulnerability to losing limbs also disappears; while the Siren is in her Aquatic Form, her limbs do not dissolve into sea foam. If the Siren loses a body part while she is in her Aquatic Form, she may retrieve her limb and attempt to reattach it as long as the Siren and her limb are in the same body of water; if her limb is thrown onto land, the Siren may attempt to bring it back into the water. The internal logic is that, because the Siren is connected to The Deluge and the waters of time, the Aquatic Form prevents the limb from dissolving by halting time for the limb and turning time back to the moment when the limb was removed. However, if the limb dissolves into sea foam or if the Siren leaves the water and regresses into her human form, the limb will not attach without actual medical assistance. Effectively, the Siren's Aquatic Form is in-and-of-itself an Alteration that is only awakened when the Siren is submerged in water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T18:29:21-08:00","id":790607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790570#post790570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would be a good idea to look at <b><i>Demon's </i></b>Demonic Form, considering that most of the mechanics would work similarly. Effectively, a Siren's Aquatic Form is akin to the <b><i>Demon's</i></b> Demonic Form in that it allows them to use all of their Alterations. However, a Siren can partially transform her body and only use some of her Alterations. For Demons, they have Modifications, Technologies, Propulsions, and Processes. They gain a fixed number when they are created and gradually develop more once they hit a certain amount of Primum. They may also lose and gain an amount of abilities when they gain Primum.<br /> <br /> However, most to all of the Siren's Alterations are passive with some allowing the Siren to perform special actions tied into her Alterations, like an ink pouch that allows the Siren to fire out smoky clouds of ink into the air. In this instance, the Alterations are more like <b><i>Beast's </i></b>Atavisms as they are something that is fundamental to the Siren. I feel that the main difference is that while supernatural creatures can see a glimpse of the Beast's true form when they activate their Atavism, the Siren's true form is only present when she becomes submerged in water. Another difference is that while a Beast's Atavisms are free action-based abilities that are free to use unless the Beast wants to enhance them using their Satiety, a Siren's Alterations are ingrained trait-based abilities that she may awaken with her Pneuma and keep awakened for a period of time.<br /> <br /> However, the longer a Siren has her Alteration active, the weaker the Refraction that protects the Siren from being exposed grows. A few minutes of having her Alteration up is no issue; allowing her Alteration to last for hours causes her true nature to rise up every now and then, with scales causing her skin to reflect in the sun or her teeth sharpening to that of piranhas. I would say that every scene beyond the scene the Siren activates her Alteration necessitates a roll by the Siren to keep a hold of the Refraction effect, with a penalty per scene equal to the amount of Alteration the Siren has active and allowing the penalty to be cumulative and gradually growing the longer the Siren has the Alterations active.<br /> <br /> As for what her Aquatic Form allows the Siren to have, the most-obvious abilities would be to have the Siren breathe underwater and swim, possibly at twice her Speed. She would also have all her Alterations active and able to be used. The Siren's vulnerability to losing limbs also disappears; while the Siren is in her Aquatic Form, her limbs do not dissolve into sea foam. If the Siren loses a body part while she is in her Aquatic Form, she may retrieve her limb and attempt to reattach it as long as the Siren and her limb are in the same body of water; if her limb is thrown onto land, the Siren may attempt to bring it back into the water. The internal logic is that, because the Siren is connected to The Deluge and the waters of time, the Aquatic Form prevents the limb from dissolving by halting time for the limb and turning time back to the moment when the limb was removed. However, if the limb dissolves into sea foam or if the Siren leaves the water and regresses into her human form, the limb will not attach without actual medical assistance. Effectively, the Siren's Aquatic Form is in-and-of-itself an Alteration that is only awakened when the Siren is submerged in water.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bSeconded. Also, How to enter Deluge? with the whole body submerged in water? If you're in a familiar Water, you receive bonuses?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790499#post790499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both? Inclusivity for Sirens. On a serious note, the particular aesthetics of an Alteration should always be flexible, much like Beast's atavisms.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bNIce work on the Alterations! My Ideas for more common traits would be:<br /> <br /> <b>Focal Lenses </b>(Fish can change the viewing distance in water, much like changing Focus on a c\u00e2mera or zooming in or out),<br /> <br /> <b>Chemoreceptors Nostrils </b>(You know that a shark smell blood from very far, right? The Chemoreceptors Nostrils may be the cause of such Smelly Ability)<br /> <br /> <b>Lateral Line </b>(A mix of Hearing and Touching, is like feeling your surrounding through vibration. This is very similar to the way we hear, and that is why the lateral line system is said to be a cross between hearing and touch. Some ichthyologists teach that the lateral line gives fishes the sense of \u201cdistant touch.\u201d Schooling fishes rely on this sense for their near-instantaneous, synchronized movement. The organs that comprise the lateral line system run along the length of a fish\u2019s body.),<br /> <br /> <b>Eletricalperception </b>\u200b(It's a way that Sharks, Rays and such have to sense when a heart beats. They sense the eletrical field that the muscle produces when beating or contracts) <br /> <br /> Those are common Senses of fish and sharks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T19:17:16-08:00","id":790631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790607#post790607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSeconded. Also, How to enter Deluge? with the whole body submerged in water? If you're in a familiar Water, you receive bonuses?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deluge is a water-based apocalypse that is going to occur in the next few years, decades, centuries, etc. This event awakens the Sirens, who are the remnants of humanity that have been swept up by The Deluge and survived by swimming up to the Surface. Realizing that this disaster was, in at least some sense, preventable if humanity itself had done differently. This allowed them to transcend time and return to what is considered to be present time and live in an alternate life. Of course, this means that Sirens were created several years before The Deluge could occur, so they are attempting to preemptively prevent it by altering events. When a Siren uses her powers in the form of Verses or Alterations, she is attempting to connect to The Deluge on a mental level, calling upon a further reincarnation of themselves and tapping into the Verses and Alterations their future selves know and have. <br /> <br /> When a Siren goes into her Aquatic Form by submerging herself, she is tapping into what her future incarnation appears to be. The process of submerging her body is relatively simple; as long as a reasonably large portion of her body is covered in some form of water, she may transform into her Aquatic Form. This can go anywhere from bathing in a bathtub, taking a shower, skinny-dipping in a lake, standing out during the rain, taking a mud-bath, or going into a steamy sauna. Considering that this is rather inconvenient at some times, a Siren may spend a point of Pneuma to prevent her transformation within that form of water. If the Siren spends time in a hot sauna and goes into a pool after, she would have to spend two points of Pneuma to prevent the sauna and the pool, one at each moment.<br /> <br /> When a Siren submerges herself within her favorite Water and transforms into her Aquatic Form, she regains a substantial amount of Pneuma back; the quality of the water reminds her of her time within The Deluge and reminds her of the fight for survival. The Siren doesn't need to spend Pneuma to prevent her transformation in her favorite Water, but she needs to allow herself to transform if she wants to regain Pneuma. If a Siren chooses to not transform immediately, she may later transform if she wants to at will. This transformation will allow the Siren to regain Pneuma if it is her favorite Water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T08:59:36-08:00","id":790872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This allowed them to transcend time and return to what is considered to be present time and live in an alternate life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was operating under the assumption that modern day people became Sirens- is that not the idea? I'd assumed that they became Sirens due to some sort of literal/metaphorical 'drowning' that exposed them to the Deluge. On another note, the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations Doc</a> now has common Alterations for you to critique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:14:38-08:00","id":790905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790872#post790872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was operating under the assumption that modern day people became Sirens- is that not the idea? I'd assumed that they became Sirens due to some sort of literal/metaphorical 'drowning' that exposed them to the Deluge. On another note, the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations Doc</a> now has common Alterations for you to critique.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's...complicated. Basically, when someone in the present starts to suffer from &quot;drowning&quot;, they see a glimpse of The Deluge in the future. However, because The Deluge is so far away in terms of time, the person who is drowning isn't necessarily seeing The Deluge through their own eyes as the person they currently are; they are seeing The Deluge as their reincarnated future self who is literally drowning in the future-time. When their future self escapes from The Deluge by reaching the surface, the person in the present time stops feeling like they've drowned and awaken as a Siren. Basically, wibbly-wobbly, timey-wimey stuff.<br /> <br /> As for Alterations, I like that Weaponry is part of the general Alterations and can be chosen twice. Boneless sounds very neat to have, especially on a Siren who has the Small-Framed and Double Jointed Merit. Pressure Sense, Drowned Beauty, and Thalassic Movement are all fairly interesting takes for Sirens, though I feel that Thalassic Movement is more of an upgrade to the Aquatic Form than as an Alteration. If it is more of an upgrade, it would be pretty interesting as it would mean that some Sirens may choose to only use their Alterations if it allows them to improve their Aquatic Form. Whalesong, I like though I feel that I should ask whether the communication is vocal or telepathic or can only be heard by the person the Siren is communicating to. Shark's Scent is interesting but it would make having a Verse that could [Sense][Blood] redundant. However, it fits really well as an Alteration and we could alter how the [Blood] Opus works, but I also feel that we could fold in Shark's Scent with Pressure Sense. I'll leave the decision up to you since you created the power. With Venomous, I feel that there should be a section that says that the Alteration synergizes with the Weaponry Alteration or another Alteration that allows the Siren to produce a layer of slime like a hagfish. A Siren can just take Venomous by itself, but having Venomous and allowing the venom to seep into her claws from Weaponry would allow interesting possible combinations. The new Alteration for Polaria, Baleen's Weight, is definitely something that I would look into as a Polarian Siren.<br /> <br /> As a Side-Note, would having animal inspirations per Alteration be feasible? Like, at the bottom of the Boneless Alteration, can there be a snippet that says &quot;Inspirations: Octopus, Squid, Cuttlefish&quot; and have that running under the Alterations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:36:21-08:00","id":790917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whalesong, I like though I feel that I should ask whether the communication is vocal or telepathic or can only be heard by the person the Siren is communicating to</div> </div> </div> </div>It's vocal, the idea was that it would be a literal song. I'll clarify it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also feel that we could fold in Shark's Scent with Pressure Sense</div> </div> </div> </div>They're both really based on Sharks anyway, so I'll add their conglomerate into the doc for you all to judge.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Venomous, I feel that there should be a section that says that the Alteration synergizes with the Weaponry Alteration or another Alteration that allows the Siren to produce a layer of slime like a hagfish</div> </div> </div> </div> I was going to put a slime Alteration into Tropicana or Gardenian, so I'll cross reference them when I'm done with them. I'll add the Weaponry thing in.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Side-Note, would having animal inspirations per Alteration be feasible</div> </div> </div> </div>I shall do that now. Everything there was animal inspired anyways so it won't be hard. And Yads, I included a few of your suggestions- thanks for the help!<br /> The timey wimey stuff is good- thanks for clarifying.<br /> EDIT: Lamian Senses and inspirations are now finished","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","user":"SquamousBeauty","date":". 12-22-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:21:52-08:00","id":790989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790917#post790917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's vocal, the idea was that it would be a literal song. I'll clarify it.<br /> <br /> They're both really based on Sharks anyway, so I'll add their conglomerate into the doc for you all to judge.<br /> I was going to put a slime Alteration into Tropicana or Gardenian, so I'll cross reference them when I'm done with them. I'll add the Weaponry thing in.<br /> <br /> I shall do that now. Everything there was animal inspired anyways so it won't be hard. And Yads, I included a few of your suggestions- thanks for the help!<br /> The timey wimey stuff is good- thanks for clarifying.<br /> EDIT: Lamian Senses and inspirations are now finished</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the contributions. With the slime Alteration, I think it might better work in Gardenia if we pick up on things like frogs, salamanders, and mudskippers, which all are covered in a layer of mucus.<br /> <br /> As another Side-Note directed for the entire thread, we might want to talk about the relationship between Sirens and Leviathans, considering that there are a lot of things that are quasi-mirrored between the two. Granted, most of this is coming from the TvTropes page for Leviathan, but it does have some issues with us.<br /> <br /> One thing is that the Marduk Society is being manipulated in order to allow their leaders to eat the flesh of the Leviathans to gain immortality, which is the modus operandi of the Flensers in Siren. The second is that Leviathans apparently have the ability to time travel in the revised version, The Cult Chronicles. Granted, it's apparently through a selection of powers and Sirens aren't necessarily time-travelers themselves, but there is a slight aspect of time that is shared between the two. Thirdly is the Primordial Waters and The Deluge. Both are at opposing ends of time, with the Primordial Waters being in the beginning and The Deluge being at the end. However, the Primordial Waters involve Tiamat, the mother of all things. The Deluge involves either Ceto or Echidna, the mother of sea creatures. Unfortunately, I'm on a time crunch so I won't be able to respond immediately due to being away from internet access, but I will see if I can read up on Leviathan and the 2nd Edition to understand what is similar and different between the two fansplats. Hopefully, <b><i>Siren</i></b> doesn't have too much that overlaps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:58:26-08:00","id":791021,"title":"","content":"I've been somewhat following Leviathan 2e. I don't feel like there's a lot of overlap in terms of themes, now that leviathan's shifted so much focus on cults. I know that there's aesthetic overlap but it's no more than, say, the overlap between Beast and Werewolf. The whole flesh eating thing isn't too bad now that the Marduk Society have diversified goals and aren't the only antagonists. If it's a concern, I think we could diversify out the Flensers- they're gonna need fleshed out at some point anyways. It might actually be better to leave the Deluge/Primordial Waters thing vague so that storyhooks can come from it. Once you add Beast and the Makara in, you get grounds for real crossover territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:26:15-08:00","id":791043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=790989#post790989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the contributions. With the slime Alteration, I think it might better work in Gardenia if we pick up on things like frogs, salamanders, and mudskippers, which all are covered in a layer of mucus.<br /> <br /> As another Side-Note directed for the entire thread, we might want to talk about the relationship between Sirens and Leviathans, considering that there are a lot of things that are quasi-mirrored between the two. Granted, most of this is coming from the TvTropes page for Leviathan, but it does have some issues with us.<br /> <br /> One thing is that the Marduk Society is being manipulated in order to allow their leaders to eat the flesh of the Leviathans to gain immortality, which is the modus operandi of the Flensers in Siren. The second is that Leviathans apparently have the ability to time travel in the revised version, The Cult Chronicles. Granted, it's apparently through a selection of powers and Sirens aren't necessarily time-travelers themselves, but there is a slight aspect of time that is shared between the two. Thirdly is the Primordial Waters and The Deluge. Both are at opposing ends of time, with the Primordial Waters being in the beginning and The Deluge being at the end. However, the Primordial Waters involve Tiamat, the mother of all things. The Deluge involves either Ceto or Echidna, the mother of sea creatures. Unfortunately, I'm on a time crunch so I won't be able to respond immediately due to being away from internet access, but I will see if I can read up on Leviathan and the 2nd Edition to understand what is similar and different between the two fansplats. Hopefully, <b><i>Siren</i></b> doesn't have too much that overlaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good contributions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Speaking of the Water Specific Alterations, I got master sloth away and got the Freshwater Sirens finished.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I haven't read up much on Leviathan, but I do know that Siren and Leviathan have very different themes and that works for me. Squamous says it best when it comes to the Flensers and Marduk Society. As for the Deluge and the Primordial Waters, I would say that the difference of &quot;End&quot; and &quot;Beginning&quot; that they seem to respectively have is also shared in the progenitor. Echidna &quot;corrupts&quot; (it's very important to note this, because she doesn't create. Not really) for the purpose of a race to survive the apocalypse. I don't know at all on Tiamat.<br /> <br /> I would say as a distinction, Ceto is the proper Siren progenitor (heck, we could even say that the Song is literally her lifeblood which the Sirens partake of when they Surface) that gave her life so that everything else had a chance to survive. Echidna, perhaps one of the first Sirens who arose to the song and perhaps the last &quot;human&quot; to die from the Deluge, went completely mad with all the death around her that arose her obsession to create a race to survive the apocalypse. I would say that this perhaps showcases the negative parts of Sirens being drawn to humanity being shown in Echidna as well, except that Echidna applies to ALL of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T16:21:30-08:00","id":791141,"title":"","content":"One problem I have so far with the deluge is how it's described as an inevitable future somehow which leaves much of the same problem as Gehenna had in VtM. I also find the whole time travel stuff nonsensical in all frankness but I think that should come with a grain of salt as I have a subjective preference for some sort of multiverse or alternate history as opposed to taking the future and going to the past with it due to a feeling that it can never be accurate due to the unknown factor. At any rate, would it not make more sense to work on the notion that while the Deluge COULD drown the world if something goes awry somehow somewhere, that it isn't a guaranteed WILL that requires time travel and timeline fuckery to avoid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T16:56:30-08:00","id":791155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791021#post791021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been somewhat following Leviathan 2e. I don't feel like there's a lot of overlap in terms of themes, now that leviathan's shifted so much focus on cults. I know that there's aesthetic overlap but it's no more than, say, the overlap between Beast and Werewolf. The whole flesh eating thing isn't too bad now that the Marduk Society have diversified goals and aren't the only antagonists. If it's a concern, I think we could diversify out the Flensers- they're gonna need fleshed out at some point anyways. It might actually be better to leave the Deluge/Primordial Waters thing vague so that storyhooks can come from it. Once you add Beast and the Makara in, you get grounds for real crossover territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791043#post791043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read up much on Leviathan, but I do know that Siren and Leviathan have very different themes and that works for me. Squamous says it best when it comes to the Flensers and Marduk Society. As for the Deluge and the Primordial Waters, I would say that the difference of &quot;End&quot; and &quot;Beginning&quot; that they seem to respectively have is also shared in the progenitor. Echidna &quot;corrupts&quot; (it's very important to note this, because she doesn't create. Not really) for the purpose of a race to survive the apocalypse. I don't know at all on Tiamat.<br /> <br /> I would say as a distinction, Ceto is the proper Siren progenitor (heck, we could even say that the Song is literally her lifeblood which the Sirens partake of when they Surface) that gave her life so that everything else had a chance to survive. Echidna, perhaps one of the first Sirens who arose to the song and perhaps the last &quot;human&quot; to die from the Deluge, went completely mad with all the death around her that arose her obsession to create a race to survive the apocalypse. I would say that this perhaps showcases the negative parts of Sirens being drawn to humanity being shown in Echidna as well, except that Echidna applies to ALL of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Okay. I did know that the two splats were significantly different in their themes. For me, I see more of a difference now.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Flensers, I think that they have different manners of dealing with Sirens based on their basis of operations. Japanese Flensers ended up harvesting a Siren in her Aquatic Form and managed to use her various parts as remedies, preserving and crushing the bones into a powder that could heal broken bones or the small amounts of fat were incorporated into a rejuvenating beauty soap. Dutch and English Flensers would harvest Sirens for their flesh for a more nourishing and immediate experience. Some Flensers even take it upon themselves to research Sirens in order to discover the secrets of life and longevity. However, the obsession towards finding a Siren grows in each and every one of them like a poison with every Siren they take. Their mindset falls under a &quot;Ends Justify the Means&quot;, as their desire to create a better quality of life comes at the expense of the future, as their push towards callous treatment of the environment causes more Sirens to arise, allowing the Flensers more prey. It's a vicious cycle, like an addiction or a consuming obsession. For Sirens, an encounter with a Flenser is a warning to keep from getting too close to humanity.<br /> <br /> Are Flensers, in terms of mechanics, Hunters or are they the Siren-equivalent of Heroes? If they are Hunters, I would presume that Sirens would have an incredibly shaky relationship with anyone who makes it their purpose to hunt down the supernatural, even those that cause Sirens difficulty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of the Water Specific Alterations, I got master sloth away and got the Freshwater Sirens finished.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a> </div> </div> </div>Sweet awesomeness. :V So I assume that for the rest of the Waters, Tropicana is now the Ocean of Growth, Gardenia is the Ocean of Preservation, and Discordia is the Ocean of Might? Is there a working subtitle for Vaporia, like the Ocean of Contact as Vaporians are focused on reaching out to mortals and leaving their life as soon as they can?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791141#post791141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem I have so far with the deluge is how it's described as an inevitable future somehow which leaves much of the same problem as Gehenna had in VtM. I also find the whole time travel stuff nonsensical in all frankness but I think that should come with a grain of salt as I have a subjective preference for some sort of multiverse or alternate history as opposed to taking the future and going to the past with it due to a feeling that it can never be accurate due to the unknown factor. At any rate, would it not make more sense to work on the notion that while the Deluge COULD drown the world if something goes awry somehow somewhere, that it isn't a guaranteed WILL that requires time travel and timeline fuckery to avoid?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with V:tM or Gehenna, so I can't exactly make a decision on that. A cursory look using TvTropes says that it's an apocalypse-situation where ancient Vampires kill their descendants and then destroy the world and that it is the overarching metaplot within V:tM.<br /> <br /> Oh. OH.<br /> <br /> Um...I think the purpose of having The Deluge be a Thing with a capital T is to give Sirens a reason to be all timey-wimey and exist in a period and have something that they &quot;Do&quot;. Werewolves have a &quot;Spirit-y Thing&quot; because of Father Wolf and Mother Luna and such. Sin-Eaters have a &quot;Death/Ghost-y Thing&quot; because of the Geists and the Underworld. Sirens have a &quot;Time-y/ and Event Causing/Preventing Thing&quot; because of The Deluge and Echidna and Ceto and...<br /> <br /> Overarchingly, let's say this: The Deluge is occurring in the Past, Present, and Future all simultaneously. It is a period of time that should not be, but is. Think <i>Chrono Trigger/Chrono Cross </i>and the End of Time/Dead Sea. It was an apocalypse that drowned humanity. In one existence. In a separate instance of the world, someone in the Chronicles of Darkness existence suffered from an experience that would be described as &quot;drowning&quot;, whether it is due to misery or due to a physical drowning. These two moments entwine as the Siren surfaces from The Deluge and lives through her &quot;drowning&quot; experience. The people from the CofD existence now know of the experience of The Deluge and understand that there is something &quot;big&quot; that is going to occur and that it'll pull people down with it, like The Deluge. The issue is that the people, now Sirens, don't know what this &quot;big&quot; deal is. It could be a horrible nuclear winter that covers the entire planet in radiation. It could be a sudden takeover by a hostile, sentient species of kudzu overgrowing and covering the planet. It could even be another great flood on the level of the actual Deluge. They know that something is coming and that they need to either A) prepare for it, B) delay its arrival, and/or C) prevent it by searching for issues in this world and pushing it towards nondestructive solutions. The Siren's existence is one of a harbinger of destruction attempting to stop it before it is too late.<br /> <br /> Because The Deluge was a conflict between humanity and nature where nature took back what humanity had stolen, Sirens of this world know that it is some issue involving civilization and the wild. They are acting as mediators, quietly allowing humanity to progress while allowing the cycle of the world to go undisturbed. However, The Deluge's life-destroying effect awakened a Siren known as Echidna early on. Echidna is taking it upon itself to create a species made from a mishmash of parts in order to survive The Deluge when it occurs on this side, horrid creatures known as the Vodianoi that are a mockery of life. The existence of the Sirens themselves have brought in Flensers, hungry immortals who dare nature to give them its best shot as they feast on the live-prolonging flesh of the Sirens. And there are the Abyssal Sirens who have given up on this world and are attempting to accelerate the process.<br /> <br /> I will say that time-travel itself is not an actual part of Siren; it was only really meant to bring Sirens into the world. Sirens themselves cannot time-travel. If anything, Sirens are more of oracles; individuals that know of the future and what it holds but do not know what leads into it and are attempting to stop something that is bigger than themselves. Basically, Homura from <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica </i>who only gets one chance and doesn't know how to prevent things from happening.<br /> <br /> Oh dear, I've gone cross-eyed. Hopefully, this would clear up some things. If not, feel free to dig it apart and give your criticisms. This is a fansplat and it does need work to make it as good as it can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":". 12-22-2015, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:01:45-08:00","id":791248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791155#post791155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Flensers, in terms of mechanics, Hunters or are they the Siren-equivalent of Heroes? If they are Hunters, I would presume that Sirens would have an incredibly shaky relationship with anyone who makes it their purpose to hunt down the supernatural, even those that cause Sirens difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that they're more akin to Hunters, abit MUCH more specialized with Sirens. And yes, I would say they would have a really shaky relationship with hunters. I would say at least on the same level that Vampires have problems with Hunters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791155#post791155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sweet awesomeness. :V So I assume that for the rest of the Waters, Tropicana is now the Ocean of Growth, Gardenia is the Ocean of Preservation, and Discordia is the Ocean of Might? Is there a working subtitle for Vaporia, like the Ocean of Contact as Vaporians are focused on reaching out to mortals and leaving their life as soon as they can?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. If nothing else I'm using them as a bases (their descriptions at least) for the Waters. As for Vaporia, the Ocean of Contact sounds nice, it actually makes me think abit to the Little Mermaid. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791155#post791155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Snip</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is as best as it gets. I have an idea actually, what if Ceto is to Sirens as Luna is to Werewolves? This is purely for comparison in the terms of &quot;these are the patrons of the supernatural splat who bless them with power&quot;? Perhaps abit interestingly enough, Luna is noted to be mood swinging and chaotic to depict the moon changing phases. Similarly, I can see Ceto in sort of the same light. She represents water as a whole and water is known for fitting in different forms into things, flowing through everything, and one day the waters might look calm but the next the sea is stormy and violent. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T00:15:12-08:00","id":791395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791248#post791248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that they're more akin to Hunters, abit MUCH more specialized with Sirens. And yes, I would say they would have a really shaky relationship with hunters. I would say at least on the same level that Vampires have problems with Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely see Flensers being specialized, but I could also see them hunting other supernaturals in their off-periods. They might go after Sin-Eaters in search for ectoplasm or after Mummies to harvest parts for other uses. Sort of a mixture of Cheiron, the Ascending Ones, and the Faithful of Shulpae with a Union/Night Watch mentality of sustaining their little bubble. As long as the Flensers are able to get the job done and support their locale, they'd be happy to do it again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is as best as it gets. I have an idea actually, what if Ceto is to Sirens as Luna is to Werewolves? This is purely for comparison in the terms of &quot;these are the patrons of the supernatural splat who bless them with power&quot;? Perhaps abit interestingly enough, Luna is noted to be mood swinging and chaotic to depict the moon changing phases. Similarly, I can see Ceto in sort of the same light. She represents water as a whole and water is known for fitting in different forms into things, flowing through everything, and one day the waters might look calm but the next the sea is stormy and violent. :3 </div> </div> </div>I would hold onto this idea for now. I wouldn't necessarily go as far as describing Ceto as a &quot;patron&quot; that granted Sirens their power, but I would say that Ceto is at least responsible for bringing the Sirens into the world and allowing them to enter the world that exists parallel to The Deluge.<br /> <br /> So, Serenity and Anchors. I want to say immediately that I feel like Sirens should not have split Touchstones that Werewolves do. A Siren's Serenity is something that allows her to face the world every day, despite knowing the looming danger that approaches with every misstep and mistake. A Siren's Serenity is something that grants the Siren clear judgment as a mediator between worlds. A Siren's Serenity is a calm that lulls before a mighty storm of judgment. Serenity is similar to Integrity in that both are used to determine mental stability and the ability to cope with a situation. However, while Integrity measures a mortal's state of mind when it comes to their self and their own person, a Siren's Serenity measures her state of mind when it comes to her own actions in the world around her. A Siren knows of the dangers that hang precariously over the world. She knows of the strained relationship next door that will lead to a suicide. She knows of the hungry earth that threatens to take the lives of mischievous trespassers. She knows of the deal that will pave the land in concrete and tip the scales of balance towards humanity. When a Siren is able to cope with these events, averting them by pushing others into action or accepting them as necessary events, she demonstrates the strength of her Serenity. When a Siren is unable to understand these events, failing to avert them, directly intervening, or accepting them as inevitable endings, she demonstrates weakness in her Serenity.<br /> <br /> The three main questions that define how an event affects a Siren goes as such:<br /> <br /> <b>Why is this event worrisome in the grand scheme? </b>Not all events need to be investigated. While helping children look for their missing pet is something that is nice to do, what would happen if the Siren were to fail? Are the consequences of the event occurring in some way dangerous or destructive? Will it lead to catastrophe or minor nuisance? When Sirens cannot look at a situation with a calm mind and factor in what aspects would cause a domino effect, they are showing a deep disconnect between their thought pattern and the world. Preventing a child's death is a great service to the world and the well-being of their family. Preventing a child from catching a cold is just plain outrageous. Sirens need to know what is important in the world and not worry about every unnecessary aspect. This question appeals to Logos, the logic behind the situation.<br /> <br /> <b>What is the most just way to handle this event? </b>Whenever a Siren intervenes by directing the pieces, they must know in what way it should be handled. When a debate is raised against two opposing sides, is it correct to agree with one side or the other? Do both sides have arguments that are valid? Do both sides have arguments that are invalid? Should emotions and alliances come into play? Is it right to split a reward evenly based on individuals or based on the level of work contributed? Is the destruction of a machine a justifiable means of stopping a forceful takeover? Should murder be considered if the situation calls for drastic measures? Sirens need to understand the gravity of a situation and whether or not it allows for certain judgments. This question appeals to Pathos, the emotion surrounding the situation.<br /> <br /> <b>What is my right to judge this event?</b> Not all events need a Siren to step in. When a family gets into a dispute over lifestyles, is it correct for the Siren to intervene? If the situation involves the Siren herself on one side of the argument, is she able to give an unbiased judgment? Is she able to if she isn't in the argument but naturally feels a certain way? Is she the best person to be an impartial judge? Will her experiences and emotions prevent her from acting correctly? Is there someone with more right than her to judge? Should Sirens be able to judge situations that directly involve her? Sirens need to realize their place in the world and figure out what their position as a mediator means. This question appeals to Ethos, the credibility that lends itself to the situation.<br /> <br /> Granted, there are several Breaking Points that may occur for a Siren at each different level of Serenity, but they all revolve around these three questions. Failing to resolve an issue might not affect a Siren at <b>Serenity 7</b> as they are willing to accept losses, but a Siren at <b>Serenity 10</b> would freak out as the failure breaks the Siren's composure. Similarly, choosing to knowingly kill a mortal for the sake of a better future may shake a Siren at <b>Serenity 4</b>, but it would take the murder of a mortal for the sake of regaining Pneuma to shock a Siren at <b>Serenity 2</b>. If a Siren has her Touchstone, a person, place, or object that reminds her of her duties and her necessity to remain calm, she gains a bonus to her breaking rolls. <br /> <br /> The Siren's position as a mediator is also defined by her <b>Sea </b>and <b>Shore</b>. A Siren's <b>Sea</b> is the persona she takes on when she has a moment to herself. It is something that ebbs and flows in her heart, allowing her to rest and be who she wants to be. It is an archetype that she allows herself to become lost in. A Siren's <b>Shore</b> is the persona she takes on when she needs to interact with the world. It is the meeting point where she sees others at their best, their worst, and whatever lies in between. It is an archetype that she puts on in order to blend with society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T21:31:18-08:00","id":791963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791395#post791395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I definitely see Flensers being specialized, but I could also see them hunting other supernaturals in their off-periods. They might go after Sin-Eaters in search for ectoplasm or after Mummies to harvest parts for other uses. Sort of a mixture of Cheiron, the Ascending Ones, and the Faithful of Shulpae with a Union/Night Watch mentality of sustaining their little bubble. As long as the Flensers are able to get the job done and support their locale, they'd be happy to do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can also imagine them going after Vampires for their blood to remain young. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791395#post791395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hold onto this idea for now. I wouldn't necessarily go as far as describing Ceto as a &quot;patron&quot; that granted Sirens their power, but I would say that Ceto is at least responsible for bringing the Sirens into the world and allowing them to enter the world that exists parallel to The Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=791395#post791395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip on Serenity</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks good. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T23:16:05-08:00","id":792005,"title":"","content":"Here's another snippet; this time, it's about the Frenzy/Death Rage equivalent of Sirens, <i><b>Dissonance.</b></i><br /> <br /> While not everything goes as planned, there are certain expectations that are held in the world. Leaves fall from trees, the weather changes every now and then, and people live their lives every day. For a Siren, a creature who spends most of her day making sure that schemes go through without much difficulty, meeting expectations is a priority. Matchmaking is expected to go off without a hitch, meetings are civil periods of discussion and debate, and everything coexists in peace. Life is meant to be as harmonious as it can.<br /> <br /> When life isn't harmonious, a Siren's mind cannot accept it.<br /> <br /> Sirens can accept failure as something that occurs naturally; not everything works out. However, when something has managed to reach a point where it is virtually impossible to fail, it triggers something in a Siren. <i>This is impossible. This cannot be. This is unacceptable.</i> A lover suddenly rejecting the Siren's affections after months of adoration, the death of a touchstone in a freak-accident that was only due to bad fortune, these fail to meet expectations. <i>Love is meant to be forever. People are meant to die in a peaceful manner.</i> This mental shutdown, this momentary denial of reality is known as <i><b>Dissonance</b></i>; the Siren's expectations of the world do not align with the reality of the world.<br /> <br /> Depending on the strength of a Siren's character, Dissonance may go smoothly. On the other hand, Dissonance could cause a terrible fate to fall. A Siren must make a Resolve + Composure roll to maintain her calm and accept reality as it is. The most immediate effect is an overwhelming feeling of loss and disappointment that holds the Siren down. It is not as severe as the panic and sorrow that almost claimed the Siren in The Deluge, but it is something that is as consuming. Effectively, the Siren is suffering from Soul Loss; the Siren has become detached from reality and is attempting to reaffirm her position in the world. The Siren is affected by the <b>Shallow End Condition</b>. Similar to the persistent Soulless Condition, the Shallow End Condition prevents the Siren from regaining Willpower naturally through sleep. However, the Shallow End Condition also causes the Siren's Sea and Shore to invert; the Siren feels that the only way to reestablish her reality is to bring an aspect of her free will into the civilized world and to incorporate the facets of her humanity into her true self. This can have disastrous effects on the Siren's life, as a Siren with, say, an outlook on the world as an Enforcer but exists in her personal time as a Wild Card, plays with the people she knows in her everyday life as some sort of mischievous spirit and becomes a stone-heart judge in her personal sanctum. Acts that benefit her Sea or Shore during this period will only restore one point of Willpower even if it comes at a great risk as the Siren cannot fully enjoy her Sea and Shore when they are complete out of the Siren's normal behavior.<br /> <br /> If a Siren is able to understand her position by gaining a point in Serenity, losing a point in Serenity, or a achieving an exceptional success on a breaking point for Serenity, she snaps out of her stupor and resolves the Shallow End Condition, releasing herself of her Dissonance. A Siren eventually breaks out of the Shallow End Condition after a set amount of time, depending on her Akasha. Sirens with low Akasha take longer to break out of her condition as her sense of time is closer-related to the flow of time in reality. Sirens with high Akasha accelerate the process as their sense of time is compounded by the timey-wimey mess of The Deluge. However, naturally breaking out of the Shallow End Condition isn't a good thing; rather, the Siren comes to the conclusion that her moment of suffering and panic meant nothing in the grand scheme of things. When a Siren resolves the Shallow End Condition by waiting it out, she begins to hear someone calling out to her. In her mind, the Siren feels as if she is hearing the Song once again, calling her to desire life and to live without fear. The voice itself is different, however. It no longer has notes of sorrow or bitterness. The words don't feel as if they are heralding the joy of life or the sweet taste of fresh air. It sounds more perfect, as if the singer has found complete clarity. The voice is does not fail in any means of the word. It just expresses pure understanding.<br /> <br /> It is the voice of Echidna, speaking to the Siren.<br /> <br /> Sirens who have resolved the Shallow End Condition through waiting it out receive the <b>Deep End Condition</b>. Sirens with this condition are still affected by their Dissonance with reality. However, while the Shallow End Condition affected the Siren's view of herself, the Deep End Condition affects the Siren's view of others. In this moment, the Siren is filled with a bitterness that grants her a mad insight. She sees the world around her not as clay waiting to be molded but as a chipped vase that has been completely ruined. At this moment, a Siren considers her Touchstones to be worthless, effecting her breaking point rolls as if she had no Touchstones. The Siren is also filled with a corrosive sense of envy against the world. <i>How dare humanity be so content with their failings when it is bringing the world down. Do they not know the true meaning of their actions? How can nature rest peacefully when it struggles to even survive the progress of humanity? How pointless!</i> The voice of Echidna whispers in the Siren's mind and directs them to find something that the Siren disagrees with. The saccharine smile of the girl in the other apartment. The students that pass by the forest and carve their initials into the trees. The untouched field that blooms every spring. These idealistic fonts that exist as if to mock the Siren's attempts to ward off the dangers that will come by defiantly enjoying the peace. The Siren becomes ill with malcontent as Echidna's voice encourages the Siren to defile these naive remnants of innocence. It is something the Siren <i>must</i> do to regain sense of reality. When a Siren effectively destroys or defiles the target of Echidna's encouragements, she may resolve the Deep End Condition and release herself of her Dissonance. However, the moment the Siren comes to her senses, she suffers from a breaking point as she realizes in full sobriety the consequences of her actions.<br /> <br /> By spending Willpower, a Siren may attempt to fight against Echidna's influence by rolling Composure + Resove vs. the Siren's Akasha. Sirens with a high Akasha hear Echidna's whispers in full force as it echoes in her mind for what seems to be eternity amplified by her connection to the timelessness of The Deluge. Success allows the Siren to resolve the Deep End Condition without having to suffer a breaking point. Exposure to the Siren's Touchstones also allows the Siren to fight against Echidna's influences without spending Willpower; however, the Siren may only attempt to fight the effects once per Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Granted, Dissonance only truly affects Sirens who follow the normal Currents, as those Sirens have not been fully influenced by Echidna. When it comes to Abyssal Sirens, who have fallen for Echidna's teachings, how does Dissonance affect them?<br /> <br /> In short, Abyssal Sirens are in a period of perpetual Dissonance. Make of that as you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":". 12-24-2015, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T03:29:27-08:00","id":792081,"title":"","content":"So...a late night cursory look at other fansplats reveals that &quot;Serenity&quot; as an Integrity stat is used by <b><i>Dragon: the Inheritance.</i></b> It even uses Dissonance as a thing, though that is more to refer to breaking points, like a Vampire's degeneration.<br /> <br /> It's definitely just a wording thing and we could choose to keep our terms. I just like having some streamlined uniqueness in these traits. Any takers on renaming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T04:47:10-08:00","id":792096,"title":"","content":"Damn; I liked it. Hurmm... Tranquillity and Turbulence?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Turmoil might also work.<br /> <br /> As a quick look at Greek since Sirens I find this:<br /> Turbulence = Tarach\u00ed (\u03a4\u03b1\u03c1\u03b1\u03c7\u03ae)<br /> Tranquillity = Irem\u00eda (\u0397\u03c1\u03b5\u03bc\u03af\u03b1)<br /> Opinions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7060,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","user":"Karavolos","date":". 12-24-2015, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T08:25:42-08:00","id":792189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792005#post792005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, Dissonance only truly affects Sirens who follow the normal Currents, as those Sirens have not been fully influenced by Echidna. When it comes to Abyssal Sirens, who have fallen for Echidna's teachings, how does Dissonance affect them?<br /> <br /> In short, Abyssal Sirens are in a period of perpetual Dissonance. Make of that as you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the whole dissonance thing. I'm sorry to be that person (especially because I've noted this two-three times by now), but the difference between Normal Current Sirens and Abyssal Current Sirens is about the same amount of difference between Changeling Courts. Purely Philosophical. I'm all for having Echidna's Sirens to be in perpetual dissonance, but Abyssal Sirens?<br /> <br /> Would Echidna want to wipe away nature like Mankind's Victory promises? Would Echidna want to destroy civilization like Primordial Darkness espouses? No, because those actions speed up the Deluge happening. What Echidna would want is more time to perfect her eugenics practices and actually make a new race out of humanity. In other words, she'd benefit more if the Sirens actually did their job, giving her more time to kidnap people, change them and experiment on them (perhaps this is good for an added dose of horror). But to make it absolutely clear from how I see it, Abyssal Sirens and Echidnal Sirens are different from each other. <br /> <br /> Abyssal Sirens are the type who tread on their philosophies based on Serenity. It has those who are tired of keeping up a balancing act of man and nature (<b>Styx, </b><b>Lethe </b>and <b>Acheron </b>respectively) and those who deal in dubious methods but ultimately get shit done when called on (<b>Cocytus </b>and <b>Phelegethon</b>). Ironically, I could see Echidna sending a Vodianoi or two against Abyssal Sirens because they aren't doing their part and giving her more time to make that new race.<br /> <br /> Echidnal Sirens are in a whole branch of their own. They're amongst the Sirens who believe the world is already doomed. They're amongst the Sirens who are willing to go against Serenity to force their goals to work (and thus Echidnal Sirens can be amongst the most monsterous ones, inside and out). They join with Echidna because they want her monstrous powers for themselves, because they want her monstrous troops to use as they desire, or because they truly believe in her cause, that the world is already doomed and that it's best to make a new race to survive.. Regardless, while Abyssal Sirens can work with Current Sirens on a good day, the Echidnal Sirens are, though understandable, uncompromisingly evil in their efforts. I'm sorry if I'm sounding bad in this paragraph, I just want to make it absolutely clear.<br /> <br /> As for the Serenity rename, I don't mind sharing if the original authors of Dragon the Inheritance don't mind the same. However, if it's required, my only suggestion is &quot;Balance&quot;.I like Kara's suggestions too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T13:48:21-08:00","id":792349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792189#post792189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the whole dissonance thing. I'm sorry to be that person (especially because I've noted this two-three times by now), but the difference between Normal Current Sirens and Abyssal Current Sirens is about the same amount of difference between Changeling Courts. Purely Philosophical. I'm all for having Echidna's Sirens to be in perpetual dissonance, but Abyssal Sirens?<br /> <br /> Would Echidna want to wipe away nature like Mankind's Victory promises? Would Echidna want to destroy civilization like Primordial Darkness espouses? No, because those actions speed up the Deluge happening. What Echidna would want is more time to perfect her eugenics practices and actually make a new race out of humanity. In other words, she'd benefit more if the Sirens actually did their job, giving her more time to kidnap people, change them and experiment on them (perhaps this is good for an added dose of horror). But to make it absolutely clear from how I see it, Abyssal Sirens and Echidnal Sirens are different from each other.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Sirens are the type who tread on their philosophies based on Serenity. It has those who are tired of keeping up a balancing act of man and nature (<b>Styx, </b><b>Lethe </b>and <b>Acheron </b>respectively) and those who deal in dubious methods but ultimately get shit done when called on (<b>Cocytus </b>and <b>Phelegethon</b>). Ironically, I could see Echidna sending a Vodianoi or two against Abyssal Sirens because they aren't doing their part and giving her more time to make that new race.<br /> <br /> Echidnal Sirens are in a whole branch of their own. They're amongst the Sirens who believe the world is already doomed. They're amongst the Sirens who are willing to go against Serenity to force their goals to work (and thus Echidnal Sirens can be amongst the most monsterous ones, inside and out). They join with Echidna because they want her monstrous powers for themselves, because they want her monstrous troops to use as they desire, or because they truly believe in her cause, that the world is already doomed and that it's best to make a new race to survive.. Regardless, while Abyssal Sirens can work with Current Sirens on a good day, the Echidnal Sirens are, though understandable, uncompromisingly evil in their efforts. I'm sorry if I'm sounding bad in this paragraph, I just want to make it absolutely clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh. Okay. I didn't know that Abyssal Sirens and Echidnal Sirens were actually separate entities. So there are three factions of Sirens then, Sirens that follow normal Current and are attempting to stop another Deluge for the sake of the world, Sirens that follow Abyssal Currents and are either indifferent to The Deluge or are using underhanded tactics for The Deluge for their own sake, and Sirens that follow Echidna and have given up on humanity completely. <br /> <br /> And don't feel bad about having to point things out or explain things. Some people, such as myself, make assumptions that would be entirely wrong. Now I know the difference in the Currents and will be able to actually improve where my ideas go for Sirens. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Serenity rename, I don't mind sharing if the original authors of Dragon the Inheritance don't mind the same. However, if it's required, my only suggestion is &quot;Balance&quot;.I like Kara's suggestions too. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792096#post792096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn; I liked it. Hurmm... Tranquillity and Turbulence?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Turmoil might also work.<br /> <br /> As a quick look at Greek since Sirens I find this:<br /> Turbulence = Tarach\u00ed (\u03a4\u03b1\u03c1\u03b1\u03c7\u03ae)<br /> Tranquillity = Irem\u00eda (\u0397\u03c1\u03b5\u03bc\u03af\u03b1)<br /> Opinions?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be entirely honest, I feel that naming things entirely in Greek or Latin is kinda cheesy. Not that I'm putting down the suggestions. It's just that we have the term &quot;<b>Akasha</b>&quot;, which is a Hindi word that refers to, &quot;a supposed universal etheric field in which a record of past events is imprinted.&quot; Granted, Sirens themselves are Greek, but we have extended the term &quot;Siren&quot; to refer to mermaids, nixies, river spirits, rusalkas, selkies, and such. We could also incorporate Nagas from Hindu/Buddhist mythology. Despite the fact that they are serpent-people, technically, they are sometimes depicted as water-based, like the nagas in Warcraft who run the gamut of mutations, which could inspire how Alterations are seen.<br /> <br /> For my push of Hindi/Sanskrit terms, <b>Pneuma</b>, which refers to &quot;breath&quot; or &quot;soul, could be changed to &quot;<b>Prana</b>&quot;, which literally means &quot;breath of life&quot; or &quot;essence of life-force&quot;. <b>Serenity</b>, the trait that gives Sirens calmness, could be worked into &quot;<b>Dharma</b>&quot;, which refers to righteousness in actions, such as duty, law, behavior that is &quot;morally&quot; correct. Like Serenity, it could also be the source of a Siren's calmness in her own actions. As for <b>Dissonance</b>, I myself am torn between calling it &quot;<b>Klesha</b>&quot;, a mental state that poisons the mind with negative emotions like anxiety, envy, and depression, or basing it on a musical term like &quot;<b>Cacophony</b>&quot;, though I feel that Cacophony is being used for the Verses.<br /> <br /> As for why else I feel like pushing for a Hindi/Sanskrit-based terminology, the working lore has Sirens from a different existence surviving The Deluge of their world and coming to existence in a parallel world where an event like The Deluge is coming. The Siren then feels that her duty to this world is to prevent this event from occurring by pushing things in the world towards coexistence or preemptively stopping things before they happen. The lore has a &quot;rebirth&quot; bend to it and a &quot;karma&quot;-like way of approaching the world by attempting to do good things to ensure a good future.It even has a &quot;Samsara&quot; aspect as Sirens are in a, as far as they know, second cycle where things will reoccur unless something changes. <br /> <br /> Still, these are my suggestions. It may give the game a slight religious bent that might clash or make people feel awkward or it could be taking from a culture too much or whatever. Hopefully, we can have a discussion about this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:46:34-08:00","id":792548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792349#post792349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be entirely honest, I feel that naming things entirely in Greek or Latin is kinda cheesy. Not that I'm putting down the suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you were I say no problems, we all have our opinions and views on things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792349#post792349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just that we have the term &quot;<b>Akasha</b>&quot;, which is a Hindi word that refers to, &quot;a supposed universal etheric field in which a record of past events is imprinted.&quot; Granted, Sirens themselves are Greek, but we have extended the term &quot;Siren&quot; to refer to mermaids, nixies, river spirits, rusalkas, selkies, and such. We could also incorporate Nagas from Hindu/Buddhist mythology. Despite the fact that they are serpent-people, technically, they are sometimes depicted as water-based, like the nagas in Warcraft who run the gamut of mutations, which could inspire how Alterations are seen.<br /> <br /> For my push of Hindi/Sanskrit terms, <b>Pneuma</b>, which refers to &quot;breath&quot; or &quot;soul, could be changed to &quot;<b>Prana</b>&quot;, which literally means &quot;breath of life&quot; or &quot;essence of life-force&quot;. <b>Serenity</b>, the trait that gives Sirens calmness, could be worked into &quot;<b>Dharma</b>&quot;, which refers to righteousness in actions, such as duty, law, behavior that is &quot;morally&quot; correct. Like Serenity, it could also be the source of a Siren's calmness in her own actions. As for <b>Dissonance</b>, I myself am torn between calling it &quot;<b>Klesha</b>&quot;, a mental state that poisons the mind with negative emotions like anxiety, envy, and depression, or basing it on a musical term like &quot;<b>Cacophony</b>&quot;, though I feel that Cacophony is being used for the Verses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is where I raise a small eyebrow. As a side note I've not paid close attention to the game and mostly read off-handedly or as it comes onto topic when me and Saulot chat, but you note that naming things in Greek or Latin is cheesy and then turn right around and push for Hindi words left and right by the looks of it? Doesn't it cause the same problem from a different angle?<br /> <br /> As for the actual names, I'm voting to keep &quot;Akasha&quot; and I like &quot;Klesha&quot; for dissonance. Pneuma should be kept I feel as it sounds a little better to me than &quot;Prana&quot; and Dharma in my opinion doesn't sound too good in comparison to Iremia. Why not mix-match?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792349#post792349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why else I feel like pushing for a Hindi/Sanskrit-based terminology, the working lore has Sirens from a different existence surviving The Deluge of their world and coming to existence in a parallel world where an event like The Deluge is coming. The Siren then feels that her duty to this world is to prevent this event from occurring by pushing things in the world towards coexistence or preemptively stopping things before they happen. The lore has a &quot;rebirth&quot; bend to it and a &quot;karma&quot;-like way of approaching the world by attempting to do good things to ensure a good future.It even has a &quot;Samsara&quot; aspect as Sirens are in a, as far as they know, second cycle where things will reoccur unless something changes.<br /> <br /> Still, these are my suggestions. It may give the game a slight religious bent that might clash or make people feel awkward or it could be taking from a culture too much or whatever. Hopefully, we can have a discussion about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to say I see where you're coming from and can even support it. However as Sirens/Mermaid myths pretty much exist everywhere I vote that while we could use Hindi as the main influence, we should have a tidbit of other cultures, most notably the Greek and Celtic ones; maybe some Japanese too. Opinion?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T00:17:38-08:00","id":792641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792548#post792548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is where I raise a small eyebrow. As a side note I've not paid close attention to the game and mostly read off-handedly or as it comes onto topic when me and Saulot chat, but you note that naming things in Greek or Latin is cheesy and then turn right around and push for Hindi words left and right by the looks of it? Doesn't it cause the same problem from a different angle?<br /> <br /> As for the actual names, I'm voting to keep &quot;Akasha&quot; and I like &quot;Klesha&quot; for dissonance. Pneuma should be kept I feel as it sounds a little better to me than &quot;Prana&quot; and Dharma in my opinion doesn't sound too good in comparison to Iremia. Why not mix-match?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the issue is less of &quot;let's use this language gratuitously rather than this language gratuitously&quot; and more of a &quot;people rely on a specific language to make things &quot;fancy&quot; too often, so let's try a language that is less-often used to shake up the formula&quot;. For me, I see a high level of usage from Latin words or Greek words because they are the root of Romance languages which also contributes to English, a language that many people use. Whether it's Latin chanting or quotes from one of the great philosophers, it's used to add an extra &quot;oomph&quot; to terms that are meant to be seen as important. <b><i>Vampire </i></b>uses it quite a bit, which would make sense as Vampires have existed for quite a long time and some of the oldest Vampires hail from ancient Rome/Greece. However, <b><i>Dragon: the Inheritance </i></b>uses it with their Juice stat, Kauchaomai, as with their forms, Drakonos <i>(though it could be argued that it's supposed to be Latvian)</i> and Anthropos. <b><i>Princess: the Hopeful </i></b>uses it to refer to their Monster-of-the-Week creatures, the Cataphractoi, <b><i>Genius: the Transgression </i></b>has their abilities known as Axioms based on Greek terms. For me, it's an issue of oversaturation. <br /> <br /> The other reason is because, if we group things together, there is a language that goes with certain concepts. For the Siren's powers, the Verses, the different styles of performing Verses are related to Italian musical terms. For the antagonists of Sirens, we have the Vodianoi, which is a Slavic creature. However, they are kept as separate entities that are partially influenced by two different languages. The Siren's Power stat is Akasha, which is a Hindi term that relates to a core aspect of the Sirens' lore. I would push for Hindi terms to refer to the Siren's attributes, like their Power stat, Juice stat, and Integrity stat. Of course, I wouldn't object for Turbulence or Tarachi as the Frenzy-like state that Sirens might go into. I would say that if we go for either Hindi-based or Greek/Latin-based, it should be pretty streamlined so that each aspect fits. I feel that if we stay with Pneuma and Iremia, we would need to change Akasha to something that would relate to Greek.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've got to say I see where you're coming from and can even support it. However as Sirens/Mermaid myths pretty much exist everywhere I vote that while we could use Hindi as the main influence, we should have a tidbit of other cultures, most notably the Greek and Celtic ones; maybe some Japanese too. Opinion? </div> </div> </div>I suggested the Sazae-oni, a creature that takes the form of a beautiful woman who seduces sailors but is actually created from a sea snail that proceeds to castrate her lovers after she's done with them. I know that the different Waters have different inspirations, so maybe the Sazae-Oni may be a possible inspiration for the Tropicana Sirens. I should brush up on my Japanese yokai so I would know more of the sea creature-based creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T04:25:03-08:00","id":792702,"title":"","content":"I don't see much benefit beyond OCD consistency to making sure all names conform to one area/language or another personally, but hey; whatever works. Anyone else have an opinion on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T05:08:14-08:00","id":792709,"title":"","content":"Does that monster with fake beautiful women on his head in order to lure men into his mouth (based on anglerfishes I think) have a name? Maybe it could fit here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 12-25-2015, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T06:32:32-08:00","id":792725,"title":"","content":"I'll confess that I never undertood where Akasha came from. I believe it fits and is a nice naem and all, but the choice of word intrigues me. I mean, in the other thread I found no background that supported the choice of Akasha as a Power Stat. For a Siren, what means Akasha? How a Siren understands it and how is it a Concept to them? right now it seems very vague and &quot;flowing with the current&quot; because it partially fits the Time aspect.<br /> <br /> \u200bDon't get me wrong, I like Hindi names, but as Karav said: Only for the OCD consistency seems a bit off. Names should have meaning to the Splat. why would a Siren refers to their inner power Akasha more than the Greek version of it: Aether (Something like the air that the gods breathed, analogous to the mortals' air)? I am feeling the Power Stat is needing a bit of background study,<br /> <br /> Don't know if I am clear enough but... that's it.<br /> <br /> That said, I suggested the name Maelstrom to something before and now I'm suggesting it as an alternative to Turbulence or any other name that may be chosen. Maybe Sticking to common English or the nice Italian makes it easier, in general.<br /> <br /> On other thought, I like the Sazae-oni idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T10:16:51-08:00","id":792767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792641#post792641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b><i>Princess: the Hopeful </i></b>uses it to refer to their Monster-of-the-Week creatures, the Cataphractoi,</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Princess the Hopeful uses loads of gratuitous language in it (and it's described as gratuitous in verse). The True Monsters of the Week are Darkspawn, but Cataphractoi and Mnemosyne are greek names (&quot;Armor&quot; and &quot;Memory&quot; fittingly), the Darknesses powers are called &quot;Umbra(e)&quot; and &quot;Caligo (Calignes for plural)&quot; which are in Latin. There's some Japanese terms in the form of Amanojaku and Nakama (Body-snatching astral beings and what a group of Princesses are called). All of the Invocation names are in Italian. I know it's not really pertaining to the discussion of &quot;Greek&quot; but just wanted to point out. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792641#post792641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other reason is because, if we group things together, there is a language that goes with certain concepts. For the Siren's powers, the Verses, the different styles of performing Verses are related to Italian musical terms. For the antagonists of Sirens, we have the Vodianoi, which is a Slavic creature. However, they are kept as separate entities that are partially influenced by two different languages. The Siren's Power stat is Akasha, which is a Hindi term that relates to a core aspect of the Sirens' lore. I would push for Hindi terms to refer to the Siren's attributes, like their Power stat, Juice stat, and Integrity stat. Of course, I wouldn't object for Turbulence or Tarachi as the Frenzy-like state that Sirens might go into. I would say that if we go for either Hindi-based or Greek/Latin-based, it should be pretty streamlined so that each aspect fits. I feel that if we stay with Pneuma and Iremia, we would need to change Akasha to something that would relate to Greek.</div> </div> </div> </div>With said gratuitousness that I pointed out above, I would say that it wouldn't hurt if we drew from two or more languages. Given that Sirens have a water motif as one of their bases and water is known for flowing everywhere eventually, I would imagine we can use that to justify why Sirens pull from more than one language. Not to mention that stories of &quot;water spirits of lead people to drown&quot; are found anywhere you look, so that could be further justification. Italian is perfect for songs since it's the general placement for where the stories for Sirens were most popularized as well as what most musical terminology originated from. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792641#post792641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggested the Sazae-oni, a creature that takes the form of a beautiful woman who seduces sailors but is actually created from a sea snail that proceeds to castrate her lovers after she's done with them. I know that the different Waters have different inspirations, so maybe the Sazae-Oni may be a possible inspiration for the Tropicana Sirens. I should brush up on my Japanese yokai so I would know more of the sea creature-based creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I read up on some of the stories to base what a few of the Waters would be on. And good luck on the youkai stuff, all I know is that there's WAAAY too much. If it helps, I recall that there was a drowned ghost youkai (Bouyurei? I don't recall how it's spelt) that comes onto ships and starts dumping water in an endless stream to drown the ship. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792709#post792709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that monster with fake beautiful women on his head in order to lure men into his mouth (based on anglerfishes I think) have a name? Maybe it could fit here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're referring to the bosses <i>Dagon </i>and <i>Bael </i>in the Devil May Cry 4 video game? If I recall correctly, those two were based off of the Ars Goetia and were Demons. But I can see Vodianoi being based off of that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792725#post792725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll confess that I never undertood where Akasha came from. I believe it fits and is a nice naem and all, but the choice of word intrigues me. I mean, in the other thread I found no background that supported the choice of Akasha as a Power Stat. For a Siren, what means Akasha? How a Siren understands it and how is it a Concept to them? right now it seems very vague and &quot;flowing with the current&quot; because it partially fits the Time aspect.<br /> <br /> \u200bDon't get me wrong, I like Hindi names, but as Karav said: Only for the OCD consistency seems a bit off. Names should have meaning to the Splat. why would a Siren refers to their inner power Akasha more than the Greek version of it: Aether (Something like the air that the gods breathed, analogous to the mortals' air)? I am feeling the Power Stat is needing a bit of background study,<br /> <br /> Don't know if I am clear enough but... that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the original author specified why she chose Akasha, but I think it's fine. I chose the Vodianoi to name Echidna's children because they were once of the few Water spirit stories I found that had no relation to beauty. :3 I would suggest leaning away from using Aether though, because that's what Demons use as their fuel.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T13:30:52-08:00","id":792816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792725#post792725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll confess that I never undertood where Akasha came from. I believe it fits and is a nice naem and all, but the choice of word intrigues me. I mean, in the other thread I found no background that supported the choice of Akasha as a Power Stat. For a Siren, what means Akasha? How a Siren understands it and how is it a Concept to them? right now it seems very vague and &quot;flowing with the current&quot; because it partially fits the Time aspect.<br /> <br /> \u200bDon't get me wrong, I like Hindi names, but as Karav said: Only for the OCD consistency seems a bit off. Names should have meaning to the Splat. why would a Siren refers to their inner power Akasha more than the Greek version of it: Aether (Something like the air that the gods breathed, analogous to the mortals' air)? I am feeling the Power Stat is needing a bit of background study,<br /> <br /> Don't know if I am clear enough but... that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792767#post792767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe the original author specified why she chose Akasha, but I think it's fine. I chose the Vodianoi to name Echidna's children because they were once of the few Water spirit stories I found that had no relation to beauty. :3 I would suggest leaning away from using Aether though, because that's what Demons use as their fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as TvTropes and Wikipedia tell me, Akasha traditionally refers to the aether where all material things come from but it was adopted into the term &quot;Akashic Records&quot;, which is a compendium of all things that have existed. In terms of what Akasha means for Sirens, I was using it to refer to how strong the Siren of this reality is connected to the Sirens of The Deluge, which allows the Siren of this reality to tap into the timelessness of The Deluge. If anything, Akasha relates to the Siren's ability to trace timelines and sense what may occur in the future. I dunno if there is a word that describes the strength of an oracle's vision, but that might be a good place to start if we do end up changing Akasha.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792767#post792767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, I read up on some of the stories to base what a few of the Waters would be on. And good luck on the youkai stuff, all I know is that there's WAAAY too much. If it helps, I recall that there was a drowned ghost youkai (Bouyurei? I don't recall how it's spelt) that comes onto ships and starts dumping water in an endless stream to drown the ship.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792725#post792725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On other thought, I like the Sazae-oni idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of Japanese folklore, there's also the Kappa, which are the turtle-frog people with the water dish on their head, and the Ningyo, mermaid-equivalent that is the basis of the &quot;eat a mermaid's flesh and gain longevity&quot; myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I suggested the name Maelstrom to something before and now I'm suggesting it as an alternative to Turbulence or any other name that may be chosen. Maybe Sticking to common English or the nice Italian makes it easier, in general. </div> </div> </div>I would second using English terms to simplify things for right now. Maelstrom is a pretty good suggestion, as it has a lot of strong connotations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T15:34:37-08:00","id":792849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792816#post792816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of Japanese folklore, there's also the Kappa, which are the turtle-frog people with the water dish on their head, and the Ningyo, mermaid-equivalent that is the basis of the &quot;eat a mermaid's flesh and gain longevity&quot; myth.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funay%C5%ABrei\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/eb/SekienFunayurei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funay%C5%ABrei\" target=\"_blank\"> Funay\u016brei - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funay%C5%ABrei\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funay%C5%ABrei </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Found what I was looking for. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792816#post792816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would second using English terms to simplify things for right now. Maelstrom is a pretty good suggestion, as it has a lot of strong connotations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maelstrom for the Morality stat? Because IIRC Turbulence and Tranquility were referring to a rename.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T16:20:53-08:00","id":792864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792849#post792849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maelstrom for the Morality stat? Because IIRC Turbulence and Tranquility were referring to a rename.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMaelstrom as the Frenzy state. Reaper wnated to rename cause Dragon: The Inheritance used it somehow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T16:44:46-08:00","id":792870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792864#post792864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bMaelstrom as the Frenzy state. Reaper wnated to rename cause Dragon: The Inheritance used it somehow</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. OH. I see now. I thought that we were solely changing the Morality Meter name, not the Frenzy state name, pardon that. Yes, Maelstrom works good for Sirens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T17:13:34-08:00","id":792876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792849#post792849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funay%C5%ABrei\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funay%C5%ABrei</a><br /> Found what I was looking for. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>These sound like a good basis for a Vodianoi, or even a Banshee that we mentioned a while back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maelstrom for the Morality stat? Because IIRC Turbulence and Tranquility were referring to a rename. </div> </div> </div>No, as the name for the Frenzy-effect. The one that was tentatively named &quot;Dissonance&quot;. <br /> <br /> Insofar, There is <b>Akasha</b> for the Power Stat, <b>Pneuma</b> for the Juice Stat, <b>Serenity</b> for the Integrity Stat, and <b>Dissonance</b>, which I feel should be switched to <b>Maelstrom</b> as a Frenzy-effect. Both <b>Akasha </b>and <b>Pneuma</b> conflict because they are two terms that are unheard of and would make it difficult for the players to grasp the concept of what they mean. For example, Vampires have Blood Potency as their Power Stat, which gives a good vision of what it is supposed to relate to when it comes to Vampires. They also have Vitae, which is an odd word to have but, because it is the Juice to Blood Potency, would relate back to the vision of what Blood Potency means. With Mages, they have Gnosis as their Power Stat, which is something that, arguably, not many people have heard of. However, their Juice Stat, Mana, is close to ubiquitous in everyday life with the rise of video gaming, so even if someone doesn't know what Gnosis refers to, they can infer that it involves magic because they know what Mana is or the connotations of Mana. Basically, if there are terms used that are kinda odd or unheard of, context clues help out. However, it's all meant to be understood with only superficial knowledge. Vampires are associated with blood, which is further emphasized by Blood Potency and allows people to understand what Vitae refers to. Mages do magic stuff using their Mana, so Gnosis would be understood as some sort of magicky thing.<br /> <br /> We do have this overarching backstory for Sirens, which is fine. Every splat needs that. However, the splat is still &quot;Mermaids that sing&quot;, like how Werewolf, despite being half-spirit enforcers, are supposed to be about &quot;werewolves and the beast within&quot;. It's reinforced by the fact that Werewolves have Primal Urge as a Power Stat, referring to their bestial nature. Akasha, while it ties into the backstory, means nothing when it's placed next to the word &quot;Siren&quot;. The same goes for Pneuma, although it could work for anyone who has a working knowledge of Greek. '<br /> <br /> Akasha works into the Siren's ability to use multiple Opuses in her Verses and allows her a set number of Alterations. It also causes her to suffer greatly from <b>Maelstrom</b>, due to it allowing Echidna to whisper to the Siren. Serenity allows a Siren to stay calm in her decisions and actions. For Akasha, maybe <b>Immersion</b> would work, as it would reinforce the idea of water, would allow players to infer that Pneuma relates to water, and it allows for some wordplay, as Sirens of this reality are only partially aware of their selves in The Deluge at Immersion 1; they are only partially immersed in their role. When Sirens reach Immersion 10, they are fully aware of their other self and have merged their selves from reality and The Deluge together. This also means that their exposure to Echidna's whispers are stronger, as they are deeply immersed in their role. As for Serenity, perhaps <b>Lucidity </b>to refer to a Siren's awareness and ability to detach herself from a situation, <b>Placidity</b> to further establish a Siren's need to remain calm and unmoving, or, as a fancy word, <b>Ataraxy</b>, which is defined as &quot;a state of serene tranquility&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T20:53:33-08:00","id":792928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792876#post792876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insofar, There is <b>Akasha</b> for the Power Stat, <b>Pneuma</b> for the Juice Stat, <b>Serenity</b> for the Integrity Stat, and <b>Dissonance</b>, which I feel should be switched to <b>Maelstrom</b> as a Frenzy-effect. Both <b>Akasha </b>and <b>Pneuma</b> conflict because they are two terms that are unheard of and would make it difficult for the players to grasp the concept of what they mean. For example, Vampires have Blood Potency as their Power Stat, which gives a good vision of what it is supposed to relate to when it comes to Vampires. They also have Vitae, which is an odd word to have but, because it is the Juice to Blood Potency, would relate back to the vision of what Blood Potency means. With Mages, they have Gnosis as their Power Stat, which is something that, arguably, not many people have heard of. However, their Juice Stat, Mana, is close to ubiquitous in everyday life with the rise of video gaming, so even if someone doesn't know what Gnosis refers to, they can infer that it involves magic because they know what Mana is or the connotations of Mana. Basically, if there are terms used that are kinda odd or unheard of, context clues help out. However, it's all meant to be understood with only superficial knowledge. Vampires are associated with blood, which is further emphasized by Blood Potency and allows people to understand what Vitae refers to. Mages do magic stuff using their Mana, so Gnosis would be understood as some sort of magicky thing<br /> <br /> We do have this overarching backstory for Sirens, which is fine. Every splat needs that. However, the splat is still &quot;Mermaids that sing&quot;, like how Werewolf, despite being half-spirit enforcers, are supposed to be about &quot;werewolves and the beast within&quot;. It's reinforced by the fact that Werewolves have Primal Urge as a Power Stat, referring to their bestial nature. Akasha, while it ties into the backstory, means nothing when it's placed next to the word &quot;Siren&quot;. The same goes for Pneuma, although it could work for anyone who has a working knowledge of Greek.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now for the counterarguments. For one, Akasha refers to a supposed etheric field that records past events. This fitting for Sirens, as the Deluge is connected to the concept of Time and as such it connects to past events and has anything within it's waters. Also, literally almost every culture has some stories on water spirits or gods, or things that connect to water in general. Though it's not so much, doesn't it sort of fulfill the same definition that Akasha does? &quot;Etheric Field&quot; in the form that the tales are worldwide, and &quot;recorded past events&quot; is the definition of history itself. Using this reasoning, Akasha can still be fitting. At the least though I can imagine Akasha being renamed to &quot;Akashic Record&quot;, to ascribe to what the Siren has learned during her time as a Siren.<br /> <br /> As for Pneuma, the original ideas behind it were for it to fit the Succubi trope as well as Siren trope, basing on the idea that Sirens feed off of human souls to keep themselves alive. Connecting to this is the idea of the water-air connection that we have for Sirens who reach the &quot;Archmaster&quot; state so to speak. Not to mention with the powers being based on music and song, a fuel stat that literally translates to &quot;Breath&quot; is fitting to power it. If it helps even more, one of the most common diseases people hear of is <b>pneum</b>onia, a disease where the lungs are swollen and air cannot move. If nothing else, it's an allusion to what it means (breath) and if the concern for a fitting enough name for the fuel stat is great enough, we might have to change Pneuma back into it's original form. Breath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneuma\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneuma\" target=\"_blank\"> Pneuma - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneuma\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneuma </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also found this if it means anything for Pneuma. Also, going by the logic used that &quot;if people don't understand the power stat but understand the fuel stat, then it should be fine&quot;, I point out that Werewolves use Essence which, while giving the connection to Spirits (and that Wolves are part spirit themselves) doesn't play out the same way that Spirits can play around with it. Another example I have is that Mummies use Pillars, which by even looking at the name seriously doesn't give the same connection to &quot;Mummies&quot; that &quot;Mana&quot; connects to &quot;Mages&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792876#post792876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Akasha works into the Siren's ability to use multiple Opuses in her Verses and allows her a set number of Alterations. It also causes her to suffer greatly from <b>Maelstrom</b>, due to it allowing Echidna to whisper to the Siren. Serenity allows a Siren to stay calm in her decisions and actions. For Akasha, maybe <b>Immersion</b> would work, as it would reinforce the idea of water, would allow players to infer that Pneuma relates to water, and it allows for some wordplay, as Sirens of this reality are only partially aware of their selves in The Deluge at Immersion 1; they are only partially immersed in their role. When Sirens reach Immersion 10, they are fully aware of their other self and have merged their selves from reality and The Deluge together. This also means that their exposure to Echidna's whispers are stronger, as they are deeply immersed in their role. As for Serenity, perhaps <b>Lucidity </b>to refer to a Siren's awareness and ability to detach herself from a situation, <b>Placidity</b> to further establish a Siren's need to remain calm and unmoving, or, as a fancy word, <b>Ataraxy</b>, which is defined as &quot;a state of serene tranquility&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Lucidity fits in with the &quot;prophecy&quot; bit, the Siren stories of songs driving people mad and keeping themselves focused in the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T22:08:59-08:00","id":792943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792928#post792928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now for the counterarguments. For one, Akasha refers to a supposed etheric field that records past events. This fitting for Sirens, as the Deluge is connected to the concept of Time and as such it connects to past events and has anything within it's waters. Also, literally almost every culture has some stories on water spirits or gods, or things that connect to water in general. Though it's not so much, doesn't it sort of fulfill the same definition that Akasha does? &quot;Etheric Field&quot; in the form that the tales are worldwide, and &quot;recorded past events&quot; is the definition of history itself. Using this reasoning, Akasha can still be fitting. At the least though I can imagine Akasha being renamed to &quot;Akashic Record&quot;, to ascribe to what the Siren has learned during her time as a Siren.<br /> <br /> As for Pneuma, the original ideas behind it were for it to fit the Succubi trope as well as Siren trope, basing on the idea that Sirens feed off of human souls to keep themselves alive. Connecting to this is the idea of the water-air connection that we have for Sirens who reach the &quot;Archmaster&quot; state so to speak. Not to mention with the powers being based on music and song, a fuel stat that literally translates to &quot;Breath&quot; is fitting to power it. If it helps even more, one of the most common diseases people hear of is <b>pneum</b>onia, a disease where the lungs are swollen and air cannot move. If nothing else, it's an allusion to what it means (breath) and if the concern for a fitting enough name for the fuel stat is great enough, we might have to change Pneuma back into it's original form. Breath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneuma\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneuma\" target=\"_blank\"> Pneuma - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneuma\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneuma </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also found this if it means anything for Pneuma. Also, going by the logic used that &quot;if people don't understand the power stat but understand the fuel stat, then it should be fine&quot;, I point out that Werewolves use Essence which, while giving the connection to Spirits (and that Wolves are part spirit themselves) doesn't play out the same way that Spirits can play around with it. Another example I have is that Mummies use Pillars, which by even looking at the name seriously doesn't give the same connection to &quot;Mummies&quot; that &quot;Mana&quot; connects to &quot;Mages&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I would like to second Akasha being renamed &quot;Akashic Record&quot;, as that would be the most recognizable term associated with Akasha. As for Pneuma, there is a significant amount of information based around our Juice Stat being &quot;Pneuma&quot;, so I would have no objections to keeping it as Pneuma for now. Once we reach the playtesting stage, We would be able to get a better feel if it works or not. My apologies for being rather hasty in my objections.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like Lucidity fits in with the &quot;prophecy&quot; bit, the Siren stories of songs driving people mad and keeping themselves focused in the present. </div> </div> </div>With that, I believe that the re-terming process is done. Tentatively, the terms go as such:<br /> <br /> Integrity Equivalent. <b>Lucidity</b><br /> Power Stat: <b>Akashic Record</b><br /> Juice Stat: <b>Pneuma</b><br /> Frenzy-Effect: <b>Maelstrom</b><br /> Virtue and Vice: <b>Shore and Sea</b><br /> X-Axis: <b>Waters</b>, ranging from <b>Polaria</b>, <b>Tropicana</b>, <b>Gardenia</b>, <b>Vaporia</b>, <b>Freshwater </b><i>(I'm going to not touch on this one as I assume people are tired of me going on about terms)</i>, and <b>Discordia</b><br /> Y-Axis: <b>Currents</b>, with the normal ones being <b>Conflict</b>, <b>Harmony</b>, <b>Healing</b>, <b>Wisdom</b>, and <b>Buoyancy</b>. The <b>Abyssal Currents</b> are <b>Dark Secrets</b>, <b>Primordial Darkness</b>, <b>Mankind's Victory</b>, <b>Dark Passions</b>, and the <b>Void</b><br /> Z-Axis?: I presume that this is on the backburner for now, but <b>Depths</b>?<br /> Abilities: <b>Verses </b>are the &quot;channeling&quot;, spell-like abilities while <b>Alterations </b>are the passive, physical-like abilities<br /> <br /> Enemies: <b>Echidnal Sirens</b> who follow Echidna's mindset, the <b>Vodianoi </b>who are Echidna's creations, the <b>Banshees </b>who are Siren-like creatures that did not surface in The Deluge, and the <b>Flensers </b>who hunt Sirens for their longevity-properties<br /> <br /> I believe that this is the list of things that are essentially set in stone now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:12:11-08:00","id":792991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=792943#post792943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I would like to second Akasha being renamed &quot;Akashic Record&quot;, as that would be the most recognizable term associated with Akasha. As for Pneuma, there is a significant amount of information based around our Juice Stat being &quot;Pneuma&quot;, so I would have no objections to keeping it as Pneuma for now. Once we reach the playtesting stage, We would be able to get a better feel if it works or not. My apologies for being rather hasty in my objections.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine. I'm sorry that all I seem to give is Counterarguments. D:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a 