rens for their longevity-properties</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bSo, what's our next step?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T11:04:55-08:00","id":793199,"title":"","content":"<br /> So, I'm at class and the homework was to make something very quick. I did this, S:tD &quot;Logo&quot;. Wanted to show you guys. I'm not the best logo designer, but i'm putting some effort in it. For a quick, 15 minutes thing, it was the best I could do.<br /> <br /> First I wanted it tobe grey, as he Sirens are mediators and tend to be &quot;Grey&quot;. Also wanted the font to look like a foreign language, hence the dots,<br /> <br /> Sorry for double posting, anyway. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/4wlbBXn.png\" target=\"_blank\">Siren Logo</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T11:37:59-08:00","id":793211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793199#post793199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm at class and the homework was to make something very quick. I did this, S:tD &quot;Logo&quot;. Wanted to show you guys. I'm not the best logo designer, but i'm putting some effort in it. For a quick, 15 minutes thing, it was the best I could do.<br /> <br /> First I wanted it tobe grey, as he Sirens are mediators and tend to be &quot;Grey&quot;. Also wanted the font to look like a foreign language, hence the dots,<br /> <br /> Sorry for double posting, anyway.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/4wlbBXn.png\" target=\"_blank\">Siren Logo</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Holy crap this is good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yes, it would look good for the logo and it's ok when it comes to double posting.<br /> <br /> Our next step? I believe that we should at least cover how Sirens regain Pnuema, the benefits and drawbacks of Akashic Record and creating the general Alterations. Although I personally have a step I should be finishing up, namely the Waters. After which, Water specific Alterations can be done. Sorry for my lack of progress, Christmas happened and my inspiration is quite literally like the tides. In one moment, out the next. &gt;&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T14:35:15-08:00","id":793272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793211#post793211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our next step? I believe that we should at least cover how Sirens regain Pnuema, the benefits and drawbacks of Akashic Record and creating the general Alterations. Although I personally have a step I should be finishing up, namely the Waters. After which, Water specific Alterations can be done. Sorry for my lack of progress, Christmas happened and my inspiration is quite literally like the tides. In one moment, out the next. &gt;&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. This is nice. Which reminds me, I imagine that one way to regain Breath is to indulge in human contact as much as nature contact? Like how we have a way for them to regain from nature (bathing in waters befitting their Water), but not one dealing with them in relationship to humans.<br /> <br /> I would say as a rule, perhaps when Sirens indulge in their connections to humanity also give them Pneuma. More specifically, when they indulge in some form of love. Platonic, Romantic, Familial or even Unconditional Love. The type doesn't matter, so long as the Siren is deeply in love with the person. Interacting with this love gives them Pneuma. Perhaps for the sake of this next idea, Sirens can get Pneuma when they see others interacting in a deep seated love? So long as it fits in one of the four types mentioned above. </div> </div> </div>I remember writing a quick snippet on Pneuma about &quot;stealing away breath&quot; by shocking or impressing others, but a love theme could work to connect them to humanity. I would have to point out that Sirens would have a significantly easier time regaining their Pneuma if they could regain it through proxy. Although, this could play into the Akashic Records, where greater forms of love are needed to gain Pneuma. A Siren at Akashic Records 1 can partake in romantic love all they want and regain Pneuma but a Siren at Akashic Records 4 or 5 need something closer than a one-night stand, as the Akashic Records demands love that will last through time.<br /> <br /> As for Akashic Records, we do have some benefits as well as drawbacks. As far as mechanics go, gaining more points in Akashic Records does this:<br /> <br /> 1. The number of Opuses a Siren may use in a Verse goes up with Akashic Records. The strength of Verses also go up.<br /> 2. The number of total Alterations a Siren has goes up.<br /> 3. The amount of Pneuma a Siren retains and may use per turn go up. It also affects the amount of Pneuma regained when submerged in a Siren's favored Water.<br /> 4. Presumably, the limit on dots in Attributes and skills goes up, as it does with Blood Potency and Primal Urge.<br /> 5. The range in which a Siren can sense another Siren or Banshee goes up.<br /> <br /> 6. The time limit to resist Maelstrom goes down, which is bad, meaning that a Siren with high Akashic Records would succumb to the Deep End Condition faster.<br /> 7. It changes the strength of love a Siren must feel in order to regain Pneuma from mortals. Presumably, it goes Romantic/Erotic -&gt; Platonic/Friendship -&gt; Familial/Companionship -&gt; Unconditional/Charity/God-like love. <br /> 8. I feel that it should also affect how much Water a Siren needs to regain Pneuma. I feel like it should go about 1 liter per point of Akashic Records for 1 Pneuma. So a Siren at Akashic Records 4-5 would need 4-5 liters of their favored water to regain 1 point of Pneuma.<br /> 9. The range that allows a Siren to sense other Sirens and Banshees also reaches out to Flensers. Because the Flensers are not connected to The Deluge or The Song, Sirens cannot sense them. However, because Flensers have consumed the flesh of Sirens, the Flensers are able to somewhat sense The Song within the Sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another idea I had is for the Siren Subsplat of the Breathless. We talked about them being used as lures for Sirens to draw people to themselves or the like? I sort of imagined that The Breathless were people who surfaced in the Deluge without hearing the Song at all. Maybe they didn't pay heed to it, maybe they focused more on reaching the surface. Either way, when they surface their condition is noticable to people, even unconsciously. For they draw the same reactions to themselves that a person who nearly drowned at the beach receives. Some people are bystanders who simply hope the person is ok. Some people are more than bystanders, who decide to try and help the Breathless if they have any trouble. Some are Lifeguards, keeping constant watch over the Breathless until everything is ok. The Breathless, whether they like it or not, draw the attentions of other people to themselves for good or ill and make it easier to love them for a time as long as they're &quot;Suffering&quot;. And of course, they make perfect &quot;Lures&quot; for Sirens to draw Pneuma from other people. </div> </div> </div>This sounds very interesting, especially considering that with social media sites and the news reporting things that could bring attention, the Breathless could show up anywhere. It would also be interesting to have as a dichotomy, showing how more humans would care about the life of a Breathless than their actions in their own life causing events for the Siren to solve.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793199#post793199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm at class and the homework was to make something very quick. I did this, S:tD &quot;Logo&quot;. Wanted to show you guys. I'm not the best logo designer, but i'm putting some effort in it. For a quick, 15 minutes thing, it was the best I could do.<br /> <br /> First I wanted it tobe grey, as he Sirens are mediators and tend to be &quot;Grey&quot;. Also wanted the font to look like a foreign language, hence the dots,<br /> <br /> Sorry for double posting, anyway.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/4wlbBXn.png\" target=\"_blank\">Siren Logo</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That is pretty. Is that a font or is it your own handiwork?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T16:07:59-08:00","id":793301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember writing a quick snippet on Pneuma about &quot;stealing away breath&quot; by shocking or impressing others, but a love theme could work to connect them to humanity. I would have to point out that Sirens would have a significantly easier time regaining their Pneuma if they could regain it through proxy. Although, this could play into the Akashic Records, where greater forms of love are needed to gain Pneuma. A Siren at Akashic Records 1 can partake in romantic love all they want and regain Pneuma but a Siren at Akashic Records 4 or 5 need something closer than a one-night stand, as the Akashic Records demands love that will last through time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm voting for this, if only to make it more of its own thing and less of &quot;Demon: The Fallen with mermaids.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The number of Opuses a Siren may use in a Verse goes up with Akashic Records. The strength of Verses also go up.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way does it get stronger? Is it a raise in effects or are we simply counting more dices the more AR you have?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The number of total Alterations a Siren has goes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I approve of this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The amount of Pneuma a Siren retains and may use per turn go up. It also affects the amount of Pneuma regained when submerged in a Siren's favored Water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also liking this; I vote for!<br /> 4. Presumably, the limit on dots in Attributes and skills goes up, as it does with Blood Potency and Primal Urge.[/QUOTE]<br /> Ayup.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. The range in which a Siren can sense another Siren or Banshee goes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>And remember Highlander; there can be only one! On a more serious notion it does bring it a little close to the supernatural awareness of DtF on a more limited scale, but I'm still okay with how this is so far.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. The time limit to resist Maelstrom goes down, which is bad, meaning that a Siren with high Akashic Records would succumb to the Deep End Condition faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems legit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. It changes the strength of love a Siren must feel in order to regain Pneuma from mortals. Presumably, it goes Romantic/Erotic -&gt; Platonic/Friendship -&gt; Familial/Companionship -&gt; Unconditional/Charity/God-like love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me gusta. I'm adding so much here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8. I feel that it should also affect how much Water a Siren needs to regain Pneuma. I feel like it should go about 1 liter per point of Akashic Records for 1 Pneuma. So a Siren at Akashic Records 4-5 would need 4-5 liters of their favored water to regain 1 point of Pneuma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice touch; this should be done!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793272#post793272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9. The range that allows a Siren to sense other Sirens and Banshees also reaches out to Flensers. Because the Flensers are not connected to The Deluge or The Song, Sirens cannot sense them. However, because Flensers have consumed the flesh of Sirens, the Flensers are able to somewhat sense The Song within the Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not put this on 5 or make a Verse or so to increase the effect to this instead?<br /> <br /> On another note the Breathless are interesting though I slightly wonder what it is about them that draws other people in. I also slightly worry if the description of how they're made doesn't risk them being too common-place, but I have a feeling I don't have a strong grasp on how Sirens themselves are made beyond drowning in some alternate reality or whatever. Sufficed to say, I'm all for adding them in with a small bit of tweaking as I feel they are interesting and could add a share to the overall game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T20:27:07-08:00","id":793391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793301#post793301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm voting for this, if only to make it more of its own thing and less of &quot;Demon: The Fallen with mermaids.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> And remember Highlander; there can be only one! On a more serious notion it does bring it a little close to the supernatural awareness of DtF on a more limited scale, but I'm still okay with how this is so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, I'm not too familiar with <b><i>Demon: the Fallen</i></b><i>.</i> What aspects made <b><i>Siren</i></b> similar?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In what way does it get stronger? Is it a raise in effects or are we simply counting more dices the more AR you have? </div> </div> </div>The current dice pool for Verses is Akashic Records + Attribute based on Conclusion, so more AR adds dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not put this on 5 or make a Verse or so to increase the effect to this instead? </div> </div> </div>Mainly for formatting purposes. Examples 1-5 are meant to be more beneficial the greater it goes up while examples 6-9 are supposed to be more detrimental. Flensers are...not exactly the nicest people towards Sirens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note the Breathless are interesting though I slightly wonder what it is about them that draws other people in. I also slightly worry if the description of how they're made doesn't risk them being too common-place, but I have a feeling I don't have a strong grasp on how Sirens themselves are made beyond drowning in some alternate reality or whatever. Sufficed to say, I'm all for adding them in with a small bit of tweaking as I feel they are interesting and could add a share to the overall game. </div> </div> </div>Basically, the formula that creates a Siren is Survive Drowning + Hearing The Song = Rebirth as a Siren with your knowledge of The Deluge reality.<br /> <br /> Surviving Drowning - Hearing The Song = Rebirth as a Breathless, who are walking Attention Black Holes, effectively. Some don't come out all too fine, leaving them catatonic and protected by a legion of sympathizers. Those who aren't are plagued by tragedy and suffering through their life, drawing in the attention of others who are enraptured by the Breathless's life. The Breathless find this existence to be increasingly disturbing as they are unable to get a moment of peace without someone calling to the Breathless and attempting to &quot;save&quot; them. There are a few Breathless who managed to use their ability to get attention to their benefit, becoming minor celebrities or humanitarians, but most Breathless are either smothered with their attention or realize that, because they are so beloved and sympathetic, they are able to get away with anything.<br /> <br /> Hearing The Song - Surviving Drowning = Rebirth as a Banshee, who are forced to see both The Deluge reality and this reality simultaneously. The tl;dr version is that Banshees are in perpetual torment and only experience release by stealing Pneuma, either through manipulation or straight-up murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T20:32:41-08:00","id":793393,"title":"","content":"Made a few changes in the Logo, making it more Dark and Edgy. Oh, Reaper, it's actually a Font that I had in a pack for long (funny that the name is Siren Script N3)<br /> <br /> \u200b<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/jjunIFr.png\" target=\"_blank\">SIren Logo - Test</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T20:39:10-08:00","id":793395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793393#post793393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Made a few changes in the Logo, making it more Dark and Edgy. Oh, Reaper, it's actually a Font that I had in a pack for long (funny that the name is Siren Script N3)<br /> <br /> \u200b<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/jjunIFr.png\" target=\"_blank\">SIren Logo - Test</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How fitting. :V On a side note, I like how the N at the end of &quot;Siren&quot; is basically a Bass clef with the dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T20:42:57-08:00","id":793396,"title":"","content":"Exactly what I wanted :P Something Musical-ish and Foreign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T21:42:57-08:00","id":793415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793391#post793391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, I'm not too familiar with <b><i>Demon: the Fallen</i></b><i>.</i> What aspects made <b><i>Siren</i></b> similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head let's see.<br /> Aquatic Form &lt;&gt; Apocalyptic Form<br /> Verses and Lores aren't too different from one another in terms of how they're described.<br /> The whole Sirens having a harder time to hide the more they indulge their supernatural life is very in line with Revelation: the more Demons use their Lores the harder it becomes for them to maintain the facade of humanity.<br /> Being the last oWoD line they also had that looming apocalypse over the horizon with Gehenna just around the corner which goes in line with the Deluge if in a different shape.<br /> <br /> That's about what I can think of for the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793391#post793391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current dice pool for Verses is Akashic Records + Attribute based on Conclusion, so more AR adds dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793391#post793391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mainly for formatting purposes. Examples 1-5 are meant to be more beneficial the greater it goes up while examples 6-9 are supposed to be more detrimental. Flensers are...not exactly the nicest people towards Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Righto.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=793391#post793391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the formula that creates a Siren is Survive Drowning + Hearing The Song = Rebirth as a Siren with your knowledge of The Deluge reality.<br /> <br /> Surviving Drowning - Hearing The Song = Rebirth as a Breathless, who are walking Attention Black Holes, effectively. Some don't come out all too fine, leaving them catatonic and protected by a legion of sympathizers. Those who aren't are plagued by tragedy and suffering through their life, drawing in the attention of others who are enraptured by the Breathless's life. The Breathless find this existence to be increasingly disturbing as they are unable to get a moment of peace without someone calling to the Breathless and attempting to &quot;save&quot; them. There are a few Breathless who managed to use their ability to get attention to their benefit, becoming minor celebrities or humanitarians, but most Breathless are either smothered with their attention or realize that, because they are so beloved and sympathetic, they are able to get away with anything.<br /> <br /> Hearing The Song - Surviving Drowning = Rebirth as a Banshee, who are forced to see both The Deluge reality and this reality simultaneously. The tl;dr version is that Banshees are in perpetual torment and only experience release by stealing Pneuma, either through manipulation or straight-up murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice; I'm sold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7060,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","user":"Karavolos","date":".  Missed a word. 12-27-2015, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T18:25:45-08:00","id":793875,"title":"","content":"Double posting like a pro. I was thinking for the logo, how about some water ripples in the background for spice value?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T08:57:23-08:00","id":794207,"title":"","content":"I'd say go for it, but then again I'm not aesthetically gifted. On a completely unrelated point, the freshwater <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations</a> are done at long last. I'm not really sure how they thematically fit the Freshwater Sirens though.<br /> I like how the Banshees are shaping up and the Breathless are a nice touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:29:20-08:00","id":794325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=794207#post794207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say go for it, but then again I'm not aesthetically gifted. On a completely unrelated point, the freshwater <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations</a> are done at long last. I'm not really sure how they thematically fit the Freshwater Sirens though.<br /> I like how the Banshees are shaping up and the Breathless are a nice touch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the new Freshwater Alterations, but I sort of need to note something on the Waterwalking one. When I noted that Freshwater Sirens could walk on land, what I meant was that instead of having the stereotypical Mermaid tail, they would be able to have legs and stuff instead. I was also grasping straws abit on the Freshwater Sirens, so if anyone has suggestions for what I could write to specify their alterations, feel free to suggest. I was thinking of using marine animal appearances that fit the areas. Freshwater Alterations therefore would be draw from Freshwater animals.<br /> <br /> I think we also need to make rules on what the basic Aquatic form is without Alterations.<br /> <br /> +Can breathe underwater indefinitely.<br /> +9 Again to Athletics rolls in water <br /> +Speed is quadrupled when swimming<br /> +Gives access to all Alterations the Siren owns<br /> <br /> -Can only breathe above water for a number of turns equal to her Stamina, after which she must roll her Stamina. Each suxx gives 30 extra seconds for how long she can be without breathing underwater. If she stays up past that, then she begins drowning in air as if anyone else has begun drowning in water.<br /> -On land, she only has her mermaid tail and thus no legs. She can only move up to her Strength in speed, suffering a form of a permanent, if specialized Knocked Down Tilt when on land. (mitigated by the Freshwater Alteration that gives legs instead of a mermaid tail).<br /> <br /> If I may suggest as an idea for both two General Alterations and a Waterwalking one.<br /> <br /> General Alterations: Octopus Tentacles - Instead of forming a fish tail, the Siren's lower half splits into eight tentacles complete with suckers. Her tentacles give +2 to all Dexterity rolls involving the use of her tentacles, in which includes use of the suckers on them. The suckers along the tentacles also give the Siren 9 Again on Brawl rolls. <br /> Inspiration: Octopus<br /> <br /> Starfish Regeneration - The Siren's regeneration factor goes past the ability of normal Sirens. When a Siren loses a limb and it doesn't return to her body, instead of taking a negative condition representing her new found disability mark the damage that severed the limb as Resistant damage. Over the course of healing, the limb slowly but surely regrows until it is completely anew.<br /> Inspiration: Starfish<br /> <br /> Freshwater Alteration: Amphibious Legs - Instead of having a fish tail, the Siren has two somewhat-human legs instead. She may move on land without any penalties unlike the normal Aquatic form.<br /> Inspiration: Frogs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:41:17-08:00","id":794328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saulotthegentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I noted that Freshwater Sirens could walk on land, what I meant was that instead of having the stereotypical Mermaid tail, they would be able to have legs and stuff instead. I was also grasping straws abit on the Freshwater Sirens</div> </div> </div> </div>I too was grasping at straws. With what you've given for the Aquatic form- namely confirmation of a tail- I think that Water Walking is in need of some re-writes. I was saving Octopus tentacles for Tropicana, but if you think they fit better as general then that's where they'll go.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saulotthegentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">she only has her mermaid tail and thus no legs</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be nit picking, but how's that gonna work with Vaporian Sirens? If their favoured water is vapours, how will a tail work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","user":"SquamousBeauty","date":".  edit:messed up the quote 12-28-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T13:00:33-08:00","id":794342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=794328#post794328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too was grasping at straws. With what you've given for the Aquatic form- namely confirmation of a tail- I think that Water Walking is in need of some re-writes. I was saving Octopus tentacles for Tropicana, but if you think they fit better as general then that's where they'll go.</div> </div> </div> </div>This project is still a WIP and thus heavily subject to change. :3 They could end up in the Tropicana Alterations later, I though that Octopi lived in all water climates though? If not, then that can be saved for Tropicana. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=794328#post794328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be nit picking, but how's that gonna work with Vaporian Sirens? If their favoured water is vapours, how will a tail work?</div> </div> </div> </div>...Reaper, any thoughts? Vaporia was mostly your idea. D:<br /> As for my own thoughts on the matter, perhaps Vaporians have insectoid appearances or bottom halves in moving? This is the only idea I have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T13:34:07-08:00","id":794363,"title":"","content":"Well, all I'd thought of was giving them some sort of gliding ability but we'll cross that bridge when we come to it. Insects does open up an interesting variety, but maybe some kind of floating jellyfish thing? I'll add the octopus to the Common and see how it compares to the Tropicana Alterations when we get there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:13:38-08:00","id":794589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we also need to make rules on what the basic Aquatic form is without Alterations.<br /> <br /> +Can breathe underwater indefinitely.<br /> +9 Again to Athletics rolls in water<br /> +Speed is quadrupled when swimming<br /> +Gives access to all Alterations the Siren owns<br /> <br /> -Can only breathe above water for a number of turns equal to her Stamina, after which she must roll her Stamina. Each suxx gives 30 extra seconds for how long she can be without breathing underwater. If she stays up past that, then she begins drowning in air as if anyone else has begun drowning in water.<br /> -On land, she only has her mermaid tail and thus no legs. She can only move up to her Strength in speed, suffering a form of a permanent, if specialized Knocked Down Tilt when on land. (mitigated by the Freshwater Alteration that gives legs instead of a mermaid tail).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too was grasping at straws. With what you've given for the Aquatic form- namely confirmation of a tail- I think that Water Walking is in need of some re-writes. I was saving Octopus tentacles for Tropicana, but if you think they fit better as general then that's where they'll go.<br /> <br /> This may be nit picking, but how's that gonna work with Vaporian Sirens? If their favoured water is vapours, how will a tail work?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Reaper, any thoughts? Vaporia was mostly your idea. D:As for my own thoughts on the matter, perhaps Vaporians have insectoid appearances or bottom halves in moving? This is the only idea I have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...maybe an automatic Tail option for each Water? One of the nixed Polarian Alterations had to do with a whale tail that could be used as a weapon. With the Freshwater Alterations granting bipedal movement, perhaps the Vaporian Alterations causes the fins on the Siren's tail to grow and extend, becoming like that of a flying fish and allowing her to propel herself forward. It's less of a free movement and more of a jumping action, but it allows the Vaporian Siren to move as if she could swim through the water vapors. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This project is still a WIP and thus heavily subject to change. :3 They could end up in the Tropicana Alterations later, I though that Octopi lived in all water climates though? If not, then that can be saved for Tropicana. </div> </div> </div>Let's simplify the process of coming up with Alterations by stating what is intended for each Water. Obviously, fish is an obvious inspiration for Sirens in general, but we should probably pinpoint what creatures are fair game for which Water.<br /> <br /> We have <b>Polaria </b>pretty much developed, focusing on blubbery animals and whales. Basically, creatures that are iconic with the arctic circles. Does that extend to penguins, who are aquatic creatures that are commonly associated with Antarctica? Is it only for a set type of creature, based on their dependency on water? Does the basis of what we use for Alterations stop at birds but continue into insects, mammals, and reptiles along with fish?<br /> <br /> <b>Freshwater</b> is definitely based on creatures that live in rivers, lakes, and ponds, but it also has a slight focus on amphibians like frogs, salamanders, and axolotls. It also has a basis in being able to go between land and water. This dichotomy might also lend itself to insects that start off in water when they are larvae, like mayflies, dragonflies, and other insects that transition from one way of life to another. There's also the inspiration of Duck for the <b>Amphibious Legs</b> Alteration, so it may work towards that idea. <br /> <br /> With that, there are the <b>Vaporians</b> who are based on bays and temperate coasts. I suggested flying fish as a basis for the mermaid tail. Surprisingly enough, Vaporians could also extend to creatures that live in deserts and gain water by collecting condensation from fog, like beetles, scorpions, snakes, and the desert rain frog. <br /> <br /> In contrast, I presume that <b>Tropicans </b>are found in tropical coasts and waters, leaning more towards coral reefs and warm open waters. Dolphins, sponges, jellyfish, and even sea turtles sound like they would be safe game. <br /> <br /> <b>Gardenians </b>would be swamps, bayous, marshes, oases, generally areas that are rich with soil and plant-life. Hippos, crayfish, crawdads, crocodiles, caiman, beavers, anacondas, creatures that are associated with the untamed wild seem to be the motif for this Water.<br /> <br /> As for <b>Discordians</b>, I'm at a loss. They're based on pollution and taint, but I can't really think of a marine animal that relates to pollution. As a cop-out, what if Discordians were actually the winged Sirens of Greek mythology? It would play in by having Discordians breaking the motif by being aerial and allow us to incorporate bird-Sirens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:49:35-08:00","id":794606,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Discordians have the ability to corrupt themselves and/or others allowing them to reshape themselves at some manner of penalty like the need to consume living beings etc could explain the bird Sirens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T05:10:03-08:00","id":794768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As for </span><b>Discordians</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">, I'm at a loss. They're based on pollution and taint, but I can't really think of a marine animal that relates to pollution. As a cop-out, what if Discordians were actually the winged Sirens of Greek mythology? It would play in by having Discordians breaking the motif by being aerial and allow us to incorporate bird-Sirens.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I'd thought of using rats, crocodiles and other sewer creatures for <b>Discordians</b>. Given how the iconic image of oil spills is a dying bird, I think that having avian features does make sense.</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...maybe an automatic Tail option for each Water?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each water is getting a Tail based <b>Alteration, </b>but I think that maybe each water should have the tail Alteration as part of their Aquatic form by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T05:43:56-08:00","id":794775,"title":"","content":"I'm not too sure on the need to make it a requirement as I could see webbed hands/feet work just as well; but then it could be a part of it alongside a tail. Not sure if replacing legs for a flipper (or two) is necessairly exclusive of a tail or not; but that could be a thing too. Any view or input?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:20:38-08:00","id":795041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=794589#post794589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...maybe an automatic Tail option for each Water? One of the nixed Polarian Alterations had to do with a whale tail that could be used as a weapon. With the Freshwater Alterations granting bipedal movement, perhaps the Vaporian Alterations causes the fins on the Siren's tail to grow and extend, becoming like that of a flying fish and allowing her to propel herself forward. It's less of a free movement and more of a jumping action, but it allows the Vaporian Siren to move as if she could swim through the water vapors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets go with this. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=794589#post794589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip on what Waters will be getting what Alterations</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these. :3 <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=794768#post794768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/FONT]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I'd thought of using rats, crocodiles and other sewer creatures for <b>Discordians</b>. Given how the iconic image of oil spills is a dying bird, I think that having avian features does make sense.</span><br /> <br /> Each water is getting a Tail based <b>Alteration, </b>but I think that maybe each water should have the tail Alteration as part of their Aquatic form by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about mixing in creatures from the Abyssal Zone as well? Angler fish and the like? Discordians can bathe in tainted water, which includes bloody and polluted waters. The polluted part draws from the rats, crocodiles and sewer creatures. The blood part draws from the most violent (and possibly creepy) beings in the seas. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't think that the Alteration added tail fin specialty should be made as the default for Sirens of that water. They should be unique and optional to emphasize use of Alterations and still giving Sirens common ground without being almost completely different due to what Water they're in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T14:43:22-08:00","id":795095,"title":"","content":"Guys, maybe i'm being too paranoid or stubborn but I don't think earth-based mammals (Rats) or Arachnids would be very fitting, I like the idea of taking alterations from animals directly related with water like Duck, Crocs and Walrus. but animals that are not so directly related may feel a bit off the theme","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T16:40:54-08:00","id":795188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=795095#post795095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, maybe i'm being too paranoid or stubborn but I don't think earth-based mammals (Rats) or Arachnids would be very fitting, I like the idea of taking alterations from animals directly related with water like Duck, Crocs and Walrus. but animals that are not so directly related may feel a bit off the theme</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the earlier suggestion I made to try and justify bird-Sirens; I agree with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T23:06:07-08:00","id":795413,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=794606#post794606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Discordians have the ability to corrupt themselves and/or others allowing them to reshape themselves at some manner of penalty like the need to consume living beings etc could explain the bird Sirens?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=795041#post795041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about mixing in creatures from the Abyssal Zone as well? Angler fish and the like? Discordians can bathe in tainted water, which includes bloody and polluted waters. The polluted part draws from the rats, crocodiles and sewer creatures. The blood part draws from the most violent (and possibly creepy) beings in the seas.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=795095#post795095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, maybe i'm being too paranoid or stubborn but I don't think earth-based mammals (Rats) or Arachnids would be very fitting, I like the idea of taking alterations from animals directly related with water like Duck, Crocs and Walrus. but animals that are not so directly related may feel a bit off the theme</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, I could see sewer crocodiles being a basis for the Discordians as well as the Bird-based sirens. Maybe Sirens take after myths and urban legends rather than actual, &quot;scientifically-feasible&quot; animals. There is a spot for the Kelpie, which are water spirits that take on the form of horse or human. Horses aren't necessarily the first thing people think about when they talk about aquatic/marine creatures, but it is something that is based in a myth that is also connected to water. Same goes for the hippocampus, It would also allow for the bird-Sirens and we could even take it onto creatures like the Loch Ness Monster. The Discordians, when they aren't being manic creatures going out of their way to push people forward, are also mirrors to the Vodianoi, who are forcibly warped creatures made by Echidna. In contrast, Discordians are naturally strange but have a working internal logic to them. <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't argue against the predators of the deep for an inspiration for Discordians, but that depends on which direction the Discordians are taking. Do Discordians lead more towards pollution, do they lean more towards blood and predation, or is it somewhere in the middle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T00:06:52-08:00","id":795432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=795413#post795413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wouldn't argue against the predators of the deep for an inspiration for Discordians, but that depends on which direction the Discordians are taking. Do Discordians lead more towards pollution, do they lean more towards blood and predation, or is it somewhere in the middle?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was imagining both honestly. On one hand, they're connected to the defilement and destruction of nature, and thus they're connected to mankind's waste. On another hand, they embody the ferocity of nature, where there's only predator or prey and kill or be killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T03:15:49-08:00","id":797253,"title":"","content":"Quick review of the <b>Currents</b>. So far, the Waters define the physical traits and a general mindset that the Sirens of that particular Water subscribe to. Polarian Sirens are colder (<i>literally and figuratively)</i> and are more morose and cynical as compared to the others while Freshwater Sirens are optimistic and are more willing to interact with humanity. The Waters are both a body type and a manner of reacting to the world. With Currents, they are the driving mentality and the ways in which a Siren wants to change the world. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Current of Conflict</b><br /> <i>&quot;Do you even care? If something is worth fighting for, you need to fight for it. Don't be the person standing on the outside and waiting for it to come. Be the force of change. Stand for what you believe in. If you want things to change, you must be willing to make them change.&quot; <b>-A Gardenian of Conflict</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;No. It is not over. Get up. Take a breath. You cannot allow yourself to give up. This cannot be how this ends&quot; <b>-A Polarian of Conflict</b><br /> <br /> &quot;C'mon, you're really going to leave things alone? You're just gonna let them win without a struggle? Wow, what a shame. And here I thought you were a scrapper. Guess we can't all be as great as we want to be. Oh, you're not giving up now? You're gonna make a stand? Heh, I knew I saw something in you.&quot; <b>-A Discordian of Conflict</b></i><br /> <br /> The sea is a fickle being. On some days, it is calm and gentle, like a drop of dew falling into a puddle. On others, it rages and storms, battering the ships within it with crashing waves and great winds. Some ships have been taken by the oceans, overwhelmed by the depths. The ones who are willing to fight against the current, willing to go against what they know to be a great force, are allowed to continue onward and make their journey. Sirens who follow the Current of Conflict believe in the fight against idleness; they want others to take charge in what they believe in rather than waiting for someone else to take the mantle. If a Siren of Conflict isn't rallying a crowd, she is most-likely going to be in the thick of the fight, clearing a path for others to travel. Sirens of Conflict are the vanguard of the Sirens, willing to take the first step towards fighting off The Deluge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Current of Harmony</b><br /> <i>&quot;Hold my hand. Can you feel the warmth from my body? I'm here for you and I'll always be here for you. You don't have to be afraid to reach out anymore.&quot;<b> -A Tropican of Harmony</b><br /> <br /> &quot;We can do whatever you want for the day. I know you're not a big fan of going out, but we've been missing you lately. You're one of us and we want you to feel like it. This is gonna be a day for you, our treat.&quot; <b>-A Freshwater of Harmony</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Your mother misses you. You haven't called her ever since you moved out here. I know it's not my business, but I think you miss her too. Here, I took a message from her. You can decide to call if you want.&quot; <b>-A Vaporian of Harmony</b></i><br /> <br /> A young child reaches their hands into a river and partakes of the life-giving nectar that runs from one end of a country to the other. It is cold, but refreshing, like a quiet respite from the world around them. How many other children have experienced the same feeling? How many adults? How about the wild creatures that treat it as a sanctuary? Or the stretch of fertile land that allows great trees to rise up? Sirens who follow the Current of Harmony believe in the power of connections and the unity of the world around then; the strength of one is only as powerful as what it reaches out into. For change to happen, everyone must be aware, or at least on the same page. A Siren of Harmony is someone who wants to make others aware of the world around them, resonating on a single note in the world. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Current of Healing</b><br /> <i>&quot;Go ahead. Scream. Cry. Let it all out. It's killing you on the inside, so you deserve it. Don't worry. I won't judge you.&quot;<b> -A Vaporian of Healing</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Hey. Look, I know you're going through a bad break-up and you want some time to yourself. That's fine. However, no one has seen you in the last few weeks, so you have two options. One, you unlock the door so we can have a talk. Or two, I drop-kick this door and take you out for drinks. What'll it be?&quot; <b>-A Gardenian of Healing</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Look at you, you little trooper. Don't worry, everything will be fine. You made it this far, so you'll be able to keep going on. I know you're going to be okay.&quot; <b>-A Freshwater of Healing</b></i><br /> <br /> Water cleanses filth, whether it is dirt on clothes or the sins of the remorseful. Whether it is a daily ablution or a baptism, water is an agent that washes away the stains of life. Even rain, one of the most innocuous manifestations of water, represents a moment of peace and clarity, washing away rage or suffering. No stain too deep to clean. No sin too severe to forgive. No fire too hot to douse. The water will come. Sirens who follow the Current of Healing believe in rehabilitation and second chances; everyone deserves a moment to recover or a chance for redemption. To give up on something is to abandon it, believing it unable to change. Are second chances not an opportunity to change? Sirens of Healing are nothing if not patient and forgiving, willing to allow someone to feel the release of peace when the healing process is over.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Current of Wisdom</b><br /> <i>&quot;History is always cursed to repeat itself. Do not dwell on things that you cannot change. Learn from them.&quot;<b> -A Polarian of Wisdom</b><br /> <br /> &quot;You can't just worry about the future when you aren't experiencing it. Come with me. I think there are some things you need to see.&quot; <b>-A Tropican of Wisdom</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Life lessons? Me? Sure. Don't keep the lights on in your car when you leave it. Fabric sheets are a good substitute for deodorant. What else...oh! Don't think that anyone knows what's good for you other than yourself. Unless they're a professional and are talking about things that you don't know better.&quot;<b> -A Discordian of Wisdom</b></i><br /> <br /> Along winding rivers that link cities, through great seas that separate countries, past the oceans that divide the continents is the unknown. How far must one travel down the current before they see a world unlike that of their own? How much can change when humans cannot communicate through the great waters? Expanding one's horizons is to travel beyond borders and seeking out the unknown. Sirens who follow the Current of Wisdom believe in expanding viewpoints and questioning the world; not everything is clear as day and not everything can be learned by simply knowing of them. A river may run for a set amount of miles and may be a set distance deep, but how far does the water actually run? What does the water mean? Sirens of Wisdom want answers from the world and want to share those answers to others, even if each answer seems to contradict one another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Current of Buoyancy</b><br /> <i>&quot;Hey, have you ever wanted to do something crazy?&quot;<b> -A Discordian of Buoyancy</b><br /> <br /> &quot;I can't really allow you to get away with this. Of course, I could always just say that I was busy with work and just happened to leave this lying around. It would also be a shame if someone were to take it and use it for their own good. But, of course, that would be just such a terrible thing to think of.&quot; <b>-A Freshwater of Buoyancy</b><br /> <br /> &quot;It looks like they're slacking off. Too bad, looks like there's nothing to stop us from going in and messing with their information. Are you in?&quot;<b> -A Vaporian of Buoyancy</b></i><br /> <br /> Water is not a force that will take being used so lightly. Waves will erode stone, rain will pierce through roofs. It will bend along curves and fill depressions with its presence, molding itself to each and every situation brought upon it. Water may eventually be forced off-course or pressured in a way it cannot overcome, but it will continue to flow and adapt as it exerts its own force against those that attempt to control it. Sirens who follow the Current of Buoyancy believe in pragmatism and infiltration; while it is nice to hope that everyone is willing to play nice, sometimes change can only occur with more drastic measures. Sirens have had to experience an apocalypse once; anything to stop a second disaster is more than welcome. Sirens of Buoyancy will level the playing field if they must.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Castaways</b><br /> <i>&quot;Really? You want me to stay around for the holidays? To be honest, I didn't really expect to be so important to you. Sure, I'd love to stay.&quot; <b>-A Tropican Castaway</b><br /> <br /> &quot;No matter how far humanity has been dragged down, they are so willing to keep hope in their heart and venture on. It's...conflicting, to say the least. I must know more.&quot; <b>-A Polarian Castaway</b><br /> <br /> &quot;I envy you. After all that has come down upon you, the struggle and the fear, you didn't give up. You're a hardy one. I wish I could be as strong as you are.&quot;<b> -A Gardenian Castaway</b></i><br /> <br /> The land and the sea share a relationship that cannot be expressed through words alone. When the sea gives, the land takes. When the land gives, the sea takes. The waves brush against the sandy beaches and pull away grains into the water. Rainwater seeps through the soil and feeds the earth, allowing the seeds within to grow and flourish. It is not a one-sided relationship where one is superior to the other; both sides are willing to exist with one another. Sirens who do not follow a Current are Castaways, living as observers within humanity. When The Deluge took life from its world, the Sirens awoke with a different view of the world, a view that told them of the failings of humanity. Without a Current to swim along, the Castaways looked to humanity as a reflection of the world that once was. Can Sirens really guide humanity when there is still so much that the Sirens need to learn, as both their human side and their Siren side? The Castaways want answers for themselves before they take to any Current, experiencing the world as a human and as a creature of the sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T13:19:54-08:00","id":797489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797253#post797253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip on normal Currents</div> </div> </div> </div>I like all of these. Sorry that I haven't been much active, trying to get motivated for making Siren after some disappointing thoughts came up, but enough about those. :3 Have made these if it helps cover the Abyssal Currents.<br /> <br /> <b>Phelegethon, The Current of Dark Passions</b> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Did those bullies hurt you again? Did they tear up your books and make you bleed? ...Good. Use this as your inspiration to actually be successful.&quot; <b>A Discordian of Phelegethon</b></i><br /> <i>&quot;Do you think your heart was the first one I've broken? To me, your tears are nothing more than drops in a river I have dug out from the earth.&quot; <b>A Freshwater of Phelegethon</b></i><br /> <br /> Nature and Humanity, as much as everyone points out the differences, share just as many similarities to each other. When they rage, they show a fury that goes unlike any other. When they suffer, they show a level of shared pain that affects everything around them. When they show joy, it goes forth and touches others like bounding static. The Abyssal Sirens who follow Phelegethon believe that emotion is like a rock thrown into the water. The bigger and more violent it is, the more ripples it will create and affect all around it. As such, the Sirens of Dark Passions seek to stoke dark and destructive impulses to empower both themselves and others.<br /> <br /> (Ideas: An idea I have for Dark Passions is that these people can be a multitude of Sirens. Some want to actually better people through pain, making them suffer and leaving them to either sink or swim. Some want to escape from their own negative emotions, and as such lash them onto other people. Some want to gain Pneuma and keep it, and don't care about what means they must go to gain it. As a whole, I believe that these are the Sirens who are fine playing the &quot;Villain&quot; role, be it to dominate the world or to make people rise up together against a common threat)<br /> <br /> <b>Cocytus, The Current of Dark Wisdom</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I admire your resolve to figure out this much and get this far. Although you're still foolish to think that you're entitled to this knowledge. It's such a shame though. The obituary's going to have an extra name on it in tomorrow's papers.&quot; <b>A Polarian of Cocytus</b></i><br /> <i>&quot;What are you willing to suffer for the knowledge I've acquired? I've suffered to gain this, and for something this mindbreaking, I'll expect the same payment to learn it from me.&quot; <b>A Gardenian of Cocytus</b></i><br /> <br /> Perhaps one thing that is clear about the depths is that they're not visible to the surface. If you want to see what lies underneath, you'll need several things for it. An oxygen tank to survive down there, scuba gear to get down there and a flashlight and googles to even see. But there's still a danger in the depths that nobody prepares for, like bloodthirsty fish biting off your arm or water pressure beginning to cave in your skull. If you truly wish to know things, you must be prepared for what you must do to reach it and what you will suffer for learning it. The Current of Dark Wisdom believes in this, and as such they are willing to wontonly throw themselves upon any scrap of forbidden or taboo knowledge others won't tolerate.<br /> <br /> (Ideas: I imagine these to be the Sirens who are kind of like the Current of Wisdom, except they're willing to do ANYTHING for knowledge with a thirst the entirety of the Deluge cannot contain. I imagine these beings to be rulebreakers, adventure archaeologists to dangerous places, and even abusers with Verses and the like. I don't know, think of it as &quot;Learn ALL The Things!&quot; taken to an extreme)<br /> <br /> <b>Lethe, The Current of Mankind's Victory</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Who cares if a few little birds get uprooted? This housing division will make more money for us and give some nice places for people to live in.&quot; <b>A Freshwater of Lethe</b></i><br /> <i>&quot;There's loads of money and profit to be made here. It's much better to be on the winning side.&quot; <b>A Tropicana of Lethe</b></i><br /> <br /> Mankind is a creative, sapient animal, able to adapt to circumstances that nature throws at them. For the longest time, humanity has drawn their living resources and inspiration from nature, and have given in return for forms of worship and praise. This has gone on no more. Since the Industrial Revolution, Humanity had simply forgotten all about nature except for what they can take from it. They rip apart trees and dig up oils to fuel their precious machines and make more wonders from what they take. This fervor for technology and ambition for more has made nature mean nothing to them. So what if they take more than they give? Humanity's the most important, they'll keep surviving even if they must wipe out all else.<br /> <br /> (Ideas: I imagine these Sirens to be like the Sirens who resonate more with their human side rather than their Siren side, rejecting it as humanity (as in the people who are mostly the reason this current exists) rejects nature. Perhaps they're people who have dealt with human cruelty and feel like they don't want to be the ones suffering from them, so they point it at nature instead. And finally, there are Sirens who are so selfish and self-serving that they simply want the benefits of screwing over nature. Although regardless, this current, along with Primordial Darkness, tend to get the most visting experiments from Echidna. :3)<br /> <br /> <b>Styx, The Current of Primordial Darkness</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Who cares if some mud men are lost under the waves? They were going to ruin this beautiful river and it's ecology just to dam it up for their hyrdoelectric stations.&quot; <b>A Gardenia of Styx</b><br /> &quot;Why anyone would be happy to ruin nature is beyond me. Karma is a bitch though, and it's a good thing I'm one too.&quot; <b>A Discordian of Styx</b></i><br /> <br /> Nature is a living and breathing ecosystem. Every animal plays a part in it, be it predator or prey, living lives together before dying to give more to the cycle of natural life. However, a strange creature rose out from the rest, a nature born of mud and land and air. They proclaimed themselves better than the cycle, and tried separating themselves from it with their higher thought and ingenuity. For a time, this was fine, for the cycle didn't suffer for their leaving. But that time has ended at the Industrial Revolution. Humanity grew ambitious and prideful, deciding to take from the cycle and give nothing but pollution and corruption in return. They hunt animals to extinction for trinkets, they deprive nature of homes to build their own, and all the while they've fought against and killed each other on the pettiest of things on the basis of &quot;difference&quot;. No more. The moment the mud monkeys forgot about nature was the moment that their time has passed. It's time for nature to take back what belongs to it, in force.<br /> <br /> (Ideas: I think these Sirens are both similar and opposite to Mankind's Victory. They resonate to nature instead of humanity and reject humanity instead. They perhaps are intimate to nature's brutality and point it against Humanity instead. Perhaps in the vein that Mankind's Victory can have Sirens who are selfish to a point that it devestates other people, I would say that Primordial Darkness are hateful of people and believes that nature/animals should have the upper hand. Would it be breaking the rules if I noted their similarities to a certain group of people noted for crazy actions for nature or not? I'll just send it in a private message in that case if it is)<br /> <br /> <b>Acheron, The Current of Apocalypse</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Who even gives a shit about anything anymore? Nature is brutal, humanity is brutal. It's better to not be on either side at all.&quot; <b>A Discordian of Acheron</b><br /> &quot;I am the harbinger of the next world, filled with water cracked cities and drowned corpses of all! Don't fight it, just dunk your heads under and breathe! Breathe until the bubbles stop! Breathe in the Deluge!&quot; <b>A Vaporian of Acheron</b><br /> <br /> Nature and Humanity are similar. They're both brutal to each other and anything that threatens them, they have entire histories dedicated to killing themselves over survival. This world is full of tragedies upon tragedies and everyone and everything tries to write them off as &quot;necessary&quot;. This current is perhaps the most radical and most distasteful out of all the Abyssal Currents, for they have come to the conclusion that neither nature nor humanity are worth upholding. They decide that the Deluge is better than to let the corruption in both survive.<br /> <br /> (Ideas: These Sirens are flat out batshit insane no matter how you look at it. They may have different backstories. Some were batshit from the beginning and decided to destroy it all. Some have come to the conclusion from the end of a list of tragedies that happened to them and thus are broken individuals before they even Drowned. Perhaps some decided that the works of other currents weren't worthwhile and the Deluge was truly immanent, so they decide to hasten it's coming. They're probably hated by both Styx and Lethe and Echidna and saying you're a part of this current is the equivalent of suicide. Socially and pinning a target on your face)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T15:54:11-08:00","id":797539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797489#post797489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like all of these. Sorry that I haven't been much active, trying to get motivated for making Siren after some disappointing thoughts came up, but enough about those. :3 Have made these if it helps cover the Abyssal Currents.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to apologize for things that are going on in real life. Stuff happens. Go ahead and take whatever time you need. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Phelegethon, The Current of Dark Passions</b><br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> (Ideas: An idea I have for Dark Passions is that these people can be a multitude of Sirens. Some want to actually better people through pain, making them suffer and leaving them to either sink or swim. Some want to escape from their own negative emotions, and as such lash them onto other people. Some want to gain Pneuma and keep it, and don't care about what means they must go to gain it. As a whole, I believe that these are the Sirens who are fine playing the &quot;Villain&quot; role, be it to dominate the world or to make people rise up together against a common threat) </div> </div> </div>I can totally see these Sirens believing themselves to &quot;play the role&quot;. Struggle does build character, after all. Besides, all of the other goody-two-shoes Sirens are only coddling humanity and make them weak. Effectively, this Current might produce scarily-effective &quot;Dark Magical Girl&quot; versions of Sirens. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cocytus, The Current of Dark Wisdom</b><br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> (Ideas: I imagine these to be the Sirens who are kind of like the Current of Wisdom, except they're willing to do ANYTHING for knowledge with a thirst the entirety of the Deluge cannot contain. I imagine these beings to be rulebreakers, adventure archaeologists to dangerous places, and even abusers with Verses and the like. I don't know, think of it as &quot;Learn ALL The Things!&quot; taken to an extreme) </div> </div> </div>I think these Sirens would pay any price if it meant getting a little closer to stopping The Deluge in this world. They'd take lives and sell souls if it meant being able to stop some catastrophic thing from happening. At best, they're Well-Intentioned Extremists. At worst, they're Dr. Belloq and Major Toht, looking for the Ark of the Covenant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Lethe, The Current of Mankind's Victory</b><br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> (Ideas: I imagine these Sirens to be like the Sirens who resonate more with their human side rather than their Siren side, rejecting it as humanity (as in the people who are mostly the reason this current exists) rejects nature. Perhaps they're people who have dealt with human cruelty and feel like they don't want to be the ones suffering from them, so they point it at nature instead. And finally, there are Sirens who are so selfish and self-serving that they simply want the benefits of screwing over nature. Although regardless, this current, along with Primordial Darkness, tend to get the most visting experiments from Echidna. :3) </div> </div> </div>And Sirens who follow Lethe are the ones that are allied with the Flensers, if I recall correctly. Given that Sirens are able to sense others and even call out to others, I presume that any Siren who follows Lethe, regardless of whether they are allied with the Flensers or not, are immediately under suspicion by other Sirens. But at least the Sirens of Lethe are on a winning side, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Styx, The Current of Primordial Darkness</b><br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> (Ideas: I think these Sirens are both similar and opposite to Mankind's Victory. They resonate to nature instead of humanity and reject humanity instead. They perhaps are intimate to nature's brutality and point it against Humanity instead. Perhaps in the vein that Mankind's Victory can have Sirens who are selfish to a point that it devestates other people, I would say that Primordial Darkness are hateful of people and believes that nature/animals should have the upper hand. Would it be breaking the rules if I noted their similarities to a certain group of people noted for crazy actions for nature or not? I'll just send it in a private message in that case if it is) </div> </div> </div>I did write up a bunch of plot points about nature slowly becoming restless and attempting to rise up against humanity. While nature's fury isn't necessarily antagonistic towards Sirens, it doesn't serve to assist the Sirens in their attempt to better the world. You can't really reason with a particularly harsh Winter or a sudden growth of aggressive kudzu. That having been said, Sirens of Styx are probably the ones that hold the leash and direct nature's fury towards humanity. I would love to see how a Siren of Lethe with a cell of Flensers handles an attack by a Siren of Styx commanding beasts. <br /> <br /> As for the similarities to a certain group, I believe it would be in bad taste to directly reference them in a post or within the splatbook. If anything, maybe a quick mention of Sirens of Styx attempting to influence certain groups or push for certain mindsets. Nothing that's meant to demonize groups, but something to give breadcrumbs for possible plot hooks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Acheron, The Current of Apocalypse</b><br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> (Ideas: These Sirens are flat out batshit insane no matter how you look at it. They may have different backstories. Some were batshit from the beginning and decided to destroy it all. Some have come to the conclusion from the end of a list of tragedies that happened to them and thus are broken individuals before they even Drowned. Perhaps some decided that the works of other currents weren't worthwhile and the Deluge was truly immanent, so they decide to hasten it's coming. They're probably hated by both Styx and Lethe and Echidna and saying you're a part of this current is the equivalent of suicide. Socially and pinning a target on your face) </div> </div> </div>Definitely liking how Sirens have all these factions and alliances. Most Sirens and humanity vs. Lethe and the Flensers vs. Styx and nature's fury vs. Echidna, her Sirens, and the Vodianoi vs. Acheron and The Deluge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T17:03:03-08:00","id":797554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797539#post797539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to apologize for things that are going on in real life. Stuff happens. Go ahead and take whatever time you need. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And now for real life info with Kara: Sally (aka Saulot) is the master of senseless apologies for no reason whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797539#post797539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely liking how Sirens have all these factions and alliances. Most Sirens and humanity vs. Lethe and the Flensers vs. Styx and nature's fury vs. Echidna, her Sirens, and the Vodianoi vs. Acheron and The Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are in an agreement on this. I like the variation and the amount of factions that can go in just about any direction; and that's without involving anything else in the World of Darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T17:51:49-08:00","id":797568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797539#post797539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can totally see these Sirens believing themselves to &quot;play the role&quot;. Struggle does build character, after all. Besides, all of the other goody-two-shoes Sirens are only coddling humanity and make them weak. Effectively, this Current might produce scarily-effective &quot;Dark Magical Girl&quot; versions of Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797539#post797539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think these Sirens would pay any price if it meant getting a little closer to stopping The Deluge in this world. They'd take lives and sell souls if it meant being able to stop some catastrophic thing from happening. At best, they're Well-Intentioned Extremists. At worst, they're Dr. Belloq and Major Toht, looking for the Ark of the Covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh me gusta. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797539#post797539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Sirens who follow Lethe are the ones that are allied with the Flensers, if I recall correctly. Given that Sirens are able to sense others and even call out to others, I presume that any Siren who follows Lethe, regardless of whether they are allied with the Flensers or not, are immediately under suspicion by other Sirens. But at least the Sirens of Lethe are on a winning side, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but now that I think of it, I would say that their relationship with the Flensers are tenuous at best, since they need to keep an eye on themselves since they do target Sirens. Who knows when they decide they'll make Siren Sushi out of a member of the crew? As for the winning side stuff, let's just say at least a minor inspiration for them are the Seers of the Throne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797539#post797539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did write up a bunch of plot points about nature slowly becoming restless and attempting to rise up against humanity. While nature's fury isn't necessarily antagonistic towards Sirens, it doesn't serve to assist the Sirens in their attempt to better the world. You can't really reason with a particularly harsh Winter or a sudden growth of aggressive kudzu. That having been said, Sirens of Styx are probably the ones that hold the leash and direct nature's fury towards humanity. I would love to see how a Siren of Lethe with a cell of Flensers handles an attack by a Siren of Styx commanding beasts.<br /> <br /> As for the similarities to a certain group, I believe it would be in bad taste to directly reference them in a post or within the splatbook. If anything, maybe a quick mention of Sirens of Styx attempting to influence certain groups or push for certain mindsets. Nothing that's meant to demonize groups, but something to give breadcrumbs for possible plot hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't name the group, I simply meant to point out how the Sirens of Styx would be like, but up to eleven because supernatural. Purely for example of course, I wouldn't name the group inside the corebook. Also, I wonder, how should we play on those plot points? I don't know whether we should go completely with the &quot;Nature is alive and trying to kill humanity&quot;. Let's say the amount of nature actively trying to bring about humanity's downfall is proportionate to the amount of humanity trying to bring about nature's downfall. That way, not all of nature has to be violent like not all of humanity is either. Also fits in with the balance theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797539#post797539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely liking how Sirens have all these factions and alliances. Most Sirens and humanity vs. Lethe and the Flensers vs. Styx and nature's fury vs. Echidna, her Sirens, and the Vodianoi vs. Acheron and The Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797554#post797554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now for real life info with Kara: Sally (aka Saulot) is the master of senseless apologies for no reason whatsoever</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. ^^&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T19:32:41-08:00","id":797604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797568#post797568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, but now that I think of it, I would say that their relationship with the Flensers are tenuous at best, since they need to keep an eye on themselves since they do target Sirens. Who knows when they decide they'll make Siren Sushi out of a member of the crew? As for the winning side stuff, let's just say at least a minor inspiration for them are the Seers of the Throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. I'm just saying that a Siren of Lethe who is allied with the Flensers know that they need to make themselves invaluable. If a Flenser loses one of their main advantages when it comes to finding Sirens <i>(that advantage being the Siren of Lethe's call)</i>, it'll probably be a while before they would be able to go out on an easy hunt. If anything, Siren Sushi is more of a punishment for Sirens who fail to help out in a hunt. It's less of an inevitability and more of an encouragement not to screw things up.<br /> <br /> And then, there are also crafty Sirens who ally themselves with the Flensers only to lead them into an ambush by their own Shoal. Underhanded? Obviously. Well-deserved? Probably.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't name the group, I simply meant to point out how the Sirens of Styx would be like, but up to eleven because supernatural. Purely for example of course, I wouldn't name the group inside the corebook. Also, I wonder, how should we play on those plot points? I don't know whether we should go completely with the &quot;Nature is alive and trying to kill humanity&quot;. Let's say the amount of nature actively trying to bring about humanity's downfall is proportionate to the amount of humanity trying to bring about nature's downfall. That way, not all of nature has to be violent like not all of humanity is either. Also fits in with the balance theme. </div> </div> </div>I would say that, gradually, nature is attempting to enforce borders so that ecosystems can recover. A mountain hiking trail is suddenly closed down because of the heightened frequency of rock slides. A mansion built in the middle of nowhere is plagued by wild animals and weeds. However, every now and then the recovery process becomes aggravated. A strange weather pattern has shut down the freeways going into a town. A freak wave takes over and brings down a fishing ship without warning. a pack of wolves comes across an isolated camping site and unleashes all hell on the unsuspecting campers. Nature itself is not making active or overt attempts to regain ground, but there is some sort of supernatural awareness that permeates the world and targets specific individuals or areas that have overstepped their bounds. It is some sort of primal force that is attempting to bring the world back into its natural state. In a sense, it's less of a &quot;Nature knows of mankind's transgressions&quot; and is more of a &quot;nature needs to refresh, so it's just gonna purge some things to make some space&quot; with a splash of &quot;something's wrong, so let's start with the purging on over-drive to get everything removed and make a clean slate&quot;. Sorta like nature's immune system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797554#post797554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are in an agreement on this. I like the variation and the amount of factions that can go in just about any direction; and that's without involving anything else in the World of Darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I'm actually intimidated at incorporating the other splats into how a Siren game would play. It would be like adding multiple wild cards and alliances that can go sour at the tip of a hat. I wish I had a flow chart program so I could actually map out all the possible relationships between these factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T19:52:56-08:00","id":797614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797604#post797604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I'm actually intimidated at incorporating the other splats into how a Siren game would play. It would be like adding multiple wild cards and alliances that can go sour at the tip of a hat. I wish I had a flow chart program so I could actually map out all the possible relationships between these factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really for the Storyteller to decide ultimately regardless of how it looks from without. For all intents a Storyteller could make an Ordo Dracul/Current of Harmony relation work out just fine if they feel they can justify it well enough even if the two would otherwise not see each other very favorably; not to mention how me and Sally tend to mix-match oWoD and nWoD in our games, even when we lean towards one way or the other which adds even more factions on our list. The way I see it that just gives so much more options to play around with and if someone else becomes intimidated they ought to go the White Wolf way of just tossing what they feel they can't grasp on out the window and make their own spin on the material. It's opinion and probably won't work flawlessly in practice, if even in theory, but why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T22:13:59-08:00","id":797664,"title":"","content":"As I love all things ocean-related, I am keeping an eye on this. Does this project have anything to do, by the way, with Undine: The Emergence?<br /> <br /> I would also like to throw out there that the ocean is swimming with microbial organisms that consume pollutants such as oil and which are responsible for the algal blooms that will suddenly decimate marine populations with their penchant for oxygen depletion and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T23:43:57-08:00","id":797686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797614#post797614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really for the Storyteller to decide ultimately regardless of how it looks from without. For all intents a Storyteller could make an Ordo Dracul/Current of Harmony relation work out just fine if they feel they can justify it well enough even if the two would otherwise not see each other very favorably; not to mention how me and Sally tend to mix-match oWoD and nWoD in our games, even when we lean towards one way or the other which adds even more factions on our list. The way I see it that just gives so much more options to play around with and if someone else becomes intimidated they ought to go the White Wolf way of just tossing what they feel they can't grasp on out the window and make their own spin on the material. It's opinion and probably won't work flawlessly in practice, if even in theory, but why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Fair enough. I do believe that there should be a little snippet on inter-supernatural relationships between the Sirens and the other creatures. Nothing as extensive as <b><i>Beast</i></b>, but enough so that there's something to incorporate into play. I'm not necessarily as experienced with any of the other gamelines aside from <b><i>Hunter</i></b>, so I don't believe I'll be able to give that much input.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797664#post797664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I love all things ocean-related, I am keeping an eye on this. Does this project have anything to do, by the way, with Undine: The Emergence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, <b><i>Siren </i></b>started off on the RPG.net forums around March 2013 and discussion died a month later. With <b><i>Undine</i></b>, I'm not sure when the development began, but the author stated that they started working on it some time early 2013 with their official post being on November 2013. I think that both started development in parallel but are technically two different beasts entirely, as Undine is based around a &quot;Coming of Age&quot; story while Siren was originally a game of balance between humanity and nature. Essentially, &quot;The Little Mermaid&quot; vs. &quot;Ferngully&quot;. <br /> <br /> That having been said, there are some similarities between the two, both back then and now. The Fuel Stat for both were initally &quot;Breath&quot; as in air and was more literal; eventually, we changed &quot;Breath&quot; to &quot;Pneuma&quot;, to refer to the breath of life and the soul, so technically Sirens are soul-drinkers who can kiss away someone's life-force. Undines also have a &quot;mermaid&quot; form that is composed of various parts known as Curiosities, like Sirens and their Alterations. Both Undines and Sirens can partially manifest their sea form, though Undines are under a timer an Sirens need to focus on maintaining their manifestation. Notably, Undines build their Curiosities from the start and stay at 5 Curiosities. A Siren's Alterations are more variable and the number of Alterations a Siren may have is limited by her Power Stat. Also, Siren didn't start codifying Alterations until this thread, a good two years after. Undines also mention something about &quot;Natural Waters&quot;, which I assume would function similarly to the Favored Waters that Sirens have, though there's not much to go on, as the document for Undine omits a large chunk of what Natural Waters are supposed to be. I assume it involves the X-Axis that the Undines have, but there's not much mentioned.<br /> <br /> I think that, if anything, Undine and Siren shared quite a bit of similarities due to what the source material is based off of, but they're two different gamelines. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also like to throw out there that the ocean is swimming with microbial organisms that consume pollutants such as oil and which are responsible for the algal blooms that will suddenly decimate marine populations with their penchant for oxygen depletion and whatnot. </div> </div> </div>I would like to say without sarcasm that this is actually pretty interesting. This may make a good example for either the Discordians or as a reason that nature's fury is attempting to make a clean slate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T15:40:56-08:00","id":798001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797604#post797604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that, gradually, nature is attempting to enforce borders so that ecosystems can recover. A mountain hiking trail is suddenly closed down because of the heightened frequency of rock slides. A mansion built in the middle of nowhere is plagued by wild animals and weeds. However, every now and then the recovery process becomes aggravated. A strange weather pattern has shut down the freeways going into a town. A freak wave takes over and brings down a fishing ship without warning. a pack of wolves comes across an isolated camping site and unleashes all hell on the unsuspecting campers. Nature itself is not making active or overt attempts to regain ground, but there is some sort of supernatural awareness that permeates the world and targets specific individuals or areas that have overstepped their bounds. It is some sort of primal force that is attempting to bring the world back into its natural state. In a sense, it's less of a &quot;Nature knows of mankind's transgressions&quot; and is more of a &quot;nature needs to refresh, so it's just gonna purge some things to make some space&quot; with a splash of &quot;something's wrong, so let's start with the purging on over-drive to get everything removed and make a clean slate&quot;. Sorta like nature's immune system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand and get behind the &quot;nature needs to recover&quot; part, at least up until it starts to wantonly attack towns and places. I can understand nature trying to stop construction and the like, but going against stuff that's been established as &quot;civilization&quot; without much of a reason is the only part that puts me off. Perhaps the reason that nature would go into civilization is because something needs to be stopped that's been planned in civilization and <b>right now</b>? Perhaps &quot;Nature&quot; (whatever we decide to call it, I fear we might be stepping on Werewolf's toes if we call it Gaia) has a perpetual form of &quot;Trace&quot; on and is in just as much danger of ripping itself as human civilization could? Think for example that with all the nuclear weaponry in the world, humanity is capable of wiping itself out, hence, a manmade apocalypse. Nature is capable of doing the same thing if it dictated it. Perhaps this &quot;Nature&quot; is a sibling of sorts to Ceto? But perhaps instead of water, this is &quot;Land&quot; or &quot;Air&quot;? And when Ceto gave her life or whatever we plan for her, this being reacted violently and as such dictates the nature side of the squabble or is an intimate part of it and is a sometimes-friend, sometimes-foe of the Sirens? Now I'm afraid I described the <b>Wyld </b>which was in WtA. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797604#post797604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I'm actually intimidated at incorporating the other splats into how a Siren game would play. It would be like adding multiple wild cards and alliances that can go sour at the tip of a hat. I wish I had a flow chart program so I could actually map out all the possible relationships between these factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that we need to go much further than a crossovers section to be honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=797664#post797664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I love all things ocean-related, I am keeping an eye on this. Does this project have anything to do, by the way, with Undine: The Emergence?<br /> <br /> I would also like to throw out there that the ocean is swimming with microbial organisms that consume pollutants such as oil and which are responsible for the algal blooms that will suddenly decimate marine populations with their penchant for oxygen depletion and whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had NO idea that Undine existed. Like Reaper says, this game is mostly based off of the ideas of Siren the Surfacing rather than on Undine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T17:33:35-08:00","id":798035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798001#post798001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand and get behind the &quot;nature needs to recover&quot; part, at least up until it starts to wantonly attack towns and places. I can understand nature trying to stop construction and the like, but going against stuff that's been established as &quot;civilization&quot; without much of a reason is the only part that puts me off. Perhaps the reason that nature would go into civilization is because something needs to be stopped that's been planned in civilization and <b>right now</b>? Perhaps &quot;Nature&quot; (whatever we decide to call it, I fear we might be stepping on Werewolf's toes if we call it Gaia) has a perpetual form of &quot;Trace&quot; on and is in just as much danger of ripping itself as human civilization could? Think for example that with all the nuclear weaponry in the world, humanity is capable of wiping itself out, hence, a manmade apocalypse. Nature is capable of doing the same thing if it dictated it. Perhaps this &quot;Nature&quot; is a sibling of sorts to Ceto? But perhaps instead of water, this is &quot;Land&quot; or &quot;Air&quot;? And when Ceto gave her life or whatever we plan for her, this being reacted violently and as such dictates the nature side of the squabble or is an intimate part of it and is a sometimes-friend, sometimes-foe of the Sirens? Now I'm afraid I described the <b>Wyld </b>which was in WtA. &gt;&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Let's talk about what is the overarching idea. First off, <b>The Deluge</b> is the Big Bad Thing that Sirens want to stop. It is bad for <b>Humanity </b>and it is bad for <b>Nature</b>. It is also, presumably, Nature's Final Solution. The Deluge is meant to kill off all life because Humanity in one reality decided to overstep their boundaries and do their Small Bad Things against Nature. Eventually, Nature becomes fed up by Humanity and pushes the Reset Button, drowning everything in The Deluge. For Nature, The Deluge is unfortunate but it is something that can be recovered from, because Nature is nothing if not patient; The Deluge is meant to be damage control, keeping Humanity from doing something <i>really stupid</i> like starting a nuclear winter. For Humanity, The Deluge is the Apocalypse that means the end of their existence. Sirens are meant to calm Nature down so that it doesn't want to start The Deluge while making sure Humanity doesn't do stupid things that would cause Nature to want to get revenge. Or to keep Humanity from harming Nature to an unrecoverable state. <br /> <br /> Let's say that Nature and Humanity have set goals. Nature wants to allow life on Earth to grow and to maintain itself so that life has something to survive on. Humanity, in broad strokes, wants to flourish as a species and expand their domain. For the most part, these ideas do not clash. Humanity is a part of life on Earth and Nature would allow them to grow. However, when Humanity's desire to flourish or expand comes at the expense of other life or it destroys part of the Earth, Nature feels the urge to lash back in order to put Humanity back in its place. While most Sirens are attempting to appease Nature, Sirens of Styx are attempting to direct this rage towards Humanity. Although this is going to destroy Humanity, at least it's going to stop The Deluge from wiping out <i>all</i> terrestrial life. In contrast, Sirens of Lethe, who are allied with Humanity and sometimes the Flensers, are attempting to effectively <i>kill</i> Nature in order to completely prevent The Deluge from happening in general. The world may become some sort of wasteland because of this, but at least humanity will be able to survive, right? In a second contrast, Sirens of Acheron <i>want</i> The Deluge because they've given up and are trying to accelerate the process. Sirens of Styx hate them because they are willing to aggravate Nature rather than allowing Nature to release its anger. Sirens of Lethe hate them because they are bringing Humanity to an early death. <br /> <br /> I think the issue might be that it is implied that Nature is sentient and <i>wants</i> to hurt Humanity in an actively malevolent way. Granted, I did make it seem that civilization was being targeted, but I didn't really intend that to happen. Perhaps it would be better to say that Nature resents Humanity and its resentment trickles down to animals and plant life. Animals that have been affected are now more hostile towards humanity while plant life disregards civilization and attempts to reclaim land through growth. This effect is more pronounced in areas where humanity has, in effect, overstepped their boundaries, like a mansion that was built in the middle of nowhere and disturbed the land around it. The more resentful of Humanity that Nature feels, the more volatile the reaction when the resentment trickles down. This is why Sirens feel the need to fight against some organizations that want to expand aggressively and without concern for the world; the Sirens are attempting to eliminate what would cause any resentment. <br /> <br /> As for examples of resentment-influenced phenomena, animals that have grown to be monstrously large, like a spider the size of a minivan or something like Kujo, aggressively expanding plant-life, something like a carnivorous flower that releases pheromones to make humans think that its an attractive person or a species of fungus that releases spores that can grow within lungs. This resentment can even manifest in things like the weather or in the earth. <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to diminish your idea. I'm just giving a suggestion for what could be an interesting concept that hasn't been approached in other game lines. I admit that I'm not familiar with <b><i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i></b>, but I feel that giving the planet a personification is something that is related to it. I also feel that having creatures feel the resentment from Nature and responding in kind fits with the idea of mediation in Siren. Effectively, no faction, Humanity, Nature, the Echidnal Sirens, the Abyssal Sirens, etc., are acting in pure malice. There are no mustache-twirling villains that are actively trying to do bad. Humanity wants to survive but its causing trouble for Nature. Nature resents Humanity, but is willing to wait it out unless Humanity does something stupid. That resentment trickles down and creates creatures that want to protect Nature by culling Humanity. Echidnal Sirens are attempting to outlast The Deluge when it's going to obviously happen. Abyssal Sirens are just following their ideal. Everyone has their own thing, which makes it difficult for Sirens to appease everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T14:21:59-08:00","id":798395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798035#post798035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Let's talk about what is the overarching idea. First off, <b>The Deluge</b> is the Big Bad Thing that Sirens want to stop. It is bad for <b>Humanity </b>and it is bad for <b>Nature</b>. It is also, presumably, Nature's Final Solution. The Deluge is meant to kill off all life because Humanity in one reality decided to overstep their boundaries and do their Small Bad Things against Nature. Eventually, Nature becomes fed up by Humanity and pushes the Reset Button, drowning everything in The Deluge. For Nature, The Deluge is unfortunate but it is something that can be recovered from, because Nature is nothing if not patient; The Deluge is meant to be damage control, keeping Humanity from doing something <i>really stupid</i> like starting a nuclear winter. For Humanity, The Deluge is the Apocalypse that means the end of their existence. Sirens are meant to calm Nature down so that it doesn't want to start The Deluge while making sure Humanity doesn't do stupid things that would cause Nature to want to get revenge. Or to keep Humanity from harming Nature to an unrecoverable state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I was under the impression that the Deluge was the end of everything though? Both Humanity and Nature would drown? I do like the &quot;Big Crunch&quot; idea though in the Deluge, with it working like a reset button. Eventually the water level will go back down, life will restart from the waters and even humanity could return. It actually brings to mind of the one Futurama Episode where they had a time machine and when at the end of the universe, the Big Crunch happened, and then the Big Bang happened again and reset time. Accelerating forwards shows them going back to the future with everything playing out exactly as it had been. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798035#post798035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say that Nature and Humanity have set goals. Nature wants to allow life on Earth to grow and to maintain itself so that life has something to survive on. Humanity, in broad strokes, wants to flourish as a species and expand their domain. For the most part, these ideas do not clash. Humanity is a part of life on Earth and Nature would allow them to grow. However, when Humanity's desire to flourish or expand comes at the expense of other life or it destroys part of the Earth, Nature feels the urge to lash back in order to put Humanity back in its place. While most Sirens are attempting to appease Nature, Sirens of Styx are attempting to direct this rage towards Humanity. Although this is going to destroy Humanity, at least it's going to stop The Deluge from wiping out <i>all</i> terrestrial life. In contrast, Sirens of Lethe, who are allied with Humanity and sometimes the Flensers, are attempting to effectively <i>kill</i> Nature in order to completely prevent The Deluge from happening in general. The world may become some sort of wasteland because of this, but at least humanity will be able to survive, right? In a second contrast, Sirens of Acheron <i>want</i> The Deluge because they've given up and are trying to accelerate the process. Sirens of Styx hate them because they are willing to aggravate Nature rather than allowing Nature to release its anger. Sirens of Lethe hate them because they are bringing Humanity to an early death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798035#post798035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue might be that it is implied that Nature is sentient and <i>wants</i> to hurt Humanity in an actively malevolent way. Granted, I did make it seem that civilization was being targeted, but I didn't really intend that to happen. Perhaps it would be better to say that Nature resents Humanity and its resentment trickles down to animals and plant life. Animals that have been affected are now more hostile towards humanity while plant life disregards civilization and attempts to reclaim land through growth. This effect is more pronounced in areas where humanity has, in effect, overstepped their boundaries, like a mansion that was built in the middle of nowhere and disturbed the land around it. The more resentful of Humanity that Nature feels, the more volatile the reaction when the resentment trickles down. This is why Sirens feel the need to fight against some organizations that want to expand aggressively and without concern for the world; the Sirens are attempting to eliminate what would cause any resentment.<br /> <br /> As for examples of resentment-influenced phenomena, animals that have grown to be monstrously large, like a spider the size of a minivan or something like Kujo, aggressively expanding plant-life, something like a carnivorous flower that releases pheromones to make humans think that its an attractive person or a species of fungus that releases spores that can grow within lungs. This resentment can even manifest in things like the weather or in the earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. So would this perhaps be somewhat like how &quot;Wounds&quot; are in Werewolf the Forsaken or &quot;Taints&quot; in Princess the Hopeful? Areas where Nature has had enough? Perhaps areas where nature were once Venerated but now are discarded and destroyed by humans? I really hope though that this idea isn't too similar to Spirits and their Loci. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798035#post798035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to diminish your idea. I'm just giving a suggestion for what could be an interesting concept that hasn't been approached in other game lines. I admit that I'm not familiar with <b><i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i></b>, but I feel that giving the planet a personification is something that is related to it. I also feel that having creatures feel the resentment from Nature and responding in kind fits with the idea of mediation in Siren. Effectively, no faction, Humanity, Nature, the Echidnal Sirens, the Abyssal Sirens, etc., are acting in pure malice. There are no mustache-twirling villains that are actively trying to do bad. Humanity wants to survive but its causing trouble for Nature. Nature resents Humanity, but is willing to wait it out unless Humanity does something stupid. That resentment trickles down and creates creatures that want to protect Nature by culling Humanity. Echidnal Sirens are attempting to outlast The Deluge when it's going to obviously happen. Abyssal Sirens are just following their ideal. Everyone has their own thing, which makes it difficult for Sirens to appease everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>To make it as short as I can, take Werewolf the Forsaken, replace Luna with Gaia (the personified earth) for Werewolves matron, add in loads of internal squabbling between the Tribes and make spirits generally nicer (save for Wyrm tainted ones) and you got Werewolf the Apocalypse. And I find this to be a fine idea. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:05:22-08:00","id":798525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798395#post798395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. I was under the impression that the Deluge was the end of everything though? Both Humanity and Nature would drown? I do like the &quot;Big Crunch&quot; idea though in the Deluge, with it working like a reset button. Eventually the water level will go back down, life will restart from the waters and even humanity could return. It actually brings to mind of the one Futurama Episode where they had a time machine and when at the end of the universe, the Big Crunch happened, and then the Big Bang happened again and reset time. Accelerating forwards shows them going back to the future with everything playing out exactly as it had been.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be entirely technical, I think the initial intention for The Deluge was to be a complete and total end of everything. Things do develop and require change and revision, though. In this revision, The Deluge is still something that is terrible overall because it kills off all of terrestrial life and probably some plant-life as well, but it's not 100% world-ending or malevolent. It's a fail-safe for the world, which makes it less &quot;bad&quot; and more &quot;natural occurrence for self-preservation&quot;.<br /> <br /> I should probably watch that episode, though. Sounds like it could provide inspiration. I do have to say, though, that The Deluge happening means that everything needs to start off from Square One, so the amoebas and surviving ocean creatures would need to go through the many years of evolution to get back to the state of &quot;humanity&quot;. By that time, the planet might actually be engulfed by the sun or whatever cosmic disaster is going to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. So would this perhaps be somewhat like how &quot;Wounds&quot; are in Werewolf the Forsaken or &quot;Taints&quot; in Princess the Hopeful? Areas where Nature has had enough? Perhaps areas where nature were once Venerated but now are discarded and destroyed by humans? I really hope though that this idea isn't too similar to Spirits and their Loci. </div> </div> </div>Hopefully, this idea won't be similar to Spirits. I was thinking that these areas are a sort of Monster Breeding Ground that cause things to enter it to mutate rapidly due to the level of resentment. Say that the location in question is tied to the largest tree in the middle of a clearing in the forest. A couple decides to have a picnic underneath the tree, where they carve their initials into the bark. Because of this, the creatures that nest within the tree, say a flock of birds or a couple of squirrels, are affected by Nature's resentment as the couple decided to disrespect nature by staking a claim in something <i>(carving the bark of the tree).</i> Over the next few days, the couple are harassed by vicious sparrows whenever they leave the house and mischievous squirrels popping in and out of their car. The assault last for some time until one of the sparrows manage to draw blood, just enough that it could be considered a serious injury. The animals take their leave and return to the tree, happy that they have managed to take revenge for nature. The carving itself is removed through the bark miraculously healing over.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the police have marked off a site up in the mountains. The spot they have taped off is an overlook over the town, something akin to a make-out point in an 80's era movie. However, nowadays it's more of a photo-op background with shoe prints embedded into the stone when it isn't covered by graffiti. The official statement by the police is that they're attempting to keep the area undisturbed for the local wildlife while rumors are flowing that it's because someone reported a dead body. Technically, neither is wrong. A hiker found a dessicated corpse that was hanging from the rock by some vines. The body belonged to a nature enthusiast who enjoyed visiting the spot and was last seen a few days ago. From the condition of the body, it would seem as if she had died months ago. Even stranger was the oddly healthy glow of the vines that covered her body.<br /> <br /> Finally, there's a warehouse in the far side of the city that has been untouched for decades. No one really talks about it aside from the talk about it being haunted by Victorian-era ghosts and such. More often, it's used as a sort of rite of initiation for teenagers who want to make a name for themselves in their circle of friends. In all honesty, it's not much to look at. Sure, the interior is pretty gloomy and spooky, but it's not too different than most abandoned buildings. Rather dusty with leaks and cracks here and there. Of course, that's just the area above ground. Underneath the foundation is a series of storage rooms and maintenance areas covered in spider webs. It's obvious that the spiders have found themselves a nice haven to be undisturbed, though a closer look into the depths of the basement will reveal creatures as large as cats and owls being caught within the webbing. At its deepest, there are old mannequins that have been repurposed into spider nests in the middle of the webs with a storm of tarantula-sized black widows crawling up the walls.If anyone were to look even closer, they would realize that those arachnids the size of dinner plates are actually <i>babies</i>.<br /> <br /> These areas of concentrated resentment probably come in two styles. The first is more of a response-based &quot;trap&quot;, where the resentment only comes out when the area has been affected. Effectively, these areas bleed resentment and will eventually heal over once amends have been made or revenge has been dealt. The second is more of a concentrated weapon, where the resentment has been bleeding out and is stored within the creatures that exist in the area. These areas are festering with resentment and will continue to bleed resentment, influencing what is at the focal point the most. For the first, there's nothing to really do other than leaving the area alone until whatever resentment that has built up is released, like a cut that needs to heal. With the second, destroying the focal point would prevent the process from continuing, like removing a cancerous tumor.<br /> <br /> We should probably think of names if we're using these, now that I think about it. Maybe the creatures could be called <b>Furies </b>after the creatures of vengeance that emerged from the earth when blood fell after Aphrodite's birth <i>(ripped completely from Wikipedia). </i>I wouldn't know where to go on for the areas of resentment. Possibly Sanctuaries as they are meant to be areas that are influenced by Nature?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To make it as short as I can, take Werewolf the Forsaken, replace Luna with Gaia (the personified earth) for Werewolves matron, add in loads of internal squabbling between the Tribes and make spirits generally nicer (save for Wyrm tainted ones) and you got Werewolf the Apocalypse. And I find this to be a fine idea. :3 </div> </div> </div>Ah. Alrighty. Well, we have Ceto and Echidna as main players in terms of patrons for Sirens, with Nature being a fairly neutral party acting in response to Humanity. The Flensers would be the main thorn when it comes to Humanity, while the Breathless are rogue agents and the Banshees are the thorn for Humanity. The Furies are generally hostile and affect Humanity the most but can blindly attack those who interfere with their plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T19:35:45-08:00","id":800046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798525#post798525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be entirely technical, I think the initial intention for The Deluge was to be a complete and total end of everything. Things do develop and require change and revision, though. In this revision, The Deluge is still something that is terrible overall because it kills off all of terrestrial life and probably some plant-life as well, but it's not 100% world-ending or malevolent. It's a fail-safe for the world, which makes it less &quot;bad&quot; and more &quot;natural occurrence for self-preservation&quot;.<br /> <br /> I should probably watch that episode, though. Sounds like it could provide inspiration. I do have to say, though, that The Deluge happening means that everything needs to start off from Square One, so the amoebas and surviving ocean creatures would need to go through the many years of evolution to get back to the state of &quot;humanity&quot;. By that time, the planet might actually be engulfed by the sun or whatever cosmic disaster is going to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, just a thought. And yes, the planet might die by then, but that's what the Song/Ceto(?) is trying to prevent. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798525#post798525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These areas of concentrated resentment probably come in two styles. The first is more of a response-based &quot;trap&quot;, where the resentment only comes out when the area has been affected. Effectively, these areas bleed resentment and will eventually heal over once amends have been made or revenge has been dealt. The second is more of a concentrated weapon, where the resentment has been bleeding out and is stored within the creatures that exist in the area. These areas are festering with resentment and will continue to bleed resentment, influencing what is at the focal point the most. For the first, there's nothing to really do other than leaving the area alone until whatever resentment that has built up is released, like a cut that needs to heal. With the second, destroying the focal point would prevent the process from continuing, like removing a cancerous tumor.<br /> <br /> We should probably think of names if we're using these, now that I think about it. Maybe the creatures could be called <b>Furies </b>after the creatures of vengeance that emerged from the earth when blood fell after Aphrodite's birth <i>(ripped completely from Wikipedia). </i>I wouldn't know where to go on for the areas of resentment. Possibly Sanctuaries as they are meant to be areas that are influenced by Nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. Pardon my lack of response, had to put some focus onto an argument elsewhere, now fully back...at least until college starts draining my soul next week. OTL<br /> Yes, Furies sound good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=798525#post798525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. Alrighty. Well, we have Ceto and Echidna as main players in terms of patrons for Sirens, with Nature being a fairly neutral party acting in response to Humanity. The Flensers would be the main thorn when it comes to Humanity, while the Breathless are rogue agents and the Banshees are the thorn for Humanity. The Furies are generally hostile and affect Humanity the most but can blindly attack those who interfere with their plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are Breathless rogue agents? I thought they were the Subsplat for Sirens? Or am I misinterpreting things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T20:52:24-08:00","id":800168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=800046#post800046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, just a thought. And yes, the planet might die by then, but that's what the Song/Ceto(?) is trying to prevent. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Ceto herself is probably fully for the prosperity of Humanity, which is why she called out to awaken the Sirens. As for The Song...we should probably make a quick blurb as to what these Big Names are supposed to mean in context with the Sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like this idea. Pardon my lack of response, had to put some focus onto an argument elsewhere, now fully back...at least until college starts draining my soul next week. OTL<br /> Yes, Furies sound good. </div> </div> </div>No worries. I'm dreading college as well. :/ <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How are Breathless rogue agents? I thought they were the Subsplat for Sirens? Or am I misinterpreting things? </div> </div> </div>While the Breathless are a good way for a Siren to effectively farm out some Pneuma from sympathy and such, they aren't exactly &quot;allied&quot; with Sirens. Essentially, these people spend most of their lives struggling and being pitied for being so tragic. They may be dragged into some addiction that is harming them while everyone around them is smothering them with empty words of sympathy and encouragements. Nothing wrong with that, but they've spent their entire lives with that sort of falseness, which I feel would embitter them.<br /> <br /> I think I would compare them to a mixture of Fetches and Stigmatics. If a Siren was able to Surface and Hear the Song, the Breathless were only able to Surface. They don't have that aspect of The Song within them, like Sirens or Banshees do, so they came back from The Deluge a bit off. They attempt to live out their lives, but they don't really feel...complete in a sense? They feel that their struggles are empty and are more of something that is dictated by fate. They are scarred, hateful individuals that want to feel that Breath of Life that they have lost.<br /> <br /> In terms of mechanics, the Breathless are a source of Pneuma for the Sirens, as they are surrounded by people who want them to feel loved. It's some sort of compulsion for these people, something that makes them want to love and protect the Breathless without anything in return. The Breathless produces Pneuma around them that may be used as Unconditional Love; Sirens who spend time around the Breathless can feel the Pneuma collecting around them. However, the Breathless is unable to feel Pneuma, as they were unable to Hear The Song, like the Sirens or the Banshees did. Because of this, the Breathless are devoid of the Breath of Life and do not retain Pneuma; Pneuma just flows around them. <br /> <br /> While the Breathless are a good feeding ground, they are also fairly unpredictable. The Song does not resonate within them, so Sirens cannot sense their presence. Sirens are also unable to Trace the Breathless or see the Breathless when they are Tracing. Some Sirens who have come across the Breathless have theorized that, because the Breathless lack the Breath of Life but managed to come back into this reality, they do not truly exist in the world. Both Sirens and Banshees were thrown back into this reality after hearing The Song, which gives them some hold in this reality. With the Breathless, their existence is more of an anomaly. Another property that the Breathless have is the ability to mute Verses that are sung in their presence. When a Siren attempts to invoke a Verse, she feels her voice disappear as soon as it leaves her mouth. The words are swallowed, the notes are diminished. Although the Breathless attracts the presence of people, it also draws the Verses into their void. While this would be a minor inconvenience when it comes to stationary Breathless, not all Breathless are docile, comatose individuals. Some of the Breathless attempt to fill their emptiness with meaning, throwing themselves into whatever they can to escape. Some take jobs as humanitarians or educators to feel some sort of importance. Others have taken the route of recreational drugs to attempt to feel something, anything. The worst-case scenario is if the Breathless decide to become killers or hunters. <br /> <br /> The Breathless are an unknown variable that could work for or against a Siren, depending on what path the Breathless takes. They aren't loyal subjects that will bow down to the Sirens, like a Ghoul to their Vampire. They're a double-edged sword that could be a serious issue for Sirens that only care for them as an easy way to gain Pneuma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T04:01:58-08:00","id":800504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=800168#post800168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries. I'm dreading college as well. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>You kids are so cute- I'M OLD.<br /> Carry on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T12:10:20-08:00","id":800676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=800168#post800168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. Ceto herself is probably fully for the prosperity of Humanity, which is why she called out to awaken the Sirens. As for The Song...we should probably make a quick blurb as to what these Big Names are supposed to mean in context with the Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to finish up the Lexicon. But in the Context we currently have, how about this? Sirens are made from people drowning in despair, although from them clawing their ways back up to the surface while being empowered by the Song, perhaps that's the metaphysical &quot;oomph&quot; that makes a Siren a Siren? I don't really know how to explain it other than a metaphysical phenomenon that echoes throughout time and draws people to surface. Perhaps it's what the Bloop was? Maybe the Song is Pneuma incarnate, the Breath of Life that refuses to die when everything else has.I have no idea for this at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=800168#post800168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I can imagine some Sirens trying to manipulate Breathless to do things based on what their Current is? Like killer breathless (amongst other types) could be amongst Dark Passions/Phelegethon. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:07:06-08:00","id":800816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=800676#post800676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to finish up the Lexicon. But in the Context we currently have, how about this? Sirens are made from people drowning in despair, although from them clawing their ways back up to the surface while being empowered by the Song, perhaps that's the metaphysical &quot;oomph&quot; that makes a Siren a Siren? I don't really know how to explain it other than a metaphysical phenomenon that echoes throughout time and draws people to surface. Perhaps it's what the Bloop was? Maybe the Song is Pneuma incarnate, the Breath of Life that refuses to die when everything else has.I have no idea for this at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty solid description of what The Song does. I was also kinda flip-flopping around what the first Breath of Life is, so The Song granting the Breath of Life sounds pretty strong. It would also justify why the Breathless are lacking the Breath of Life. I do feel that Surfacing should be a Big Name term, considering that Surfacing would make the difference between a Siren and a Banshee. Perhaps the Bloop was a physical manifestation of the Surfacing process in which a vast number of Sirens Surfaced in a remarkably short amount of time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. I can imagine some Sirens trying to manipulate Breathless to do things based on what their Current is? Like killer breathless (amongst other types) could be amongst Dark Passions/Phelegethon. </div> </div> </div>That would be interesting. It would definitely put importance on a Siren actually working alongside her Current, even if she is a Castaway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T23:03:11-08:00","id":801169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=800816#post800816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty solid description of what The Song does. I was also kinda flip-flopping around what the first Breath of Life is, so The Song granting the Breath of Life sounds pretty strong. It would also justify why the Breathless are lacking the Breath of Life. I do feel that Surfacing should be a Big Name term, considering that Surfacing would make the difference between a Siren and a Banshee. Perhaps the Bloop was a physical manifestation of the Surfacing process in which a vast number of Sirens Surfaced in a remarkably short amount of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I don't mind the Bloop being used, it was definitely discussed (or at least brought up) in the original thread. And now that I'm finishing up on Aquatic Form, I must ask. Is the transformation like a Werewolves where most clothes don't survive the transformation? At the least I can see a shirt surviving, but pants would be ripped with the Tail's appearance (perhaps not so for Freshwater Sirens with Amphibious Legs Alteration),<br /> <br /> Oh lord I already imagine a player coming up with a Stanza called &quot;Song of Houdini's Pants&quot; which basically works like the Werewolves Rite of Dedication (or whatever it's called, it's alternate name is &quot;Rite of Pants&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=800816#post800816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be interesting. It would definitely put importance on a Siren actually working alongside her Current, even if she is a Castaway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if Castaways would use Breathless in a special way. I mean, I can imagine them using Breathless as a way to get Pneuma as a whole (since that's what Sirens would generally do with Breathless when not current wise) but not having anything more special than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T00:08:48-08:00","id":801196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=801169#post801169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. I don't mind the Bloop being used, it was definitely discussed (or at least brought up) in the original thread. And now that I'm finishing up on Aquatic Form, I must ask. Is the transformation like a Werewolves where most clothes don't survive the transformation? At the least I can see a shirt surviving, but pants would be ripped with the Tail's appearance (perhaps not so for Freshwater Sirens with Amphibious Legs Alteration),<br /> <br /> Oh lord I already imagine a player coming up with a Stanza called &quot;Song of Houdini's Pants&quot; which basically works like the Werewolves Rite of Dedication (or whatever it's called, it's alternate name is &quot;Rite of Pants&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is that I was thinking about that about an hour ago and started reading the &quot;Magic Pants&quot; trope on TvTropes. Honestly, I can see the Alterations going two ways when it comes to clothes:<br /> <br /> 1) The clothes get ripped apart because, obviously, changing the mass and composition of one's body is going to affect the clothes in such a way. Alterations are considered to be physical, biological changes that affect the material world.<br /> <br /> 2) The clothes don't get ripped apart because the Siren's Aquatic Form is tied to her other self in The Deluge Reality. By using her Alterations or accessing her Aquatic Form, she's just pulling part of her existence in The Deluge into the other Reality. Alterations are considered to be metaphysical manifestations that become corporeal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know if Castaways would use Breathless in a special way. I mean, I can imagine them using Breathless as a way to get Pneuma as a whole (since that's what Sirens would generally do with Breathless when not current wise) but not having anything more special than that. </div> </div> </div>I would say that Castaways, despite not having a Current, are able to stop a Breathless from following a Current by virtue of what the Castaways are in comparison to the other Currents. The other Sirens are busy moving alongside a flow and want to bring the Breathless along for the ride. The Castaways, effectively being stationed on land or on a rock rather than flowing with the Currents, are introspective and, rather than trying to change the world, they want to take a minute to reflect before they take on a Current. A Castaway interacting with a Breathless would essentially be a sort of &quot;blind-leading-the-blind&quot; situation, but it would provide the Breathless with some sort of grounding influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T11:09:55-08:00","id":801514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=801196#post801196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The funny thing is that I was thinking about that about an hour ago and started reading the &quot;Magic Pants&quot; trope on TvTropes. Honestly, I can see the Alterations going two ways when it comes to clothes:<br /> <br /> 1) The clothes get ripped apart because, obviously, changing the mass and composition of one's body is going to affect the clothes in such a way. Alterations are considered to be physical, biological changes that affect the material world.<br /> <br /> 2) The clothes don't get ripped apart because the Siren's Aquatic Form is tied to her other self in The Deluge Reality. By using her Alterations or accessing her Aquatic Form, she's just pulling part of her existence in The Deluge into the other Reality. Alterations are considered to be metaphysical manifestations that become corporeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I would say perhaps that making Alterations pop up on human form would damage clothes whereas shifting to Aquatic Form makes them disappear?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=801196#post801196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that Castaways, despite not having a Current, are able to stop a Breathless from following a Current by virtue of what the Castaways are in comparison to the other Currents. The other Sirens are busy moving alongside a flow and want to bring the Breathless along for the ride. The Castaways, effectively being stationed on land or on a rock rather than flowing with the Currents, are introspective and, rather than trying to change the world, they want to take a minute to reflect before they take on a Current. A Castaway interacting with a Breathless would essentially be a sort of &quot;blind-leading-the-blind&quot; situation, but it would provide the Breathless with some sort of grounding influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Perhaps as a comparison, I was under the impression that Castaways were akin to Vampire Unaligned, Werewolf Ghost Wolves, Apostate Mages, Courtless Princesses/Changelings. They don't follow a Y Splat because they don't believe in the Y-Splats causes, they're trying to do things their own way (kind of like how you've explained them) and/or they don't believe in their purpose and/or want to distance themselves from doing anything dealing with it. Or they just see joining a side as pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:42:49-08:00","id":802442,"title":"","content":"Sorry for double post, I just finished Gardenia and making a page on the Aquatic Form. Also, commenting can be done on the Waters, so if you have better ideas for how things should be written and the like, feel free to point out. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_NkxCJ7gyQq599uf4yBJCarTh_HuHqx0jJUqtxvw484/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_NkxCJ7gyQq599uf4yBJCarTh_HuHqx0jJUqtxvw484/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_NkxCJ7gyQq599uf4yBJCarTh_HuHqx0jJUqtxvw484/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_NkxCJ7gyQq599uf4yBJCarTh_HuHqx0jJUqtxvw484/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T20:27:33-08:00","id":802622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=801514#post801514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. I would say perhaps that making Alterations pop up on human form would damage clothes whereas shifting to Aquatic Form makes them disappear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. I can see the clothing damage being a drawback when a Siren is attempting to hold onto an Alteration in her human form for too long. There was talk about a way for Sirens to disguise her temporary use of her Alterations, where the longer she holds onto an Alteration along with how many Alterations he is attempting to hold, the harder it is for the Siren to keep up the illusion that her Alterations are just &quot;natural abilities&quot; that aren't supernatural.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. Perhaps as a comparison, I was under the impression that Castaways were akin to Vampire Unaligned, Werewolf Ghost Wolves, Apostate Mages, Courtless Princesses/Changelings. They don't follow a Y Splat because they don't believe in the Y-Splats causes, they're trying to do things their own way (kind of like how you've explained them) and/or they don't believe in their purpose and/or want to distance themselves from doing anything dealing with it. Or they just see joining a side as pointless. </div> </div> </div>I think the main difference is that the Currents aren't traditional Factions. Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Changelings, etc. follow a group with an organized way of thought. The Currents seem more loose and are akin to viewpoints and philosophies rather than establishments. They are kinda like a Promethean's Refinements or a Sin-Eater's Archetype; they're loose, amorphous ideals and beliefs that aren't really taught or enforced. Now that I think about it, we should define what Currents are meant to be exactly.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry for double post, I just finished Gardenia and making a page on the Aquatic Form. Also, commenting can be done on the Waters, so if you have better ideas for how things should be written and the like, feel free to point out. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_NkxCJ7gyQq599uf4yBJCarTh_HuHqx0jJUqtxvw484/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a> </div> </div> </div>The take on Gardenians is pretty interesting. The way that I was envisioning them was more of a forceful being who thinks in terms of &quot;Sink or Swim&quot; rather than a protectorate and maintainer of cycles. That's not to say that I don't like the take. It's definitely interesting. I would say that I feel they need some sort of emphasis that, despite them being in tune with nature, they aren't &quot;peace-loving hippies&quot;. There is little bits in there about not taking Mother Earth's gifts for granted and how they receive and give back to the world. I feel that a &quot;standing your ground&quot; viewpoint might also give them some ground in how they are.<br /> <br /> I remember in <b><i>Princess </i></b>that the sections for the Callings describe Oaths that their Calling follows. And <b><i>Demon</i></b> had a section for each Incarnation about possible ways of Falling. I think the Waters could be enhanced by having a short snippet about what knowledge they see the world through, to sort of tie in the idea that the Sirens are oracles. It would also help create an umbrella that would allow a specific character to find a niche in one of the Waters<br /> <br /> With the <b>Polarians</b>, their &quot;Hat&quot; is death and endings. That is their big schtick and it's definitely reflected in how they view the world, so one of the things that they <b>Know</b> <i>(as in it's a Big Name term, something that is really important)</i> is that <b>&quot;All Things Come to an End&quot;</b>. It's an inevitability that bad things will happen, but there is no point in having those bad things drag along. The Polarians want humanity to grieve and move on rather than dwelling on the bad things that have happened. What I feel that is sort of implied by the Polarians is that, while things die and come to an end, <b>&quot;The World Still Moves&quot;</b>, in that not everything is going to stop when someone suffers from a bad day. The death of a child is tragic, of course, but the world will not stop to grieve. There may be time off, but everyone is expected to continue their own lives after a certain point. <br /> <br /> With the <b>Freshwater</b>, their &quot;Hat&quot; is birth and inspiration. Something that they Know would be something like <b>&quot;The Future is Now&quot;</b>, meaning that within a single moment is the opportunity to create something bigger and better. The Freshwaters are close with humanity, closer than the other Waters, and they want humanity to act with knowledge and responsibility. I feel they also know that <b>&quot;Life is Always Changing&quot;</b>, meaning that every day is a unique experience and that what happened in The Deluge may be averted in this world as long as things are changing.<br /> <br /> With the <b>Gardenians</b>, their &quot;Hat&quot; is nature and the cycle. The thing that they Know is that <b>&quot;History Repeats Itself&quot;</b> in that, the way that nature has a cycle, humanity and history have a cycle in which things repeat; by seeing what aspects are constantly appearing, the Sirens may be able to isolate what the leading event that calls upon The Deluge is and stop it before it repeats. They could also Know that <b>&quot;You Get As Much As You Give&quot;</b>, reflecting on the idea of giving back to the earth and receiving from the earth; acting in kindness begets kindness in return while acting in cruelty begets cruelty in return. <br /> <br /> The other three. the <b>Tropicans</b>, <b>Vaporians</b>, and <b>Discordians</b>, are kinda more up in the air, but I know that the Vaporians are a sort of outsider who would prefer to make contact and leave while Discordians are essentially trollish and chaotic individuals.<br /> <br /> I also just noticed that the Stereotypes omit Demons and Beasts. Is there a particular reason for that?<br /> <br /> Also, I am pretty unfamiliar with how Google Docs work. Is there a way to compile all the pages for Siren together and add them to the first post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T22:24:54-08:00","id":802724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802622#post802622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly. I can see the clothing damage being a drawback when a Siren is attempting to hold onto an Alteration in her human form for too long. There was talk about a way for Sirens to disguise her temporary use of her Alterations, where the longer she holds onto an Alteration along with how many Alterations he is attempting to hold, the harder it is for the Siren to keep up the illusion that her Alterations are just &quot;natural abilities&quot; that aren't supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>We need to come up with a system for Refractions. How exactly should they be carried out? Any non Siren rolls Resolve + Composure - the Siren's Serenity? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802622#post802622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main difference is that the Currents aren't traditional Factions. Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Changelings, etc. follow a group with an organized way of thought. The Currents seem more loose and are akin to viewpoints and philosophies rather than establishments. They are kinda like a Promethean's Refinements or a Sin-Eater's Archetype; they're loose, amorphous ideals and beliefs that aren't really taught or enforced. Now that I think about it, we should define what Currents are meant to be exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Philosophical beliefs on what they should do or how they act now as a Siren? Normal Currents believe that because they know of the Deluge, they should stop it as a generality, but they can also do things specialized as long as it fits with their Current? The Abyssal Currents differ in their ways. Dark Passions and Wisdom can be in it for dealing with the Deluge, for themselves, for other people, etc etc. Mankind's Victory, Primordial Darkness and Void tend to be much more entrenched within the world and fighting a secret war using corporations and powers against each other that most other Sirens have to deal with cleaning up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802622#post802622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The take on Gardenians is pretty interesting. The way that I was envisioning them was more of a forceful being who thinks in terms of &quot;Sink or Swim&quot; rather than a protectorate and maintainer of cycles. That's not to say that I don't like the take. It's definitely interesting. I would say that I feel they need some sort of emphasis that, despite them being in tune with nature, they aren't &quot;peace-loving hippies&quot;. There is little bits in there about not taking Mother Earth's gifts for granted and how they receive and give back to the world. I feel that a &quot;standing your ground&quot; viewpoint might also give them some ground in how they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies, I was partially borked when writing that and I base the Waters off of the ideas for the original Oceans. Gardenia being the equivalent to Indian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802622#post802622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember in <b><i>Princess </i></b>that the sections for the Callings describe Oaths that their Calling follows. And <b><i>Demon</i></b> had a section for each Incarnation about possible ways of Falling. I think the Waters could be enhanced by having a short snippet about what knowledge they see the world through, to sort of tie in the idea that the Sirens are oracles. It would also help create an umbrella that would allow a specific character to find a niche in one of the Waters<br /> <br /> <b>Snip on Philosophies</b><br /> <br /> The other three. the <b>Tropicans</b>, <b>Vaporians</b>, and <b>Discordians</b>, are kinda more up in the air, but I know that the Vaporians are a sort of outsider who would prefer to make contact and leave while Discordians are essentially trollish and chaotic individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me gusta, I've felt that the sections didn't have enough in them. Will add. Tropicans will be based off of Pacific (their normal ideas were to accumulate power and give it in turn, with themes of celebration and passion as we've thought). Vaporians did have that gadfly idea that you had, and I'd include kind of broken and insensate individuals to Discordia too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802622#post802622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also just noticed that the Stereotypes omit Demons and Beasts. Is there a particular reason for that?<br /> <br /> Also, I am pretty unfamiliar with how Google Docs work. Is there a way to compile all the pages for Siren together and add them to the first post?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just really disinterested in Demon and Beast and as such didn't make any stereotypes for them. Other people are free to make them up if they wish, but I'm just demotivated to make them myself. I'll add the doc links up tomorrow if it's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T00:24:43-08:00","id":802885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802724#post802724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need to come up with a system for Refractions. How exactly should they be carried out? Any non Siren rolls Resolve + Composure - the Siren's Serenity?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I remember, Refraction allows for a Siren to hide one Alteration for free for a single scene. Activating an additional Alteration puts a strain on the Siren's ability, which makes it harder for her to conceal it and the strain is amplified whenever the Siren needs to focus. I think that having the Siren roll Akashic Record + Lucidity <i>(that's the Integrity stat now)</i> to control her Alterations might work, as she's attempting to keep a hold of her alternate form, allowing bits of it to come out without releasing her full potential. The roll is probably needed for when the Siren activates an additional Alteration and when she is under mental or physical duress.<br /> <br /> Say this: A Siren is been jailed and needs to escape from her cell. There's a guard on post, so the Siren also needs to figure out a way to escape from the guard as well. The Siren decides to take the stealthy way out, so she, being a Polarian, uses one of the Alterations exclusive to her Waters, <b>Camouflage</b>. Activating the Alteration is easy, so the Siren doesn't need to roll her Lucidity. However, that was the first phase as it was meant to allow her to escape the bars undetected. The Siren decides to activate a second Alteration, <b>Boneless</b>, to slip herself through the bars. She rolls her Akashic Record + her Lucidity - 1 for the additional Alteration that scene. She succeeds and passes herself through the bars without alerting anyone. However, the guard notices that the person in the cell is no longer there, so they notify the other guards, which puts the area on lockdown. The Siren realizes that she needs to get away as soon as she can, which prompts duress and forces her to roll her Akashic Record + her Lucidity - 1 for her additional Alteration - another 1 because she succeeded in maintaining her form previously. If the Siren is then attacked after succeeding, she would roll AR + Lucidity - 1 for Alterations - 2 for two previous successes. However, if she decides to activate yet another Alteration, then she would need to roll AR + Lucidity - 2 for two additional Alterations - 3 for three previous successes.<br /> <br /> In terms of math, it would go: Dice Pool = Akashic Record + Lucidity - (# of Alterations -1) - (# of prior successes)<br /> <br /> The rolls would prompt when the Siren is stressed, when she is physically assaulted, or at the start of each new scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Philosophical beliefs on what they should do or how they act now as a Siren? Normal Currents believe that because they know of the Deluge, they should stop it as a generality, but they can also do things specialized as long as it fits with their Current? The Abyssal Currents differ in their ways. Dark Passions and Wisdom can be in it for dealing with the Deluge, for themselves, for other people, etc etc. Mankind's Victory, Primordial Darkness and Void tend to be much more entrenched within the world and fighting a secret war using corporations and powers against each other that most other Sirens have to deal with cleaning up. </div> </div> </div>The Currents are kinda like ways to interact with others or in what ways to influence the future. Like with the Current of Healing. Generally speaking, Sirens who follow the Current of Healing want others to recover, whether it is from emotional pain or physical pain. Some Sirens do so by helping others pick up the broken pieces, others help by allowing others to vent. The Normal Currents are sort of progressive and are trying to push humanity forward, whether it is from healing troubles, connecting with others, or facing an obstacle. The Abyssal Currents, in general, are more selfish in away or at least destructive.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Passions</b>, like the Current of Conflict, asks for confronting obstacles. However, it is also significantly more aggressive and asks more for vengeance than anything. <b>Dark Wisdom</b>, similar to the Current of Wisdom, seeks knowledge of the world. However, the pursuit of knowledge takes priority over everything else, including self-preservation. Both are meant to interact with humanity in a way; the two may even encourage humanity towards ruthlessness. While it is a kind of extreme, they both can deal with The Deluge.<br /> <br /> <b>Mankind's Victory</b> and <b>Primordial Darkness</b> could also work into interaction with humanity and prevention of The Deluge. Mankind's Victory is more about allowing others to do as they want without restriction as humanity has demonstrated their dominance as a species. It partially deals with The Deluge by asking others to act without restraint; maybe this will encourage others to speak up without regards to the power hierarchy and such and make the changes necessary to stopping The Deluge. Primordial Darkness operates in the inverse, forcibly reminding humanity that, in the end, the earth will survive long after humanity has run its course. They would be enforcing the hierarchy, making sure to place the Earth on top.<br /> <br /> <b>The Void</b> would be an outlier, as they are the ones that actively want to bring the world into ruin by hastening the coming of The Deluge. It's still technically a way to interact with humanity and approach The Deluge; they're just kinda negative for the most part.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My apologies, I was partially borked when writing that and I base the Waters off of the ideas for the original Oceans. Gardenia being the equivalent to Indian. </div> </div> </div>No worries. If that's how the original Ocean was intended, then that's how it was intended. It's providing some sort of structure and there are things that can help flesh out some of the more vague details.<br /> <br /> On a side-note, I almost typed out &quot;bague retails&quot;. I am tired. :V<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Me gusta, I've felt that the sections didn't have enough in them. Will add. Tropicans will be based off of Pacific (their normal ideas were to accumulate power and give it in turn, with themes of celebration and passion as we've thought). Vaporians did have that gadfly idea that you had, and I'd include kind of broken and insensate individuals to Discordia too. </div> </div> </div>Ah. Gotcha. I just needed to double-check on the original post to see the Ocean's original intentions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just really disinterested in Demon and Beast and as such didn't make any stereotypes for them. Other people are free to make them up if they wish, but I'm just demotivated to make them myself. I'll add the doc links up tomorrow if it's fine. </div> </div> </div>I can hash out some Stereotypes for Demons and Beasts in the morning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T12:29:38-08:00","id":803267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802885#post802885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I remember, Refraction allows for a Siren to hide one Alteration for free for a single scene. Activating an additional Alteration puts a strain on the Siren's ability, which makes it harder for her to conceal it and the strain is amplified whenever the Siren needs to focus. I think that having the Siren roll Akashic Record + Lucidity <i>(that's the Integrity stat now)</i> to control her Alterations might work, as she's attempting to keep a hold of her alternate form, allowing bits of it to come out without releasing her full potential. The roll is probably needed for when the Siren activates an additional Alteration and when she is under mental or physical duress.<br /> <br /> Say this: A Siren is been jailed and needs to escape from her cell. There's a guard on post, so the Siren also needs to figure out a way to escape from the guard as well. The Siren decides to take the stealthy way out, so she, being a Polarian, uses one of the Alterations exclusive to her Waters, <b>Camouflage</b>. Activating the Alteration is easy, so the Siren doesn't need to roll her Lucidity. However, that was the first phase as it was meant to allow her to escape the bars undetected. The Siren decides to activate a second Alteration, <b>Boneless</b>, to slip herself through the bars. She rolls her Akashic Record + her Lucidity - 1 for the additional Alteration that scene. She succeeds and passes herself through the bars without alerting anyone. However, the guard notices that the person in the cell is no longer there, so they notify the other guards, which puts the area on lockdown. The Siren realizes that she needs to get away as soon as she can, which prompts duress and forces her to roll her Akashic Record + her Lucidity - 1 for her additional Alteration - another 1 because she succeeded in maintaining her form previously. If the Siren is then attacked after succeeding, she would roll AR + Lucidity - 1 for Alterations - 2 for two previous successes. However, if she decides to activate yet another Alteration, then she would need to roll AR + Lucidity - 2 for two additional Alterations - 3 for three previous successes.<br /> <br /> In terms of math, it would go: Dice Pool = Akashic Record + Lucidity - (# of Alterations -1) - (# of prior successes)<br /> <br /> The rolls would prompt when the Siren is stressed, when she is physically assaulted, or at the start of each new scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. This is good. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802885#post802885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Currents are kinda like ways to interact with others or in what ways to influence the future. Like with the Current of Healing. Generally speaking, Sirens who follow the Current of Healing want others to recover, whether it is from emotional pain or physical pain. Some Sirens do so by helping others pick up the broken pieces, others help by allowing others to vent. The Normal Currents are sort of progressive and are trying to push humanity forward, whether it is from healing troubles, connecting with others, or facing an obstacle. The Abyssal Currents, in general, are more selfish in away or at least destructive.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Passions</b>, like the Current of Conflict, asks for confronting obstacles. However, it is also significantly more aggressive and asks more for vengeance than anything. <b>Dark Wisdom</b>, similar to the Current of Wisdom, seeks knowledge of the world. However, the pursuit of knowledge takes priority over everything else, including self-preservation. Both are meant to interact with humanity in a way; the two may even encourage humanity towards ruthlessness. While it is a kind of extreme, they both can deal with The Deluge.<br /> <br /> <b>Mankind's Victory</b> and <b>Primordial Darkness</b> could also work into interaction with humanity and prevention of The Deluge. Mankind's Victory is more about allowing others to do as they want without restriction as humanity has demonstrated their dominance as a species. It partially deals with The Deluge by asking others to act without restraint; maybe this will encourage others to speak up without regards to the power hierarchy and such and make the changes necessary to stopping The Deluge. Primordial Darkness operates in the inverse, forcibly reminding humanity that, in the end, the earth will survive long after humanity has run its course. They would be enforcing the hierarchy, making sure to place the Earth on top.<br /> <br /> <b>The Void</b> would be an outlier, as they are the ones that actively want to bring the world into ruin by hastening the coming of The Deluge. It's still technically a way to interact with humanity and approach The Deluge; they're just kinda negative for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mixing both philosophy and how they enact their duties? :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802885#post802885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries. If that's how the original Ocean was intended, then that's how it was intended. It's providing some sort of structure and there are things that can help flesh out some of the more vague details.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Granted, some of them aren't specific (Pacific for example) so we can put our own ideas onto things. For example, Tropicana will have that theme of passion and celebration that IIRC you brought up. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=802885#post802885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can hash out some Stereotypes for Demons and Beasts in the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. :3 Speaking of which, posted up the Doc links I've made so far. Will edit to put in more. Should I also edit the message to change the X and Y splats to what we've had? Change X to Waters and change the Abyssal Current names and the like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:18:38-08:00","id":803432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=803267#post803267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mixing both philosophy and how they enact their duties? :3</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, considering that Waters describes overall appearance and personality. The Currents definitely seem more malleable, where it probably is commonplace to see a Siren switching Currets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed. Granted, some of them aren't specific (Pacific for example) so we can put our own ideas onto things. For example, Tropicana will have that theme of passion and celebration that IIRC you brought up. :3 </div> </div> </div>When I was reading on the Oceans, I thought that the Pacific, being an Ocean of Growth, meant that those Sirens that follow it would be companions that prefer to latch onto a single person and see their growth. Essentially, out of most portrayals of mermaids in the media, the Sirens of Tropicana would be the &quot;love-interest&quot; types, but more in a sense that they enjoy seeing others develop into better people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you. :3 Speaking of which, posted up the Doc links I've made so far. Will edit to put in more. Should I also edit the message to change the X and Y splats to what we've had? Change X to Waters and change the Abyssal Current names and the like? </div> </div> </div>It would help out any new viewers who open up the topic. It would also help to compile some of the information so that we don't have to go page-by-page looking for a specific post.<br /> <br /> As for Stereotypes, I have these:<br /> <br /> <b>POLARIA</b><br /> <b><i>Demons:</i></b><i> &quot;You run. And you continue to run. What is it that terrifies you so?&quot;<br /> <b>Beasts:</b> &quot;I do not fear what hides itself in the dark.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>FRESHWATER<br /> <i>Demons: </i></b><i>&quot;You're kinda sad, being reborn and all but taking over the lives of others. Why not make something of your own?&quot;<br /> <b>Beasts:</b> &quot;Big teeth, check. Sharp claws, check. Kinda boring and old-school, don't you think?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>GARDENIA</b><br /> <b><i>Demons:</i></b><i> &quot;Trespasser! You do not belong in this world!&quot;<br /> <b>Beasts:</b> &quot;Feed as much as you want, but beware that there is always a bigger fish waiting to continue the cycle.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T22:47:27-08:00","id":803588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=803432#post803432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly, considering that Waters describes overall appearance and personality. The Currents definitely seem more malleable, where it probably is commonplace to see a Siren switching Currets.<br /> <br /> When I was reading on the Oceans, I thought that the Pacific, being an Ocean of Growth, meant that those Sirens that follow it would be companions that prefer to latch onto a single person and see their growth. Essentially, out of most portrayals of mermaids in the media, the Sirens of Tropicana would be the &quot;love-interest&quot; types, but more in a sense that they enjoy seeing others develop into better people.</div> </div> </div> </div>*stamps both with Sally Seal of Approval because saying &quot;Me gusta&quot; is beginning to sound stale*<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=803432#post803432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would help out any new viewers who open up the topic. It would also help to compile some of the information so that we don't have to go page-by-page looking for a specific post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=803432#post803432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Stereotypes, I have these:</div> </div> </div> </div>I like them. :3 The only thing is...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=803432#post803432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>GARDENIA</b><br /> <b><i>Demons:</i></b>[I] &quot;Trespasser! You do not belong in this world!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am extremely tempted to switch out &quot;Trespasser&quot; with &quot;Die, Monster!&quot; &gt;w&gt; (I'm mostly joking just to note)<br /> <br /> And in case the reference wasn't caught, here's where it's from.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7z65s0fqDw4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7z65s0fqDw4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7z65s0fqDw4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7z65s0fqDw4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T00:25:35-08:00","id":803606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=803588#post803588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*stamps both with Sally Seal of Approval because saying &quot;Me gusta&quot; is beginning to sound stale*</div> </div> </div> </div>I always go for &quot;This Pleases Gaga&quot;. It's my favorite way to express approval.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like them. :3 The only thing is...<br /> <br /> I am extremely tempted to switch out &quot;Trespasser&quot; with &quot;Die, Monster!&quot; &gt;w&gt; (I'm mostly joking just to note)<br /> <br /> And in case the reference wasn't caught, here's where it's from.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7z65s0fqDw4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7z65s0fqDw4</a> </div> </div> </div>Completely unintentional, but that is pretty hilarious. I do feel that the Gardenians would be the most-vocal when it comes to expressing their disapproval of creatures that should not be. Vampires, Sin-Eaters, and Mummies are unfortunate creatures that have once lived but are trying to prolong their cycle. They are terrible creatures worthy of disdain, but nothing will draw their ire as much as Prometheans, terrible creatures that defile the cycles of the natural world, and Demons, beings that are, in and of themselves, alien to the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T22:19:24-08:00","id":804258,"title":"","content":"I've edited the first post to be fitting to the ideas we've come up with, a brief summary so to speak. If there needs to be any changes, please let me know.<br /> <br /> To ask, what should we be focusing on next? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T23:16:32-08:00","id":804270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=804258#post804258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To ask, what should we be focusing on next? :3</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as what grounds we have touched on: <br /> <br /> <b>Write-Up; Information within the Documents:</b><br /> The Waters; Polaria, Freshwater, Gardenia<br /> Alterations; General, Polaria, Freshwater<br /> Antagonists; Vodianoi<br /> Lexicon<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b><br /> Anchors and Advantages; Sea and Shore, Properties of being a Siren, the Maelstrom, Trace<br /> The Structure of the Verses; a working list of Opuses, Introductions, Conclusions, and their Pneuma cost<br /> <br /> <b>Fluff:</b><br /> The Currents; Normal and Abyssal<br /> Lore and Backstory; The Deluge and the Song<br /> Antagonists; The Flensers, The Breathless, Banshees, Furies<br /> <br /> <br /> Those are the bases that have been touched and are effectively essential to the Sirens to make them Sirens. Of things that haven't been solidified, there are Merits <i>(which can wait until later in development)</i>, the meaning of Shoals, and potentially high-level gaming. There are also possible plot hooks that can be brainstormed, but those are on standby for right now. <br /> <br /> I'll try to compile the information so that there is a reference page for most of the mechanics and fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T00:17:02-08:00","id":804286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=804270#post804270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll try to compile the information so that there is a reference page for most of the mechanics and fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I'd appreciate it. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:41:10-08:00","id":804716,"title":"","content":"Damm, we have come a long way since the start. That's awesome!<br /> <br /> \u200bMy suggestions right now is to finish the writing on the Waters and Alterations. Maybe write a few sample characters to make sure everything is in place.<br /> <br /> And, for further development:<ul><li>\u200bA Blue book on Ocean and Sea based campaigns.</li> <li>The Dark Eras of Siren (Idea: Golden Age of Piracy)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T14:52:53-08:00","id":804723,"title":"","content":"Sorry for not being active recently- exams got me bad. I've gotta say everything this far seems pretty cool! <br /> And now for something not so cool- I've added some Gardenian <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations</a>. I'm pretty sure <b>Fetid Touch</b> and <b>Swimmerets </b>need some attention, so go ahead and critique them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5929-squamousbeauty","name":"SquamousBeauty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T16:57:47-08:00","id":804807,"title":"","content":"So, I was working on a sample interactive sheet so I could write sample character and show you guys. I'm doing the final graphic touches and will be posting the Interactive version tomorrow (if I can manage to have some free time). <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/89189128/StDSheet%201-page.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Siren Sheet</a><br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: Re-doing the borders, those are damm ugly right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T18:26:50-08:00","id":804885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=804716#post804716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damm, we have come a long way since the start. That's awesome!<br /> <br /> \u200bMy suggestions right now is to finish the writing on the Waters and Alterations. Maybe write a few sample characters to make sure everything is in place.<br /> <br /> And, for further development:<ul><li>\u200bA Blue book on Ocean and Sea based campaigns.</li> <li>The Dark Eras of Siren (Idea: Golden Age of Piracy)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Characters would be child's play. I'm dreading the further developments, but we'll cross that bridge when we get there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry for not being active recently- exams got me bad. I've gotta say everything this far seems pretty cool!<br /> And now for something not so cool- I've added some Gardenian <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations</a>. I'm pretty sure <b>Fetid Touch</b> and <b>Swimmerets </b>need some attention, so go ahead and critique them all. </div> </div> </div>Nice. I would say that with Fetid Touch, the inspirations would be more of the Poison Dart Frog than the Hagfish or Eel. Hagfish produce a slime that is more for escape. If anything, the Hagfish's slime is similar to a Squid's inkpouch, but that's more of a technical thing. I'm not entirely familiar with the grappling mechanics or poison mechanics, however, so I can't really make the call.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I was working on a sample interactive sheet so I could write sample character and show you guys. I'm doing the final graphic touches and will be posting the Interactive version tomorrow (if I can manage to have some free time). <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/89189128/StDSheet%201-page.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Siren Sheet</a><br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: Re-doing the borders, those are damm ugly right now. </div> </div> </div>That is extraordinarily neat, especially with the touch of having the staff over the sections. I do have to ask what the splotches are supposed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:35:48-08:00","id":804973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SquamousBeauty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=804723#post804723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for not being active recently- exams got me bad. I've gotta say everything this far seems pretty cool!<br /> And now for something not so cool- I've added some Gardenian <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1A9SzALrfnV_vsRRPbgIvu-02o7calLwHp9CIeiIOHw4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Alterations</a>. I'm pretty sure <b>Fetid Touch</b> and <b>Swimmerets </b>need some attention, so go ahead and critique them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how the Swimmerets are. I'll admit, I'm usually grasping at straws when I write up the Alterations section due to looking for special animal traits of animals in the region. Sufficed to say, we can brush up and even add more, so the work is more shared.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=804885#post804885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is extraordinarily neat, especially with the touch of having the staff over the sections. I do have to ask what the splotches are supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>They appear like Coral Reefs. Regardless, I LOVE how this sheet looks! Great work Yads! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I would like to take a post to just thank everyone for their contributions to the project and all of us working together, we can make this into something great. And I would also like to thank that we all are able to work together without getting into headaches of arguments over little things or at least they stay at a friendly level. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:03:32-08:00","id":804988,"title":"","content":"Um...quick heads up. My friend was looking over my shoulder when I was checking out the sheet and noticed that &quot;Siren: the Drowning&quot; shortens down to &quot;STD&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yeah. What were the other words that were available to be swapped out with &quot;Surfacing&quot; or &quot;Drowning&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:38:52-08:00","id":805006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=804988#post804988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um...quick heads up. My friend was looking over my shoulder when I was checking out the sheet and noticed that &quot;Siren: the Drowning&quot; shortens down to &quot;STD&quot;.<br /> <br /> So yeah. What were the other words that were available to be swapped out with &quot;Surfacing&quot; or &quot;Drowning&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be lying if I didn't say I laughed at that. Anyways, this game is still WiP so we can change the title if needs be, but to be honest I feel we're still fine keeping it as Siren the Drowning. The only reasoning I have for this is that Werewolf the Forsaken gets away with having the abbreviation of &quot;WTF&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:14:38-08:00","id":805016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=805006#post805006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be lying if I didn't say I laughed at that. Anyways, this game is still WiP so we can change the title if needs be, but to be honest I feel we're still fine keeping it as Siren the Drowning. The only reasoning I have for this is that Werewolf the Forsaken gets away with having the abbreviation of &quot;WTF&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. I will say, however, that when I downloaded the character sheet, the file name was &quot;StDSheet&quot;. :V","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T23:44:14-08:00","id":805056,"title":"","content":"Personally I preferred &quot;the Surfacing&quot; but it's not a big deal anyway; we're all adults here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also love the style of the sheet, very well made. Do you think you can make a 1E version of it somewhere down the line too for those of us who are not fans of GMC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7060,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","user":"Karavolos","date":". 01-10-2016, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:07:53-08:00","id":806452,"title":"","content":"Made a few changes in the borders of the sheet. The stains are a mix of Petals/Corals or even Ink Stains in a music sheet. here's the new sample for you, guys! <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/51v88svrv1s9ycg/StDSheet%201-page.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Siren Sheet</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:37:39-08:00","id":806525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=806452#post806452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Made a few changes in the borders of the sheet. The stains are a mix of Petals/Corals or even Ink Stains in a music sheet. here's the new sample for you, guys! <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/51v88svrv1s9ycg/StDSheet%201-page.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Siren Sheet</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it's not minded being said, I kind of like the previous version abit more, but I'll roll with what the majority of people decide on is good. :3 This one does look nice by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http