look for a specific mention of something. I will also be updating it with information about mechanics soon.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThanks for the nice words and for the GDoc, finally I can see our progress fully. So, keeping the sheet and all in second place, let's try to work the backstory a little more?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:47:52-08:00","id":808311,"title":"","content":"Yes, we should. Pardon my lack of response, school restarted for me and I won't be able to properly contribute until Friday at least. &gt;&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:34:25-08:00","id":808333,"title":"","content":"For a second I thought the game was abandoned again. What a relief. I'm going to re-read the Reaper compilation so I can have a nice and round idea for the backstory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T20:01:52-08:00","id":808405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808333#post808333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a second I thought the game was abandoned again. What a relief. I'm going to re-read the Reaper compilation so I can have a nice and round idea for the backstory</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I wouldn't dream of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T22:47:30-08:00","id":808472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=806564#post806564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThanks for the nice words and for the GDoc, finally I can see our progress fully. So, keeping the sheet and all in second place, let's try to work the backstory a little more?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808311#post808311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, we should. Pardon my lack of response, school restarted for me and I won't be able to properly contribute until Friday at least. &gt;&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the same for me. I have classes on Thursday, which is going to increase the work I have throughout the week. I can probably hash out a couple things here and there, but it'll be more intermittent.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808333#post808333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a second I thought the game was abandoned again. What a relief. I'm going to re-read the Reaper compilation so I can have a nice and round idea for the backstory</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of what we have for backstory, we already established what The Deluge is and means and how it plays into the dual realities of Sirens. There are a few points that could be built upon, such as the idea of Serenia, the sunken library that contains all of history in The Deluge. We can also discuss the sort of &quot;divine&quot; backstory, with Ceto and Echidna. We could even talk about Nuwa, a Chinese creator goddess with a serpentine body who saved a world raging with wildfires, floods, and predatory animals by restoring the pillars of heaven and created humanity from clay, or even Noah, who created an ark and allowed for life to continue after the flood.<br /> <br /> I have a few free-floating thoughts about The Deluge and what it means throughout History, which was a Big Name Theme:<br /> <br /> 1) The Deluge has happened before, though it was more regional than it was global. Each of these little floods was Nature's way of eliminating a troubling aspect before it grew too large, which is why there are figures like Noah or Nuwa who helped humanity through the floods. Now, The Deluge has threatened to take over on a global level.<br /> <br /> 2) Serenia, the drowned library that contains all of history, contains information about previous realities in which The Deluge occurred and in which the preceding Sirens transferred their consciousness forward. It is far down in The Deluge, deeper than the Hadal Zone. It is under the control of Echidna, a Siren who has abandoned humanity in order to create a species that can outlast the effects of The Deluge.<br /> <br /> 3) If The Deluge is a sort of reset button that has been pushed multiple times, there should be a sort of &quot;backup&quot; that allowed the Sirens to continue their existence in a different realm at a different time. Whereas The Deluge is a literal thing that has swallowed up the material world in one reality, there is a sort of &quot;in-between&quot; area that allowed the Siren to continue existing and prevent The Deluge. This is the actual area where a Siren becomes a Siren, rather than within The Deluge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:12:13-08:00","id":808757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808472#post808472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of what we have for backstory, we already established what The Deluge is and means and how it plays into the dual realities of Sirens. There are a few points that could be built upon, such as the idea of Serenia, the sunken library that contains all of history in The Deluge. We can also discuss the sort of &quot;divine&quot; backstory, with Ceto and Echidna. We could even talk about Nuwa, a Chinese creator goddess with a serpentine body who saved a world raging with wildfires, floods, and predatory animals by restoring the pillars of heaven and created humanity from clay, or even Noah, who created an ark and allowed for life to continue after the flood.<br /> <br /> I have a few free-floating thoughts about The Deluge and what it means throughout History, which was a Big Name Theme:<br /> <br /> 1) The Deluge has happened before, though it was more regional than it was global. Each of these little floods was Nature's way of eliminating a troubling aspect before it grew too large, which is why there are figures like Noah or Nuwa who helped humanity through the floods. Now, The Deluge has threatened to take over on a global level.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my version of Demon: The Fallen the regional flood is more in line with what I run with; if more around the area of the Mediterranean if only because it spares the effort of explaining why there are no flood myths in every culture (though there are a lot that have it), ignoring the problems with the Ark story in the first place (like how two individuals can populate an entire species).<br /> Sufficed to say I think running floods on a regional scale- or otherwise one separate from our reality -would be the wisest course of action. If Sirens have any bindings towards the Gauntlet and Spirits, a possible way of explaining it could be that the Gauntlet to the &quot;Deluge&quot; breaches and the water floods into our world until it can be subsided. The problem of course is the heavy tie to Werewolf. We could also go an opposite way and run that the Deluge is a doom on both ends<br /> As for the individuals, they could either have been lucky, savvy or possibly guided by Sirens (if not Sirens themselves). I could see Noah being a Breathless for instance, with all the animals coming over and so on. I'll put a quick link for potential material we can pull from existing flood myths:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_flood_myths\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_flood_myths\" target=\"_blank\"> List of flood myths - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_flood_myths\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_flood_myths </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808472#post808472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Serenia, the drowned library that contains all of history, contains information about previous realities in which The Deluge occurred and in which the preceding Sirens transferred their consciousness forward. It is far down in The Deluge, deeper than the Hadal Zone. It is under the control of Echidna, a Siren who has abandoned humanity in order to create a species that can outlast the effects of The Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm starting to draw comparisons towards Princess: The Hopeful, we have the fall happening in another reality (or so) leading to a part of it kinda sorta remaining with info (library for Siren, Dreamlands/Alhambra for Princess) with a &quot;Queen&quot; having gone kinda badish but has good intentions (Echidna/Twilight Queens). Not sure if it's necessairly bad, let alone breaking, but I think we should add a small bit of spice to them somehow to vary them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808472#post808472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) If The Deluge is a sort of reset button that has been pushed multiple times, there should be a sort of &quot;backup&quot; that allowed the Sirens to continue their existence in a different realm at a different time. Whereas The Deluge is a literal thing that has swallowed up the material world in one reality, there is a sort of &quot;in-between&quot; area that allowed the Siren to continue existing and prevent The Deluge. This is the actual area where a Siren becomes a Siren, rather than within The Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I hate the God-Machine for being too intrusive on the non-DtD lines in my opinion, it sounds very in line with how it acts in my opinion; while I'm not sure why it would let the Sirens run those issues over its Angels, I could see it press the button a few times when it loses control too much.<br /> The &quot;In between area&quot; you talk about sounds a lot like Twilight (not to be mistaken for the shitty movie) to me which brings more ties towards Werewolf. That said, I like the idea of Sirens turning into Sirens away from the real world which in my opinion goes a long way to explain why we don't have Sirens up our asses if all you have to do is just about drown and hear a song underwater during the process (grain of salt, I'm still not sure on the proper process despite having had it explained a few times, it doesn't click somehow), tho it still doesn't quite explain how they actually end up going to another world and back a l\u00e1 Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7060,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","user":"Karavolos","date":".  More fixing 01-14-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:49:24-08:00","id":809711,"title":"","content":"Alrighties. Now that it's Friday, I doth owe a post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808472#post808472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of what we have for backstory, we already established what The Deluge is and means and how it plays into the dual realities of Sirens. There are a few points that could be built upon, such as the idea of Serenia, the sunken library that contains all of history in The Deluge. We can also discuss the sort of &quot;divine&quot; backstory, with Ceto and Echidna. We could even talk about Nuwa, a Chinese creator goddess with a serpentine body who saved a world raging with wildfires, floods, and predatory animals by restoring the pillars of heaven and created humanity from clay, or even Noah, who created an ark and allowed for life to continue after the flood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall anything about Serenia being discussed. Unless if that was referring to a Siren &quot;Capital&quot; so to speak. Like Princesses have the Kingdoms, Mages Atlantis, Mummy Irem and Werewolf Pangea etc etc. In which case I can say that I do recall minor mention but not entirely what it was supposed to be about. I'm all for the Ceto and Echidna ideas, I believe we just need to specify what Ceto's part is in all of this. As for Nuwa, I believe that it might be in a minor bad taste to do her, if only because she sounds minorly alike to Tiamat who is being used for Leviathan. But I digress, it's still a WIP and anything can change ofc.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I also wonder. Usually for X-Splats (or Y-Splats in the case of Wolves, Changelings and Princesses), there's usually a figure who's appointed as the progenitor of the splat. I was thinking that the Deluge mostly follows real world cosmology when it comes to temperatures (meaning that areas can change so to speak. like one place that was Gardenia can fall under Polaria's influence in winter) at least. Which made me sort of think of this idea. What if Ceto had a hand on making the Currents? Rather, her children did (which are all mythological water figures)? Ack, I realize that this is very close when it comes to Werewolf the Forsaken, so it might not be a good idea. What if Ceto just flatly made the current Currents (English language at it's finest ladies and gentlemen!) and we didn't have any of those &quot;Progenitors of the splat&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808472#post808472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The Deluge has happened before, though it was more regional than it was global. Each of these little floods was Nature's way of eliminating a troubling aspect before it grew too large, which is why there are figures like Noah or Nuwa who helped humanity through the floods. Now, The Deluge has threatened to take over on a global level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how this sounded. I can also see it something like the &quot;apocalypses the other splats faced&quot; for Sirens, only marking when the Song first appeared in the world and some people of the future (Noah) surviving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808472#post808472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Serenia, the drowned library that contains all of history, contains information about previous realities in which The Deluge occurred and in which the preceding Sirens transferred their consciousness forward. It is far down in The Deluge, deeper than the Hadal Zone. It is under the control of Echidna, a Siren who has abandoned humanity in order to create a species that can outlast the effects of The Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. I know it might sound bad, but I sort of imagined the Deluge to be the sort of place where you can find a record (or pieces of records) of events, but only if the Siren cared enough to look. To get a complete story of events, the Siren would have to look really hard to get all of the pieces, which would be only around the Deluge version of the locations that the event took place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=808472#post808472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) If The Deluge is a sort of reset button that has been pushed multiple times, there should be a sort of &quot;backup&quot; that allowed the Sirens to continue their existence in a different realm at a different time. Whereas The Deluge is a literal thing that has swallowed up the material world in one reality, there is a sort of &quot;in-between&quot; area that allowed the Siren to continue existing and prevent The Deluge. This is the actual area where a Siren becomes a Siren, rather than within The Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Kara said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T15:06:20-08:00","id":809863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall anything about Serenia being discussed. Unless if that was referring to a Siren &quot;Capital&quot; so to speak. Like Princesses have the Kingdoms, Mages Atlantis, Mummy Irem and Werewolf Pangea etc etc. In which case I can say that I do recall minor mention but not entirely what it was supposed to be about. I'm all for the Ceto and Echidna ideas, I believe we just need to specify what Ceto's part is in all of this. As for Nuwa, I believe that it might be in a minor bad taste to do her, if only because she sounds minorly alike to Tiamat who is being used for Leviathan. But I digress, it's still a WIP and anything can change ofc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serenia/Sirenia was an idea that was brought up in the first few pages by Yads Dom. I think it's supposed to be a capital, but the main thing I remember is the word &quot;Library&quot;. As for Ceto and Echidna, we've established that Ceto is the one who awakened the Sirens while Echidna is a Siren gone completely rogue. These are Big Name Ideas, so we could reiterate these points. With Nuwa, she could possibly be an example of a powerful Siren who managed to prevent one instance of The Deluge a long time ago. It could also play into the tentative &quot;History&quot; theme that was mentioned way back, where Ceto and Echidna would follow the birth of Sirens and the defection of Echidna and Nuwa would follow the reason for why Sirens are asked to stop The Deluge and care for humanity. This would also allow us to incorporate ideas from different mythologies without having any clashes. Ceto and Echidna is one tale based on Greek mythology and is within a sort of bubble while Nuwa is another tale based on Chinese mythology and exists within another bubble. The two don't overlap but their stories trickle down to explain the mindset of Sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, I also wonder. Usually for X-Splats (or Y-Splats in the case of Wolves, Changelings and Princesses), there's usually a figure who's appointed as the progenitor of the splat. I was thinking that the Deluge mostly follows real world cosmology when it comes to temperatures (meaning that areas can change so to speak. like one place that was Gardenia can fall under Polaria's influence in winter) at least. Which made me sort of think of this idea. What if Ceto had a hand on making the Currents? Rather, her children did (which are all mythological water figures)? Ack, I realize that this is very close when it comes to Werewolf the Forsaken, so it might not be a good idea. What if Ceto just flatly made the current Currents (English language at it's finest ladies and gentlemen!) and we didn't have any of those &quot;Progenitors of the splat&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm down with either Progenitors or having something effectively influence the Currents. With the Waters, they seem to be more naturally influenced by climate and location, so we could tie in the Waters with Nature. As for Currents, I wouldn't mind the normal Currents being established while the Abyssal Currents are more of rogue/maverick schools of thought that branched out from them. If Ceto did have a hand in creating the Currents, we should probably talk about the importance and the influence Ceto has over the Sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my version of Demon: The Fallen the regional flood is more in line with what I run with; if more around the area of the Mediterranean if only because it spares the effort of explaining why there are no flood myths in every culture (though there are a lot that have it), ignoring the problems with the Ark story in the first place (like how two individuals can populate an entire species).<br /> Sufficed to say I think running floods on a regional scale- or otherwise one separate from our reality -would be the wisest course of action. If Sirens have any bindings towards the Gauntlet and Spirits, a possible way of explaining it could be that the Gauntlet to the &quot;Deluge&quot; breaches and the water floods into our world until it can be subsided. The problem of course is the heavy tie to Werewolf. We could also go an opposite way and run that the Deluge is a doom on both ends<br /> As for the individuals, they could either have been lucky, savvy or possibly guided by Sirens (if not Sirens themselves). I could see Noah being a Breathless for instance, with all the animals coming over and so on. I'll put a quick link for potential material we can pull from existing flood myths:<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_flood_myths\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_flood_myths</a></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how this sounded. I can also see it something like the &quot;apocalypses the other splats faced&quot; for Sirens, only marking when the Song first appeared in the world and some people of the future (Noah) surviving.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do feel that I should read up on Demon: the Fallen now. For regional floods, that would fall under Nature and the trickle of Resentment that influences the world. The mythical flood that Noah experienced was meant to eliminate the evils of the old world, but it could be a relatively true story that Sirens of yesteryear had to experience. Nature was fed up with the disrespect humanity showed within the area, so its resentment caused a massive flood. Noah was subtly warned/influenced by the Sirens to construct the Ark and save what he could in the area. <br /> <br /> It could be that minor events that affect a region could be called a Flooding while the Big Name Apocalypse that affects the world is &quot;The Deluge&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to draw comparisons towards Princess: The Hopeful, we have the fall happening in another reality (or so) leading to a part of it kinda sorta remaining with info (library for Siren, Dreamlands/Alhambra for Princess) with a &quot;Queen&quot; having gone kinda badish but has good intentions (Echidna/Twilight Queens). Not sure if it's necessairly bad, let alone breaking, but I think we should add a small bit of spice to them somehow to vary them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm. I know it might sound bad, but I sort of imagined the Deluge to be the sort of place where you can find a record (or pieces of records) of events, but only if the Siren cared enough to look. To get a complete story of events, the Siren would have to look really hard to get all of the pieces, which would be only around the Deluge version of the locations that the event took place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back on page 2, Yads Dom suggested this: <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Going to the Deluge, they would be able to access Sirenuse (Another possible name, taken from Greek Mythology), where all their History past, presente and future would be stocked, alongside with the whole world and nature. Entire cities, submerged, from all times. Better than Time as Motif, as you said: History as Motif. Do not Forget, Always Remenber the time of Our Death (The Subjective Future or the True Death, when their Paradise was lost).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which was then responded by SaulottheGentle:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The reason for this is because the Deluge/Astral reflects humanity and nature's thoughts on things. If there's nobody doing anything and really bad stuff is going on, then it will certainly reflect in the Deluge's premonitions. Perhaps Serenia (Cantre'r Gwaelod, Kitezh, Llys Helig, Dilmun and Ys are all names of mythological lost kingdoms under the waves) is the only place that holds any meaning of the Siren's history, only now ruled by or distorted into Echidna's view.</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My suggestion was attempting to compound on these ideas. I'm not necessarily sure as to where to go on from this idea, however.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I hate the God-Machine for being too intrusive on the non-DtD lines in my opinion, it sounds very in line with how it acts in my opinion; while I'm not sure why it would let the Sirens run those issues over its Angels, I could see it press the button a few times when it loses control too much.<br /> The &quot;In between area&quot; you talk about sounds a lot like Twilight (not to be mistaken for the shitty movie) to me which brings more ties towards Werewolf. That said, I like the idea of Sirens turning into Sirens away from the real world which in my opinion goes a long way to explain why we don't have Sirens up our asses if all you have to do is just about drown and hear a song underwater during the process (grain of salt, I'm still not sure on the proper process despite having had it explained a few times, it doesn't click somehow), tho it still doesn't quite explain how they actually end up going to another world and back a l\u00e1 Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Kara said.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the general process goes like this.<br /> <br /> 1) Humanity in Dimension A does something really stupid --&gt; Nature, in response, hits the reset button and drowns everyone in The Deluge<br /> <br /> 2) Humanity in Dimension A is drowning from The Deluge --&gt; Their consciousness is transported into an &quot;in-between&quot; area between Dimension A and Dimension B<br /> <br /> 3) Dimension A Humans &quot;Hear the Song&quot; and &quot;Surface&quot; --&gt; Their consciousness is warped so that their being is that of the Sirens<br /> a) When Dimension A Humans fail to Hear the Song but they Surface, their consciousness warps and becomes a Breathless. Breathless are unaware of what they are.<br /> b) When Dimension A Humans fail to Surface, their consciousness warps and becomes a Banshee. Banshees are unaware of what they are.<br /> <br /> 4) Dimension A Sirens become aware of what they are --&gt; Their consciousness is transferred to Dimension B, where it blends with their consciousness from Dimension B<br /> <br /> 5) The Sirens now exist in Dimension B, where Dimension A has been abandoned. <br /> <br /> <br /> I can explain more in a couple hours. I just need to head out somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T22:06:47-08:00","id":810084,"title":"","content":"Much obliged on the explaining, I have a better view on how Sirens are made. Tho I'm still somewhat confused on all the dimensional travel stuff, but I digress. Does it mean tho that there is essentially an infi-dimension of sorts one can keep on hopping between when the balance in the current dimension goes to shit one way or the other with the previous ones essentially becoming Lower Depths that can be peered into or even exploited to a degree but otherwise has to abandoned for the next one where it begins anew to try and make sure it doesn't happen again? It does have a certain &quot;time&quot; aspect to it if that's something of value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T22:34:46-08:00","id":810090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serenia/Sirenia was an idea that was brought up in the first few pages by Yads Dom. I think it's supposed to be a capital, but the main thing I remember is the word &quot;Library&quot;. As for Ceto and Echidna, we've established that Ceto is the one who awakened the Sirens while Echidna is a Siren gone completely rogue. These are Big Name Ideas, so we could reiterate these points. With Nuwa, she could possibly be an example of a powerful Siren who managed to prevent one instance of The Deluge a long time ago. It could also play into the tentative &quot;History&quot; theme that was mentioned way back, where Ceto and Echidna would follow the birth of Sirens and the defection of Echidna and Nuwa would follow the reason for why Sirens are asked to stop The Deluge and care for humanity. This would also allow us to incorporate ideas from different mythologies without having any clashes. Ceto and Echidna is one tale based on Greek mythology and is within a sort of bubble while Nuwa is another tale based on Chinese mythology and exists within another bubble. The two don't overlap but their stories trickle down to explain the mindset of Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>New idea, what if Echidna is an &quot;ascended Siren&quot; gone wrong or at Lucidity 0? Kind of like how when Archmages bottom out at Wisdom 0, they basically become Puella Magi Madoka Magica Witches rather than casting spells that washes off Paradox from themselves and flings to other people. Instead of becoming a Siren with bird or sky traits, they basically become Cthulhu monsters with nearly the same insane reasoning as them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And if I may ask, what are your ideas on Nuwa? I don't recall her being brought up anywhere until now, but I vaguely like the thoughts, don't get me wrong. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm down with either Progenitors or having something effectively influence the Currents. With the Waters, they seem to be more naturally influenced by climate and location, so we could tie in the Waters with Nature. As for Currents, I wouldn't mind the normal Currents being established while the Abyssal Currents are more of rogue/maverick schools of thought that branched out from them. If Ceto did have a hand in creating the Currents, we should probably talk about the importance and the influence Ceto has over the Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. Perhaps as ideas, how are these for Progenitors? Their stories seem the most fitting for the current in question. <br /> Currents:<br /> <b>Buoyancy:</b> Mami Wata <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mami_Wata\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mami_Wata</a><br /> <b>Conflict: </b>Mazu, Neith or Ran <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazu_(goddess\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazu_(goddess</a>) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neith\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neith</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%A1n\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%A1n</a><br /> <b>Harmony: </b>Sulis <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulis\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulis</a><br /> <b>Healing: </b>Atargatis <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atargatis\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atargatis</a><br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>Saraswati <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saraswati\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saraswati</a><br /> <br /> <b>Acheron: </b>Bochica <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bochica\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bochica</a><br /> <b>Cocytus: </b>Nephthys or Sedna <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nephthys\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nephthys</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sedna_(mythology\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sedna_(mythology</a>)<br /> <b>Lethe: </b>Gomtihttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gomti_River<br /> <b>Phelegethon: </b>Boann or Calypso <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boann\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boann</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calypso_(mythology\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calypso_(mythology</a>)<br /> <b>Styx: </b>Chalchiuhtlicue <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalchiuhtlicue\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalchiuhtlicue</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel that I should read up on Demon: the Fallen now. For regional floods, that would fall under Nature and the trickle of Resentment that influences the world. The mythical flood that Noah experienced was meant to eliminate the evils of the old world, but it could be a relatively true story that Sirens of yesteryear had to experience. Nature was fed up with the disrespect humanity showed within the area, so its resentment caused a massive flood. Noah was subtly warned/influenced by the Sirens to construct the Ark and save what he could in the area.<br /> <br /> It could be that minor events that affect a region could be called a Flooding while the Big Name Apocalypse that affects the world is &quot;The Deluge&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having a REALLY hard time following all of the Timeywhimeyball stuff and I apologize for it. To just make it very simple, The Deluge is just a Bad Future where Sirens connect with their last incarnation in this world and Surface when they Drown. When it comes to interacting with Time, they can read through it like 3 trillion page encyclopedia on world history but they can't actually time travel or anything like that? I'm sorry for putting it in a really simple way but I'm getting headaches trying to think more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T22:36:30-08:00","id":810091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=810084#post810084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much obliged on the explaining, I have a better view on how Sirens are made. Tho I'm still somewhat confused on all the dimensional travel stuff, but I digress. Does it mean tho that there is essentially an infi-dimension of sorts one can keep on hopping between when the balance in the current dimension goes to shit one way or the other with the previous ones essentially becoming Lower Depths that can be peered into or even exploited to a degree but otherwise has to abandoned for the next one where it begins anew to try and make sure it doesn't happen again? It does have a certain &quot;time&quot; aspect to it if that's something of value.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be a possible explanation. If there is at least two dimensions, it serves to believe that there is an infinite number of dimensions. However, there are probably catches when it comes to dimension-hopping. The main one I can name is that Sirens only exist within a single dimension, meaning that they can only go from A to B. When they fail to protect B, that's it for their existence. The humans of Dimension B are the ones that become Sirens in Dimension C, where the Sirens of Dimension B die out from the vagaries of time reclaiming them. Whatever is left by the Sirens of Dimension B are left floating around the &quot;in-between&quot; realm as debris. <br /> <br /> To keep this sort of &quot;decay&quot; from reducing the number of Sirens and humans in the dimensions as the Sirens die out, the Dimensions keep a running tally of the number of entities in the world. Effectively, let's say that each Dimension consists of, for argument's sake, 20 entities. Dimension A has a total of 5 Sirens and 15 non-Sirens. When Dimension A dies from the Deluge, the 5 Sirens die out and 2 of those non-Sirens become Sirens. The two Sirens then travel into Dimension B and are melded into 2 of the 20 non-Siren entities. This means that in Dimension B, there are 2 Sirens and 18 non-Sirens. When Dimension B dies, the 2 Sirens die. out of the 18 non-Sirens, 3 become Sirens. When they travel to Dimension C, the 3 Sirens meld into 3 of the 20 non-Sirens. And so on and so forth. This could also lead into a situation where one individual whose sort of &quot;soul&quot; information exists in three instances within Dimension A, B, and C, can be a Siren twice, being a Siren in Dimension A, losing their Siren status in Dimension B, and becoming a Siren again in Dimension C.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is more complex, timey-wimey dimensional stuff that sort of exceeds what Sirens are, so take this with a grain of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T22:56:36-08:00","id":810095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serenia/Sirenia was an idea that was brought up in the first few pages by Yads Dom. I think it's supposed to be a capital, but the main thing I remember is the word &quot;Library&quot;. As for Ceto and Echidna, we've established that Ceto is the one who awakened the Sirens while Echidna is a Siren gone completely rogue. These are Big Name Ideas, so we could reiterate these points. With Nuwa, she could possibly be an example of a powerful Siren who managed to prevent one instance of The Deluge a long time ago. It could also play into the tentative &quot;History&quot; theme that was mentioned way back, where Ceto and Echidna would follow the birth of Sirens and the defection of Echidna and Nuwa would follow the reason for why Sirens are asked to stop The Deluge and care for humanity. This would also allow us to incorporate ideas from different mythologies without having any clashes. Ceto and Echidna is one tale based on Greek mythology and is within a sort of bubble while Nuwa is another tale based on Chinese mythology and exists within another bubble. The two don't overlap but their stories trickle down to explain the mindset of Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if Echidna was a fallen Ascended Siren? Kind of like how Archmages who hit Wisdom 0 become Puella Magi Madoka Magica Witches? :3 And instead of the bird like motifs the Ascended Sirens take up, they instead take up Cthonic appearances of utter monstrosity? :3<br /> <br /> Also, it seems like you have some thoughts on Nuwa and Noah or how they play into the game. Could you explain further how so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm down with either Progenitors or having something effectively influence the Currents. With the Waters, they seem to be more naturally influenced by climate and location, so we could tie in the Waters with Nature. As for Currents, I wouldn't mind the normal Currents being established while the Abyssal Currents are more of rogue/maverick schools of thought that branched out from them. If Ceto did have a hand in creating the Currents, we should probably talk about the importance and the influence Ceto has over the Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Progenitors for Currents.<br /> <b>Buoyancy: </b>Mami Wata <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mami_Wata\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mami_Wata</a><br /> <b>Conflict: </b>Neith or Ran <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neith\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neith</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%A1n\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%A1n</a><br /> <b>Harmony: </b>Sulis <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulis\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulis</a><br /> <b>Healing:</b> Grannus (or Nuwa?) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grannus\u200b\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grannus\u200b</a><br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>Saraswati <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saraswati\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saraswati</a><br /> <br /> <b>Acheron: </b>Bochica <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bochica\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bochica</a><br /> <b>Cocytus: </b>Nephthys <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nephthys\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nephthys</a><br /> <b>Lethe: </b>Gomti <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gomti_River\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gomti_River</a><br /> <b>Phelegethon: </b>Calypso <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calypso_(mythology\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calypso_(mythology</a>)<br /> <b>Styx: </b>Chalchiuhtlicue <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalchiuhtlicue\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalchiuhtlicue</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel that I should read up on Demon: the Fallen now. For regional floods, that would fall under Nature and the trickle of Resentment that influences the world. The mythical flood that Noah experienced was meant to eliminate the evils of the old world, but it could be a relatively true story that Sirens of yesteryear had to experience. Nature was fed up with the disrespect humanity showed within the area, so its resentment caused a massive flood. Noah was subtly warned/influenced by the Sirens to construct the Ark and save what he could in the area.<br /> <br /> It could be that minor events that affect a region could be called a Flooding while the Big Name Apocalypse that affects the world is &quot;The Deluge&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>To note, the ideas I've given after this post are a little bit outdated and as such things have changed. D: <br /> <br /> If it's fine for me to say, it feels like explaining the mechanics of the Deluge have become a small bit of a timeywhimeyball headache and I just want to ask for clarity. The Deluge is just a Bad End Future where almost everyone's future incarnations are at. People who Drown in the nWoD become Sirens, Breathless or Banshees and as such connect with their last incarnation to do so. As for the Deluge, they can read through the Deluge and the history imprinted on it (given that it's somehow connected to time it could be constantly changing in accordance to changing circumstances) and read through it like a trillion page encyclopedia of world history, but they can't actually time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T23:00:36-08:00","id":810098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serenia/Sirenia was an idea that was brought up in the first few pages by Yads Dom. I think it's supposed to be a capital, but the main thing I remember is the word &quot;Library&quot;. As for Ceto and Echidna, we've established that Ceto is the one who awakened the Sirens while Echidna is a Siren gone completely rogue. These are Big Name Ideas, so we could reiterate these points. With Nuwa, she could possibly be an example of a powerful Siren who managed to prevent one instance of The Deluge a long time ago. It could also play into the tentative &quot;History&quot; theme that was mentioned way back, where Ceto and Echidna would follow the birth of Sirens and the defection of Echidna and Nuwa would follow the reason for why Sirens are asked to stop The Deluge and care for humanity. This would also allow us to incorporate ideas from different mythologies without having any clashes. Ceto and Echidna is one tale based on Greek mythology and is within a sort of bubble while Nuwa is another tale based on Chinese mythology and exists within another bubble. The two don't overlap but their stories trickle down to explain the mindset of Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if Echidna was a fallen Ascended Siren? Kind of like how Archmages who hit Wisdom 0 become Puella Magi Madoka Magica Witches? :3 And instead of the bird like motifs the Ascended Sirens take up, they instead take up Cthonic appearances of utter monstrosity? :3<br /> <br /> Also, it seems like you have some thoughts on Nuwa and Noah or how they play into the game. Could you explain further how so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm down with either Progenitors or having something effectively influence the Currents. With the Waters, they seem to be more naturally influenced by climate and location, so we could tie in the Waters with Nature. As for Currents, I wouldn't mind the normal Currents being established while the Abyssal Currents are more of rogue/maverick schools of thought that branched out from them. If Ceto did have a hand in creating the Currents, we should probably talk about the importance and the influence Ceto has over the Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Progenitors for Currents.<br /> <b>Buoyancy: </b>Mami Wata<br /> <b>Conflict: </b>Neith or Ran <br /> <b>Harmony: </b>Sulis <br /> <b>Healing:</b> Grannus (or Nuwa?) <br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>Saraswati <br /> <br /> <b>Acheron: </b>Bochica <br /> <b>Cocytus: </b>Nephthys <br /> <b>Lethe: </b>Gomti <br /> <b>Phelegethon: </b>Calypso <br /> <b>Styx: </b>Chalchiuhtlicue <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=809863#post809863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel that I should read up on Demon: the Fallen now. For regional floods, that would fall under Nature and the trickle of Resentment that influences the world. The mythical flood that Noah experienced was meant to eliminate the evils of the old world, but it could be a relatively true story that Sirens of yesteryear had to experience. Nature was fed up with the disrespect humanity showed within the area, so its resentment caused a massive flood. Noah was subtly warned/influenced by the Sirens to construct the Ark and save what he could in the area.<br /> <br /> It could be that minor events that affect a region could be called a Flooding while the Big Name Apocalypse that affects the world is &quot;The Deluge&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>To note, the ideas I've given after this post are a little bit outdated and as such things have changed. D: <br /> <br /> If it's fine for me to say (and yes I have read your most recent post before this one), it feels like explaining the mechanics of the Deluge have become a small bit of a timeywhimeyball headache and I just want to ask or clarify for clarity. The Deluge is just a Bad End Future where almost everyone's future incarnations are at. People who Drown in the nWoD become Sirens, Breathless or Banshees and as such connect with their last incarnation to do so. As for the Deluge, they can read through the Deluge and the history imprinted on it (given that it's somehow connected to time it could be constantly changing in accordance to changing circumstances) and read through it like a trillion page encyclopedia of world history, but they can't actually time travel outside of &quot;The Deluge being the apocalypse&quot;. And there's ALWAYS a chance for an apocalypse if you look at truly intergalactic proportions, like a freak meteor coming this way, a black hole's emission blasting through Earth, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T00:03:37-08:00","id":810119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=810098#post810098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if Echidna was a fallen Ascended Siren? Kind of like how Archmages who hit Wisdom 0 become Puella Magi Madoka Magica Witches? :3 And instead of the bird like motifs the Ascended Sirens take up, they instead take up Cthonic appearances of utter monstrosity? :3<br /> <br /> Also, it seems like you have some thoughts on Nuwa and Noah or how they play into the game. Could you explain further how so?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cthonic or Lovecraftian? Because Cthonic refers to the underworld and death. I like the idea of Echidna having Ascended and becoming more death-like in appearance. <br /> <br /> As for Nuwa and Noah, I was thinking that they could be a sort of legendary example of Sirens and individuals who were influenced by Sirens. With Echidna being a Siren who has defected and Ceto being the Ur-progenitor of all Sirens, I felt that it would be interesting to explore other mythologies to see what would make for interesting Sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Progenitors for Currents.<br /> <b>Buoyancy: </b>Mami Wata<br /> <b>Conflict: </b>Neith or Ran<br /> <b>Harmony: </b>Sulis<br /> <b>Healing:</b> Grannus (or Nuwa?)<br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>Saraswati<br /> <br /> <b>Acheron: </b>Bochica<br /> <b>Cocytus: </b>Nephthys<br /> <b>Lethe: </b>Gomti<br /> <b>Phelegethon: </b>Calypso<br /> <b>Styx: </b>Chalchiuhtlicue </div> </div> </div>Hmm...I can see these deities being progenitors, but it's almost misleading. I wouldn't necessarily say that the Currents were started out by Progenitors, but more-so that the Currents existed, but weren't necessarily codified until these beings sort of exemplified the aspects of the Currents. I guess it would be more correct to say that examples to follow would be these beings. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To note, the ideas I've given after this post are a little bit outdated and as such things have changed. D:<br /> <br /> If it's fine for me to say (and yes I have read your most recent post before this one), it feels like explaining the mechanics of the Deluge have become a small bit of a timeywhimeyball headache and I just want to ask or clarify for clarity. The Deluge is just a Bad End Future where almost everyone's future incarnations are at. People who Drown in the nWoD become Sirens, Breathless or Banshees and as such connect with their last incarnation to do so. As for the Deluge, they can read through the Deluge and the history imprinted on it (given that it's somehow connected to time it could be constantly changing in accordance to changing circumstances) and read through it like a trillion page encyclopedia of world history, but they can't actually time travel outside of &quot;The Deluge being the apocalypse&quot;. And there's ALWAYS a chance for an apocalypse if you look at truly intergalactic proportions, like a freak meteor coming this way, a black hole's emission blasting through Earth, etc etc. </div> </div> </div>No worries. It is pretty unclear, especially because it's almost all ad hoc and made-up on the spot. I would say that it's kinda like this: The Deluge pops in and drowns everyone. This effectively renders Dimension A that The Deluge happened in a lifeless realm as Nature attempts to heal. This causes the Sirens to pop up in Dimension B that exists parallel. Said Siren can perform a sort-of time travel that is limited to a parallel shift of consciousness into Dimension A. This would allow them to have access to the history of Dimension A. The &quot;in-between&quot; realm is something like a Celestial Ocean that allows a Siren to move from Dimension A to Dimension B and vice-versa. This Celestial Ocean also contains remnants of other Dimensions, though Sirens cannot truly interact with these other Dimensions nor can they contact Sirens that are traveling through their own Dimensions. However, there is debris that is lost in the Celestial Ocean that hints at possible outcomes. Some of this jetsam is from WAY back, like a newspaper that mentions that Lincoln was assassinated by a general. It's a partial deviation from this reality, but it does state that there is a possibility that Lincoln would be assassinated by a general, giving Sirens that were alive during the Civil War information about Lincoln. Some of this jetsam could be fairly new, like a notebook that mentions a leak of natural gas affecting a town. <br /> <br /> The Deluge is still the Big Bad Thing that Sirens want to stop, because it effectively means the end of the Sirens and of humanity in Dimension B and the birth of Sirens that need to go through this cycle again in Dimension C. And the threat of imminent, galactic-scale death is always possible, though that could possibly change if we ever decide to include information for an Infinite Macabre setting hack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T09:02:15-08:00","id":810252,"title":"","content":"Anyone seen The Man in the High Castle? The Deluge is starting to make me think of it like the movies in that show.<br /> For those who don't know, in the show the Axis won WW2 so Nazi Germany and the Japanese Empire rule most of the world (with Italians also around somewhat). In the show there are these movies from lord knows where showing what could've been ranging from the allies winning the war to Soviet propaganda made by Stalin after his death in the Axis world etc. It's a bit of a spoiler but it becomes increasingly apparent that there are alternate realities at play there not least when one Japanese guy suddenly wakes up in what seems to be our 1950's or so when the Cuba embargo by the U.S. was put into play. Not the most eloquent description, but it's about the long and the short of it; is it comparable to how you imagine the Deluge, Reaper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T10:00:52-08:00","id":810271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=810119#post810119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cthonic or Lovecraftian? Because Cthonic refers to the underworld and death. I like the idea of Echidna having Ascended and becoming more death-like in appearance.<br /> <br /> As for Nuwa and Noah, I was thinking that they could be a sort of legendary example of Sirens and individuals who were influenced by Sirens. With Echidna being a Siren who has defected and Ceto being the Ur-progenitor of all Sirens, I felt that it would be interesting to explore other mythologies to see what would make for interesting Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I thought that Cthonic referred to &quot;Like Cthulhu&quot; rather than &quot;underworld and death&quot;. Lovecraftian is more fitting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=810119#post810119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...I can see these deities being progenitors, but it's almost misleading. I wouldn't necessarily say that the Currents were started out by Progenitors, but more-so that the Currents existed, but weren't necessarily codified until these beings sort of exemplified the aspects of the Currents. I guess it would be more correct to say that examples to follow would be these beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it'd be kind of like the Supernal Realms before the Watchtowers so to speak? They existed but didn't have anything special to them or were overly codified until the Fall occurred? I'm fine with doing something similar like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=810119#post810119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Celestial Ocean is like the Gauntlet so to speak (in comparison I should say)? Like the Time River that Yads brought up?<br /> <br /> I must apologize, I sort of get this explanation better, let's just say its 75-99% explained for me, but I'm kind of borked which is why I can't fully grasp things and that understanding can't get up to 100%. I'm only this way for the moment at least (I totally blame college classes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T17:20:31-08:00","id":810408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=810252#post810252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone seen The Man in the High Castle? The Deluge is starting to make me think of it like the movies in that show.<br /> For those who don't know, in the show the Axis won WW2 so Nazi Germany and the Japanese Empire rule most of the world (with Italians also around somewhat). In the show there are these movies from lord knows where showing what could've been ranging from the allies winning the war to Soviet propaganda made by Stalin after his death in the Axis world etc. It's a bit of a spoiler but it becomes increasingly apparent that there are alternate realities at play there not least when one Japanese guy suddenly wakes up in what seems to be our 1950's or so when the Cuba embargo by the U.S. was put into play. Not the most eloquent description, but it's about the long and the short of it; is it comparable to how you imagine the Deluge, Reaper?</div> </div> </div> </div>Effectively. It does work out a bit differently for Sirens. The main thing is that at one dimension has been effectively bricked by The Deluge. The Sirens may still access the dimension, but there isn't anything that is progressing in the dimension other than floating bodies and water for days. The other dimension that the Sirens can access has not been affected by The Deluge and is teeming with life. There may be differences here and there, but the general composition of both dimensions is the same. Houses may have different families living within them, media may be following different trends at different points, and so forth. Both realities are set in stone and don't &quot;bleed&quot; into one another. When it comes to the &quot;in-between&quot; realm, that's when reality begins to leak. A Siren traveling between the two dimensions may end up finding pieces of information that hit to key points in other dimensions. A Siren may find information about an unsolved murder in her dimension that was solved in another dimension or she may find evidence of a secret deal that happened in a dimension a few weeks from the &quot;now&quot; of the Siren's living dimension. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=810271#post810271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it'd be kind of like the Supernal Realms before the Watchtowers so to speak? They existed but didn't have anything special to them or were overly codified until the Fall occurred? I'm fine with doing something similar like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically. Each Current flows, but there never really was any meaning to them until a mythical being, like Mami Wata, Calypso, etc. demonstrated and gave the Currents a purpose.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the Celestial Ocean is like the Gauntlet so to speak (in comparison I should say)? Like the Time River that Yads brought up?<br /> <br /> I must apologize, I sort of get this explanation better, let's just say its 75-99% explained for me, but I'm kind of borked which is why I can't fully grasp things and that understanding can't get up to 100%. I'm only this way for the moment at least (I totally blame college classes). </div> </div> </div>I believe so. In effect, it's the crossroads between realities. It's not exactly something like Arcadia or the Underworld because it's more of a tunnel passage than an actual realm itself. Sirens can't exactly stay inside the Celestial Ocean for a long period of time because the Celestial Ocean is always flowing, pushing the Sirens from one reality to the other. It's the interdimensional equivalent of an airport's conveyor belt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T08:54:19-08:00","id":810646,"title":"","content":"As long as the realities remain New World of Darkness (which includes earth and all other realities attached to it or the people on it (Underworld, Shadow, Astral, etc) and Deluge (Future bad end), I'm fine with that. Any more than that and I feel it would be too complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T14:20:53-08:00","id":810815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=810646#post810646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as the realities remain New World of Darkness (which includes earth and all other realities attached to it or the people on it (Underworld, Shadow, Astral, etc) and Deluge (Future bad end), I'm fine with that. Any more than that and I feel it would be too complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The realities are probably attached to the location that the Siren is linked to. If we ever get to the whole &quot;Infinite Macabre&quot; scenario that sets the game in a space opera, it could change. However, the realities are firmly placed in Earth.<br /> <br /> I think an important distinction to make is that the Celestial Ocean only attaches the natural world, not any of the supernatural realms like Arcadia, the Shadow, etc. The Celestial Ocean only exists to those who are able to Surface from The Deluge, meaning that Sirens and the Breathless are fundamentally connected to it. In relation to alternate realms and the Celestial Ocean, Arcadia exists as a constant beyond space and time; it is unaffected by separate realities. Individuals who are meant to become Changelings may change between realities, but they are all taken to the same plane of existence. The same goes for the Astral Realms. The Shadow is partially different in that it would be linked to the specific instances of the realities, where some structures may be radically different based on what existed or happened in that reality. Similarly, the Underworld is tied to the realities as well, depending on who has died in that reality.<br /> <br /> Basically, anything that goes beyond plausible explanation and exists in a sort of &quot;dream&quot; state is not tied to reality while things that are plausible and are part of the natural process of the world is tied to reality. <br /> <br /> To put the Celestial Ocean into more visual terms, it is akin to the Wood Between the Worlds in <i>The Chronicles of Narnia</i> or the Sea of Doors in <i>Bioshock: Infinite.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:06:29-08:00","id":811280,"title":"","content":"Augh, the moment I feel less borked and ready to contribute yet school is coming tomorrow. &gt;&gt; Anyways, what shall we do next? I believe I might need to put down the &quot;know&quot; things that Reaper posted that would add abit more fluff to the Siren Waters this week. I might/should get to work on Tropicana sometime too. &gt;&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T17:24:17-08:00","id":811402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=811280#post811280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Augh, the moment I feel less borked and ready to contribute yet school is coming tomorrow. &gt;&gt; Anyways, what shall we do next? I believe I might need to put down the &quot;know&quot; things that Reaper posted that would add abit more fluff to the Siren Waters this week. I might/should get to work on Tropicana sometime too. &gt;&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>The most-obvious thing we should do after the Waters would be the Currents and fleshing out what they mean and how they interact. We might also want to push on codifying the lore or at least establishing what events are important when it comes to a Siren. The main thing is the Surfacing and The Song, which are key points that create a Siren. It kinda raises the question of how much does it change the once-mortal's perspective on life, especially considering that the Sirens merge two existences together. How much of Dimension A's memories flow into Dimension B's? There is a lot of questions that are raised and should be answered.<br /> <br /> I think this version of <i><b>Siren </b></i>kinda deviated from what the typical depiction of Sirens are. I'm not saying that it's wrong, but I think some of my ideas are going too far into the &quot;high sci-fi&quot; direction. It's mainly how I justified Sirens, the &quot;time&quot; theme, and the idea of alternate dimensions. It's considerably jarring when the other aspects of <b><i>Siren </i></b>revolve around music, nature, and mythology. <br /> <br /> Taking a step back, the key lore of <b><i>Siren</i></b> is that humanity is going to be wiped out by The Deluge, an apocalyptic flood. The last of humanity began a melody known as The Song to express their profound regret and sorrow over the state of the world under The Deluge. This caused Ceto to awaken the Sirens and send them either back in time or to an alternate dimension. Echidna is a running antagonistic force to the Sirens and she controls a sort of stronghold known as Serenia, a great library that holds the history of the world within it. She is also the creator of the Vodianoi, amalgamations of humanity and sea creatures in order to create a life form that can withstand The Deluge. Eventually, the Currents were created from exceptional, mythical Sirens exemplifying a certain way of interacting with humanity. The Celestial Ocean, a realm that exists between realms, allows the Sirens access to their previous life as well as granting them a way to see into alternate realities.<br /> <br /> I think, as someone has said before, that the multiple realities idea muddles the general feel of Sirens. Considering that Sirens are oracles with the ability to Trace events and are meant to be mediators between humanity and nature, while factoring in that there is a theme of History and a Music-based motif, maybe it would be better to make the &quot;alternate realities&quot; into &quot;Oral History&quot;. Rather than being from a bad future, Sirens are actually from the past where The Deluge has already happened. The world has already reset multiple times, meaning that there has been lineages of Sirens that have attempted to stop The Deluge of their time. Some had succeeded, some had failed. However, The Deluge always comes to claim them. When The Deluge comes, it wipes out humanity as well as the Sirens in its waves. Some Sirens accept their failure, passing on their nature to the Sirens of the new world. Some Sirens refuse to accept their failure, disappearing into the depths of the Celestial Ocean, as did Echidna, the Siren of the first world. When a Siren is born into the new world, they hear an echo that ripples in their mind, like a drop of water in a lake. That echo, that sound is the remnants of The Song, the haunting melody sang by the lost humans of the first world. It is The Song that awakens the Sirens. The Sirens of the new world must struggle, the waves of many Deluges surrounding them in a whirlpool of suffering. When a Siren Surfaces from these memories, they are alive. <br /> <br /> When a Siren emerges after Hearing the Song and Surfacing, they have gained the essence that makes them a Siren. The Song that echoed in their mind were the words of Sirens past, warning them of a disaster that awaits their world. The chorus of voices whisper to them, urging them to take up their mantle in order to stop the coming storm. The many records that have been drowned by The Deluge may be gone, but the struggle of the Sirens will live on as long as one Siren fights. <br /> <br /> Hopefully, this would remove the complexity of multiple universes without losing on what the core of Sirens is meant to be. It would also allow us to justify the idea of submerged lands that was mentioned a while ago, with Mu, Lemuria, Ys, etc. being lands that existed before The Deluges of the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:35:35-08:00","id":811737,"title":"","content":"To me it turns more confusing without the multiple universes aspect but at the same time I see what you're saying and can see how people may dislike it based on the notion that alternate realities exist might feel intrusive on other lines since it'd mean they have to have been covered on those scales too.<br /> That said, I am again confused on how exactly Sirens work now that they're from the past instead; is it some sort of reincarnation scheme? Does a Siren switch hosts using humans somehow via music (and drowning)? That could run with the &quot;mermaids tricking people into the oceans&quot; stories. Or it could just be their way of pro-creating. But it makes me wonder, are Sirens biologically immortal? Living at the bottom of the ocean or so? And how does the Deluge actually happen? How is humanity still here if it supposedly has been victimized by it several times already? We need to map this out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:59:47-08:00","id":812149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=811737#post811737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it turns more confusing without the multiple universes aspect but at the same time I see what you're saying and can see how people may dislike it based on the notion that alternate realities exist might feel intrusive on other lines since it'd mean they have to have been covered on those scales too.<br /> That said, I am again confused on how exactly Sirens work now that they're from the past instead; is it some sort of reincarnation scheme? Does a Siren switch hosts using humans somehow via music (and drowning)? That could run with the &quot;mermaids tricking people into the oceans&quot; stories. Or it could just be their way of pro-creating. But it makes me wonder, are Sirens biologically immortal? Living at the bottom of the ocean or so? And how does the Deluge actually happen? How is humanity still here if it supposedly has been victimized by it several times already? We need to map this out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe it would work like this: Sirens aren't completely immortal. They are long-living at 300 years if they can sequester themselves and avoid any contact with chemicals or the Flensers. The main thing is that Sirens were awakened to stop the next instance of The Deluge at this time. The Sirens that managed to stop one of the instances were able to live a calm life with humanity until the next instance. When The Deluge is not stopped, the Sirens give up their existence in order to empower the next generation of Sirens. Some Sirens who refuse to fully give up their existence are thrown into the Celestial Ocean where they are cursed to watch the lineage of Sirens succeed and fail over time. The oldest of these Sirens is Echidna, who is able to reach out into the material world and create her Vodianoi. <br /> <br /> With The Deluge, it is Nature's reset button that destroys life above the sea as it attempts to recover from a major disaster. Note that The Deluge is not necessarily always based on water. It could be a natural disaster on a small-scale that allows Nature to repair a damaged landscape without interference. Smaller instances of The Deluge is known as Flooding, the arguably best-known being the flood that Noah experienced. Sirens are meant to deal with Floodings immediately while The Deluge is a sort of disaster that is waiting on the horizon. While the Floodings are meant to &quot;patch things up&quot;, The Deluge is meant to &quot;shut everything down and start from scratch&quot;. The Deluge is the last resort for Nature as it tries to start again from square one. The implications of this is that humanity has existed multiple times before and have failed to right their wrongs before The Deluge hit, creating this sort of cycle of inevitability.<br /> <br /> Because The Deluge is a reset, it destroys any evidence of previous life on earth as it returns to the beginning of life. Time and time again, humans rise as a dominant species and continue on their lives as expected. The major difference is the existence of Sirens, who are able to see glimpses of the past existences due to their connection with the Celestial Ocean. This is sort of where the &quot;Oral History&quot; idea comes in. Humanity does not remember their past existences but Sirens are able to sense the past. The memories may be fuzzy the further the memories go into the past, but it grants them some sort of insight that drives them to make changes in the world so that humanity may live, even if it is just for a little bit longer. <br /> <br /> I also want to say that there are things that managed to escape from The Deluge, considering that The Deluge is meant to affect terrestrial life. Things that manage to hide deep within the oceans or escape into orbit are able to survive The Deluge. However, this means that they will have to experience eras of change and evolution to return to a point where humanity exists as top-dog. If these things are able to survive for that long, they could be drastically different, warped from years of breeding or aged to the point where they decay at a light touch. It's a myth among Sirens, but some believe that deep down in the oceans, past the Hadal Zone, exists a breed of Sirens that have long-since lost their connection to the Celestial Ocean. They are hungry beings who are unable to think, unable to remember The Song. They have grown into titanic creatures that will exist even when The Deluge comes, time and time again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:45:35-08:00","id":812210,"title":"","content":"Since your paragraph sort of implies that Sirens can Time Travel, a thing we sort of decided wouldn't be possible (at least for normal Sirens) and that could create plot holes for Siren. How about for the sake of your reset button idea, we state that Ascended Sirens are capable of travelling through time the same way that normal Sirens Trace? That's the only problem I can see at the moment.<br /> <br /> I have one other bad thought. If we incorporate the &quot;Deluge = Nature's reset button&quot;, doesn't that make the Deluge an utter certainty? Doesn't it have the same feel of hopelessness like Werewolf the Apocalypse did because like the game line it does have a minor feel of &quot;the apocalypse is going to happen no matter what&quot;. I just want to avoid &quot;Darkness Induced Apathy Syndrome&quot; and show that the Deluge is at least avoidable.<br /> <br /> And also, for some reason all the talk of the Deluge being a reset button reminds me of Undertale, which I just got through. I now totally imagine Echidna having the sameish personality as Flowey. I'll put Flowey's story and how I see it fitting Echidna into the spoilers.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Simply put, Flowey is a soulless (fitting considering we're chatting on Sirens) Flower who was reincarnated from his human remains. In the Genocide/No Mercy route, he tells the Player that he lacked a soul, so he lacked compassion, mercy, empathy, but he kept any traits other than that (rage, sadness, joy, every emotion not empathy). He had the power to &quot;Reset&quot;, to send everything back to the way it was back in time. Simply put, he at first repeated a timeline and did good acts, then did evil acts (such as murdering people with the excuse of &quot;just because I want to know&quot;) which he did again and again until he basically saw every possibility that could be done, in a sense he's basically stuck rereading a book with multiple endings depending on how you read it. Everything is predictable and boring. The only thing that makes things different and not predictable is the player character (to which he's attached to) and he wants to do something that will make things unpredictable again.<br /> <br /> How I see it is that Echidna shares these specific traits. She's been around enough to know that the Deluge WILL happen time and time again because the timeline is predictable and repeating itself. Humanity and Nature are both basically predictable to Echidna, and her attempts at destroying that predictability and something to survive the Deluge (perhaps also her desperately trying to love something despite being utterly incapable of it along with being her Eugenics experiments) is the Vodianoi. At best, they're only partially successful, but the only people who present new variables or branching off paths so to speak are Sirens (and any other Supernatural beings really) as a whole. They're fully capable of creating new paths out that could even fix the Deluge. Perhaps her attachment to Sirens plays out in her wanting them to join her side or something. But I feel this would derail Echidna being the &quot;Eugenics mad momma Antagonist&quot;.</div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> And I think on the case of the last paragraph, could we please keep those only as myth rather than actual antagonists? It feels like the game has enough Antagonists (The Abyssal Currents, Echidna and her Vodianoi, at least half of the Breathless and Banshees population). I'm sorry if bad for these thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:12:07-08:00","id":812255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812210#post812210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one other bad thought. If we incorporate the &quot;Deluge = Nature's reset button&quot;, doesn't that make the Deluge an utter certainty? Doesn't it have the same feel of hopelessness like Werewolf the Apocalypse did because like the game line it does have a minor feel of &quot;the apocalypse is going to happen no matter what&quot;. I just want to avoid &quot;Darkness Induced Apathy Syndrome&quot; and show that the Deluge is at least avoidable..</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI agree a lot with this.<br /> <br /> I didn't thought at first that another realities existed in Siren. The only two things that existed were the &quot;Here and Now&quot; and the &quot;Future&quot;. When a Siren surfaces it is far more a Calling of the Song than a reincarnation kind of thing. I mean, the Song needs new soldiers so it calls out humans that have the traumatic experience and are compeled enough to fight against the Deluge. When you surfaces your whole body is brought to the Deluge where you hear the Song. You effectively travels to the future with your whole body, but that's the only place you can access. The Deluge is Geographically locked, so if you Flows from this Realm to the Deluge in Brazil you appear in the counterpart for Brazil in the Deluge.<br /> <br /> Effectively, the Deluge is a Astral Realm like Arcadia that reflects the possible future of the world. Don't think we need to have lots of complex aspects like many realities and time travels in the game. The Trace would work like visions of the possible future of a thing or person, a future that is imprinted in the deluge if you know where to look.<br /> <br /> I.e: A Siren wants to to understand if the new Paper Factory that is coming to town will have some impact in the city. He then goes in the Deluge to see if that factory has a reflection there (much like the Shadow) and realizes the location there is full of hints about a poisoning from chemicals of the factory (Newspaper articles and so on), now the Siren has a more clear perception of what and how things went bad and can try to stop that from happening.<br /> <br /> Hope I could explain the way I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:53:25-08:00","id":812280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812210#post812210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry if bad for these thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Yad's explanation of the Deluge sold it to me. The biggest concern I have is if we can run it as an Astral Realm that presumably is bleeding into the Earth by causing the Floods and all without involving the Werewolf by necessity since they exclusively deal with spiritual stuff coming from other places. I need to ask on clarification on if the Deluge has happened globally and if so when and how? What is it that actually causes the Deluge? Climate change? The Astral Realm bleeding into Earth? Nature-aligned Sirens trying to make it win? Even if Nature in and of itself is a sentient enough force to push reset buttons we ought to explain how it's done and how catastrophies can start risking the entire planet or so. Also are these &quot;titanic beings&quot; at all related to Leviathan by chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T19:59:06-08:00","id":812331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since your paragraph sort of implies that Sirens can Time Travel, a thing we sort of decided wouldn't be possible (at least for normal Sirens) and that could create plot holes for Siren. How about for the sake of your reset button idea, we state that Ascended Sirens are capable of travelling through time the same way that normal Sirens Trace? That's the only problem I can see at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to write around with the idea that Sirens are using their Trace to peer into the Celestial Ocean in order to see past events rather than them actually time-traveling. Sirens are still stuck in whatever time period they are in but they feel like there are things that they know without experiencing them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one other bad thought. If we incorporate the &quot;Deluge = Nature's reset button&quot;, doesn't that make the Deluge an utter certainty? Doesn't it have the same feel of hopelessness like Werewolf the Apocalypse did because like the game line it does have a minor feel of &quot;the apocalypse is going to happen no matter what&quot;. I just want to avoid &quot;Darkness Induced Apathy Syndrome&quot; and show that the Deluge is at least avoidable.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812255#post812255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI agree a lot with this.<br /> <br /> I didn't thought at first that another realities existed in Siren. The only two things that existed were the &quot;Here and Now&quot; and the &quot;Future&quot;. When a Siren surfaces it is far more a Calling of the Song than a reincarnation kind of thing. I mean, the Song needs new soldiers so it calls out humans that have the traumatic experience and are compeled enough to fight against the Deluge. When you surfaces your whole body is brought to the Deluge where you hear the Song. You effectively travels to the future with your whole body, but that's the only place you can access. The Deluge is Geographically locked, so if you Flows from this Realm to the Deluge in Brazil you appear in the counterpart for Brazil in the Deluge.<br /> <br /> Effectively, the Deluge is a Astral Realm like Arcadia that reflects the possible future of the world. Don't think we need to have lots of complex aspects like many realities and time travels in the game. The Trace would work like visions of the possible future of a thing or person, a future that is imprinted in the deluge if you know where to look.<br /> <br /> I.e: A Siren wants to to understand if the new Paper Factory that is coming to town will have some impact in the city. He then goes in the Deluge to see if that factory has a reflection there (much like the Shadow) and realizes the location there is full of hints about a poisoning from chemicals of the factory (Newspaper articles and so on), now the Siren has a more clear perception of what and how things went bad and can try to stop that from happening.<br /> <br /> Hope I could explain the way I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812280#post812280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yad's explanation of the Deluge sold it to me. The biggest concern I have is if we can run it as an Astral Realm that presumably is bleeding into the Earth by causing the Floods and all without involving the Werewolf by necessity since they exclusively deal with spiritual stuff coming from other places. I need to ask on clarification on if the Deluge has happened globally and if so when and how? What is it that actually causes the Deluge? Climate change? The Astral Realm bleeding into Earth? Nature-aligned Sirens trying to make it win? Even if Nature in and of itself is a sentient enough force to push reset buttons we ought to explain how it's done and how catastrophies can start risking the entire planet or so. Also are these &quot;titanic beings&quot; at all related to Leviathan by chance?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main thing that's throwing The Deluge off is that we all agree that it's at least an Apocalyptic event. It is the complete end of the world, which leads into Gehenna and the issues that came with that. In order to change that, there should be some lore that states that it is possible to actually stop The Deluge, which is where the idea of having multiple Deluges in the past came in. With every victory against The Deluge, the Sirens successfully allow humanity to live for a few more millennia before another Deluge comes. Of course, the Sirens that were successful will be long dead before The Deluge comes back, so they procreate or find more Sirens in order to teach them about The Deluge before it's too late. The Deluge has taken the world before already, but it has also been avoided several times before. <br /> <br /> The Celestial Ocean is a means to incorporate the idea of having The Deluge be a realm without having to make it so that there are obvious solutions to issues. Knowing that, in the future, a factory is going to be the utter death of a city is kinda railroad-y, even if all the hints and clues point towards it. However, if a Siren wants to learn more about the factory, she visits the Celestial Ocean, where she sees the possible paths that the factory can take. It could be dumping out chemicals and cause huge environmental damage, as it says on a newspaper. It could also possibly switch to a cleaner, more eco-friendly process, as stated in another newspaper. There is more information on the two possibilities, enticing the Siren to actually investigate the factory and either stop it if it's moving in a harmful direction or nudge it subtly so that it goes on the &quot;right&quot; path. <br /> <br /> The Deluge itself, the end-all apocalypse, is global and is meant to occur some time in the future from now. The Floodings, disasters that are in effect miniature Deluges, are regional and occur sporadically. In order to not step on Werewolf's toes, The Deluge and the Floodings are entirely natural events in technicality <i>(as in they are not necessarily influenced by ghosts, spirits, etc. They are technically natural responses made by Nature). </i>The rate at which Floodings appear indicates how much longer the Sirens have until The Deluge comes. The reason for why The Deluge and Floodings occur is because Nature has been agitated to the point where it's resentment to those who disturb it bleeds out into the wildlife, leading to things like feral creatures, strange variations in the weather, and natural disasters without warning. A few pages back, I was describing what happens when certain areas are affected by Nature's resentment. I didn't give the phenomenon a name but Floodings might be a name for now.<br /> <br /> As for the beings, see below.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also, for some reason all the talk of the Deluge being a reset button reminds me of Undertale, which I just got through. I now totally imagine Echidna having the sameish personality as Flowey. I'll put Flowey's story and how I see it fitting Echidna into the spoilers.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Simply put, Flowey is a soulless (fitting considering we're chatting on Sirens) Flower who was reincarnated from his human remains. In the Genocide/No Mercy route, he tells the Player that he lacked a soul, so he lacked compassion, mercy, empathy, but he kept any traits other than that (rage, sadness, joy, every emotion not empathy). He had the power to &quot;Reset&quot;, to send everything back to the way it was back in time. Simply put, he at first repeated a timeline and did good acts, then did evil acts (such as murdering people with the excuse of &quot;just because I want to know&quot;) which he did again and again until he basically saw every possibility that could be done, in a sense he's basically stuck rereading a book with multiple endings depending on how you read it. Everything is predictable and boring. The only thing that makes things different and not predictable is the player character (to which he's attached to) and he wants to do something that will make things unpredictable again.<br /> <br /> How I see it is that Echidna shares these specific traits. She's been around enough to know that the Deluge WILL happen time and time again because the timeline is predictable and repeating itself. Humanity and Nature are both basically predictable to Echidna, and her attempts at destroying that predictability and something to survive the Deluge (perhaps also her desperately trying to love something despite being utterly incapable of it along with being her Eugenics experiments) is the Vodianoi. At best, they're only partially successful, but the only people who present new variables or branching off paths so to speak are Sirens (and any other Supernatural beings really) as a whole. They're fully capable of creating new paths out that could even fix the Deluge. Perhaps her attachment to Sirens plays out in her wanting them to join her side or something. But I feel this would derail Echidna being the &quot;Eugenics mad momma Antagonist&quot;.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And I think on the case of the last paragraph, could we please keep those only as myth rather than actual antagonists? It feels like the game has enough Antagonists (The Abyssal Currents, Echidna and her Vodianoi, at least half of the Breathless and Banshees population). I'm sorry if bad for these thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to be sorry. When projects grow, they tend to cause disagreement when it comes to direction.<br /> <br /> I can see that connection. I feel that Echidna would encourage the Sirens to fight back against The Deluge so that she herself can break the cycle with her creation. The longer she has to continue her operations on living humans, the better-prepared the Vodianoi will be when The Deluge comes.<br /> <br /> As for the titanic beings, they are almost entirely myth in a sense that Ascension into winged Sirens is a myth. Most Sirens are willing to dismiss it as a fool's errand, but some Sirens are morbidly curious as to if it is true, most-likely the Sirens of Dark Wisdom. They postulate that, in theory, it is not impossible; however, no Siren is willing to even attempt it as it would mean giving up their connection to humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:27:16-08:00","id":812349,"title":"","content":"I vote for &quot;Floodings&quot; being the name for &quot;miniture-Deluges.&quot; The last question I have is how Nature can be sentient; is it akin to Gaia in Werewolf: The Apocalypse where the planet itself is alive to some extent? Is there some outward force that looks down and go &quot;this is messed up&quot; a l\u00e1 God(-Machine)? Or is it one of those &quot;you decide lel ;D&quot; that White Wolf sometimes do with the mystery being left up to the Storyteller? Other than this question I feel everything I'm curious about has been answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:38:46-08:00","id":812352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812331#post812331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to write around with the idea that Sirens are using their Trace to peer into the Celestial Ocean in order to see past events rather than them actually time-traveling. Sirens are still stuck in whatever time period they are in but they feel like there are things that they know without experiencing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Pardon me, I thought you were writing up that they could time travel and I misread it. D:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812331#post812331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing that's throwing The Deluge off is that we all agree that it's at least an Apocalyptic event. It is the complete end of the world, which leads into Gehenna and the issues that came with that. In order to change that, there should be some lore that states that it is possible to actually stop The Deluge, which is where the idea of having multiple Deluges in the past came in. With every victory against The Deluge, the Sirens successfully allow humanity to live for a few more millennia before another Deluge comes. Of course, the Sirens that were successful will be long dead before The Deluge comes back, so they procreate or find more Sirens in order to teach them about The Deluge before it's too late. The Deluge has taken the world before already, but it has also been avoided several times before.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the multiple Deluges in the past were really extremely large scale floodings? I can get behind that, and hopefully it doesn't interfere with other Splat's cosmology. If it doesn't, then it could mean that Sirens are potentially one of the oldest splats on Earth. Fittingly so, as most life began from the water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812331#post812331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Celestial Ocean is a means to incorporate the idea of having The Deluge be a realm without having to make it so that there are obvious solutions to issues. Knowing that, in the future, a factory is going to be the utter death of a city is kinda railroad-y, even if all the hints and clues point towards it. However, if a Siren wants to learn more about the factory, she visits the Celestial Ocean, where she sees the possible paths that the factory can take. It could be dumping out chemicals and cause huge environmental damage, as it says on a newspaper. It could also possibly switch to a cleaner, more eco-friendly process, as stated in another newspaper. There is more information on the two possibilities, enticing the Siren to actually investigate the factory and either stop it if it's moving in a harmful direction or nudge it subtly so that it goes on the &quot;right&quot; path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind this, gives more gameplay potential. Especially given IIRC this was one of the problems Werewolf the Apocalypse faced too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812331#post812331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deluge itself, the end-all apocalypse, is global and is meant to occur some time in the future from now. The Floodings, disasters that are in effect miniature Deluges, are regional and occur sporadically. In order to not step on Werewolf's toes, The Deluge and the Floodings are entirely natural events in technicality <i>(as in they are not necessarily influenced by ghosts, spirits, etc. They are technically natural responses made by Nature). </i>The rate at which Floodings appear indicates how much longer the Sirens have until The Deluge comes. The reason for why The Deluge and Floodings occur is because Nature has been agitated to the point where it's resentment to those who disturb it bleeds out into the wildlife, leading to things like feral creatures, strange variations in the weather, and natural disasters without warning. A few pages back, I was describing what happens when certain areas are affected by Nature's resentment. I didn't give the phenomenon a name but Floodings might be a name for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Floodings sound good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812331#post812331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the titanic beings, they are almost entirely myth in a sense that Ascension into winged Sirens is a myth. Most Sirens are willing to dismiss it as a fool's errand, but some Sirens are morbidly curious as to if it is true, most-likely the Sirens of Dark Wisdom. They postulate that, in theory, it is not impossible; however, no Siren is willing to even attempt it as it would mean giving up their connection to humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of like the Wyrd Transcendance for Changelings or becoming an Empress in PtH? If so, then me gusta.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder. Echidna has been around for a VERY long time given how it seems to be coming up, and the idea I have for her atm is that she's an Ascended Siren at Lucidity 0. I was thinking, perhaps one bonus for an Ascended Siren (no matter what their Morality is at) would be straight up Age Immortality? As in they stop aging altogether? Would seal up the plothole of &quot;How has Echidna lived for 1000+ years and yet Sirens can only live up to be about 300 years old&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:46:22-08:00","id":812355,"title":"","content":"Jellyfishes are biologically immortal; maybe she found a way to draw from that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T22:01:23-08:00","id":812388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812349#post812349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vote for &quot;Floodings&quot; being the name for &quot;miniture-Deluges.&quot; The last question I have is how Nature can be sentient; is it akin to Gaia in Werewolf: The Apocalypse where the planet itself is alive to some extent? Is there some outward force that looks down and go &quot;this is messed up&quot; a l\u00e1 God(-Machine)? Or is it one of those &quot;you decide lel ;D&quot; that White Wolf sometimes do with the mystery being left up to the Storyteller? Other than this question I feel everything I'm curious about has been answered.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the main thing that I'm sorta blocked on. I'm writing with the implication that Nature is able to feel but attempts to restrain itself. It works for the most part, but every now and then its &quot;emotions&quot; bleed into the world. Kinda like a parent who keeps a facade in public but mumbles their true feelings when the doors are closed. That sort of negative emotion affects the children, who may then actually act on those feelings. That's sort of the logic behind the Furies, animals that have been imbued with Nature's resentment and desire to harm humanity. This includes unnaturally feral animals and &quot;dire&quot; beasts, like giant spiders that prey on humans that wander in the basements of abandoned houses. It's a twist on the idea that the Earth is a living organism. I would say that it is canon that, considering we have a running lineage of sorts with Ceto and Echidna, some Sirens believe Nature to be a being named Gaia who gave birth to Ceto, and by proxy the Sirens themselves and Echidna. This would be a specific sect of Sirens and isn't entirely true; it's just a belief that some hold.<br /> <br /> It would be <i>very</i> interesting to think what a Werewolf would think when they speak to a Siren about their cosmology. It also sounds like a headache that could end in a bloodbath.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812352#post812352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see. Pardon me, I thought you were writing up that they could time travel and I misread it. D:</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I've said before, if there is a point of contention, it probably means that something is unclear and should be pointed out before it makes it into print and confuses everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the multiple Deluges in the past were really extremely large scale floodings? I can get behind that, and hopefully it doesn't interfere with other Splat's cosmology. If it doesn't, then it could mean that Sirens are potentially one of the oldest splats on Earth. Fittingly so, as most life began from the water. </div> </div> </div>Potentially. If Werewolf's story of Father Wolf and Luna is true, then Werewolves would technically be the first to exist and continue their lineage. If Beast's story of the Dark Mother is true, then the Beasts were in the world first while everything else branched out from them. And that's not including the God Machine or Spirits. I believe that Sirens want their story to be true because it gives weight to their struggle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kind of like the Wyrd Transcendance for Changelings or becoming an Empress in PtH? If so, then me gusta.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder. Echidna has been around for a VERY long time given how it seems to be coming up, and the idea I have for her atm is that she's an Ascended Siren at Lucidity 0. I was thinking, perhaps one bonus for an Ascended Siren (no matter what their Morality is at) would be straight up Age Immortality? As in they stop aging altogether? Would seal up the plothole of &quot;How has Echidna lived for 1000+ years and yet Sirens can only live up to be about 300 years old&quot;. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812355#post812355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jellyfishes are biologically immortal; maybe she found a way to draw from that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I threw up the idea that if a Siren fails to stop The Deluge, the essence of her being as sacrificed to the Celestial Ocean, where it will be recycled onto a potential Siren in the next world. I also added that if a Siren refuses to accept their failure, their consciousness becomes trapped in the Celestial Ocean. Essentially, Sirens that deny their failure go into a type of Purgatory and Echidna was the first Siren to ever deny her failure. Considering that idea is new and subject to change, we can totally trash that idea and say that Echidna is an Ascended Siren with Lucidity 0. Or mix it and say that, because Echidna Ascended and failed to stop the Deluge, she is stuck in in the Celestial Ocean. She has been viewing each instance of The Deluge running its course while being unable to do a thing about it. However, her Ascendance granted her enough presence in the world to be able to manipulate things in the world, which is how she discovered that she could make the Vodianoi. <br /> <br /> I would also say that Jellyfish Immortality could be an Alteration that is specific to Echidnal Sirens. It would definitely contrast to the other Sirens.<br /> <br /> As a Side-Note, the more that we mention the Vodianoi, the more I feel incredibly terrible for them. They're kinda like Ghouls that were turned without warning and it makes them kinda tragic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T22:56:01-08:00","id":812399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the main thing that I'm sorta blocked on. I'm writing with the implication that Nature is able to feel but attempts to restrain itself. It works for the most part, but every now and then its &quot;emotions&quot; bleed into the world. Kinda like a parent who keeps a facade in public but mumbles their true feelings when the doors are closed. That sort of negative emotion affects the children, who may then actually act on those feelings. That's sort of the logic behind the Furies, animals that have been imbued with Nature's resentment and desire to harm humanity. This includes unnaturally feral animals and &quot;dire&quot; beasts, like giant spiders that prey on humans that wander in the basements of abandoned houses. It's a twist on the idea that the Earth is a living organism. I would say that it is canon that, considering we have a running lineage of sorts with Ceto and Echidna, some Sirens believe Nature to be a being named Gaia who gave birth to Ceto, and by proxy the Sirens themselves and Echidna. This would be a specific sect of Sirens and isn't entirely true; it's just a belief that some hold.<br /> <br /> It would be <i>very</i> interesting to think what a Werewolf would think when they speak to a Siren about their cosmology. It also sounds like a headache that could end in a bloodbath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm okay with this and feel satisfied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I've said before, if there is a point of contention, it probably means that something is unclear and should be pointed out before it makes it into print and confuses everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concur; we should be able to ask away anything and be sure we're all on the same pages without getting a headache because someone missed a point somewhere. It works better in the long-run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I threw up the idea that if a Siren fails to stop The Deluge, the essence of her being as sacrificed to the Celestial Ocean, where it will be recycled onto a potential Siren in the next world.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit like God-Machine Angels as far as I know? There is a risk that they are to be replaced and are done so via recycling afaik; which is one of the more quoted reasons they turn into Demons. Grain of salt, I haven't read the Descent. I'm on board with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also added that if a Siren refuses to accept their failure, their consciousness becomes trapped in the Celestial Ocean. Essentially, Sirens that deny their failure go into a type of Purgatory and Echidna was the first Siren to ever deny her failure. Considering that idea is new and subject to change, we can totally trash that idea and say that Echidna is an Ascended Siren with Lucidity 0. Or mix it and say that, because Echidna Ascended and failed to stop the Deluge, she is stuck in in the Celestial Ocean. She has been viewing each instance of The Deluge running its course while being unable to do a thing about it. However, her Ascendance granted her enough presence in the world to be able to manipulate things in the world, which is how she discovered that she could make the Vodianoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>This ties in a little with the below quote, but what if the Jellyfish Immortality has a drawback that it also makes Echidna very frail or unable to act much outside of her immediate element or something? I'm no expert on Jellyfish, but as far as I know they are mostly just along for the ride with little input of their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also say that Jellyfish Immortality could be an Alteration that is specific to Echidnal Sirens. It would definitely contrast to the other Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Side-Note, the more that we mention the Vodianoi, the more I feel incredibly terrible for them. They're kinda like Ghouls that were turned without warning and it makes them kinda tragic.</div> </div> </div> </div>As is befitting the World of Darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:59:13-08:00","id":812531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially. If Werewolf's story of Father Wolf and Luna is true, then Werewolves would technically be the first to exist and continue their lineage. If Beast's story of the Dark Mother is true, then the Beasts were in the world first while everything else branched out from them. And that's not including the God Machine or Spirits. I believe that Sirens want their story to be true because it gives weight to their struggle.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's loads of nearly immortal immortals in the WoD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I threw up the idea that if a Siren fails to stop The Deluge, the essence of her being as sacrificed to the Celestial Ocean, where it will be recycled onto a potential Siren in the next world. I also added that if a Siren refuses to accept their failure, their consciousness becomes trapped in the Celestial Ocean. Essentially, Sirens that deny their failure go into a type of Purgatory and Echidna was the first Siren to ever deny her failure. Considering that idea is new and subject to change, we can totally trash that idea and say that Echidna is an Ascended Siren with Lucidity 0. Or mix it and say that, because Echidna Ascended and failed to stop the Deluge, she is stuck in in the Celestial Ocean. She has been viewing each instance of The Deluge running its course while being unable to do a thing about it. However, her Ascendance granted her enough presence in the world to be able to manipulate things in the world, which is how she discovered that she could make the Vodianoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind having a mix of the two. Echidna is definitely someone that can be interacted with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also say that Jellyfish Immortality could be an Alteration that is specific to Echidnal Sirens. It would definitely contrast to the other Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind the thought of it being general, but I digress. I imagine that it would be the most subtle of Echidna's Alterations, if to make up that you can decide whatever age you want to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812388#post812388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Side-Note, the more that we mention the Vodianoi, the more I feel incredibly terrible for them. They're kinda like Ghouls that were turned without warning and it makes them kinda tragic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add in the fact that almost all of the Vodianoi were kidnapped from humanity and are traumatized so harshly that they'd never recover from it and it's almost the same as a True Fae making Changelings. The Vodianoi are just as much tragic as they are monsters and perhaps the only release is death. Or Archmaster level Life and Mind to fix the damages.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:10:48-08:00","id":812657,"title":"","content":"One thing I don't recall being adressed: Vodianoi are humans kidnapped from the present or the corpses from the Deluge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:24:28-08:00","id":812705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812657#post812657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I don't recall being adressed: Vodianoi are humans kidnapped from the present or the corpses from the Deluge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely humans kidnapped from the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:29:22-08:00","id":812896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812399#post812399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit like God-Machine Angels as far as I know? There is a risk that they are to be replaced and are done so via recycling afaik; which is one of the more quoted reasons they turn into Demons. Grain of salt, I haven't read the Descent. I'm on board with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as well-versed in Demon as I would like, but as far as I know, Angels are built to fulfill their mission and then be dismantled when the job is done so that they can be reused for more Angels. I believe that failing would also lead to dismantling but it could also lead to a Fall and turning into a Demon. The main thing that is different is that Angels are given an objective and have no real depth beyond fulfilling the objective. With Sirens, they are all given the objective to stop The Deluge but they are allowed to live out their lives without being reprimanded for not actively doing everything to stop The Deluge. Sure, Echidna might pop in and berate the Sirens for not doing anything <i>(the big reason why Echidnal Sirens would go against Sirens of Lethe, Phlegethon, and Acheron)</i> but Sirens are able to get off fairly fine. The other big difference is that, when Sirens succeed in stopping The Deluge, they are allowed a free life for the rest of their existence. There are still Floodings here and there, but they have successfully pushed The Deluge back and can allow the next generation to prepare for the next coming. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812399#post812399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This ties in a little with the below quote, but what if the Jellyfish Immortality has a drawback that it also makes Echidna very frail or unable to act much outside of her immediate element or something? I'm no expert on Jellyfish, but as far as I know they are mostly just along for the ride with little input of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812531#post812531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the thought of it being general, but I digress. I imagine that it would be the most subtle of Echidna's Alterations, if to make up that you can decide whatever age you want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that Echidna discovered the Jellyfish Immortality Alteration some time after her Ascendance and her failure, taking on the Alteration while she was stuck in the Celestial Ocean. That Alteration is how she is able to remain fully conscious in the Celestial Ocean. Her physical being was purged from the world but her existence was ingrained into the Celestial Ocean, where she hid in Serenia, the sunken library that records all of history. Assuming that the Celestial Ocean is the transitional realm that allows Sirens to see into the other instances of The Deluge, perhaps it's impossible for Sirens to actually spend expended time in the Celestial Ocean. That having been said, the Jellyfish Immortality Alteration could allow Echidnal Sirens access to the Celestial Ocean for an indefinite period, as they dissolve the physical barriers that prevent the Siren from staying in the Celestial Ocean. Echidna could have appointed guardians to patrol and protect Serenia from non-Echidnal Sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812531#post812531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind having a mix of the two. Echidna is definitely someone that can be interacted with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about immediate interaction, but Echidna does whisper to Sirens suffering from Turbulence and she does prevent the Sirens access to Serenia, but she's probably like a Kereboi from Geist. She has a stat block, which means that she can be interacted with and technically killed, but you'd be hard-pressed to actually stop her permanently. Plus, it would kinda break the game. She could possibly be spoken with and &quot;reasoned&quot; with, but it's like speaking with a deity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812531#post812531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add in the fact that almost all of the Vodianoi were kidnapped from humanity and are traumatized so harshly that they'd never recover from it and it's almost the same as a True Fae making Changelings. The Vodianoi are just as much tragic as they are monsters and perhaps the only release is death. Or Archmaster level Life and Mind to fix the damages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see Echidna assigning some of her Sirens to human-retrieval, luring humans into a false sense of security before taking them to be altered. It could even be a specialized Stanza that is sung by the Echidnal Siren as well as Echidna, as some sort of ritual. It would offer more opportunities for Sirens to engage in <i>Concerto Grosso</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:45:57-08:00","id":813050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812896#post812896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be that Echidna discovered the Jellyfish Immortality Alteration some time after her Ascendance and her failure, taking on the Alteration while she was stuck in the Celestial Ocean. That Alteration is how she is able to remain fully conscious in the Celestial Ocean. Her physical being was purged from the world but her existence was ingrained into the Celestial Ocean, where she hid in Serenia, the sunken library that records all of history. Assuming that the Celestial Ocean is the transitional realm that allows Sirens to see into the other instances of The Deluge, perhaps it's impossible for Sirens to actually spend expended time in the Celestial Ocean. That having been said, the Jellyfish Immortality Alteration could allow Echidnal Sirens access to the Celestial Ocean for an indefinite period, as they dissolve the physical barriers that prevent the Siren from staying in the Celestial Ocean. Echidna could have appointed guardians to patrol and protect Serenia from non-Echidnal Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, at least 90% of the sea is unknown given how big it is. There's plenty of potential for Echidna to have loads of Alterations that could be used by non-Echidna Sirens just because the Animal hasn't been discovered yet. :3 <br /> <br /> Hrm, if it's fine, I would like to suggest that there's two versions of the Jellyfish Immortality. One helps them with age and can be accessed by any Siren the other is the Echidnal Alteration you suggested. The General Siren version allows for saaay a Siren to either be able to be unable to age (and choose at what age she appears to be) or extend her life past the usual 300 by about Akashic Record x 10 years. Which would mean that she'd at best get to live an extra 100 years, but nothing more. The reasoning for this is that while the Siren can live a long time, they are still vulnerable to all other versions of death. I believe you've also written up that it's almost uncommon for a Siren to live the full 300 years. :3<br /> <br /> The Echidnal version does as you described it to it, given that it's easier to do it and allows for living in the Celestial Ocean indefinitely. <br /> <br /> I should note that Vodianoi are as much footsoldiers as they are lapdogs, which means they could easily do much of the low work so that the Echidnal Sirens could do much more important work than what the footsoldiers can handle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812896#post812896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about immediate interaction, but Echidna does whisper to Sirens suffering from Turbulence and she does prevent the Sirens access to Serenia, but she's probably like a Kereboi from Geist. She has a stat block, which means that she can be interacted with and technically killed, but you'd be hard-pressed to actually stop her permanently. Plus, it would kinda break the game. She could possibly be spoken with and &quot;reasoned&quot; with, but it's like speaking with a deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the problems that come with &quot;If it has stats then you can kill it&quot;, but I believe it would be fine. If an St wants to base a game on killing Echidna, then it should be fine to do it. Although I must note that Echidna has thousands, if not then millions, of Vodianoi around her capital and hundreds of Sirens being around as well. If she can be taken down, it should take quite awhile preferably to do so. Maybe even the subject of a whole chronicle.<br /> <br /> I have an utterly evil idea. What if Echidna was connected to her Vodianoi and her Sirens (and anyone who takes up Echidnal Alterations) in a way that's like an infection or virus? If Echidna herself dies, she can transfer her consciousness to another body of a Siren or Vodianoi and continue where she left off. This would make her EXTREMELY hard to kill at the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=812896#post812896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Echidna assigning some of her Sirens to human-retrieval, luring humans into a false sense of security before taking them to be altered. It could even be a specialized Stanza that is sung by the Echidnal Siren as well as Echidna, as some sort of ritual. It would offer more opportunities for Sirens to engage in <i>Concerto Grosso</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just imagine some Vodianoi (read: all of them) being susceptible to loving Sirens like Sirens love any human or thing with all the implications of falling to Turbulence. They have this connection to Echidna automatically, but they can form one with Sirens. This can range from the same amount of affection a dog has for it's owner to a level of Stockholm Syndrome where they believe kindness is &quot;they haven't hit me today, they must like me!&quot;<br /> <br /> I imagine an even more tragic aspect being that they at least have one person in their lives that should they run into them again, they regain some flash of their human life or feeling for it. This is actually like how Sirens love humans or things, because it's a truly human emotion. Even though they're basically at animal level of thought, there's that one chain of humanity that reminds them what it was like to be human.<br /> <br /> Augh, now I feel compelled to give Vodianoi one chance at which they can become a completely normal human again, sort of holding a &quot;Love Redeems&quot; theme to it. Just one chain, nothing else. I can also imagine that Echidna makes it a point not to send Vodianoi to where their normal human lives were at, to make it so they never turn back to normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:32:34-08:00","id":813140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=813050#post813050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, at least 90% of the sea is unknown given how big it is. There's plenty of potential for Echidna to have loads of Alterations that could be used by non-Echidna Sirens just because the Animal hasn't been discovered yet. :3<br /> <br /> Hrm, if it's fine, I would like to suggest that there's two versions of the Jellyfish Immortality. One helps them with age and can be accessed by any Siren the other is the Echidnal Alteration you suggested. The General Siren version allows for saaay a Siren to either be able to be unable to age (and choose at what age she appears to be) or extend her life past the usual 300 by about Akashic Record x 10 years. Which would mean that she'd at best get to live an extra 100 years, but nothing more. The reasoning for this is that while the Siren can live a long time, they are still vulnerable to all other versions of death. I believe you've also written up that it's almost uncommon for a Siren to live the full 300 years. :3<br /> <br /> The Echidnal version does as you described it to it, given that it's easier to do it and allows for living in the Celestial Ocean indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the general Siren Alteration could be based on Lobsters, who are theorized to be unable to die of old age but are more-likely to die when they attempt to molt out of their shells the longer they live while the Jellyfish-based Alteration is almost 100% biologically immortal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I should note that Vodianoi are as much footsoldiers as they are lapdogs, which means they could easily do much of the low work so that the Echidnal Sirens could do much more important work than what the footsoldiers can handle. </div> </div> </div>Huh. It would be interesting to see the Vodianoi popping up in the Celestial Ocean. Like, Vodianoi that turned out pretty okay but are essentially mindless, making them unsuited for being the lifeform that lives through The Deluge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know the problems that come with &quot;If it has stats then you can kill it&quot;, but I believe it would be fine. If an St wants to base a game on killing Echidna, then it should be fine to do it. Although I must note that Echidna has thousands, if not then millions, of Vodianoi around her capital and hundreds of Sirens being around as well. If she can be taken down, it should take quite awhile preferably to do so. Maybe even the subject of a whole chronicle.<br /> <br /> I have an utterly evil idea. What if Echidna was connected to her Vodianoi and her Sirens (and anyone who takes up Echidnal Alterations) in a way that's like an infection or virus? If Echidna herself dies, she can transfer her consciousness to another body of a Siren or Vodianoi and continue where she left off. This would make her EXTREMELY hard to kill at the least. </div> </div> </div>I can see that. I would still err on not giving Echidna explicit statistics other than Lucidity 0, Akashic Record 10 <i>(+?)</i>, and a collection of exclusive Alterations. It would be interesting to see how a Chronicle based on defeating Echidna would go.<br /> <br /> Considering that there is a sort of running theme of lineages and survival, I can see Echidna having influenced some of the Ascended Sirens whom she uses as backups in case her current form is dissolved. It would also possibly give her access to the real world, which could be a serious threat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just imagine some Vodianoi (read: all of them) being susceptible to loving Sirens like Sirens love any human or thing with all the implications of falling to Turbulence. They have this connection to Echidna automatically, but they can form one with Sirens. This can range from the same amount of affection a dog has for it's owner to a level of Stockholm Syndrome where they believe kindness is &quot;they haven't hit me today, they must like me!&quot;<br /> <br /> I imagine an even more tragic aspect being that they at least have one person in their lives that should they run into them again, they regain some flash of their human life or feeling for it. This is actually like how Sirens love humans or things, because it's a truly human emotion. Even though they're basically at animal level of thought, there's that one chain of humanity that reminds them what it was like to be human.<br /> <br /> Augh, now I feel compelled to give Vodianoi one chance at which they can become a completely normal human again, sort of holding a &quot;Love Redeems&quot; theme to it. Just one chain, nothing else. I can also imagine that Echidna makes it a point not to send Vodianoi to where their normal human lives were at, to make it so they never turn back to normal. </div> </div> </div>That would be an interesting parallel, as we have the Banshees who embody a raw Opus and are driven mad by their unstoppable visions, the Breathless who are devoid of the Breath of Life but are surrounded by Unconditional Love, and the Vodianoi who hunger for love and are formed by twisted Malformations, dark mirrors to the Siren's ability to for Verses, partake in Pneuma, and transform through Alterations.<br /> <br /> The Vodianoi, given the desire to find love, seem like the &quot;Creature from the Black Lagoon&quot; searching for a mate, something that mirrors the Siren's &quot;mermaid&quot; image. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T10:19:27-08:00","id":813467,"title":"","content":"I like the way the Vodianoi are turning out; I look forward to seeing them in play at this rate.<br /> One thing I don't like is the automatic &quot;virus&quot; thingy Echidna is suggested to have. It reminds me too much of the bullshit Gehenna scenario where [Tzimisce] became connected to every single human on the planet and if I recall might as well have become them. I would suggest that while we could maintain the aspect and possibility that such a thing as making &quot;back-ups&quot; of yourself does exist, it requires at the very least effort to create that either takes consent or going through heavy resistance even for a being such as Echidna. Opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:06:36-08:00","id":813822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=813467#post813467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the way the Vodianoi are turning out; I look forward to seeing them in play at this rate.<br /> One thing I don't like is the automatic &quot;virus&quot; thingy Echidna is suggested to have. It reminds me too much of the bullshit Gehenna scenario where [Tzimisce] became connected to every single human on the planet and if I recall might as well have become them. I would suggest that while we could maintain the aspect and possibility that such a thing as making &quot;back-ups&quot; of yourself does exist, it requires at the very least effort to create that either takes consent or going through heavy resistance even for a being such as Echidna. Opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Echidna could be grooming a selection of Sirens who are meant to Ascend and then sacrifice their lives to become Echidna's new vessel. Either that or Echidna is attempting to create a brood to continue her legacy. One of the most-prominent names could be Scylla, a sea monster who is actually one of the mythological Echidna's children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T04:41:27-08:00","id":815358,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T07:02:34-08:00","id":815422,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna run this thought by people and see what they think. What if unlike normal Alterations, Echidnal Alterations/Malformations (The first name I used to describe Echidnal Alterations was &quot;Malformations&quot;) can be bought without any limit that the Siren's Akashic Record imposes? The costs for this is that obviously unlike the normal alterations, Malformations are present on both Aquatic and Human forms (this is explained as Echidna being a blender of Human and Fish DNA, since there will always be both in her Malformations, they appear in both forms because they attach to both) and for each Malformation you have above your Akashic Record, the more in thrall to Echidna you become? This would be shown as anything that would help Echidna's cause (which can even include helping out the normal Currents because they're helping Echidna by giving her more time) getting a mechanical bonus (equal to Number of Malformations - Akashic Record) to those actions but trying to do anything but those actions would recieve an equal penalty? What do people think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:40:59-08:00","id":816947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=815422#post815422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna run this thought by people and see what they think. What if unlike normal Alterations, Echidnal Alterations/Malformations (The first name I used to describe Echidnal Alterations was &quot;Malformations&quot;) can be bought without any limit that the Siren's Akashic Record imposes? The costs for this is that obviously unlike the normal alterations, Malformations are present on both Aquatic and Human forms (this is explained as Echidna being a blender of Human and Fish DNA, since there will always be both in her Malformations, they appear in both forms because they attach to both) and for each Malformation you have above your Akashic Record, the more in thrall to Echidna you become? This would be shown as anything that would help Echidna's cause (which can even include helping out the normal Currents because they're helping Echidna by giving her more time) getting a mechanical bonus (equal to Number of Malformations - Akashic Record) to those actions but trying to do anything but those actions would recieve an equal penalty? What do people think?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds interesting. So both Echidnal Sirens and Vodianoi have access to Malformations and are drawn to performing acts that would benefit Echidna? I know that I mentioned somewhere that Echidnal Sirens could be theorized to be locked into a special form of Turbulence that influences them to commit dangerous acts against humanity. It could be that Echidnal Sirens are driven by their Turbulence to abduct humans as specimens for Echidna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:22:18-08:00","id":818080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=816947#post816947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds interesting. So both Echidnal Sirens and Vodianoi have access to Malformations and are drawn to performing acts that would benefit Echidna? I know that I mentioned somewhere that Echidnal Sirens could be theorized to be locked into a special form of Turbulence that influences them to commit dangerous acts against humanity. It could be that Echidnal Sirens are driven by their Turbulence to abduct humans as specimens for Echidna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps this bonus is that idea put into form? What do you think? :3 And the Vodianoi are especially screwed, since they're basically stuck at Akashic Record 0. Hence any Malformation they get guarantees they become influenced by Echidna and they can't escape it by raising their Akashic Record because they're not Sirens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:46:51-08:00","id":818124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=818080#post818080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps this bonus is that idea put into form? What do you think? :3 And the Vodianoi are especially screwed, since they're basically stuck at Akashic Record 0. Hence any Malformation they get guarantees they become influenced by Echidna and they can't escape it by raising their Akashic Record because they're not Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost feel as if the Vodianoi are significantly sympathetic, but at least the Sirens won't be seen as unsympathetic considering that the Sirens' fight is more towards The Deluge and Echidna. It's also interesting to note that the Vodianoi are effectively reduced to a chance die to resist Echidna, meaning that there is an actual mechanic that describes the struggle that the Vodianoi have to retain their mental faculties.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:23:59-08:00","id":818634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=818124#post818124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I almost feel as if the Vodianoi are significantly sympathetic, but at least the Sirens won't be seen as unsympathetic considering that the Sirens' fight is more towards The Deluge and Echidna. It's also interesting to note that the Vodianoi are effectively reduced to a chance die to resist Echidna, meaning that there is an actual mechanic that describes the struggle that the Vodianoi have to retain their mental faculties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If nothing else, I sense that it will make Sirens who take up Echidnal Alterations as more destestable. Sirens can safely take up to their Akashic Record in Malformations and in a way that bypass normal Alteration rules, and even so, there's still the factor that they become influenced by Echidna if they take over their Akashic Record. This fits into the type of Sirens who'd serve Echidna to plunder her mutagenic powers (those who take up to their Akashic Record in Malformations) and the Sirens who might genuinely believe in her cause because they'd serve Echidna either way (those who take up to and over their Akashic Record in Malformations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:55:15-08:00","id":818915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=818634#post818634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. If nothing else, I sense that it will make Sirens who take up Echidnal Alterations as more destestable. Sirens can safely take up to their Akashic Record in Malformations and in a way that bypass normal Alteration rules, and even so, there's still the factor that they become influenced by Echidna if they take over their Akashic Record. This fits into the type of Sirens who'd serve Echidna to plunder her mutagenic powers (those who take up to their Akashic Record in Malformations) and the Sirens who might genuinely believe in her cause because they'd serve Echidna either way (those who take up to and over their Akashic Record in Malformations).</div> </div> </div> </div>So Malformations are open to all Sirens, like the Centimani Path for Prometheans. For Sirens unaligned with Echidna, perhaps each Malformation reduces her dice pool to resist Maelstrom. Also, I just realized that I referred to the Frenzy-State as Turbulence instead of Maelstrom in my earlier posts. Whoops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T19:50:05-08:00","id":818942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=818915#post818915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Malformations are open to all Sirens, like the Centimani Path for Prometheans. For Sirens unaligned with Echidna, perhaps each Malformation reduces her dice pool to resist Maelstrom. Also, I just realized that I referred to the Frenzy-State as Turbulence instead of Maelstrom in my earlier posts. Whoops.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not very well read on the Centimani Path, so anything similar to them are unintentional. I would say that that would perhaps be a fine idea for Sirens. How about we list it like this?<br /> <br /> <b>Echidnal Echoes Condition (Persistent)</b><br /> Malformations have three DNA inside of them. Human, Fish, and Echidna. When the Siren takes a number of Malformations greater than her Akashic Record, the part that is Echidna begins to infect her like a virus, making her begin to sympathize with Echidna's goals, and find it harder to ignore them. Take the Siren's Malformations - Akashic Record if the number of Malformations she owns is greater than her Akashic Record. This is a bonus to all rolls that aid Echidna's plots...and a penalty to things which would go against them or herself.<br /> <b>Bonus/Penalty: ______</b><br /> <b>Beat: </b>When the Siren follows through with Echidna's plans. It must be enough to activate the bonus.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>The Siren has more Malformations than her Akashic Record.<br /> <b>Resolving the Condition: </b>The Siren's Akashic Record grows to be higher than the number of Malformations she owns.<br /> <b>Resolving the Condition: </b>The Siren removes her Malformations entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Scylla's Condition (Persistent)</b><br /> Despite the loyalty that Echidna's Sirens show to her, there are many who take her Malformations without her knowledge or consent. With this, she cursed her illegal cells, for those who do not align with her must find to do so...or find that they shall fall to their nastier side.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a beat everytime the Siren falls to Maelstrom with this Condition.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>If the Siren owns Malformations but isn't aligned with Echidna (I.E. Is in a Current without true loyalty to Echidna).<br /> <b>Resolving the Condition: </b>The Siren removes her Malformations entirely.<br /> <br /> The reason I call the latter &quot;Scylla's Condition&quot; is because the monster was a nymph Hera was jealous of, and thus she cursed her to become a monster. As well, I also imagine a way to remove Malformations (on Sirens at least). Simply put, Echidna's Malformations become a part of your DNA when she puts them in, and to take them out would be like ripping out a part of your genetic code to reassert itself. I think that taking off a Malformation would be an extended roll, the Threshold being the total number of Malformations you have and the dicepool is Akashic Record + Lucidity. You can choose any number of Malformations you have, even all of them if you wish. The reason the Threshold is all of the malformations is because its Echidna's DNA resisting being pulled out. When you reach up to the number of successes required, the Siren is able to take off the Malformation....however, she then automatically takes Resistant Aggravated damage equal to the number of Malformations she had taken off. <br /> <br /> Just in case if it's not known, Resistant Damage cannot be healed magically (not even mages can do it) and it must be allowed to heal at a natural rate. And yes, it's possible for a Siren to kill herself by getting off too many Malformations at once. I would also like to note that taking off Malformations off of a Vodianoi are impossible save for turning them completely back to normal. I would like to think that how Echidna gives Malformations to her Sirens and her Vodianoi are separate ways. With the Sirens, she does it like plastic surgery with the finest of tools. With Vodianoi, she's like a back alley surgeon whose only implement is a rusty chainsaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T19:32:04-08:00","id":819640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=818942#post818942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not very well read on the Centimani Path, so anything similar to them are unintentional. I would say that that would perhaps be a fine idea for Sirens. How about we list it like this?<br /> <br /> <b>Echidnal Echoes Condition (Persistent)</b><br /> Malformations have three DNA inside of them. Human, Fish, and Echidna. When the Siren takes a number of Malformations greater than her Akashic Record, the part that is Echidna begins to infect her like a virus, making her begin to sympathize with Echidna's goals, and find it harder to ignore them. Take the Siren's Malformations - Akashic Record if the number of Malformations she owns is greater than her Akashic Record. This is a bonus to all rolls that aid Echidna's plots...and a penalty to things which would go against them or herself.<br /> <b>Bonus/Penalty: ______</b><br /> <b>Beat: </b>When the Siren follows through with Echidna's plans. It must be enough to activate the bonus.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>The Siren has more Malformations than her Akashic Record.<br /> <b>Resolving the Condition: </b>The Siren's Akashic Record grows to be higher than the number of Malformations she owns.<br /> <b>Resolving the Condition: </b>The Siren removes her Malformations entirely.<br /> <br /> <b>Scylla's Condition (Persistent)</b><br /> Despite the loyalty that Echidna's Sirens show to her, there are many who take her Malformations without her knowledge or consent. With this, she cursed her illegal cells, for those who do not align with her must find to do so...or find that they shall fall to their nastier side.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a beat everytime the Siren falls to Maelstrom with this Condition.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>If the Siren owns Malformations but isn't aligned with Echidna (I.E. Is in a Current without true loyalty to Echidna).<br /> <b>Resolving the Condition: </b>The Siren removes her Malformations entirely.<br /> <br /> The reason I call the latter &quot;Scylla's Condition&quot; is because the monster was a nymph Hera was jealous of, and thus she cursed her to become a monster. As well, I also imagine a way to remove Malformations (on Sirens at least). Simply put, Echidna's Malformations become a part of your DNA when she puts them in, and to take them out would be like ripping out a part of your genetic code to reassert itself. I think that taking off a Malformation would be an extended roll, the Threshold being the total number of Malformations you have and the dicepool is Akashic Record + Lucidity. You can choose any number of Malformations you have, even all of them if you wish. The reason the Threshold is all of the malformations is because its Echidna's DNA resisting being pulled out. When you reach up to the number of successes required, the Siren is able to take off the Malformation....however, she then automatically takes Resistant Aggravated damage equal to the number of Malformations she had taken off.<br /> <br /> Just in case if it's not known, Resistant Damage cannot be healed magically (not even mages can do it) and it must be allowed to heal at a natural rate. And yes, it's possible for a Siren to kill herself by getting off too many Malformations at once. I would also like to note that taking off Malformations off of a Vodianoi are impossible save for turning them completely back to normal. I would like to think that how Echidna gives Malformations to her Sirens and her Vodianoi are separate ways. With the Sirens, she does it like plastic surgery with the finest of tools. With Vodianoi, she's like a back alley surgeon whose only implement is a rusty chainsaw.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is there a book that describes Resistant Damage? Other than that, these sound pretty interesting as Conditions. As for the Vodianoi, it might be best to leave the idea of reforming the Vodianoi as a Story Hook and not explicitly state whether or not there is a way for the Vodianoi to return to being human. Maybe they could be reformed to thinking as a human, but that should be the extent of explicit information about the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T08:30:54-08:00","id":819809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=819640#post819640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a book that describes Resistant Damage? Other than that, these sound pretty interesting as Conditions. As for the Vodianoi, it might be best to leave the idea of reforming the Vodianoi as a Story Hook and not explicitly state whether or not there is a way for the Vodianoi to return to being human. Maybe they could be reformed to thinking as a human, but that should be the extent of explicit information about the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage uses Resistant Damage in that Pattern Scouring (ripping mana from your body, damaging yourself in the process) and taking Paradox (when you don't want it to have a random effect, the Mage can take the Paradox onto himself and suffer his suxx in Resistant Damage). Princess also uses Resistant Damage as part of the cost and drawback of Tempesta Charms. <br /> <br /> I think that at the very least, Vodianoi should have one explained mechanical way to make a Vodianoi back to human. The ST is free to devise other ways, but if nothing comes up or the ST doesn't want to make one, then there's at least one way to do it. :3 Now I wonder, should Breathless and Banshees also have ways of going back to normal? I don't think Banshees should recieve a way (I'm still abit in favor of them being the Siren subsplat, their madness being more containable with a Siren's help), but the Breathless I think should have one. Simply put, Sirens become Sirens by surviving some despair in their life and listening to something that urges them to continue on. Breathless only have the surviving part, but still hurt by the experience. I feel like they should be able to return back to normal if they manage to fix whatever made them into a Breathless. I think this is fine, because Breathless are both like a nearly drowned person washed ashore and like a scab over a healed wound that people only want to pick at. They can get better eventually, but if they're continually being picked at, then they won't heal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T11:37:41-08:00","id":819899,"title":"","content":"In my opinion I don't think they should simply rid the splat like that. That said, I'm somewhat open to the notion if it has a good explanation behind how it's done which so far I think it lacks, from what I see the option is mostly there cuz Saulot feels a need to have a happy ending at all times if plausible (coming from someone who knows him well). Sirens seem to have something of an evolutionary spin on them; do you de-evolve the Voidanoi? Is there some magic ritual available to reverse their changes (and minds)? Time magic? SCIENCE?! Ahem. How is it done in your minds exactly? C:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T17:11:58-08:00","id":820042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=819899#post819899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion I don't think they should simply rid the splat like that. That said, I'm somewhat open to the notion if it has a good explanation behind how it's done which so far I think it lacks, from what I see the option is mostly there cuz Saulot feels a need to have a happy ending at all times if plausible (coming from someone who knows him well). Sirens seem to have something of an evolutionary spin on them; do you de-evolve the Voidanoi? Is there some magic ritual available to reverse their changes (and minds)? Time magic? SCIENCE?! Ahem. How is it done in your minds exactly? C:</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I feel that returning a Vodianoi or Breathless to human would not be such a simple task. Echidna and her Sirens make it a point to not let them return where they were taken from (although slip ups are entirely plausible to happen), and even if they enter the Deluge to search for the Vodianoi of the person kidnapped, it wouldn't be easy because the person IS going to be deformed from what they originally looked like, and two, you still need to dig through their lizard brain and more animalisitc behavior (and Echidna's influence) to find the human underneath.<br /> <br /> As for Breathless and Sirens first time entering the Deluge is basically the same, meaning that a Breathless beginning to drown must be significant enough for what would cause a Siren to drown. Perhaps a person Drowns because they missed some bill payment for the fifth time and their house is gonna get taken away. A Siren surfaces by figuring out or clinging onto the hope of resolving it (plausible with Verses). The Breathless will claw their way to survive it no matter the cost to themselves, (their aura of making people like them may let them off the hook for now, but they're still in danger of losing their house if they don't meet it the next time). The Breathless could be relieved of his status if he managed to fulfill the thing that caused him to drown, which in this case would be being able to pay off his mortgage and truly own his house. He would remain Breathless even if he lost his house, because he hadn't fulfilled the reason of &quot;keeping it&quot;. I imagine now that moral sirens would seek to make Breathless back to normal humans, and less moral ones keep them as they are to feed off of Pneuma.<br /> <br /> In my mind, Vodianoi are actually de-evolved humans. They're pretty much wracked with trauma that Echidna causes in making them what they are and it's so bad that they've lost their sapience. It doesn't help that part of their DNA is now fish/marine animal and as such they gain the same responses of an animal. I feel that, like in the story of the Little Mermaid, the way a Vodianoi can be redeemed is through the love of a human they knew in their old life. They need to have it hung in their face like a hook with a wriggling worm, and like a fish they need to be enticed to follow it before they latch onto the hook.<br /> <br /> Think of it like this, Vodianoi cannot interact with humans in a normal way since they're at the same level as animals. Even though they've lost their sapience, they still do carry their sentience and thus can recognize people they've seen or known before and have feelings such as love. As such, redeeming a Vodianoi I imagine would be almost akin to stalking them (preferably from the Deluge and using powers to let the Vodianoi (and the Siren redeeming him/her) see from the deluge and into reality. Which in turn brings back the vodianoi's human feelings. The feelings the Vodianoi must feel are not the syringe injected drug like false feelings that Echidna gives to them for herself, they must be true feelings of love. Any kind of love will do, but it must be specified, directed and judged. It must be the kind of love that can touch the soul of someone. The process is basically like re-emphasizing the human genes, the higher thought that came upon the lizard brain which made humans more than just instinctual animals, with their humanity (even if it's twisted if they're not the best of people before becoming Vodianoi) coming back out. If their humanity manages to overcome the fish features, all of their Malformations will rip off as their DNA rejects the animal like parts and their sapience returns. If they're in the Deluge, they're thrown up back into reality. Wet, maybe abit cold, but undoubtedly alive. And I believe that they'd also flatly forget their time as a Vodianoi, as the animal thought and fish are pushed out in favor of human thought. <br /> <br /> For example, a Vodianoi going along the drowned city of Chicago sees a lady through the veil of the Deluge. He doesn't know why, but he remembers feelings of warmth from her touch, the same feelings he gets when he sees the shiny band stuck on his webbed hand....and can't help but feel a twinge of rage as he sees another man talking to her and taking her into an alley against her will. He might pop out of the Deluge and brutally slaughter the man, only to run away like a scared animal when the woman screams. But he'll keep watching her, feeling his once doused emotions come back lighting like Saint Elmo's Fire....and Echidna's cells will try to reject by drowning the fire underneath orders to further her plots. If the fire is great enough, he may even look on his hand and see that it's not just anything. It's his wedding ring, the same she has on. The next thing he remembers is the feeling of ripping. Fish parts ripping away from his body. Fish memories ripping away from his brain. Himself ripping out of the deluge. The woman wakes up, hearing the sound of a thud and seeing her unconscious husband on the bedroom floor. Cold, unconscious, sopping wet and been gone for months....but breathing, alive, and back.<br /> <br /> Of course, the above story is only possible because the Vodianoi wasn't being watched. In almost all cases, Vodianoi will have leashes around them. However, it's possible to change the leash to your hands and teach him things he once knew if you try hard enough. Mechanic wise? It would be an extended roll with one roll per session and if you make it at the end, you're back to normal. Story wise? There's gonna be alot of sessions where you must play out and actively help the beast return to human and not scare the one of their affections away (it would discourage them to continue connecting afterall). This is how I imagine Vodianoi redemption to be like.<br /> <br /> And as for the Happy Ending bit, that is something I like, but I keep it only for when I serve as a Storyteller. When I'm working on a game, I try to remain professional and suggest only what feels as fitting. I mostly just suggested the &quot;get out of splat&quot; methods since most Subsplats do have ways to return back to normal humans. That and that love is a part of the game, so I felt it would be fitting for the Vodianoi and the stories of how love can redeem a demon back to being a human.<br /> <br /> On another note, beginning on Tropicana. Hopefully I'll get it done tomorrow or next Thursday. Depends on how high my inspirations is at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T13:28:22-08:00","id":821169,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post, I've gotten done with Tropicana. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:19:17-08:00","id":821239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=821169#post821169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the double post, I've gotten done with Tropicana. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that once we start playtesting, I would go for a Tropican Siren first. They hit that sweet spot between &quot;incredibly fun&quot; and &quot;incredibly dangerous&quot;. <br /> <br /> ...as I was typing, I just realized that the Tropicans are basically Undyne. I'm slow to the punchline.<br /> <br /> As for the Vodianoi, I like how they kinda feel like a reference to &quot;The Fly&quot;. I also feel that a Vodianoi's redemption is like a Siren's Ascendance with a slight mix of ghosts and allowing a ghost to pass on peacefully. I can see a story hook where a Shoal of Sirens is keeping an eye on multiple Vodianoi, attempting to help them be redeemed, which is causing trouble with another Shoal who believe the increased presence of the Vodianoi means that there are Echidnal Sirens in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:31:48-08:00","id":821250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=821239#post821239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that once we start playtesting, I would go for a Tropican Siren first. They hit that sweet spot between &quot;incredibly fun&quot; and &quot;incredibly dangerous&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...as I was typing, I just realized that the Tropicans are basically Undyne. I'm slow to the punchline.<br /> <br /> As for the Vodianoi, I like how they kinda feel like a reference to &quot;The Fly&quot;. I also feel that a Vodianoi's redemption is like a Siren's Ascendance with a slight mix of ghosts and allowing a ghost to pass on peacefully. I can see a story hook where a Shoal of Sirens is keeping an eye on multiple Vodianoi, attempting to help them be redeemed, which is causing trouble with another Shoal who believe the increased presence of the Vodianoi means that there are Echidnal Sirens in the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, I'm happy they're liked. ^w^ As for being like Undyne, I admit that was unintentional at first. For one, I didn't exactly have her in mind when typing (I was thinking more &quot;the Thrashing Dragons&quot; from Kindred of the East, but Undyne is indeed fitting for this Water~) and for the other I was thinking of her when it came to the Current of Conflict or how they did things. Perhaps Undyne is a Tropicana of Conflict? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:27:10-08:00","id":821321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=821250#post821250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice, I'm happy they're liked. ^w^ As for being like Undyne, I admit that was unintentional at first. For one, I didn't exactly have her in mind when typing (I was thinking more &quot;the Thrashing Dragons&quot; from Kindred of the East, but Undyne is indeed fitting for this Water~) and for the other I was thinking of her when it came to the Current of Conflict or how they did things. Perhaps Undyne is a Tropicana of Conflict? :3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Definitely. She cares about putting her 100% into things and she's willing to take a stand if she needs to. Of course, Tropicana's general mindset is a bit more &quot;cheerful&quot; thank Undyne's general mindset, but there is that overlap in there. <br /> <br /> It definitely would be good to categorize some of the more iconic/popular depictions of mermaids/sirens/fish people so that we have some general understanding of the Waters and Currents. Like, Ariel in the Disney version of <i>The Little Mermaid</i> is entirely a Freshwater of Harmony considering that her defining trait is her curiosity of humanity. Princess Ruto from <i>Ocarina of Time</i> may be a Gardenian Castaway, considering that she's the Sage of Water, attends to Lord Jabu Jabu, and starts her personal development when she meets Link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T19:17:09-08:00","id":821369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=821321#post821321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely. She cares about putting her 100% into things and she's willing to take a stand if she needs to. Of course, Tropicana's general mindset is a bit more &quot;cheerful&quot; thank Undyne's general mindset, but there is that overlap in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I feel I might be putting the Waters down as abit too kind. I mean, being an evil person is a possibility too. It's also kind of why I put down how Tropicanians are basically passionate. They can love whatever they want....and they can also hate whatever they want too. So long as it's in a grip of a burning passion, it's good enough for a Tropican Siren.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=821321#post821321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It definitely would be good to categorize some of the more iconic/popular depictions of mermaids/sirens/fish people so that we have some general understanding of the Waters and Currents. Like, Ariel in the Disney version of <i>The Little Mermaid</i> is entirely a Freshwater of Harmony considering that her defining trait is her curiosity of humanity. Princess Ruto from <i>Ocarina of Time</i> may be a Gardenian Castaway, considering that she's the Sage of Water, attends to Lord Jabu Jabu, and starts her personal development when she meets Link.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuppers, should do. I imagine that Undyne would fit underneath Tropicana or Current of Conflict? Which one should we use her for? If anyone can come up with good examples of what would be good for Water Inspirations or Current Inspirations, please feel free to speak up. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:10:39-08:00","id":822737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=821369#post821369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I feel I might be putting the Waters down as abit too kind. I mean, being an evil person is a possibility too. It's also kind of why I put down how Tropicanians are basically passionate. They can love whatever they want....and they can also hate whatever they want too. So long as it's in a grip of a burning passion, it's good enough for a Tropican Siren.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like it. It definitely carves out a niche for the Tropicans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yuppers, should do. I imagine that Undyne would fit underneath Tropicana or Current of Conflict? Which one should we use her for? If anyone can come up with good examples of what would be good for Water Inspirations or Current Inspirations, please feel free to speak up. :3 </div> </div> </div>I think Undyne is pretty solidly a Tropican of Conflict. As for the two Waters that don't have a write-up, I can't really think of examples that are distinctly mermaids or at least fish-based. The Vaporians would be pretty similar to Cole from <i>Dragon Age: Inquisition</i>, popping in and out of existence whenever they are needed. Someone who would be tangentially related would be Lapiz Lazuli from <i>Stephen Universe. </i>As for a mythological example, the Tuatha De Danann of Irish mythology covered themselves in a mist in order to move around undetected. The Discordians, being wildcards with a strange way of thinking, could be anything. They'd be Jinx from <i>League of Legends</i>, wanting to do something that disturbs the still waters and calls forth action. I can't really think of a stand-out trickster character who is also a mermaid-type creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T14:44:01-08:00","id":823742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=822737#post822737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Undyne is pretty solidly a Tropican of Conflict. As for the two Waters that don't have a write-up, I can't really think of examples that are distinctly mermaids or at least fish-based. The Vaporians would be pretty similar to Cole from <i>Dragon Age: Inquisition</i>, popping in and out of existence whenever they are needed. Someone who would be tangentially related would be Lapiz Lazuli from <i>Stephen Universe. </i>As for a mythological example, the Tuatha De Danann of Irish mythology covered themselves in a mist in order to move around undetected. The Discordians, being wildcards with a strange way of thinking, could be anything. They'd be Jinx from <i>League of Legends</i>, wanting to do something that disturbs the still waters and calls forth action. I can't really think of a stand-out trickster character who is also a mermaid-type creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. On that note, I added inspirations after the specific waters of which you've pointed out. Also, it's not much of an update but I've started to edit the Vodianoi Google Docs and I even added a few Malformations. Enjoy. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:13:35-08:00","id":827083,"title":"","content":"Just passing by to keep the thread alive and running, since i'm unable to stop more than a few minutes in front of the PC. Loving everything, and saving every GDocs link!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:28:43-08:00","id":827435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=827083#post827083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just passing by to keep the thread alive and running, since i'm unable to stop more than a few minutes in front of the PC. Loving everything, and saving every GDocs link!</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to see you still like it. I'm beginning work on Vaporia. To note, you don't need to resave the Waters Google Doc multiple times, as those get updated the more I change it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T09:27:48-08:00","id":828826,"title":"","content":"I'm writing up Vaporia at the moment. Reaper, if I may ask, how exactly would Vaporia be done? At least appearance and philosophy wise? I can't help but feel like I'd get more than a few things wrong.<br /> <br /> Also, I've read up a little on other splats and I have an idea for one way Pneuma can be used. Vampires can spend Vitae to bring up their Physical Attributes. Geniuses can use Mania to raise their Mental Attributes. For Sirens, I was thinking we that Sirens could use Pneuma to raise their Social Attributes. It's certainly fitting for them in my eyes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:11:02-08:00","id":828972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Pardon the triple posting. I finished up Vaporia. If it looks like it's halfheartedly done and the person writing was borked, I can confirm I was borked and I will go over it when I'm less borked. But for now, Vaporia is finished. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T17:07:03-08:00","id":829027,"title":"","content":"Eugh. Sorry for not being up to date on the thread. School. And also I came down with a weird cold <i>(I don't usually get sick, but when I do, it's AWFUL).</i><br /> <br /> It makes sense that Sirens would be able to spend Pneuma to raise their Social Attributes considering that Sirens are, in and off themselves, a very social Splat. <br /> <br /> As for the Vaporians, I feel that the write-up is fairly poignant to what I intended Vaporians to be but the story characterizes them more towards the Discordians. The Vaporians are long-time thinkers, playing key parts in a story before disappearing to contemplate. They are the Lady of the Lake offering the sword to Arthur. What they do is calculated, always built from the bottom up but often strange and arbitrary. Why does the man throw out food into the water every Sunday morning? People may try to understand, but only he knows the reason why. He needs to train the fish to come up to the water every Sunday morning so that a fisherman may land the perfect catch in the upcoming week. That fisherman plays an important part in the overall story. Vaporians make contact in secrecy, allowing others to think that what happens is just luck and fate.<br /> <br /> I think Vaporians would be the &quot;Thieves&quot; of the Sirens, disappearing for extended times to accomplish what they need to do in secrecy. No words, no questions. They stand apart from the Tropicans who want to take the limelight and the Freshwater who want to enjoy life. The Vaporians are kinda a foil to the Gardenians; both have a &quot;job&quot; that they need to do but they go about their &quot;jobs&quot; differently, Gardenians need to stay in one place to maintain things while Vaporians move around to make sure that things get started.<br /> <br /> I feel that Vaporians would also look the most drab out of all the Sirens. Polarians are dark and morose, Freshwaters are bubbly and full of life, Gardenians are strong and solid, Tropicans are bright and vibrant, and Discordians are entirely kooky and clashy. The Vaporians would be drowned out and muted, grey and pastels that have gone through the wash one too many times. Something that won't really catch your eye unless you are looking right at it. <br /> <br /> A possible source of inspiration may be Marie from Persona 4 Golden. She's kinda super spoilery, but the main thing is that she has amnesia and feels that she should search for her past. She's cold and antisocial but has moments of profound introversion and plays a very important part in the plot. She also advises the protagonist to forget about looking for the truth and stop meddling in her affairs. For spoilers, see below.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The main reason why I feel that she fits the Vaporians is because she is actually an avatar of Kusumi-no-Okami, a spy who watches the real world and is meant to absorb the fog if Ameno-Sagiri, a being who wants to give into humanity's desires to end their suffering and turn them into Shadows, is defeated. Once she realizes who she really is, she attempts to die by herself in order to protect humanity. She is also able to manipulate the weather. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T11:27:04-08:00","id":829335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829027#post829027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eugh. Sorry for not being up to date on the thread. School. And also I came down with a weird cold <i>(I don't usually get sick, but when I do, it's AWFUL).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Is fine. Don't worry. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829027#post829027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Vaporians, I feel that the write-up is fairly poignant to what I intended Vaporians to be but the story characterizes them more towards the Discordians. The Vaporians are long-time thinkers, playing key parts in a story before disappearing to contemplate. They are the Lady of the Lake offering the sword to Arthur. What they do is calculated, always built from the bottom up but often strange and arbitrary. Why does the man throw out food into the water every Sunday morning? People may try to understand, but only he knows the reason why. He needs to train the fish to come up to the water every Sunday morning so that a fisherman may land the perfect catch in the upcoming week. That fisherman plays an important part in the overall story. Vaporians make contact in secrecy, allowing others to think that what happens is just luck and fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon that, will use that as inspiration or as the new story. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829027#post829027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Vaporians would be the &quot;Thieves&quot; of the Sirens, disappearing for extended times to accomplish what they need to do in secrecy. No words, no questions. They stand apart from the Tropicans who want to take the limelight and the Freshwater who want to enjoy life. The Vaporians are kinda a foil to the Gardenians; both have a &quot;job&quot; that they need to do but they go about their &quot;jobs&quot; differently, Gardenians need to stay in one place to maintain things while Vaporians move around to make sure that things get started.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, I can see that working. Thanks for making the distinction between Vaporians and Freshwater Sirens, I didn't get that in my head until now and part of why I was borked in writing them. That and that I didn't have much other in mind save &quot;Manic Pixie Dream Girl&quot;. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829027#post829027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that Vaporians would also look the most drab out of all the Sirens. Polarians are dark and morose, Freshwaters are bubbly and full of life, Gardenians are strong and solid, Tropicans are bright and vibrant, and Discordians are entirely kooky and clashy. The Vaporians would be drowned out and muted, grey and pastels that have gone through the wash one too many times. Something that won't really catch your eye unless you are looking right at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will apply the changes. I can't help but get the idea that Vaporians are a mix of Guardians of the Veil, Autumn Court and Court of Spades. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829027#post829027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A possible source of inspiration may be Marie from Persona 4 Golden. She's kinda super spoilery, but the main thing is that she has amnesia and feels that she should search for her past. She's cold and antisocial but has moments of profound introversion and plays a very important part in the plot. She also advises the protagonist to forget about looking for the truth and stop meddling in her affairs. For spoilers, see below.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Will list her under Inspirations. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T14:48:54-08:00","id":829421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829335#post829335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, I can see that working. Thanks for making the distinction between Vaporians and Freshwater Sirens, I didn't get that in my head until now and part of why I was borked in writing them. That and that I didn't have much other in mind save &quot;Manic Pixie Dream Girl&quot;. &gt;&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's probably because somewhere down the line the wires got crossed. I could've swore that &quot;Manic Pixie Dream Girl&quot; was more for the Discordians than the Vaporians.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will apply the changes. I can't help but get the idea that Vaporians are a mix of Guardians of the Veil, Autumn Court and Court of Spades. :3 </div> </div> </div>I kinda see the Waters as representing some sort of role within a theatre production. The Polarians are the playwrights who construct a tragedy for the audience to know. The Tropicans are the lead, being the face of the play and the one in the spotlight. The Freshwaters are the supporting cast who build the narrative and give a sense of reality into the play. The Vaporians are callboys and callgirls running to make sure everything is in place without being seen by the audience. The Gardenians are the technicians that make sure that the lights are functioning, the microphones are on, and such. Finally, the Discordians are the needed comedy relief who come in to give the audience a breather before the play continues.<br /> <br /> Vast simplification, but this is kinda the way they play out. Tropicans, Freshwaters, and Discordians are the Waters that are most-likely going to go out of their way to meet with humanity while the Polarians, Vaporians, and Gardenians are the ones who are fine with being in the dark.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T17:00:32-08:00","id":829468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829421#post829421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's probably because somewhere down the line the wires got crossed. I could've swore that &quot;Manic Pixie Dream Girl&quot; was more for the Discordians than the Vaporians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely recall that the Vaporians were compared to that when you brought out a name for them being &quot;Ocean of Contact&quot;. I could be wrong. Also, there's a tiny problem. SquanamousBeauty, the one who had written the Alterations doc until now, hasn't seemed to been online since January 10th. I don't know if this will be a problem, because we can write up the Alterations ourselves, but I can't help but feel that small tinge of worry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829421#post829421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda see the Waters as representing some sort of role within a theatre production. The Polarians are the playwrights who construct a tragedy for the audience to know. The Tropicans are the lead, being the face of the play and the one in the spotlight. The Freshwaters are the supporting cast who build the narrative and give a sense of reality into the play. The Vaporians are callboys and callgirls running to make sure everything is in place without being seen by the audience. The Gardenians are the technicians that make sure that the lights are functioning, the microphones are on, and such. Finally, the Discordians are the needed comedy relief who come in to give the audience a breather before the play continues.<br /> <br /> Vast simplification, but this is kinda the way they play out. Tropicans, Freshwaters, and Discordians are the Waters that are most-likely going to go out of their way to meet with humanity while the Polarians, Vaporians, and Gardenians are the ones who are fine with being in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. In that case, the Currents would be more along with how the Waters roles in the play? Conflict are the heroes or the warriors who deal with the drama, Wisdom plays the wise people role in the plays (be it the wizard, the librarian or the sage), Harmony are the leaders and teachers who can instigate the drama or lead it to it's resolution, Buoyancy are the wizecrackers and jokers who can play the fool with double entendres for allies to pick up on. Healing keeps the plot going and tend to play secondary roles. On the Abyssal Currents, they serve as antagonists and as the foils to the currents. Dark Passions could be a dark version to Conflict, Dark Wisdom to Wisdom, Harmony to Mankind's Victory, Healing to Styx, and Buoyancy to Void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T21:52:44-08:00","id":829577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829468#post829468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely recall that the Vaporians were compared to that when you brought out a name for them being &quot;Ocean of Contact&quot;. I could be wrong. Also, there's a tiny problem. SquanamousBeauty, the one who had written the Alterations doc until now, hasn't seemed to been online since January 10th. I don't know if this will be a problem, because we can write up the Alterations ourselves, but I can't help but feel that small tinge of worry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely forgotten that this forum has a &quot;search&quot; option which also filters through threads. I made an off-hand remark that Discordians were manic and similar to the Vodianoi. I think that's where it came from.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, SquanamousBeauty is only offline due to personal issues or a time crunch. We can probably build some Alterations on our own if it comes to that. The Alterations may have a different feel to them in comparison to the ones SB wrote, but it shouldn't be too much of an issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. In that case, the Currents would be more along with how the Waters roles in the play? Conflict are the heroes or the warriors who deal with the drama, Wisdom plays the wise people role in the plays (be it the wizard, the librarian or the sage), Harmony are the leaders and teachers who can instigate the drama or lead it to it's resolution, Buoyancy are the wizecrackers and jokers who can play the fool with double entendres for allies to pick up on. Healing keeps the plot going and tend to play secondary roles. On the Abyssal Currents, they serve as antagonists and as the foils to the currents. Dark Passions could be a dark version to Conflict, Dark Wisdom to Wisdom, Harmony to Mankind's Victory, Healing to Styx, and Buoyancy to Void. </div> </div> </div>I did feel that the Abyssal Currents were dark mirrors to the normal Currents.<br /> <br /> The comparison of the Waters to different roles in a play was more for the ease of explaining their distinct roles. If the Waters have a general feel as to what the Sirens do, the Currents could be a &quot;what do they seek to change through their actions?&quot; sort of splat.<br /> <br /> I can see the <b>Current of Conflict</b> handling drama but I can also feel them working to break stalemates, pushing people along to work harder to accomplish what they think is right. <b>Freshwaters of Conflict</b> handle interpersonal conflicts as an impartial third while <b>Tropicans of Conflict</b> play a dangerous power game at board meetings and such. <b>Gardenians of Conflict</b> are forceful individuals that attempt to prevent harmful changes to the natural cycle. <b>Polarians of Conflict</b> encourage others to fight to the bitter end <i>(Cold War jokes engage) </i>until only one is left standing while <b>Vaporians of Conflict</b> plant seeds of doubt to make sure that people want to challenge institutions and big ideas. <b>Discordians of Conflict </b>might actively play a part in creating conflict, reveling in there being conflict all around them. The Current of Conflict, as translated into the theatre, would be the key moments, the tension that demonstrates the strength of character the actors have in their roles. The <b>Current of Dark Passions</b> would be them taking this <i>too far</i>, stepping over the Moral Event Horizon and descending into infamy.<br /> <br /> The<b> Current of Wisdom </b>would be mentor-roles but it also includes long-range planning and tactics. <b>Freshwaters of Wisdom</b> would definitely play the mentor or possibly even a caregiver for young children, watching over them and making sure they don't get into too much trouble while imparting what knowledge they have. <b>Tropicans of Wisdom</b> would be like a godfather, someone who exudes experience and knowledge behind a hardened facade; an intimidating figure due to their reputation but willing to share what they know. <b>Gardenians of Wisdom</b> would be custodians and librarians, archivists who wants to make sure that there is something to be passed down. <b>Polarians of Wisdom</b> find wisdom in death, looking to the failings of others as warnings to those still alive. <b>Vaporians of Wisdom</b> would be messengers and codebreakers, passing notes and letting others in on a secret. <b>Discordians of Wisdom</b> would be the poster child for &quot;Manic Pixie Dream Girl&quot;, wandering into someone's life in order to deliver some ground-breaking knowledge while doing something utterly incomprehensible. The Current of Wisdom is the underlying message, the overall theme that the playwright has constructed. The <b>Current of Dark Wisdom</b> turns this into a harmful message that has been censored but is attempting to be unveiled.<br /> <br /> The <b>Current of Harmony </b>are otherwise interwoven into the plot by virtue of meeting people and building rapport. While the Freshwaters are generally people persons, <b>Freshwaters of Harmony </b>feel that every connection they make is in some way special, no matter the circumstances. <b>Tropicans of Harmony</b> are lovers and confidants, pretty much the iconic movie mermaid.<b> Gardenians of Harmony </b>maintain relationships between households and between aspects of nature, raising families or developing the cycles in nature. <b>Polarians of Harmony</b>, in a stark contrast, would focus more on ending toxic relationships for the better of the world. <b>Vaporians of Harmony</b> build and rebuild connections, mending broken ties or searching for missing persons. <b>Discordians of Harmony </b>ignore all social restrictions, willing to extend a helping hand out to the most unlikely individuals. The Current of Harmony would be the barkers and advertisers asking their audience to come and enjoy the show. The <b>Current of Mankind's Victory </b>is a perversion of this, bending down to the will of humanity in order to please them at the expense of the world.<br /> <br /> The <b>Current of Healing</b> is one of second chances and rebirth, a cleansing of sins and a chance to do better. <b>Freshwaters of Healing</b> are emotional crutches, individuals that encourage others to continue without giving up or falling into despair. <b>Tropicans of Healing</b> reach out in order to allow others to heal, extending their connections to cover others and allowing the wounded to bask in the hearth. <b>Gardenians of Healing</b> are intimately aware of the healing process and will allow that process to occur, even if it means meddling in someone's affairs. <b>Polarians of Healing </b>prefer to rip off the bandage in one stroke, reveling in pain and cathartic healing. <b>Vaporians of Healing </b>do not ask questions, allowing others to grieve without a word as to why. Discordians of Healing find solstace in jokes and distractions, serving as a sort of numbing agent for the wounded. The Current of Healing is a tragedy that offers a sense of closure at the end. The <b>Current of Primordial Darkness</b> does not find closure, calling upon the forces of nature in order to find something that allows them to heal.<br /> <br /> The <b>Current of Buoyancy</b>, from what I assumed they were, were pragmatic and secretive, the &quot;Lighter Grey&quot; in the Black and White. I feel like the Current of Harmony would work better as wisecrackers and jokers. The Current of Buoyancy felt more like someone who on the whole is plainly visible but dips down in the depths to make sure that they, and others, can stay afloat; they do a dirty job so no one else needs to. <b>Freshwaters of Buoyancy</b> live to give and get favors, meeting up with questionable people and making connections that are best kept a secret. <b>Tropicans of Buoyancy</b> gladly play the villain or rival to humanity, pushing others to put their 100% through a sense of competition. <b>Gardenians of Buoyancy</b> play a secret game behind the scenes, maintaining the cycle by allowing others to rise to power when their time is due and lower them down when they overstay their welcome. <b>Polarians of Buoyancy</b> are effectively executioners in a sense, ending a relationship or making sure someone is unable to arrive on time in order to stop events from occurring. <b>Vaporians of Buoyancy</b> are infiltrators and thieves, stealing away items and information for better use. <b>Discordians of Buoyancy</b> are a devil's advocate, either encouraging others to break some rules or teach through example. <b>The Void</b> mirrors this by having Echidna sympathizers following her extreme actions &quot;for the greater good&quot;, a well-intentioned extremist who thinks that it's more pragmatic to build a race that outlives the next Deluge.<br /> <br /> Just some more stuff to mold what we have in terms of the Waters and the Currents.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And I completely forgot about the Castaways. I'll talk about them tomorrow, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":".  WHOP