class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829577#post829577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did feel that the Abyssal Currents were dark mirrors to the normal Currents.<br /> The comparison of the Waters to different roles in a play was more for the ease of explaining their distinct roles. If the Waters have a general feel as to what the Sirens do, the Currents could be a &quot;what do they seek to change through their actions?&quot; sort of splat.<br /> EDIT: And I completely forgot about the Castaways. I'll talk about them tomorrow, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel somewhat bad that you make long posts and usually my response is around the equivalent of &quot;k&quot;. But yes, that feels like the general gists of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T22:56:37-08:00","id":829591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=829590#post829590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, it does? And here I've been looking through each thread with Control + F to find stuff. &gt;&gt; But yes, hopefully it's that and nothing else. And I was thinking the Alterations would have some edits to them for more differentiation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It should be a floating little bar near the toolbar of your browser. It has a &quot;Post Reply&quot; Button on the left and a page navigation tool and a filter on the right. To the left of the page nav is a search bar thingy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel somewhat bad that you make long posts and usually my response is around the equivalent of &quot;k&quot;. But yes, that feels like the general gists of it. </div> </div> </div>No worries. I tend to type out a lot anyways. Just felt like we should at least have some idea of what the Currents mean when attached to a Water.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T14:12:35-08:00","id":830505,"title":"","content":"To ask, how would you all imagine the Discordian Sirens to be like? I wonder how they should go or be like, especially given how they're the last X Splat in Siren. The only thing I have to work with at the moment is the Atlantic Ocean, their &quot;original&quot; version so to speak.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Atlantic: Ocean of Might. This ocean is associated with the &quot;noble ocean warrior&quot; ideal of Sirens, though many tempestuous members are just as happy with a rusty harpoon, a sawed-off shotgun and an excuse as with a golden sword. They have an affinity for the Streams of Rusted Iron and Dueling Rites.</li> </ol>As well, I wonder. With the X splats nearing their end of development, what shall we do next? The Y Splats? Mechanics for Alteration? Perhaps ideas for the Z Splats or what they should be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T15:30:07-08:00","id":830555,"title":"","content":"I'm not particularly involved and mostly glance at the posts, but I guess like how I think Reaper views them which is a dark(er) version of the other currents that dip into extremes in everything, whether in favor of man or nature (or otherwise)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T15:57:50-08:00","id":830574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=830505#post830505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To ask, how would you all imagine the Discordian Sirens to be like? I wonder how they should go or be like, especially given how they're the last X Splat in Siren. The only thing I have to work with at the moment is the Atlantic Ocean, their &quot;original&quot; version so to speak.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Atlantic: Ocean of Might. This ocean is associated with the &quot;noble ocean warrior&quot; ideal of Sirens, though many tempestuous members are just as happy with a rusty harpoon, a sawed-off shotgun and an excuse as with a golden sword. They have an affinity for the Streams of Rusted Iron and Dueling Rites.</li> </ol>As well, I wonder. With the X splats nearing their end of development, what shall we do next? The Y Splats? Mechanics for Alteration? Perhaps ideas for the Z Splats or what they should be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that Discordian Sirens are a personification of whirlpools, tempests, and tidal waves. They are incredibly volatile, switching from one extreme to the next. One moment, they will be smiling, joyous in their life. Another, they have overturned tables and torn posters off the wall. In another, they quietly brood, sipping from their tea as they contemplate the horrors of The Deluge. In yet another, they mentally exit the world, going off on their own little journey to spread knowledge to humanity. They have been polluted, either by the blood of others filling the ocean or by swimming through seas of oil and rust. They are inconsistent, touched by the ages and maddened by revelations. However, they carry a spark of clarity that shines brightly through their antics. A mumbling madwoman torches a building down, taking the serial killer hiding within it. An eccentric socialite invests their time and money in political underdogs, hoping to overturn the corruption that is abound.<br /> <br /> The main word would be &quot;rebellion&quot;. Discordians are the jester of the court, a being who is considered a non-threat due to their madness but still stands close enough to the crowns to have an ear in the important discussions. They see each Deluge as a chance to try again, like a reset in a game. They are mad with possibilities, the Fool who journeys through the world in order to learn and Ascend. They are the mad oracle, the ones who hear an answer, every answer, but seek to put the answers to a question. <i>&quot;This man must live.&quot;</i> But why? <i>&quot;Run to the forest and wait for it.&quot; </i>What am I waiting for? <i>&quot;These people are your destiny. Meet with them.</i>&quot; Who are they? Discordians may never ask, but they will know.<br /> <br /> In terms of theatre, Discordians are the acts during the intermission. They exist somewhere outside of the grand scheme but can hint to the audience things that are coming up or give them a quick synopsis to catch up. With the other Waters, a Discordian is considered to be many things. The Tropicans think of Discordians as cute little madmen, keeping them on a short leash before unleashing them on someone they don't like; it's a sort of condescending pity. The Polarians are very much wary of the Discordians, aware of their mad insight; they give them a wide berth as they contemplate how to work their plans around a screwy little squirrel. The Vaporians like the Discordians to an extent, happy that the Discordians are willing to work for change but worried whenever there is a disaster that needs to be cleaned up. The Gardenians, in contrast, are partially terrified by the Discordians and partially appreciative; their rebellion calls for the end and rebirth of cycles. The Freshwaters are genuinely saddened by Discordians, believing their madness to be an unfortunate side-effect of the Deluge. <br /> <br /> The Discordians themselves consider their brothers and sisters to be, in few words, too caught up in their role to truly understand their madness. The Discordians know and see with true clarity. That is why some treat the world as a comedy, laughing mad. That's why some treat the world as a tragedy, reduced to hysteria. What Discordians Know with a capital letter is that <b>You Don't See the Depths from the Surface</b>. That is to say, the truth is not always on the surface of things, nor is it easy to find. There are many layers to the truth, depending on perspective. For example, the Discordians are insane. That statement is true to an extent. Discordians are also intensely aware of the world. That is also a truth. It is also a lie, as with the previous statement. Discordians will let themselves sink if it means that they can see the Depths. Discordians also Know that <b>The Gears of the World Need a Push</b>. Discordians are not exactly subtle. Neither are rebellions. A Discordian knows that the Deluge is coming and they will see to it that it stops, even if it means stopping catastrophes at their youngest without explanation.<br /> <br /> As for the next thing in development, we could probably go into the Y-Splat or the Verses. Something to round off character creation and playability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T18:27:03-08:00","id":830665,"title":"","content":"So the Discordians are basically mermaid Malkavians from VtM?<br /> I agree that Y-Splat and Verses is a good next step when the Discordians are done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T20:37:33-08:00","id":830761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=830665#post830665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Discordians are basically mermaid Malkavians from VtM?<br /> I agree that Y-Splat and Verses is a good next step when the Discordians are done.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are similar, yes. Considering that Sirens are, by their nature, oracular, it feels right to have a &quot;Mad Oracle&quot; type, or at least someone who is more strongly the Mad Oracle. The Polarians are the &quot;Old Seers/Wise Elders&quot;, the Gardenians are the &quot;Enigmatic Keepers of Knowledge&quot; type. The Tropicans and Freshwaters are more towards the &quot;Mermaid&quot; side of Siren and the Vaporians are kinda in between with their mystique.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel that Lissandra from League of Legends is a possible inspiration for the Polarians as well as the myth of the Yuki-Onna. They aren't necessarily mermaids, but they are mysterious figures that relate close to ice. Lissandra's lower body is also pure ice. She fits the idea considering that she's existed for countless millennia and has been playing a sort of puppetmaster in the scheme of things in the Freljord.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Admittedly, not the most-familiar with VtM so I double-checked on the general specs of the Malkavians and found out that a term for them is &quot;Fishmalk&quot;.<br /> <br /> I...eugh...what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":". 02-15-2016, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T23:27:12-08:00","id":830864,"title":"","content":"Try not to think about the fishmalks c:<br /> Anyway by the sound of it to me so far, the Discordians are roughly what I would expect from those who jump off the morality meter a l\u00e1 draugr, wretched, insert here. What draws people into them and makes you wanna side with any of them? Do they have any redeeming factors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T03:05:31-08:00","id":830930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=830864#post830864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try not to think about the fishmalks c:<br /> Anyway by the sound of it to me so far, the Discordians are roughly what I would expect from those who jump off the morality meter a l\u00e1 draugr, wretched, insert here. What draws people into them and makes you wanna side with any of them? Do they have any redeeming factors?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main thing about Discordians, aside from their madness, is the fact that they want to push for change. All Sirens want to change the world in order to prevent The Deluge, but a Discordian is willing to take charge. Freshwaters want to experience life and be out with the people, but that only goes so far. Tropicans have that passion and force that can drive for change, but they are more focused on invested change. Gardenians are preservers who actively go against unnecessary change. Polarians are thinkers who come up with plans rather than being right in there. Vaporians are agents who slink in secrecy, but they operate differently than the Discordians.<br /> <br /> Discordians would consider themselves willing pawns in the game that Sirens play against a force they cannot predict. They are the vanguard who push forward in order to allow their brothers and sisters an opening. They are the first stand, taking up arms against the Flensers or the Furies or whatever decides to go at their Shoal. They are the fall guys, willing to damage their own reputation if it means that the real perpetrator can act without notice. In a sense, the Discordians are fanatics willing to throw themselves as martyrs if it means that the &quot;good guys win&quot;. That is their internal logic. Who cares if everyone thinks that they're insane? Let them watch so the Vaporians can come in without notice. Let them be in awe so the Polarians can plan for a little longer. Even in a Shoal of only Discordians, they find themselves able to operate in all the chaos, splashing around until their ripples become waves. <br /> <br /> A possible inspiration for the Discordians is Ophelia from Hamlet or anyone who invokes the image of Ophelia. Discordians have been broken with the knowledge that there have been Deluges that have washed away worlds. Discordians are solidly aware of the dangers of the world; the Flensers hunger for the rejuvenating flesh of the Sirens, the Furies are burning with Nature's indignant rage, and Echidna whispers to the Discordians' brethren. This madness is like a safeguard, something that allows them to cope with the world.<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, don't the CofD-friendly gamelines offer some sort of &quot;passive&quot;? Beasts have Birthrights which allow them some sort of benefit based on their Family, Demons have Conditions based on their Agenda, Vampires have Clan Banes, and Werewolves have Auspice Benefits. Sirens do have have an advantage when they enter their Favored Water, but that's a little basic and is universal, like the favored prey of Werewolves. Should the Waters also offer some sort of extra oomph? It'll help differentiate the Waters and add emphasis to having a variety of Waters.<br /> <br /> Say, the Freshwaters, because they thrive in the presence of others, gains some sort of bonus when they are within a crowd of people they know. And the Tropicans, because they put in their all when it comes to their passions, have stronger specialties. The Discordians could have some sort of benefit when it comes to their Lucidity, being made of stronger stuff or being protected by their madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T04:50:22-08:00","id":830956,"title":"","content":"So the Discordians are trying to take the short-term route to victory and damn the consequences/hope that gives the others what they need to starve the deluge and pick up the pieces afterwards?<br /> As far as 2E and God-Machine goes, I'll stay away from that part as I don't want to touch them much of any (latter) or at all (former).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T05:03:34-08:00","id":830959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=830956#post830956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Discordians are trying to take the short-term route to victory and damn the consequences/hope that gives the others what they need to starve the deluge and pick up the pieces afterwards?<br /> As far as 2E and God-Machine goes, I'll stay away from that part as I don't want to touch them much of any (latter) or at all (former).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Possibly. Starving the Deluge without any colateral damage is the best-case scenario. Mainly, the Discordians feel that the other Waters are too involved in other situations to make the first push. They have a &quot;Don't Think, Feel&quot; type of a mindset when it comes to accomplishing tasks. When the Discordians aren't making the charge, they're attempting to cope with their situation. Like an onion, the Discordians have layers. Mad Oracle Vanguard with Mood Swings and Meta-Knowledge. When they feel playful, they will play. When they want to make a stand, they will make a stand.<br /> <br /> I feel like this quote would be appropriate for a non-Discordian who deals with one on a daily basis: <i>&quot;So which facet of your personality am I speaking with right now?&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:16:36-08:00","id":830973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=830761#post830761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are similar, yes. Considering that Sirens are, by their nature, oracular, it feels right to have a &quot;Mad Oracle&quot; type, or at least someone who is more strongly the Mad Oracle. The Polarians are the &quot;Old Seers/Wise Elders&quot;, the Gardenians are the &quot;Enigmatic Keepers of Knowledge&quot; type. The Tropicans and Freshwaters are more towards the &quot;Mermaid&quot; side of Siren and the Vaporians are kinda in between with their mystique.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Admittedly, not the most-familiar with VtM so I double-checked on the general specs of the Malkavians and found out that a term for them is &quot;Fishmalk&quot;.<br /> <br /> I...eugh...what.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say that while Oracular stuff is a theme for Sirens, I don't think that not all Sirens exactly need to play it out. Like how not all Princesses are Hopebringers, not all Wolves are Spirit cops, Etcetc. But of course what I'm saying is needless because there are places where it's not played out. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/b/b4/Fishmalk.gif/revision/latest?cb=20070313201126\" target=\"_blank\">http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/...20070313201126</a><br /> Fishmalks are basically a stereotype of players who play as the &quot;Insane&quot; splat for shits and giggles rather than playing the insanity as something to be taken seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T17:49:52-08:00","id":832212,"title":"","content":"I forgot to mention something. The Vaporians were rewritten (at least their story part). Anything else required for Vaporians?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T18:56:04-08:00","id":832237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=832212#post832212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot to mention something. The Vaporians were rewritten (at least their story part). Anything else required for Vaporians?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None from me. Two thumbs up. :V","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:59:35-08:00","id":833958,"title":"","content":"Just a small update, but I'm beginning on Discordia and finishing up the Waters~<br /> <br /> I also have a small idea for the Currents. What if one of their nicknames was some fitting fish for them? Like Buoyancy (being tricksters) could have Clownfish as a nickname, Cocytus have &quot;Bottomfeeders&quot;, Conflict has &quot;Swordfish&quot;, etcetc. Just a thought. And also, I have an idea for a stereotype that the Current of Wisdom would have on Cocytus (Current of Dark Wisdom being a semi-official name for them :3).<br /> <br /> Wisdom on Dark Wisdom: &quot;Stop using my name and drown back to the depths you came from!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T19:13:41-08:00","id":835508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=833958#post833958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a small update, but I'm beginning on Discordia and finishing up the Waters~<br /> <br /> I also have a small idea for the Currents. What if one of their nicknames was some fitting fish for them? Like Buoyancy (being tricksters) could have Clownfish as a nickname, Cocytus have &quot;Bottomfeeders&quot;, Conflict has &quot;Swordfish&quot;, etcetc. Just a thought. And also, I have an idea for a stereotype that the Current of Wisdom would have on Cocytus (Current of Dark Wisdom being a semi-official name for them :3).<br /> <br /> Wisdom on Dark Wisdom: &quot;Stop using my name and drown back to the depths you came from!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see that. Those nicknames could also reflect on the possible symbol for them. The Current of Conflict is a swordfish for the whole &quot;gallant fight for righteousness&quot; angle while the Current of Dark Conflict could be two betta fish fighting to represent fury and dominance. The Current of Wisdom could be an octopus considering that they are one of the most-intelligent of marine life while the Current of Dark Wisdom are a bottomfeeder, possibly a sea cucumber. Not to sure of the other Currents, but I feel like an oyster could be used for Mankind's Victory, as they are used to create pearls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T15:09:23-08:00","id":836701,"title":"","content":"Finally, the Discordians are....99% complete. They just need a few more alteration ideas. They're otherwise done. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now then, I believe we all were to brainstorm for the Y Splats? I have an idea on the representative animals/logos, including Reapers ideas for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Buoyancy: </b>Clownfish. It's a phonetic pun (they're the tricksters and thieves) with the image of a clownfish resting in the middle of an anemonie. There's tentacles that surround the clownfish that has dents or marks that look like faces, with maybe a fish or two caught in them with evil looking faces on them. I feel a good analogy for calling them clownfish is that &quot;They know how to get allies and if their enemies try hurting them, they can get their allies, temporary or not, to get them in their place&quot;. It could also work as an idea of luring an enemy to where others more capable could get them in the Clownfish's place.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>Octopus. As Reaper said, it's fitting because they're the most Intelligent animal. I imagine as an image for them, it shows an octopus facing forwards with four of it's tentacles in some graceful pattern behind it. In it's front, it's two innermost tentacles hold a book and a scroll respectively. It's outer two tentacles help in holding the two things, but they're both damaged, showing how knowledge can be a bane as much as a benefit.<br /> <br /> <b>Conflict: </b>Swordfish. I imagine their symbol to be a simple show of three swords. One on the right is a pirate's cutlass, rusted in spots and with a red cloth over the handle. On the left is a graceful rapier, more akin to an ornament than a weapon, but it represents the nobility the Current of Conflict holds.The middle sword looks odd, unconventional to be a sword as there's no visible hilt to hold. However, the reason for this is because the middle blade is a Swordfish skull for their iconography.<br /> <br /> <b>Lethe/Mankind's Victory: </b>Horse. It's very unorthodox for a game set about water and marine animals, but there's a few reasons I chose this. For one, I imagine the symbol to be like a human heraldry of a wealthy family (perhaps befitting Mankind's Victory). For another, there's stories of how Horses and the Ocean have been together. Poseidon had created horses from the waves and made fish-horse hybrids known as Hippocampi. Kelpie and Kappas are both known to take the forms of horses to lure travellers to ride on them before diving into the water to drown them. And finally, the Horse is known as a symbol for Pride, that it will do what it wants if no control is on it. This fits Lethe throwing away control for their desires to screw nature and letting their pride do all their decision making for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Styx/Primordial Darkness: </b>Shark. I see Styx as the people who'd see themselves as the Apex Predator after becoming a Siren and wanting to go out against the petty humans. Having the Shark as an image is fitting for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Phelegethon/Dark Passions: </b>Dolphin. I know, also unorthodox. But I tell you now, they are assholes. These animals basically drag other animals or fish down to the bottom of the ocean just to rape them. They grope people, they kill porpoises because it looks like their children. Heck, dolphins kill their own children, have LOADS of STDs and kill pufferfish to get high off of them. They are evil as hell and the ways they are evil is fitting for Dark Passions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:54:00-08:00","id":836818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=836701#post836701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, the Discordians are....99% complete. They just need a few more alteration ideas. They're otherwise done. :3<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rascgDKjoe2ieYRN2h4-p7gS5E15W5kAEIhtr-Zqpms/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit, I love the Stereotype they have for the Freshwaters. As for Alterations, I feel like the Discordians could be based on creatures that live in extreme conditions, like various sea worms, or have some form of defensive mechanism, like the sting of a sea anemone. They could even take on some aspects of animals that are sensitive to mutations, like frogs that develop extra limbs or dual-headed turtles. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now then, I believe we all were to brainstorm for the Y Splats? I have an idea on the representative animals/logos, including Reapers ideas for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Buoyancy: </b>Clownfish. It's a phonetic pun (they're the tricksters and thieves) with the image of a clownfish resting in the middle of an anemonie. There's tentacles that surround the clownfish that has dents or marks that look like faces, with maybe a fish or two caught in them with evil looking faces on them. I feel a good analogy for calling them clownfish is that &quot;They know how to get allies and if their enemies try hurting them, they can get their allies, temporary or not, to get them in their place&quot;. It could also work as an idea of luring an enemy to where others more capable could get them in the Clownfish's place.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom: </b>Octopus. As Reaper said, it's fitting because they're the most Intelligent animal. I imagine as an image for them, it shows an octopus facing forwards with four of it's tentacles in some graceful pattern behind it. In it's front, it's two innermost tentacles hold a book and a scroll respectively. It's outer two tentacles help in holding the two things, but they're both damaged, showing how knowledge can be a bane as much as a benefit.<br /> <br /> <b>Conflict: </b>Swordfish. I imagine their symbol to be a simple show of three swords. One on the right is a pirate's cutlass, rusted in spots and with a red cloth over the handle. On the left is a graceful rapier, more akin to an ornament than a weapon, but it represents the nobility the Current of Conflict holds.The middle sword looks odd, unconventional to be a sword as there's no visible hilt to hold. However, the reason for this is because the middle blade is a Swordfish skull for their iconography.<br /> <br /> <b>Lethe/Mankind's Victory: </b>Horse. It's very unorthodox for a game set about water and marine animals, but there's a few reasons I chose this. For one, I imagine the symbol to be like a human heraldry of a wealthy family (perhaps befitting Mankind's Victory). For another, there's stories of how Horses and the Ocean have been together. Poseidon had created horses from the waves and made fish-horse hybrids known as Hippocampi. Kelpie and Kappas are both known to take the forms of horses to lure travellers to ride on them before diving into the water to drown them. And finally, the Horse is known as a symbol for Pride, that it will do what it wants if no control is on it. This fits Lethe throwing away control for their desires to screw nature and letting their pride do all their decision making for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Styx/Primordial Darkness: </b>Shark. I see Styx as the people who'd see themselves as the Apex Predator after becoming a Siren and wanting to go out against the petty humans. Having the Shark as an image is fitting for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Phelegethon/Dark Passions: </b>Dolphin. I know, also unorthodox. But I tell you now, they are assholes. These animals basically drag other animals or fish down to the bottom of the ocean just to rape them. They grope people, they kill porpoises because it looks like their children. Heck, dolphins kill their own children, have LOADS of STDs and kill pufferfish to get high off of them. They are evil as hell and the ways they are evil is fitting for Dark Passions. </div> </div> </div>I can see all of these fitting. With Lethe, I think it would be more-fitting for the horse to at least be half-fish, like most of the depictions of the hippocampus. It would also be a visual reference to the idea that the Sirens of Lethe are abandoning nature (the fish half that tails behind the hippocampus) in order to serve humanity (the horse half that makes up the front).<br /> <br /> Also, dolphins are full on evil and completely fit Phelegethon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T05:11:39-08:00","id":836975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=836818#post836818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, I love the Stereotype they have for the Freshwaters. As for Alterations, I feel like the Discordians could be based on creatures that live in extreme conditions, like various sea worms, or have some form of defensive mechanism, like the sting of a sea anemone. They could even take on some aspects of animals that are sensitive to mutations, like frogs that develop extra limbs or dual-headed turtles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it's not too &quot;not-serious&quot; for the Discordians or the game. And yes, extreme and mutationy things sound like a good idea. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=836818#post836818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see all of these fitting. With Lethe, I think it would be more-fitting for the horse to at least be half-fish, like most of the depictions of the hippocampus. It would also be a visual reference to the idea that the Sirens of Lethe are abandoning nature (the fish half that tails behind the hippocampus) in order to serve humanity (the horse half that makes up the front)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuppers, sounds good.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the next question now is, should there be special benefits associated with being in a Current? Because if not, then there's little difference between being in a Current and being a Castaway. We have the part of a favored Conclusion down, is there anything else we could list?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T07:45:22-08:00","id":837550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry for double posting, I was looking over the old Siren thread and got all the ideas dealing with currents (And one with Oceans because it interested me) and these are the ideas that came out. I certainly like the ideas of the Currents being academic or knowledge based, fitting as a subtle pun for &quot;school&quot; (of fish ofc) and how Sirens can get knowledge by Tracing and seeking through the Deluge. I imagine it being merit and knowledge based would be befitting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T19:51:41-08:00","id":837877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=836975#post836975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the next question now is, should there be special benefits associated with being in a Current? Because if not, then there's little difference between being in a Current and being a Castaway. We have the part of a favored Conclusion down, is there anything else we could list?<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Sorry for double posting, I was looking over the old Siren thread and got all the ideas dealing with currents (And one with Oceans because it interested me) and these are the ideas that came out. I certainly like the ideas of the Currents being academic or knowledge based, fitting as a subtle pun for &quot;school&quot; (of fish ofc) and how Sirens can get knowledge by Tracing and seeking through the Deluge. I imagine it being merit and knowledge based would be befitting them.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> Hmm, it could be that each Current helps a Siren refine her ability to Trace. I wrote before that Tracing functions similarly to the Psychometry merit in that a Siren may Trace by asking a specific question and reviewing the past of what she is Tracing. Perhaps the Currents influence how well the Sirens may Trace.<br /> <br /> For example, a Siren of Conflict would be able to Trace things that are muddled and messy. They enjoy walking through old battlegrounds because they can play entire wars in their head through Tracing. They can see where a soldier lost his arm or where a cannon was placed to fire on the enemy. This extends to things such as crowded areas or national disasters that cause mass chaos. Most Sirens are unable to focus their Trace in order to navigate through this maze of disorder. For a Siren of Conflict, it's a bit trivial to understand what has happened where.<br /> <br /> A Siren of Wisdom has an &quot;enhanced&quot; Trace. When a Siren Traces an office building, does she see the files being handled and passed from employee to employee? Does she see the tired look in the worker's eye after working overtime for an entire week? Sirens of Wisdom catch each and every detail down to the very hairs that cling to the intern's shirt after having a wild one-on-one with his higher-up in the restroom. A Siren of Wisdom sees all of these minute details in her Trace.<br /> <br /> A Siren of Harmony has a knack for putting 1 and 1 together. When she decides to Trace, her mind wanders to another place, an outlying memory of the world that connects to what she is Tracing. Effectively, a Siren of Harmony is able to answer two questions when Tracing, lining up two different concepts and bringing them to the point in which they crossed over. The bomber who devastated a shelter downtown? He was on a train and made contact with an informant who gave him the information needed to formulate his plan. In a Siren of Harmony's mind, the lines connect with little issue.<br /> <br /> A Siren of Healing goes to where it all started, to the first transaction made. She Traces two feuding families and sees their exchanges through the years, gradually accelerating back to the first moment that a dirty look was shot nearly a century ago. She Traces a doll that belongs to a missing child and sees the moment that she leaves the house as well as the abuse she had to endure over the years that eventually led to her running away. A Siren of Healing doesn't just see the branches when she Traces; she goes down to the very roots.<br /> <br /> A Siren of Buoyancy is able to Trace in such a way that it allows her to see the secrets that lie in plain sight. The Siren Traces back through the fire and sees the face of the man through his mask. She sees through the tinted windows of his car and sees the empty can of gasoline and a crude map of possible marks. The Siren Traces the remains of an old tree and sees the trail of illegal dumping that leads to a signature being forged on a document. The Siren may not see the entire picture, but she sees enough to understand what has been undergoing in the shadows. <br /> <br /> In order to balance the fact that they do not receive an associated Conclusion and no special effects for their Trace, the Castaways are able to Trace without spending Pneuma once per scene; their spectator nature makes it easier to see the Visions.<br /> <br /> Maybe all of this could be associated with the Currents.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T20:25:51-08:00","id":837899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=837877#post837877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Me gusta. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe this goes for Abyssal Currents as well? :3 <br /> <br /> Cocytus seeks to learn the occult knowledge and taboo secrets others fear to touch. As such, when they use Trace, they're able to look into the threads of where the dark knowledge they seek may lie, like a man who finds a map that leads to an old family heirloom despite his dying parents stating &quot;to never casually use it save in direst need&quot;. <br /> <br /> Phelegethon seeks to learn about social weaknesses, failings in human nature where a Siren can make use of for her own ends and enjoyment. She finds which jock has a broken heart from a past break up, and seeks to fill the void herself. At least, until she dumps him and leaves an even bigger void in her place.<br /> <br /> Lethe seeks to learn of business opportunities, places where the Siren can make a profit off of another's suffering for her gain, especially if it's against nature. This also conveniently doesn't show the error of the Sirens actions, which I feel is entirely befitting of Lethe. :3<br /> <br /> Styx's version is somewhat akin to Healing, although instead it shows only instances of pure festering pain and the level of hatred and resentment that's turned out because of it. The Styxian Sirens feel that if restitution wasn't made (with the (perhaps somewhat legitimate) excuse of &quot;if you were truly apologetic you would've turned yourself earlier you pedophiliac c***&quot;) then the person they're punishing at best isn't gonna be sleep for the next month. At worst they'll be found half eaten and drowned face down in the nearest water source....if they're even found at all.<br /> <br /> Finally, Acheron. I think that Acheron would tell them of every weak point of where the Siren desires to strike to make it all fall to pieces. <br /> <br /> I would say though that given Echidnal Siren's aren't exactly a &quot;Current&quot;, I'd say that her Siren's Trace are basically the same as a Castaways. If not, then it should be focused around finding things the Siren should do that would benefit Echidna or her plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T21:09:16-08:00","id":837913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=837899#post837899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Me gusta. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe this goes for Abyssal Currents as well? :3<br /> <br /> Cocytus seeks to learn the occult knowledge and taboo secrets others fear to touch. As such, when they use Trace, they're able to look into the threads of where the dark knowledge they seek may lie, like a man who finds a map that leads to an old family heirloom despite his dying parents stating &quot;to never casually use it save in direst need&quot;.<br /> <br /> Phelegethon seeks to learn about social weaknesses, failings in human nature where a Siren can make use of for her own ends and enjoyment. She finds which jock has a broken heart from a past break up, and seeks to fill the void herself. At least, until she dumps him and leaves an even bigger void in her place.<br /> <br /> Lethe seeks to learn of business opportunities, places where the Siren can make a profit off of another's suffering for her gain, especially if it's against nature. This also conveniently doesn't show the error of the Sirens actions, which I feel is entirely befitting of Lethe. :3<br /> <br /> Styx's version is somewhat akin to Healing, although instead it shows only instances of pure festering pain and the level of hatred and resentment that's turned out because of it. The Styxian Sirens feel that if restitution wasn't made (with the (perhaps somewhat legitimate) excuse of &quot;if you were truly apologetic you would've turned yourself earlier you pedophiliac c***&quot;) then the person they're punishing at best isn't gonna be sleep for the next month. At worst they'll be found half eaten and drowned face down in the nearest water source....if they're even found at all.<br /> <br /> Finally, Acheron. I think that Acheron would tell them of every weak point of where the Siren desires to strike to make it all fall to pieces.<br /> <br /> I would say though that given Echidnal Siren's aren't exactly a &quot;Current&quot;, I'd say that her Siren's Trace are basically the same as a Castaways. If not, then it should be focused around finding things the Siren should do that would benefit Echidna or her plans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That all sounds solid. It also gives me a think on if Echidna's Sirens could be considered foils to the Castaways, like how the Abyssal Currents mirror the normal Currents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T21:48:10-08:00","id":837931,"title":"","content":"Goodies, and it's fitting for Echidnal Sirens to mirror the Castaways. :3 I think this is at least enough to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:34:33-08:00","id":839119,"title":"","content":"To sort of try balling around some of the ideas and make more convos on this thread, I looked on the beginning thread and saw a few ideas. For one, there's Grottos and the Z-Splats.<br /> <br /> Grottos/Lagoons were to be the Siren's version of a Sanctum/Haven/Hallow/Palace. There was nothing at all said of what they were supposed to look like or be like. For this, I would like to suggest that an idea on them that they're safe havens a Siren can create in the Deluge and can even live in. I don't know how to explain it better than in Disney's the Little Mermaid, how well Ariel's place is hidden and filled with mementos from the human world of things gotten from shipwrecks.<br /> <br /> The ideas for Z-Splats included the idea of them to be named &quot;Choruses&quot; and the powers they grant would be called &quot;Arias&quot;. What should Choruses be based around as a theme? Z-Splats tend to be centered around either an X or Y Splat philosophy or belief or are some outgrowing of it, but they still cover some theme that's plausible for the gameline. Legacies still study magic or find special use for it, Lodges incorporate their beliefs to the Shadow, Embassies are focused on making friendly connections to humanity and making concepts hostile to it non-threatening or more welcoming. How would Choruses work in this case? Special ways for Sirens to carry out their work or focus on a certain task? I can imagine a Chorus that plays cupid, another whose focus is to provide more food to the starving (basing off of the idea of the one jesus story where he split a few fish and bread to hundreds of people), etcetc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T10:07:37-08:00","id":839275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=839119#post839119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grottos/Lagoons were to be the Siren's version of a Sanctum/Haven/Hallow/Palace. There was nothing at all said of what they were supposed to look like or be like. For this, I would like to suggest that an idea on them that they're safe havens a Siren can create in the Deluge and can even live in. I don't know how to explain it better than in Disney's the Little Mermaid, how well Ariel's place is hidden and filled with mementos from the human world of things gotten from shipwrecks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. Should it function similar to Havens, Residential Areas, and Dedicated Locuses in CofD, Tombs and Hollows in CtL and MtC, or Boltholes in DtD? The Havens in CofD work off of having a Safeplace and provide extra benefits per dot. Tombs and Hollows are divided into subcategories that are increased separately. Boltholes provide a flat benefit and add on extra layers per dot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ideas for Z-Splats included the idea of them to be named &quot;Choruses&quot; and the powers they grant would be called &quot;Arias&quot;. What should Choruses be based around as a theme? Z-Splats tend to be centered around either an X or Y Splat philosophy or belief or are some outgrowing of it, but they still cover some theme that's plausible for the gameline. Legacies still study magic or find special use for it, Lodges incorporate their beliefs to the Shadow, Embassies are focused on making friendly connections to humanity and making concepts hostile to it non-threatening or more welcoming. How would Choruses work in this case? Special ways for Sirens to carry out their work or focus on a certain task? I can imagine a Chorus that plays cupid, another whose focus is to provide more food to the starving (basing off of the idea of the one jesus story where he split a few fish and bread to hundreds of people), etcetc? </div> </div> </div>Hmm, as far as the splats go right now, the Oceans represents the &quot;background&quot; of someone, the place in which someone would grow up, so to speak. The Currents represents the &quot;mindset&quot;, the beliefs that develop over time. The Z-Splat could work as a sort of &quot;profession&quot;, a cause that the Sirens choose to devote themselves to. I wouldn't know what to base their names on but I'm almost leaning towards song titles or genres for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T10:48:01-08:00","id":839294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=839275#post839275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see that. Should it function similar to Havens, Residential Areas, and Dedicated Locuses in CofD, Tombs and Hollows in CtL and MtC, or Boltholes in DtD? The Havens in CofD work off of having a Safeplace and provide extra benefits per dot. Tombs and Hollows are divided into subcategories that are increased separately. Boltholes provide a flat benefit and add on extra layers per dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to get some info on most of the stuff listed sans Hollows, I will get back to this when I have the info and make an answer. So far I'm leaning towards CtL Hollow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=839275#post839275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, as far as the splats go right now, the Oceans represents the &quot;background&quot; of someone, the place in which someone would grow up, so to speak. The Currents represents the &quot;mindset&quot;, the beliefs that develop over time. The Z-Splat could work as a sort of &quot;profession&quot;, a cause that the Sirens choose to devote themselves to. I wouldn't know what to base their names on but I'm almost leaning towards song titles or genres for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we should stick away from that, at least away from naming Choruses or Arias after specific songs. Let's just say my reasoning is because &quot;showing your iTunes list online is inviting a flame war&quot; and because Princess sort of has that schtick for the Inspire Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:29:16-08:00","id":839362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=839294#post839294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we should stick away from that, at least away from naming Choruses or Arias after specific songs. Let's just say my reasoning is because &quot;showing your iTunes list online is inviting a flame war&quot; and because Princess sort of has that schtick for the Inspire Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point. On the flip side, they could be named for operas, plays, or ballets. Such as with the &quot;cupid&quot; idea you had, they could be &quot;The Hearts of Cygnus&quot;, entirely entwined in creating romances and matching people up in order to &quot;heal&quot; their aching heart could be themed towards &quot;Swan Lake&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> After all, the two main characters decide to drown themselves if it means being able to die together.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T14:49:44-08:00","id":839445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=839362#post839362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point. On the flip side, they could be named for operas, plays, or ballets. Such as with the &quot;cupid&quot; idea you had, they could be &quot;The Hearts of Cygnus&quot;, entirely entwined in creating romances and matching people up in order to &quot;heal&quot; their aching heart could be themed towards &quot;Swan Lake&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> After all, the two main characters decide to drown themselves if it means being able to die together.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. In that case, I'm all for it if it's like that. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:37:09-08:00","id":839523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=839445#post839445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. In that case, I'm all for it if it's like that. :3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Presumably, the Choruses/Arias are more similar to Embassies and Entitlements than Lodges and Legacies in that they are open to all Sirens regardless of Water or Current. There are probably some Choruses/Arias that appear more to Sirens of a Current or a Water; the <b>Hearts of Cygnus</b> would probably attract a fair bit of Freshwaters for being so ideal and the Tropicans for wanting others to follow their heart as well as some Siren who follow the Current of Harmony and Healing.<br /> <br /> Walking a similar path, the Chorus/Aria known as <b>Carmen's Reprise</b> focuses on demonstrating the dark side of humanity by bringing out jealousy and envy. Through seduction, insulting needling, and utter defiance, Carmen's Reprise works to show the ugliness within someone in order to defame them and bring them down. It attracts a fair amount of Tropicans wanting to demonstrate their dominance and some Discordians who believe it to be fun, but it also brings in Vaporians who play tempters that hide in every corner. It's based around the opera <i>Carmen, </i>the gypsy woman who seduces men for fun until she becomes bored of them and sends them on their way.<br /> <br /> Yet another, the <b>Retainers of the Madame</b>, take a more cynical route by taking care of those who have suffered from heartbreak, caring for young children who were abandoned or easing others into a normal routine after a death or divorce. They do nothing to stop the heartbreak; they only provide the cushion afterwards. Polarians make up the majority though there are Gardenians who follow this mindset found in their numbers. This one is based on <i>Madama Butterfly</i>.<br /> <br /> Of course, these three are based around the idea of love, though they approach the idea in three different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T05:24:45-08:00","id":839816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=839523#post839523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, these three are based around the idea of love, though they approach the idea in three different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god I love these. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yes, these are perfect for setting off the Z-Splats. As well, I think that there could be some Choruses that are Current only, if only in the case of the Abyssal Currents. For example, some Choruses that are Styxian only would be cut off from Letheans. If nothing else, I imagine the Choruses would be mainly open to all currents plus Dark Passions and Dark Wisdom. The few that are left are Styxian and Lethean. The reason that Acheron wasn't mentioned is because I think they're too few in number to hold up any.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I have an idea for a few other Current symbols. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> <b>Harmony: </b>Coral. The reason for this being is because it is a living creature that serves as a home for other fish, providing safe places for them. Perhaps the only flaw I have with this is that Coral can literally die of being too stressed, although this might be fitting for the Current of Harmony. They try not to get too stressed over stuff because they have the most stress out of all the currents.<br /> <br /> <b>Cocytus/Dark Wisdom: </b>Anglerfish. They live in the abyssal zone of creatures, the oddity of their characteristics (bioluminessence) draws other fish to them. However, follow the oddity only provided by them too closely, and you may get caught in their jaws. I feel it fits the Sirens who join this current. :3<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:50:09-08:00","id":841054,"title":"","content":"Pardon my lack of writing, Midterms are killing my soul. However, I did get an idea for something else in this game. I've read that in the Bible, Leviathan was associated with the Primodial Sea, whereas Behemoth is an opposite associated with the Primordial Earth. There's also a third associated with the Primodial Sky called &quot;Ziz&quot;. The idea I had was that these could be used in making the Siren Backstory. I imagine that with the figures we have (Ceto, Echidna, Leviathan, Behemoth and Ziz), this is the idea I have.<br /> <br /> Behemoth is the monster who stirred the earth and shaped it according to his being to be strong and immutable. Ziz was responsible for bringing the law of nature and life onto the land. Leviathan was responsible for the creation of life, and thus brought the waters that were essential to life. I imagine one of the first of these beings born was Ceto, whose duty brought by Ziz was to nurture the world they created and ensure it survived. Ceto did her job, peacefully and calmly without complaint. Behemoth too desired to have something of his own, and with Leviathan's help, he gave life to humanity, this being a literal allegory to Humanity being referred to as &quot;children of the earth&quot;. From this, Ceto fell in love with humanity, and had the idea to use Humanity to help her quest as even she had her hands full sooner or later. With an ok from the three, Ceto introduced her duties to the humans who would listen to her plight, and those who did and followed her were granted the ability to survive on both land and Sea. In other words, she brought forth the Sirens. Ziz was happy enough to watch from the heavens, as everything would follow it's laws. Things were overall fine....<br /> <br /> Until Behemoth started to get jealous of Leviathan's power. Behemoth alone couldn't create life. He could shape the immutable and turn coal to diamond, and could even strengthen the life on earth because part of his blood went into it....but the power of creation was not his to have. Only Leviathan could wield it. As such, Behemoth started testing his boundaries, turning Humanity and the creatures of the Earth against Leviathan. Since they were acting in Ziz's laws, Ziz did nothing. I don't have any ideas for how any of this was carried out, all I have in mind is that it ended in Leviathan's Death and since one of the fundamental parts of reality that represented water and life died, the Deluge broke out to kill all life in a tidal wave of water. Think of it like Posiedon's Death in God of War 3. The water level rises and floods occur, killing anyone who could not evacuate. I imagine it to also be a time when it was Siren versus Siren too, since some would relate more to Behemoth than the other three. <br /> <br /> Anyways, with the Deluge breaking out and Behemoth still not having any of Leviathan's power, knowing the chaos erupting because of it, Ceto decided to go a step further and fill out the missing Leviathan's position her self. Behemoth, still mad with rage turns it onto Ceto. Ziz comes down, feeling that the laws it created were perverted and made useless, and with Ceto constructed a special barrier, created from the crushed hopes and dashed dreams of the lives that lived unfulfilled in Behemoth's recklessness. This barrier is known as &quot;The Song&quot;, and it was designed in mind not only to keep Behemoth at bay, but to also send out Ceto's plight for those who have the heart to survive even if all hope seems lost to join her in her quest.<br /> <br /> What else can be said? Echidna's story has a few additions. She believes that holding back Behemoth is futile, that the world is doomed no matter what. So she does something different. She decides instead that, if the apocalypse is gonna happen, then it's best to simply wait it out and survive it. Let the barrier fall and let Behemoth drown in the wake of the Deluge. And to do that....she tries to plunder and recreate the dead Leviathan's mutagenic powers, which to an extent is successful. However, she's still pretty mad and like a eugenics scientist, still trying to find what she can do to make the ultimate race to survive. Until then, she at least in part supports the Barrier remaining up, but when she finds the ultimate race, there's no question that she's going to withdraw her support.<br /> <br /> I also imagine more than a few game terms could benefit from this backstory. Their fuel stat &quot;Pneuma&quot; is literally &quot;divine breath&quot; and part of a human's soul. In a sense, it could be Ziz's divine laws in immaterial form that gives Sirens strength. And how they get it? From indulging in their love with a certain Human, bathing in a water from where they surfaced in or killing a person, they regain Pneuma because it serves as a reminder that their duties are being rewarded and thus are not in vain. Not to mention that the Siren's Ascended splat literally has to do with the wind/air and as such, could connect more wholesomely to being a part of Ziz's divine laws or upholding them more personally.<br /> <br /> And what of Behemoth? If I remember correctly Reaper, your idea was that Echidna spoke to Sirens in Maelstrom and the idea of Floodings and places filled with Resentment had growing animals and the like? As an idea, what if we shifted the Maelstrom chatting to being Behemoth's insane whispers, and the Floodings/Resentment places being tainted with Behemoth's hatred? For the former, Sirens are created from air, sea AND land and thus could get input from Behemoth. As for the latter, the seal that is the Song isn't perfect. There's sometimes a note that's dissonant, which gives a crack that Behemoth's power may slip through.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the long post, but what does everyone think of these ideas? It still needs to be fleshed out, but I feel it works with the Siren's backstory in a nutshell. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:41:49-08:00","id":842167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Made the Currents Document and starting with Buoyancy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sorry for triple posting, I've added this to the first post as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum