tly Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:06:49-08:00","id":845551,"title":"","content":"Hey, you're welcome, it's nice to work on something so fun. I liked the background idea. My only question is: Are &quot;The Three Monsters&quot; spirits, creatures that came before this earth (and if so, are they physical?) or Something entirely new?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:06:19-08:00","id":845669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=845551#post845551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, you're welcome, it's nice to work on something so fun. I liked the background idea. My only question is: Are &quot;The Three Monsters&quot; spirits, creatures that came before this earth (and if so, are they physical?) or Something entirely new?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd saaay that the answer could be left ambiguous so the ST can decide on what they are exactly. I'm willing to say that they're primordial beings, but I'm afraid that may cross over with Leviathan D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:16:44-08:00","id":846448,"title":"","content":"Just did a quick endgame playtest on the rules so far. It was epic. at the end, a Tropicana of the Current of Conflict needed to stop hundreds of Vodianois who were about to catch a Human who had inked in her skin (Blindspot, anyone?) a stanza to a Verse that allegedly could accelerate the Deluge. After the party took the girl to a safe place trough Area - City -Travel (A Clownfish Freshwater that fought like hell to stop the &quot;Black Sheep&quot; of the Party to just kill the girl and burn her body), the Tropicana stayed so He could do a last Sacrifice. He waited till all the Vodianoi got close and used Global - Earth - Destroy, So everything under them was at a breaking point and collapsed taking a portion of the city's Ghetto down with them. Everyone cheered. <br /> <br /> Now i'm going to sleep cause it's 3:30 am right now. Later I'll explain everything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T07:39:23-07:00","id":846560,"title":"","content":"Nice. :3 Sorry if the playtest didn't do so well due to not everything being fleshed out completely, but I hope it went well enough. How many players were there? Who was the ST? Were there any criticisms of the mechanics, good or bad? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T08:21:58-07:00","id":846574,"title":"","content":"Let's start, I was the ST, there were 3 players. Tropicana/Conflict, Freswater/Bouyancy, Vaporia/Wisdom. It was a simple one-shot game, they needed to Trace a event directly to a girl who had no memory whatsoever and had this glowing Music Score on her back. As soon they found out about the Girl, a group of vodianoi attacked. It all wnet worse when the whole city got infested by a Global - Emotion - Disturb effect that made everyone hate each other. Well, after that, they decided to plan a trap to the Vodianoi and created a Musical beacon that made every vodianoi of the city meet them at the Downtown, where the Earthquake scene happened.<br /> <br /> \u200bCritiscisms - The interpretation on the Verse became confusing at some points, because they had so many options. After a while I just compared The Verses to Creative Magic from Mage and all became clear. But we need to flesh out all the description and make a coherent list of words (i'll format everything).<br /> <br /> The tracing part I improvised, but they Liked. I made them go into the Deluge to the exact area where the girl lived and Traced her with a Int + Investigation Roll, the Vaporia had a excepcional sucess. But the tracing part need to be fleshed out because we have no concrete rules.<br /> <br /> They LOOOVED the idea of Stanzas being written down in a completely unknown language. They kept talking about making stanzas and all.<br /> <br /> besides that it was a short One-Shot, and nothing much happened. I'm working on a two session long game to work on the rest of the mechanics<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T08:33:10-07:00","id":846580,"title":"","content":"Alrighties. I think I should make the systems and advantages part of the game just so that there's something to refer to. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:45:53-07:00","id":846654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I instead revised the intro and did some things. Can anyone who's reading this please criticize it or tell me if any changes need to be made? I feel like they may be required, not to mention I am heavily borked from writing all of that. &gt;&lt;&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:37:59-07:00","id":847093,"title":"","content":"liked a lot the introduction. Suggested a few other paragraphs in the Gdoc, and added a section for myths and facts that I'll shortly expand<br /> <br /> \u200bhope thats not a problem, if it is feel free to delete everything. after you say everything is good to go i'll format ans post<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: I wonder what happened to our friend Reaper...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 03-14-2016, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:28:05-07:00","id":847177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=847093#post847093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">liked a lot the introduction. Suggested a few other paragraphs in the Gdoc, and added a section for myths and facts that I'll shortly expand<br /> <br /> \u200bhope thats not a problem, if it is feel free to delete everything. after you say everything is good to go i'll format ans post<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: I wonder what happened to our friend Reaper...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's still around. I checked his page and he's been on today. Unless he says anything it's prolly best to assume Life is intruding on him at the moment. Anyways, I think I'm going to start getting some mechanics written up for the Systems and Advantages so there's something to play with for games. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T14:44:39-07:00","id":847312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=847177#post847177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's still around. I checked his page and he's been on today. Unless he says anything it's prolly best to assume Life is intruding on him at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> From what has happened since my last post, I am intrigued by the idea of incorporating Leviathan, Behemoth, and Ziz into Siren, though I feel as if it does affect some of our earlier ideas. I feel that it might work easier if, rather than Leviathan being death, both Leviathan and Behemoth are bleeding out from Behemoth's conflict against Leviathan, causing the Deluges, the Floodings, the Furies, etc.<br /> <br /> When Behemoth manipulated humanity into turning against Leviathan, Leviathan was given a mortal blow and sank to the bottom of the ocean, its blood filling the ocean and inadvertantly causing the first Deluge to occur. This Deluge caused many human lives to be destroyed and motivated Ceto to take the place of Leviathan while they were indisposed. Behemoth, unsatisfied, attempted to launch a second attack, this time on Ceto, when Ziz decided to intervene and sing The Song in order to quell Behemoth's rage and protect Ceto. While this did break Behemoth's control on humanity, it did nothing to calm the already grieving and vengeful humans, leading to humanity's uprising against Behemoth. This time, Behemoth was given a mortal blow and it retreated into the wild where it laid down and began to petrify, turning into a great mountain. However, Behemoth's anger would not die down; its anger at humanity for having the gall to rise up against its creator filled its life-stream as its blood began to cascade down into the earth. From the Blood of the Behemoth came the Furies, aspects of nature warped by Behemoth's rage and inspired to go against humanity. <br /> <br /> The Blood of the Leviathan created the Deluges as an attempt to stop their failed offspring, a way to root out the issues and start from scratch. The Blood of the Behemoth created the Furies as an attempt to enact revenge against humanity, a last bout of anger unleashed onto the world. For Ceto, her love of humanity extends beyond the domain of both Leviathan and Behemoth. She wanted her children, the Sirens, to help protect humanity from the devastation of the Deluges and the wrath of the Furies as she attempts to effectively do &quot;damage control&quot; and stop the Blood of the Leviathan and the Blood of the Behemoth from exerting any more influence on the world. For Echidna, she views the Deluge and the Furies to be inevitabilities and feels that the best way to resolve this problem is to create a new species that can withstand the Deluges and defend themselves against the Furies. In order to do so, Echidna dived into the deepest abyss of the oceans and the great catacombs of the earth to partake in the Blood of the Leviathan and the Blood of the Behemoth. This gave her a mockery of both their abilities: a means to create life and a means to modify life. This allowed her to create the Vodianoi, mutated humans given shape from Behemoth and life from Leviathan. They are imperfect beings, maddened creatures forced into existence by an insane creator, but they are proof that there is a way to survive the Deluge and the Furies. Echidna whispers to Sirens, tempting them to her side where they are given a taste of Echidna's powers through Echidnal Alterations and turned into enforcers. They search the realm of humans for possible test subjects for Echidna while she experiments with her abilities and creates her brood of Vodianoi. While she is able to morph their bodies with Behemoth's power and breathe life back into them with Leviathan's power, there is still something lacking. There is something missing from this mad equation of hers that prevents her precious Vodianoi from coming into the world.<br /> <br /> Ziz.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I feel that the main thing is that the three beings, Leviathan, Behemoth, and Ziz, are more entwined with their own engagements to be too concerned with the well-being of humanity. Ceto is all for the well-being of humanity while Echidna could not give a damn about humanity. The mortal blows of both Leviathan and Behemoth changes that, creating the Deluges that threaten to consume all life and the Furies that thirst for the blood of humanity. Ziz, working only to maintain the laws of life onto the world, would now be allied with Ceto and her Sirens in an attempt to calm the Deluges and eliminate the Furies. Echidna is also attempting to fight back against the Deluges and the Furies but is working on her own terms, creating the Vodianoi in order to survive the two phenomena. This puts her at ends with Ceto, who is angered by Echidna's attempts to change humanity. However, some of Ceto's Sirens agree with Echidna's beliefs and have defected. This is not even including the Sirens who follow the Currents of Lethe, Styx, and Acheron who effectively follow their own set of rules. <br /> <br /> There are so many factions now that it's causing my head to spin. Hopefully, my input isn't too unclear.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised that we actually have a playtest in now. Of the mechanics, the Tracing mechanics should definitely be fleshed out. It's kinda vague out of necessity but should probably be set in stone at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:12:44-07:00","id":847491,"title":"","content":"I completely get your input. I apologize once more for I haven't discussed some of my own thoughts on the matter, but part of the reason I had thought up of a backstory is mainly to fill a few fluff plot holes. For example, what we have at the moment is Floodings, Resentment, Furies and Maelstrom, which I was hoping to find some way to explain them. I know you gave the one idea of Maelstrom being Echidna speaking to Sirens and telling them to get back at whoever triggered it, but it kinda didn't sit well with me. Her telling them to kill someone wouldn't feel fitting for her plans, she'd try driving them to her side or to do their job rather than lashing out at things.<br /> <br /> This is where the Three come in, as they feel like they could fill in those plotholes. Behemoth is angry and resentful of Leviathan for having an ability he never could wield. I put him as one of the founders for the Sirens to justify that whenever they're having a Maelstrom, it's all due to Behemoth whispering to their minds to kill whatever's stopping them. I also imagine him as the reason for places filled with Resentment and Floodings occuring, because they're places where the Song is weakest, his seal cracking and his will able to be more apparent on the world. Furies are probably people who are wholesomely part of the Earth as part of Behemoths manifested will beyond Resentment. Your explanation of Furies and places filled with Resentment going after humans nicely explains how they came into being (Behemoth's rage at humanity being manifested). <br /> <br /> As for Leviathan, I mostly had him in there to explain how the Deluge happened and perhaps serving as a sacrificial lion. To note, Leviathan did not die from just humanity turning against nature alone, Behemoth had control over the moving earth as well. He could make earthquakes and tsunamis (as they're underwater earthquakes) happen, volcanoes erupt to extinguish the sea, many other things as well. In short, Leviathan's death was meant to also show that just as humanity can end nature, it is plausible for nature to turn on itself and end itself. His sole ability to create new life also explains both why and how Echidna has mutagenic powers and the mentioned example of Behemoth being sealed away also gives a reason why she desires to make a new race out of humanity outside of &quot;lol random apocalypse&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finally, Ziz. To be honest, I felt he had to be there since he basically came with the package of Leviathan and Behemoth. He helps explain why the Song holds sway (maybe it's the manifestation of the laws he set upon the world magically set up) and how Ceto and Ziz are able to hold back Behemoth, I don't think that Ceto would have enough power to hold him back alone. Although I do like what you've said in that the one thing that Echidna lacks for her Vodianoi is something Ziz has. In my mind, Ziz is what gave intelligence and thought to things, and as a note, all Vodianoi are basically at the level of animals in mind. In this sense, having the ability to bestow intelligence (or rather, at least keep the intelligence intact) would prolly give some VERY huge steps to finishing Echidna's plans.<br /> <br /> __________<br /> In this sense, Leviathan is more akin to a dead god, and thus having little to do with the plot outside of Echidna trying to revive his mutagenic powers and/or use them for herself. Behemoth is behind most of the reason that the world is so doomed, his greedy actions creating resentment and outbursts of the Deluge on Earth. Heck, the backstory I'm writing up currently has Humanity going the same way that it kinda is in the WoD in terms of &quot;apocalypse happening&quot;, but the Three made the Sirens to deal with that. Behemoth's actions however messed up Sirens as a rule, hence why the WoD is considerably more doomed than the Earth in the Deluge is. Maybe the WoD is a timeline where the Three didn't exist and the only strands still connecting the two timelines is the Song itself?<br /> <br /> At the least, I don't imagine that the factions have really changed alot. It's still Currents (most Sirens + Ceto + Ziz) vs Echidna vs Abyssals vs Behemoth (and the Deluge in General). Also, we don't absolutely have to have all of the faction heads to be visited or physical beings in a game in case that's a bother. For example, let's think of it in these terms. Echidna is like the Queen of Tears/Judges of Duat/Kereberoi/True Fae in terms of appearance. She CAN appear as a character in a chronicle and can be interacted with, and can even have character stats. Ceto is like Luna/Exarchs/God Machine. She may appear in a chronicle/story once or twice, depending on how the plot demands, but otherwise stands as someone who remains in the background. Finally, people like Ziz, Behemoth and Leviathan? They're most likely people never to appear in casual play, mostly people as a part of the backstory whose relevance depends on the ST's whims.<br /> <br /> Anyways, pardon for the long winded post, and I must note that these are mostly ideas and feelings I had and they can be changed if so desired. Speaking of which, I read abit into Leviathan and noticed how they used abit of Ziz, Leviathan and Behemoth a bit already (I really skimmed but knowing they're there even in mentioning puts me off abit), so I've sent an email to the maker of Leviathan to see if there's any parts it does crossover or if we could still use them. And of course, if they're disliked we can throw them out all together. I'm willing to work with what is most wanted in the gameline. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T06:31:25-07:00","id":847651,"title":"","content":"I'm putting The rough first draft together, and as we add more information i'll edit. In The introduction i'm getting The &quot;introduction&quot; and The &quot;lexicon&quot; document togheter and adding more words. If any of you guys want me to add anything or correct or would simply like to give ideas to The introduction just say it or add on The introduction Gdocs as i'm constantly viewing it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:09:40-07:00","id":847660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=847651#post847651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm putting The rough first draft together, and as we add more information i'll edit. In The introduction i'm getting The &quot;introduction&quot; and The &quot;lexicon&quot; document togheter and adding more words. If any of you guys want me to add anything or correct or would simply like to give ideas to The introduction just say it or add on The introduction Gdocs as i'm constantly viewing it</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. If it's fine, I did do a few small edits of what you made, and I think something you posted was a really good idea. Renaming Aquatic form. You used Antediluvian Form, but &quot;Antediluvian&quot; means &quot;Before the Flood&quot;. Wouldn't it be more fitting to name it &quot;Diluvian Form&quot;? Also, I was wondering. Should there be any penalties to having Higher Akashic Record? I think one thing we can do is make the Refraction Dicepool smaller as Akashic Record rises. Let's say that a person is viewing a Siren with an Alteration on. They roll Wits + Composure to notice it, but depending on the Siren's Akashic Record there will be a special penalty applied to it. For example, at Akashic Record 1-2, there'd be a -5 penalty. 3-4, it'd be -4.5-6 and it's -3, 7-8 and it's -2 and finally 9-10 and it'd be -1 to the roll.<br /> <br /> Akashic Record also limits Attributes and Pneuma/Fuel Stat like normal Supernatural Advantage, but I also imagine that Alterations are also limited by Akashic Record as well. If so, how many Alterations can a Siren have at AR 1? I want to say that they can have AR + 3 Alterations (meaning at maximum of AR 10 they could only have 13), but that's just my own opinion. What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:24:14-07:00","id":847670,"title":"","content":"Nice. No probs on the Diluvian form. I like the idea of the Akashic Record penalties. Also feel like it should affect the Maelstrom. <br /> <br /> On ither note, we need to add the new conceots we created to the lexicon, i'll try to gather the ones left and post here so we define them.<br /> <br /> While writting the Myths and Facts i couldn't answer my on question so i decided to aks: Do Sirens becone Sea Foam when they die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T07:39:55-07:00","id":847682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=847670#post847670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. No probs on the Diluvian form. I like the idea of the Akashic Record penalties. Also feel like it should affect the Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> On ither note, we need to add the new conceots we created to the lexicon, i'll try to gather the ones left and post here so we define them.<br /> <br /> While writting the Myths and Facts i couldn't answer my on question so i decided to aks: Do Sirens becone Sea Foam when they die?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties, I'll check on how Death Rage and Frenzy functions for Vampires and Werewolves respectively since it's supposed to be similar to that. And it seems like they do on the last part. <br /> <br /> Reaper: &quot;If a Siren is ever to lose a body part while she is in her human form, she must find medical help immediately before the lost part dissolves into sea foam. Flesh cut off the Siren's body will only last for 1 hour when exposed to the air before it dissolves. If a Siren is decapitated, it's a done deal; the Siren's head dissolves into sea foam while the body is fresh for an hour. If the body part is placed on ice, however, it may last for several months. Some hunters that know of this capture Sirens and force them to live in a tank as they systematically cut off pieces of her body in order to steal away some of her longevity.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T16:57:37-07:00","id":847923,"title":"","content":"So&lt; I was thinking about something that I don't know if is needed to this game. Many splats have itens that have powers or something and during the playtest one of the players wondered what would happened if he brought a item from one of the possible futures from the Deluge. I couldn't answer, but my Idea is that Yes, and they would have power. One of the downside of the itens would be that if the future from where the item comes were to be dismantled then the item would also be dismantled. (that could bring interesting gameplay with players trying to assure the continuity of a future just so they could maintein the item). but I don't know, it's just not enough, so I decided to ask what you guys think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T21:01:12-07:00","id":847992,"title":"","content":"That certainly is plausible, but how would these items be like exactly? I'm lacking ideas at the moment, but what comes to mind is that the items are some lost codification of a Verse or something having to deal with a Verse (maybe each item is a physical form of a word of power) that helps with the use of Verses using the said item representing a word in it. Although this idea of mine feels abit unoriginal. What do other people have? The ideal of things from the mortal world that Ariel collected in her grotto feels like it could be something to use for these things.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm mostly finished with Systems and Advantages, but I need to list how Lucidity works. Does anyone have any ideas for how Lucidity should be like or sins in it? :3 And Backstory too.<br /> <br /> Backstory: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uaVZUrGdIszSjF7f-CSA_gv-h9oTV1rKupTu_Hr4iUw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Systems and Advantages: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dHPB-rGUo_ObHiCSzSkqhZYovEY56tKBBVwu2_i8eNw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Also, I had an idea for a possible Chorus. <br /> <br /> <b>The Freeshooters </b>are a gathering of Sirens in the Dark Wisdom Current who've acknowledged the usability of the Spirit world and the Denizens who live there. By using special Verses (Area-Spirit-Sense), Sirens are able to begin touching and seeing the invisible realm....but few are willing to deal with the selfish beings who live there. The Sirens in this Chorus however tend to deal with them more than any other Siren. The method of their power is deceptively simple. A Siren must first appease the spirit and get it's attention, after which she must do what she can to fill it's Essence pool for one day. If she completes this, then she gains the Fettered Condition [GMC 227] as the Spirit is now fettered to the Siren for the duration of the pact. The Siren is now free to ask any favors of the Spirit equal to her Akashic Record for whatever she desires so long as it's within the Spirit's capabilities. This includes asking it to use Numina and Influences, but they may not ask the Spirit to violate it's own Ban. However, one of these favors the Spirit may twist and use however or whenever the Spirit desires, usually when it would benefit best and almost always at a cost to the Siren who invoked the deal. Upon using up all favors, the Fettered Condition becomes automatically resolved and the Spirit is free to go on it's way.<br /> <br /> This Chorus is inspired ofc by the <b>Der Freischutz </b>opera (basically &quot;The Freeshooter&quot; in German) where a man made a deal with the devil for seven magical bullets that would hit wherever he desired, but the last one would be cursed by the devil and hit where he desired it to hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T05:20:37-07:00","id":848093,"title":"","content":"So, here\u2019s what I was thinking about the items (which I\u2019ll call Treasures, for now):<br /> <br /> Katana of the Dreadful Requiem<br /> <br /> In 2018, Mr. Flitzbreuer, an office worker with little to no accomplishments in his life, will kill a vampire.<br /> It will happen too fast. The vampire will enter the house of Mr. Flitzbreuer at late night expecting an easy meal and will find the Wife of Flitzbreuer, Nora, sleeping on the couch while watching tv with her 5 years old daughter. But something will go wrong, the vampire will have no intension to kill them, but a thirst so powerful will take care of him that he will not be able to hold his hand or his teeth. He will attack impetuously with a thirsty never seen before, he will then kill Wife and Daughter, blood-soaking all the living room, painting red the walls. <br /> Mr. Flitzbreuer will arrive late that night, enough to only find the corpses of his wife and daughter on the floors along the house. And a man standing still in the middle of the room. Spooked, Mr. Flitzbreuer will hold on to the decorative katana he once bought in a travel to chinatown. The vampire will fall to his knees, begging to be killed, the man will answer to his prayers and will cut the vampire body with a rage that he wouldn\u2019t thought possible. <br /> Crazy, the man will throw the katana away and will run, run for how long God knows, until his name become a whisper in the dark.<br /> <br /> Treasure\u2019s Appearence: The katana looks like a common katana found in a chinese shop or gift shop, it\u2019s blade is not reground anymore and the hilt is covered in leather... at least for a human. For a Siren the blade is centuries old with a red glimmer of blood.<br /> <br /> Treasure\u2019s Power: The Katana can emulate the Stanza \u201cRequiem for my Valentine\u201d, This causes extra damage in a Vampire as if the Katana always sang the [Touch]-[Vampire]-[Destroy] Verse.<br /> <br /> Conditions for existence:<br /> <br /> -Mr. Flitzbreuer and his family must be alive until October 2018<br /> - The Vampire must have Humanity 8 by the time of the attack<br /> -Mr. Flitzbreuer must buy the Katana at Chinatown in February 2016","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T05:52:14-07:00","id":848099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=848093#post848093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here\u2019s what I was thinking about the items (which I\u2019ll call Treasures, for now):</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I like how these sound, but I'll wait until Reaper has his say on it. IT does sound fitting. As a small notion though, I think that there shouldn't be a word directly translating to &quot;Vampire&quot;, but they can be implied/specified in the Opuses used. For example, &quot;Touch-Death-Blood-Destroy&quot; for vampires. If I may also ask, how does the Systems and Advantages look? I kinda expanded Refraction to cover doing Verses in a manner that they're obviously supernatural invoking Refraction. There's also ways to spend and regain Pneuma that I wonder if people like or dislike too. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:03:46-07:00","id":848105,"title":"","content":"I liked how pneuma conected to willpower in metohds of taking. I found all The writting pleasing and nice. And although I have no notions of mechanics I think The advantages are balanced and coherent.<br /> <br /> For a idea: How about we tweak The retainer merit so we could have a merit that represent The loving ones (and thus source of pneuma) of a Siren? The more dots more pneuma she can regains whenever she spends a given time with them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:30:48-07:00","id":848337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=848105#post848105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked how pneuma conected to willpower in metohds of taking. I found all The writting pleasing and nice. And although I have no notions of mechanics I think The advantages are balanced and coherent.<br /> <br /> For a idea: How about we tweak The retainer merit so we could have a merit that represent The loving ones (and thus source of pneuma) of a Siren? The more dots more pneuma she can regains whenever she spends a given time with them</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If they eat off pieces of the human soul, then something needs to be there to represent the harm onto the human. Speaking of which, I'm way ahead of you on the second notion. Here's some merits I came up with in school today, enjoy. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xRA_GYddwXqrH1pTKOeLQj6swAnw5BMLh-8fBhkwBGE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xRA_GYddwXqrH1pTKOeLQj6swAnw5BMLh-8fBhkwBGE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xRA_GYddwXqrH1pTKOeLQj6swAnw5BMLh-8fBhkwBGE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xRA_GYddwXqrH1pTKOeLQj6swAnw5BMLh-8fBhkwBGE/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T14:29:42-07:00","id":849454,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, sorry for double posting, but I've gotten finished with Lucidity and filled out quite a few conditions for them. Comments are welcomed. If I may ask, what do you guys think a Lucidity 0 Siren should be like? Furthermore, I got confirmation from Kings (the current Leviathan writer). Behemoth, Ziz and Leviathan are indeed in Leviathan the Tempest, but he said we were free to use them. What do you guys rule? I'm fine with throwing out the backstory I made out of respect for Kings and Leviathan the Tempest. Plus, we still do have that one idea of the Chronos story from the beginning I think. I will post these links onto the first post as well. :3 <br /> <br /> Systems and Advantages: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dHPB-rGUo_ObHiCSzSkqhZYovEY56tKBBVwu2_i8eNw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Conditions: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nh62Lgt_318WJ26AT8zdc7pIW44xA08JS-WzBEUPVGs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T07:06:52-07:00","id":852398,"title":"","content":"Pardon the triple post. I've gotten done with writing up the Currents of Conflict and Harmony and I wanted to give an update. I've also edited the Currents between an introductory paragraph and a history paragraph. I've also did abit of editing to Pneuma on Systems and Advantages to make the willpower loss more apparent rather than taking just one willpower every time. It now takes up to half the successes the Siren received on the roll for harvesting Pneuma, and it can eat up Permanent Willpower dots too. I've also edited the Relationships to give up to Dots in the Relationship Merit * 2 for a dicepool to give Pneuma. And I'll be doing the Current of Healing which shall be coming up soon. <br /> <br /> Currents: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> The question still stands on whether we should redo the backstory or no. Flood mythology is used world over, usually it's a story of some heavenly force wiping everything away because it was all corrupt. People, nature, everything. I imagine we can use this as a general outline, now all that's left is filling up the spots. What I have in mind for sure is that Echidna, her Sirens and perhaps her first Vodianoi are made up of people who survived the Deluge and are mad as hell at whoever caused it (I'm currently musing on Ceto being one of the causes for the Deluge, although she does genuinely want humanity to survive. Maybe she made Sirens as a response to the Deluge's coming?). Echidna's love extends over humanity, but it's a selfish love that doesn't take into consideration on whether the people she makes into Vodianoi are happy or not with how they are, she does what she thinks is best for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T03:20:32-07:00","id":853416,"title":"","content":"Just throwing in my support! I appreciate the basic gist of what this game wants to accomplish, even if I find it difficult to navigate through the information to get a better grasp of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T18:27:06-07:00","id":853782,"title":"","content":"Formatting the Introduction as I write. I noticed that a few concepts are not in the Lexicon (Grottos, Furies, Treasures, and a few others) and cannot find anything related to Sources and Inspirations. There are any or should I not care about these?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the Pdf that I'm going to post is not the final one, we can still add and edit, after every retweak i'll update the Pdf till we have Final chapters that I'll put together to form the Corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 03-26-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T19:35:00-07:00","id":853816,"title":"","content":"Sorry for double posting but here is the early PDF from the Introductory chapter. It comprises the Introduction Gdoc and the Lexicon Gdoc of Saulothe with additions from myself. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3dg8R2JqoV1NzRkejVMQWNwdEk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Introduction</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:09:11-07:00","id":853867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=853416#post853416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just throwing in my support! I appreciate the basic gist of what this game wants to accomplish, even if I find it difficult to navigate through the information to get a better grasp of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much, we appreciate it alot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If it helps, I've edited all of the google documents onto the first post to make navigation easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=853782#post853782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Formatting the Introduction as I write. I noticed that a few concepts are not in the Lexicon (Grottos, Furies, Treasures, and a few others) and cannot find anything related to Sources and Inspirations. There are any or should I not care about these?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the Pdf that I'm going to post is not the final one, we can still add and edit, after every retweak i'll update the Pdf till we have Final chapters that I'll put together to form the Corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's mostly my own fault when it comes to a few entries missing. I forgot to set them into the Lexicon Link, I'll edit them in right now. Although speaking of them, I feel like sooner or later we'll need to talk about how the Deluge is as an alternate realm, how to navigate through it, what's there of interest that can be of use to Sirens and what can be used there to make as part of a story. Grottos and Treasures are just the tip of the Iceberg, and as far as we have in our things, the Deluge appears like reality does, except submerged underwater with places looking damaged by water and (from a passing comment on the original thread) people walking appearing like drowned corpses. What else should we have as a part of them that makes it a place for Sirens to enter? The best that comes to mind is that the ability to Trace is much easier in the Deluge than in Reality. As well, I also imagine that the Deluge can serve as a refuge for the Sirens willing to live in it, as of now the Diluvian form's transformation is indefinite. <br /> <br /> We should also probably work out the Resentment and Floodings, and Furies as a result. To spitball for this, how about we call these places as &quot;Quagmires&quot; (which means both &quot;wetlands&quot; and &quot;awkward situations&quot;). I still feel like we need to choose out what the backstory would be like before we do this, so that we don't have a headache trying to connect the dots later. But so far, my ideas on Quagmires that we've all had so far: They're places where Nature takes vengeance for whatever is carried out against it. I imagine that Resentment is something that can build up or be released, so I imagine it could be like &quot;Healthboxes&quot; for how many they have. I imagine they have Temporary Resentment and Permanent Resentment. They can spend Temporary Resentment to boost animals or fill things with rage, and perhaps Permanent Resentment can be spent to make Floodings occur. I also imagine that Quagmires are more akin to Genius Loci, with their living manifestations being the Furies themselves. <br /> <br /> Out of fear of TL;DR, I'll make an alternate backstory document. I'm still sort of waiting for any note on if we should change the backstory or not from people. D: <br /> <br /> Otherwise, you've done a perfect job as always with making this into a PDF. I greatly appreciate it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T12:49:57-07:00","id":856663,"title":"","content":"Eugh. I feel as if I haven't checked in for a while. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of Sirens having their own item-subtype. It's also interesting that the Treasures are effectively magic wands from Dungeons &amp; Dragons, which I don't believe has been approached yet in any splat. I do feel like there should also be a Treasure subtype known as Trinkets or something similar that offer a less substantial power. A possible Trinket could be a music box that always plays a different tune when opened and offers a point of Pneuma to the Siren that first opens it during that lunar rotation.<br /> <br /> For the backstory, I think the main issue is that we keep coming up with good ideas that are muddling the main structure of the narrative. We had a basic frame with Ceto and Echidna being opposing sides of the same coin fighting against this cosmic force known as The Deluge. Then we added in the Furies, the Breathless, and the Banshees that operate on their own agenda, which is fine and helped create this sort of network of alliances. And then we added in the idea of Behemoth, Leviathan, and Ziz which needed to be worked into the narrative in some way, shape, or form. And then we have the Sirens, who were once human but discovered their nature due to a mystical sensation of Drowning allowing them to awaken their powers. And then there's the Vodianoi, who are once-human creations of Echidna. And then there's the Flensers who are hunting down the Sirens for their longevity-increasing flesh.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> I think we need to approach the main concept behind the backstory to Siren, namely Ceto, Echidna, and The Deluge. Without the names that relate to a culture, Ceto effectively becomes the Mother of Sirens while Echidna becomes the Mother of the Vodianoi. They are the Open Palm and the Closed Fist who seek to protect humanity from one great force: The Deluge.<br /> <br /> A) Originally, The Deluge was a major &quot;The End&quot; force that wiped out humanity several decades in the future, which awakened Ceto and Echidna and inspired them to travel back in time to turn others into Sirens in order to prevent this Deluge from occurring.<br /> <br /> B) This was changed to avoid comparisons to the Armageddon that was Gehenna in WoD (the original World of Darkness), so it became a reoccuring &quot;Reset&quot; button that reverted humanity and civilization back to its root components. Isolated cases were Floodings. We also brought up the idea of the Furies, who acted alongside the Floodings as a means to take revenge on humanity for their pride. This ended up creating an unnamed being that I'm going to call &quot;Gaia&quot; for brevity's sake. The Deluge was Gaia's attempt to reset the world to a point where she could recover all the damage that was done to the world and start anew, effectively giving humanity a second chance. There is no saying as to how many times The Deluge succeeded, but it is implied that this is not the first time that the world was flooded.<br /> <br /> C) This third iteration of the backstory involves three beings: Behemoth, Leviathan, and Ziz. This one plays up the ideas of factions and war by having Leviathan rule over the sea and having Behemoth rule over the land while Ziz is the divine arbitrator who encourages the world to exist in balance. This also introduces the idea that there is a backstory to all humanity, as Leviathan created humanity while Behemoth shaped them. As well, this also introduces a reason as to why the first Sirens came to be in the world as they were humans that allied themselves to Ceto and were changed to become Sirens. The war between Behemoth and Leviathan explains The Deluge as something that is not due to &quot;Gaia&quot; but due to the death of Leviathan causing the first destructive waves. <br /> <br /> The third iteration is the most developed and offers great explanations as to why and what things are in the Siren universe. However, it feels as if it steps on the toes of some of the other gamelines by establishing several ideas. It also is a bit mythical, as in it's established as being so far in the past that most of it could be embellishments and exaggerations made to fill in missing information by Sirens as the ages went by. <br /> <br /> <b>Of things that are clearly Things (as in Sirens are 100% positive that these things exist through experience): </b>The Sirens that exist now were awakened from mortal humans who had no knowledge of what Sirens were. They became who they are now because of The Song, a life-changing melody that helped a Siren Surface while she was Drowning. The &quot;Ceto&quot; being created Sirens in order to prevent the devastation that is The Deluge and the Floodings that occur in its wake. The &quot;Echidna&quot; being is also attempting to prevent the devastation of The Deluge by creating Vodianoi off of the humans. The Sirens are &quot;supposed&quot; to be on the side of humanity, so they are to act as protectorates while figuring out ways to prevent the Floodings. There are also the Quagmires, areas that seek to harm humanity, similar to the Floodings. The Quagmires may cause harm themselves or they may alter the surrounding wildlife to become Furies, creatures that seek out humanity and desire to harm them. There are also the Banshees: Sirens that ended up &quot;drowning&quot; before they Surfaced as Sirens. The Banshees are starved of Pneuma and seek out humans in order to steal their lifeforce in order to fill the void that exists within themselves. The Breathless are Sirens that Surfaced without hearing The Song, preventing them from becoming Sirens. They become voids to the Sirens, preventing them from using Verses and removing themselves from a Siren's ability to sense The Song within others. And then there are the Flensers, hunters that seek to gain longevity by harvesting the body parts of Sirens and consuming them.<br /> <br /> <b>Of things that might be Things (as in Sirens would know this through word of mouth, possibly from Ceto or Echidna's mouth): </b>The story of Behemoth, Leviathan, and Ziz as well as the creation of humanity and Sirens. The story behind The Deluge's existence and the possibility of there being a &quot;Gaia&quot; being who created Quagmires and Floodings. The possibility that The Deluge may have happened before and wiped out all of civilization once before. The possibility of Sirens becoming Ascendants and becoming one with the sky. <br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> I think that the backstory of Siren would benefit by giving Sirens <i>just enough</i> for them to be okay with being a Siren and knowing what a Siren's duty is; as long as we can justify why a Siren exists, that should be enough to suspend disbelief and allow us some wiggle-room in terms of actual lore. Like with Changelings. Changlings know that they were human and they know that they were changed because of their time in Arcadia with the True Fae. Or with Sin-Eaters, who know that they were supposed to die but ended up making a deal with a Geist and surviving. Or with Beasts, who had reoccurring nightmares about monsters before accepting the monster as themselves.<br /> <br /> Sirens, when they were mortals, we bogged down by emotional baggage or terrible circumstances, feeling as if they were being held down underwater. Eventually, this process became too overwhelming and the mortal ended up feeling as if they were Drowning, dragged into the undertow by grasping hands and forced to struggle. Then, they heard The Song which filled them up with the will to live and allowed them to Surface. This has all been said before but the big change is that the mortal, when they metaphorically Surface, finds themselves brought into The Deluge (I think we renamed the Realm as something else, didn't we? Isn't it something like the Celestial Ocean now?) where their body has changed into their Diluvian Form and they are allowed a glimpse into the world of the Sirens. They may even hear the voice of Ceto or Echidna calling out to them. Afterwards, they are awakened from their vision and are brought back to the material realm. They are different, changed. They may attempt to push off that episode as just a hallucination, but they know something is different about themselves. They are even more certain when they realize that they can sense others who have gone through the same process (the ability to sense other Sirens through their Akashic Record stat, that is also still a Thing, right?).<br /> <br /> From there, a Siren begins to learn about Ceto, Echidna, The Deluge, and their role in the world as a Siren (the things that are clearly Things). As for things that might be Things, Sirens may come across possible theories as to why and how they came to be. One such theory points to a trinity of creatures: Behemoth, Leviathan, and Ziz, that helped create the world and humanity. A war between two of the creatures ended up causing The Deluge. Another points to a sister-being to Ceto, a &quot;Gaia&quot; being who has become resentful of humanity and seeks to reset her once-beautiful world so that she can start again. Some Sirens may find themselves speaking to a hybrid-being like themselves who speak of Luna and a Father Wolf, comparing their Luna to Ceto. Other Sirens may find creatures of dreams and hunger talking about their Dark Mother and making comparisons to Echidna. There may be right answers; there may be wrong answers. Sirens may never know what the truth is but it doesn't keep them from trying to search for the answer. <br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr: </b>Ceto and Echidna are real while everything else is purposefully vague for the purpose of storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T15:57:46-07:00","id":856753,"title":"","content":"I see. Thank you for the post Reaper. And don't worry, we know you read even if you don't comment on it.<br /> <br /> I like your ideas on how to deal with the backstory and feel they are the best to use. I don't believe we did fully rename the &quot;drowned version of reality that Sirens come to when they drown and can casually interact with&quot;. However, I feel that we can say that &quot;The Deluge&quot; refers to the apocalypse that will happen, and &quot;Celestial Ocean&quot; refers to the drowned reality where it has already been done and where Echidna and Ceto are. <br /> <br /> Also, I finished up all the currents! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Enjoy~<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1go6cG6UeSK0ybu0xkMSGQiIwe2bwqgh7uZ9Bkxmhdu0/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:07:00-07:00","id":856806,"title":"","content":"Sweet awesomeness. We've got most of the character creation up to speed.<br /> <br /> So, Tracing. We don't really have any concrete rules for that aside from interpretation, which is sorta a safety net during this playtesting period. As for what we have right now, Sirens can spend a point of Pneuma to ask a question and begin Tracing, which effectively creates a vision of what is being Traced and runs through it as if it were a cassette tape that can be rewound and played at any time. Each Current affects the Tracing by allowing a Siren of that Current to focus on certain details or sift through anything that is making the scene unclear.<br /> <br /> The Dice Pool that Yads Dom came up with is Int + Investigation, so let's say that Int + Investigation is the base Dice Pool for Tracing. How about this: when a Siren asks her question and begins Tracing, she effectively creates a 3D snapshot of the scene at a moment that would offer some answer to her question. For each success, the Siren can refine this snapshot by adding a timeline to it, expanding the overall area the snapshot holds, focusing on subjects within this snapshot, or eliminating extraneous noise that clogs up the Trace. Each Current has their own specialty that effectively gives the Siren a free point in one of these refinements, so some Sirens are better at Tracing certain scenes.<br /> <br /> Let's say that the initial parameters for a Trace goes as follows: <b>The Time of the Trace</b> is suspended, meaning that it is a single moment or frame in time. <b>The Area of the Trace</b> is roughly a room if indoors or a distinct stretch of land (such as a street's length between two other streets) if outdoors. <b>The Focus of the Trace</b> is blurry unless the Siren that is Tracing already knows pertinent facts about the scene such as the individuals within the scene or the rough time. <b>The Noise of the Trace</b> varies between scenes depending on the number of individuals, the quality of the weather, etc; it is the extra details that exist within the scene that do not serve to answer the question that the Siren asked. Sirens may spend a success on their Tracing roll to increase these parameters by an amount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 800px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Condition</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Time</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Area</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Focus</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Noise</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Initial</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Snapshot, a single frame that describes the answer to the question</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Indoors</b>: one room<br /> <b>Outdoors</b>: a distinct area (around a landmark, street, etc.)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Blurry unless the Siren knows certain aspects in the scene</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Varies</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+1 success</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">15 minutes, roughly 7.5 minutes before and after the snapshot</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Indoors</b>: any adjacent room<br /> <b>Outdoors</b>: a block</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Allows for one subject to be detailed, a Size 4+ object and anything on/within it</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Removes an instance of clutter, mess, or dust</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+2 successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 hour, 30 minutes before and after the snapshot</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Indoors</b>: the entire building<br /> <b>Outdoors</b>: a district</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Allows for one category of object to be detailed (humanoid, documents, cars, etc.)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Removes obstructions like curtains that hide signs</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+3 successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">A division of 4 hours, malleable as long as the snapshot is within it</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Indoors</b>: the plot of land a building is on<br /> <b>Outdoors</b>: a city</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Allows for any object within the Area to be detailed</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Removes an instance of debris, crowds, sounds, etc.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+4 successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">A 24-hour period; malleable as long as the snapshot is within it</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Indoors</b>: the surrounding neighborhood<br /> <b>Outdoors</b>: a county or region</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Provides information that the Siren would normally be unable to infer (the personal history of objects)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Removes all instances of smoke, fire, weather, etc.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+5 successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">A full week; malleable as long as the snapshot is within it</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Indoors</b>: an entire city<br /> <b>Outdoors</b>: a state or country, depending on location</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Allows the Siren to interact with the scene, opening drawers or accessing computers</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Removes anything that does not pertain to the question asked</td> </tr> </table></div> Say that Morgan, a Polarian of Wisdom, wants to find out what happened the moment before a shooting occurred. He is on the site of the shooting and asks the question &quot;How did this all start?&quot; He begins Tracing and envisions the scene: he sees the victim under the streetlight as a blurry figure walks out from an alleyway and points a gun at them. The vision is dark as midnight and is utterly quiet, something that has been assumed from what the police report stated. As a Polarian of Wisdom, Morgan is able to pull out the details from a scene and chooses to focus on the shooter. The blurry figure begins to take shape within the scene, becoming a woman, roughly in her late 30s, wielding a silenced pistol in her hands. She's wearing rather plain clothes, a shirt that has seen its fair share of better days and jeans that have been worn down into fraying threads. Disposable and unassuming. That is as much as Morgan's Current bonus will give him so he begins his roll. His Intelligence is 3 and his Investigation is 2, so he rolls 5 dice and ends up with 2 successes. He decides that, while he knows what the shooter looks like, he doesn't know how it began. He spends one of his successes to expand the timeline. The vision begins to animate, playing through roughly 15 minutes worth of time. Within that amount of time, he sees the victim on his phone, talking about waiting to be picked up. Morgan also sees the shooter on their phone during that time, listening intently without response. As the victim gets off their phone, they turn towards the victim and becomes shocked, as if they recognized the shooter. The gun fires and the victim goes down. The shooter leaves the scene through the alleyway and disappears into the void. Morgan decides to spend his last success to expand the area of the Trace, extending it from the one street that leads into alleyways to a rough, block-sized area. The scene plays as usual but Morgan decides to focus on the alleyway that the shooter came from. Because the vision is represented as a 3-dimensional snapshot in his mind, Morgan walks his consciousness down the alleyway and discovers a car parked on the other side of the buildings that separate the street. He hears the gunshot and sees the shooter running in his direction. The car door opens to reveal a shadowy figure at the wheel alongside a passenger. The shooter jumps in and the car speeds off. Morgan is unable to distinctly recognize the license plate or the make of the car, only recognizing the number of people and the general size and color of the car. Reviewing the scene, Morgan decides that he has as much information as he can muster and releases the Trace.<br /> <br /> Sirens are also able to share their Traces with other Sirens. The number of extra Sirens that can view a Trace is equal to the Tracing Siren's Akashic Records. Any additional Siren in the Trace can use their Current bonus to refine the Trace but only the Tracing Siren may spend successes to refine the Trace.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Hopefully, this should be a suitable prototype for the Tracing mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1417,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","user":"Reaper Verse","date":".  Formatting. :V 03-31-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:44:58-07:00","id":856829,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Although there's still technically 7 factions I need to get to writing up. The Abyssal Currents, the Castaways and the Echidnal Sirens. I love how the Tracing looks, you did a good job. Is it possible to do it as an extended roll perchance? The limit of rolls being the Sirens Intelligence + Investigation, and being able to spend successes on whatever aspects the Siren desires? And if so, how much time should be between the rolls?<br /> <br /> As well, where should I put it in the documents? Should it be in Systems and Advantages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:25:22-07:00","id":856862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=856829#post856829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. Although there's still technically 7 factions I need to get to writing up. The Abyssal Currents, the Castaways and the Echidnal Sirens. I love how the Tracing looks, you did a good job. Is it possible to do it as an extended roll perchance? The limit of rolls being the Sirens Intelligence + Investigation, and being able to spend successes on whatever aspects the Siren desires? And if so, how much time should be between the rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...The main thing that would make an Extended Action undesirable is that Extended Actions are meant to eventually &quot;succeed&quot;. They open a lock or uncover a buried treasure; there is some sort of end goal. With Tracing, it's more of an interpretation. There isn't really an end goal other than &quot;What is the answer?&quot; and there isn't an exact answer to an interpretation. The end goal is also set as a number of successes that you're supposed to reach over a period of time. That number, as written in the CofD, goes from 5 to 20. I think it may be better to have Tracing function as an Instant Action so that Sirens can't just wait out a solution. If it becomes an Extended Action, it could just be used as a &quot;Solve this Plot Point&quot; ability, which is useful but kinda boring.<br /> <br /> But as a way to incorporate this, I would suggest the idea that a scene can be Traced several times before becoming &quot;Overexposed&quot; and untraceable. Each additional Trace on a scene adds a -2 penalty to the Dice Pool and a Failure causes the scene to become Overexposed. Given that the maximum possible feasible Dice Pool is 10 (if you put all your points in Int and Investigation), I think that should be a fair amount. Beginning Sirens who are more well-rounded would probably have a Dice Pool between 4-6, which means that a scene can be Traced maybe once or twice over before becoming Overexposed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As well, where should I put it in the documents? Should it be in Systems and Advantages? </div> </div> </div>I think it should go in Systems and Advantages. It's something that is pretty much a core aspect to Sirens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T20:00:00-07:00","id":856883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=856862#post856862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...The main thing that would make an Extended Action undesirable is that Extended Actions are meant to eventually &quot;succeed&quot;. They open a lock or uncover a buried treasure; there is some sort of end goal. With Tracing, it's more of an interpretation. There isn't really an end goal other than &quot;What is the answer?&quot; and there isn't an exact answer to an interpretation. The end goal is also set as a number of successes that you're supposed to reach over a period of time. That number, as written in the CofD, goes from 5 to 20. I think it may be better to have Tracing function as an Instant Action so that Sirens can't just wait out a solution. If it becomes an Extended Action, it could just be used as a &quot;Solve this Plot Point&quot; ability, which is useful but kinda boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there have been several examples in the past of Extended rolls being done without them being meant as &quot;how to get to the end point&quot; and more of &quot;how to keep going past the end point to make things greater&quot;. For example, 1e Changeling Contracts that caused some weather effect that was only made greater by going past the required successes. Verdant Spring is the best example. The second Clause's base effects is to create rain. 5 Suxx creates a light rain, but a Changeling can go further up to 25 suxx, which makes a deluge that causes flooding. One rule of 1e Spellcasting in Mage is that most of the spells can be done as Extended and roll past it even if it hits the threshold. Mage in particular is a good example of where the successes can be spent on different things, kind of like how Tracing is done.<br /> <br /> I'd say that a Siren is limited by their dicepools, the location they're Tracing at and how much Pneuma they're wanting to spend to make the rolls. They would need to spend their successes if they desired to get greater odds in seeing the past as it truly was or to get as much as they desire to know about. Granted, making it extended could easily solve problems, might I perhaps suggest that, if Tracing is done as an Extended action, a small precaution we can take is making each additional roll beyond the first requiring 1 Pneuma to do? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=856862#post856862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as a way to incorporate this, I would suggest the idea that a scene can be Traced several times before becoming &quot;Overexposed&quot; and untraceable. Each additional Trace on a scene adds a -2 penalty to the Dice Pool and a Failure causes the scene to become Overexposed. Given that the maximum possible feasible Dice Pool is 10 (if you put all your points in Int and Investigation), I think that should be a fair amount. Beginning Sirens who are more well-rounded would probably have a Dice Pool between 4-6, which means that a scene can be Traced maybe once or twice over before becoming Overexposed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good. :3 If I may still note, there is the chance of some Sirens (especially elders) having Akashic Record 6+, beginning to allow them to have 11-20 dice pools if they raised their attributes/skills that high. Although I think you were referring to normal/beginning Sirens, to which I say that's fine.<br /> <br /> I wonder, given how Tracing is. Is it possible for Sirens to, instead of Tracing the past to Trace the future? I mean, there is a small bit of the theme being &quot;things that have happened in the past are doomed to happen again&quot; as well as a small bit of talk about Sirens being oracular in nature, which includes more foresight rather than hindsight.<br /> <br /> I also apologize for not remarking on something earlier, but I like the idea of Trinkets. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:51:21-07:00","id":856948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=856883#post856883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that a Siren is limited by their dicepools, the location they're Tracing at and how much Pneuma they're wanting to spend to make the rolls. They would need to spend their successes if they desired to get greater odds in seeing the past as it truly was or to get as much as they desire to know about. Granted, making it extended could easily solve problems, might I perhaps suggest that, if Tracing is done as an Extended action, a small precaution we can take is making each additional roll beyond the first requiring 1 Pneuma to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, I would say that Sirens could be able to Trace as an Extended Action as long as they are within the Celestial Ocean. This allows the Siren to access the timelessness that is the Celestial Ocean which allows them the time and ability to Trace beyond what is possible. However, I would say that this would also Overexpose the scene so its mainly used when the Sirens are sure that they have as much evidence as they need when it comes to solving the issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder, given how Tracing is. Is it possible for Sirens to, instead of Tracing the past to Trace the future? I mean, there is a small bit of the theme being &quot;things that have happened in the past are doomed to happen again&quot; as well as a small bit of talk about Sirens being oracular in nature, which includes more foresight rather than hindsight. </div> </div> </div>Hmm...I think, in the Siren-universe, it has come across many times in discussion and that at least several Sirens have attempted to Trace forward. Attempts to Trace forward in the material realm ended with massive headaches and exhaustion while attempts made in the Celestial Ocean are more relaxing. However, no results have shown up from these experiments. Not even the madness of the Discordians has given them the insight needed to see the future, nor has the influence of Echidna granted her Sirens the gift of prophecy.<br /> <br /> And yet, Sirens have been able to take a glimpse into the future.<br /> <br /> Although a Siren cannot Trace into the future (within the Celestial Ocean or not), she may be able to have visions of the future while she is residing within the Celestial Ocean. I would say that the Storyteller should secretly roll a Siren's Lucidity in an Extended Roll. Once these secret rolls accumulate a certain amount of successes, the Siren is granted a vision of the future. The vision may be vague or confusing, but it grants the Siren some sort of insight into their future. Presumably, this should either reveal an important plot point or it could grant a condition that grants the Siren a +1 bonus to rolls that are made towards some sort of agenda. The downside to this process is that the Siren's presence within the Celestial Ocean becomes known to the patrolling Echidnal Sirens. It's a risk vs. reward system of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:56:27-07:00","id":857077,"title":"","content":"Great ideas! I'm liking the tracing ideas and liked the trinkets one too!<br /> <br /> Well, let me att. you guys with what I'm working on over the Structure of the &quot;Corebook&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b>Introduction (80%)</b><br /> <b>- How to Use this Book (Almost Done)</b><br /> <b>- Theme and Mood (Done)</b><br /> <b>- Facts and Fiction (Done)</b><br /> <b>- Sources and Inspirations <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">(Not Done, would like you guys to help out on this)</span></b><br /> <b>- Lexicon (Almost Done, Needing writing for: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Floodings, Furies, Celestial Ocean, Trinkets, Treasures, Grottos</span>, etc...)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1 - (50%)</b><br /> <b>- Common Knowledge and Simple Descriptions over the main features of being a Siren. i.e: Trace, The Deluge. the closest to a Backstory that we can provide. (Partly Written)</b><br /> <b>- Akashic Record Write-up and Merits, Lucidity explanation.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 2 - (60%)</b><br /> <b>- Currents (Lovely Written)</b><br /> <b>- Waters (Writen)</b><br /> <b>- Diluvean Form creation (Almost)</b><br /> <b>- (?)Abyssal Currents (?)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 3 - (50%)</b><br /> <b>- System and Advantages (Being Written)</b><br /> <b>- Examples of Treasures and Trinkets</b><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 4 - (10%)</b><br /> <b>- Antagonists</b><br /> <b>- Flensers</b><br /> <b>- Abyssal and Echidnal Currents</b><br /> <b>- Vodianoi and Furies</b><br /> <br /> <b>Appendix 1 - Only if you guys want</b><br /> <b>- Story Hooks </b><br /> <b>- Drowned City</b><br /> <b>- Character sheets anf such.</b><br /> <br /> \u200bI'm Looking for criticismo and Ideas ^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","user":"Yads Dom","date":". 04-01-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T10:57:16-07:00","id":857193,"title":"","content":"Thank you Yads. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd say that when it comes to the Sources and Inspirations, Reaper provided a good list on what I think is one of the first posts he made in the thread. He did on the 42nd post. It really is the meaning of life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784572#post784572\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784572#post784572\"> Siren: The Surfacing (nWoD Abandoned Fangame Resurrection) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784572#post784572\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=784572#post784572 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hello everyone, I've been lurking on these forums and the RPG.net forums abit and loved how ideas for fangames were blossoming at these places, so if it's ok, I've </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As well, I've added the terms you've specified to the Lexicon and abit more. Sorry for forgetting to add until now.<br /> Lexicon Doc: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aDfvgZKcEUyieGuDiAK5I7xE776xqjjlyW7GdrS_5i0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> As for other things, I would suggest that the Abyssal Currents are kept within the Antagonists chapter, and the Echidnal Current and Vodianoi are put together into one section, with the Echidnal Alterations/Malformations in the same part too. Quagmires and Furies should have a section in the Antagonists part. I also believe that the section for the Verses and Alterations should be set into Chapter 3 (since they weren't listed at all).<br /> <br /> I believe we should have the Appendix 1. Most gamelines have a City where it shows a good example of the gamelines problems that they're trying to fix. For example, Princess the Hopeful has Detroit Michigan as a &quot;Princesses vs Darkness&quot; city. For our gameline, might I suggest a city that has pollution as a major issue? I would also like to suggest that the Celestial Ocean has it's own appendix to describe how it's like and mechanics for moving about there. I think the Choruses (aka the Z Splat) should be listed within the Appendix 1 too. <br /> <br /> Finally, I think that the Corebook should have Waters and Currents in that order, rather than the other way around. The main reason being that Waters are the X/Inherent Splat and Currents are the Y/Social Splat. <br /> <br /> And even though things seem to be going well, we still do have abit of work. If we want to write up more about Currents for example, what societal structure is like, making more merits and stuff. As I read off of a WoD fansplat creation thing, we might feel the need to edit or add in new things or even revise. I don't mean that we won't ever be done, I'm meaning that we may always feel something new to add in. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:30:29-07:00","id":857823,"title":"","content":"Pardon the double post, but I've added Trace as a New Advantage and put Song of the School as a part of Akashic Record. I also made a new way to get Pneuma without kissing people willy nilly or dealing with a Relationship. It instead deals with the Waters Knowledges, since they seemed to mainly be there for fluff. I decided they should be used as a mechanic to regain Pneuma. What do you guys think? Should I put in that it takes willpower from the person they interacted with as well? Since draining willpower seems to be a big part of Pneuma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dHPB-rGUo_ObHiCSzSkqhZYovEY56tKBBVwu2_i8eNw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dHPB-rGUo_ObHiCSzSkqhZYovEY56tKBBVwu2_i8eNw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dHPB-rGUo_ObHiCSzSkqhZYovEY56tKBBVwu2_i8eNw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dHPB-rGUo_ObHiCSzSkqhZYovEY56tKBBVwu2_i8eNw/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T18:44:21-07:00","id":860702,"title":"","content":"Pardon the triple post, but I'm beginning on the Abyssal Currents. I need to ask you guys something though. I'm having the one dillemna of &quot;Acheron, the Echidna Current or &quot;Destroy everything&quot; current&quot; debate again and it's wearing me out. One of the reasons I think it should be the Echidna Current is because it feels fitting for them to have a fitting Trace, a Conclusion they use above others (in this case Disturb) and having a Current of their own. Not to mention that Acheron was the one where I had trouble coming up with an animal for, and making it the Echidnal Current gives me an idea what would symbolize it. A viper. For the meaning of &quot;shedding old skin and coming into a new form of life&quot;, which is befitting for Echidna's research, and it's basically a visual pun, given that Echidna means &quot;She-Viper&quot;. <br /> <br /> On the other, I can only find a negative reason against Acheron being the &quot;destroy the world&quot; current. It sounds like generic evilness that would be easily crushed by any other members of the currents because they don't want that. Heck, I can't imagine such a current having much support. Not to mention destroying both nature and civilization would mean having loads of Lucidity degenerations.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Sorry for bringing this up a third time, and if any of you have ideas for Siren or stuff, or even writing, I'd love to hear them and/or see them, I've been getting inspirationally dry as of late. =m=","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T22:11:46-07:00","id":860793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=860702#post860702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon the triple post, but I'm beginning on the Abyssal Currents. I need to ask you guys something though. I'm having the one dillemna of &quot;Acheron, the Echidna Current or &quot;Destroy everything&quot; current&quot; debate again and it's wearing me out. One of the reasons I think it should be the Echidna Current is because it feels fitting for them to have a fitting Trace, a Conclusion they use above others (in this case Disturb) and having a Current of their own. Not to mention that Acheron was the one where I had trouble coming up with an animal for, and making it the Echidnal Current gives me an idea what would symbolize it. A viper. For the meaning of &quot;shedding old skin and coming into a new form of life&quot;, which is befitting for Echidna's research, and it's basically a visual pun, given that Echidna means &quot;She-Viper&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the other, I can only find a negative reason against Acheron being the &quot;destroy the world&quot; current. It sounds like generic evilness that would be easily crushed by any other members of the currents because they don't want that. Heck, I can't imagine such a current having much support. Not to mention destroying both nature and civilization would mean having loads of Lucidity degenerations.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Sorry for bringing this up a third time, and if any of you have ideas for Siren or stuff, or even writing, I'd love to hear them and/or see them, I've been getting inspirationally dry as of late. =m=</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...<br /> <br /> In Shin Megami Tensei 4, there's a sort of dichotomy between Law and Chaos, asking the question of &quot;Should the world exist in Order where everything is regulated and everyone is equal or in Anarchy where everyone gets what they deserve and those who seek are rewarded&quot;. There is a middle ground of Neutral but there is also a separate middle alignment. There is a group called the White. They have lived a long time. A LONG time. As in, they have seen the cycle go on over and over, seeing the world under complete Order or complete Anarchy. They have seen people rise to change the world so that it could be a nice neutral. The cycle goes on. People live. People die. People go on to change the world. People go on to destroy it. It isn't just centuries. It isn't just millennia. It's epochs upon epochs watching this constant cycle going on and on causing people to suffer and beg for their lives. The White want to end this cycle. They want to end this cycle and make sure that it can never come again.<br /> <br /> They want to bring the world back into the Void, turning into nothingness so that no one must go through this cycle of pain ever again.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would be easier to paint the Abyssal Currents as not antagonists and rather champions who act contrary to what Ceto wished. The Current of Dark Passions seek to delve into the negative aspects of humanity and unleash the pain as a means of cathartic healing. The Current of Dark Knowledge want to seek out answers by abandoning their connections to morality. The Current of Mankind's Victory wants to ride out humanity's destructive path rather than direct it into something more acceptable. The Current of Primordial Darkness have all but turned on humanity in general to appease the world. <br /> <br /> With the Current of the Void, I feel that they could be written so that they are attempting to avert the belief that the Deluge is the end. They want it to come so that the world can be reset. They want to end all of life in order to begin again. Or perhaps they feel that it is the best for the world to begin again from scratch. Perhaps Sirens who follow the Current of the Void have gone too deep in their Trace, discovering secrets that they should not have known. Maybe the Sirens have lived too long in the world and have yet to see anything change. Or they have seen the path of the world within the Celestial Ocean and feel that there is no way to escape. For these Sirens, it's simply easier and more peaceful to end everything. Wipe out humanity. Make sure none of this will ever occur again. <br /> <br /> Their animal could be the coelacanth, a creature thought to have gone extinct but has managed to live for quite a bit of time. Or it could be a horseshoe crab, a creature that has not evolved into something more complicated for several million years. <br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> As for ideas and stuff, I want to throw out an idea: Trinkets and Treasures that allow a Siren to access an Introduction, Opus, or Conclusion that she would normally not be able to use. A rainbow conch that seems fragile is able to affect an [Area] before shattering into a thousand shards. A ship in the bottle can be broken to grant a Siren the ability to [Travel]. Just a quick idea, but it could be an interesting addition to a low-level Chronicle, giving the Sirens a taste of power. It could even tie into some sort of lore, like the Trinkets/Treasures release a little portion of the Song when it is used and collecting a certain amount and memorizing the notes allows the Siren access to an incredibly powerful Stanza.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T17:44:57-07:00","id":861458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=860793#post860793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...<br /> <br /> In Shin Megami Tensei 4, there's a sort of dichotomy between Law and Chaos, asking the question of &quot;Should the world exist in Order where everything is regulated and everyone is equal or in Anarchy where everyone gets what they deserve and those who seek are rewarded&quot;. There is a middle ground of Neutral but there is also a separate middle alignment. There is a group called the White. They have lived a long time. A LONG time. As in, they have seen the cycle go on over and over, seeing the world under complete Order or complete Anarchy. They have seen people rise to change the world so that it could be a nice neutral. The cycle goes on. People live. People die. People go on to change the world. People go on to destroy it. It isn't just centuries. It isn't just millennia. It's epochs upon epochs watching this constant cycle going on and on causing people to suffer and beg for their lives. The White want to end this cycle. They want to end this cycle and make sure that it can never come again.<br /> <br /> They want to bring the world back into the Void, turning into nothingness so that no one must go through this cycle of pain ever again.<br /> <br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> <br /> With the Current of the Void, I feel that they could be written so that they are attempting to avert the belief that the Deluge is the end. They want it to come so that the world can be reset. They want to end all of life in order to begin again. Or perhaps they feel that it is the best for the world to begin again from scratch. Perhaps Sirens who follow the Current of the Void have gone too deep in their Trace, discovering secrets that they should not have known. Maybe the Sirens have lived too long in the world and have yet to see anything change. Or they have seen the path of the world within the Celestial Ocean and feel that there is no way to escape. For these Sirens, it's simply easier and more peaceful to end everything. Wipe out humanity. Make sure none of this will ever occur again.<br /> <br /> Their animal could be the coelacanth, a creature thought to have gone extinct but has managed to live for quite a bit of time. Or it could be a horseshoe crab, a creature that has not evolved into something more complicated for several million years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Alright, this seems to be fine, sorry that I've been having that problem alot. And also, I have an idea what to name Echidna's current. Even though the five rivers of the Underworld have been taken up, there's still Oceanus. It's said to be the ocean at the edges/end of the world. It'd be fitting for Echidna's queendom to be named such, as no silly &quot;current&quot; could hold the might and majesty of her works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=860793#post860793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it would be easier to paint the Abyssal Currents as not antagonists and rather champions who act contrary to what Ceto wished. The Current of Dark Passions seek to delve into the negative aspects of humanity and unleash the pain as a means of cathartic healing. The Current of Dark Knowledge want to seek out answers by abandoning their connections to morality. The Current of Mankind's Victory wants to ride out humanity's destructive path rather than direct it into something more acceptable. The Current of Primordial Darkness have all but turned on humanity in general to appease the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's best if we do both. One where they see themselves as heroes and another where they're the antagonist. This lets STs be able to paint them however they want to show them and players with more play room or things to use if they decide to play in the Abyssal current. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=860793#post860793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for ideas and stuff, I want to throw out an idea: Trinkets and Treasures that allow a Siren to access an Introduction, Opus, or Conclusion that she would normally not be able to use. A rainbow conch that seems fragile is able to affect an [Area] before shattering into a thousand shards. A ship in the bottle can be broken to grant a Siren the ability to [Travel]. Just a quick idea, but it could be an interesting addition to a low-level Chronicle, giving the Sirens a taste of power. It could even tie into some sort of lore, like the Trinkets/Treasures release a little portion of the Song when it is used and collecting a certain amount and memorizing the notes allows the Siren access to an incredibly powerful Stanza.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. That's a good idea, I think the Trinkets should cover the &quot;fragile one time use&quot; things, and Treasures can cover holding a single verse. To ask though, you said an idea for a Trinket was a music box whose tune changes each day, and the first siren who listens gets one Pneuma. I'm just wondering what kind of Trinkets should be able to exist, since it seems that multiple ones can. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:42:01-07:00","id":861826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=861458#post861458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Alright, this seems to be fine, sorry that I've been having that problem alot. And also, I have an idea what to name Echidna's current. Even though the five rivers of the Underworld have been taken up, there's still Oceanus. It's said to be the ocean at the edges/end of the world. It'd be fitting for Echidna's queendom to be named such, as no silly &quot;current&quot; could hold the might and majesty of her works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. To be honest, I wouldn't have thought that Echidna would have an ego that would lead to her creating a queendom. It might be because we do have some details about Ceto and Echidna's personalities that are more open to interpretation. However, I'm totally not against the idea; it would be interesting to have an antagonist that does have some sort of agenda outside of &quot;harassing the player characters&quot; or &quot;general nefarious scheming&quot;. <br /> <br /> So our general plan in terms of lore is that the main two entities that are defined and known in the world of all Sirens are Ceto, the mother of Sirens, and Echidna, the mother of the Vodianoi, while everything else (The Leviathan/Behemoth war, &quot;Gaia&quot;, Ascendance) are all sorts of myths that Sirens are attempting to sift through in order to find a grain of truth? The main thing I wonder is how feasibly &quot;corporeal&quot; Ceto and Echidna feel in a Chronicle. They both fill the role of &quot;Mythical Progenitor&quot; that basically every splat has but they also have some physical weight to them. Like the Kereboi from Geist. <br /> <br /> Echidna already has things going for her: She's the figurehead who is acting contrary to Ceto by taking humanity and forcing them to survive the devastating waves of The Deluge by altering their being. She also is taking the role as the leader of her troop of Sirens by creating this sort of territory for her own experiments and presumably for some of her most loyal soldiers somewhere within The Celestial Ocean. She's also rather underhanded as she whispers to other Sirens and tempts them into her legion. All of this, I feel she does because she genuinely believes that her way is the best way to protect humanity and the Sirens. Despite how extreme this behavior comes across, it feels like she is trying her best to make the best out of what she sees as a bad situation. Granted, she's still a very extreme being. Kidnapping humans in order to see what she can change within them is not exactly &quot;hero&quot; material.<br /> <br /> I don't think we talked that much about Ceto's character other than her being the mother of all Sirens who adores humanity. What else is there to her as the &quot;good&quot; Siren's figurehead?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's best if we do both. One where they see themselves as heroes and another where they're the antagonist. This lets STs be able to paint them however they want to show them and players with more play room or things to use if they decide to play in the Abyssal current. </div> </div> </div>That might be for the best. I think a good way to make it significantly easier is to ask the question: &quot;How light/dark does the Current of the Void go?&quot; A lighter shade of the Void means that the Sirens of the Void are tired and feel that the only way to allow others peace is to let go and allow the world to end. A darker shade of the Void means that the Sirens of the Void have fully given up and gone mad at the realization that everything they do is a futile effort. It would at least give them more depth in portrayal as &quot;I can't handle going through one more life; may everything be destroyed&quot; is more complicated and interesting than &quot;Doom, destruction, and devastation!&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. That's a good idea, I think the Trinkets should cover the &quot;fragile one time use&quot; things, and Treasures can cover holding a single verse. To ask though, you said an idea for a Trinket was a music box whose tune changes each day, and the first siren who listens gets one Pneuma. I'm just wondering what kind of Trinkets should be able to exist, since it seems that multiple ones can. </div> </div> </div>I always think in terms of balance. How much use should utility have over raw power? What is a good cost for raw power that is relatively easy to find? What about things that amplify abilities? It would require the user to have said ability in the first place.<br /> <br /> Yads Dom suggested Treasures and included the idea that some Treasures would be able to access a Stanza. I don't remember much about the Verses, but I think that developing a Stanza (a Verse that has a set function and can be recalled multiple times with ease) costs some amount of Experience. That's a pretty fair trade-off: the cost of having an Introduction, two Opuses, and a Conclusion fitted into a Stanza placed into a single, possibly permanent-use Treasure.<br /> <br /> The Music Box idea is meant to be a utility item that is very nice to have but doesn't function enough times to be considered a Treasure. A point of free Pneuma is very nice but it only works once every lunar cycle, the time between each full moon. That's 14 days for a single point of Pneuma and it only gives it to the first Siren that uses it during that period. It does have its uses but its not entirely impressive, a Trinket at best.<br /> <br /> The Rainbow Conch and the Ship in a Bottle grant one-time access to a portion of a Verse, meaning that it's fairly valuable to Sirens who need some sort of contingency plan, don't have access to the part of the Verse that the items are offering, or want to save some Pneuma to be used at a later time. The main thing is that they are single-use, so they are significantly weaker than a full-on Treasure. <br /> <br /> I think that Trinkets are mainly defined by what they are able to do and to what extent they can do it. Think Grenades or Status-curing items in Final Fantasy. They have their uses but they tend to be in the bottom tier when it comes to items. Mainly, they are convenient to have despite there being better options, like the actual spells that have the same effect only at a larger scale. With Treasures, I feel that they are defined by their past, their power, and their &quot;OP&quot;-ness. Like a Summon. The Katana of the Dreadful Requiem is fairly powerful when it comes to vampire-slaying, considering that its a weapon and that it has the [Touch]-[Death]-[Blood]-[Destroy] Verse. I would totally say that, not only can a Siren use the Stanza to touch a Vampire and effective use Turn Undead, but that the Katana itself is some sort of bane. But that's mainly because [Touch] is a very short range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T21:31:33-07:00","id":862412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=861826#post861826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. To be honest, I wouldn't have thought that Echidna would have an ego that would lead to her creating a queendom. It might be because we do have some details about Ceto and Echidna's personalities that are more open to interpretation. However, I'm totally not against the idea; it would be interesting to have an antagonist that does have some sort of agenda outside of &quot;harassing the player characters&quot; or &quot;general nefarious scheming&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, the ideas for Echidna in the original thread included that she had an underwater fortress of a city in the Celestial Ocean, populated by her Sirens, Vodianoi, experiments and herself of course. She's also a representation of eugenics practices that violate ethics, that seek out to create the &quot;master race&quot; so to speak. If nothing else, I'd think it'd be in character for Echidna to be like a nazi elitist when it comes to making the perfect survivor out of humanity, the only problem is what's the correct formula? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=861826#post861826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So our general plan in terms of lore is that the main two entities that are defined and known in the world of all Sirens are Ceto, the mother of Sirens, and Echidna, the mother of the Vodianoi, while everything else (The Leviathan/Behemoth war, &quot;Gaia&quot;, Ascendance) are all sorts of myths that Sirens are attempting to sift through in order to find a grain of truth? The main thing I wonder is how feasibly &quot;corporeal&quot; Ceto and Echidna feel in a Chronicle. They both fill the role of &quot;Mythical Progenitor&quot; that basically every splat has but they also have some physical weight to them. Like the Kereboi from Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Although personally speaking, it might be more fitting to refer to Echidna as &quot;Queen of Monsters&quot; or &quot;The Monster Queen&quot;, since all Vodianoi aren't technically birthed, they're human and fish DNA put into a blender and they're the result of it. They do have physical weight to them, and if we choose them to exist as well, the progenitors of the Currents are also beings who could fit as the bills as potentially physically meetable people.<br /> <br /> I have to admit, when it comes to backstory, we may need to take a page out of Vampire's book. If I recall correctly, their backstory wasn't entirely made out in terms of &quot;how are we vamps&quot;, they have some differing stories to how the first vampire was conceived/embraced, and their Covenants all have some mythological founders (Dracula for Ordo Dracul anyone? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). All in all, it at least feels like it'd give a more direct piece of inspiration for where we're going, since the similarities, which are completely unintentional on my end, are still kind of there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=861826#post861826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Echidna already has things going for her: She's the figurehead who is acting contrary to Ceto by taking humanity and forcing them to survive the devastating waves of The Deluge by altering their being. She also is taking the role as the leader of her troop of Sirens by creating this sort of territory for her own experiments and presumably for some of her most loyal soldiers somewhere within The Celestial Ocean. She's also rather underhanded as she whispers to other Sirens and tempts them into her legion. All of this, I feel she does because she genuinely believes that her way is the best way to protect humanity and the Sirens. Despite how extreme this behavior comes across, it feels like she is trying her best to make the best out of what she sees as a bad situation. Granted, she's still a very extreme being. Kidnapping humans in order to see what she can change within them is not exactly &quot;hero&quot; material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the bit of narcissism and manipulation you've added to her. :3 If I may ask though, what were the bits about Maelstrom again? I'm still feeling abit iffy on the idea of Echidna whispering to Sirens in Maelstrom, if you'll pardon me saying so. D:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=861826#post861826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we talked that much about Ceto's character other than her being the mother of all Sirens who adores humanity. What else is there to her as the &quot;good&quot; Siren's figurehead?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd say that Ceto has as much influence over Sirens as Luna has over Werewolves, and I'd say that Ceto's personality is basically like that of Calypso in the Calypso and Davy Jones in Pirates of the Caribbean. Ceto is like the seas themselves: fickle, unpredictable, a definite mood swinger who may be calm one moment, and raging for no reason the next. But her love extends over all of humanity the same, maybe even in her own way.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=861826#post861826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be for the best. I think a good way to make it significantly easier is to ask the question: &quot;How light/dark does the Current of the Void go?&quot; A lighter shade of the Void means that the Sirens of the Void are tired and feel that the only way to allow others peace is to let go and allow the world to end. A darker shade of the Void means that the Sirens of the Void have fully given up and gone mad at the realization that everything they do is a futile effort. It would at least give them more depth in portrayal as &quot;I can't handle going through one more life; may everything be destroyed&quot; is more complicated and interesting than &quot;Doom, destruction, and devastation!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that sounds perhaps the best on how to do them. Thank you for your help. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=861826#post861826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yads Dom suggested Treasures and included the idea that some Treasures would be able to access a Stanza. I don't remember much about the Verses, but I think that developing a Stanza (a Verse that has a set function and can be recalled multiple times with ease) costs some amount of Experience. That's a pretty fair trade-off: the cost of having an Introduction, two Opuses, and a Conclusion fitted into a Stanza placed into a single, possibly permanent-use Treasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Verses are basically Introduction-Opus-Conclusion. Introduction = The noun you're targeting, Opus = the things being manipulated in the Verse, Conclusion = How the Opus is being manipulated in, on, or onto the Introduction target. All Conclusions are tied to a single Attribute save Disturb, which gives 10-Lucidity dice. The basic roll for Verses is Attribute (used by the Conclusion) + Akashic Record, and Stanzas are basically codified verses, much like Mage Rotes so to speak. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=861826#post861826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Music Box idea is meant to be a utility item that is very nice to have but doesn't function enough times to be considered a Treasure. A point of free Pneuma is very nice but it only works once every lunar cycle, the time between each full moon. That's 14 days for a single point of Pneuma and it only gives it to the first Siren that uses it during that period. It does have its uses but its not entirely impressive, a Trinket at best.<br /> <br /> The Rainbow Conch and the Ship in a Bottle grant one-time access to a portion of a Verse, meaning that it's fairly valuable to Sirens who need some sort of contingency plan, don't have access to the part of the Verse that the items are offering, or want to save some Pneuma to be used at a later time. The main thing is that they are single-use, so they are significantly weaker than a full-on Treasure.<br /> <br /> I think that Trinkets are mainly defined by what they are able to do and to what extent they can do it. Think Grenades or Status-curing items in Final Fantasy. They have their uses but they tend to be in the bottom tier when it comes to items. Mainly, they are convenient to have despite there being better options, like the actual spells that have the same effect only at a larger scale. With Treasures, I feel that they are defined by their past, their power, and their &quot;OP&quot;-ness. Like a Summon. The Katana of the Dreadful Requiem is fairly powerful when it comes to vampire-slaying, considering that its a weapon and that it has the [Touch]-[Death]-[Blood]-[Destroy] Verse. I would totally say that, not only can a Siren use the Stanza to touch a Vampire and effective use Turn Undead, but that the Katana itself is some sort of bane. But that's mainly because [Touch] is a very short range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. That's fitting.<br /> <br /> And I think I know one thing else that we don't have a general guideline over, but should probably be brought up sometime. The Celestial Ocean. How will we do this plane of existence? So far, all I have is the ideas we have that it will be a physical realm where Sirens may find Treasures, Trinkets and stuff. They may also hold Vodianoi and the like in it as well, definitely Grottos.<br /> <br /> I suddenly have an idea. Given that the Celestial Ocean looks like the post apocalyptic earth after the Deluge, what if that's how it's like? I got the idea from the 60 Seconds game. Pretty much, people hiding in bomb shelters (aka Grottos), raiders and looters are abound, but so too are people just trying to survive and protect people. There may be radiation poisoning (Vodianoi) or the like going about, and people exploiting it (Echidna). And sometimes, there's army drops or generous people who help others survive or get out of there (Current Sirens). What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:45:43-07:00","id":862447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=862412#post862412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, the ideas for Echidna in the original thread included that she had an underwater fortress of a city in the Celestial Ocean, populated by her Sirens, Vodianoi, experiments and herself of course. She's also a representation of eugenics practices that violate ethics, that seek out to create the &quot;master race&quot; so to speak. If nothing else, I'd think it'd be in character for Echidna to be like a nazi elitist when it comes to making the perfect survivor out of humanity, the only problem is what's the correct formula?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that most mad scientists would want to do their work in secrecy in a not-so-subtle lair of sorts. I suppose &quot;world domination&quot; is always one of the end goals, but Echidna feels like she actually believes she is doing good, so she doesn't really fall under that umbrella. I'd feel that she would bask in the idea that she's the Savior and that she is the one who is able to rescue everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the bit of narcissism and manipulation you've added to her. :3 If I may ask though, what were the bits about Maelstrom again? I'm still feeling abit iffy on the idea of Echidna whispering to Sirens in Maelstrom, if you'll pardon me saying so. D: </div> </div> </div>I like to think that Echidna believes herself to be this sort of Chessmaster who cheats in such a way that you feel that she should be able to get away with it. With the Maelstrom, the assumption is that the PC Sirens are at least allied to Ceto and follow the normal (there might need to be a word for this) Currents. When a Siren falls to the Maelstrom, it is because there is some fundamental challenge to the Siren's worldview that causes her to question herself. A Siren of Buoyancy can't laugh off the fact that her behavior caused someone in her Shoal to get severely hurt or a Siren of Harmony is completely shut out of her best friend's life with no warning. The Siren is no longer to swim with the Current as smooth as she did before; the dips and dives have knocked her unbalanced and she is struggling to regain some sort of hold to her surrounding. In comes Echidna, who attempts to use this vulnerability to lure the Siren astray from Ceto (or her Currents, as this is assuming that the 5 main Currents are the main tenets that Ceto upholds). <i>&quot;You can't keep faking your attitude like your gracious leader expects you to do. Come with me and you won't have to put up this facade anymore.&quot; &quot;Not everyone is willing to coexist peacefully, so why not just give up on them? I'll give you some wonderful new friends who will care for you as you will for them.&quot; </i>Even if the Sirens don't defect, Echidna will accept making the Siren question Ceto as a leader as a suitable victory. After all, that useless figurehead is working on something futile. Echidna's the one who is actually working to make tangible changes (or at least, that's what Echidna believes of her counterpart).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say that Ceto has as much influence over Sirens as Luna has over Werewolves, and I'd say that Ceto's personality is basically like that of Calypso in the Calypso and Davy Jones in Pirates of the Caribbean. Ceto is like the seas themselves: fickle, unpredictable, a definite mood swinger who may be calm one moment, and raging for no reason the next. But her love extends over all of humanity the same, maybe even in her own way. </div> </div> </div>Ahh. Okay. I was thinking that Ceto was geared more towards an all-loving, benevolent ruler but that could be an interesting angle to work with. Can we say that, in contrast to Echidna's obsession with transformation and general disdain for all things Ceto, Ceto works by having her finger in many pies and all-together ignoring Echidna's sad attempts to get her sea-goat? As in, Ceto is a concepts person, dreaming up many ways to solve plans and having her Sirens follow up on them. She wants humanity to change its path to prevent them from experiencing the Deluge but she also needs some groups to go in to repair the damage caused by the Floodings. Meanwhile, the Furies are causing trouble in a section of the world and she needs to figure out a means to control them. And then there's the Song. Is there a way to repurpose it into some sort of protective veil to keep the Deluge calm? Ceto's plans expand as far as the oceans themselves and she is only one partially-omnipotent being. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think I know one thing else that we don't have a general guideline over, but should probably be brought up sometime. The Celestial Ocean. How will we do this plane of existence? So far, all I have is the ideas we have that it will be a physical realm where Sirens may find Treasures, Trinkets and stuff. They may also hold Vodianoi and the like in it as well, definitely Grottos.<br /> <br /> I suddenly have an idea. Given that the Celestial Ocean looks like the post apocalyptic earth after the Deluge, what if that's how it's like? I got the idea from the 60 Seconds game. Pretty much, people hiding in bomb shelters (aka Grottos), raiders and looters are abound, but so too are people just trying to survive and protect people. There may be radiation poisoning (Vodianoi) or the like going about, and people exploiting it (Echidna). And sometimes, there's army drops or generous people who help others survive or get out of there (Current Sirens). What do you think? </div> </div> </div>Did...did we just unintentionally create a splat that can be used as a metaphor for nuclear war? I'm totally for that if we can keep that general mindset running.<br /> <br /> I think we could probably think of a good basis for what it is in terms of its place in the CofD. The Shadow and the Underworld are Dark and Gloomy while Arcadia is Wild and Untamed and the Supernal Realms (in general) are Vast and Dreamy. I feel that the Celestial Ocean is effectively a Fallen Paradise being Rediscovered. It is the end of the world, so there is destruction and decay that can be freely traversed to the miles of water that stretches up beyond the limits of the sky. The drowned remnants of a life long past and currently ongoing become a reminder of what the Sirens are fighting for and become imbued by the hope that came off of the Song. The beings that treat this world as their reality have build a sort of territory system as a means to stay organized in a world that had once lost the meaning of the word &quot;order&quot;. <br /> <br /> One of the things that we should address is the place that blue-book Mortals have in the world of Sirens. To stay on topic, can non-Sirens gain access to the Celestial Ocean in some way? Is there a sort of gateway that leads into the Celestial Ocean itself (I don't think we actually discussed this yet)? Is there something that keeps the Flensers out or are they attempting to break in? Or are there Flensers that are still alive in this sunken world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:49:04-07:00","id":862745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=862447#post862447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that most mad scientists would want to do their work in secrecy in a not-so-subtle lair of sorts. I suppose &quot;world domination&quot; is always one of the end goals, but Echidna feels like she actually believes she is doing good, so she doesn't really fall under that umbrella. I'd feel that she would bask in the idea that she's the Savior and that she is the one who is able to rescue everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty true, that's something that I think Genius touches on, the flaw being that their Wonders can't survive human observation. I can at least imagine her perhaps taking over spaces &quot;because she knows better&quot; than the petty humans living in the dying world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=862447#post862447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think that Echidna believes herself to be this sort of Chessmaster who cheats in such a way that you feel that she should be able to get away with it. With the Maelstrom, the assumption is that the PC Sirens are at least allied to Ceto and follow the normal (there might need to be a word for this) Currents. When a Siren falls to the Maelstrom, it is because there is some fundamental challenge to the Siren's worldview that causes her to question herself. A Siren of Buoyancy can't laugh off the fact that her behavior caused someone in her Shoal to get severely hurt or a Siren of Harmony is completely shut out of her best friend's life with no warning. The Siren is no longer to swim with the Current as smooth as she did before; the dips and dives have knocked her unbalanced and she is struggling to regain some sort of hold to her surrounding. In comes Echidna, who attempts to use this vulnerability to lure the Siren astray from Ceto (or her Currents, as this is assuming that the 5 main Currents are the main tenets that Ceto upholds). <i>&quot;You can't keep faking your attitude like your gracious leader expects you to do. Come with me and you won't have to put up this facade anymore.&quot; &quot;Not everyone is willing to coexist peacefully, so why not just give up on them? I'll give you some wonderful new friends who will care for you as you will for them.&quot; </i>Even if the Sirens don't defect, Echidna will accept making the Siren question Ceto as a leader as a suitable victory. After all, that useless figurehead is working on something futile. Echidna's the one who is actually working to make tangible changes (or at least, that's what Echidna believes of her counterpart).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I think I found what was iffy in my thoughts. Namely, it's that Echidna is influencing Sirens to do things that would usually hasten the coming of the Deluge, which ultimately doesn't benefit Echidna at all. She would benefit more from the Currents doing their actual jobs rather than facing Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> That said, I do imagine Maelstrom going abit as you say, a Siren being influenced to work under darker impulses. However, as for who and what is whispering to them...<br /> <br /> Let's see from the other splats that face a Frenzy or something that makes them tried emotionally. Vampires face it from their Beast, who's basically the animalistic instincts of the Vampire. The need to feed, to sleep, to kill. Werewolves Death Rage stems from a werewolf's &quot;Wolf&quot; instincts, times that try them emotionally (mostly things that would drive them to rage) where they'd lash out like a rabid beast. Princesses face Sensitivity from watching callous acts be inflicted upon the world, manifesting as an emotional reaction to another's suffering.<br /> <br /> I list these for potential inspiration as well as ideas to stick away from so as not to copy the splat. Now, Sirens are basically connected to humanity, nature and their combined survival, so it feels unfitting for them to yield to animalistic instincts. I do believe in the idea you presented, that the Sirens basically go into a state where they're more inclined to go into their darker urges, but I don't think Echidna should be the one giving the orders. I think it should be the same force behind the Furies, that makes a Siren move through their resentment. It gives more to tie the Furies into the gameline (I imagine they'd at least not kill a Siren on sight, and the best the relationship gets is that they're active allies of Styx).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=862447#post862447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh. Okay. I was thinking that Ceto was geared more towards an all-loving, benevolent ruler but that could be an interesting angle to work with. Can we say that, in contrast to Echidna's obsession with transformation and general disdain for all things Ceto, Ceto works by having her finger in many pies and all-together ignoring Echidna's sad attempts to get her sea-goat? As in, Ceto is a concepts person, dreaming up many ways to solve plans and having her Sirens follow up on them. She wants humanity to change its path to prevent them from experiencing the Deluge but she also needs some groups to go in to repair the damage caused by the Floodings. Meanwhile, the Furies are causing trouble in a section of the world and she needs to figure out a means to control them. And then there's the Song. Is there a way to repurpose it into some sort of protective veil to keep the Deluge calm? Ceto's plans expand as far as the oceans themselves and she is only one partially-omnipotent being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Yes, I didn't mean for Ceto to be &quot;goodness good who is the most absolute good&quot;, I think she's more akin to Luna in the sense that &quot;There's a danger to the world and it must be taken out by whatever means necessary&quot;.<br /> <br /> I believe what you said is feasible. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=862447#post862447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did...did we just unintentionally create a splat that can be used as a metaphor for nuclear war? I'm totally for that if we can keep that general mindset running.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe we just did. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I must say, I believe one of the ideas for the Deluge (the event) is that it basically was a &quot;Cover all apocalypse&quot;. It covers human made apocalypse, ice age that wipes out all things, everything killing each other, etc etc. I just had an idea: The Waters can also represent the kinds of apocalypses that wipe out life on earth on a grand scale. Polaria is ice ages, Tropicana is heat death or the sun's supernova, Gardenia is nature induced apocalypse, Freshwater is human induced apocalypse, Discordia is basically when everything just kills each other, and Vaporia....I have no idea. Suggestions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=862447#post862447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we could probably think of a good basis for what it is in terms of its place in the CofD. The Shadow and the Underworld are Dark and Gloomy while Arcadia is Wild and Untamed and the Supernal Realms (in general) are Vast and Dreamy. I feel that the Celestial Ocean is effectively a Fallen Paradise being Rediscovered. It is the end of the world, so there is destruction and decay that can be freely traversed to the miles of water that stretches up beyond the limits of the sky. The drowned remnants of a life long past and currently ongoing become a reminder of what the Sirens are fighting for and become imbued by the hope that came off of the Song. The beings that treat this world as their reality have build a sort of territory system as a means to stay organized in a world that had once lost the meaning of the word &quot;order&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I spoke to Kara earlier about ideas to justify any sorts of society in the Celestial Ocean, or how people are still about in the first place. I brought up the ideas that some people were aware that the Deluge was going to happen, and as such, they did what Noah did. They made ships to live on when the flood would kill them all. Now that it's happened, it's basically trying to continue living. The obvious hardships is growing or keeping up food, but perhaps even worse is that they're easy targets for Echidna for test subjects...<br /> <br /> Also suggested, I had the idea that Echidna and/or Ceto came unto humanity before the Deluge happened. Simply put, one of the two came onto them and gave them the means to survive underwater. I believe Echidna's the most fitting in this case, as it would be a test run of doing her mutagenic powers. Simply put, people still died regardless, but it gave them time to make underwater living a possibility for them. After the Deluge however, Echidna perhaps decided it was time to take her due. So she instated her queendom as the only amount of society to exist in the drowned world. People could submit and live as her vassals, or they could be captured and made into her Vodianoi, mindless animals who listen to their masters until the end of time. Now, everyone is just hiding away, trying to keep surviving past the apocalypse as much as they could. They perhaps only go out for food or ruined supplies, but each time they do, they risk getting captured by Echidna's Vodianoi or Sirens, or they get killed in their violent attempts to flee. The survivors still can have some vestiges of society, but too many exist in lonely waters, trying to live for just one more day. Perhaps some instead of hiding away choose to drift and scavenge off of what they can.<br /> <br /> There's still people in the Deluge who still antagonize other survivors. Perhaps there's pirates amongst the survivors, who steal or take from other survivors. Maybe some hoard what few materials they could save from the depths before selling or trading to other people. My friend typed up a word doc for the possible types of people post Deluge, want me to send to your email? Or copy and paste to Google Docs and post here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=862447#post862447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that we should address is the place that blue-book Mortals have in the world of Sirens. To stay on topic, can non-Sirens gain access to the Celestial Ocean in some way? Is there a sort of gateway that leads into the Celestial Ocean itself (I don't think we actually discussed this yet)? Is there something that keeps the Flensers out or are they attempting to break in? Or are there Flensers that are still alive in this sunken world?</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't talked at all how one can enter the Celestial Ocean. I saaaay maybe it's possible to enter the Celestial Ocean from Quagmires, or a place that once had a Quagmire but that faded now. It might make it hard for Flensers to enter the Deluge unless we come up with some other way.<br /> <br /> As for Flensers, I believe that they pay more attention to Sirens and getting their flesh to live longer. However, I do see a VERY good plot hook in them entering the Deluge. I imagine the Flensers to be the type of people who see themselves as the biggest fish in the ocean, who have loads of money from nature exploitation, and thus they can get almost any resource they need....which would ultimately benefit any survivors in the Deluge. Even though the survivors have little to give in return to the Flensers, the Flensers prolly wouldn't ask for monetary payment. They'd simply ask for the survivors to sell out any Sirens they find in the Celestial Ocean. This produces some conflict between survivors and Sirens, and gives perhaps a good reason for some Sirens to try not dealing with Survivors out of fear if they may betray them.<br /> <br /> I don't know whether Flensers are still alive in the Celestial Ocean post-Deluge. The good point about &quot;future apocalypse scenario&quot; stuff is that we don't need to worry about technological advances or human evolution, since they are either destroyed or the present Humans and post-Deluge Humans are still similar enough to be called the same. However, I would like to believe that in the simple manner of speaking that if there are Flensers in the post-Deluge, they are not speaking of their prior affiliations. It's because they had a hand in the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> That said, I do believe in a funny idea. Perhaps some of the Future Flensers are still selfish, trying to live at the top and screwing everyone else over. However, perhaps some are remorseful. They now know what the people they've hunted down have been trying to prevent, and by hunting them they only brought forth what could've been prevented. In this sense, some of these future Flensers may try to help the Sirens, giving them ways to Trace back on Flenser plans and stop them before they even begin.<br /> <br /> What do you think? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:38:46-07:00","id":863299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=862745#post862745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. I think I found what was iffy in my thoughts. Namely, it's that Echidna is influencing Sirens to do things that would usually hasten the coming of the Deluge, which ultimately doesn't benefit Echidna at all. She would benefit more from the Currents doing their actual jobs rather than facing Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> That said, I do imagine Maelstrom going abit as you say, a Siren being influenced to work under darker impulses. However, as for who and what is whispering to them...<br /> <br /> <b><i>[...]</i></b><br /> <br /> I list these for potential inspiration as well as ideas to stick away from so as not to copy the splat. Now, Sirens are basically connected to humanity, nature and their combined survival, so it feels unfitting for them to yield to animalistic instincts. I do believe in the idea you presented, that the Sirens basically go into a state where they're more inclined to go into their darker urges, but I don't think Echidna should be the one giving the orders. I think it should be the same force behind the Furies, that makes a Siren move through their resentment. It gives more to tie the Furies into the gameline (I imagine they'd at least not kill a Siren on sight, and the best the relationship gets is that they're active allies of Styx).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you're going for. It would be nice to tie in the Furies in a way that would make them relate stronger with the Sirens. As far as the &quot;Who&quot;, I almost feel that we shouldn't define who or what is whispering, only that they are a festering Chthonic being who works in a manner similar to the Floodings and the Deluge. It is some sort of unforgiving force that seeks to quench its indignant fury with the blood of humanity. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe we just did. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I must say, I believe one of the ideas for the Deluge (the event) is that it basically was a &quot;Cover all apocalypse&quot;. It covers human made apocalypse, ice age that wipes out all things, everything killing each other, etc etc. I just had an idea: The Waters can also represent the kinds of apocalypses that wipe out life on earth on a grand scale. Polaria is ice ages, Tropicana is heat death or the sun's supernova, Gardenia is nature induced apocalypse, Freshwater is human induced apocalypse, Discordia is basically when everything just kills each other, and Vaporia....I have no idea. Suggestions? </div> </div> </div>Possibly something to do with the atmosphere. The atmosphere does give this planet some protection from the harmful cosmic radiation and protects from the extreme amounts of sunlight that has since rendered Venus into this burning wasteland. Or it could be harmful chemical storms or things that go beyond the surface of the Earth. Gardenia could be the earth becoming unstable or utterly barren.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed. I spoke to Kara earlier about ideas to justify any sorts of society in the Celestial Ocean, or how people are still about in the first place. I brought up the ideas that some people were aware that the Deluge was going to happen, and as such, they did what Noah did. They made ships to live on when the flood would kill them all. Now that it's happened, it's basically trying to continue living. The obvious hardships is growing or keeping up food, but perhaps even worse is that they're easy targets for Echidna for test subjects...<br /> <br /> Also suggested, I had the idea that Echidna and/or Ceto came unto humanity before the Deluge happened. Simply put, one of the two came onto them and gave them the means to survive underwater. I believe Echidna's the most fitting in this case, as it would be a test run of doing her mutagenic powers. Simply put, people still died regardless, but it gave them time to make underwater living a possibility for them. After the Deluge however, Echidna perhaps decided it was time to take her due. So she instated her queendom as the only amount of society to exist in the drowned world. People could submit and live as her vassals, or they could be captured and made into her Vodianoi, mindless animals who listen to their masters until the end of time. Now, everyone is just hiding away, trying to keep surviving past the apocalypse as much as they could. They perhaps only go out for food or ruined supplies, but each time they do, they risk getting captured by Echidna's Vodianoi or Sirens, or they get killed in their violent attempts to flee. The survivors still can have some vestiges of society, but too many exist in lonely waters, trying to live for just one more day. Perhaps some instead of hiding away choose to drift and scavenge off of what they can.<br /> <br /> There's still people in the Deluge who still antagonize other survivors. Perhaps there's pirates amongst the survivors, who steal or take from other survivors. Maybe some hoard what few materials they could save from the depths before selling or trading to other people. My friend typed up a word doc for the possible types of people post Deluge, want me to send to your email? Or copy and paste to Google Docs and post here? </div> </div> </div>Hmm...I don't know how I feel about mortals at least being able to survive the Deluge and becoming survivors. I don't know why. I think it's mainly because the other kinds of Realms have their own sort of &quot;native&quot; lifeform and humans are more of guests than anything. I would say at least the humans that aren't Flensers should be significantly altered. Sorta going back to the idea that the Deluge is both a physical and metaphysical thing, maybe the waves stripped away an essence of humanity from the survivors, rendering them a mere shadow of what they are now. It would give Ceto a stronger desire for wanting to protect the mortals who lived before the Deluge; having mortals live at basically full capacity would mean that there is some glimmer of hope of bringing back life as they knew it. By having the humans lose something vital through the Deluge, it would mean that they aren't the humans that Ceto grew to love; they are miserable creatures that have no hope, no spark of humanity.<br /> <br /> I would also say that it would probably be best to post the Google Docs so everyone else can take a look through it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We haven't talked at all how one can enter the Celestial Ocean. I saaaay maybe it's possible to enter the Celestial Ocean from Quagmires, or a place that once had a Quagmire but that faded now. It might make it hard for Flensers to enter the Deluge unless we come up with some other way.<br /> <br /> As for Flensers, I believe that they pay more attention to Sirens and getting their flesh to live longer. However, I do see a VERY good plot hook in them entering the Deluge. I imagine the Flensers to be the type of people who see themselves as the biggest fish in the ocean, who have loads of money from nature exploitation, and thus they can get almost any resource they need....which would ultimately benefit any survivors in the Deluge. Even though the survivors have little to give in return to the Flensers, the Flensers prolly wouldn't ask for monetary payment. They'd simply ask for the survivors to sell out any Sirens they find in the Celestial Ocean. This produces some conflict between survivors and Sirens, and gives perhaps a good reason for some Sirens to try not dealing with Survivors out of fear if they may betray them.<br /> <br /> I don't know whether Flensers are still alive in the Celestial Ocean post-Deluge. The good point about &quot;future apocalypse scenario&quot; stuff is that we don't need to worry about technological advances or human evolution, since they are either destroyed or the present Humans and post-Deluge Humans are still similar enough to be called the same. However, I would like to believe that in the simple manner of speaking that if there are Flensers in the post-Deluge, they are not speaking of their prior affiliations. It's because they had a hand in the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> That said, I do believe in a funny idea. Perhaps some of the Future Flensers are still selfish, trying to live at the top and screwing everyone else over. However, perhaps some are remorseful. They now know what the people they've hunted down have been trying to prevent, and by hunting them they only brought forth what could've been prevented. In this sense, some of these future Flensers may try to help the Sirens, giving them ways to Trace back on Flenser plans and stop them before they even begin.<br /> <br /> What do you think? :3 </div> </div> </div>I think we could totally add another Hunter group to fill the parts that the Flensers don't really work in. Granted, the Flensers are the big thing that are causing the Sirens issues but I can totally see a sort of &quot;Explorers and Conquistadors&quot; Compact who are the ones that enter the Celestial Ocean on a regular basis. <br /> <br /> Let's say that the Flensers, or at least the antediluvian Flensers, have little to no interest in the Celestial Ocean and only really want to hunt Sirens for their longevity bits (and possibly other supernaturals to test out what works). The ones who managed to live through the Deluge and now (or will? Timey wimey tidbits and such) still need some Siren flesh to prolong death but they also have some sort of desire to work things out to prevent the Deluge. Or they're gonna run themselves into the ground trying to get their Siren fix. Either way, I like the idea of them possibly existing in the Celestial Ocean.<br /> <br /> As for the other possible Hunters, the Explorer!Hunters could be old-school conquistadors who created the story of the Fountain of Youth when they discovered the Celestial Ocean and found a Treasure that produced a stream of miraculous healing water when used. The Treasure itself has long since been destroyed or misplaced so these Explorer!Hunters have been launching expeditions into the Celestial Ocean in order to steal whatever Treasures and Trinkets they can find. If we're still using the survivors, the Explorer!Hunters could also be attempting to establish colonies and trade with the survivors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:45:27-07:00","id":863363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863299#post863299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see what you're going for. It would be nice to tie in the Furies in a way that would make them relate stronger with the Sirens. As far as the &quot;Who&quot;, I almost feel that we shouldn't define who or what is whispering, only that they are a festering Chthonic being who works in a manner similar to the Floodings and the Deluge. It is some sort of unforgiving force that seeks to quench its indignant fury with the blood of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, if you don't mind that it'll kind of take out your idea. I'm sorry if it's bad. <br /> <br /> Although when it comes to Furies, might I suggest a small idea? I mean, we aren't going to directly state the eldritch force behind the Furies and Maelstrom, but as abit of fluff, I imagine that the Furies would only say that they are the products of the Earth and it's anger. Who or what is the &quot;Earth&quot; will be kept ambiguous. Maybe it's Gaia, sister of Ceto who, unlike Ceto, is more easily damagable and thus harder to repair. Maybe it's Behemoth, whose futile rage against Leviathan and his own inability to create life continues to this day through his Furies and the Sirens, who are one third of his blood. Maybe, the Current Sirens believe, it's Echidna, who voices through them to destroy what they love so the only connection left to existence is her. Of course, for the Current Sirens, the screams of denial from the Echidnals only fuel the rumors more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863299#post863299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly something to do with the atmosphere. The atmosphere does give this planet some protection from the harmful cosmic radiation and protects from the extreme amounts of sunlight that has since rendered Venus into this burning wasteland. Or it could be harmful chemical storms or things that go beyond the surface of the Earth. Gardenia could be the earth becoming unstable or utterly barren.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, that's perfect. Now the only question is, should we portray any of these apocalyptic effects within the Celestial Ocean? One part about post apocalyptic scenarios is that there's still danger in the environment, even if it's not apparent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863299#post863299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...I don't know how I feel about mortals at least being able to survive the Deluge and becoming survivors. I don't know why. I think it's mainly because the other kinds of Realms have their own sort of &quot;native&quot; lifeform and humans are more of guests than anything. I would say at least the humans that aren't Flensers should be significantly altered. Sorta going back to the idea that the Deluge is both a physical and metaphysical thing, maybe the waves stripped away an essence of humanity from the survivors, rendering them a mere shadow of what they are now. It would give Ceto a stronger desire for wanting to protect the mortals who lived before the Deluge; having mortals live at basically full capacity would mean that there is some glimmer of hope of bringing back life as they knew it. By having the humans lose something vital through the Deluge, it would mean that they aren't the humans that Ceto grew to love; they are miserable creatures that have no hope, no spark of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's indeed the best way to put it. The Song was created by the weeping tears of dead humans, trying to reach back and stop the end from ever occurring. The Survivors however are not dead, or maybe the effort to create the Song simply sucked whatever was left of a soul out of them. That's not to say that they're under the effects of Soul Loss, but that they simply have the most hollow bits of a soul left in them. The consequence isn't totally magical, the Song isn't the only reason why they only have a shred of a soul left. Another reason is that they simply do not have a future left. Sure, if the Sirens succeed, then the Earth is not doomed in the past. But in the Future that is the Celestial Ocean, there's no salvation waiting for the survivors of the Deluge. Just because the past is fixed doesn't mean that their future will change, because they're separate.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm prolly getting the timelines stuff wrong, and if so, please correct me. This idea adds on some Grimdark/Fridge Horror to Siren, but I can't help but feel like &quot;there should be a way for the survivors to have even a marginally happy ending&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863299#post863299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also say that it would probably be best to post the Google Docs so everyone else can take a look through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty, here it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ad0iueKvZLp-3pesQ34SqWCX5iE2etm2JBVUvb-wW4U/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ad0iueKvZLp-3pesQ34SqWCX5iE2etm2JBVUvb-wW4U/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ad0iueKvZLp-3pesQ34SqWCX5iE2etm2JBVUvb-wW4U/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ad0iueKvZLp-3pesQ34SqWCX5iE2etm2JBVUvb-wW4U/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863299#post863299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we could totally add another Hunter group to fill the parts that the Flensers don't really work in. Granted, the Flensers are the big thing that are causing the Sirens issues but I can totally see a sort of &quot;Explorers and Conquistadors&quot; Compact who are the ones that enter the Celestial Ocean on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> Let's say that the Flensers, or at least the antediluvian Flensers, have little to no interest in the Celestial Ocean and only really want to hunt Sirens for their longevity bits (and possibly other supernaturals to test out what works). The ones who managed to live through the Deluge and now (or will? Timey wimey tidbits and such) still need some Siren flesh to prolong death but they also have some sort of desire to work things out to prevent the Deluge. Or they're gonna run themselves into the ground trying to get their Siren fix. Either way, I like the idea of them possibly existing in the Celestial Ocean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that Flensers would have at least abit of interest in the Celestial Ocean, if that they'd think it was another aspect or way of getting to Sirens, whether through Survivors, kidnapping whatever Siren they find or perhaps even finding Echidnal Sirens hiding places and attacking them via pollution. One good part about the Celestial Ocean: It's already a dead land, so it won't hurt them to dump whatever pollution they have into the celestial ocean, especially since Sirens get aggravated from it. I do like your idea of making a hunter compact that deals with and/or against Sirens, but I believe that the Flensers should be one of the main antagonist of Siren. Hunter is another gameline and all, but I'm not against the idea of making a compact as an example for Siren Hunters that aren't Flensers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863299#post863299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the other possible Hunters, the Explorer!Hunters could be old-school conquistadors who created the story of the Fountain of Youth when they discovered the Celestial Ocean and found a Treasure that produced a stream of miraculous healing water when used. The Treasure itself has long since been destroyed or misplaced so these Explorer!Hunters have been launching expeditions into the Celestial Ocean in order to steal whatever Treasures and Trinkets they can find. If we're still using the survivors, the Explorer!Hunters could also be attempting to establish colonies and trade with the survivors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing this, I believe that the Siren main city should be in or somewhere near Florida. The reasoning being of the myth that Ponce De Leon, the first governor of Puerto Rico, had went unto Florida in search of the Fountain of Youth. Not to mention that the BP Oil Spill is generally still fresh in people's memories, although to be on the safe side, we should find a city that's been having pollution problems before the Oil Spill. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the hunters could be known as &quot;Conquistadors of Leon&quot; or &quot;Ponce's Pirates&quot;, maybe even both with the former as a derogatory/informal name. As we really should use Survivors, as they add an element of gameplay into the Celestial Ocean, I believe that Kara's Ark idea could help in this regard. <br /> <br /> I would also like to apologize in advance. My inspiration to write is dry at the moment, so if it's alright, I'm going to take a short break on writing. &gt;&lt;&quot; I'll hopefully get back onto the Abyssal Currents (which I've barely begun) by this Saturday.<br /> <br /> I'm also pleased to announce that SquamousBeauty has been online for abit, and I sent him a PM that if he desires to come back onto the Siren Thread, he may do so and he has shown some interest in returning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T16:15:50-07:00","id":863374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863299#post863299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...I don't know how I feel about mortals at least being able to survive the Deluge and becoming survivors. I don't know why. I think it's mainly because the other kinds of Realms have their own sort of &quot;native&quot; lifeform and humans are more of guests than anything. I would say at least the humans that aren't Flensers should be significantly altered. Sorta going back to the idea that the Deluge is both a physical and metaphysical thing, maybe the waves stripped away an essence of humanity from the survivors, rendering them a mere shadow of what they are now. It would give Ceto a stronger desire for wanting to protect the mortals who lived before the Deluge; having mortals live at basically full capacity would mean that there is some glimmer of hope of bringing back life as they knew it. By having the humans lose something vital through the Deluge, it would mean that they aren't the humans that Ceto grew to love; they are miserable creatures that have no hope, no spark of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I donno about this cuz on the one hand there are still people around sure, but humans are primarily land-dwelling creatures and without land and capacity of creating sustainable amounts of food and resources we would be fucked sooner or later. Even scavenging, beyond the danger, would be pretty limited as water will probably ruin most materials mankind could still use efficiently in a world were we don't have steady access to land and technology. The way I see it, humanity would be slowly decaying with the people left trying to endure as long as possible to try and run away from that inevitable point; which could still explain why Ceto wants to prevent such a fate where only fishes survive. Without land, a lot more than just humanity will die out, including birds and insects; which in and of itself can fuck at least a portion of sea life. Not ideal conditions.<br /> <br /> But yeah, no land no crops, no hunting; scavenging food ranges between difficult to impossible with everything underwater- nevermind dangers -and eating fish all the time would cause health problems without a varied cuisine. And that's without touching in other problems like having a lack of resources to efficiently maintain ships or create new technology and so on; humanity stagnates to death, in a painful manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T16:45:21-07:00","id":863382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863363#post863363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, if you don't mind that it'll kind of take out your idea. I'm sorry if it's bad.<br /> <br /> Although when it comes to Furies, might I suggest a small idea? I mean, we aren't going to directly state the eldritch force behind the Furies and Maelstrom, but as abit of fluff, I imagine that the Furies would only say that they are the products of the Earth and it's anger. Who or what is the &quot;Earth&quot; will be kept ambiguous. Maybe it's Gaia, sister of Ceto who, unlike Ceto, is more easily damagable and thus harder to repair. Maybe it's Behemoth, whose futile rage against Leviathan and his own inability to create life continues to this day through his Furies and the Sirens, who are one third of his blood. Maybe, the Current Sirens believe, it's Echidna, who voices through them to destroy what they love so the only connection left to existence is her. Of course, for the Current Sirens, the screams of denial from the Echidnals only fuel the rumors more.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's alright. I'm never super attached to things. Plus, if things work better when they get revamped, then that's all for the better. I like that we could incorporate the lore that we have been building up as possible explanations for the Furies. That works really well and plays into the whole idea that there is only so much that the Sirens know (such as with the limits on Tracing, the air of secrecy that Echidna has, and the fact that the Song is currently all broken up).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see, that's perfect. Now the only question is, should we portray any of these apocalyptic effects within the Celestial Ocean? One part about post apocalyptic scenarios is that there's still danger in the environment, even if it's not apparent. </div> </div> </div>I would say so. It could be that there are moments where it's becoming apparent that <i>something</i> is coming soon and that the Sirens that are currently within the Celestial Ocean should either prepare or evacuate. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's indeed the best way to put it. The Song was created by the weeping tears of dead humans, trying to reach back and stop the end from ever occurring. The Survivors however are not dead, or maybe the effort to create the Song simply sucked whatever was left of a soul out of them. That's not to say that they're under the effects of Soul Loss, but that they simply have the most hollow bits of a soul left in them. The consequence isn't totally magical, the Song isn't the only reason why they only have a shred of a soul left. Another reason is that they simply do not have a future left. Sure, if the Sirens succeed, then the Earth is not doomed in the past. But in the Future that is the Celestial Ocean, there's no salvation waiting for the survivors of the Deluge. Just because the past is fixed doesn't mean that their future will change, because they're separate.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm prolly getting the timelines stuff wrong, and if so, please correct me. This idea adds on some Grimdark/Fridge Horror to Siren, but I can't help but feel like &quot;there should be a way for the survivors to have even a marginally happy ending&quot;. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863374#post863374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I donno about this cuz on the one hand there are still people around sure, but humans are primarily land-dwelling creatures and without land and capacity of creating sustainable amounts of food and resources we would be fucked sooner or later. Even scavenging, beyond the danger, would be pretty limited as water will probably ruin most materials mankind could still use efficiently in a world were we don't have steady access to land and technology. The way I see it, humanity would be slowly decaying with the people left trying to endure as long as possible to try and run away from that inevitable point; which could still explain why Ceto wants to prevent such a fate where only fishes survive. Without land, a lot more than just humanity will die out, including birds and insects; which in and of itself can fuck at least a portion of sea life. Not ideal conditions.<br /> <br /> But yeah, no land no crops, no hunting; scavenging food ranges between difficult to impossible with everything underwater- nevermind dangers -and eating fish all the time would cause health problems without a varied cuisine. And that's without touching in other problems like having a lack of resources to efficiently maintain ships or create new technology and so on; humanity stagnates to death, in a painful manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my main grievance with having mortal survivors in the Celestial Ocean is that it feels much more like a &quot;Blue Book&quot; topic than a &quot;Siren&quot; topic. It would also depend on the general population of the survivors. How many would be assumed to be left alive? How does that number compare to the number of Sirens that exist within the Celestial Ocean and the number of Vodianoi that Echidna has created and released? <br /> <br /> I remember in one of the little fluff bits that I wrote that I interpreted the humans who drowned in the Deluge as effectively being in a state of stasis. They're drowning, but they aren't necessarily &quot;dead&quot;. The Song is what awakened some and allowed them to Surface as Sirens. We're still using the &quot;drowning&quot; and &quot;surfacing&quot; for when the Siren realizes that they aren't entirely human. Is there any way of this idea being how the humans are? Stuck in a state of stasis and constant suffering until they can be released for Surfacing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe that Flensers would have at least abit of interest in the Celestial Ocean, if that they'd think it was another aspect or way of getting to Sirens, whether through Survivors, kidnapping whatever Siren they find or perhaps even finding Echidnal Sirens hiding places and attacking them via pollution. One good part about the Celestial Ocean: It's already a dead land, so it won't hurt them to dump whatever pollution they have into the celestial ocean, especially since Sirens get aggravated from it. I do like your idea of making a hunter compact that deals with and/or against Sirens, but I believe that the Flensers should be one of the main antagonist of Siren. Hunter is another gameline and all, but I'm not against the idea of making a compact as an example for Siren Hunters that aren't Flensers. </div> </div> </div>I was gonna say that hunting other supernaturals for the Flensers is like the Malleus Maleficarus hunting non-vampires and non-witches: it happens every now and then but it's not what they focus on. Flensers would hunt Sirens because they know, beyond a shadow of a doubt, that Siren flesh is rejuvenating. However, being the sort of merchants that they are, they may attempt to expand and explore their options. After all, they may have taken down a werewolf on one of their Siren-hunts. What would happen if you cut a little of the Siren flesh with the grounded teeth of a wolfman?<br /> <br /> And it would be interesting to see more examples of mortals that make life harder for the Sirens. How would a Siren handle her mission when her mission involves saving these people that she believes should not be saved? But I see your point of Hunter being a different line. The Flensers would be the big issue that would cause a Siren danger while the Explorer!Hunters are more of a nuisance that can be somewhat safely dealt with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seeing this, I believe that the Siren main city should be in or somewhere near Florida. The reasoning being of the myth that Ponce De Leon, the first governor of Puerto Rico, had went unto Florida in search of the Fountain of Youth. Not to mention that the BP Oil Spill is generally still fresh in people's memories, although to be on the safe side, we should find a city that's been having pollution problems before the Oil Spill.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the hunters could be known as &quot;Conquistadors of Leon&quot; or &quot;Ponce's Pirates&quot;, maybe even both with the former as a derogatory/informal name. As we really should use Survivors, as they add an element of gameplay into the Celestial Ocean, I believe that Kara's Ark idea could help in this regard. </div> </div> </div>Do you think the Celestial Ocean should be a part of the &quot;Storytelling&quot; section or would it work better as an Appendix that expands into the actual details of the Celestial Ocean? It definitely seems very extensive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also like to apologize in advance. My inspiration to write is dry at the moment, so if it's alright, I'm going to take a short break on writing. &gt;&lt;&quot; I'll hopefully get back onto the Abyssal Currents (which I've barely begun) by this Saturday.<br /> <br /> I'm also pleased to announce that SquamousBeauty has been online for abit, and I sent him a PM that if he desires to come back onto the Siren Thread, he may do so and he has shown some interest in returning. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>No worries. We'll try to keep the idea train rolling so that we have some possible topics to explore on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T17:35:00-07:00","id":863397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863382#post863382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say so. It could be that there are moments where it's becoming apparent that <i>something</i> is coming soon and that the Sirens that are currently within the Celestial Ocean should either prepare or evacuate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties, then if nothing else, there's already some tilts in the GMC book that we could use that could be disasters happening in the oceans. Polaria suffering from regular bouts of the Extreme Cold and Ice (maybe should make appropriate for underwater, such as Frozen Over? The place is just so cold and unpredictable that it's hard to swim regularly) Tilts, Tropicana from the Extreme Heat Tilt. Gardenia suffers from the Tsunami Tilt (modified Earthquake tilt to work underwater and rolling to resist not being thrashed about in the water), Freshwater suffers from the Manmade Disease Tilt (let's say that Freshwater suffers disease storms every once in awhile, and if you're caught you must make a Stamina + Akashic Record roll per turn you spend in the storm. Failure means you become inflicted with the Sick Tilt, specifically the Grave version). Vaporia suffers from the Radiation tilt, which is abit like Freshwater's save that instead of inflicting the Sick tilt, it inflicts the Poisoned Tilt, Grave version. Finally, Discordia. Let's say that Discordia randomly suffers one of the above Tilts.<br /> <br /> Normally, survivors (and Sirens) within the Waters only suffer these tilts after a scene has passed and they're outside of a Grotto for the Scene. However, when a storm is about to hit, then they suffer the said tilt each turn, or however the tilt is normally supposed to affect places. <br /> <br /> With this in mind, I'd like to suggest that Echidna has basically used Verses to stabilize her portions of the Celestial Ocean. I do imagine it's possible to use Area/Global-Weather-Freeze/Temper/Earth/Disease/Radiation-Calm to stop a storm from going on in the area the Siren's at in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863382#post863382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my main grievance with having mortal survivors in the Celestial Ocean is that it feels much more like a &quot;Blue Book&quot; topic than a &quot;Siren&quot; topic. It would also depend on the general population of the survivors. How many would be assumed to be left alive? How does that number compare to the number of Sirens that exist within the Celestial Ocean and the number of Vodianoi that Echidna has created and released?</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's more of a concern that they're human rather than a different being altogether? I can see the problem, but how about this as a comparison. Geist the Sin Eaters deals with the Underworld, which is filled with Ghosts. They're essentially dead humans, and yet the splat can still interact with them on a daily basis in a way that it isn't considered entirely blue book. Same for Spirits and Werewolves. Does this perhaps solve the grievance? <br /> <br /> Kind of like ghosts, the Survivors of the Deluge were once human. Once. However, they've been so fundamentally changed that they can be considered as in another state of being altogether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863382#post863382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember in one of the little fluff bits that I wrote that I interpreted the humans who drowned in the Deluge as effectively being in a state of stasis. They're drowning, but they aren't necessarily &quot;dead&quot;. The Song is what awakened some and allowed them to Surface as Sirens. We're still using the &quot;drowning&quot; and &quot;surfacing&quot; for when the Siren realizes that they aren't entirely human. Is there any way of this idea being how the humans are? Stuck in a state of stasis and constant suffering until they can be released for Surfacing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. I think a new problem arises. The factor that the humans in stasis would become Sirens...when the Deluge happens more than likely in the future. Imagine if a person drowned in the 1800s. There's no way that they'd still be in stasis in the 2000s, since the Deluge would've happened sometime after the 2000s. <br /> <br /> How about this to kind of solve it: When a Siren drowns and sees the other humans in stasis, they're basically seeing all of the Sirens that were and the Sirens that are to be? They see into the past and future of the Song, like a recording that plays in their head. This way, there can be a distinction between a Survivor and a &quot;Static Siren&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, if this is a bad idea and they're wanted to be the same beings, I think the best way to put them both as the same thing would be that the Celestial Ocean changes to reflect how the places would be affected if circumstances are not messed with. For example, the real world may look pristine, but within it hides a company whose secret works are damaging the local nature. This reflects in the Celestial Ocean with the place being controlled by Freshwater, as humanity is causing the conflicts and it perhaps shows a building of the company that doesn't exist in reality, but is known to be planned to be built in the future. The people in the Celestial Ocean are also basically the same as the people in reality, except that they're basically like puppets, mimicking their old lives like nothing's changed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863382#post863382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was gonna say that hunting other supernaturals for the Flensers is like the Malleus Maleficarus hunting non-vampires and non-witches: it happens every now and then but it's not what they focus on. Flensers would hunt Sirens because they know, beyond a shadow of a doubt, that Siren flesh is rejuvenating. However, being the sort of merchants that they are, they may attempt to expand and explore their options. After all, they may have taken down a werewolf on one of their Siren-hunts. What would happen if you cut a little of the Siren flesh with the grounded teeth of a wolfman?<br /> <br /> And it would be interesting to see more examples of mortals that make life harder for the Sirens. How would a Siren handle her mission when her mission involves saving these people that she believes should not be saved? But I see your point of Hunter being a different line. The Flensers would be the big issue that would cause a Siren danger while the Explorer!Hunters are more of a nuisance that can be somewhat safely dealt with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It's prolly obvious already from the way they've been talked about on this thread, but Flensers are definitely people/corporations who make money off of exploiting the environment and making it suffer, that gives perhaps abit more characterization to them outside of people who eat Siren Flesh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863382#post863382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think the Celestial Ocean should be a part of the &quot;Storytelling&quot; section or would it work better as an Appendix that expands into the actual details of the Celestial Ocean? It definitely seems very extensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the Celestial Ocean should perhaaaaps....be in the same section that Werewolf puts the Shadow or where Geist puts the Underworld. If they either don't describe it in either of those books or it's unclear, I think it should be as part of the Appendix section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:59:05-07:00","id":865281,"title":"","content":"Pardon my double post, but I was wondering. There's something else we need to add to Systems and Advantages outside of Maelstrom mechanics (what were they again if I may ask? I know they involved having two conditions). Namely, what happens to a Siren at Lucidity 0? What do they become? My only idea is that they basically become what Sirens are renowned for. They freely wreck people, places and things for shits and giggles, they kill whoever they meet because all they desire is Pneuma...and the thought's stopped. Easy come, easy go. &gt;&gt;&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T18:02:52-07:00","id":865769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=863397#post863397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alrighties, then if nothing else, there's already some tilts in the GMC book that we could use that could be disasters happening in the oceans. Polaria suffering from regular bouts of the Extreme Cold and Ice (maybe should make appropriate for underwater, such as Frozen Over? The place is just so cold and unpredictable that it's hard to swim regularly) Tilts, Tropicana from the Extreme Heat Tilt. Gardenia suffers from the Tsunami Tilt (modified Earthquake tilt to work underwater and rolling to resist not being thrashed about in the water), Freshwater suffers from the Manmade Disease Tilt (let's say that Freshwater suffers disease storms every once in awhile, and if you're caught you must make a Stamina + Akashic Record roll per turn you spend in the storm. Failure means you become inflicted with the Sick Tilt, specifically the Grave version). Vaporia suffers from the Radiation tilt, which is abit like Freshwater's save that instead of inflicting the Sick tilt, it inflicts the Poisoned Tilt, Grave version. Finally, Discordia. Let's say that Discordia randomly suffers one of the above Tilts.<br /> <br /> Normally, survivors (and Sirens) within the Waters only suffer these tilts after a scene has passed and they're outside of a Grotto for the Scene. However, when a storm is about to hit, then they suffer the said tilt each turn, or however the tilt is normally supposed to affect places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm completely down for all of these. I would say we could rework the Vaporian Disaster as the Heavy Wind Tilt (and probably rename it Strong Currents) to represent the force of the wind pushing about while the Discordian Disaster could be the Radiation Tilt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With this in mind, I'd like to suggest that Echidna has basically used Verses to stabilize her portions of the Celestial Ocean. I do imagine it's possible to use Area/Global-Weather-Freeze/Temper/Earth/Disease/Radiation-Calm to stop a storm from going on in the area the Siren's at in question. </div> </div> </div>I can definitely see this. Perhaps Echidna has some Sentry Sirens who are assigned warding duty and are constantly singing a Verse of [Area/Global] - [Weather] - [The Respective Opus] - [Calm] to protect the territories that Echidna has calmed or values.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it's more of a concern that they're human rather than a different being altogether? I can see the problem, but how about this as a comparison. Geist the Sin Eaters deals with the Underworld, which is filled with Ghosts. They're essentially dead humans, and yet the splat can still interact with them on a daily basis in a way that it isn't considered entirely blue book. Same for Spirits and Werewolves. Does this perhaps solve the grievance?<br /> <br /> Kind of like ghosts, the Survivors of the Deluge were once human. Once. However, they've been so fundamentally changed that they can be considered as in another state of being altogether. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I think we need a sort of basis for the Survivors. What do they look like? How do they act? How do they think? <br /> <br /> As a frame of reference, I kinda want to compare them to the Ghost People from Fallout 3: Dead Money. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://fallout.wikia.com/wiki/Ghost_people\" target=\"_blank\">http://fallout.wikia.com/wiki/Ghost_people</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hrm. I think a new problem arises. The factor that the humans in stasis would become Sirens...when the Deluge happens more than likely in the future. Imagine if a person drowned in the 1800s. There's no way that they'd still be in stasis in the 2000s, since the Deluge would've happened sometime after the 2000s.<br /> <br /> How about this to kind of solve it: When a Siren drowns and sees the other humans in stasis, they're basically seeing all of the Sirens that were and the Sirens that are to be? They see into the past and future of the Song, like a recording that plays in their head. This way, there can be a distinction between a Survivor and a &quot;Static Siren&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I'm good for this idea if we can continue solidifying the look and feel of the Survivors. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe that the Celestial Ocean should perhaaaaps....be in the same section that Werewolf puts the Shadow or where Geist puts the Underworld. If they either don't describe it in either of those books or it's unclear, I think it should be as part of the Appendix section? </div> </div> </div>I know that Princess describes the Dreamlands in the Appendix. We could probably mention the Celestial Ocean a bit in the Storytelling area while going into detail in the Appendix.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pardon my double post, but I was wondering. There's something else we need to add to Systems and Advantages outside of Maelstrom mechanics (what were they again if I may ask? I know they involved having two conditions). Namely, what happens to a Siren at Lucidity 0? What do they become? My only idea is that they basically become what Sirens are renowned for. They freely wreck people, places and things for shits and giggles, they kill whoever they meet because all they desire is Pneuma...and the thought's stopped. Easy come, easy go. &gt;&gt;&quot; </div> </div> </div>Hmm...We haven't talked much about the Banshees or the Breathless ever since we brought them up either. I know that the Banshees are starved for Pneuma because they cannot naturally gain Pneuma from any kind of Water. I also ended up comparing the Banshees to Draugrs, the Humanity 0 version of Vampires. We could probably wrap up everything so that Lucidity 0 Sirens become Banshees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:25:17-07:00","id":866051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=865769#post865769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm completely down for all of these. I would say we could rework the Vaporian Disaster as the Heavy Wind Tilt (and probably rename it Strong Currents) to represent the force of the wind pushing about while the Discordian Disaster could be the Radiation Tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, that sounds perfect enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=865769#post865769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can definitely see this. Perhaps Echidna has some Sentry Sirens who are assigned warding duty and are constantly singing a Verse of [Area/Global] - [Weather] - [The Respective Opus] - [Calm] to protect the territories that Echidna has calmed or values.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If I may note (although it prolly goes without saying), perhaps another benefit when it comes to Grottos is that while a Siren, Survivor or anyone in the Celestial Ocean is in one, they are considered immune to the effects the Disaster has, or perhaps mitigates some of it? <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I still need to list out how Grottos are exactly like. What I have so far is basically like Changeling the Lost Hollows and Mage the Awakening Sanctums.<br /> <br /> Grotto (1+, Special)<br /> Has two traits which can rank from one to five. Security and Insulation. Security measures how defensible the Grotto is, how hard it is to enter it for those it does not belong to. For each dot in Security, add a penalty to all attempts to break into the Grotto. Insulation on the other hand measures how well the Grotto keeps the outside waters and the disasterous weather out. For each dot in Insulation, add an equivalent bonus to all rolls when a Disaster is taking effect.<br /> <br /> I can't help but feel like it should have a third trait, like most other Sanctum/Hollow/Haven merits, but I'm fine if there isn't. Security and Insulation at least cover apocalypse bunker themes and also &quot;safety vault&quot; where Sirens can place all of their Treasures or Trinkets, like Ariel in the Little Mermaid (although I'm talking more the disney version).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=865769#post865769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I think we need a sort of basis for the Survivors. What do they look like? How do they act? How do they think?<br /> <br /> As a frame of reference, I kinda want to compare them to the Ghost People from Fallout 3: Dead Money.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://fallout.wikia.com/wiki/Ghost_people\" target=\"_blank\">http://fallout.wikia.com/wiki/Ghost_people</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I think this is a good enough reference.<br /> <br /> I think I can at least give my ideas on what they look like too. They look like perhaps a direct mix of fish and human that aren't completely either. Their eyes look like a fish's, they have gills on their necks (can breathe underwater) and may (or may not) still be able to breathe on land. Their hands are webbed and they have small extensions of fins down their arms, and their feet are like flippers. Are we still sort of going with the idea that they're people who've been altered by Echidna to be able to live underwater? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=865769#post865769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm good for this idea if we can continue solidifying the look and feel of the Survivors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, now the only question is, what do we do with these static Sirens? I think they shouldn't be easily messed with, or even visible in the Celestial Ocean unless if a Siren was using Trace or Area-Water-Human-Sense.<br /> <br /> Actually, I have an idea. It's been a legend that mermaids can be created by one mermaid drowning a human and making them into one themselves? It's kind of like how Vampires do the Embrace. This is something I felt that should be included in Siren somehow, but I didn't know how to, but your relisting of the static humans now gives me an idea. Basically, I imagine a Siren does an extended action of taking all of the Pneuma away from a human while drowning them in the Celestial Ocean, specifically where their static self is at. Although like Vampire, this drains a point of Akashic Record from a Siren to do, as they're ripping a piece of the Song from themselves and imbuing it into the human they've got. <br /> <br /> How does this sound if I may ask? The idea can be dropped if it's bad. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=865769#post865769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that Princess describes the Dreamlands in the Appendix. We could probably mention the Celestial Ocean a bit in the Storytelling area while going into detail in the Appendix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. This is good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=865769#post865769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...We haven't talked much about the Banshees or the Breathless ever since we brought them up either. I know that the Banshees are starved for Pneuma because they cannot naturally gain Pneuma from any kind of Water. I also ended up comparing the Banshees to Draugrs, the Humanity 0 version of Vampires. We could probably wrap up everything so that Lucidity 0 Sirens become Banshees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty then. Is there anything special about Banshees we should note? I think they should be naturally within the Celestial Ocean, able to rip gates into reality (we still need to talk about how this is possible. I'm willing to say that any Siren can enter the Celestial Ocean from a pool of water large enough to hold her entire diluvian form) and striking for Pneuma before returning to the Celestial Ocean like the starved animals they are. They basically almost only ever come to reality to get Pneuma?<br /> <br /> Heck, we could even liken it to like how people can't survive without water, Banshees can't survive without Pneuma, aka air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:45:06-07:00","id":866921,"title":"","content":"I know I was meant to post something of the Abyssal Currents yesterday, and I apologize to say that I basically got borked from two college papers I had to write. =m= I'll just throw up what little I wrote/managed to get up. EDIT: I've managed to finish up Acheron as I originally promised.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 04-18-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T17:43:12-07:00","id":867952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=866051#post866051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. If I may note (although it prolly goes without saying), perhaps another benefit when it comes to Grottos is that while a Siren, Survivor or anyone in the Celestial Ocean is in one, they are considered immune to the effects the Disaster has, or perhaps mitigates some of it?<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I still need to list out how Grottos are exactly like. What I have so far is basically like Changeling the Lost Hollows and Mage the Awakening Sanctums.<br /> <br /> Grotto (1+, Special)<br /> Has two traits which can rank from one to five. Security and Insulation. Security measures how defensible the Grotto is, how hard it is to enter it for those it does not belong to. For each dot in Security, add a penalty to all attempts to break into the Grotto. Insulation on the other hand measures how well the Grotto keeps the outside waters and the disasterous weather out. For each dot in Insulation, add an equivalent bonus to all rolls when a Disaster is taking effect.<br /> <br /> I can't help but feel like it should have a third trait, like most other Sanctum/Hollow/Haven merits, but I'm fine if there isn't. Security and Insulation at least cover apocalypse bunker themes and also &quot;safety vault&quot; where Sirens can place all of their Treasures or Trinkets, like Ariel in the Little Mermaid (although I'm talking more the disney version).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the missing third trait was the Size of the Grotto, as many of the &quot;Safe Place&quot; merits have a Size trait. <br /> <br /> On a side-note, the Safe Places did have a slight change with 2E. Namely, the specific creature's Safe Place requires at least one dot in the Safe Place merit before the creature can receive their Safe Place. For Vampires, the new Haven allows them to sense danger when asleep and increases their general capabilities. For Werewolves, their Dedicated Locus gives them easier access to Essence. We could follow this trend and have the Grotto protect the Sirens from the disasters in the Celestial Ocean and offer a place for the Sirens to converge while in the Celestial Ocean, as the new Safe Place already protects the area from being broken into.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. I think this is a good enough reference.<br /> <br /> I think I can at least give my ideas on what they look like too. They look like perhaps a direct mix of fish and human that aren't completely either. Their eyes look like a fish's, they have gills on their necks (can breathe underwater) and may (or may not) still be able to breathe on land. Their hands are webbed and they have small extensions of fins down their arms, and their feet are like flippers. Are we still sort of going with the idea that they're people who've been altered by Echidna to be able to live underwater? </div> </div> </div>They sound a little like the Deep One hybrids from Lovecraft. We could say that they were essentially a beta-test made by Echidna in order to experiment with mass-alterations. Sorta like the Survivors were proto-Vodianoi that were not correctly altered and were eventually abandoned. The mixture of the physical transformation and the constant exposure to the harsh conditions of the Celestial Ocean could have caused further alterations that Echidna could not anticipate, leading to the sort of disdain that she has for the Survivors. I can see Echidna caring more for her Vodianoi, seeing them as her actual children, while abandoning the Survivors, seeing them as mistakes that she cannot repeat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alright, now the only question is, what do we do with these static Sirens? I think they shouldn't be easily messed with, or even visible in the Celestial Ocean unless if a Siren was using Trace or Area-Water-Human-Sense.<br /> <br /> Actually, I have an idea. It's been a legend that mermaids can be created by one mermaid drowning a human and making them into one themselves? It's kind of like how Vampires do the Embrace. This is something I felt that should be included in Siren somehow, but I didn't know how to, but your relisting of the static humans now gives me an idea. Basically, I imagine a Siren does an extended action of taking all of the Pneuma away from a human while drowning them in the Celestial Ocean, specifically where their static self is at. Although like Vampire, this drains a point of Akashic Record from a Siren to do, as they're ripping a piece of the Song from themselves and imbuing it into the human they've got.<br /> <br /> How does this sound if I may ask? The idea can be dropped if it's bad. &gt;&gt; </div> </div> </div>That would be interesting. I can see some Gardenians and Polarians choosing to &quot;enlist&quot; some new Sirens though this method. It would also allow for some interesting scenarios and ramifications, such as how the new Sirens are treated by Sirens who were &quot;naturally&quot; created by suffering from the Drowning and Surfacing. Perhaps this could create some Choruses that focus on being the &quot;Original Generation&quot; Sirens for being the &quot;Enlisted&quot; Sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alrighty then. Is there anything special about Banshees we should note? I think they should be naturally within the Celestial Ocean, able to rip gates into reality (we still need to talk about how this is possible. I'm willing to say that any Siren can enter the Celestial Ocean from a pool of water large enough to hold her entire diluvian form) and striking for Pneuma before returning to the Celestial Ocean like the starved animals they are. They basically almost only ever come to reality to get Pneuma?<br /> <br /> Heck, we could even liken it to like how people can't survive without water, Banshees can't survive without Pneuma, aka air. </div> </div> </div>Here is what I wrote up for the original idea for Banshees:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I believe that Banshees would be an antagonist the same way that a Draugr in <b>Vampire</b> would be an antagonist; they are more tragic monsters that need to be put down for their own sake and for the sake of the world. When Sirens surface, they are aware of the world in real time and the world in The Deluge; they are able to distinctly see and understand the two worlds as being separate entities. With Banshees, they see the world as both reality and The Deluge simultaneously. They see skyscrapers and restaurants as monuments of an old civilization shattered by water pressure. They see the sun blocked out by the sea, the light bouncing back and forth along the ripples of the waves. They see the drowned, bloated corpses of the people they used to know <i>standing in front of them and talking about the new baby</i>. <s><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">In terms of game mechanics, Banshees have a Lucidity of N/A. While a Siren can reach Lucidity 0, she doesn't become a Banshee. More-likely, we could work in Lucidity 0 Sirens as those who follow Echidna. Banshees have a Lucidity of N/A because, unlike Lucidity 0 Sirens, Banshees cannot aspire to see the world beyond it being a state of gestalt horror. Lucidity 0 Sirens still see the world, though under a different light. The blending of the two worlds places the Banshees in a state of pure torment in which they can do nothing but feel horror. Their Akashic Record is also N/A, as they are always connected to The Deluge</span></s><br /> <br /> The only way that Banshees are able to feel any sort of respite from this pain is to steal away Pneuma. However, there are a few issues with this. Because Banshees were never able to surface, they do not have a favored Water, so they cannot regain Pneuma from being submerged in water. They are only able to gain Pneuma by stealing it away from mortals. This is usually done via force, literally taking the air out of a human's lungs through a kiss of death or straight-out murdering the human. Some Banshees attempt to go about this in a subtle manner, sneaking into homes and stealing the life from the sleeping mortals. Others are more explicit, appearing as ghostly apparitions and leading unsuspecting humans to an early death. If the Banshee is lucky, they'll be able to rest for the week. If the Banshee is not, it means another day of suffering.<br /> <br /> Banshees are also locked in a perpetual Trace, seeing the paths and actions that have lead to certain events. This Trace bleeds the Banshees of their Pneuma, which is why they hunger for the life force. Banshees suffer from a specialized version of Maelstrom where, instead of wanting to destroy things that mock their suffering, they feel temporary release when they are able to push them into motion. Their Trace allows them to see things that matter to humanity, things that are deemed important and are in contact with humans on a daily basis. By being an agent of destruction, Banshees are able to mitigate their pain, even for a slight instant. <br /> <br /> I feel that Banshees also have access to one Opus. There is no Introduction or Conclusion. Banshees are constantly howling the raw, primal force of the Opus, affecting the world through sheer power. The sudden drought that has been popping up in a single country? A Banshee invoking [Light]. A group of business people wandering into the middle of a busy street. A Banshee invoking [Human]. They are invoking a single Opus without an Introduction or Conclusion, allowing it to flow wildly and affect whatever comes near. If a Siren wants to invoke the same Opus that the Banshee is, the two Verses become locked into a <i>Concerto Grosso</i>. Once we solidify the rules for <i>Concerto Grosso</i>, the Banshees will probably have a slightly modified version considering that Banshees do not use a traditional Verse.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wrote them so that they were more terrestrial creatures tied to the material realm, but it could be that they bob between the material realm and the Celestial Ocean, possibly more when they begin hungering for Pneuma. It could be that Survivors carry no Pneuma, which is why the Banshees hunt down mortals in the material realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=866921#post866921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I was meant to post something of the Abyssal Currents yesterday, and I apologize to say that I basically got borked from two college papers I had to write. =m= I'll just throw up what little I wrote/managed to get up. EDIT: I've managed to finish up Acheron as I originally promised.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about it. Real life comes before this. Acheron sounds incredibly dark and I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T18:50:10-07:00","id":868028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=867952#post867952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the missing third trait was the Size of the Grotto, as many of the &quot;Safe Place&quot; merits have a Size trait.<br /> <br /> On a side-note, the Safe Places did have a slight change with 2E. Namely, the specific creature's Safe Place requires at least one dot in the Safe Place merit before the creature can receive their Safe Place. For Vampires, the new Haven allows them to sense danger when asleep and increases their general capabilities. For Werewolves, their Dedicated Locus gives them easier access to Essence. We could follow this trend and have the Grotto protect the Sirens from the disasters in the Celestial Ocean and offer a place for the Sirens to converge while in the Celestial Ocean, as the new Safe Place already protects the area from being broken into.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES. That's the lost trait, it literally slipped my mind. XD And I see. Would that take out the Insulation part of the merit? I don't mind it's loss, I actually had an idea for something that could replace it. Accomadation, it ranks from 1 to 5 and ranks how many people the Grotto can take care of basic needs for, which include sleep, shelter from the outside and nourishment. It's rank cannot be higher than Size dots.<br /> <br /> This way, I imagine that one Grotto could perhaps be enough for an Undersea village by Grotto Size 5, Accomadation 5. I imagine that Accomadation also still fits the apocalypse bunker themes, as it's a part of the merit that would require upkeep to maintain. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=867952#post867952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They sound a little like the Deep One hybrids from Lovecraft. We could say that they were essentially a beta-test made by Echidna in order to experiment with mass-alterations. Sorta like the Survivors were proto-Vodianoi that were not correctly altered and were eventually abandoned. The mixture of the physical transformation and the constant exposure to the harsh conditions of the Celestial Ocean could have caused further alterations that Echidna could not anticipate, leading to the sort of disdain that she has for the Survivors. I can see Echidna caring more for her Vodianoi, seeing them as her actual children, while abandoning the Survivors, seeing them as mistakes that she cannot repeat.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps for more mental imagery: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3tTHn2tHhcI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3tTHn2tHhcI</a><br /> <br /> But a small bit of joking aside, this is a good idea, and also seems to fit within Echidna's theme of mutagenics. If I might also add, I imagine that given her abilities, she might still kidnap survivors from time to time. Sure, they were mistakes, but with her powers, she can &quot;correct&quot; those mistakes and make them into the Vodianoi they're meant to be. Now what about Survivors personality wise. Do they still have an ability to communicate? How do they get along with another Survivor not of their own? <br /> <br /> Would it be fitting if they had their Virtue and Vice reversed? Simply put, they regain all of their willpower when they do their Vice and only get one dot when they do their Virtue. The reason being that every day in the Celestial Ocean is another attempt at survival, and as such a Survivor cannot be generous or selfless with their equipment, supplies and the like. If there were survivors like that, then they're long dead, having been taken advantage of already. As such, Survivors need to be selfish and take care of their own/themselves first. This is the only way that any Survivor can hope to survive longer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=867952#post867952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be interesting. I can see some Gardenians and Polarians choosing to &quot;enlist&quot; some new Sirens though this method. It would also allow for some interesting scenarios and ramifications, such as how the new Sirens are treated by Sirens who were &quot;naturally&quot; created by suffering from the Drowning and Surfacing. Perhaps this could create some Choruses that focus on being the &quot;Original Generation&quot; Sirens for being the &quot;Enlisted&quot; Sirens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty then. :3 I also imagine it makes it a hell of a lot easier for scenarios. It could explain why Acheron isn't a fully dead Current (they simply drown more people who want to end everything).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=867952#post867952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is what I wrote up for the original idea for Banshees:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin