at Banshees also have access to one Opus. There is no Introduction or Conclusion. Banshees are constantly howling the raw, primal force of the Opus, affecting the world through sheer power. The sudden drought that has been popping up in a single country? A Banshee invoking [Light]. A group of business people wandering into the middle of a busy street. A Banshee invoking [Human]. They are invoking a single Opus without an Introduction or Conclusion, allowing it to flow wildly and affect whatever comes near. If a Siren wants to invoke the same Opus that the Banshee is, the two Verses become locked into a <i>Concerto Grosso</i>. Once we solidify the rules for <i>Concerto Grosso</i>, the Banshees will probably have a slightly modified version considering that Banshees do not use a traditional Verse.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wrote them so that they were more terrestrial creatures tied to the material realm, but it could be that they bob between the material realm and the Celestial Ocean, possibly more when they begin hungering for Pneuma. It could be that Survivors carry no Pneuma, which is why the Banshees hunt down mortals in the material realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. This is fitting for the game, is it fine if they're between the realms? Just making sure. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=867952#post867952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry about it. Real life comes before this. Acheron sounds incredibly dark and I love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I was hoping to capture that aspect in it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T19:34:56-07:00","id":868074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=868028#post868028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YES. That's the lost trait, it literally slipped my mind. XD And I see. Would that take out the Insulation part of the merit? I don't mind it's loss, I actually had an idea for something that could replace it. Accomadation, it ranks from 1 to 5 and ranks how many people the Grotto can take care of basic needs for, which include sleep, shelter from the outside and nourishment. It's rank cannot be higher than Size dots.<br /> <br /> This way, I imagine that one Grotto could perhaps be enough for an Undersea village by Grotto Size 5, Accomadation 5. I imagine that Accomadation also still fits the apocalypse bunker themes, as it's a part of the merit that would require upkeep to maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would definitely be interesting. It would also allow us to continue fleshing out the qualities of the Celestial Ocean. I never actually thought about some basic things like renewable resources or even food and how that would change in the Celestial Ocean. Now we have a way of breaching that subject and giving it some weight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it helps for more mental imagery: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3tTHn2tHhcI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3tTHn2tHhcI</a><br /> <br /> But a small bit of joking aside, this is a good idea, and also seems to fit within Echidna's theme of mutagenics. If I might also add, I imagine that given her abilities, she might still kidnap survivors from time to time. Sure, they were mistakes, but with her powers, she can &quot;correct&quot; those mistakes and make them into the Vodianoi they're meant to be. Now what about Survivors personality wise. Do they still have an ability to communicate? How do they get along with another Survivor not of their own?<br /> <br /> Would it be fitting if they had their Virtue and Vice reversed? Simply put, they regain all of their willpower when they do their Vice and only get one dot when they do their Virtue. The reason being that every day in the Celestial Ocean is another attempt at survival, and as such a Survivor cannot be generous or selfless with their equipment, supplies and the like. If there were survivors like that, then they're long dead, having been taken advantage of already. As such, Survivors need to be selfish and take care of their own/themselves first. This is the only way that any Survivor can hope to survive longer. </div> </div> </div>Personality-wise, I feel that the Survivors, baseline, do not have any Pneuma and do not have that sort of spark of life. Sort of like the Breathless. I'd say that they are emotionally drained and are more concerned about scavenging and survival than they are interacting and creating support networks. No pack means that all the food they find is for themselves. I would say that they would be almost non-verbal due to their lack of need to communicate with others, as well. Some Survivors may band together (especially when a Siren is attempting to protect them from Echidna and her sentries), but it's less due to their chemistry and more due to the practical sense of having a larger group to carry more food and defend the supplies. <br /> <br /> I can see a lot of sense for a Survivor to have their Virtue and Vice switched. It would also probably explain how being a Survivor changes humans from being social creatures to being solitary creatures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. This is fitting for the game, is it fine if they're between the realms? Just making sure. :3 </div> </div> </div>I don't see a reason to discourage it. It mirrors how a Siren is generally in the material realm but eventually comes into the Celestial Ocean to take care of any business she has in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T20:42:52-07:00","id":868132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=868074#post868074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would definitely be interesting. It would also allow us to continue fleshing out the qualities of the Celestial Ocean. I never actually thought about some basic things like renewable resources or even food and how that would change in the Celestial Ocean. Now we have a way of breaching that subject and giving it some weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties, taking out Insulation and replacing with Accomadation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=868074#post868074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personality-wise, I feel that the Survivors, baseline, do not have any Pneuma and do not have that sort of spark of life. Sort of like the Breathless. I'd say that they are emotionally drained and are more concerned about scavenging and survival than they are interacting and creating support networks. No pack means that all the food they find is for themselves. I would say that they would be almost non-verbal due to their lack of need to communicate with others, as well. Some Survivors may band together (especially when a Siren is attempting to protect them from Echidna and her sentries), but it's less due to their chemistry and more due to the practical sense of having a larger group to carry more food and defend the supplies.<br /> <br /> I can see a lot of sense for a Survivor to have their Virtue and Vice switched. It would also probably explain how being a Survivor changes humans from being social creatures to being solitary creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, this sounds good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=868074#post868074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a reason to discourage it. It mirrors how a Siren is generally in the material realm but eventually comes into the Celestial Ocean to take care of any business she has in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok then.<br /> <br /> After we finish the Abyssal Currents, what comes next? Flensers and Furies? Ack, we should prolly continue with the Survivors and fleshing out the Celestial Ocean before touching those two, but to set it out before I forget, here's the ideas I had on the Furies.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If so, I somewhat have some beginning ideas on Furies and Quagmires, their mechanics at least and what they'd be considered as. Quagmire's are places filled with Resentment, and Furies are like the Spiritual Avatar of a Quagmire. A Quagmire has two tracks, one is Permanent Resentment and the other is Temporary Resentment. Temporary Resentment is like a fuel stat for Furies/the Quagmire that they use to power their Numina, and they have ways to get it back which are almost the same as ways to regain Pneuma, but only the &quot;killing a person to get it all back&quot; and &quot;dealing with a relationship&quot; ways work. Although for the latter part, the Furies get it back if they're dealing with someone they hate rather than love and they can do it without the Relationships merit.<br /> <br /> Permanent Resentment can raise or lower depending on if the Quagmire/Fury becomes appeased or if it's aggravated more, and killing the Fury doesn't destroy the Quagmire. As an added thing, my current thought on Furies is that they're like Ephemeral entities that can possess anything in the Resentment's domain for free and they can add up the Quagmire's Size (how much landmass it affects) and Permanent Resentment and spread the dots across Power, Resistance and Finesse for the Fury's stats.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T08:34:15-07:00","id":870222,"title":"","content":"Pardon the Double Post, but I finished Cocytus~<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:04:38-07:00","id":870431,"title":"","content":"Hey, Just updating my status: I'm going to finish The introduction formatting and The Currents too! Expect a new post soon this weekend! Nice work Saul, everything os so well written!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:22:42-07:00","id":871346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=870431#post870431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Just updating my status: I'm going to finish The introduction formatting and The Currents too! Expect a new post soon this weekend! Nice work Saul, everything os so well written!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thankies. :3 Lethe is next on the list, although I feel myself being abit stumped on them already. Would they be allies with the Flensers at all? Or not? The image I have for Flensers in my head is that they're like Pentex except more water based (think fishing industries who overfish or oil companies who dig into the depths. Here's a wiki article to explain Pentex. And yes, I'm aware that they're Werewolf the Apocalypse peeps. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Pentex\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Pentex</a><br /> <br /> Overall, there's Pentex and the Black Spiral Dancers, the Werewolves who've turned to the Wyrm (a force of entropy who's now crazy and wants to destroy everything) and who spread corruption throughout the world, naturally, spiritually and morally. They're basically trying to destroy everything, and Pentex has the same goal. <br /> <br /> Using this as a basis, let's look at the relationship between the two. Black Spiral Dancers and Pentex are working against other werewolves to destroy everything. Whereas, Mankind's Victory is working to advance Humanity's progress by whatever means necessary...and Flensers are working to make things worse the world over so more Sirens would surface so they can eat their flesh. Obviously, there's some bits of tension that can surface between Flensers and Lethe. Overall, here's my thoughts on the matter:<br /> <br /> Flensers and Lethe are both very much similar. The lower and mainly newer people in the organizations would be naive and believing that they're backing the right cause. Afterall, Humanity's got the right way to do things, who cares if a few trees fall where nobody can hear them. But the higher they go, then the more prevalent would the selfish mindset come into full view. Screw nature, humanity is the best way to do things, and in the case of the Flensers they'd add in &quot;we need more Sirens to eat and keep up our immortal lives&quot;. I believe that to resolve this, Flensers and Lethe would probably show themselves as an affable and genteel organization willing to help those &quot;genetically challenged&quot; to help conform into their new identities before filling them with propaganda of how Humanity has the right way. I imagine that for Sirens who didn't enter this way (Which would be any Siren not new to the game), they'd perhaps know that they're trying to advance human technology and damage nature. In this sense, I imagine some Sirens would join Lethe, if not out of the ideal of advancing technology, then out of spite towards the Furies and/or whatever force is behind their creation. Perhaps they've been hurt by Nature before. Perhaps the Furies have killed some Loved ones. Although as a rule, I imagine that if the Flensers worked with Mankind's Victory, they'd keep their habits of eating Siren flesh a secret from the entire Current. I'd also imagine that as a rule, anyone who's of a certain status in the Flensers above &quot;newbie/apprentice&quot; could have access to the Siren's flesh they've compiled over the years. I also imagine that Flensers do perhaps recommend Letheian Sirens to capture non-Letheian ones, to which the captured's fates can be one of two things. Either they're killed and put on ice away from Sirens eyes to eat their flesh later, they're turned over to the Current of Lethe to be indoctrinated (remember, Lethe's favored Conclusion is &quot;Control&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). I also imagine that if the highers up have extensive failures from Letheian Sirens, I can imagine them pulling &quot;you have outlived your usefulness&quot; and &quot;firing them&quot;. Mainly by killing them and saving their flesh.<br /> <br /> I can also imagine them encouraging research on the Siren condition, mainly as a way for humanity to try establishing dominion over what they don't understand. Mainly as experiments. For the most part, the higher ups are basically looking for new ways to make more Sirens that boil down to &quot;Sirens drown other people or nature becomes worse and calls despaired people into Sirens&quot;.<br /> <br /> In general, the Flensers are basically people who use &quot;for humanity's advancement&quot; as a front and really mean &quot;we want immortality in our lifetimes&quot;. Letheians here would be mostly unfortunate dupes, the ones who are naive would be in disbelief if the truth was revealed and the more sane ones would turn on them en masse. <br /> <br /> I think the only problem I have is that this makes the Flensers (and by extension the Current of Lethe) more akin to Leviathan 1e (what little there is)'s Marduk Society, where most of the members are optomists for humanity and their higher ups are Immortal sorcerors who eat Leviathan Flesh to maintain their immortality and powers. Since the Marduk Society in Leviathan 2e have seem to noticed the Sorcerors and decided &quot;fuck this&quot;, kicked them out and had an internal revolution and become more considerably grey, still trying to be heroes even though they've lost half their numbers, Is there still a problem with the Flensers being too close to the Marduck Society in this sense? <br /> <br /> Ah, and here's a small idea I had on the Flensers in a Mystery Cult form. I hope at least the last one is ESPECIALLY fitting~<br /> 1: Fishers. They're basically beginning in the Flensers tasked with menial jobs. They gain the Direction Sense Merit to represent always being able to find where they are in regard to being in nature.<br /> 2: Boatswain: They're Flensers tasked with more important jobs as they begin to get more initiated. They can get the Indomitable Merit without requiring Resolve 3, to represent becoming resistant to the Sirens manipulations and the like.<br /> 3: Second Mates: These Flensers are now beginning to know the actual meaning of the Flenser's beliefs and idealiologies, to eat Siren flesh to keep themselves alive. As such, a Flenser at this level may begin to partake in the Siren Flesh, and they also gain the Unseen Sense merit in regards to Sirens.<br /> 4: First Mates: These Flensers are ruthless bastards in regards to nature, and they gain the Alternate Identity Merit at 3 dots, all the better to throw anyone who're looking for them off their trails. <br /> 5: Captains: The leaders of the Flensers and the longest lived, and they know intuitively how to manipulate people and places to following their own ends. Some even claim they have supernatural powers from all the flesh they've eaten for the years...and they're not wrong. They gain the Psychometry Merit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T18:07:16-07:00","id":873421,"title":"","content":"Pardon the Double Post, just wanted to set up some updates! I added a few new Malformations to the Vodianoi, created and filled out ALOT of the Celestial Ocean Document, and added a Tilts section to the Conditions and Tilts Document. If I'm stumped on Lethe, it doesn't stop me from writing on other parts of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Edit: I'll just edit this post until there's replies so as not to triple or quadruple post. However, I've added Maelstrom to the Systems and Advantages as well as an explanation on the Banshees, which are now when a Siren lowers to Lucidity 0.<br /> <br /> Systems and Advantages: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dHPB-rGUo_ObHiCSzSkqhZYovEY56tKBBVwu2_i8eNw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Vodianoi: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-LQD_y7kgREnvf0Dg3U1uaDFRhMuOVJzM3UwckjjE8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Celestial Ocean: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NE26FQw_RvtHgU9TedHuMvVqAkWbuftaRF33mtRqIkc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> Conditions and Tilts: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nh62Lgt_318WJ26AT8zdc7pIW44xA08JS-WzBEUPVGs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 04-25-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:36:49-07:00","id":874896,"title":"","content":"Ok, I know that I'm making a triple post, but I don't care. I feel like I have a REALLY good idea on how to get past my borking on Letheians! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1417_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1417\" data-vbnamecard=\"1417\">Reaper Verse</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9279\" data-vbnamecard=\"9279\">Yads Dom</a>.<br /> <br /> So, you know how the Flensers eat Siren flesh to prolong their immortality and stuff right? And how that bit was because Flensers eat Siren flesh to sustain themselves? I have a way past that! What if the SIRENS in Lethe (at least the mid Status to high Status ones) ate other Sirens flesh too!? I mean, Sirens flesh can make people immortal so long as they keep eating it! So like if a Siren ate another Siren's flesh, wouldn't it freeze her aging for a time? They do still (if imperceptibly since they have a life expectancy of 300 years) age! Sirens who join Lethe not only want to destroy Nature, but they want to outlive it's downfall! So if both Sirens and Flensers eat other Sirens flesh, then they have no issues! I know I'm sounding excited, and it's because I feel like this is one huge breakthrough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Will edit further links onto this message until a different response from someone not myself.<br /> <br /> And I've also started editing the Alterations today. I hope it's fine, granted I didn't have any correspondence with Squamous nor has he appeared back on this thread.<br /> <br /> Alterations: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-Wn-NQHrxS_3vHMDurtCDx4A-sWZuY-ima6QFt4tO9I/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 05-02-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:22:42-07:00","id":881674,"title":"","content":"I know I said I wouldn't post again until someone else posted here, but I would like to note that it's finals week next week, which is why I haven't been working much on Siren. I'll come back to it after finals, sorry for the lack of update on my end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:39:14-07:00","id":891378,"title":"","content":"Pardon this new post. I'm finally done with finals. I decided to at least finish up Lethe before I posted again, so here it is. This is mainly working from the ideas of &quot;Lethe is allied with Flensers&quot;. Reaper, Yads, anyone, do you have any thoughts? I doubt I'll make any new posts unless if important things come up on my end, or unless if someone else (as in anyone who isn't me) posts on this thread. So until either or happens, I'll be editing in new news onto this post. For now, enjoy Lethe. :3<br /> <br /> Abyssal Currents: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:20:26-07:00","id":891745,"title":"","content":"Hey Saul!! Sorry for being gone for so long, life caught me good, I actually shoudn't be here while i'm at my job, but i'm using my citar break, so.<br /> <br /> I like how Lethe is conceived as an Antagonist/Core Playable Faction, it's a nice twist to The common style of The game. As always: Wonderfuly Written. You rock! I'll be around again as soon as I can, while that, of you want me to write something or to come up with mechanics, Just say, I'll do that while I c\u00e1!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:33:14-07:00","id":891811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=891745#post891745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Saul!! Sorry for being gone for so long, life caught me good, I actually shoudn't be here while i'm at my job, but i'm using my citar break, so.<br /> <br /> I like how Lethe is conceived as an Antagonist/Core Playable Faction, it's a nice twist to The common style of The game. As always: Wonderfuly Written. You rock! I'll be around again as soon as I can, while that, of you want me to write something or to come up with mechanics, Just say, I'll do that while I c\u00e1!</div> </div> </div> </div>Warning, this is abit TL;DR, sorry for that. D:<br /> <br /> It's alright. Pardon my saying I wouldn't post unless someone else did, I felt like I was posting too many times in a row. ^^&quot; But yes, I understand and don't worry. Life sadly comes first.<br /> <br /> I'm glad to see that Lethe is liked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If it's fine, I just want to see if the documents I've made in the past few weeks are good and mechanically sound. Which mainly includes the Celestial Ocean (All of what's currently there), Systems and Advantages (only Maelstrom, Flow and Beaching), Alterations and Vodianoi (Mainly Malformations) Documents. I should also note that in the Alterations Document, I pretty much had the idea of splitting up the 24 Skills into 24 Alterations, and giving 4 to each Water, meaning that each water will have four skills associated with it. I also set the bonus system for these skills (and certain other things) to be &quot;Half Akashic Record, rounded up&quot;. This way, the bonus created by Alterations is still malleable so to speak. I'll still set or find a way for Malformations to be mechanically more powerful though. Is this a good idea or a bad one?<br /> <br /> Though for all documents, I'd like to note that they're all still WIP, so nothing is really set in stone until we feel like we have a good system or story set up.<br /> <br /> I hope it's also fine to bring up, but I've also been having second thoughts on Conclusions. I know I said &quot;maybe they should be attached to an attribute to be used generically&quot;, but recently I've been getting the feeling that Verses (since the Abyssal Currents are nearly done, I'm starting to think on the Verses and their mechanics) might be <i>too </i>freeform. So to counteract this, I was thinking that Conclusions could perhaps be 1-5 Dot rated powers, with new powers or new levels of effectiveness being able to be drawn.<br /> <br /> For example, let's use the <b>Protect </b>Conclusion. When used as a verse, it'll automatically give it's dot level in Armor rating to the person, object or place it's used on to protect from damages. But there's a catch. The Opuses invoked in the Conclusion must be present, but the need for presence can lower the higher the dot level is. So if a Siren used Target-Water-Protect, the target was in the water and she has Protect 1, then the Water would slightly move to protect the target. Protect 2 might require the target to be right next to the water, Protect 3 may require the target to be in X Yards of Water. Protect 4 would rip water from any surrounding source to come out and protect the target, whereas Protect 5 could literally make pipes burst or take all of the moisture out of thin air to protect the target.<br /> <br /> If we go this way, I fear we may have to lose the Attribute attachment, but it also brings in the idea of Conclusions having lower Exp costs. What do you think? D:<br /> <br /> EDIT: I've also finished up Phelegethon, the Abyssal Current of Dark Passions. I hope it's good enough. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 05-19-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T22:42:36-07:00","id":897587,"title":"","content":"Pardon the Double Post, but I'd like to note that the <b>Abyssal Currents are finally finished! </b>Styx is finished. What does anyone think? :3<br /> <br /> Abyssal Currents: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:13:48-07:00","id":900924,"title":"","content":"Alrighties. Despite the triple post, I'll note that I'll try not to make any newer comments until a significant development has been made or the like. I may revise loads of things in the upcoming times, mainly making grammar better rather than any active rewriting. So far, the only thing that's gotten any actual revisions is Lucidity in the Systems and Advantages Document. I've written it so that it was more clear cut as a tight rope between nature and civilization as well as a way to use Relationships to keep the Siren afloat if either Civilization or Nature fall. I feel the revision also makes Lucidity abit more symbolic for the Abyssal Currents. It makes Lethe the appraisal of civilization and disregard of nature. It makes Styx the appraisal of nature and disregard of civilization. It makes Phelegethon the disregard of Relationships, and finally Acheron is the disregard of almost everything in Lucidity. <br /> <br /> ...What does this mean for Cocytus though? If I want to have the Abyssal Currents as representations of throwing away certain aspects of Lucidity, I feel I should edit the Lucidity chart to include more sins that would make Cocytus abit dangerous to join...perhaps sins against dealing with evil entities and not acting on wise decisions like traces?<br /> <br /> Actually, there's already a few sins like that! One against not acting on Traces, and two on dealing with otherworldly entities that would endanger existence! Granted, I imagine Cocytus is a catch all faction that would deal with anything outside of normal Siren purviews in general. <br /> <br /> Anyways, if nothing else, I've begun writing on Quagmires and Furies. I got permission from the Kings Raven to be able to use Princess the Hopeful's Taints as a guideline for writing Quagmires, hence the similarity they have to Taints. I should note that I used the Dream Version specifically.<br /> <br /> Without any further ado, all new links will be put here. Quagmires have been finished (or at least their first draft), and Furies can be finished sooner or later.<br /> <br /> <b>Quagmires and Furies: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FROqRxseIDDxep0Iu2Kd_eF5-NBfg0PuKntzpgosy64/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T10:37:43-07:00","id":903645,"title":"","content":"<b><i>[A wild Reaper Verse appears!]</i></b><br /> <br /> Yikes. Haven't been on for quite a while. I should get better towards doing that. :V<br /> <br /> I love each one of the Abyssal Currents and how they all have a different umbrella to stand under. They have character and it helps them stand apart from both the regular Currents and from each other Abyssal Current.<br /> <br /> And then a shocking swerve with the Quagmires. They are really interesting and serve as a great way to shake up a Chronicle. I do want to say that the first thing I thought of as a Quagmire would be Camp Crystal Lake from the <i>Friday the 13th</i> series. It doesn't exactly fit, considering that most of the horror that occurred was due to a mother's maddened grief over losing her son and the son's anger at the death of his mother, but it feels like it fits the &quot;legend&quot; of Camp Crystal Lake. <br /> <br /> Sorta like, people think the land itself has been cursed somehow due to the actions of two people. Despite the fact that it is considered a dangerous area, people are still attempting to use the land, forcing the mother/son to act in an attempt to drive them away. The films themselves provide a different context, but the whole idea of Camp Crystal Lake could serve as a sort of example for the Quagmires. <br /> <br /> Do we have a working name for the creatures that become altered by the Quagmires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T12:30:49-07:00","id":903713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=903645#post903645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>[A wild Reaper Verse appears!]</i></b><br /> <br /> Yikes. Haven't been on for quite a while. I should get better towards doing that. :V</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, stuff happens. :3 Here's a short rundown of what's been done.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems and Advantages</b> - (Mainly Lucidity, adding Maelstrom and Lucidity 0 stuff)<br /> <b>Vodianoi</b> - Only Malformations. They're not all finished.<br /> <b>Celestial Ocean</b> - At least I've started up on fluff and descriptions for it as well as mechanics to give it the &quot;apocalypse has been done&quot; feel to it. I don't have a way of entry into them (I'm figuring we could let Sirens enter it from a body of water large enough to hold their Diluvian Form). I also haven't done any writing on Survivors yet.<br /> <b>Conditions and Tilts</b>- Mainly describing new Tilts from the Celestial Ocean. I should prolly write up the Hunted Condition that was in Quagmires too. &gt;&gt;&quot;<br /> <b>Alterations </b>- They're mostly the same as Squamous had them, but due to a lack of activity on his end, I've sort of picked up and started writing for them. I've made a separate document so that the original Squamous had isn't affected.<br /> <b>Abyssal Currents</b> - As you've read them, they're basically fully complete. :3 The only issue I can think of is &quot;did I forget to add in Echidna as an Abyssal Current or should they be something else entirely?&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=903645#post903645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love each one of the Abyssal Currents and how they all have a different umbrella to stand under. They have character and it helps them stand apart from both the regular Currents and from each other Abyssal Current.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=903645#post903645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then a shocking swerve with the Quagmires. They are really interesting and serve as a great way to shake up a Chronicle. I do want to say that the first thing I thought of as a Quagmire would be Camp Crystal Lake from the <i>Friday the 13th</i> series. It doesn't exactly fit, considering that most of the horror that occurred was due to a mother's maddened grief over losing her son and the son's anger at the death of his mother, but it feels like it fits the &quot;legend&quot; of Camp Crystal Lake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I admit, I was basing off of our earlier ideas and ball rolling on Quagmire's being nature's vengeance, so I mostly focused on that. But now that you brought it up, the idea of it having the same horror story value as Camp Crystal Lake makes me happy. If nothing else, does the Creature of the Black Lagoon also work for a good Quagmire (and Fury) setting? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=903645#post903645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorta like, people think the land itself has been cursed somehow due to the actions of two people. Despite the fact that it is considered a dangerous area, people are still attempting to use the land, forcing the mother/son to act in an attempt to drive them away. The films themselves provide a different context, but the whole idea of Camp Crystal Lake could serve as a sort of example for the Quagmires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties, I'll take notes of the inspirations for the Gameline and put them in another document. In case if I haven't noted yet, I've made the entire documents folder for Siren visible to the public and commenting is allowed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=903645#post903645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have a working name for the creatures that become altered by the Quagmires?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't thought of any, but after reading abit on &quot;Gaia&quot; on Wikipedia, I have one idea for a name. How does &quot;Therons&quot; sound? It's Greek for &quot;Hunter; Untamed&quot; and it's also a part of a generic title for Female Deities who govern animals (in this case being &quot;Potnia Theron&quot;, which means &quot;Mistress of the Animals&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:39:05-07:00","id":903809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=903713#post903713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Celestial Ocean</b> - At least I've started up on fluff and descriptions for it as well as mechanics to give it the &quot;apocalypse has been done&quot; feel to it. I don't have a way of entry into them (I'm figuring we could let Sirens enter it from a body of water large enough to hold their Diluvian Form). I also haven't done any writing on Survivors yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, it may depend on how we visualize the Sirens' entrance into the Celestial Ocean. If it's something like a gradual process where the Siren merges with the water to enter the Celestial Ocean, then the large body of water would work. If it's like a portal, I would say that things as shallow as puddles work as long as the Siren can fit her entire body through. If we want to make it even easier, it could be something like &quot;as long as the Siren is sufficiently covered in water&quot; and allow travel through the rain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Abyssal Currents</b> - As you've read them, they're basically fully complete. :3 The only issue I can think of is &quot;did I forget to add in Echidna as an Abyssal Current or should they be something else entirely?&quot;. </div> </div> </div>As far as I recall, Echidnal Sirens aren't necessarily part of a Current. It's more of a question of whether or not the players should be able to side with Echidna. The general feel of the game seems like we should be rooting for the normal Currents but people will want to play &quot;evil&quot; campaigns so it would be inclusive to have Echidnal Sirens as an offshoot of all the other Currents. Possibly a sort of &quot;going off the deep end&quot; like a Hunter becoming a Slasher. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you. I admit, I was basing off of our earlier ideas and ball rolling on Quagmire's being nature's vengeance, so I mostly focused on that. But now that you brought it up, the idea of it having the same horror story value as Camp Crystal Lake makes me happy. If nothing else, does the Creature of the Black Lagoon also work for a good Quagmire (and Fury) setting? </div> </div> </div>I feel like anything that has a sufficient &quot;Nature vs. Man&quot; theme would work as a Quagmire. Creature from the Black Lagoon would be more like a regular encounter with a Vodianoi though, considering that the Black Lagoon doesn't necessarily have a legacy behind it and the fact that the Creature was a sort of one-off encounter. Kinda like going into a nondescript forest and seeing Bigfoot. <br /> <br /> I listed Camp Crystal Lake because it has a legacy behind it, despite the entire thing being because of a serial murderer instead of pseudonatural weirdness. A better example for Quagmires may be something like the Bermuda Triangle, a natural area that has a lot of weirdness attached to it and a sort of legacy. It's an area that has been around for some time but most people say to avoid it because of all the bad mojo going on. <br /> <br /> Of archetypical areas that I feel work as a Quagmire, I feel like these fit the bill:<br /> -<b>The Bermuda Triangle</b> (and a joke in <i>Siren</i> could be that the Sirens have all but discovered that the Bermuda Triangle is indeed strange but not necessarily a Quagmire)<br /> This could be a sort of baseline for <i>very large</i> Quagmires that spread out their Spite.<br /> <br /> -<b>Aokigahara</b>, the Suicide Forest in Japan (a Quagmire'd copy may have vines that grow in the shape of nooses and attempt to strangle anyone who comes deep enough into the forest)<br /> This could cover most types of heavily vegetated Quagmires that want to kill off humanity.<br /> <br /> -<b>Amigara Fault</b>, from <i>The Enigma of Amigara Fault. </i>It's a horror manga where people feel driven to enter human-shaped crevaces within this cliffside.<br /> This would be mountainous areas and it could possibly describe Quagmires that attempt to compel mortals into acting in certain ways.<br /> <br /> -Homes that become <b>infested by honey bees in the walls or snakes from underground or even black mold</b> (entirely explainable occurrences, Quagmire'd, it is an attempt by the Quagmire to control the living organisms in the area)<br /> This is a way to incorporate Quagmires into an area that is a little light on natural elements.<br /> <br /> -<b>Isla de las Muneca</b>s, the Island of the Dolls in Mexico (Quagmire'd, it could be that the dolls are a means to appease the Quagmire to keep it from spreading outside of the island)<br /> A possible way to show Appeasement and even incorporate the idea of mortals reacting to the supernatural nature of Quagmires.<br /> <br /> -<b>Pripyat</b>, a city in the Ukraine that was evacuated due to the Chernobyl Power Plant disaster (Quagmire'd, some Sirens suspect that the Chernobyl disaster was an attempt to <i>destroy an existing Quagmire </i>and believe that it only ended up creating an even <i>larger</i> Quagmire)<br /> That having been said, most Ghost Towns could be used to describe ways to destroy or escape from Quagmires.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a side-note, I was searching for natural locations that have a sort of grim/horror feel and most of them are centered somewhere in Japan. I thought this was kinda funny and fitting considering that the Flensers are based on a Japanese belief concerning mermaids and their immortality-causing flesh. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't thought of any, but after reading abit on &quot;Gaia&quot; on Wikipedia, I have one idea for a name. How does &quot;Therons&quot; sound? It's Greek for &quot;Hunter; Untamed&quot; and it's also a part of a generic title for Female Deities who govern animals (in this case being &quot;Potnia Theron&quot;, which means &quot;Mistress of the Animals&quot;). </div> </div> </div>I think it sounds pretty fine, though I feel that there is a more official term that can be used to describe large animals that are meant to fight against humanity. I tried looking at the myth of Hercules (because he had to deal with the Nemean Lion, the Cretan Bull, etc) but the only words I can find are Labours (which refer to the acts he had to perform) and Monsters (which is too generic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T16:58:38-07:00","id":903854,"title":"","content":"I see. I like the mentioning of the Bermuda Triangle as a possible Quagmire. Prolly one that's gone WAAAY out of control.<br /> <br /> I was also hoping to ask. The next really big thing I can see coming up (that needs conceptualization that I don't think I could do on my own) is the Verses. I think the Introduction and Opuses are fine and don't really need any revision. My major thought at the moment is Conclusions however. As I posted above, I had an idea on how to write them...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=891811#post891811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope it's also fine to bring up, but I've also been having second thoughts on Conclusions. I know I said &quot;maybe they should be attached to an attribute to be used generically&quot;, but recently I've been getting the feeling that Verses (since the Abyssal Currents are nearly done, I'm starting to think on the Verses and their mechanics) might be <i>too </i>freeform. So to counteract this, I was thinking that Conclusions could perhaps be 1-5 Dot rated powers, with new powers or new levels of effectiveness being able to be drawn.<br /> <br /> For example, let's use the <b>Protect </b>Conclusion. When used as a verse, it'll automatically give it's dot level in Armor rating to the person, object or place it's used on to protect from damages. But there's a catch. The Opuses invoked in the Conclusion must be present, but the need for presence can lower the higher the dot level is. So if a Siren used Target-Water-Protect, the target was in the water and she has Protect 1, then the Water would slightly move to protect the target. Protect 2 might require the target to be right next to the water, Protect 3 may require the target to be in X Yards of Water. Protect 4 would rip water from any surrounding source to come out and protect the target, whereas Protect 5 could literally make pipes burst or take all of the moisture out of thin air to protect the target.<br /> <br /> If we go this way, I fear we may have to lose the Attribute attachment, but it also brings in the idea of Conclusions having lower Exp costs. What do you think? D:</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than that...well, is there anything else we should note when speaking on Verses? I think I recall we talked about making contexts for Opuses or something and defining them, basically where they can apply or be used. And if the idea I presented is used, we'll need to come up with ideas for powers for 1-5 levels on each Conclusion, which should be generic enough that it can be applied anywhere but kinda functionally useless without a Verse to &quot;specify&quot; what the conclusion is being used for. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot to note, we also spoke that Verses would be pulled out rhythmically and stuff. They can be sung out or played on an instrument, but if they're too obvious then they can invoke Refraction. I also had the idea a Siren could use a point of Pneuma to be able to bypass the &quot;need to do rhythmically&quot; part. Exhaling the breath of life instead of actually speaking and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 05-30-2016, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T17:19:02-07:00","id":903863,"title":"","content":"What I like about Quagmires is that they both embody the the &quot;sentient, malevolent location&quot; trope, but their very existence makes them a sympathetic antagonist Sirens understand-they're wounded, scared animals lashing out at what they think is causing them pain, not demons.<br /> <br /> One of the things about Pripyat is that people trying to be off the grid still live there, and despite the radiation it's actually become rather forested again. We could have the Quagmire as one that's been partially appeased, enough so that animal and plant life can go back, and it even allows a few humans that stay away from its heart to dwell there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T23:07:54-07:00","id":904743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=903863#post903863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I like about Quagmires is that they both embody the the &quot;sentient, malevolent location&quot; trope, but their very existence makes them a sympathetic antagonist Sirens understand-they're wounded, scared animals lashing out at what they think is causing them pain, not demons.<br /> <br /> One of the things about Pripyat is that people trying to be off the grid still live there, and despite the radiation it's actually become rather forested again. We could have the Quagmire as one that's been partially appeased, enough so that animal and plant life can go back, and it even allows a few humans that stay away from its heart to dwell there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I admit, I'm abit happy when people point out things that didn't come to mind at first. Mainly that the Quagmires can be related to wounded, scared animals. And yes, that sounds like a good idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:01:12-07:00","id":909840,"title":"","content":"Pardon the Double Posting again, but I'm going to post the new updates here until another response. I'm sorry if it sounds bad of me to say &quot;I won't post until someone else does&quot;, but this is mainly so that whenever this thread gets bumped, it won't be me giving out each an every little update I do or thing I type. That said, I've gotten abit more done in Alterations. I've added or retyped a few in Gardenia and made and finished Tropicana. I want to make an Alteration that gives the Siren some &quot;electric eel&quot; like quality (inflicting the Stunned Tilt) but I can't help but feel that anything like that would be Echidnal only. Or at least, something that expands upon that.<br /> <br /> I've also been thinking on the nature of the Celestial Ocean, more things that could be a part of it or something. I was looking back onto our old discussions on &quot;if it should be a bad end future timeline&quot;, &quot;if it should be a part of the Astral Realms or be how the Sirens picture it&quot;, etc etc.<br /> <br /> I was thinking, maybe we could write it as if it were like the Astral/Dreamlands, mostly the Anima Mundi? It's stated to be the Soul of the Universe and containing the ideals of the natural world and <b>mankind's impact on it</b>. It's also stated that when a person enters it, they get a sensation of vast size that makes a person feel small by comparison. TL;DR up ahead with bolded text before each idea so it's less of a headache to go through.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">How I feel this fits into Siren is in a couple of ways. For one, it would feel fitting that the Soul of the Universe would seek out and create beings to uphold it. In fact, an example I have of this is in the Nasuverse (I think it includes Melty Blood, Fate/Stay Night and Boundary of the Void), there's a being called Alaya, who is the collective will of humanity to survive. It's modus operandi is to create Counter Guardians. In short, it gives the contracted one miracle in exchange for serving as a Counter Guardian after death and fix problems that would lead to humanity dying as a whole. It feels like we can do that here, except with the soul of the Universe doing it instead.<br /> <br /> <b>HOW IT CAN FIT WITH LORE/MECHANICS ON THE ANIMA MUNDI</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There's still more than a few things that are fitting. Given it's description of &quot;Warping the minds of those who enter it and making their very being into a part of the realm&quot;, a magical effect that makes people lose their individuality and become one with everything. Mages call this &quot;The Ecstatic Wind&quot;, and Princesses know this as &quot;The Gales&quot;. My idea is that Sirens know them by a much, much, MUCH different name. &quot;The Song&quot;. To explain this, one idea for the ideal of Universal Harmony is that it can be dangerous or even a bad thing. The idea was that the Song is an ideal that obliterates distinctions (between Land and Sea for example), but like most ideals that would promise harmony, it would instead lead to the downfall of both sides (aka Causing the Deluge). The Song in a sense can be a danger of the ideal, since it enchants humans to walk into the sea as if it were land in search of beauty.<br /> <br /> To give mechanical ideas on how this can fit in already made material, let's say that the Song is why the Waters are capable of migrating and shifting in the Celestial Ocean. It's why it can shift according to changes in reality altogether, and also why Sirens are capable of changing their Alterations by focusing on one of the Waters too. It also makes their Supernatural Advantage fitting in name, since &quot;Akashic Record&quot; covers &quot;the records of the world&quot;.<br /> <br /> It also gives a small reference to Werewolf the Apocalypse. In nWoD terms, the Shadow and Astral were both the same place in the oWoD, and Werecreatures could enter the Umbra (what it was called in the oWoD) via entering a reflective surface and interact with everything like it were physical. Sirens can do the same thing here, but with water.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>HOW IT STILL CAN DEAL WITH TIME THEMES</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">But there's still one problem. We did agree that the Celestial Ocean would have time themes, acting like a bad end future. We also agreed on History themes too, such as &quot;what has happened may happen again&quot;. I have an idea on this. Simply put, Mages have the Dream Merit, and Princesses have the White Rabbits merit. Both merits are basically the Astral/Dreamlands telling the Mage/Princess of things to come, or hints of things to come. Given this, what if the Celestial Ocean shows that to a Siren? Things to come in the future if they continue as they are now? This way, it still fits in with Time themes.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>THEN WHAT ARE CETO AND ECHIDNA</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There's one problem. All beings in the Astral/Dreamlands are ultimately ephemeral beings. How can they affect anything on earth? I say, we take the Luna Route. She took a form to mate with Father Wolf, and thus had half spirit, half man kids. Ceto, or the being behind her (if we still use Leviathan, I feel that revamping the Celestial Ocean can help us make a coherent backstory) were able to deal with humanity and raise them to a higher level where they became Sirens. It also helps explain why to the Sirens, the Astral/Dreamlands is a physical place. What are these beings exactly? We could say that they're basically Gods of the Anima Mundi. In particular, Echidna and Ceto are closer to humanity, hence how they're capable of taking a physical form and why Sirens have a physical form too.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>FURTHER IDEAS ON HOW THINGS CAN FIT TOGETHER</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As well, another idea was how the Anima Mundi makes everyone who walked into it get a sensation of vast size that makes the individual feel small by comparison. What better way to symbolize that than to make it's imagery the same as an ocean? Furthermore, this also gives some more meaning to the Furies, Survivors, and Therons (I thought it would be a good idea to add in sea creatures a siren can interact with in the Celestial Ocean), as they could be signs of people (Survivors) or nature (Furies) suffering.<br /> <br /> Finally, how would the Tenemos and Oneiros be represented? I had earlier ideas that, given the Celestial Ocean shows more of the Anima Mundi than anything else, there would be different levels to the Celestial Ocean. I had the idea that there were the Reefs (Tenemos), which would be the most populated by the Survivors (representation of human individuals). I also imagine that there's the Surface (Oneiroi), which would have tons of different debris floating like trash on the water. Sirens could potentially pick these up and use Trace to see through the object to whatever human it belonged to. In truth, each of these objects are representative of a person. There's also the Skies, but I feel that as a whole, no Siren is able to access them. It's thematically fitting that they're unable to get too close to an ideal. In this case, getting closer to humanity. However, an Ascended Siren (I think we still need a name for these) are capable of going up to the Skies. I also had the idea of a more dangerous zone known as &quot;The Depths&quot;, which would be where more dangerous things lurk and where Echidna herself is known to live. In a sense, going to the Depths means going deeper into the Anima Mundi.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>HOW THIS DOESN'T INTRUDE ON OTHER GAMELINES</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, so they're another supernatural that can enter the Astral. Mage, Princess, Changeling (though they can only go through Oneiroi), Beasts, and to list off two other fansplats, Demigod and Dragons. Dragons are possibly the most similar, given that they call it the &quot;Dreamtide&quot; and in a smaller sense, their fuel stat is Breath, which is what Siren's used to be before renaming to Pneuma.<br /> <br /> Here's what I think that separates Sirens from the rest. First off, they aren't capable of going towards another's &quot;Oneiros&quot; section. The Skies are just out of reach for a Siren. Second, the Song doesn't affect them like it does other people. Mages and Princesses can be trapped by the Gales. To solve this, the Song simply passes through Sirens like a wind going through a hollow cave. They can't be endangered by the Song, but it's possible for other people to become enthralled. Finally, I imagine that unlike Mages (though like Princesses), there's simply no difference between the Tenemos and the Anima Mundi for Sirens. But unlike Princesses, the Tenemos is much more saturated with the Anima Mundi and thus much more heavily influenced. Finally, unlike how Mages and Princesses enter via their Oneiros/Crawlspace, and Beasts enter from their Lairs (which if I read correctly, are within the Tenemos), Sirens are mainly found in the Anima Mundi instead.<br /> <br /> I think this can actually bring in some personal horror to a Siren. Since they can enter in anywhere to the Celestial Ocean, but don't use an Oneiros to enter it, what does it say about the Siren? I'm not willing to slap on mechanics, lore or anything on this. If a person or player asks this, I simply want the answer to be &quot;use your imagination and let it make the result&quot;. C:</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What do you guys think on these ideas? Is there any plot holes or places where I'm going against what we have established?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I finally got onto starting the Verses section! Most of the Introductions and Opuses we considered have been written up, as well as a system for how Verses can be carried out and how it can be carried out for benefice or penalties. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Oh my god it's 1:21 AM I'm so tired. OTL</span><br /> <br /> <b>Verses: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L-dSlUhZEv84MJgAGXdlKGUkl3zqj8X4YsI1mPmAU10/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Alterations: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-Wn-NQHrxS_3vHMDurtCDx4A-sWZuY-ima6QFt4tO9I/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 06-10-2016, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:39:52-07:00","id":918343,"title":"","content":"Pardon my lack of posting or updating, but I would like to note that I got onto the Conclusions section! Like most conventional powers, these are split up into five different (but still general) effects. So far, Calm, Control and Destroy are finished. Any thoughts? Link is on the post above.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT: </b>The Disturb Conclusion is finished! I admit, I had alot of fun with this one, especially the Encore Performance power. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And now the Invoke Conclusion is finished too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Protect is finished as well. I feel that may require revision or something because I feel I did badly on it. &gt;&gt;&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 06-23-2016, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T17:10:59-07:00","id":924182,"title":"","content":"Pardon my going back and forth on writing things up, my inspiration rises and falls for different things to work on this. Anyways, I would like to say that Furies are finished! And to note, the Craft Vessel Numina is from Princess the Hopeful, I got King's Raven's ok to use it. :3 The Furies are on the bottom half of the link. Long story short:<br /> <br /> <b>Furies: </b>They're ephemeral entities connected to a Quagmire. Their stats depend on the Quagmires Resentment and Spite, and they're kind of like Poison Ivy in a way. They can make their own bodies which are reminiscent of Spriggans or Elementals found in Mythology. I hope you guys like them. :3<br /> <br /> <b>Quagmires and Furies: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FROqRxseIDDxep0Iu2Kd_eF5-NBfg0PuKntzpgosy64/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:59:30-07:00","id":925391,"title":"","content":"Hm.<br /> <br /> Want me to write up a Fury? I've got this lovely idea for the Tikbalang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T14:31:45-07:00","id":925492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=925391#post925391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Want me to write up a Fury? I've got this lovely idea for the Tikbalang.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be appreciated, thank you for offering. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's be a good idea to have an example Fury and Quagmire. <br /> <br /> Also as a general post here, I'd like to note that I made another Siren the Drowning Thread on the Rpg.net forums. I will note that I will keep tabs on both threads and if any breakthroughs or major notifactions will be posted upon both threads.<br /> <br /> RPG.net Siren the Drowning thread: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?785183-nWoD-Siren-the-Surfacing-Fansplat-Ressurection\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...t-Ressurection</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T18:29:37-07:00","id":926197,"title":"","content":"Okay then.<br /> <br /> Can I also say we might want to rewrite the Fury Attribute rules, though? Maybe something like &quot;a number of dots to be distributed among the Fury's Attributes, which all start at one, equal to/equal to two times the dots in Spite its Quagmire has&quot;? Or maybe &quot;The Fury gets extra points in all Attributes equal to the Spite dots of the Quagmire, divided by three (minimum 1)&quot;? Otherwise, all but the most toxic Quagmires have Furies that are absurdly weak, and I don't think that's the intention.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Lesser Fury: The American Tikbalang</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Of course this is the right path. The question is whether you're following it-not my fault if you trip.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> It's easy to forget, but Quagmires are clever. They come into this world inherently understanding exactly what hurt the planet so much they condensed out of its pain, and what was behind that pain. True, they don't really spend that much time wondering if their lashing will actually solve that pain (they are, when it comes down to it, wounded beasts-not known for nuance), but when they unleash their Flood, they genuinely wish to direct it at the source of their pain (or something tangentially related, if they are frustrated and are sick of existing as Quagmires). They at least have a good sense as to the motives as to how they formed, to better counter them in the first place. Generally, the kind of actions that scar the earth badly enough for a Quagmire to form over the damage was motivated by greed, a callous disregard for the world, or more likely both-but sometimes, it was made because the causes could see no other way. African poachers who need ivory money to feed their destitute villages, miners in toxic coal plants that have no other skills, and the desperate clawing of failing businesses that have lost all other recourse don't often have the malice that clinches the opening of a Floodgate, but sometimes, the world isn't that neat-especially if the causes' desperation was the aftereffect of human cruelty to them. The Furies produced by such a well-intentioned act of destruction inherently know this, leading to a being that, while it doesn't <i>respect </i>humans, understands they are not all evil threats to their territory. This makes them both less and more dangerous. Less, because they actually bother wondering if the humans nearby deserve their wrath and have a sense of primal morality that can be appeased. More, because their sympathy with humans also gives them a similar pack instinct-the calmer Furies recognize the value of having not just minions, but intelligent advisors and lieutenants, in pursuing their revenge. Perhaps it is actually the evolutionary design of the planet that calm Furies come into existence when the causes for their pain have, themselves, someone to blame-all Furies can truly offer is karma, but karma is a temptation few can match.<br /> <br /> The Hawaiian Fury that calls itself the Tikbalang is an example of this. Its Quagmire formed in Halekala National Part in response to the introduction of a sprig of kudzu, that most invasive of vines, to the area thanks to a team of reckless drug runners not checking their cargo as well as they should have. Thankfully for the park, the Quagmire was able to control the plant's spread long enough that the park officials noticed and quickly burned out the kudzu before it became a real ecological danger. In the normal course of events, the Quagmire should have dissipated, were it not for the fact that the dealers weren't keeping to the profession willingly-rather, they had the misfortune of their female family members being targeted for trafficking by the Filipino branch of the Yakuza, the Japanese version of the mafia. However, one of the higher-ranking members, a charming sociopath by the name of Daiki, had been running behind significantly when it came to getting an excess of narcotics sold safely, so he decided to expand the market a little bit, start shipping to American buyers. Being a rather cheap sort, he decided to blackmail the girls' relatives into helping him-in effect, toxifying their innocence. This, combined with the fact that he had no real intention of fulfilling his end of the bargain (too useful), and the Yakuza's own business of helping with illegal dumping, was what caused the Quagmire to pool, and the unwilling smugglers' Filipino beliefs gave the Tikbalang-named after a guardian of sacred sites that works by tricking would-be intruders-its form. Seeing as how further catastrophe to the islands was narrowly averted by the Tikbalang's own quick thinking when a park ranger was passing by the defiled site, its new agenda is to punish the true defilers of both its ground and the sacred act of mating (Tikbalangs are heavily associated with weddings) with extreme prejudice-and to ensure a new invasive species doesn't take root.<br /> <br /> Much like the horse-headed bogeymen that are its namesake, it is also very cunning in pursuing this; it's approached the smugglers in complete honesty about its motives and goals. Apparently, Daichi doesn't know what a forming mystery cult looks like-or vigilantes, for that matter.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>In its true form, the American Tikbalang looks mostly like its namesake-a long-limbed, naked man with the feet and head of an animal. It's not a true example of the myth though, and it shows-rather than a horse's head and hooves, it has the talons and face of a Hawaiian hawk, showing its more aggressive nature. More pertinently to Sirens, it is just as much a creature born of the woods as it is one that lives in them-what appears to be swarthy islander skin is, in fact, the flexible bark of tropical trees, and in place of a mythical tikbalang's three horns it has great green ferns, swaying in the wind.<br /> <br /> It is a testament to the park service that the American Tikbalang lacks an element many other Furies take for granted when sculpting a Vessel-Pollution, namely. Maybe if it could find another example of an invasive species it would count, but frankly, the Tikbalang doesn't want to test the theory; it not only likes its mind, it feels dirty to go against the reason it was born in the first place. Instead, it mostly uses Air, Water, and Plant elements when making a new form to interact with its creators and cultists, favoring either versatility or endurance depending on its needs. It uses Flesh, occasionally, when the cultists bring it a hapless criminal to vent their fury on in its bloodiest ceremony, but that is currently a rare occasion-mostly because of lack of opportunity, not because the Tikbalang can't see a use for the talents of violent thugs. In all Vessels, it appears to be an old, long-bearded man of Filipino descent, body scarred from years of living off the land-but always having the three horn-leaves, shrunken and hidden, somewhere on its body, growing out of its sculpted skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>Some Sirens may wonder why, exactly, they need to get involved with the American Tikbalang and its unwilling criminals turned mystical vigilantes. It obviously likes, or at least tolerates, humans enough to work with them openly-it isn't even particularly invasive when regaining Pneuma, letting its cult kiss it when they don't need to speak for a while or tagging along on their missions of justice. Since the focus of its ire probably deserves to be made into fertilizer, what's the big problem? The problem is that, as with most Furies, the Tikbalang thinks like an animal, and animals see things in terms of species, and species don't have much variation-a man of Japanese descent that has committed any crime, no matter how minor, is obviously a Yakuza and one of Daiki's allies, worthy only of being sacrificed to the park. Its cultists are more capable of nuance and convincing it otherwise, but given how wise the Tikbalang comes off as (and it is genuinely perceptive, even without its Omen Trance Numen), they don't usually question it unless they see evidence otherwise. Beyond any sense of obligation to innocent jaywalkers, the Tikbalang isn't as good as hiding its crimes as it is as masterminding them-the Hawaiian PD is slowly starting to think they may have a racially motivated serial killer on their hands, and it won't be long until they figure out it has something to do with the schedule of a particular merchant ship. Any Siren that wishes to avoid police scrutiny into their domains is advised to at least talk down the Tikbalang.<br /> <br /> Even nonviolent contact, however, is bound to be eerie and hazardous-the Tikbalang was partially formed from its makers' own moral conflicts, and it inflicts this doubt in others as a facet of its nature. Its Influence affects all forms of being lost, includingin a metaphysical, spiritual sense, allowing it to inflict crippling feelings of self-doubt and inadequacy on strangers, which combined with its other Numina lead to a pretty psychologically devastating assault. Worse, it does so even-<i>especially</i>-if it suspects the intruder on its territory is a potential friend, as it wants to see if the subject is capable of the same self-assessment and guilt as its creator-cult, and thus similar enough to count as a packmate. Those that fail, running away or collapsing into a gibbering pile of shattered self-image, it judges to be to different from its pack to be of any use-it doesn't kill these, and usually leads them out, but it will take some convincing before it ever lets anyone near the grove where it and the cult perform their rites to heal the Quagmire, and only if they submit to another test.<br /> <br /> Still, the object of both the Fury and its accidental creators' ire is a genuinely evil man, one who leads some of the worst people in a very bad bunch. The American Tikbalang is a living reminder that people who are hazardous to the Earth are often dangers to their fellow man in their avarice as well-humans are as much part of the environment as the trees and the air, and by scarring one element, you affect the others, however indirectly. Thus, the Tikbalang can be something of a wild card in any story it figures in, being both an immoderate response to a real wrong and a dangerous outsider to the criminal underworld, one motivated not by money or even power, but the incorruptible desire to tear down everything a family has built and piss on the ruins with its former victims.<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue: </b>Sympathetic<br /> <br /> <b>Vice: </b>Merciless<br /> <br /> <b>Rank: </b>2 (the American Tikbalang was initially 3, but destroying the kudzu Appeased the Quagmire enough to lost a dot in Resentment)<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 1, Finesse 3, Resistance 2 (the Quagmire has a Spite rating of 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Influence: </b>Being Lost 2, Woods 1<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Twilight Form, Craft Vessel, Image<br /> <br /> <b>Max Pneuma:</b> 15<br /> <br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Hallucination, Omen Trance, Pathfinder","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-05-2016, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T18:35:36-07:00","id":926198,"title":"","content":"Also: Did we ever nail down what targets a Siren for being called?<br /> <br /> I don't see it in the Gdocs folder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T23:40:22-07:00","id":926293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=926197#post926197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay then.<br /> <br /> Can I also say we might want to rewrite the Fury Attribute rules, though? Maybe something like &quot;a number of dots to be distributed among the Fury's Attributes, which all start at one, equal to/equal to two times the dots in Spite its Quagmire has&quot;? Or maybe &quot;The Fury gets extra points in all Attributes equal to the Spite dots of the Quagmire, divided by three (minimum 1)&quot;? Otherwise, all but the most toxic Quagmires have Furies that are absurdly weak, and I don't think that's the intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the problem. I'll rewrite it to &quot;a number of dots to be distributed among the Fury's Attributes, which all start at one, equal to the dots in Spite its Quagmire has&quot;. Would it be a good idea to say that the Fury may distribute the dots in Spite across the Attributes as they like? Otherwise, thank you for pointing this out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=926197#post926197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Example Lesser Fury: The American Tikbalang</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Of course this is the right path. The question is whether you're following it-not my fault if you trip.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I am absolutely in love with this. Thank you for writing this out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=926198#post926198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: Did we ever nail down what targets a Siren for being called?<br /> <br /> I don't see it in the Gdocs folder.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean &quot;what makes a human into a Siren&quot;? That would be &quot;the Song&quot;. I didn't mark it down yet. I was thinking of getting every major part finished before moving onto writing fluff and background stuff that we have figured out. <br /> <br /> Long story short, the Song is basically a phenomenon that can make people into Sirens. It can be heard by people who are undergoing some very rough part of their life or the like, where it feels almost like being in the middle of the ocean without a life jacket and the boat that put you out there is mockingly going &quot;try your best&quot;. If the human is able to get through their predicament, (the means don't really matter, what matters is that they try to survive it no matter what), they become attuned to the Song and become a Siren.<br /> <br /> What we have down for how it came to be is that, given the Celestial Ocean is like a bad end future for humanity, the Song is Humanity's attempt at reaching back, trying to claw their way for hope when they have none themselves. We do have some figures for the Celestial Ocean that are tied into the Song. We came up with Ceto being the Siren's progenitor as a whole, and Echidna being one of her first Sirens gone rogue. <br /> <br /> I know I'm going off onto a tangent, but even though there's a Backstory google doc in there (which has a small story on how the Song came to be), we were iffy on using that. The reason being, the three people in the Sirens backstory (Behemoth, Leviathan and Ziiz) were going to be used in Leviathan the Tempest. Although Kings did give an ok that we could use the same, the only reason I'm against it is out of respect for Kings and LtT.<br /> <br /> Also, if it's of no consequence to note, I just got done with the Restore Conclusion today. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T04:19:27-07:00","id":926357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=926293#post926293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see the problem. I'll rewrite it to &quot;a number of dots to be distributed among the Fury's Attributes, which all start at one, equal to the dots in Spite its Quagmire has&quot;. Would it be a good idea to say that the Fury may distribute the dots in Spite across the Attributes as they like? Otherwise, thank you for pointing this out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works. I'll edit my guy to adjust.<br /> <br /> And that was the info I was looking for on the Song, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:51:47-07:00","id":926655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=926293#post926293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long story short, the Song is basically a phenomenon that can make people into Sirens. It can be heard by people who are undergoing some very rough part of their life or the like, where it feels almost like being in the middle of the ocean without a life jacket and the boat that put you out there is mockingly going &quot;try your best&quot;. If the human is able to get through their predicament, (the means don't really matter, what matters is that they try to survive it no matter what), they become attuned to the Song and become a Siren.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is with World of Darkness books and &quot;it happens when you go through hard times&quot;? Is this really the thematically appropriate method for everything? Why not have it handed to them by some godlike force when they become aware of the world's suffering? Maybe give them some sort of divinely-offered choice? Maybe it happens during a near-death experience, like say, drowning? I can see them forming out of someone drowning, meeting some dark god while effectively dead, then waking up as a siren...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T16:18:22-07:00","id":926702,"title":"","content":"Personally I argue near-death experiences like drowning qualifies as &quot;hard times,&quot; but I digress. Whatever the case while I sympathize with splats coming around from more than just periods of stress or so, I find the notion of needing divine intervention for something equally as unnecessary; especially for a line that has little to do with with the concept of deities like Siren.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T16:50:13-07:00","id":926719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=926655#post926655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is with World of Darkness books and &quot;it happens when you go through hard times&quot;? Is this really the thematically appropriate method for everything? Why not have it handed to them by some godlike force when they become aware of the world's suffering? Maybe give them some sort of divinely-offered choice? Maybe it happens during a near-death experience, like say, drowning? I can see them forming out of someone drowning, meeting some dark god while effectively dead, then waking up as a siren...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because hard times tend to be a test of character and whether or not you can still hold it together or break apart in the aftermath. I will note that not all books or methods of becoming a supernatural are through hard times. Vampires can embrace anyone they want, Mummies come and go whenever, Sin-Eaters pop up from a contract with a Geist upon death, and Dragons are made by finding (or being given) a Heart to eat.<br /> <br /> Although I'm sort of with Kara on this one. Becoming a Siren should be something earned and not so easily given. Were it able to be given by some divinity for example, it would completely kill off Echidna's reasons for kidnapping and mutating humans to make the perfect survivor (which Sirens are meant to be) and they'd instead shift to &quot;trying to control this divinity to make more people into Sirens&quot; which I feel wouldn't be fitting in Siren's themes when it comes to Echidna. I do appreciate the thoughts, but I don't think that divine intervention is somewhere I'd like to take Siren.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T18:20:47-07:00","id":926753,"title":"","content":"I know nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T23:01:43-07:00","id":929573,"title":"","content":"Pardon my lack of new messages on this thread. I've been taking a short break to ST for a friend. Sadly making for Siren and STing both take from inspiration, but I promise that I will get back into making things for Siren. For now, I am working on the Sense Conclusion. What I have so far is:<br /> <br /> Sense in general: Reading the Introduction target to see if they have the Opus within them, or scanning the Introduction area for the Opus targets<br /> <br /> Sense 1: Reading the target to see if they contain the opus (think like reading chemical composition, corpse decay/forsenic science or the like)<br /> Sense 2: Sensing the Opus like using a Radar within Sensory radius (Think of the Sense Life spell from Mage 1e, but make it so you can specify with the Opus)<br /> Sense 3: Read specific parts within the target that the opus specifies. This can be up to being able to read another being's character sheet for example.<br /> Sense 4: More intimate reading of objects or people. Being able to read into memories, past experiences or usages (somewhat like Trace, but more unlimited)<br /> Sense 5: Being able to throw your senses elsewhere. Essentially able to do near astral projection perhaps. Dunno if this is a good idea or not for the power.<br /> <br /> What does anyone think? And if it's not minded being noticed, welcome back online Yads Dom and Reaper! Glad to see that you're both ok. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T08:54:05-07:00","id":932035,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, I have an update. I've gone through and revised most of the Verses Document, mainly making wording better and specifying why Refraction (what protects Sirens from being seen for what they are when using Verses or Alterations in mundane form) occurs. Stanzas have been rewritten to be abit more like Mage Rotes, and I've also revised some of the Conclusion powers to they'd be better used for any Opus at all.<br /> <br /> I've also cleaned up Extended Verse rolls and made a Threshold for them! The Threshold for an extended verse is equal to the Conclusion dot rating of the power times the number of opuses in the verse. So to make a Rainstorm appear, one would normally need Location-Water-Weather-Invoke 3. Let's say the Location was up to an entire city. Invoke 3 x 2 Opuses would mean the Threshold would normally be 6, but adding the +6 to extended thresholds for the Location Introduction, that would make it up to 12. <br /> <br /> Finally, I've managed to finish up the Sense Conclusion! It goes basically like I've said it would in the previous post. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L-dSlUhZEv84MJgAGXdlKGUkl3zqj8X4YsI1mPmAU10/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L-dSlUhZEv84MJgAGXdlKGUkl3zqj8X4YsI1mPmAU10/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L-dSlUhZEv84MJgAGXdlKGUkl3zqj8X4YsI1mPmAU10/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L-dSlUhZEv84MJgAGXdlKGUkl3zqj8X4YsI1mPmAU10/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T18:17:39-07:00","id":933673,"title":"","content":"Holy crap, I'm on a roll. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have some excellent news. I've finally finished off the Vaporian Alterations and I've began and finished the Discordian Alterations as well! I've been stumped for awhile on Vaporia, given that they're based on seas with strong currents and/or foggy vistas, but I couldn't find examples of those. Instead, I elected to make most of the Vaporian Alterations to be based off of the <i>weirdest</i> traits found in marine animals. I had the same problem with Discordia, but then I decided to make their Alterations based all around violence or viciousness. I hope this is enjoyed. <br /> <br /> I've also managed to finish up the &quot;Creating a Siren&quot; section. It's abit of a minor achievement, but it's something. I've also made out Experience Costs table at the end, if anyone would like to suggest adjusting costs, just let me know. <br /> <br /> I was also kind of hoping to ask for some feedback on an idea I had. Up until now, I felt that Siren was well off in terms of gameline and everything fitting together. But now I feel like the Mood should be changed. Right now, I don't feel the mood of &quot;Uncertainty&quot; fits it well enough. Yeah, life is bound to be turbulent, the same goes for everyone. But the point is, I don't feel like it would be that way for Sirens all the time. Hence why I feel a change is in order. And the change I have in mind is making the Mood about &quot;Survival&quot; or something like that. In short, I feel that Sirens would be better played as both intermediaries between Civilization and Nature and as the ultimate Survivalists.<br /> <br /> The reason I feel the theme fits so much now is because a Siren's Drowning and subsequent Surfacing are born from the attempt to survive in spite of problems, the Song was born out of an attempt to pull back and survive. There's Echidna and her obsession with making the greatest survivalists who can live in the Celestial Ocean, the Celestial Ocean itself and Survivors being like a post apocalyptic wasteland, and finally hiding from Flensers and general human populace whenever Refraction occurs. <br /> <br /> What do you all think?<br /> <br /> <b>Creating a Siren Section: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1m5Ug5JlIOSeW2crJ_DfMFfdD0E4F0D_o9EMTcOWKAY0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Diluvian Form and Alterations: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_NkxCJ7gyQq599uf4yBJCarTh_HuHqx0jJUqtxvw484/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T21:59:49-07:00","id":936419,"title":"","content":"I can now say with glee that Verses are finally done! At least, how they'll be is done! There may be tweaking required to make Conclusions or Verses better, so if anyone has any criticisms, feel free to give them! The Transform and Travel Conclusions are as follows!<br /> <br /> <b>Transform: </b>One of the more sorcerous/alchemical of Conclusions, belonging to the Current of Dark Secrets and no other current, this Conclusion allows for a Siren to transform her target into her chosen Opus for a time.<br /> Transform 1: Muta - You can cause cosmetic changes within the target.<br /> Transform 2: Cambiare - You may change basic sentient beings (plants or bugs) or objects of a homogenous nature into either the same or the other. You may give Pneuma to another person or Siren, or with the right Opuses you may turn Pneuma into Fuel stats for other Supernaturals.<br /> Transform 3: Variazioni - The Siren may now change any sentient (but non-sapient being) or objects of a heterogeneous nature into either the same or other. The Siren can change an object into gas, solid or liquid, The Siren may also cause drastic changes, such as changing gender, ethnicity, body structure or size. May even hand Merits for the duration of the Verse, but the Merit dots given cannot be more than the Siren's Transform dots.The Siren may even turn objects into Treasures.<br /> Transform 4: Transition - The Siren may now choose and transform any sapient beings (supernatural or not) into any of the beings from the previous powers and vice versa.<br /> Transform 5: Mordent - The Siren may transform anyone into exactly anything she desires without need to worry about the details. The limit to this power is the Siren's Imagination, Pneuma and Willpower pools. This also allows a Siren to become the embodiment of an Opus while it's active (such as a living shadow like most splats use).<br /> <br /> <b>Travel: </b>The Conclusion of Travel, which belongs to the Celestial Current of Buoyancy, makes all kinds of transitions, entrances and exits possible. Be it Physical destinations, trying to get through social maneuvering or moving emotions and thoughts are possible with this.<br /> Travel 1: Trobar Leu - Eliminates penalties when trying to reach a goal.<br /> Travel 2: Canso - Adds bonuses when trying to reach a goal with minor manipulation of the opus to help, or adds penalties onto people trying to get to a goal. Only applies when Opuses do.<br /> Travel 3: Trobar Ric - Allows for being able to go through chosen opuses as if swimming through them. For example, going through walls, flight and going through radioactive material is all possible with this. Allows for moving concepts elsewhere and opening gates to other worlds.<br /> Travel 4: Tenso - Allows for straight up Teleportation from one source of an opus to another, like the much used &quot;Shadow Step&quot; in the WoD. She may take successes from a concept's application, but she must later pay up for taking those successes where they weren't hers.<br /> Travel 5: Trobar Clus - Co-Location with bodies made of the Opus and twisting physical dimensions by the Opuses.<br /> <br /> I can't help but feel like Transform is lacking Conceptual Applications, and that Travel is very much lacking in the final power. Otherwise, these are the last two major things to set within the Verses section! I will put in a small sidebar on &quot;whether or not verses can affect other supernatural splat powers&quot;. My basic answer is &quot;it's up to your ST, to make it fair he may want to make it so other splats can do the same to Sirens&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Verses Document: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1L-dSlUhZEv84MJgAGXdlKGUkl3zqj8X4YsI1mPmAU10/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I believe the next step to take for Siren is to revise the Mood to Survival. I feel it better fits with Siren's themes. I know, there hasn't been any comments on the decision, but I'm assuming that since there hasn't been any, then there's probably nothing wrong with it the idea.<br /> <br /> The next step after this? I feel like it would be appropriate to finally go into detail on our two pure antagonist factions. There's Echidna and her Sirens, who continually seek to make the new species out of humanity that will survive the apocalypse, and the Flensers, who seek to eat Siren flesh to keep themselves young and seek to make new resources to allow humanity to come to their greatest amount of potential through technology. Specifically, I'm thinking Cybernetics a'la Deus Ex or the like.<br /> <br /> My main reasoning is to give the Flensers a sympathetic point of view. Sure, they can be selfish and destroying nature to get whatever resources they need, but they use said resources to give a much better quality of life to people by making their bodies better. Perhaps more than a few Flensers are those they've helped. Of course, why do they use Cybernetics when they're more concerned about Siren flesh to eat? Perhaps the Flensers are jealous of the Sirens, trying to become superhuman themselves. The one thing they haven't unlocked is longevity...so until they do, it's prolly better to steal it from Sirens until they don't need them anymore.<br /> <br /> And given the view count, I feel it's almost obligatory to post this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SiMHTK15Pik\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SiMHTK15Pik\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SiMHTK15Pik </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SiMHTK15Pik\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SiMHTK15Pik </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thank you to the people who have been watching the Siren thread. I appreciate each and every one of you. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 07-24-2016, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T23:33:29-07:00","id":937957,"title":"","content":"I know I'm making a new post here, and it's not much of an update. It's more of a question really. I've changed the Mood to Survival. That's it on the changes part.<br /> <br /> Now for the Question part. I was hoping to ask, to the people who're watching this thread. I'm just sort of curious, why almost nobody has posted a comment to here other than myself, Reaper or Yads. I mean, I have sort of asked a couple times if there's any thoughts or criticisms on the gameline multiple times before, or ideas I've had. And the only additions I see are mainly views. No answers to the thoughts I had and mulling over. <br /> <br /> I mean, is there nothing to say on this game? Am I communicating badly or overall handle thoughts from other people poorly? Or is everything going fine on this game as it is and the reason for no commenting is because there's almost no reason to do so?<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm fine with double posting and updating this thread. I do love making this fansplat and I will not stop until the game is fully done. But I do want to at least ask and see why nobody is commenting. I'm feeling uncertain on the ideas I have for this gameline, and I do at least want some feedback or criticism to feel like effort isn't being wasted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:35:10-07:00","id":937980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=937957#post937957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, I'm fine with double posting and updating this thread. I do love making this fansplat and I will not stop until the game is fully done. But I do want to at least ask and see why nobody is commenting. I'm feeling uncertain on the ideas I have for this gameline, and I do at least want some feedback or criticism to feel like effort isn't being wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that I think might turn people off is perhaps the way that the information on the splat seems to be spread throughout the whole of the thread, as opposed to being collected (as far as i've seen). It makes it more difficult access. It's an interesting splat, to say the least, but perhaps if you collected the information it might help? I apologise if I just missed it somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:52:53-07:00","id":938182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=937980#post937980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I think might turn people off is perhaps the way that the information on the splat seems to be spread throughout the whole of the thread, as opposed to being collected (as far as i've seen). It makes it more difficult access. It's an interesting splat, to say the least, but perhaps if you collected the information it might help? I apologise if I just missed it somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there is a google docs link to all of the Siren Documents I've made and completed up to now on the bottom of the first post. Unless if it's more of a problem that I'm not keeping track of all of the ideas present and that were discussed in the thread that I didn't completely record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:07:07-07:00","id":938184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=938182#post938182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But there is a google docs link to all of the Siren Documents I've made and completed up to now on the bottom of the first post. Unless if it's more of a problem that I'm not keeping track of all of the ideas present and that were discussed in the thread that I didn't completely record.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Sorry, ignore me being my idiot self. *facepalms*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:24:42-07:00","id":938229,"title":"","content":"Happens to the best of us, no worries; these docs are also likely spread across the pages in the thread that are in writing moment 29 in number. Lotta pages to filter through if you don't know where to look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T12:19:38-07:00","id":938268,"title":"","content":"Just a small correction, but the link to ALL of the Google Docs is in this index right here that is right on the bottom of the first post in this thread. I did link the docs and stuff throughout the pages, but that was only for easy reference for people who wanted to see the newest changes that I was posting about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0Bwda1WVb-LLcYVMyYl95MDAxa0U&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0Bwda1WVb-LLcYVMyYl95MDAxa0U&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0Bwda1WVb-LLcYVMyYl95MDAxa0U&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0Bwda1WVb-LLcYVMyYl95MDAxa0U&amp;usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:57:55-07:00","id":939838,"title":"","content":"I'm proud to note that the Current of Echidna has been created! They're named the Current of Oceanus and are found before Phelegethon and after Lethe. :3 <br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Currents Document: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rt_e-yAhSTDH0L3jhdi3G6kdiqvANHdzavmvDOKpYmA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> With this, I can truly feel like saying Abyssal Currents are done. I feel like I should go about and edit the History section for all of them, make them more mysterious on their origins and potentially vague on whether they exist today. I'm thinking of also revising/creating the backstory for Sirens, the only question I have for anyone watching is &quot;what do you think it should be like&quot;?<br /> <br /> Going from the top, here's the ideas had on the Siren's Backstory that we made here and that was on the original Siren thread.<br /> <b>1:</b> Echidna is a central antagonist to Siren and one of the very few, possibly the only one to survive the Deluge.<br /> <b>2: </b>The Song is intriniscally tied to creating Sirens. It calls those who are trying to survive despite the odds.<br /> <b>3: </b>The Sirens have a matron known as Ceto who has as much importance to Sirens as Luna does to Werewolves.<br /> <b>4: </b>Sirens, at least the Celestial ones, accept that they were called to stop the Deluge from happening.<br /> <b>5: </b>The Deluge is the apocalypse that destroys the world and can take on different forms. It can be flooding, natural disasters, human caused, ice age or heat death, etc. Can be speculated to be a restart button for existence. <br /> <b>6: </b>There is a post apocalyptic remnant of the old world called the Celestial Ocean, where Survivors, Therons, Vodianoi and Echidna live that should be able to be travelled to for Sirens and as an exploratory part of the game. Treasures (Verses sealed into an object) and Trinkets can be found here.<br /> <b>7: </b>The idea that the Bloop is a manifestation of the Song, and that the Song didn't start occurring until the Industrial Revolution where men and woman started to care less about nature.<br /> <br /> Now the only question I have is, what would be a good backstory to make out of this? The idea I had involved old Gods, manifestations of the Sky, Sea and Land who made humanity and the world. They also made Ceto as the creator of the Sirens. However, the being of Land would go against the Sea, wanting the Sea's power of creation for himself. Failing in this, his rage is what caused the Deluge to happen the first time. The manifestation of the Sky and Ceto attempted to pull back time to avoid this, and in doing so created the Song, which would call forth people into becomming Sirens. Echidna was supposed to be able to get the fallen Sea's mutagenic powers of creation, in which she's still learning to use in making her Vodianoi. <br /> <br /> Any thoughts? Ideas? Other thoughts or ideas for the Backstory? What do you all think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:56:11-07:00","id":943170,"title":"","content":"I would like to take a small moment to apologize for the lack of doing things for the last few days. I've been having some horrible head problems and I feel like they're finally passing. I might be on a small break for the rest of the week though. Birthday and all. =w=<br /> <br /> Anyways, I want to take this time to finally announce some of the completion rate of Siren. Here's the outline, very short, sweet and to the point!<br /> <br /> <b>Siren Outline: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/193K-SoDpvFVylHKMbLb4wQaTLDlr1nTDdDkfIeqcjRs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I would like to believe that Siren is much over 50% done already. And out of nearly 8 months of working on this, I can say this has eaten up alot of time to make! Anyways, most of the sections left that are unfinished are mainly short sections. The only exceptions that come to mind are the Flensers and Cybernetics.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>, would it be fine if we used the Fury you created wtihin the Honolulu section? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 08-03-2016, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:37:22-07:00","id":943561,"title":"","content":"It's fine. Also, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:06:38-07:00","id":946294,"title":"","content":"Alright. Now that my little vacation is over, I'm going to post some new stuff I've gotten finished for this game. For starters, I've created the Siren Sub-Splat, <b>the Breathless!</b> They're people who failed their Drowning, and because of it their soul is wounded. They exude an aura almost like a dying person calling for help, and as such, most mortals are drawn to them like flies to honey. What's more, the wound in their soul can be reached through by Sirens and touch other people. In mechanical terms, when a Siren feeds from a Breathless, they instead gain Pneuma from almost anyone else within sight of the Breathless.<br /> <br /> As for another note, I also have something else good to announce! <b>The Introduction to Siren</b> is complete! This includes the awesome Logo Yads Dom made awhile back, a Special Thanks to those who both originally created the project and those who continued to create it, a couple of introductory paragraphs, Theme and Mood, a few myths and facts of Sirens in the game, a How to Use This Book section and finally Sources and Inspirations! <br /> <br /> I must say, I feel proud that we managed to come this far, to have the Introduction 100% done! And we're not gonna stop until we're done!<br /> <br /> <b>Introduction Document: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Breathless Document: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EjHUmaamxPZIylKJ3gOYWXYtT9llhlRm5v4ZL5voSTU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:55:04-07:00","id":949665,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, it's update time. I admit, I have been abit demotivated this past week. Mainly due to revising the Celestial Current's Histories to make them more vague and mysterious and consume less space on paper. I mainly revised because I wanted to give less information on the Pre-Diluvian World, and to make it plausible for STs to decide whether the Currents arose in the future and were brought back in time or were always there since the beginning of time.<br /> <br /> Now then! I am very pleased to announce that <b>Chapter Two: The Surfacing </b>is complete! This section contains the Waters, Celestial Currents and the Breathless Document all rolled up into one good chapter. I hope the writing is good enough, I'm pretty drained after loads of editing. =w=&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll also announce a few minor things. First, the <b>Lexicon </b>has been added to the Introduction, found at the end of it to be specific. As well, I know I said I was going to work on the Flensers at some point, and I promise I will. But I feel like I can work better if I work on the parts I'm inspired on rather than the ones I temporarily lack inspiration for. I'm sorry for breaking that promise that they would be done right after Echidna and Vodianoi were.<br /> <br /> So far, I believe I want to finish up the <b>Merits </b>page and perhaps start on the ideas we held for <b>the Ascended. </b>You know how Vampires have Golconda, Mages have Archmastery and Changelings have....well, True Faedom/Wyrd Transcendance? The Ascended are basically the ideas we had in the past for Sirens who would take bird motifs. We haven't done loads of work on them to be honest, but I have some ideas for the requirements and given powers of Ascended Sirens. The first idea I have is making them be able to be split between Land, Sea and Sky, and each of them have their own conclusions and associated powers. Either way, with these two things out of the way, Chapter 3: The Antediluvian Symphony will be complete and then Chapter One or the Flensers would be next. :3<br /> <br /> I have also taken the liberty of making a Folder within the document to hold all of the singular documents that I'm finished with instead of the Chapter Documents. Oh, and I would like to thank Polter Geist for some edit suggestions and grammar corrections. :3<br /> <br /> <b>Introduction: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Chapter 2 - The Surfacing: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BixAH8CJOcG0z40bNmJ6psZha7r6a6WUFDbg-sBYdb4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Finished Singular Siren Documents: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0Bwda1WVb-LLcbjFRamQwd09tb1k&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/folderview?...1k&amp;usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:34:18-07:00","id":952035,"title":"","content":"Alright. New update! <b>Chapter 3, The Antediluvian Symphony </b>is complete! This chapter contains <b>Creating a Siren, Systems and Advantages, Merits, Diluvian Form and Alterations, and finally Verses! </b>I hope you guys enjoy it. For now, I'm skipping the Ascended ideas. I feel I need more commentary or inspiration before I go onto that.<br /> <br /> I've also gone ahead and made the Celestial Ocean into two parts, one part explaining rules for mundane sources of water (I find it a tiny bit funny how no World of Darkness book, New or Old, has covered this yet) and the other explaining the Celestial Ocean itself! I hope you all enjoy these. :3<br /> <br /> <b>The Mundane and Celestial Oceans: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NE26FQw_RvtHgU9TedHuMvVqAkWbuftaRF33mtRqIkc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Chapter 3 - The Antediluvian Symphony: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Br5u6ylBDdzNDG6Q_r09pohkyGvgq3hSWVuJPDPrRXA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:16:22-07:00","id":955306,"title":"","content":"Good news everyone! <b>Chapter One, From Murky Depths </b>is complete! This chapter contains mostly small pieces of info on Siren things, their backstory and their culture! The next project now is bound to be Flensers and their Cybernetics! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter One - From Murky Depths: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxkSoqONxPa497tUdVETEIzDkjZL1sGukz_gWN5-MNE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:58:19-07:00","id":957294,"title":"","content":"Alright, I have a good update today. So far, the fluff and story behind the Flensers is up! Their Bio-Engineering and Cybernetics are in the works still and will take some time to complete. I've also added in two sections to Chapter 3 underneath Systems and Advantages, one explaining the effects of Siren's Flesh (under Refraction and Akashic Record) and the other explaining the Siren's thing that causes them aggravated damage underneath Pneuma, bioweaponry.<br /> <br /> <b>Flensers: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Oio9TA0pKf1vImcDUCABOwPc7i6M1iFB6krvLzMIFHU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Chapter 3: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Br5u6ylBDdzNDG6Q_r09pohkyGvgq3hSWVuJPDPrRXA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I admit, the game is inching so much closer to completion. All that even remains is the Z-Splat, the Flenser Cybernetics and Bio-Engineering, filling out the Conditions and Tilts section and finally finishing up Honolulu. I know it's abit early yet, so I believe I'll ask now.<br /> <br /> <b>Is anyone interested in Playtesting Siren the Drowning? </b>There's no special requirements that I have, all I want is for a set of willing players (at least 3, at most 5) and perhaps a Storyteller as well willing to play out this game and give their respective critiques. All the players are required to do is basically read through the book, at least the first three chapters (the first half of the fourth chapter is allowed as it contains the Abyssal Currents, but only Acheron, Cocytus and Phlegethon are allowed) to have a feel of the rules. As for the criticism, I simply want constructive criticism, no negative criticism for bad reasons. Please feel free to PM me or post here on whether you desire to be an ST or Playtesting. <br /> <br /> I'll admit, I do want someone who's had experience in STing before, but if nobody like that applies then I'm willing to accept people who've had no experience. So please, feel free to PM me with anything at all. :3 I must note that Siren isn't fully complete, simply close to it. So the playtesting may not take for awhile, a half month's time is my estimate at the moment for how long it'll take me to finish up Siren in terms of content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T09:15:39-07:00","id":963244,"title":"","content":"I would like to start out this post with an apology. This isn't exactly an update on the game itself. The closest it gets is that I've described the benefits of Status on the Flensers and began the fluff on Gene Mods.<br /> <br /> It's more that...well....I'm feeling like I'm lacking inspiration on Siren at the moment. It may be due to it being the only thing I've worked on, that I may be feeling more inspiration elsewhere. Either way though, if it's fine, I'm going to take a break from Siren. I would still like to thank the people who've taken the time to look at this project, and I promise that I'll get back to it sometime. But for now, I just want a break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:49:44-07:00","id":967813,"title":"","content":"I have some inspiration back, and I managed to come up with a few of the Genetic Modifications the Flensers will use. I know they're mostly handing out physical merits, but those are the among the best things I can think of to give for them. The major credit however goes to Karavolos. Without him, I would have no idea how to structure these.<br /> <br /> As a further note, something on my to-do list is to make a Condition dealing with eating Siren Flesh and how Gene Mods can consume stored years. Perhaps they also age someone faster, since they're replacing cells at a faster rate than people should be able to?<br /> <br /> <b>Flensers Document, Gene Mods are in the latter half (look on the Outline): </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Oio9TA0pKf1vImcDUCABOwPc7i6M1iFB6krvLzMIFHU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:43:00-07:00","id":971063,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, time for a new post. And by a new post, I mean more of a huge update and milestone completion! I've finished the Cybernetics within the Flensers document, which also means that the Flensers are complete, which also means that <b>Chapter 4, the Antagonists Chapter is COMPLETE. </b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have to admit, I'm feeling really happy about all of this. Managing to get this far with the project. As it stands, I will now say that Siren is 75-80% Complete! All that's left is finishing up the Conditions and Tilts, possibly making the Z-Splat of Choruses to finish off Appendix 1, and finally making the whole of Appendix 2, which covers the city of Honolulu, Hawaii. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I still feel like that there's still something wrong with the project, that it's not completely perfect. To this end, I was hoping to ask to anyone who views this post, do you have any constructive criticism on Siren whatsoever? I'm sorry that I'm asking for people to comment, I simply want to see what others think.<br /> <br /> So without further ado, here is Chapter 4, along with the other chapters! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Introduction: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v99pb5A0cxMR-K0Svpu1xtZ-DEMa4OHDWszGCVBQkCE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Chapter 1 - From Murky Depths: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxkSoqONxPa497tUdVETEIzDkjZL1sGukz_gWN5-MNE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Chapter 2 - The Surfacing: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BixAH8CJOcG0z40bNmJ6psZha7r6a6WUFDbg-sBYdb4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Chapter 3 - The Antediluvian Symphony: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Br5u6ylBDdzNDG6Q_r09pohkyGvgq3hSWVuJPDPrRXA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Chapter 4 - Shedding Light Upon the Depths: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1g52Gv2hBwPSFSayuWsnubBZqUF6ZQBz74OOto7xSnCI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T18:51:05-07:00","id":975325,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say that i'm extremely proud of you and am happy to have been a small part of this project. You are awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T18:53:09-07:00","id":975326,"title":"","content":"Double posting like a pro: I'm going to read it right now, and I'll be back to say what I Think!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T19:24:28-07:00","id":975336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=975325#post975325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to say that i'm extremely proud of you and am happy to have been a small part of this project. You are awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would've never had any ideas on how to do this project or what direction to go into without the commentary/help from you and Reaper. Think of it like this: You and Reaper gave me/created a coloring book and the outlines, I simply colored them in. My only hope is that I used the best colors. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=975326#post975326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double posting like a pro: I'm going to read it right now, and I'll be back to say what I Think!</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it's all liked. The one thing about Fansplats is that they're almost never finished until there's nothing more for the creators to say, so feel free to comment or bring up any changes and I'll be willing to evaluate them all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:40:54-07:00","id":976665,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, not much of an update, but I've done an edit explaining how the Flensers have managed to make Cybernetics and Gene Mods in the present time and why they keep them a secret. <b>Added Parts: &quot;</b>For the Flensers, there were two roadblocks to realizing their ambitions. The most obvious one was the factor of being noticed in their work. In the present time, Flenser\u2019s don\u2019t seem to have the need to be secret about their work. However, back in the 15th Century when science was facing oppression for, as they reasoned, \u201ctampering with God\u2019s domain or with what only the holy book can proclaim\u201d, the Flensers have long since kept their studies a secret.<br /> The second roadblock was something along the lines of scientific ethics. If they wished to truly exceed humanity\u2019s limits, they were required to break a few of those rules. Even today, the Flensers conduct experiments that can permanently disrupt the DNA of the test subject or Cybernetics that can go haywire. But like the horrid experiments committed by the Axis Powers of World War 2, the Flensers experiments yield advanced results. This combination of secrecy and lack of scientific ethics is what has lead the flesh hunters to creating their arsenal of Gene Mods and Cybernetics.&quot;<br /> <br /> In other notes, I haven't gotten much of a start on Choruses. Given they're the Z-Splat, the original ideas we had for them was they would be based on plays or operas in their themes and the like. We don't have much of mechanics set up, but I'm open to any and all suggestions. :3<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T19:58:32-07:00","id":976898,"title":"","content":"I just want to applaud you for getting so far on Siren. Sincerely and genuinely. It takes a lot of drive to work on projects like these and I have to give you props for going the distance.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm back from the grave! Seriously though, I'm finally done with school <i>(for the most part; I still need to come back to campus to sign things but no more classes!)</i> and I'm going to give the documents a good look-through to see what I've missed for the last...half of a year or so? <br /> <br /> I'll try to toss in my two cents every now and then, especially considering that I have free time now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T01:04:02-07:00","id":977058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reaper Verse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=976898#post976898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to applaud you for getting so far on Siren. Sincerely and genuinely. It takes a lot of drive to work on projects like these and I have to give you props for going the distance.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm back from the grave! Seriously though, I'm finally done with school <i>(for the most part; I still need to come back to campus to sign things but no more classes!)</i> and I'm going to give the documents a good look-through to see what I've missed for the last...half of a year or so?<br /> <br /> I'll try to toss in my two cents every now and then, especially considering that I have free time now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thankies. As said before and as I will always say, I wouldn't have come this far without you or Yads giving me the ideas that fueled the inspiration that continued this project along. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And welcome back to you too, feel free to send any comments and evaluations, I'll look at them all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T15:07:14-07:00","id":981051,"title":"","content":"Pardon my lack of developments on this. Life has been intruding on me heavily and recently something bad has happened. This project isn't forgotten and I will be sure to continue it up to completion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:24:20-07:00","id":982134,"title":"","content":"(Now that I've read the thread)<br /> <br /> Just wanted to say that I am very impressed with all the effort gone into Siren. You have it in a 90% ready to play build for the guide. Without a doubt I can say that it's topped Leviathan: the Tempest as my favorite aquatic folklore fan made game line.<br /> <br /> I plan on introducing it to my crossover game at some point, where anything well developed of official and fan material has the potential to be included. Siren creates a lot of synergy with Princess, the central venue of my game as all of the player characters are Nobility. Princesses and Sirens are both driven to try to change the world for the better with many different approaches, some running counter and antagonistic to each other, and both have a wide variety of opponents towards their goals without having to resort to crossover (even though that is a favorite of mine). Princesses are driven from the cataclysm of Darkness and the Fall of the past kingdoms while Sirens have passed and scene the likely apocalypse of the future Deluge.<br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to constructive criticism, I would have commented on the GDocs but felt it would better facilitate discussion if done in the thread.<br /> <br /> In terms of Celestial Alertations, don't Tropicana's <b>Poison Immunity</b> and Discordia's <b>Dolphin's Pervsion</b> do exactly the same thing?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Poison Immunity</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Not all fish are vulnerable to poisons. The clownfish make their home in the middle of the poisonous anemone without fear of their poisons or being eaten. The Siren\u2019s colors shift out into some form or pattern, much like how you can tell how \u201cred and yellow, kill a fellow\u201d applies to snakes. <u><i>The Siren may add half her Akashic Record, rounded up, to all rolls to resist poisons of all kinds (save pollutants).</i></u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inspiration: Clownfish</span></i></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dolphin\u2019s Perversion</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">How is it that as animals, dolphins are commonly one of the most beloved in media or signs, and yet they are really one of the most depraved amongst the animals in the seas? They rip off the heads of other fishes to masterbate with them, they get high from pufferfish, they rape their own species and drag down other beings to drown and rape. The Siren may match their level in perversion, gaining a dolphin\u2019s dorsal fin upon her face. <u><i>The Siren adds half her Akashic Record, rounded up, to all rolls to hold off poison and drugs.</i></u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inspiration: Dolphins</span></i></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In short, both provide the benefit of adding half Akashic Record to resisting natural poisons (excludes BioToxin). Given the wording of Dolphin's Perversion, wouldn't it be better as a sort &quot;faux pax&quot; defense? As like Dolphins, those of the Discordian Waters are willing to go to the extremes to enact change with behavior that, while not criminal, is very much a cultural taboo. Yet they emerge from the act without having their reputation drop or even enhanced because of it? Unless that sounds too complex for an Alteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T20:16:21-07:00","id":982527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982134#post982134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Now that I've read the thread)<br /> <br /> Just wanted to say that I am very impressed with all the effort gone into Siren. You have it in a 90% ready to play build for the guide. Without a doubt I can say that it's topped Leviathan: the Tempest as my favorite aquatic folklore fan made game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much. I greatly appreciate this comment and I'm happy you like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982134#post982134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I plan on introducing it to my crossover game at some point, where anything well developed of official and fan material has the potential to be included. Siren creates a lot of synergy with Princess, the central venue of my game as all of the player characters are Nobility. Princesses and Sirens are both driven to try to change the world for the better with many different approaches, some running counter and antagonistic to each other, and both have a wide variety of opponents towards their goals without having to resort to crossover (even though that is a favorite of mine). Princesses are driven from the cataclysm of Darkness and the Fall of the past kingdoms while Sirens have passed and scene the likely apocalypse of the future Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I know of the similarities to Princess (the most blatant ones are that I've used Taint mechanics as a base for Quagmires and even used the &quot;Craft Vessel&quot; Numen that Goalenu use, both of which with King's permission) and I've imagined a few crossovers for Siren-Princess campaigns in the case if I make a crossovers section, mainly with Lethe and Flensers working with Tears and Styx and Furies working with Storms. The latter of which would only happen if the Stormites weren't mistaking a Quagmire for a Taint. ;3<br /> <br /> I'm happy that Siren is good enough to stand on it's own without Crossovers. One of the things I feel should be needed for a gameline is the ability for the world to be able to sustain itself first, and hopefully if it covers enough areas then it could be made Crossover friendly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982134#post982134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to constructive criticism, I would have commented on the GDocs but felt it would better facilitate discussion if done in the thread.<br /> <br /> In terms of Celestial Alertations, don't Tropicana's <b>Poison Immunity</b> and Discordia's <b>Dolphin's Pervsion</b> do exactly the same thing?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Poison Immunity</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Not all fish are vulnerable to poisons. The clownfish make their home in the middle of the poisonous anemone without fear of their poisons or being eaten. The Siren\u2019s colors shift out into some form or pattern, much like how you can tell how \u201cred and yellow, kill a fellow\u201d applies to snakes. <u><i>The Siren may add half her Akashic Record, rounded up, to all rolls to resist poisons of all kinds (save pollutants).</i></u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inspiration: Clownfish</span></i></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dolphin\u2019s Perversion</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">How is it that as animals, dolphins are commonly one of the most beloved in media or signs, and yet they are really one of the most depraved amongst the animals in the seas? They rip off the heads of other fishes to masterbate with them, they get high from pufferfish, they rape their own species and drag down other beings to drown and rape. The Siren may match their level in perversion, gaining a dolphin\u2019s dorsal fin upon her face. <u><i>The Siren adds half her Akashic Record, rounded up, to all rolls to hold off poison and drugs.</i></u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Inspiration: Dolphins</span></i></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In short, both provide the benefit of adding half Akashic Record to resisting natural poisons (excludes BioToxin). Given the wording of Dolphin's Perversion, wouldn't it be better as a sort &quot;faux pax&quot; defense? As like Dolphins, those of the Discordian Waters are willing to go to the extremes to enact change with behavior that, while not criminal, is very much a cultural taboo. Yet they emerge from the act without having their reputation drop or even enhanced because of it? Unless that sounds too complex for an Alteration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah jeeze. I think I actually noticed this when I finished up Alterations, forgot it, and didn't remember until you brought it up now. XD <br /> <br /> I would say Alterations should be connected to biological functions, something the body or it's reflexes can reproduce or learn even if it borders on magic without going fully overboard. I can see your idea working though. Afterall, for how evil the dolphins are, people still see them as &quot;cutesy ocean creatures&quot;. :3 Not to mention I wanted five of the Alterations for the Discordians to have direct connotations to the Abyssal Currents, and given Phlegethon outright uses Dolphins and are meant to abuse their relationships, an Alteration that fits that would be suitable. <br /> <br /> How does this sound as a revision?<br /> <br /> <b>Dolphin's Perversion</b><br /> How is it that as animals, dolphins are commonly one of the most beloved in media or signs, and yet they are really one of the most depraved amongst the animals in the seas? They rip off the heads of other fishes to masterbate with them, they get high from pufferfish, they rape their own species and drag down other beings harm the same way. The Siren may match their level in perversion, gaining the mark of the dolphin's cute little facial features. Whenever someone views upon the Siren acting upon baser urges or the person is under the influence of something that makes them act upon their baser urges, any Social penalties the Siren would take instead become Bonuses. The person doesn't forget the acts the Siren has committed, but for some reason they just seem more...excusable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:00:56-07:00","id":982798,"title":"","content":"If it is not too late, I would like to share a antagonist idea i came up with for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:08:02-07:00","id":982805,"title":"","content":"Do tell, I see no harm from a suggestion alone personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:16:03-07:00","id":982808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982798#post982798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is not too late, I would like to share a antagonist idea i came up with for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to, you don't need my permission to post here. :3 I should probably note/warn that I feel Siren has more than enough antagonists (Flensers, Quagmires/Furies, the six Abyssal Currents and the Vodianoi for Echidna's and Banshees (Lucidity 0 Sirens)). But please don't misunderstand, I don't want to stop you from posting your idea. It may still be used for Honolulu, the major city for Sirens we're planning on using for them or it may be applicable for one of the antagonists above with something new or unique for them. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:37:50-07:00","id":982817,"title":"","content":"My basic idea is a corporation named Poseidon International, a multi-national corporation founded by a Norwegian oceanographer named Roy Petterson. The corporation is based in Oslo, Norway and claims to be researching the ocean to figure out how it's untapped resources can benefit humanity. The general public is aware of two of their projects, both of which seem to be benevolent. The first being a study of sea sponges to see how they are resistant to cancer and a way to possibly transplant that trait to humans. and the second being a search for a cheaper method of desalination. However, the general public is unaware of a third, more insidious experiment. This experiment involves the capturing of Sirens and the harvesting of their DNA in a attempt to make humans amphibious so it could make colonizing the bottom of the ocean possible.<br /> <br /> Although the sirens consider Poseidon to be ignorant Flensers unaware of the secret potency of their flesh, if you were to call one of their scientists one you would be barraged with insults and a possible punch to the face. Even though Poseidon and the Flensers have some similarities, the differences out measure the similarities. In fact, Fesnsers and Poseidon hate each other with a burning passion. The Flensers accuse Poseidon of stealing their lawful prey while Poseidon accuses them of killing creature that could possibly benefit humanity. This often results in Poseidon research ships and Flenser vessels fighting each other in gun fights.<br /> <br /> How Poseidon figured out about the existence of Sirens is unknown. Theories range from one of their research vessels stumbling upon a wounded one all the way to an Abyssal Siren being the current chairman of the company. The most horryfing theory however, is the idea that the entire corporation is serving Echidna. This theory states that the comapny is trying to aid Echidna by capturing sirens and crossing their DNA with humans. Whatever theory is true the sirens know one thing, Poseidon will continue to be a constant threat to their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:24:49-07:00","id":982848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982817#post982817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My basic idea is a corporation named Poseidon International, a multi-national corporation founded by a Norwegian oceanographer named Roy Petterson. The corporation is based in Oslo, Norway and claims to be researching the ocean to figure out how it's untapped resources can benefit humanity. The general public is aware of two of their projects, both of which seem to be benevolent. The first being a study of sea sponges to see how they are resistant to cancer and a way to possibly transplant that trait to humans. and the second being a search for a cheaper method of desalination. However, the general public is unaware of a third, more insidious experiment. This experiment involves the capturing of Sirens and the harvesting of their DNA in a attempt to make humans amphibious so it could make colonizing the bottom of the ocean possible.<br /> <br /> Although the sirens consider Poseidon to be ignorant Flensers unaware of the secret potency of their flesh, if you were to call one of their scientists one you would be barraged with insults and a possible punch to the face. Even though Poseidon and the Flensers have some similarities, the differences out measure the similarities. In fact, Fesnsers and Poseidon hate each other with a burning passion. The Flensers accuse Poseidon of stealing their lawful prey while Poseidon accuses them of killing creature that could possibly benefit humanity. This often results in Poseidon research ships and Flenser vessels fighting each other in gun fights.<br /> <br /> How Poseidon figured out about the existence of Sirens is unknown. Theories range from one of their research vessels stumbling upon a wounded one all the way to an Abyssal Siren being the current chairman of the company. The most horryfing theory however, is the idea that the entire corporation is serving Echidna. This theory states that the comapny is trying to aid Echidna by capturing sirens and crossing their DNA with humans. Whatever theory is true the sirens know one thing, Poseidon will continue to be a constant threat to their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must admit, when I was first reading this, I did get the impression of Flensers at first. However, when it got to where the company and Flensers are at each others throats, I couldn't help but feel like it was odd. Don't misunderstand, this feels like a &quot;good&quot; kind of &quot;odd&quot; to me, not being Flensers but antagonizing them instead. <br /> <br /> As I kept on reading, I felt the idea coming along that, given the company's purposes, what if they were serving Echidna but they simply didn't know it? I was surprised to see that that was one of the theories at the end. Heck, it's entirely plausible. Echidna isn't the most sane of beings, but she does know to leave most of the work of dealing with the Pre-Diluvian world to her Sirens. So long as they expand her research, the better. :3 <br /> <br /> I was thinking, would it be ok to implement this as one of the factions present in Honolulu? As much as I'd like to write them as &quot;They're totally being controlled by Echidna or her sirens&quot;, I will resist that and make sure to leave them ambiguous on &quot;how they know/care about sirens&quot;. <br /> <br /> Which makes me also wonder, what do they do with the Sirens they capture? Keep them unconscious and alive? It's hard to test on Siren DNA when it doesn't stick around very long after it's cut off, so I imagine they maaaay need to have live subjects, as grimdark as that sounds. Although that gives another ambiguous factor: That the Sirens captured are given the choice to be test subjects or to join Echidna's Abyssal Current. Those who choose to join are sometimes seen again, but marked with enough Malformations that they suffer from the Echidnal Echoes Condition. This can give a hook for Sirens to investigate what they do with who they capture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:52:33-07:00","id":982868,"title":"","content":"Most of the time they tend to keep them alive as long as physically possible depending on the specimen in question and where it is caught. For example, if it is caught in the Baltic it can expect a long lifespan since they have a facility in Danzig where they can be expected to live for awhile before the experiments kill them. But if they are caught in the middle of the Pacific ocean by say a research vessel or one of their faster patrol boatsit spells bad new for the siren. Since they are not near one of their facilities they have three options what they could do with it, they can try to keep it contained until they safely arrive in either Honolulu, Danzing, or the Echo Base in the Arctic. they could also tag it with a tracker hidden discretely somewhere on its body and come back for it later with a lot more boats and hope it would lead them to a large gathering of Sirens. The third and more drastic notion is that they perform a very lethal DNA extraction right there on the boat, which would kill it and would leave one less test subject for the company. I am fine with them being in Honolulu as an enemy faction for the sirens to fight and i could describe the staff of the facility if you want.<br /> <br /> Also, how would The Abyssal Sirens view them? I want to know because they are some of the more &quot;common&quot; antagonists in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:16:00-07:00","id":982879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982868#post982868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the time they tend to keep them alive as long as physically possible depending on the specimen in question and where it is caught. For example, if it is caught in the Baltic it can expect a long lifespan since they have a facility in Danzig where they can be expected to live for awhile before the experiments kill them. But if they are caught in the middle of the Pacific ocean by say a research vessel or one of their faster patrol boatsit spells bad new for the siren. Since they are not near one of their facilities they have three options what they could do with it, they can try to keep it contained until they safely arrive in either Honolulu, Danzing, or the Echo Base in the Arctic. they could also tag it with a tracker hidden discretely somewhere on its body and come back for it later with a lot more boats and hope it would lead them to a large gathering of Sirens. The third and more drastic notion is that they perform a very lethal DNA extraction right there on the boat, which would kill it and would leave one less test subject for the company. I am fine with them being in Honolulu as an enemy faction for the sirens to fight and i could describe the staff of the facility if you want.<br /> <br /> Also, how would The Abyssal Sirens view them? I want to know because they are some of the more &quot;common&quot; antagonists in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Sirens could notice a tracker on them if they searched themselves. If nothing else, I can see it still working if they put a tracking chip into a flechette that would dig into the Siren. The only problem on the Siren is the need to dig it out, which is impossible unless they use Self-Blood-Restore to heal the wound (Which magically takes out foreign objects) or Target-Earth (Since the Flechette is made of metal)-Invoke to make it tear out of their body. The only problem I can further see is having the resources to make tracking chips and the like. <br /> <br /> As for the Abyssal Sirens, it depends on the Current. <br /> <br /> Acheron would try using them as dupes, trying to get them to do utterly atrocious things on their behalf. When they outlive their usefulness, then the Acheron Siren(s) would try exposing them for their &quot;human testing&quot; experiments and get them to have a breakdown of massive proportions.<br /> <br /> Cocytus would be interested in finding out how they know about Sirens and trying to get that information. I imagine the most likely possibilities are that they'd prolly either get caught by an Echidnal Siren and be summarily kept as a live subject, find out that there's Echidnals present and try to vamoose to sell the Info to other Sirens, or they'd prolly wouldn't care about Poseidon International. One thing I already see about them is that they don't have the same advantages Flensers do (let's say Poseidon International is like a Compact compared to the Flenser's Conspiracy in Hunter Terms) and thus would be easier to ward off. <br /> <br /> Lethe Sirens are Allied with Flensers, so they tend to have the same opinion as the Flensers do, which is basically &quot;Unless they take our quarry from us, they're not worth our time&quot;. Perhaps a little moreso in that the Lethe Sirens can be targeted by Poseidon International, and as such would be more willing to take them down before they can crop up.<br /> <br /> Oceanus Sirens, AKA Echidnals, depend on the company's status. If Poseidon International doesn't belong to them, then they will seek to take control of it with any means necessary. If they do, then there's little change. <br /> <br /> Phlegethon Sirens think more of themselves and their needs than the needs of others. They don't care if Poseidon is in the area, the Siren will still have fun. Although if the Siren becomes a target of Poseidon, then she may treat the hunt like a game of cat and mouse, liking it for the thrill.<br /> <br /> Finally, Styx Sirens would treat them the same as Flensers, or perhaps even worse. They are taking live Sirens as test subjects. Given that Styx tends to see themselves as the apex predators/beings, they would crush that which would treat them as prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:33:45-07:00","id":982896,"title":"","content":"Thanks for describing the opinions. I agree with the tracker part and i could cut it out if you want. Also, their advantage is when send in entire research fleets since they tend to cover more ground then a single boat. Also, even tough they are crap at capturing single sirens they truly excel at capturing groups. I was also thinking of having one of the Oceanus Sirens' infiltrate the company's Board of Directors and influence them from within. Would that be okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:12:24-07:00","id":982922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982896#post982896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for describing the opinions. I agree with the tracker part and i could cut it out if you want. Also, their advantage is when send in entire research fleets since they tend to cover more ground then a single boat. Also, even tough they are crap at capturing single sirens they truly excel at capturing groups. I was also thinking of having one of the Oceanus Sirens' infiltrate the company's Board of Directors and influence them from within. Would that be okay?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably best. Although I think it should be the opposite when it comes to Sirens. They're best at capturing singular Sirens and trying to catch groups of them is an utter disaster. It's indeed ok to have one of the Echidnals Infiltrating the Board of Directors, I love the idea of it. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:28:36-07:00","id":982932,"title":"","content":"Alright they will be good at capturing individuals. Are you okay with the idea of their research fleets because i can cut that out too? Also, how familiar would the siren be with Poseidon? Would they be a fairly new enemy they barely consider a threat or would they consider them a true threat and look for ways to cripple them? I am also sorry if they seem too much like PENTEX from werewolf the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:37:00-07:00","id":982964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982527#post982527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happy that Siren is good enough to stand on it's own without Crossovers. One of the things I feel should be needed for a gameline is the ability for the world to be able to sustain itself first, and hopefully if it covers enough areas then it could be made Crossover friendly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the best Chronicles projects have a mix of foes beyond 'ourselves but evil' and 'potential Hunter conspiracy' and Siren definitely fits that build. Much like the Twilight vs Radiant Queens in Princess, the Abyssal currents take their own perspective of the inherent conflict (Nature vs Civilization in this case) to the antagonizing extreme. Beyond them, there's the 'bottomed out integrity' Banshees, the avatars of Nature in the form of Quagmires and Furies, Echidna's forces and humanity's transgressions against Sirens in the form of Flensers; the latter benefitting from having a lot more nuance than 'evil Alchemists, as no rational Alchemist would otherwise appear in a Chronicle' connotation in Promethean.<br /> <br /> This mix also allows for ambiguity for who is in the 'right' which I find a strength for Storytelling. Whether you have players with characters in the opposing factions or not, you can create a spectrum where your common player factions question how different they really are from their opponents. And it provides a lot of options for 'Enemy Mine' situations. Your characters can struggle with having to effectively team up with their sworn foes against a greater threat.<br /> <br /> I have a variety of Crossover thoughts, although I will save those for when the discussion returns to that topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dolphin's Perversion</b><br /> How is it that as animals, dolphins are commonly one of the most beloved in media or signs, and yet they are really one of the most depraved amongst the animals in the seas? They rip off the heads of other fishes to masterbate with them, they get high from pufferfish, they rape their own species and drag down other beings harm the same way. The Siren may match their level in perversion, gaining the mark of the dolphin's cute little facial features. <u><i>Whenever someone views upon the Siren acting upon baser urges or the person is under the influence of something that makes them act upon their baser urges, any Social penalties the Siren would take instead become Bonuses. The person doesn't forget the acts the Siren has committed, but for some reason they just seem more...excusable.</i></u> </div> </div> </div>That's a fitting revision.<br /> <br /> That sounds close to something I was going to suggest involving Vices, although that's hampered by Sirens having Flow and Beaching instead of Virtue and Vice. I don't know of any standard set of social penalties but the effect reminds me of a Princess Charm, somewhat. Another idea, involving Social Maneuvers, was that the Siren with <i>Dolphin's Perversion</i> could attempt Hard Leverage without the drawbacks of Failure or lowered Impression. However it would only work once per person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:57:13-07:00","id":982972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982932#post982932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright they will be good at capturing individuals. Are you okay with the idea of their research fleets because i can cut that out too? Also, how familiar would the siren be with Poseidon? Would they be a fairly new enemy they barely consider a threat or would they consider them a true threat and look for ways to cripple them? I am also sorry if they seem too much like PENTEX from werewolf the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say they shouldn't have entire fleets of ships. That would be the Flensers at best, but they wouldn't by any means actually do that, that would draw national attention to them. I would say the Poseidon International would at best have a few research ships, equipped enough with the essentials that the Flensers have without dipping into Cybernetics or Gene Mods (so Scuba gear, Automatic Underwater Rifle and air tanks). I would say that the Poseidon International could've basically been a water research lab/organization that's been around long enough so that the Flensers would disregard them when they (the Flensers) were forming/getting more organized, but not too new because the Flensers would either try to get them into the Siren trade or crush them. <br /> <br /> For an analysis/timeline of this, let's say Poseidon International started sometime in the 1800s. The Flensers were beginning to get together around the 1400-1500s and have gotten fully organized during the 1700s. In the Flenser's perspective, Poseidon International would be a child compared to them and as long as they didn't learn about Sirens, they'd be fine. So they disregarded them instead and let them grow. I would say they don't cover as much ground as Flensers do (and Flensers can be found on pretty much every shore), but they're enough for the Flensers to take notice (such as having at least one lab per major body of water).<br /> <br /> For how they learned about Sirens, I'm tempted to say that they stumbled upon it in the 1900s. I want to say a Shoal of Echidnal Sirens came to them, offering them ways to make their dreams come true with the catch that they must capture (non-Echidnal) Sirens to attain it. Then they pretty much show how Echidna's DNA warping goes and lets them do the research. This way, they serve Echidna's goals by expanding her research, and having the hunters in Posiedon taking out non-Echidnal Sirens in the process so Echidnals could do their duties without inteference.<br /> <br /> As an added incentive to service, the Echidnals could offer a blessing, allowing them to become like the humanity they wish to create. In Game terms, higher ups in the company (and/or hunters) would be granted Malformations (this covers the Alterations only Echidna can grant and the Alterations of all waters that Echidna grafts on to people). This does mean that some people have to limit their public appearances (For Sirens, Malformations are present on both Diluvian and Land forms. For humans, this would mean that Malformations are basically always present on them), but they do become more powerful.<br /> <br /> The real twist here is that anyone with Malformations in the company would suffer from the Echidnal Echoes Condition, which means they are almost completely subservient to Echidna and her Sirens.So in short, they would basically be Unwitting Pawns of Echidna.<br /> <br /> Of course, these are just my ideas on how to make the company like. Don't worry about them being too much like Pentex from WtA. The Flensers cover the exact same ground as PENTEX, the only difference is that Flensers don't want to corrupt everything for the Evlulz, more for the Siren Flesh and getting resources for their Cybernetics/Gene Mods.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the TL;DR post I just made. &gt;w&gt;&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:07:00-07:00","id":982980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982964#post982964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the best Chronicles projects have a mix of foes beyond 'ourselves but evil' and 'potential Hunter conspiracy' and Siren definitely fits that build. Much like the Twilight vs Radiant Queens in Princess, the Abyssal currents take their own perspective of the inherent conflict (Nature vs Civilization in this case) to the antagonizing extreme. Beyond them, there's the 'bottomed out integrity' Banshees, the avatars of Nature in the form of Quagmires and Furies, Echidna's forces and humanity's transgressions against Sirens in the form of Flensers; the latter benefitting from having a lot more nuance than 'evil Alchemists, as no rational Alchemist would otherwise appear in a Chronicle' connotation in Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that I'm unaware of Alchemists in Promethean and if there's overt similiarites to them in the Flensers, I'm utterly unaware of them. ^^&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982964#post982964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This mix also allows for ambiguity for who is in the 'right' which I find a strength for Storytelling. Whether you have players with characters in the opposing factions or not, you can create a spectrum where your common player factions question how different they really are from their opponents. And it provides a lot of options for 'Enemy Mine' situations. Your characters can struggle with having to effectively team up with their sworn foes against a greater threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982964#post982964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a variety of Crossover thoughts, although I will save those for when the discussion returns to that topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't wait to hear them. I'll save mine for when we get to those too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=982964#post982964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fitting revision.<br /> <br /> That sounds close to something I was going to suggest involving Vices, although that's hampered by Sirens having Flow and Beaching instead of Virtue and Vice. I don't know of any standard set of social penalties but the effect reminds me of a Princess Charm, somewhat. Another idea, involving Social Maneuvers, was that the Siren with <i>Dolphin's Perversion</i> could attempt Hard Leverage without the drawbacks of Failure or lowered Impression. However it would only work once per person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. :3 I think I may actually use the idea you presented, it feels much more fitting especially with the GMC rules. I'll save the version I made for a Pre-Gmc version of Siren. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T19:24:52-07:00","id":983082,"title":"","content":"As for Alchemists and Flensers, their only similarity is that they prey upon the player characters. Alchemists can drain the Vitriol (i.e. specialized Experience from the Pilgrimage) from Prometheans and have a Magnitude trait to mimic Promethean abilities and store Pyros. They gather in guilds interested in a certain cause. Much of the critique, mostly from others on this site, is the notion that to have Alchemists be villains they would have to disregard their humanity to prey upon the Created. An Alchemist off focused on something else wouldn't be a threat and then wouldn't appear in (the majority of) the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Flensers have been given their own rules and abilities derived from centuries of science and eating Siren flesh. In my viewpoint I like it how there are quite the fraction of Flensers who do realize their transgression when eating Siren flesh and it drives them to find a way where such a practice would not be needed. Yet until then they still need their fix...<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022</span></span><br /> <br /> I've spent the evening drafting up new Alterations and Merits for consideration and critique. I don't think they overlap too greatly with the current list. If anything sounds too complex it could be split into separate criteria.<br /> <br /> These first two I would have listed as Alterations that could effect the Siren's human form, although given only Malformations do that and there are no drawbacks using it turning them into Merits gave it better universal coverage. (Yet a Malformation similarity is listed far below)<br /> <br /> <b>Carnivorous (</b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once per scene, the Siren may gain 1 Pneuma from eating the flesh of an animal native to her Water, minimum of Size 1. She gains an additional Pneuma if she hunted the creature herself. Much like the regular way of regaining Pneuma from her Water, multiple Waters may overlap in regard to the species eaten for this benefit.<br /> <br /> <b>Herbivorous (</b>\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once per scene, the Siren may gain 1 Pneuma from eating vegetation or fungus native to her Water, minimum of Size 1. She gains an additional Pneuma if this vegetation was raised and harvested by herself. Much like the regular way of regaining Pneuma from her Water, multiple Waters may overlap in regard to the species eaten for this benefit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The following Alterations I will list with ideas for category.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Barbed Quills</b><br /> <i>(General or Discordia)</i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Siren's Diluvian form may have rough tiny scales or fine slender spines. This augments her unarmed strikes as 0L damage. She may fire these quills as a Short Burst (up to 5 shots) with a range of 5/10/20 both above and under the water, rolling Dexterity + Firearms. It costs 1 Pneuma to replenish these quills. Additionally, whenever the Siren is in a grapple they may spend 1 Pneuma to leave these quills in her opponent as a 1 Lethal attack. This requires another Pneuma to replenish the quills, as above.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Inspiration: Sea urchins, pufferfish, lionfish</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mollusk's Beak</b><br /> <i>(General, Tropicana or Discordia)</i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Siren has a sharp beak for a mouth that can dislocate or perhaps sharp pincers elsewhere on her body. As a full round action she can bypass the Durability of an object to harm it. She subtracts the greater of her Strength or half Akashic Record from the Durability of the object, leftover value being inflicted as Structure damage. The Siren is denied her Defense when piercing Durability.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Inspiration: Octopi, squids</i><br /> <br /> <b>Bioluminescence</b><br /> <i>(Tropicana or Polaria)</i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Faint light glows from the Siren, which can be activated or dampened reflexively. When active she has a soft illumination no greater than a flashlight. This applies as a penalty of half Akashic Record to avoid being noticed, however the dexterous Siren may distract with her light to receive a bonus of half Akashic Record to her Defense for the first round of combat. For 1 Pneuma the Siren may inflict the Blinded Tilt on a single opponent for half Akashic Record turns.<br /> <i>Inspiration: anglerfish, many deep sea creatures</i></span><br /> <br /> <b>Blowhole</b><br /> <i>(General or Polaria)</i><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">A secondary breathing orifice exists along the Siren's back. She gains the benefit of the 9-again rule when using her Stamina to manage breathing in Diluvian form. She may spend 1 Pneuma to expel a poisonous substance from her system, reducing the remaining Toxicity by Akashic Record. If removing a major pollutant like Biotoxin, the rejection of the substance also inflicts 1 Lethal damage.</span><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Inspiration: whales, porpoises and other cetaceans</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Spectral Vision</b><br /> <i>(Gardenia or Tropicana)</i><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Siren's eyes are enhanced to see across a wider spectrum. She ignores any penalty to perception that is -1. She can recognize unusual features like bloodstains, body fluids and other residues or trace evidence, unless they were rigorously cleaned. This grants a bonus of half Akashic Record to such a search or investigation. The Siren receives this bonus a number of times per scene up to her Wits.<br /> <i>Inspiration: Shrimp</i><br /> <br /> <b>Horrendous Consumption (Malformation)</b><br /> How wil humanity (mainly Echidna's agents) survive the blighted aftermath of the apocalypse? This requires the means to find nutrition from the most dubious of sources. The Vodinaoi can eat their chosen food to avoid deprivation regardless of its state, suffering no drawbacks or damage from spoiled and rotten food. Because of the body odor produced from their altered digestive tract, the stench applies a -2 penalty against the Vodinaoi, such as for some Social rolls or when tracking them by scent. Once a scene, when feasting on the selected food the Vodinaoi can gain 1 Willpower for every Size category eaten. Sirens may chose to gain Pneuma instead.<br /> <br /> This Malformation can only be taken once. Select the category of food for the Vodinaoi to consume:</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Carnivore's Diet:</i> you are sustained by meat and flesh, however fresh or processed, including other animal byproducts (like eggs and milk). If you attack a creature with the intent to eat it your successful attack gains an additional point of damage (only Bashing or Lethal). Treat any vegetation or fungal matter as a Toxicity 2 substance if ingested.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Herbivore's Diet:</i><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> you are sustained by the vegetation and fungal matter of nature. Instead of gaining Willpower you may instead gain temporary dice used for being attuned to your environment for the rest of the scene. This bonus can be divided amongst rolls pertaining to nature such as Science, Survival or Animal Ken. Treat any meat or animal byproduct as a Toxicity 2 substance when ingested.</span></span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:24:15-07:00","id":983115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983082#post983082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Alchemists and Flensers, their only similarity is that they prey upon the player characters. Alchemists can drain the Vitriol (i.e. specialized Experience from the Pilgrimage) from Prometheans and have a Magnitude trait to mimic Promethean abilities and store Pyros. They gather in guilds interested in a certain cause. Much of the critique, mostly from others on this site, is the notion that to have Alchemists be villains they would have to disregard their humanity to prey upon the Created. An Alchemist off focused on something else wouldn't be a threat and then wouldn't appear in (the majority of) the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Flensers have been given their own rules and abilities derived from centuries of science and eating Siren flesh. In my viewpoint I like it how there are quite the fraction of Flensers who do realize their transgression when eating Siren flesh and it drives them to find a way where such a practice would not be needed. Yet until then they still need their fix...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. :3 I hope it's not minded noting, but even though there is a faction of Flensers who do want to find a way to immortality, in my mind there's room for both those with good and bad intentions. The good intentions is as you said, finding out how to achieve immortality without the need of Siren flesh, but still consuming it until then. The bad intentions? Probably that Siren Flesh is the most appealing way to achieve immortality and when Sirens aren't required anymore, the Flensers could care less about dealing with them.<br /> <br /> To compare to other gamelines, Siren Flesh isn't addictive like Vampire Blood, they aren't enforced to be sociopaths like the Knights of the Bloody Chalice (Dragon the Embers), and they don't need to have a Beast tied to their soul and lose taste of worldly pleasures due to undeath (Vampire). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983082#post983082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022</span></span><br /> <br /> I've spent the evening drafting up new Alterations and Merits for consideration and critique. I don't think they overlap too greatly with the current list. If anything sounds too complex it could be split into separate criteria.<br /> <br /> These first two I would have listed as Alterations that could effect the Siren's human form, although given only Malformations do that and there are no drawbacks using it turning them into Merits gave it better universal coverage. (Yet a Malformation similarity is listed far below)<br /> <br /> <b>Carnivorous (</b>\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Herbivorous (</b>\u2022\u2022)</div> </div> </div> </div>I must admit, I'm happy this line has given inspiration to write. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If nothing else, I will give my thoughts on things.<br /> <br /> First off, the Merits. I like how they look, but there's only one problem. Pneuma is to Sirens as Vitae is to Vampires. It's a vital part of the human that without such, they suffer. The difference being, Pneuma is literally pieces of the human soul and Vitae is blood. <br /> <br /> Actually, I don't think there's a problem with the merits. I think the problem lies in that I didn't think of extra feeding mechanics already present within Sirens. For comparison, Vampires can feed from blood so long as it's from a human or animal, the latter being less nourishing and &quot;cold&quot; blood being like eating a can of old dog food. Sirens can only feed from humans and from bathing in something reminiscent to their Water...and that's it.<br /> <br /> How about this, what if I made the Carnivorus merit a part of Siren feeding: They can regain 1 point of Pneuma from eating an animal reminiscent of the Water they belong to, and there was a merit in Carnivorous's place that allowed a Siren to gain Pneuma without killing the animal? Let's call it <b>A Siren's Best Friend.</b><br /> <br /> Otherwise, I don't see how the Herbivorous merit can work, since...well, plants don't exactly seem to have souls? ALTHOUGH, it could be more the Siren drawing from the plant's connection to her Water, and her Water's connection to the Song that gives her Pneuma. In which case, I can see the Herbivorous merit working. :3 That and I think I would happily edit in the Furies section that &quot;They are considered to own both &quot;A Siren's Best Friend&quot; and &quot;Herbivorous&quot; Merits.&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983082#post983082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Barbed Quills</b><br /> <b>Mollusk's Beak</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these are insidious ideas. Which means I ABSOLUTELY LOVE THEM. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983082#post983082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bioluminescence</b><br /> <i>(Tropicana or Polaria)</i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Faint light glows from the Siren, which can be activated or dampened reflexively. When active she has a soft illumination no greater than a flashlight. This applies as a penalty of half Akashic Record to avoid being noticed, however the dexterous Siren may distract with her light to receive a bonus of half Akashic Record to her Defense for the first round of combat. For 1 Pneuma the Siren may inflict the Blinded Tilt on a single opponent for half Akashic Record turns.<br /> <i>Inspiration: anglerfish, many deep sea creatures</i></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> <br /> I admit, I've actually had this Alteration idea on my mind for the longest time. And yet I couldn't ever find any ideas on how to implement it. I hope you don't mind if I use this? Or any of these in Siren? ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983082#post983082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blowhole</b><br /> <i>(General or Polaria)</i><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">A secondary breathing orifice exists along the Siren's back. She gains the benefit of the 9-again rule when using her Stamina to manage breathing in Diluvian form. She may spend 1 Pneuma to expel a poisonous substance from her system, reducing the remaining Toxicity by Akashic Record. If removing a major pollutant like Biotoxin, the rejection of the substance also inflicts 1 Lethal damage.</span><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Inspiration: whales, porpoises and other cetaceans</span></i></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of this, mainly as if it acts almost like a second mouth for a Siren. Otherwise, I worry that it may sound abit like the Anuran Breath Alteration, although it aids on remaining on land/sea longer without need for breathing/staving off drowning.<br /> <b>Anuran Breath (Freshwater)</b><br /> Out of all the creatures that crawled out of the water, one of the first important things they had to do was learn how to breathe. For Sirens with this Alteration, they touch a piece of that evolution in their Diluvian Forms. Sirens in Diluvian Form without water to breathe in are considered to automatically gain their Stamina in successes on the roll to hold their breath, and when rolling their Stamina to gain further successes, it\u2019s considered as a rote action. If a Siren calls upon this Alteration while in Land form, she instead gains this benefit in regards to being underwater. On the Land Form, the Siren gains pseudo-gills on her neck.<br /> <i>Inspiration: Frog, Toad, Salamander, Lung Fish</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983082#post983082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spectral Vision</b><br /> <i>(Gardenia or Tropicana)</i><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Siren's eyes are enhanced to see across a wider spectrum. She ignores any penalty to perception that is -1. She can recognize unusual features like bloodstains, body fluids and other residues or trace evidence, unless they were rigorously cleaned. This grants a bonus of half Akashic Record to such a search or investigation. The Siren receives this bonus a number of times per scene up to her Wits.<br /> <i>Inspiration: Shrimp</i></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><br /> <br /> This sounds a little bit like the <b>Underwater Eyes </b>and <b>Killer Whale's Instinct </b>Alterations, which help perception rolls and Investigation rolls respectively. Although I now feel like I should edit Underwater Eyes abit so that it does a major version of what this Alteration does (negating penalties to Perception rolls underwater) and this Alteration should cover a Bonus to Perception rolls. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983082#post983082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Horrendous Consumption (Malformation)</b><br /> How will humanity (mainly Echidna's agents) survive the blighted aftermath of the apocalypse? This requires the means to find nutrition from the most dubious of sources. The Vodinaoi can eat their chosen food to avoid deprivation regardless of its state, suffering no drawbacks or damage from spoiled and rotten food. Because of the body odor produced from their altered digestive tract, the stench applies a -2 penalty against the Vodinaoi, such as for some Social rolls or when tracking them by scent. Once a scene, when feasting on the selected food the Vodinaoi can gain 1 Willpower for every Size category eaten. Sirens may chose to gain Pneuma instead.<br /> <br /> This Malformation can only be taken once. Select the category of food for the Vodinaoi to consume:</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983082#post983082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Carnivore's Diet:</i> you are sustained by meat and flesh, however fresh or processed, including other animal byproducts (like eggs and milk). If you attack a creature with the intent to eat it your successful attack gains an additional point of damage (only Bashing or Lethal). Treat any vegetation or fungal matter as a Toxicity 2 substance if ingested.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Herbivore's Diet:</i><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> you are sustained by the vegetation and fungal matter of nature. Instead of gaining Willpower you may instead gain temporary dice used for being attuned to your environment for the rest of the scene. This bonus can be divided amongst rolls pertaining to nature such as Science, Survival or Animal Ken. Treat any meat or animal byproduct as a Toxicity 2 substance when ingested.</span></span></span></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this Malformation as well. :3<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T22:47:34-07:00","id":983161,"title":"","content":"Being upfront, these ideas were inspired by elements from the partially complete Undine: the Emergence document. Not word for word, mind, but curious as for how that separately developed idea formed around the time Siren was first being implemented. Curiosity being that game's version of Alterations, and Sirens being one of the Splats on top of it!<br /> <br /> <b>Carnivorous and Herbivorous</b><br /> More of the idea with these is that the Penuma gain is less from digestion and more the symbolic nature of it. The Siren gains a bit of power from her place juxtaposed in the circle of life as befitting her Water and the food chain of the ecosystem. There's no true 'soul' to feed from, true, unless it can be ruled that the Pneuma is granted from the Water bridging to the Song like you say.<br /> <br /> If eating the animal is seen as harsh, you could switch it so that the base Pneuma is gained from play with the animal and the second from being killed and eaten. I'll note that in my original draft it didn't have to imply the Siren killed every animal to feed from personally. A Siren with the merit could easily gain the Pneuma from having lobster bisque out with friends one night. They may sit on the spectrum of being friends to all of nature but to eat is a very natural thing. The animals may have fun musicals in the Lion King but the lions still eat the antelope.<br /> <br /> <b>Blowhole</b><br /> The main effect of the Alteration is the poison/Toxicity removal system, although as not every Alteration is Pneuma dependent I didn't want it to be the only thing the Alteration did. I had forgotten Anuran Breath had the rote quality with it, kind of the main point if its the main 'breathe out of water' alteration. One possible fix is to reduce Anuran Breath to 8-agin and leave Blowhole at 9, the two then stacking to 8. Still, besides the use of 'sneezing' out of ones Blowhole it would be interesting if there was a different breath related effect that could be kept. As mammals cetaceans use their Blowholes to breathe and can stay submerged for quite the length of time...yet Sirens don't have that issue underwater and Anuran Breath does enough prolonging out in the air.<br /> <br /> <b>Spectral Vision</b><br /> What I found most interesting from the ability suggested was that some animals, many smaller sea critters, see in an enhanced vision spectrum beyond the visible spectrum we know and can thus see things that are there but aren't always noticed. Like having UV lights on all the time (err, might make your next motel visit all the more uncomfortable). It's true sensory Alterations can be tricky to not overlap, as there are already several senses derived from the different mechanics sea life use (and the Killer Whale's/Orca's Instinct boosting Investigation already).<br /> <br /> What could be useful is tying this Alteration to another newer subsystem in 2E, the Investigative routine (not the skill, the finding Clues and whatnot) much like the Investigative Prodigy merit but without the rating. Since such searches can use a variety of skills, it could be that the Siren's efforts always allow them to find at least 1 Clue even if failing (Dramatic Failure as usual) and their uncovered Clues gain an extra Element (free dice) as well.<br /> <br /> Another way of taking it would be the Aura Sight/Twilight viewing ability, although that's less important for Sirens and the Sense Conclusion already does that job.<br /> <br /> <b>Horrendous Consumption</b><br /> This was always going to be the harsher depiction of the dietary Merits above, fitting Echidna's theme that for every adaption she makes there's an evolutionary advantage lost.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> Feel free to include whatever you think is worthy for the system, I like tossing ideas out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:08:09-07:00","id":983171,"title":"","content":"I like the suggestion for their backstory. I will try to write their history soon and if you don't mind I will borrow some of your suggestions.<br /> Also, I am just picturing a siren throwing a elderly boardmember into the ocean in a attempt to drown him and much to her horror, he starts breathing underwater<br /> Finally, here is a story hook for the Corporation <br /> A Grand Party: You have recently found out that a new luxury cruise liner is arriving in Honolulu. Normally you would not care, but then one of your contacts tells you something that catches your interest. It turns out Edward Garcia, one of Poseidon's bigwigs is celebrating his 78th birthday on the cruise liner. You decide to take advantage of this opportunity to cripple Poseidon by killing Edward. But it does not cross your mind that this opportunity seems too easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:17:29-07:00","id":983175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983161#post983161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being upfront, these ideas were inspired by elements from the partially complete Undine: the Emergence document. Not word for word, mind, but curious as for how that separately developed idea formed around the time Siren was first being implemented. Curiosity being that game's version of Alterations, and Sirens being one of the Splats on top of it!</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. :3 Well, that's fine too. There's few splats that are not land based.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983161#post983161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Carnivorous and Herbivorous</b><br /> More of the idea with these is that the Penuma gain is less from digestion and more the symbolic nature of it. The Siren gains a bit of power from her place juxtaposed in the circle of life as befitting her Water and the food chain of the ecosystem. There's no true 'soul' to feed from, true, unless it can be ruled that the Pneuma is granted from the Water bridging to the Song like you say.<br /> <br /> If eating the animal is seen as harsh, you could switch it so that the base Pneuma is gained from play with the animal and the second from being killed and eaten. I'll note that in my original draft it didn't have to imply the Siren killed every animal to feed from personally. A Siren with the merit could easily gain the Pneuma from having lobster bisque out with friends one night. They may sit on the spectrum of being friends to all of nature but to eat is a very natural thing. The animals may have fun musicals in the Lion King but the lions still eat the antelope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. And no, I don't mean for it to be seen as harsh. I mean, I'm mostly having ideas of getting Theron familiars or the like for Sirens, hence why I brought up the idea in the first place. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983161#post983161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blowhole</b><br /> The main effect of the Alteration is the poison/Toxicity removal system, although as not every Alteration is Pneuma dependent I didn't want it to be the only thing the Alteration did. I had forgotten Anuran Breath had the rote quality with it, kind of the main point if its the main 'breathe out of water' alteration. One possible fix is to reduce Anuran Breath to 8-agin and leave Blowhole at 9, the two then stacking to 8. Still, besides the use of 'sneezing' out of ones Blowhole it would be interesting if there was a different breath related effect that could be kept. As mammals cetaceans use their Blowholes to breathe and can stay submerged for quite the length of time...yet Sirens don't have that issue underwater and Anuran Breath does enough prolonging out in the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties, will do. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983161#post983161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spectral Vision</b><br /> What I found most interesting from the ability suggested was that some animals, many smaller sea critters, see in an enhanced vision spectrum beyond the visible spectrum we know and can thus see things that are there but aren't always noticed. Like having UV lights on all the time (err, might make your next motel visit all the more uncomfortable). It's true sensory Alterations can be tricky to not overlap, as there are already several senses derived from the different mechanics sea life use (and the Killer Whale's/Orca's Instinct boosting Investigation already).<br /> <br /> What could be useful is tying this Alteration to another newer subsystem in 2E, the Investigative routine (not the skill, the finding Clues and whatnot) much like the Investigative Prodigy merit but without the rating. Since such searches can use a variety of skills, it could be that the Siren's efforts always allow them to find at least 1 Clue even if failing (Dramatic Failure as usual) and their uncovered Clues gain an extra Element (free dice) as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see...if I may ask, what book covers that? I'm lacking the newest corebook for the CoD and working mostly from the GMC book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983161#post983161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Horrendous Consumption</b><br /> This was always going to be the harsher depiction of the dietary Merits above, fitting Echidna's theme that for every adaption she makes there's an evolutionary advantage lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how you worded that. For the most part, the reason I set Malformations to have disadvantages was because that seemed like the theme for the &quot;Dark side&quot; powers. Power at a price and all that. But just how you said that makes me think for once of how it'd be explained in game. Echidna is trying to make the perfect race. A perfect race would have no need to evolve anymore, which is what you said in how evolutionary advantages being lost. Thanks for inspiring that. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983161#post983161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel free to include whatever you think is worthy for the system, I like tossing ideas out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've added alot of what you posted in already. :3<br /> <br /> If it's fine to bring up an idea for Siren, I've been thinking on something. As it stands, I wanted to implement some stuff about the connection of Sirens between themselves and the Song. So far, the echoes of these ideas have resulted in the idea of the Song of the School and Trace (which was more of an expansion of the Psychometry Merit)...and yet these don't feel like they have enough of a connection to Sirens or the Song. Right now, I'm sort of thinking of melding the Song of the School and Trace to being automatic abilities Sirens have access to, making something new that Sirens can make use of out of the old mechanics.<br /> <br /> The start of my ideas is that they would still have Trace like abilities, seeing into the past and whatnot, but with Verses the Siren may affect the past as if she used the verse there at that time. Of course, the idea of &quot;Overtracing&quot; still exists, and some events are nearly impossible to mess with. This is fitting in more of the original symbology of how Sirens could somehow deal with Time. An in game perspective is that the Song has messed with Time that it's managed to be heard in the past, before the Deluge has happened.<br /> <br /> I also imagine Sirens being able to use the echoes of the Song within them, aka their Akashic Record, to be able to pinpoint other Sirens or beings with souls. An automatic ability Sirens would have is the ability to &quot;send&quot; an echo back, sort of like &quot;I heard your message&quot; and stuff. Perhaps the Currents have made special versions of this &quot;Call&quot; that allows them to speak to each other like how the US used the Navajo Native American Language for secret messages in WW2. This could even be wrapped up as different dialects of the Bel Canto Language. :3<br /> <br /> So far, these are just ideas, but what do you guys think of them? The basic ideas I have seem to have a theme of post-cognition, recording, replaying and editing so far...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:20:20-07:00","id":983178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983171#post983171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the suggestion for their backstory. I will try to write their history soon and if you don't mind I will borrow some of your suggestions.<br /> Also, I am just picturing a siren throwing a elderly boardmember into the ocean in a attempt to drown him and much to her horror, he starts breathing underwater<br /> Finally, here is a story hook for the Corporation<br /> A Grand Party: You have recently found out that a new luxury cruise liner is arriving in Honolulu. Normally you would not care, but then one of your contacts tells you something that catches your interest. It turns out Edward Garcia, one of Poseidon's bigwigs is celebrating his 78th birthday on the cruise liner. You decide to take advantage of this opportunity to cripple Poseidon by killing Edward. But it does not cross your mind that this opportunity seems too easy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alrighties, feel free to take your time. :3 Pardon the double post. &gt;w&gt;&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:26:17-07:00","id":983184,"title":"","content":"What do you think of the storyhook? Also, what would Echnida herself think of the group. Would she view them as temporary expendable servants or as secondary servants she likes but not as much as her sirens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:47:27-07:00","id":983189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983184#post983184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of the storyhook? Also, what would Echnida herself think of the group. Would she view them as temporary expendable servants or as secondary servants she likes but not as much as her sirens?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's well enough. I don't think Sirens would have much of an incentive to kill him unless if they knew exactly what he was advocating in his company, or at least knew what his company was into. And even then, I think that the Celestial Currents would at their best, try to kill him and replace him with someone who's more...easily swayed towards ending the inhumane experiments. The Abyssals on the other hand would either make the most of the knowledge, kill him without trying to make things better or place someone more favored towards him and subsume the company to themselves. The first is Cocytus, Acheron and Phlegethon, the second is Styx and the third is Lethe and Flensers. :3<br /> <br /> As for Echidna herself, I imagine that would depend on her level of involvement in the company. She does have her own experiments to pull and she leaves interaction with the prediluvian world to her Sirens. If the company doesn't do well, then she wouldn't exactly care and see them as only good to continue their experiments...but as <i>her </i>test subjects. If the company does well enough and helps expand her &quot;research&quot;, then she'll see them as a potential asset to be looked into and protected. Regardless, if they fail then she has her plans to try and take as many personnel into the Celestial Ocean and straight to her, she's always wanting more humans to make into her perfect race and her children, the Vodianoi.<br /> <br /> I would say though, as both a word of god on Siren and because I love speculating this sort of stuff, that Echidna loves all of humanity and Sirens to the point where she's basically blind to how much harm her eugenics studies does to the people she kidnaps. She believes that she knows what's best for Humanity, and everything she does is for their own good. She has a looser leash for Sirens, since she views them as more capable of surviving without her help, but she still wishes for each and every one of them to join her cause. For hers is the one that survived the Deluge itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:55:01-07:00","id":983190,"title":"","content":"Alright. Also the storyhook is when the Sirens know about the companies motives. Also, would it make sense if my company hired a flenser? My basic idea is Poseidon got tired of failed hunts and decided to hire one. His name is Ahab and he only agreed to help out due to the fact they offered to pay him in siren flesh that came from failed experiments. Also, how would the celestial currents view Poseidon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T00:20:42-07:00","id":983198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983190#post983190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. Also the storyhook is when the Sirens know about the companies motives. Also, would it make sense if my company hired a flenser? My basic idea is Poseidon got tired of failed hunts and decided to hire one. His name is Ahab and he only agreed to help out due to the fact they offered to pay him in siren flesh that came from failed experiments. Also, how would the celestial currents view Poseidon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that doesn't feel in character for a Company who's butting heads with the Flensers. That and Flensers usually attempt to keep their members with themselves or kill them for spare parts (if they have Cybernetics). Although that said, I can imagine one reason a Flenser Hunter would join the company is to act as a mole, feeding back information to their higher ups and acting like they want to get out of the Flensers. Basically being a double agent and all.<br /> <br /> As for the Celestial Currents, I imagine that they'd view Poseidon International almost like they view the Flensers. Except they'd be more willing to deal with Poseidon because they lack the Cybernetics and Gene Mods Flensers make use of. Depending on the Siren, they could view them as worse or more sympathetic as the flensers, as they do want to make humanity better...but at the cost of Siren lives. I imagine the most concrete view I can give is that the Current of Buoyancy would be waiting for the moment they're finally called in to do the dirty work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:27:22-07:00","id":983422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983198#post983198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that doesn't feel in character for a Company who's butting heads with the Flensers. That and Flensers usually attempt to keep their members with themselves or kill them for spare parts (if they have Cybernetics). Although that said, I can imagine one reason a Flenser Hunter would join the company is to act as a mole, feeding back information to their higher ups and acting like they want to get out of the Flensers. Basically being a double agent and all.<br /> <br /> As for the Celestial Currents, I imagine that they'd view Poseidon International almost like they view the Flensers. Except they'd be more willing to deal with Poseidon because they lack the Cybernetics and Gene Mods Flensers make use of. Depending on the Siren, they could view them as worse or more sympathetic as the flensers, as they do want to make humanity better...but at the cost of Siren lives. I imagine the most concrete view I can give is that the Current of Buoyancy would be waiting for the moment they're finally called in to do the dirty work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. I will cut the flenser idea then. Also, is it okay if the history of the company is explained through a employee initiation video? I also came up with another storyhook that involves stopping the construction of a new research vessel. Finally,Is it bad that i i could picture a statue of Echnida in the middle of the boardroom and the board bowing before it after each meeting if I go with the whole board serves her idea? Also, when you write this faction down in the rulebook can you credit me for creating it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-07-2016, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:50:20-07:00","id":983467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983422#post983422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense. I will cut the flenser idea then. Also, is it okay if the history of the company is explained through a employee initiation video? I also came up with another storyhook that involves stopping the construction of a new research vessel. Finally,Is it bad that i i could picture a statue of Echnida in the middle of the boardroom and the board bowing before it after each meeting if I go with the whole board serves her idea? Also, when you write this faction down in the rulebook can you credit me for creating it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you mean writing through a style of Employee initiation video, then I'm all for it. You might not want to include details of their Siren hunting stuff in it except in subtle ways or just saying &quot;we have more research, but only higher personnel are allowed and gaining access to this information will result in your termination.&quot; And yes, the &quot;termination&quot; is meant to be ambiguous on whether they end the employee who knows too much or if the company simply fires them. :3<br /> <br /> I would recommend using the symbol of the Current of Oceanus, the Ourobouros (the Snake eating it's own tail). Let's say the symbolism of eternity and evolution goes great with the She-Viper. :3 And of course I will credit you for this. ^^<br /> <br /> And also, I have a little general update myself. I've made the basic outline I have for Honolulu. I must note that it's EXTREMELY basic in terms of what's present already, pretty much the essentials that will come in the future. But otherwise, it's a start at the least.<br /> <br /> <b>Honolulu, City of the Drowned: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BiTTr3TcJju90pSGTjuQx3Jli3dl3vibURAtVsWYcEg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:27:54-07:00","id":983496,"title":"","content":"My idea is that they get rid of incompetent employees by giving them to Oceanus sirens. Also, is it okay if the creator of the Siren project used to be a German scientist during WW2? Is it bad to say Oceanus sirens often have a habit of following Poseidon research boats. Finally, Is it okay that I named them after the Greek god of oceans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-07-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:47:43-07:00","id":983543,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post but another question popped into my head. Would it be okay if Poseidon had a henchman like Jaws from the James Bond films?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:57:48-07:00","id":983550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983496#post983496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What section would Poseidon be under. Also, my idea is that they get rid of incompetent employees by giving them to Oceanus sirens. Also, is it okay if the creator of the Siren project used to be a German scientist during WW2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Poseidon would be underneath Chapter 3, after the Statuses of the Currents (Abyssal and Celestial) and Flensers and with the descriptions of the rest of the Independent Hunters (I'm imagining to make at least two other sets of hunters available in Honolulu). <br /> <br /> I would say that that's fine. If I may give a suggestion, what if the German Scientist was already echidna influenced or an Echidnal Siren? It seems fitting for Echidna of all people to be interested in humans trying to make a &quot;master race&quot;. <br /> <br /> I hope it's also not minded for me to note, but I have at least one bit of criteria for Poseidon International (and this goes for the other Independent Hunters), the maximum amount of space they can have is up to a single page within a Google Doc at Times New Roman 12 point font. This is only so that descriptions aren't too long and the like, as well to keep them short and sweet. I hope that's fine. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:01:12-07:00","id":983551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983543#post983543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the double post but another question popped into my head. Would it be okay if Poseidon had a henchman like Jaws from the James Bond films?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say only do what seems reasonable for hunters to have. In other words, yes. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:09:00-07:00","id":983555,"title":"","content":"Alright thanks. Also, if Poseidon only takes up a single page can you include the facts I told here, but condensed? I am also wondering if their base in Honolulu can be a corporate skyscraper with a oriental theme?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-07-2016, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:12:35-07:00","id":983583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983555#post983555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright thanks. Also, if Poseidon only takes up a single page can you include the facts I told here, but condensed? I am also wondering if their base in Honolulu can be a corporate skyscraper with a oriental theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, just a summary of the company acts, it's history and what they're doing in Honolulu (for both research reasons and number of sirens) is enough. It can be a corporate building, but might I suggest at the very least that it's not &quot;the tallest building around&quot;? Both because it would be a huge tactical disadvantage if the Flensers (or Sirens for that matter) really did decide to strike, and that lower size means it's easier to defend. Not to mention I sorta can't see why they'd make a skyscraper for a corporate building in a different country than where they're based (Poseidon being based in Scandanavia as opposed to Hawaii which is almost literally on the other side of the world). I also don't see a justification why they'd make use of an oriental motif unless they were oriental based or the area they were in is oriental based. Ack, I'm sorry if I'm being control freaky or giving differing opinions or the like. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:20:24-07:00","id":983586,"title":"","content":"My justification for the building is that it is the headquarters for the American Branch. I will get rid of the skyscraper and replace it with a modest five story office building with no theme at all. Also. I can make the history of the company and make a list of the board of directors if you want. Also I decided to go with the Echnida servant route. Also, would it be safe to assume that Echinda's sirens would be all over the building?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-07-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:31:50-07:00","id":983591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983586#post983586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My justification for the building is that it is the headquarters for the American Branch. I will get rid of the skyscraper and replace it with a modest five story office building with no theme at all. Also. I can make the history of the company and make a list of the board of directors if you want. Also I decided to go with the Echnida servant route. Also, would it be safe to assume that Echinda's sirens would be all over the building?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say we need examples of at least one Echidnal and one pure human in the board of directors. Otherwise, you're free to write as much as you wish. I can write up the summary if you wish. :3<br /> <br /> As for Echidnal Sirens in the building, I would say that if they are present, they would be within the Poseidon International within the Celestial Ocean. They would've fortified it to be a Safe Place and Grotto at rating 5, and in it are housed the Vodianoi dispatched with them to serve as the &quot;big guns&quot; should the human hunters fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:01:06-07:00","id":983602,"title":"","content":"Do you want me to post the basic backbone of the two? You know things like name, age, background and stuff like that? Also, the Oceanus are using the submerged ruins of the Hawaiian building as a base, sounds good to me<br /> Finally, the history will come out tonight or tommorow. I intend for them to start as an oceanographer's club and evolve into the morally ambiguous Corp we know today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-07-2016, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:43:46-07:00","id":983639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983602#post983602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you want me to post the basic backbone of the two? You know things like name, age, background and stuff like that? Also, the Oceanus are using the submerged ruins of the Hawaiian building as a base, sounds good to me<br /> Finally, the history will come out tonight or tommorow. I intend for them to start as an oceanographer's club and evolve into the morally ambiguous Corp we know today.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright. Take as much time as you need for writing them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:38:06-07:00","id":983668,"title":"","content":"Here are the two board members.<br /> <br /> Name: Rolf Tevit<br /> Age: 51<br /> Race: Human<br /> Appearance: <a href=\"http://www.learnspanishtoday.com/img/businessman.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.learnspanishtoday.com/img/businessman.jpg</a>. Basically this except he has scales on his arms due to Echidna's so-called blessing.<br /> Brief Background: Rolf Tevit is a member of Poseidon's mysterious Board Of Directors and is in charge of the Marketing Department. In the few public he has made, he was described as a seemingly kind, generous individual who had a good sense of humor. The only thing that seemed odd about him is the fact he never rolled up his sleeves, even when washing his hands. What the public does not know is that underneath his sleeves are sharp,green scales. As a member of the Board, he is in the know about the goals of Poseidon and their master, Echidna. Beyond the facade of feigned kindness is a cold, ruthless man who will kill anyone who stands in the way of his goals or the goals of his beloved company.<br /> <br /> Name: Arya Mitter<br /> Age: Seems to be in her early to late 30s.<br /> Race: Siren of the Oceanus Current.<br /> Appearance: <a href=\"https://thumb7.shutterstock.com/display_pic_with_logo/2805838/302535671/stock-photo-young-businesswoman-smiling-302535671.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://thumb7.shutterstock.com/disp...-302535671.jpg</a>. Picture this but with sharp teeth.<br /> Deluvian Form: <a href=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/82TjznfOmZY/maxresdefault.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.ytimg.com/vi/82TjznfOmZY/maxresdefault.jpg</a><br /> Brief Background: This mysterious woman is part of Poseidon's Board Of Directors, yet her name does not show up on any official list. She recently replaced Donagon Carlyle, who was slain by Sirens in Honolulu. The distinction Donagon and Arya have that sets them apart from the rest of the Board is the fact they are sirens. In fact, Donogan and Arya are the Oceanus' and by extension Echidna's emissaries to Poseidon. This cold, calculating siren enjoys her new position on the top of the corporate food-chain and uses her knew found powers of commanding both Poseidon security forces and scientists with glee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:32:45-07:00","id":983726,"title":"","content":"Finally the event you have been waiting for, the history of Poseidon International! &quot; Cue fanfare.&quot;<br /> &quot;Note, the reason this history is in first-person is because this history is being told from the point-of view of a Employee Instruction tape&quot;.<br /> Hello new employee, my name is Dr. Ernst Egarsson, CEO and current chairman of Poseidon Labs International. Let me be the first one to welcome you to your new job in Poseidon and I, along with the rest of the board hope you have a long, happy career with us. The purpose of this tape is to explain the history of our proud corporation. This tape will only consume a little amount of time and when this tape is over you may start your workday.<br /> <br /> Our proud corporation had it's start in 1885 with a more humble origin.It all started with a club under the name &quot; The Oceanography Enthusiasts Club&quot; which was founded by amateur Norwegian oceanographer Roy Petterson. This club was founded by Roy for the purpose of meeting and discussing developments in the world of oceanography with fellow enthusiasts. Even though most clubs back then only admitted the social elite Roy's welcomed in anyone who had in interest in the Ocean or Oceanography. Within 5 years of finding this marvelous club, membership soared from 5 to 50 members and was recognized as a scientific organization by the Swedish government.<br /> <br /> Tragically, Roy died in 1895 while on a expedition with fellow oceanographer, Sir Duncan Smith. The official cause of death was apparently a shipwreck which killed all hands on-board. Unfortunately, Roy's death destabilized the club and half of it's members left upon hearing this bad news. The club's new leader, Sven Lagersson, was extremely unpopular with the club due to his heavy drinking and utter disregard for club rules. In 1900, the club formerly dissolved after Sven died in a bar fight. The final meeting was held on New Year's Eve 1899, what the good men of the club did not know was that among the visitors to the club's final meeting was a youth who would one day form the Modern-day Poseidon Corporation. His name was Daniel Herre.<br /> <br /> Good old Daniel Herre, father of our corporation, was avid an visitor to the club and was upset about it's dissolution. Daniel then started his own study of the ocean with the help of Roy's personal diary, which was published due to a specification in his will that wished for that to happen after he died. As he read through Roy's diary, Daniel became aware of how beneficial the sea could be for humanity. So with a loan from his rich cousin, Daniel went out and started Poseidon's Bounty, the grandfather of our corporation. Unfortunately, technology in the 1900s was not up to snuff with our technology so Poseidon's Bounty mostly sold fish. In 1920, Daniel made a discovery that changed the face of his company. He was supervising the catching of a new bounty of fish when he saw that the net accidentally caught some lose seaweed. Taking this seaweed home with him, he absent-mindidly placed it in a potted plant. When he woke up the next morning, he found that the seaweed had rotted and as a result, it made a great fertilizer for the plant. This was the birth of our first product &quot; Neptune's Fertilizer&quot; one of the first fertilizers made of seaweed.<br /> <br /> Wanting to repeat his success with the seaweed. Daniel spent the next 15 years scouring the ocean looking to make potentially useful products. The products varied from cleaning powder made from crushed-up sea shells all the way to sandpaper made of shark-skin. In 1940, The Nazi's invaded Norway and Daniel was forced to take his company's fortune and flee to America, bankrupting Poseidon's Bounty in the process. After the war, Daniel met and befriended Dr. Emil Grund, a former German scientist who was pardoned from being tried in the Nuremberg Trials due to the fact his experiments never killed anyone. The two realized that they both shared an interest in the ocean and went into business together forming the modern-day Poseidon Labs International.<br /> <br /> During our 61 years in business, we at Poseidon labs have made many discovery's from the ocean which benefited mankind. Of course we still sell &quot; Neptune's Fertilizer&quot; and some of the other products Poseidon's Bounty sold. But, are scientists are making new discovery's everyday and have made wonderful products which have definitely helped mankind. We have two experiments for which you are qualified for. &quot;Project Graft&quot;, the study of sea sponges and their resistance to cancer and &quot;Project Shaker&quot;, an attempt to find a process that makes Desalination of water possible. Of course we have higher-level experiments but they are for high-level staff and are completely restricted for new employees. And, if i hear about you or any other new employee trying to get into the project or even accessing files about it, i will personally make sure that you are terminated and that you will never work in this business again. I thank you for choosing a career with Poseidon International, now good luck and remember our slogan.&quot; The best bounty is Neptune's Bounty.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-08-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"J