So maybe he can cause the scales to cover other parts of the body and protect vital areas. Also, you don't have to post the NPCS and board-member appearances in the book, i just used them as a visual-aid on what the NPCS look like. Also, is it okay if I made Arya delight in bossing around the employees under her jurisdiction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-08-2016, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T15:38:39-07:00","id":984093,"title":"","content":"Another think i would like to add. If you can a picture description to the independent hunters page i would like it to be this.<br /> It shows a siren swimming franctlicaly away from a motor boat which is being piloted by two men in suits with a third man in black aiming a tranquilizer gun at the siren.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:28:05-07:00","id":984108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984093#post984093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another think i would like to add. If you can a picture description to the independent hunters page i would like it to be this.<br /> It shows a siren swimming franctlicaly away from a motor boat which is being piloted by two men in suits with a third man in black aiming a tranquilizer gun at the siren.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties, got both suggestions down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:29:52-07:00","id":984109,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Also, Rolf would probably be in Hawaii to promote a new project. This project is a Sea World like place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T17:25:13-07:00","id":984132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=983175#post983175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see...if I may ask, what book covers that? I'm lacking the newest corebook for the CoD and working mostly from the GMC book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chronicles of Darkness (the second edition) has a few new systems alongside Social Maneuvering that had been introduced in GMC. In fact, the second half of the book is the GMC again with a few layout tweaks.<br /> <br /> The main two for consideration are the Investigative and Chase rules. These are semi-optional for Storyteller preference but there are Merits that work with these new systems, Social Maneuvering and Investigative and Chase. They roughly equate to Social, Mental and Physical categories but their primary use is to given more storytelling tools to the players.<br /> <br /> <b>Investigation</b><br /> For the Investigative system (which is just titled Investigation, I use the other word for distinction from the skill) it can be a slow burn type of system, used for when there is a case or mystery of some kind that the players are trying to solve can span most of a chronicle. It's best for the Storyteller to not over plan a mystery to leave room for player input. Based on the group's intent a set threshold of Clues are required to complete the investigation.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo uncover a Clue, the player specifies a specific dice pool to discover the clue. These can be of different Attributes, Skills, Merits or special abilities, although each time the same skill is used it confers a cumulative penalty. Each Clue has a number of Elements, disposable die bonuses that can be used on other actions related to the investigation. At default a Clue has 1 Element and gains more from certain criteria:<ul><li>An Exceptional Success when uncovering the Clue</li> <li>The player had a Specialty pertaining to the Clue</li> <li>The player had 4+ dots in the Skill uncovering the Clue</li> <li>Merits that react with Clues</li> </ul>Clues can also get tagged, which impacts how their Elements are used. Even with the Elements have been used the Clue remains for tracking progress of the investigative effort. To use Elements a character draws from a single Clue, or from a number of Clues equal to their Investigation skill if they have it. The most common end goal, to uncover the truth, is automatic if the players have found the requisite number of Clues and have an equal number of Elements.<br /> <br /> <br /> Given that, I may rephrase <b>Spectral Vision</b> like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Siren has enhanced vision for both infrared and ultraviolet spectrums, being able to see residues and evidence not visible to the naked eye. Their failures to uncover Clues never get the Incomplete tag, and their successfully uncovered Clues gain an additional element. </div> </div> </div>However, the Alteration should still have another more commonly used benefit. I like the idea of being able to see more details although a proper mechanic is lacking, since we already had requisite skill boost Alterations.<br /> <br /> <b>Chase</b><br /> Chases refer to scenes where the characters quickly need to reach a goal, such a pursuing an opponent, although it can also represent 'chasing' after someone's slippery logic in a social setting.<br /> <br /> At the start, each side is set with a target number they need to accomplish their goal, with various factors like time and other stat differences. The target number indicates how many <i>successful actions</i> they need to reach their goal, not the number of successes resulting from the roll. What rolls are needed are set by whoever has the Edge.<br /> <br /> The Edge indicates which side has the most advantage. The side with the advantage indicates what obstacle they present and thus what dice roll is needed. Success and failure mark off their target numbers, but regardless of results each side needs to estimate their result. If you rolled the number of successes you guessed you can claim the Edge. Using a different dice pool then that set by the Edge confers a cumulative penalty.<br /> <br /> Since there's already several merits pertaining to the Edge, all tied to physical implementation, it would likely be unessecary to bring that into Alterations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like how you worded that. For the most part, the reason I set Malformations to have disadvantages was because that seemed like the theme for the &quot;Dark side&quot; powers. Power at a price and all that. But just how you said that makes me think for once of how it'd be explained in game. Echidna is trying to make the perfect race. A perfect race would have no need to evolve anymore, which is what you said in how evolutionary advantages being lost. Thanks for inspiring that. :3 </div> </div> </div>Consider that a lucky choice of terminology.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it's fine to bring up an idea for Siren, I've been thinking on something. As it stands, I wanted to implement some stuff about the connection of Sirens between themselves and the Song. So far, the echoes of these ideas have resulted in the idea of the Song of the School and Trace (which was more of an expansion of the Psychometry Merit)...and yet these don't feel like they have enough of a connection to Sirens or the Song. Right now, I'm sort of thinking of melding the Song of the School and Trace to being automatic abilities Sirens have access to, making something new that Sirens can make use of out of the old mechanics.<br /> <br /> The start of my ideas is that they would still have Trace like abilities, seeing into the past and whatnot, but with Verses the Siren may affect the past as if she used the verse there at that time. Of course, the idea of &quot;Overtracing&quot; still exists, and some events are nearly impossible to mess with. This is fitting in more of the original symbology of how Sirens could somehow deal with Time. An in game perspective is that the Song has messed with Time that it's managed to be heard in the past, before the Deluge has happened.<br /> <br /> I also imagine Sirens being able to use the echoes of the Song within them, aka their Akashic Record, to be able to pinpoint other Sirens or beings with souls. An automatic ability Sirens would have is the ability to &quot;send&quot; an echo back, sort of like &quot;I heard your message&quot; and stuff. Perhaps the Currents have made special versions of this &quot;Call&quot; that allows them to speak to each other like how the US used the Navajo Native American Language for secret messages in WW2. This could even be wrapped up as different dialects of the Bel Canto Language. :3<br /> <br /> So far, these are just ideas, but what do you guys think of them? The basic ideas I have seem to have a theme of post-cognition, recording, replaying and editing so far... </div> </div> </div>Just making sure, if the Sirens can work their Verses into the events they Trace, they aren't actually changing the past? Or we introduce <i>Time Hollow</i> and <i>Ghost Trick</i> levels of shenanigans to the sense of continuity. Unless the Sirens are merely able to 'see' how things could have gone differently by working their influences. And for the particularly insidious, they could rework and event (Overtrace it so much, if you will) that it obscures the true reality of the event if others try to Trace it.<br /> <br /> The communicative aspect sounds like the Siren could leave her commentary on the event for other Sirens to uncover when they Trace.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I thought that the <i>Deluge</i> Opus handled Trace enhancement with its figurative implementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T22:00:15-07:00","id":984245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984132#post984132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicles of Darkness (the second edition) has a few new systems alongside Social Maneuvering that had been introduced in GMC. In fact, the second half of the book is the GMC again with a few layout tweaks.<br /> <br /> The main two for consideration are the Investigative and Chase rules. These are semi-optional for Storyteller preference but there are Merits that work with these new systems, Social Maneuvering and Investigative and Chase. They roughly equate to Social, Mental and Physical categories but their primary use is to given more storytelling tools to the players.<br /> <br /> <b>Investigation</b><br /> *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. ^^ I must admit, I was thinking of using a modified version of those rules for Trace, but I don't think they may exactly fit when I think of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984132#post984132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that, I may rephrase <b>Spectral Vision</b> like this:<br /> <br /> However, the Alteration should still have another more commonly used benefit. I like the idea of being able to see more details although a proper mechanic is lacking, since we already had requisite skill boost Alterations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984132#post984132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chase</b><br /> Chases refer to scenes where the characters quickly need to reach a goal, such a pursuing an opponent, although it can also represent 'chasing' after someone's slippery logic in a social setting.<br /> <br /> At the start, each side is set with a target number they need to accomplish their goal, with various factors like time and other stat differences. The target number indicates how many <i>successful actions</i> they need to reach their goal, not the number of successes resulting from the roll. What rolls are needed are set by whoever has the Edge.<br /> <br /> The Edge indicates which side has the most advantage. The side with the advantage indicates what obstacle they present and thus what dice roll is needed. Success and failure mark off their target numbers, but regardless of results each side needs to estimate their result. If you rolled the number of successes you guessed you can claim the Edge. Using a different dice pool then that set by the Edge confers a cumulative penalty.<br /> <br /> Since there's already several merits pertaining to the Edge, all tied to physical implementation, it would likely be unessecary to bring that into Alterations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Alrighties then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984132#post984132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just making sure, if the Sirens can work their Verses into the events they Trace, they aren't actually changing the past? Or we introduce <i>Time Hollow</i> and <i>Ghost Trick</i> levels of shenanigans to the sense of continuity. Unless the Sirens are merely able to 'see' how things could have gone differently by working their influences. And for the particularly insidious, they could rework and event (Overtrace it so much, if you will) that it obscures the true reality of the event if others try to Trace it.<br /> <br /> The communicative aspect sounds like the Siren could leave her commentary on the event for other Sirens to uncover when they Trace.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I thought that the <i>Deluge</i> Opus handled Trace enhancement with its figurative implementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that they are changing the past. Otherwise, how else would the Song have been able to pull back from a bad end future to make Sirens? :3<br /> <br /> Non-jokingly, I would say that Sirens may include their Verses into a Trace and like you said, there would be those insidious enough to overtrace reality so that others couldn't uncover it. I could see this as something the Current of Wisdom would use to cover up &quot;That Which Should Not Be&quot; as well as how Acheron has survived to this day (by covering their steps to the point nobody can follow them). <br /> <br /> Anyways, here's my ideas so far on revamping Trace. It has five factors:<b> Time, Range, Clarity, Audience and Verse.</b> When a Siren invokes Trace, they must spend 1 Pneuma and a point of Willpower (if they put any suxx into Verse, it becomes a point of permanent Willpower) and roll Akashic Record + Resolve to see how many suxx they get, then they choose how many suxx they spend on each of the mechanics. The higher suxx, the higher strength the Siren may put into a mechanic. If the Siren uses Verse, then she must pay the Verses cost in the subsequent turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Time </b>allows a Siren to see forwards and backwards through time, seeing past or probable future events. The more suxx put into Time, the farther forwards or backwards she may see. Seeing forwards shows the most likely occurrance, but it's easily disrupted by things such as controlling fate or simple dumb luck. Since Time doesn't take into account for this, Sirens tend to see looking forwards with Trace as unreliable at best.<br /> <br /> <b>Range</b> allows a Siren to choose how far her Trace can pull, allowing her to see elsewhere and even exert force with more suxx invested. She may even speak telepathically to people with this. With no suxx, the Trace can only affect the Siren herself, and with one suxx, she may use the Trace on things within her line of sight. With more suxx invested to this, the Siren may communicate to those at a greater distance. With investment to Time as well, a Siren can look into the past or future of places or people far away from her.<br /> <br /> <b>Clarity</b> allows the Trace to have greater definition when Tracing things. She may read into the composition of objects and see physical and mental traits of people. With investment to Time, the Siren may get her defined answers instead of seeing things through a set timeframe. With Investment to Range, the Siren may speak more than a simple phrase and add more words to her telepathic messages.<br /> <br /> <b>Audience</b> allows the Trace to affect a group of people outside of the siren, and by itself it allows a Siren to try to &quot;listen&quot; into other active traces. With more suxx put into this, the group of people can grow very large. With investment to Time, the Siren shares a Time Trace's Vision with the Audience. With investment to Range, the Siren may hold a group conversation with people. With Investment to Clarity, a Siren may pre-record a message that she wants any specific audience members to hear and leaving others out.<br /> <br /> <b>Verse </b>is simply what allows a Siren to wield a Verse during her Tracing. The amount of Suxx put into this equals the dot level of the Conclusion the Siren may use through the Trace. With Investment to Time, a Siren may use Verses in the past. With Investment to Range, a Siren may use Verses at the places she sees, as if she were actually there (and thus negating the Amour modifier normally required to affect places out of sensory vision). Clarity and Audience have no effect with this. <br /> <br /> There's also the idea of Sirens being able to Trace other Sirens, but due to Song's nature (and thus a Siren's as well) of achronality, if the Siren doesn't wish to be traced, she may reflexively roll Akashic Record + Composure to contest the use of the trace. The Resisting Siren's suxx is subtracted from the Tracing Sirens suxx that they may spend, and if the Resisting Siren's suxx is higher, then she completely blocks the Trace from occurring.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T22:30:38-07:00","id":984255,"title":"","content":"Is the sea world like place okay for a plot hook? If it is, the basic plot is having you try to stop construction of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-09-2016, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T01:27:46-07:00","id":984311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984255#post984255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the sea world like place okay for a plot hook? If it is, the basic plot is having you try to stop construction of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ofc, this is a game about Sirens so there should be plot hooks based in the sea. Just feel free to shoot up any plot hooks you have in mind and I'll add in whichever ones seem good for the setting. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T06:32:32-07:00","id":984370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984311#post984311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ofc, this is a game about Sirens so there should be plot hooks based in the sea. Just feel free to shoot up any plot hooks you have in mind and I'll add in whichever ones seem good for the setting. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Would Sirens interfere in the building of a aquatic theam park like Sea World?<br /> Also here is two more<br /> There is rumors of a new Poseidon research vessel being built. The boat is apparently the size of a oil tanker and can hold up to five labs. You know if this boat every makes to the ocean it will be a nightmare. So you and the rest of your shoal decide to destroy this boat before it could ever be built.<br /> You find yourself captured by Poseidon and decide to plot an escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-09-2016, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:06:52-07:00","id":984379,"title":"","content":"In a future post I'll mark down mechanics of present Investigative or Chase merits to see if there's any new ideas to be had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984245#post984245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, here's my ideas so far on revamping Trace. It has five factors:<b> Time, Range, Clarity, Audience and Verse.</b> When a Siren invokes Trace, they must spend 1 Pneuma and a point of Willpower (if they put any suxx into Verse, it becomes a point of permanent Willpower) and roll Akashic Record + Resolve to see how many suxx they get, then they choose how many suxx they spend on each of the mechanics. The higher suxx, the higher strength the Siren may put into a mechanic. If the Siren uses Verse, then she must pay the Verses cost in the subsequent turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Time </b>allows a Siren to see forwards and backwards through time, seeing past or probable future events. The more suxx put into Time, the farther forwards or backwards she may see. Seeing forwards shows the most likely occurrance, but it's easily disrupted by things such as controlling fate or simple dumb luck. Since Time doesn't take into account for this, Sirens tend to see looking forwards with Trace as unreliable at best.<br /> <br /> <b>Range</b> allows a Siren to choose how far her Trace can pull, allowing her to see elsewhere and even exert force with more suxx invested. She may even speak telepathically to people with this. With no suxx, the Trace can only affect the Siren herself, and with one suxx, she may use the Trace on things within her line of sight. With more suxx invested to this, the Siren may communicate to those at a greater distance. With investment to Time as well, a Siren can look into the past or future of places or people far away from her.<br /> <br /> <b>Clarity</b> allows the Trace to have greater definition when Tracing things. She may read into the composition of objects and see physical and mental traits of people. With investment to Time, the Siren may get her defined answers instead of seeing things through a set timeframe. With Investment to Range, the Siren may speak more than a simple phrase and add more words to her telepathic messages.<br /> <br /> <b>Audience</b> allows the Trace to affect a group of people outside of the siren, and by itself it allows a Siren to try to &quot;listen&quot; into other active traces. With more suxx put into this, the group of people can grow very large. With investment to Time, the Siren shares a Time Trace's Vision with the Audience. With investment to Range, the Siren may hold a group conversation with people. With Investment to Clarity, a Siren may pre-record a message that she wants any specific audience members to hear and leaving others out.<br /> <br /> <b>Verse </b>is simply what allows a Siren to wield a Verse during her Tracing. The amount of Suxx put into this equals the dot level of the Conclusion the Siren may use through the Trace. With Investment to Time, a Siren may use Verses in the past. With Investment to Range, a Siren may use Verses at the places she sees, as if she were actually there (and thus negating the Amour modifier normally required to affect places out of sensory vision). Clarity and Audience have no effect with this.<br /> <br /> There's also the idea of Sirens being able to Trace other Sirens, but due to Song's nature (and thus a Siren's as well) of achronality, if the Siren doesn't wish to be traced, she may reflexively roll Akashic Record + Composure to contest the use of the trace. The Resisting Siren's suxx is subtracted from the Tracing Sirens suxx that they may spend, and if the Resisting Siren's suxx is higher, then she completely blocks the Trace from occurring.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking a step back to look at the previous Trace chart:<br /> <br /> <b>Time</b> looks to be the same factor, it now can peer into the past or towards the most likely future.<br /> <br /> <b>Range </b>is the modified version of Area. Would it be dependent on what target the Siren is focusing on? A person, a place, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Clarity</b> is a fusion of Focus and Noise to some degree, for as it increases the Siren sees the fine details unobstructed.<br /> <br /> <b>Audience </b>is a new category which is how 'softly' the Siren can impact events, leaving messages and working the events of her Trace with a group of observers. Could this be used to bring other non-Sirens along with the Trace? Could she use Audience to 'tap into' the Trace of another without being noticed?<br /> <br /> <b>Verse</b> quite simply impacts how the Siren could effect the events of the Trace with her Verses.<br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to how a Trace occurs, does the Siren pay her costs at the start and disperse her successes (both rolled and bonus) over the parameters she wants from the start? Or while experiencing the Trace is she able to expend the pool of successes towards any parameter, enhancing the degree of her Trace on the spot. Does 'investment' mean she needs an already set expense of a parameter or spending for both Audience and Range (example) at the point to hold a group conversation.<br /> <br /> Since Time, Range and Clarity cover the same parameters as the previous chart, I suggest any of these are available after the Siren spends her first Pneuma to activate the Trace. Since Audience is more involved this sounds like the criteria to require a Willpower point, either spent at Trace activation or during the Trace. I do like how to use Verse it requires a Willpower dot for the high stakes, as it keeps the Siren from altering things this way too frequently. The one caveat to the price for including a Verse, I feel, would be the Sense Conclusion. As this Conclusion merely brings information to the Siren's awareness and has no tangible aspect, using Sense to enhance the Trace further should only cost a Willpower point instead of a dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:31:27-07:00","id":984384,"title":"","content":"Hey Metal, if you do that crossover do you think Poseidon would make a decent villain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:59:51-07:00","id":984399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984384#post984384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Metal, if you do that crossover do you think Poseidon would make a decent villain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that directed at me?<br /> <br /> I haven't been following the Poseidon development yet but from a logistical standpoint I would say 'not anytime in the near or distancing future.' The scope of your Chronicle plays a big part in how one finds villains, scope as how expansive you picture the setting to be.<br /> <br /> For example, my current Princess game is in the Minnesota around the Twin Cities (I need to make a dedicated Chronicle thread at some point) and there are few plots that go outside of the cities since the Dreamlands provides so much variety. Given the Great Lakes are right there in the MidWest I planned to use them at a point for further Leviathan and now Siren elements. The story already crosses over with Changeling, Promethean, Leviathan and Genius. I have two others slated to be introduced, one official and one fan made, but I'm more of an reactionary storyteller. I see where my players have interest and arrange my story hooks to that input. Genius and Promethean in particular need a lot more development.<br /> <br /> For an international cooperation, I guess they may have trade or influence around the Great Lakes? My primary effort is to have the more obvious villains drawn from the Princess guide, as we're in the middle of getting one of the group's NPC friends exorcised of an Amanojaku, a rogue Dreamlander figment. I do have ideas for a future Siren character, from the idea that with Darkness + Taint Opuses you have a Siren that can interact with the Outer Darkness to a great degree. I'll save that draft towards commentary I had about character creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the short, I would have to introduce Sirens first before giving any of their antagonists real weight, and Siren material currently stands third in line. From what little I know of Poseidon it would be interesting fodder for the NPC Seeker of Hearts in the Embassy to Economics, the white collar crime Princess part of the NPC Nakama/team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:10:04-07:00","id":984409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984399#post984399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that directed at me?<br /> <br /> I haven't been following the Poseidon development yet but from a logistical standpoint I would say 'not anytime in the near or distancing future.' The scope of your Chronicle plays a big part in how one finds villains, scope as how expansive you picture the setting to be.<br /> <br /> For example, my current Princess game is in the Minnesota around the Twin Cities (I need to make a dedicated Chronicle thread at some point) and there are few plots that go outside of the cities since the Dreamlands provides so much variety. Given the Great Lakes are right there in the MidWest I planned to use them at a point for further Leviathan and now Siren elements. The story already crosses over with Changeling, Promethean, Leviathan and Genius. I have two others slated to be introduced, one official and one fan made, but I'm more of an reactionary storyteller. I see where my players have interest and arrange my story hooks to that input. Genius and Promethean in particular need a lot more development.<br /> <br /> For an international cooperation, I guess they may have trade or influence around the Great Lakes? My primary effort is to have the more obvious villains drawn from the Princess guide, as we're in the middle of getting one of the group's NPC friends exorcised of an Amanojaku, a rogue Dreamlander figment. I do have ideas for a future Siren character, from the idea that with Darkness + Taint Opuses you have a Siren that can interact with the Outer Darkness to a great degree. I'll save that draft towards commentary I had about character creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the short, I would have to introduce Sirens first before giving any of their antagonists real weight, and Siren material currently stands third in line. From what little I know of Poseidon it would be interesting fodder for the NPC Seeker of Hearts in the Embassy to Economics, the white collar crime Princess part of the NPC Nakama/team.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, sorry if i annoyed you with that question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-09-2016, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:37:05-07:00","id":984429,"title":"","content":"It wasn't annoyance, my dear Killerclown, although I see where my first line gives off that thought.<br /> <br /> My handle on the site is <b>meta</b>blender, so I was just making sure you meant me when you referred to 'metal.'<br /> <br /> The rest of my comment merely reflects how scope and setting need to be minded in a Chronicle. At the moment my game stays quite Local and has plenty to work with already. If Poseidon become more developed and the story started going that direction I would use them as villains. There just needs to be an chain of nuance on how to get a group of Princesses involved with taking down a Siren hunting company controlled by Echidnal forces. Although there is the Leviathan hating anti-villain Storms Princess who wouldn't take kindly to such a company either...<br /> <br /> Place also plays a part. Beyond Honolulu, if there was another American city used for a plug and play Siren setting I would suggest one of the cities along the Great Lakes given how they were the backbone of early water trade in the region. That could be Duluth, MN on Lake Superior; Milwaukee Wisconsin on Lake Michigan or Detroit Michigan as the Detroit river connects the Lakes to the St. Lawrence seaway that goes out to the ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:49:23-07:00","id":984440,"title":"","content":"Sorry, i misread your name. Also, I would say that Poseidon would probably have a lab in the Great Lakes. Also, from what I have read from Princess, I would think the Outer Darkness would have abit of influence in the company. Especially when they are helping fulfill the goals of Echinda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-09-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:04:19-07:00","id":984589,"title":"","content":"I got one more question. Would Poseidon employees be able to control the Vodianoi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:09:33-07:00","id":984660,"title":"","content":"There's the <b>Pack Leader's Mark</b> Malformation can be used to control other Vodinaoi. Echidna only grants it to her Sirens or Vodinaoi that show loyalty and leadership qualities, plus it's also a highly visible tattoo on your face. If Poseidon can gain Malformations that could be one only select agents have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:20:18-07:00","id":984663,"title":"","content":"Some members of the corporation, most likely the Board and higher-ups would have that. Also can i have your opinion on a henchman for the corporation? He is basically one of the corporation's test subjects who was chosen to test a new steroid made of shark testosterone. The result made him extremely strong but kinda dimwitted. Also, as you can tell, a lot of Poseidon's experiments center around the ocean.Including the whole kidnapping sirens and using their DNA to make amphibious humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:59:40-07:00","id":984686,"title":"","content":"Also Sally, if any supplements for this come out and i am allowed to write one, i would make it about Poseidon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T18:34:17-07:00","id":984696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984379#post984379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a future post I'll mark down mechanics of present Investigative or Chase merits to see if there's any new ideas to be had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984379#post984379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking a step back to look at the previous Trace chart:<br /> <b>Time</b> looks to be the same factor, it now can peer into the past or towards the most likely future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984379#post984379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Range </b>is the modified version of Area. Would it be dependent on what target the Siren is focusing on? A person, a place, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;Dependent&quot;. If you mean it can only capture what the Siren specifies, then...yes? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984379#post984379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Clarity</b> is a fusion of Focus and Noise to some degree, for as it increases the Siren sees the fine details unobstructed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I thought it would be easier to put them as one thing. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984379#post984379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Audience </b>is a new category which is how 'softly' the Siren can impact events, leaving messages and working the events of her Trace with a group of observers. Could this be used to bring other non-Sirens along with the Trace? Could she use Audience to 'tap into' the Trace of another without being noticed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I would say yes, a Siren can tap into the Trace of another without being noticed. The Song is open to all Sirens and cannot be &quot;shut off&quot;. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984379#post984379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Verse</b> quite simply impacts how the Siren could effect the events of the Trace with her Verses.<br /> <br /> In regards to how a Trace occurs, does the Siren pay her costs at the start and disperse her successes (both rolled and bonus) over the parameters she wants from the start? Or while experiencing the Trace is she able to expend the pool of successes towards any parameter, enhancing the degree of her Trace on the spot. Does 'investment' mean she needs an already set expense of a parameter or spending for both Audience and Range (example) at the point to hold a group conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The Siren must pay her costs (1 Pneuma and Willpower) and then roll to see how many suxx she has, then spend those successes depending on what she desires the Trace to show her. I would say a Siren may use Trace as an extended action, but each roll takes longer than the last and it will most likely Overtrace the circumstance the Siren chose. <br /> <br /> In the terms of Investment, what I mean is something like the old trace chart in terms of &quot;how many suxx invested&quot;. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Investment</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Time</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Range</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Clarity</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Audience</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Verse</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">No Successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Snapshot, a single frame that answers the question.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within the Siren's Sensory perception.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Vague answer or call to the Siren's Trace. Single word for Range or vague premonition through Time via obscure symbology.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One person.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Cannot make use of Verses</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">One Success</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Hour into the past or the future.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within the range of a building from the Siren.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">General Answer or call to the Siren's Trace, summed up in one sentence with Range and capable of showing a vague answer to Time Traces.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Two people.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">May make use of one verse using a Conclusion at one dot of power.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Two Successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Day into the past or the future</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within the range of a city block from the Siren.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">An answer or call to the Siren's Trace, summed up to two sentences with Range or showing a general answer to time Traces.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Four people.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">May make use of one verse using a Conclusion at 2 dots of power.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Three Successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Week into the past or future.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within the range of half a mile from the Siren.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">A specified answer or call to the Siren's Trace, summed up in a paragraph with range or showing a direct answer to Time traces.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Eight people</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">May make use of one verse using a Conclusion at 3 dots of power.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Four Successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Month into the past or Future</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within the range of a mile from the Siren.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">A complete answer or call to the Siren's Trace, summed up as long as the Siren may think a complete message or showing a complete answer throughout the time frame.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Sixteen people</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">May make use of one verse using a Conclusion at 4 dots of power.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Five Successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Year into the past or future.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Within the range of a city from the Siren.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">An enlightening answer or call to the Siren's Trace, which can give Range or Time Traces to hold encyclopedic answers to the Siren's question or answering.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Thirty Two people</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">May make use of one verse using a Conclusion at 5 dots of power.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984379#post984379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Time, Range and Clarity cover the same parameters as the previous chart, I suggest any of these are available after the Siren spends her first Pneuma to activate the Trace. Since Audience is more involved this sounds like the criteria to require a Willpower point, either spent at Trace activation or during the Trace. I do like how to use Verse it requires a Willpower dot for the high stakes, as it keeps the Siren from altering things this way too frequently. The one caveat to the price for including a Verse, I feel, would be the Sense Conclusion. As this Conclusion merely brings information to the Siren's awareness and has no tangible aspect, using Sense to enhance the Trace further should only cost a Willpower point instead of a dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Even if a Siren doesn't invest in certain parts of a Trace, she still has access to them (if in very limited fashions). And I'm happy the Verse cost is liked. <br /> <br /> Although now, I need to think up of Overtrace Mechanics. So far, my ideas are that Overtrace can be beneficial or harmful. Traces used to call people or look upon the future gain a flat +1 to each further trace used to see it. Even though this goes against the purpose of Overtracing, it's still a drawback in the factor that the bonus goes toward all Sirens trying to trace it. However, in the case a Verse is used to act in the future or past or a Verse is used through the Range Trace, then the condition immediately loses the bonuses after making the roll for the Trace, and when the Siren uses her Verse to act, the Overtraced Condition still applies, but instead levying a penalty equal to the successes gained on the Verse + the number of suxx invested into the Verse Function of the Trace. <br /> <br /> <br /> And also for notice, here's the current writing for Poseidon International. This doc will also be updated as Honolulu's Chapter 3, which covers the forces at work in Honolulu. <br /> <br /> <b>Honolulu's Chapter 3: Current Events and Secret Societies: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14jX3EEDWtjYk25fP7jNIro2M12MeOjpcmqKX7PB8dBI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T19:00:32-07:00","id":984710,"title":"","content":"I like it so far Sally. I wonder what stereotypes the sirens, furies and flensers would have for Poseidon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T20:55:52-07:00","id":984736,"title":"","content":"Sorry for double posting but i got one more question. How much control should Poseidon have over the Vodianoi? Should it be that Poseidon threats them like mindless brutes and the Vodianoi often don't listen to them? Or, should it be the same type of control Echinda's sirens have over them that have the Vodianoi acting like dogs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T22:35:40-07:00","id":984751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984736#post984736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for double posting but i got one more question. How much control should Poseidon have over the Vodianoi? Should it be that Poseidon threats them like mindless brutes and the Vodianoi often don't listen to them? Or, should it be the same type of control Echinda's sirens have over them that have the Vodianoi acting like dogs</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that only one Siren and one manager in each Poseidon location (and who own the Pack Leader's Mark) has control over the Vodianoi. I would say that most of Poseidon aren't even aware of them save the Sirens within Poseidon and the single manager at each location. If they're released, they're sent after Sirens already going through the water or in the Celestial Ocean in the form of a zerg rush.Otherwise, the Vodianoi cannot be controlled by most of the employees at Poseidon, but if any human personnel saw them, they may think of them as the fruits of Poseidon's labor at evolutionizing humanity. <br /> <br /> As for Stereotypes the others would have on them, we should prolly wait on those. They aren't even written up yet and I plan on handling that myself. ^^&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:42:09-07:00","id":984859,"title":"","content":"So when I had those other Alteration ideas I didn't have one for Vaporia. I was interested if some Sirens could have a means of personal flight, besides using a Self-Wind-Travel Verse, so we have both Vaporia and Echidnal versions.<br /> <br /> <b>Swan's Feathers</b><br /> A set of feathery wings appear on the Siren's body, such as her back or arms. With them she is able to glide to control her fall damage. Provided she has not be restrained or reached terminal velocity reduce all fall damage to 1 Resistant Bashing. The Siren can gain height under her own power but can only fly for Akashic Record + 1 minutes before she must rest her wings for a half hour. Her flight speed is equal to her land speed +3 (or if she spends a Willpower point, she may use her swim speed as base if it is faster).<br /> <br /> <b>Dragoon's Wings</b><br /> Thick membranes form the wings of the Vodinaoi. They spend a point of Willpower to activate their flight for a scene and can fly tirelessly with a flight speed of their land speed +5. However their lithe bodies of hollowed bones are incredibly fragile. Whenever the Vodinaoi takes damage they suffer an additional point of damage of the same type. This includes fall speed if the Vodinaoi's wings were restrained.<br /> <br /> <br /> This also raises a question I had. Vodinaoi can only use Echidna's Malformations, correct? But Furies can use Alterations depending on what material their vessel is crafted from. Since a good third to half of the Alterations use Akashic Record in some way, do Furies have an Akashic Record? And given the disparity of Quagmires forming on Earth and Echidna sitting in the depths of the Deluge, no Fury would have a Malformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T10:19:27-07:00","id":984932,"title":"","content":"Not sure if I've missed something, but I don't think wings are ideal on any water-based creature that does beneath the waves, especially not feathered wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:04:07-07:00","id":984952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984859#post984859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when I had those other Alteration ideas I didn't have one for Vaporia. I was interested if some Sirens could have a means of personal flight, besides using a Self-Wind-Travel Verse, so we have both Vaporia and Echidnal versions.<br /> <br /> <b>Swan's Feathers</b><br /> A set of feathery wings appear on the Siren's body, such as her back or arms. With them she is able to glide to control her fall damage. Provided she has not be restrained or reached terminal velocity reduce all fall damage to 1 Resistant Bashing. The Siren can gain height under her own power but can only fly for Akashic Record + 1 minutes before she must rest her wings for a half hour. Her flight speed is equal to her land speed +3 (or if she spends a Willpower point, she may use her swim speed as base if it is faster).<br /> <br /> <b>Dragoon's Wings</b><br /> Thick membranes form the wings of the Vodinaoi. They spend a point of Willpower to activate their flight for a scene and can fly tirelessly with a flight speed of their land speed +5. However their lithe bodies of hollowed bones are incredibly fragile. Whenever the Vodinaoi takes damage they suffer an additional point of damage of the same type. This includes fall speed if the Vodinaoi's wings were restrained.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I feel what Kara's saying, but I would say, so that it'd still be fitting in there, only the mechanics that reduce fall damage should remain for the Vaporia version. As for the Malformation idea, I'd say that's something Echidna might make use of only within the material realm. Otherwise, most Vodianoi who'd stay within the Celestial Ocean wouldn't use them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984859#post984859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also raises a question I had. Vodinaoi can only use Echidna's Malformations, correct? But Furies can use Alterations depending on what material their vessel is crafted from. Since a good third to half of the Alterations use Akashic Record in some way, do Furies have an Akashic Record? And given the disparity of Quagmires forming on Earth and Echidna sitting in the depths of the Deluge, no Fury would have a Malformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I must note though that Echidna's Malformations cover both &quot;Alterations Echidna magically grafts onto her Sirens/Vodianoi&quot; as well as &quot;Alterations only Echidna can give (and hence why they're listed with their own section and not in the Vodianoi)&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would say that Furies would use their Rank/the Quagmire's Resentment in place of Akashic Record. I'll add in a note of such. As for owning Malformations, yes, the Furies don't have access to any Vodianoi. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:14:27-07:00","id":984985,"title":"","content":"So your saying that the most likley person to be able to control the Vodinaoi would be building managers and the sirens in the company? I would also think that the board could control them too. Also, do you want info on Arctic Base Echo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:25:54-07:00","id":985146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984985#post984985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your saying that the most likley person to be able to control the Vodinaoi would be building managers and the sirens in the company?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't I just say that in the last post?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984985#post984985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also think that the board could control them too. Also, do you want info on Arctic Base Echo?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I have enough information and mechanics for Poseidon to manage with what's already there; I don't intend on making them a main antagonist for the entire gameline, just a thing that exist in a certain place or a few to give potential storytellers suggestions on what they can use in their chronicles.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:35:36-07:00","id":985152,"title":"","content":"Ok, and yes you did say that. Also, if Poseidon was in a canon gameline which one do you think they could fit in? Also, was the idea of destroying a oil tanker sized research vessel under construction an okay plot hook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-10-2016, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:19:00-07:00","id":985176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=985152#post985152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, and yes you did say that. Also, if Poseidon was in a canon gameline which one do you think they could fit in? Also, was the idea of destroying a oil tanker sized research vessel under construction an okay plot hook?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not canon, but maybe Genius or Leviathan would work quite well. Otherwise, you don't need to ask me on what's ok or not for plot hooks. Here's an empty google doc that anyone can edit, feel free to fill it up with plot hook ideas. I'll look through them and pick which ones work well enough in the game when furthering Honolulu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hjXVDjWIvTGA5yR9RkWTkr4LMEZZmxaAUIKHunh1OzI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hjXVDjWIvTGA5yR9RkWTkr4LMEZZmxaAUIKHunh1OzI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hjXVDjWIvTGA5yR9RkWTkr4LMEZZmxaAUIKHunh1OzI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hjXVDjWIvTGA5yR9RkWTkr4LMEZZmxaAUIKHunh1OzI/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That said, I don't want to sound bad or dismissive, but I can't help but feel like you may desire to develop Poseidon beyond what capability it may have in Siren. If I may be so bold to ask, that is if it is your desire, could you please make a new topic if you want to develop Poseidon in a different direction or small talk about ideas for how to homebrew it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:00:37-07:00","id":985202,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I annoyed you during my time collaborating with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:24:55-07:00","id":985215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984932#post984932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if I've missed something, but I don't think wings are ideal on any water-based creature that does beneath the waves, especially not feathered wings.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=984952#post984952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I feel what Kara's saying, but I would say, so that it'd still be fitting in there, only the mechanics that reduce fall damage should remain for the Vaporia version. As for the Malformation idea, I'd say that's something Echidna might make use of only within the material realm. Otherwise, most Vodianoi who'd stay within the Celestial Ocean wouldn't use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgot to write down the inspiration. Many waterfowl, such as swans, ducks, some geese and loons have <i>water repellent</i> feathers. They both swim, dive and fly, although it is true that the wings provide no use underwater. The webbed feet of waterfowl isn't only to paddle on the surface, it provides their main thrust to dive for prey. Quite similarly, a Siren with this alteration would use her wings out of the water and let her tail and other fins propel her as they swim.<br /> <br /> I do know the ability to fly is quite OP in a Chronicles system, which is why I tried to temper it with needed limitations. Sirens can only fly for a limited time, Vodinaoi with the Malformation version can fly indefinitely but are much more fragile. It's a delicate balance of pros and cons to give access to such an ability with a decent leash as to the frequency of use. There's also the consideration that for a Siren, given she would be in Diluvian form, would still have to manage how long she can breathe out of the water when using her wings to fly. Or is there still a system for a Siren to partially transform to only use one of their Alterations in their human guise?<br /> <br /> Plus, I saw it as a way to bring back some avian features into the Siren game, given the birdlike sirens of early myth. Whereas we now equate Sirens with mermaids and similar water nymphs/aquatic legends.<br /> <br /> All that being said, just a minute after I posted the draft I felt like the Alteration and Malformation needed to be revised. Would an extra step in the mechanics (unfurling the wings, as it were) help downplay the benefits of the ability?<br /> <br /> <b>Swan's Feathers</b><br /> With them she is able to glide to control her fall damage. Provided she has not be restrained or reached terminal velocity reduce all fall damage to 1 Resistant Bashing. The Siren can gain height under her own power but can only fly for Akashic Record + 1 minutes before she must rest her wings for a half hour. Her flight speed is equal to her land speed +3. Once per scene she may spend 1 Willpower to activate one of these effects: a) double the length of time she can fly before resting; b) use her maximum swim speed to calculate flight speed.<br /> <br /> <b>Dragoon's Wings</b><br /> Thick membranes form the wings of the Vodinaoi. They spend a point of Willpower to activate their flight for a scene and can fly tirelessly with a flight speed of their land speed +5. However their lithe bodies of hollowed bones are incredibly fragile. Whenever the Vodinaoi takes damage they suffer an additional point of damage of the same type. This includes fall speed if the Vodinaoi's wings were restrained. While swimming, however, the cumbersome wings remove the 10-again quality for underwater movement, unless the Vodinaoi spends 1 Willpower to restore the quality for 1 scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:57:16-07:00","id":985700,"title":"","content":"I have one more question. When i am done filling the google document, how do i link up the updated document? Also, is it okay if one of the plot hooks involves a crossover with either Demon or Werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-11-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:14:14-07:00","id":985709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=985202#post985202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I annoyed you during my time collaborating with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I seem annoyed. But yes, feel free to fill up that google doc with whatever ideas you have. ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=985215#post985215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgot to write down the inspiration. Many waterfowl, such as swans, ducks, some geese and loons have <i>water repellent</i> feathers. They both swim, dive and fly, although it is true that the wings provide no use underwater. The webbed feet of waterfowl isn't only to paddle on the surface, it provides their main thrust to dive for prey. Quite similarly, a Siren with this alteration would use her wings out of the water and let her tail and other fins propel her as they swim.<br /> <br /> I do know the ability to fly is quite OP in a Chronicles system, which is why I tried to temper it with needed limitations. Sirens can only fly for a limited time, Vodinaoi with the Malformation version can fly indefinitely but are much more fragile. It's a delicate balance of pros and cons to give access to such an ability with a decent leash as to the frequency of use. There's also the consideration that for a Siren, given she would be in Diluvian form, would still have to manage how long she can breathe out of the water when using her wings to fly. Or is there still a system for a Siren to partially transform to only use one of their Alterations in their human guise?<br /> <br /> Plus, I saw it as a way to bring back some avian features into the Siren game, given the birdlike sirens of early myth. Whereas we now equate Sirens with mermaids and similar water nymphs/aquatic legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, then it makes more sense to have in the game.^^ And yes, Sirens still have the ability to pull out Alterations upon their human forms. Costs one pneuma to do so, but it risks Refraction to do such.<br /> <br /> As for the bird features, if it piques any interest, there is some ideas waaaay back for creating an &quot;Ascended&quot; form for Sirens. Namely, something in the same vein as Archmastery for Mages, The Inheritance for Beasts, Queendom for Princesses, etcetc. I think we had ideas for two versions of this, one being for a Siren who gains an aerial form that allows flight and various other powers (which he had no ideas on as of yet). The other version was becoming an utterly abyssal monstrosity with mutagenic powers, AKA what Echidna is. We're still open for those ideas of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=985215#post985215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that being said, just a minute after I posted the draft I felt like the Alteration and Malformation needed to be revised. Would an extra step in the mechanics (unfurling the wings, as it were) help downplay the benefits of the ability?<br /> <br /> <b>Swan's Feathers</b><br /> With them she is able to glide to control her fall damage. Provided she has not be restrained or reached terminal velocity reduce all fall damage to 1 Resistant Bashing. The Siren can gain height under her own power but can only fly for Akashic Record + 1 minutes before she must rest her wings for a half hour. Her flight speed is equal to her land speed +3. Once per scene she may spend 1 Willpower to activate one of these effects: a) double the length of time she can fly before resting; b) use her maximum swim speed to calculate flight speed.<br /> <br /> <b>Dragoon's Wings</b><br /> Thick membranes form the wings of the Vodinaoi. They spend a point of Willpower to activate their flight for a scene and can fly tirelessly with a flight speed of their land speed +5. However their lithe bodies of hollowed bones are incredibly fragile. Whenever the Vodinaoi takes damage they suffer an additional point of damage of the same type. This includes fall speed if the Vodinaoi's wings were restrained. While swimming, however, the cumbersome wings remove the 10-again quality for underwater movement, unless the Vodinaoi spends 1 Willpower to restore the quality for 1 scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've put these Alterations into the book. :3<br /> <br /> And as an extra thing, I've fully rewritten Trace within the book as well to be fitting to the new idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:19:51-07:00","id":985713,"title":"","content":"Thanks and i accept your aplogy. I am just kinda excited because this my first time actually posting in the forums. Also, i might soon try to homebrew an idea for a splat, fan-made or official. If i choose fan-made, it will probably be something for either Princess or Genius, when i get around to reading them. For official, it would probably be for Werewolf, possibly a idigam cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:37:06-07:00","id":985726,"title":"","content":"Here is five possible storyhooks. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hjXVDjWIvTGA5yR9RkWTkr4LMEZZmxaAUIKHunh1OzI/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...KHunh1OzI/edit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:02:12-07:00","id":985790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=985700#post985700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one more question. When i am done filling the google document, how do i link up the updated document? Also, is it okay if one of the plot hooks involves a crossover with either Demon or Werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to link it up if you don't want to. Because it's in the Siren folder in my google drive, I can always take a peek at it. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:05:18-07:00","id":985794,"title":"","content":"Ok. Also would you like to hear my home brew idea for Princess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:20:48-07:00","id":985799,"title":"","content":"I would, send me a PM; this is the wrong place for it alas.<br /> Or you can make a topic of your own where you can post and discuss any homebrew idea you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:23:22-07:00","id":985800,"title":"","content":"Hey kara, I guess I will send you a pm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T17:54:09-07:00","id":985820,"title":"","content":"Did you get my pm. Also, sorry for posting off of topic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T00:30:19-07:00","id":985985,"title":"","content":"So I did, carry on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T00:38:15-07:00","id":985988,"title":"","content":"I would like to announce that along with finished Trace Mechanics, I've also changed the Trace section of each of the Currents! So far, each of them get an automatic bonus on one of the pieces of the trace.<br /> <br /> <b>Buoyancy and Acheron: </b>Time<br /> <b>Conflict and Phlegethon: </b>Range<br /> <b>Harmony and Lethe: </b>Audience<br /> <b>Healing and Styx: </b>Verse<br /> <b>Wisdom and Cocytus: </b>Clarity<br /> <br /> <b>Oceanus: </b>Whatever Echidna dictates is important for the individual missions her Sirens have. One Siren may be able to get a bonus on Time while another requires Range and gets a bonus on Range to suit her. :3<br /> <br /> I hope this makes an interesting dynamic. I've also added in five new merits! I hope you all enjoy them.<br /> <br /> <b>[1] Sea\u2019s Temperament</b><br /> Most Sirens living close to water, mainly near sea, tend to gain this merit. Your character\u2019s mood rises and falls with the sea, affecting her emotions and her Maelstrom. At low tide, your character\u2019s mood seems calmer and emotions more distant. Your character gains a +1 bonus on attempts to resist maelstrom.<br /> <br /> Drawback: Your character\u2019s mood also rises with High tide, making her more active and irritable. During high tide, your character takes a -1 penalty to resist Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> <b>[1] Weather Sense</b><br /> Your character has a knack for reading upcoming weather. Perhaps she simply knows that old fables about telling the weather rings true for her. Maybe the Siren\u2019s Trace subconsciously tells her of things to come. The Siren may gain an automatic Trace roll concerning upcoming weather within the next 24 hours. The roll is considered to be free, and with each success the ST must tell of the weather type, Environmental Level(s) and/or if it was caused by a Quagmire or not.<br /> <br /> <b>[3] Eye of the Storm</b><br /> The Siren\u2019s Maelstrom is more like a hurricane. The entry and exit are furious waves, but if the Siren tries to focus then she may find the calm medium to hide until the storm passes. Whenever the Siren faces Maelstrom and she fails, she has the option of spending a point of Willpower to force a re-roll. The second roll\u2019s results, no matter the outcome, are kept.<br /> <br /> <b>[1-2] Enchanting Voice</b><br /> There\u2019s simply something about the Siren\u2019s voice that others find divine and hard to ignore. Each song makes others swoon, and each insult cuts deep. Sirens without beauty, but bearing this merit show that beauty isn\u2019t just in physical appearance. This merit grants a +1 to all Social rolls that involve her voice at one dot. At two dots, this merit grants a +2 to all Social rolls instead. This Merit can stack with Striking Looks and Drowned Beauty merits.<br /> <br /> <b>[2] Aura Eater</b><br /> The act of feasting from Pneuma feeds from the soul of the victim itself. Many cultures claim the soul shows in the form of an aura, which can depict the health of one\u2019s mental and emotional state. To an extent, the Siren has this quality. For each point of Pneuma she feeds from another, she gains acute awareness of one of their emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:25:16-07:00","id":986542,"title":"","content":"So each Current no longer has a thematic Trace bonus? It makes sense with the new qualities of the Trace, although some of the previous write ups don't quite mesh with the new properties of the Trace bonus.<br /> <br /> I especially like Aura Eater for one of the new Merits.<br /> <br /> I think a few pages back you mentioned the desire to make a Theron Companion style merit. Therons are the creatures of the Deluge long evolved into new forms much like the Castaways, the Deluge descendants of humanity, correct? What properties do Therons have, and the benefits a Siren would have from bringing back a faithful pet? Also the Theron might need its own Refraction or it would obviously be seen as a never before seen species.<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Happy to see that I've been able to contribute a few ideas. There's one more complex idea that has been playing in my mind over the last several days. Whether you find it to your liking depends if you want another character category. Siren is pretty robust already with Celestial Currents, Abyssal Currents, Breathless, Castaways/Therons, Echidna &amp; Vodinaoi, Quagmires, Furies and Flensers/antagonistic humans. I leave it your judgement if another classification would be too much.<br /> <br /> Although I see it more as a 'minor ascension' to one of the previous character types.<br /> <br /> I know Undine: the Emergence had no connection to Siren, the initial draft taking a different direction with the merfolk myths. (Sirens and Leviathans make up some of its rudimentary splats). Its theme of a mythical being from the aquatic biome being drawn to and wishing to fit within humanity reminds me much of Promethean. It being a 1E based draft that was never finished, we do not know the full outlook of the game beyond this first theme. Without it being a retread of Promethean trying to be the mermaid becoming human doesn't sound like it would make a full game.<br /> <br /> Although, such an idea could play into Siren. Question: could there be 'Undines' that have their origins as avatars of nature that became Sirens, their humanity a secondary aspect?<br /> <br /> Or in other words, a Fury becoming curious about facets of humanity neither it or its Quagmire expected. From its own curiosity or the encouragement of other Sirens (of any Current) it builds a connection to the Song. And at a point, its crafted Vessel becomes a true Diluvian Form and with it a human guise as well. The new being is still a Siren but one from nature rather than humanity, finding its own place along the strife of Civilization and Nature.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is a rare occurrence that can't really be planned for, as deceptively complex like making an Angel fall or achieving the New Dawn. Given how a Quagmire and thus the Fury forms both are violence incarnate against the ravages of Civilization. A budding future!Siren Fury would likely need an event at the creation of or early in the Quagmire's history that would form a Relationship with a human. Said human would both have to emphasize with the Quagmire and make efforts to further its cause. A Curiosity mechanic could track the sway of the Fury towards becoming a Siren, likely needing to beat the Resentment or Spite of the Quagmire. Let alone that becoming more like a human would jeopardize its ability to enact the Quagmire's vengeance.<br /> <br /> The end result, a new Siren, would have its Rank reduced to a lesser Akashic Record rating, which limits how many of previous Alterations it had that it could keep. Potentially a fragment of its former abilities could be kept, such as its Vessel's material benefits, although a new Siren version would have to be added.<br /> <br /> Drawbacks of this process is that the 'Undine' Siren (or whatever classification for the new entity) would start at lower Lucidity and perhaps be more prone to Malestroms (having extra triggers associated from its Quagmire). Plus, when bottoming out of Lucidity instead of a Banshee it returns to an equally vindictive Fury, now unbound from the Quagmire it generated from, never to redeemed again.<br /> <br /> If this addition is viable, there could even be Character Creation only merits to reflect a player creating an Siren from a former Fury. Of course this begs the clarification: is the Fury a separate entity created the same time as a Quagmire? Or the Quagmire's acting avatar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T22:41:53-07:00","id":986593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=986542#post986542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So each Current no longer has a thematic Trace bonus? It makes sense with the new qualities of the Trace, although some of the previous write ups don't quite mesh with the new properties of the Trace bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I guess I'll do full revisions on the Trace parts then. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=986542#post986542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I especially like Aura Eater for one of the new Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad it's liked. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=986542#post986542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a few pages back you mentioned the desire to make a Theron Companion style merit. Therons are the creatures of the Deluge long evolved into new forms much like the Castaways, the Deluge descendants of humanity, correct? What properties do Therons have, and the benefits a Siren would have from bringing back a faithful pet? Also the Theron might need its own Refraction or it would obviously be seen as a never before seen species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Survivors are the Deluge remnants of humanity. Castaways are Sirens who didn't join a Current. For what little I have on Therons, they're like marine animals with alterations (or land mammals who evolved to have aquatic traits). I know it sounds bad or weird given most of the Alterations rely on having Akashic Record. I imagined in place of this, they'd have an effective Rank equal to their merit dots. <br /> <br /> If it's anything, the further ideas I had on the Theron Pet merit, I was thinking of having the merit be styled like Dogmeat from Fallout 4. Especially fitting with how the Celestial Ocean was made with the &quot;post apocalyptic wasteland&quot; idea in mind. The Theron could see if any Survivors or Vodianoi are about, or may retrieve items to keep a Siren alive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=986542#post986542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Happy to see that I've been able to contribute a few ideas. There's one more complex idea that has been playing in my mind over the last several days. Whether you find it to your liking depends if you want another character category. Siren is pretty robust already with Celestial Currents, Abyssal Currents, Breathless, Castaways/Therons, Echidna &amp; Vodinaoi, Quagmires, Furies and Flensers/antagonistic humans. I leave it your judgement if another classification would be too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like we have abit more than we should have to be honest. Although I feel we could fit in one more splat if we attempted to squish a few splats together.<br /> <br /> Social Splats: Celestial and Abyssal Currents (Including Vodianoi in with Oceanus because that's Echidna's current), Castaways<br /> Subsplats: Survivors, Therons, Breathless<br /> Antagonists: Quagmires/Furies (Being the same thing, a Fury is more like a directed sapience that can make it's own body), Flensers, Echidna and Vodianoi<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=986542#post986542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I see it more as a 'minor ascension' to one of the previous character types.<br /> <br /> *snip Undine the Emergeance*<br /> <br /> Although, such an idea could play into Siren. Question: could there be 'Undines' that have their origins as avatars of nature that became Sirens, their humanity a secondary aspect?<br /> <br /> Or in other words, a Fury becoming curious about facets of humanity neither it or its Quagmire expected. From its own curiosity or the encouragement of other Sirens (of any Current) it builds a connection to the Song. And at a point, its crafted Vessel becomes a true Diluvian Form and with it a human guise as well. The new being is still a Siren but one from nature rather than humanity, finding its own place along the strife of Civilization and Nature.<br /> <br /> *snip bits of Lore and Mechanics*<br /> <br /> If this addition is viable, there could even be Character Creation only merits to reflect a player creating an Siren from a former Fury. Of course this begs the clarification: is the Fury a separate entity created the same time as a Quagmire? Or the Quagmire's acting avatar?</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem I can see at the moment is that the Quagmire and the Fury are really one in the same thing. The Fury is the sapient Avatar of a Quagmire, and a Quagmire is required for a Fury to exist. Not to mention, a Fury does....somewhat have a connection to the Song. For now, the best I can come up with is that they're manifestations of the Song that appear in response to humanity screwing up things and that need immediate action. Heck, perhaps they're one of the many souls of the lost humanity that make up the Song that are driven by rage.<br /> <br /> Although, I do have some ideas from yours on how this could still be played out, if using an aerial motif instead. Pretty much, long ago in Siren we had ideas on implementing an Earth, Sea and Sky motif. So far, we already have loads of sea motifs in Sirens, and an Earth motif in the form of Furies/Quagmires (and possibly Flensers, a fitting irony that the two opposing sides would be on the same in terms of motifs). The only thing missing thus far is a part that fits the Sky motif. I was thinking, given the idea you presented (and not to mention I hate how the entry to the Celestial Ocean works atm), what would happen if a Quagmire had an opposing factor in the form of satisfaction and love? What if Furies had let go of their chains of rage and reach an &quot;Unbound&quot; state?<br /> <br /> Pretty much, this idea is to bring forth ideas for Sylphs. Embodiments of the Song that can be helpful to Sirens or humanity? So far, I imagine they're more Ephemeral beings, may claim a place as a fetter (which then serves as an entry way to the Celestial Ocean, I'll write that Quagmires can serve as the same function). A Sylph can be created by &quot;redeeming&quot; a Fury, but so can a Sylph be enraged until they become a Fury. No other ideas atm, only that Sylphs are something akin to the Rainbow at the end of the Flood in the Story of Noah's Ark. They represent the possibility that the Deluge will not happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T15:11:16-07:00","id":987460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=986593#post986593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, I do have some ideas from yours on how this could still be played out, if using an aerial motif instead. Pretty much, long ago in Siren we had ideas on implementing an Earth, Sea and Sky motif. So far, we already have loads of sea motifs in Sirens, and an Earth motif in the form of Furies/Quagmires (and possibly Flensers, a fitting irony that the two opposing sides would be on the same in terms of motifs). The only thing missing thus far is a part that fits the Sky motif. I was thinking, given the idea you presented (and not to mention I hate how the entry to the Celestial Ocean works atm), what would happen if a Quagmire had an opposing factor in the form of satisfaction and love? What if Furies had let go of their chains of rage and reach an &quot;Unbound&quot; state?<br /> <br /> Pretty much, this idea is to bring forth ideas for Sylphs. Embodiments of the Song that can be helpful to Sirens or humanity? So far, I imagine they're more Ephemeral beings, may claim a place as a fetter (which then serves as an entry way to the Celestial Ocean, I'll write that Quagmires can serve as the same function). A Sylph can be created by &quot;redeeming&quot; a Fury, but so can a Sylph be enraged until they become a Fury. No other ideas atm, only that Sylphs are something akin to the Rainbow at the end of the Flood in the Story of Noah's Ark. They represent the possibility that the Deluge will not happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>For how you present Slyphs they sound a lot like Qashmallim from Promethean. If Slyphs and Furies are primarily Ephemeral beings the helpful/harmful pairing sounds a lot like Elpidos and Lilithim Qashmallim. In that they are avatars of a supernatural force (in this case, the hopeful aspects from the Song) that interact with the player characters in unusual way.<br /> <br /> That parallel aside I do like bringing in all the various aspects of nature (earth sky and sea) in some respects into the game, helps build up the emphasis for how Sirens represent the balance of two worlds and keeps the game from being 'water stuck' in all of its facets.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine that at default Slyphs are free roaming, casting themselves out with the wind. At times they will fetter themselves to a beautiful place, perhaps a few, and wouldn't stray far from such places. If enough anger and pollution troubles their place, the formerly pretty place is now a Quagmire and the Slyph a Fury. If the reciprocation of Fury and Slyph is played to full hilt, there should be some sort of track to determine a Fury's growing redemption or a Slyph's growing anger.<br /> <br /> How much did you want Slyphs and Furies to be alike, if they chiefly represent different biomes? Do the fettered beautiful places that Slyphs take as homes offer benefits in place of a Quagmire's spite? Do Slyphs craft their own vessels the way Furies do? And if Slyphs tend to the entrances to the Celestial Ocean, wouldn't Quagmires have the same connection in regards to the Deluge?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, to help Slyphs stand out all the more it may be better to distance them from Furies. What legends do they pull from besides acting as gatekeepers to the Celestial Ocean and the benevolence of the Song?<br /> <br /> In regards to my earlier idea, a possible 'Undine' would be the unintended product of a Quagmire or further mutation of an animal/corpse that was within the Quagmire. Hmm... for each Quagmire is there only one Fury? If a Quagmire produced multiple crafted vessels is the Fury essentially splitting itself over multiple bodies? Or can it make lesser servitors from materials from nature? The latter leans closer to the idea of there being a 'non-human origin Siren' if it isn't directly tied to the entity of a Quagmire/Fury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:29:17-07:00","id":987642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=987460#post987460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For how you present Slyphs they sound a lot like Qashmallim from Promethean. If Slyphs and Furies are primarily Ephemeral beings the helpful/harmful pairing sounds a lot like Elpidos and Lilithim Qashmallim. In that they are avatars of a supernatural force (in this case, the hopeful aspects from the Song) that interact with the player characters in unusual way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware of the similarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=987460#post987460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That parallel aside I do like bringing in all the various aspects of nature (earth sky and sea) in some respects into the game, helps build up the emphasis for how Sirens represent the balance of two worlds and keeps the game from being 'water stuck' in all of its facets.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine that at default Slyphs are free roaming, casting themselves out with the wind. At times they will fetter themselves to a beautiful place, perhaps a few, and wouldn't stray far from such places. If enough anger and pollution troubles their place, the formerly pretty place is now a Quagmire and the Slyph a Fury. If the reciprocation of Fury and Slyph is played to full hilt, there should be some sort of track to determine a Fury's growing redemption or a Slyph's growing anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. I hope it's not bad to keep a theme that isn't played upon in backstory so much. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=987460#post987460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much did you want Slyphs and Furies to be alike, if they chiefly represent different biomes? Do the fettered beautiful places that Slyphs take as homes offer benefits in place of a Quagmire's spite? Do Slyphs craft their own vessels the way Furies do? And if Slyphs tend to the entrances to the Celestial Ocean, wouldn't Quagmires have the same connection in regards to the Deluge?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, to help Slyphs stand out all the more it may be better to distance them from Furies. What legends do they pull from besides acting as gatekeepers to the Celestial Ocean and the benevolence of the Song?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say they're the same thing at opposite ends of a spectrum. Furies are parts of Nature first and spirits (I don't mean in the exact same way as normal WoD Spirits) second (represented by them requiring a Quagmire to come into existence first) and fueled by hatred of those who desecrate the Earth. Sylphs on the other end are spirits first and part of nature second, and fueled by their love for the Earth or the people. <br /> <br /> For reference, this would mean most Sylphs are by default in their unbound state and in Twilight. They have a default Akashic Record/Rank rating, as well as Power, Finesse and Resistance that don't need any reliances on the existence of a Quagmire. Though in comparison to Furies, this would mean Sylphs tend to be as weak and inconsistent as the winds they take after. Seeing a Sylph is a much rarer event than seeing a Fury.<br /> <br /> However, Sylphs are capable of Fettering themselves to a place by declaring it as a &quot;Shrine&quot; (though I imagine they dislike doing this unless if they were persuaded to). Here, they may grow in power and energy akin to how Furies grow. Their Akashic Record/Rank then becomes a stat rating called &quot;Tranquility&quot; (which is basically like a Quagmire's Resentment), and they may grow further with points of Harmony (which is basically like a Quagmire's Spite). A Sylph becomes stronger at a Shrine through acts of kindness towards both Nature and Civilization, the world in harmony and a shrine even makes it seem like the world apart could be closer together for all their differences, unlike the Quagmires who taint animals to lash out at the people who crosses their path. They would give benefits in place of a Quagmire's Anathemas, but kinda like Quagmires, they will not function for those who are disturbing the peace at the shrine.<br /> <br /> I would say though that the Sylphs have a &quot;Torment&quot; rating (and yes, that's a shout out to Demon the Fallen) that starts out as Empty. If acts that would normally increase a Quagmire's Resentment/Spite is committed in the presence of a Sylph or in their Shrine, if the Sylph would normally gain a dot of Resentment, they instead gain a dot of Torment. Should the Torment meter ever match the Sylph's Tranquility/Rank rating, then the Sylph is torn apart by her torment at the world, devolving into hatred against those who would disrupt the natural balance and becoming a Quagmire on the spot (which will eventually spawn a Fury). <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I imagine Furies would have an equivalent in the form of &quot;Appeasement&quot;. Instead, it fills up when someone does things that would normally build Tranquility in a Shrine and when it becomes equal to the Fury's Resentment, then they shift and become a Sylph.<br /> <br /> I would say that yes, both Quagmires and Shrines give entry into the Deluge. The only difference is who's more active as a gatekeeper. I imagine Sylphs would allow anyone to go in so long as they appeared peaceful (and I imagine it's easy for a Flenser to lie and say &quot;we're just going fishing&quot; to them), and Furies would be wary and keep track of people who went in and out (they can be fooled by Lethe Sirens, unless their status as such was known), and would attack any non-Sirens who were deemed a threat.<br /> <br /> I would say that Sylphs and Furies are two parts of the same coin. To explain them with an example, they're like the Maenads, the mad followers of Dionysus. They may sing songs and spread peace and merriment one day, but if you slight them you may just turn them stark raving mad and they will tear you limb from limb. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=987460#post987460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to my earlier idea, a possible 'Undine' would be the unintended product of a Quagmire or further mutation of an animal/corpse that was within the Quagmire. Hmm... for each Quagmire is there only one Fury? If a Quagmire produced multiple crafted vessels is the Fury essentially splitting itself over multiple bodies? Or can it make lesser servitors from materials from nature? The latter leans closer to the idea of there being a 'non-human origin Siren' if it isn't directly tied to the entity of a Quagmire/Fury.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only one Fury for one Quagmire. I like the idea of making lesser servitors from materials. Perhaps that could be a new numen?<br /> <br /> <b>Craft Elemental Vessels</b><br /> The Fury divides a portion of it's power into a few Vessels of it's choosing. It may maintain a number of Vessels equal to it's Resentment, but they may only be made of a singular material that could be used in the Craft Vessel Numen, and the Fury is free to divide her Power, Finesse and Resistance between her bodies and she may spread an additional number of total Resentment dots amongst the same attributes. All Vessels make use of the same Willpower and Pneuma pools the original Fury is capable of using. This costs 1 point of Pneuma per Vessel the Fury desires to create and uses the same rolling procedures as the Craft Vessel Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:57:39-07:00","id":991653,"title":"","content":"So I've been thinking on something else I've disliked for awhile. Basically, the current Refraction Mechanics. As it stands, it's basically a sneak peak into the Siren's true form without giving much of a detriment to the Siren themselves.<br /> <br /> I was thinking as a fix for this. What if instead of showing people the Siren's true form, the Siren becomes forced to roll to keep herself from going into her Diluvian Form? It would give more significance to hiding their true nature (espeically for Sirens without at least Tentacles, Amphibious Legs or the Andaconda Tail Alterations because without those their speed is HEAVILY hampered <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). What do people think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T19:06:35-07:00","id":991655,"title":"","content":"That sounds fine. Also, I made an edit to the Poseidon plot hook involving the werewolf crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:34:59-07:00","id":992150,"title":"","content":"Alrighties. I would like to apologize for the lack of consistency between my posting. Inspiration flickers on and off, but I promise I will stay on this project until I feel it is completely finished. <br /> <br /> First off, how does this look for Refraction revision?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b> Refraction</b><br /> The Song beats forever through the Siren's soul, empowering them through the Siren's Akashic Record and forming out the Verses they sing. Although the greater the Siren's Akashic Record grows, the more the Song wishes to fly out and recruit more people. To this end, Siren's speculate it's favored recruitment method is to show off the Diluvian Form of it's Sirens. Why it does this, no Siren knows. They only know to call this phenomenon as &quot;Refraction&quot;. Mundanely, it simply means the change in direction of a wave due to a change in it's transmission medium. Supernaturally speaking, Sirens use this term because when they enact a Verse or wield an Alteration, they risk being changed completely into their Diluvian form by force.<br /> <br /> Refraction requires two things in order to work. First, it requires a Siren in their Land Form with an Alteration active or using a Verse. Without a Siren, Refraction obviously cannot happen. Second, it requires a mortal viewer with a soul and that is sapient. Animals and plants cannot trigger Refraction, and strangely to Sirens nor do the other supernatural denizens of the World of Darkness trigger it. Some Sirens speculate that they lack ownership of a soul, while others suggest that due to their nature they cannot necessarily be &quot;recruited&quot; by the Song.<br /> <br /> Once the top two requirements are met, the Siren is forced to roll Resolve + Composure with their Akashic Record as a Penalty to this roll. <br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Siren is forced to change into her Diluvian Form as a reflexive action. Furthermore, all viewers of the Siren must roll their own Resolve + Composure. Success only grants them no effects, while a failure forces them to suffer the Spooked Condition [GMC 183].<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Siren turns into her Diluvian form as an Instant action. Depending on how well most characters can take it, they may suffer a breaking point upon viewing her form.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The Siren manages to compose her form. Though she may seem like she shifts, she remains in her Land form....for now. If it was caused by an Alteration being present, the Siren may face subsequent rolls of Refraction at the ST's discretion.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The Siren manages to keep her form under control. Furthermore, she doesn't trigger Refraction in front of her viewers for the rest of the Scene.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Second off, I hope it's not minded to kinda call back on this, but I was thinking it might also be fine to bring up any Crossovers discussions if it's desired? Or ideas for that matter. I think you wanted to talk on that, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12284_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12284\" data-vbnamecard=\"12284\">-metablender</a> :3<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:53:46-07:00","id":992162,"title":"","content":"It looks pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:07:09-07:00","id":993155,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, I've read through the Poseidon Plot hooks Killerclown, and I must say that most of them seem good. :3 I'm sorry if it seemed like I hadn't looked through them.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking. I had some new ideas on Siren and I wanted to run it by some people to see if any thoughts were had on them.<br /> <br /> First, Choruses. I was thinking what if instead of being named after plays and the like or being themed around them, what if they were based around musical genres? Stuff like Hip Pop, Country, Death Metal, etcetc and then base the theme of them around what that genre's songs tend to be about? I also imagine the mechanical benefits of joining a Chorus is:<br /> 1: Tracing your fellow Chorus members can be done for free. It's almost like &quot;being connected through the Song&quot;.<br /> 2: Performing Verses in the musical genre that your Chorus uses gains double the bonuses in using.<br /> <br /> Second, Ascended Sirens. We haven't talked alot on this, but I do feel like I have ideas for them. Pretty much, I was thinking that the Siren could reach a new level of power and it would depend on her Lucidity level for it. There's two different ways the Siren Ascension can take place. One is the Ascension, the other is the Descension. They both require Akashic Record 6. And perhaps befittingly, I imagine they both would be privvy to Celestial and Abyssal currents respectively.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascension:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ascension is achieved when the Siren is at Lucidity 7 and up. The Siren has been able to rise above the needs of Civilization and Nature and reach an unchained state, showing her detachment away from the physical world and her care for the world going toward the greater good: keeping it alive.I imagine this form would be achieved upon proving that the Siren has the needs of the greater good in her heart. I don't have ideas fluff wise or mechanics wise yet.<br /> <br /> An Ascended Siren gains a third form. Her scales and tail fin are replaced with a brilliant feathers and she regains her legs. She trades out all of her fins for a pair of wings instead. While the Siren has this form, she may gain more dots within her Conclusions (up to 10) which can heavily increase the range and power of her Verses.The Siren also bears a peace of mind unlike any other, making her immune to Maelstrom. Due to her connection to the Song as well (perhaps Ascended Sirens are outright manifestations of the Song), the Siren never willingly suffers Refraction.<br /> <br /> Perhaps as an added bonus, the Siren may also access Twilight in this form and their 300 years of life are extended to eternity. The only drawback is that the Siren may only keep her Ascension so long as she remains at Lucidity 7 and up. If she faces Dissonance and degenerates below Lucidity 7, then she loses the form. She can regain it if she manages to get at least Lucidity 7 again though.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Descension:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Descension on the other half is Lucidity 3 and below. Unlike Ascension, the Siren cares too much for the living world to be able to abandon it. Perhaps she's tied down by her Relationships and doesn't wish to leave them. Perhaps she's too connected to one half of the spectrum. Mechanics and Fluff wise, still no ideas. I can only imagine that Descension would involve a major act that would show the Sirens dedication to the few over the many.<br /> <br /> You can definitely tell what a Descended Siren is. For you see, she becomes forced to remain in her Diluvian form. She doesn't suffer the normal penalties for remaining in Diluvian form: she's capable of breathing out of water, her speed doesn't suffer and the like. Due to this form, she also doesn't suffer from Refraction, much like the Ascended form does. However, for her choice of the few over the many, the Siren gains a new power. She gains the ability to mutagenically enhance herself and other people, introducing new characteristics upon those she touches.<br /> <br /> Like the Ascended Sirens, Descended Sirens can also live to be immortal. They do lose the benefits of this form if they rise above Lucidity 3. Perhaps as another good notion, a Siren cannot reach Lucidity 0 when they've attained this form. If she does degenerate that far, then the Siren instead enters a Maelstrom and remains in it for a number of days equal to her Akashic Record. Afterwards, she returns to normal.<br /> <br /> It should go without saying that Echidna is indeed a Descended Siren.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Finally, Relationships.I feel like I've done an uninspired job on them. Pretty much, I want to change them to make them feel like they mean something. I want to play up on the Relationship aspect of Sirens and that they're important. I want to make it plausible for Sirens to get worried if their Relationships are in danger of being lost. I want to accurately show the mythos of how most water spirits have acted in their love for humans, with love, madness and even possibly death. I will definitely make a Yandere reference somewhere for emphasis. The only problem I have is that I'm afraid it may be close to the Touchstones as in Werewolf and Vampires. But then again, would it be a good idea to use the Touchstone system as a base?<br /> <br /> I know I'm supposed to work on Honolulu and all, and I really do want to. But I feel like these three pieces are the last ones in the puzzle before I can say Siren mechanics and fluff are complete.<br /> <br /> I'm really sorry for calling on people like this, but I feel like I really need feedback on these. Could I ask for your opinions <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1417_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1417\" data-vbnamecard=\"1417\">Reaper Verse</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9279\" data-vbnamecard=\"9279\">Yads Dom</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12284_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12284\" data-vbnamecard=\"12284\">-metablender</a>, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12186\" data-vbnamecard=\"12186\">Killerclown</a>? Again, I'm really sorry for calling on people like this. You don't have to read the entire thing if you don't want to. &gt;&lt;&quot;<br /> <br /> Also Leliel, given Honolulu is beginning to be written up, I was hoping to ask on what historical sources you used when writing up this Fury? Since he'll be set into the setting (if that's ok) and the talk of drug runners and the Filipino branch of the Yakuza may be required as part of the setting in Honolulu and I just want to see the resources you used so I could have some reference when writing up the drug runners and Yakuza as possible plot points. The post for the fury is in this link. Thank you again for making that Fury by the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=926197#post926197\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...197#post926197</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/>