sage\"><br /> Also Leliel, given Honolulu is beginning to be written up, I was hoping to ask on what historical sources you used when writing up this Fury? Since he'll be set into the setting (if that's ok) and the talk of drug runners and the Filipino branch of the Yakuza may be required as part of the setting in Honolulu and I just want to see the resources you used so I could have some reference when writing up the drug runners and Yakuza as possible plot points. The post for the fury is in this link. Thank you again for making that Fury by the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=926197#post926197\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...197#post926197</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly?<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yakuza\" target=\"_blank\"> Wikipedia</a>. I'm no organized crime buff, I was just inspired by the fact they're involved in illegal dumping-Japan has <i>extremely </i>strict and punitive laws about that, so businesses that can't be bothered pay them to smuggle waste around to more convenient sites. There is, however, <a href=\"http://listverse.com/2013/10/23/10-odd-facts-about-the-yakuza/\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a>; it has a lot of the stranger and more unique habits of the Yakuza laid out (such as the fact they're actually pretty politically interested-they're known to be backers of the Liberal Democrat Party, which despite the name's association here in the States are more or less the Japanese UKIP-borderline fascist authoritarian ultranationalists). <br /> <br /> Also, like the Endgame systems, though I can't stick around to give a good critique of the systems right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:04:02-07:00","id":993656,"title":"","content":"I like the endgame stuff to. Also, when you start playing siren and you use Poseidon let me know how it goes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-26-2016, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:42:59-07:00","id":993711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993504#post993504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly?<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yakuza\" target=\"_blank\"> Wikipedia</a>. I'm no organized crime buff, I was just inspired by the fact they're involved in illegal dumping-Japan has <i>extremely </i>strict and punitive laws about that, so businesses that can't be bothered pay them to smuggle waste around to more convenient sites. There is, however, <a href=\"http://listverse.com/2013/10/23/10-odd-facts-about-the-yakuza/\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a>; it has a lot of the stranger and more unique habits of the Yakuza laid out (such as the fact they're actually pretty politically interested-they're known to be backers of the Liberal Democrat Party, which despite the name's association here in the States are more or less the Japanese UKIP-borderline fascist authoritarian ultranationalists)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Alright, thank you so much for this. Ironically, I think I actually stumbled on that one article before when STing for a game involving PC Yakuza.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993504#post993504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, like the Endgame systems, though I can't stick around to give a good critique of the systems right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad they're liked. Don't worry about it, I'm sorry for calling up for commentary like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993656#post993656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the endgame stuff to. Also, when you start playing siren and you use Poseidon let me know how it goes</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. &gt;w&gt; I will. Speaking of which, we're still looking for playtesters for anyone who reads this and is interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:00:41-07:00","id":993720,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I would also wanted you to know that if you want me too add anymore details to Poseidon I will","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:36:58-07:00","id":993744,"title":"","content":"Ascended and Descended forms for Sirens are sounding top notch. It seems like Siren consistently finds the cream of the crop amongst similar mechanics and systems to bring the best all into one game.<br /> <br /> <br /> When it gets to the Crossover conversation, there was one point I wanted to address first. Siren presents a particular platform to make or break a crossover and storytellers will want to think twice about what game lines they chose to include, whether Siren is the sole focus or part of the ancillary background.<br /> <br /> Let me quote a few sections on the Deluge and Celestial Oceans to build upon:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In truth, the Deluge is the culminations of all apocalypses, past and future. It is to this extent that the event that causes the Deluge to occur is ultimately unclear because in today\u2019s day and age it\u2019s possible for anything and everything to have a hand in causing the Deluge. Afterall, an apocalypse caused by hands of man is just as plausible as a freak backlash caused by nature or the cosmos.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Perhaps the one thing that it lacks is the existence of any other realities that would normally be connected to the Earth. There is no Shadow, Underworld, Hedge, nor is there any Twilight for that matter. This calms some Sirens, as it means they have less they\u2019re required to deal with. To others, it simply freaks them out because the Deluge isn\u2019t just a danger to a single reality, but to all realities connected to the Earth when it happens.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>In short, when working with Siren in a crossover setting it is the ultimate exercise of conversation of detail. Consider that the sister venue paired with Siren will play a part in the Deluge. If Sirens are the muses, oracles, and stand-takers of the conflict between Civilization and Nature, another society of supernatural figures will have their own impact on both and thus a massive impact on the Deluge.<br /> <br /> Although the Delgue has no Twilight and no connection to other realms, its cataclysms in a crossover venture should hint to where these realms originally were. The cataclysm is decidedly supernatural in origin but should still be shaped by how that venue interacts with both Civilization and Nature. Entering the Deluge of a Geist game reveals a dead sea where the dead of the Underworld have been spat out. The Deluge from a Promethean game is the result of of the Firestorm to end all firestorms. In a Changeling game the Deluge contains the last of the Hedge's thorns when Arcadia cut all ties with Earth. With a Leviathan crossover the Rift and the Deluge have become one and the same, only as the ultimate end instead of the origin of primordial waters. And Princess could have the Second Fall, with Darkness having taken all of the world and not just the former kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Dealing with other Supernatural figures will be harder than dealing with humanity. As they are no longer mortal they don't fit as easily in the conflict of Nature and Civilization. But they have their own influence on the conflict, however realized, much as Sirens can be both preventers and instigators to changing trends.<br /> <br /> This is decidedly more of a thematic problem, one to shape the entire scope of your Chronicle. Thankfully when it comes to the mechanics of Crossovers that becomes very easy with the applications of the Opuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:28:09-07:00","id":993839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993744#post993744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ascended and Descended forms for Sirens are sounding top notch. It seems like Siren consistently finds the cream of the crop amongst similar mechanics and systems to bring the best all into one game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993744#post993744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it gets to the Crossover conversation, there was one point I wanted to address first. Siren presents a particular platform to make or break a crossover and storytellers will want to think twice about what game lines they chose to include, whether Siren is the sole focus or part of the ancillary background.<br /> <br /> In short, when working with Siren in a crossover setting it is the ultimate exercise of conversation of detail. Consider that the sister venue paired with Siren will play a part in the Deluge. If Sirens are the muses, oracles, and stand-takers of the conflict between Civilization and Nature, another society of supernatural figures will have their own impact on both and thus a massive impact on the Deluge.<br /> <br /> Although the Delgue has no Twilight and no connection to other realms, its cataclysms in a crossover venture should hint to where these realms originally were. The cataclysm is decidedly supernatural in origin but should still be shaped by how that venue interacts with both Civilization and Nature. Entering the Deluge of a Geist game reveals a dead sea where the dead of the Underworld have been spat out. The Deluge from a Promethean game is the result of of the Firestorm to end all firestorms. In a Changeling game the Deluge contains the last of the Hedge's thorns when Arcadia cut all ties with Earth. With a Leviathan crossover the Rift and the Deluge have become one and the same, only as the ultimate end instead of the origin of primordial waters. And Princess could have the Second Fall, with Darkness having taken all of the world and not just the former kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Dealing with other Supernatural figures will be harder than dealing with humanity. As they are no longer mortal they don't fit as easily in the conflict of Nature and Civilization. But they have their own influence on the conflict, however realized, much as Sirens can be both preventers and instigators to changing trends.<br /> <br /> This is decidedly more of a thematic problem, one to shape the entire scope of your Chronicle. Thankfully when it comes to the mechanics of Crossovers that becomes very easy with the applications of the Opuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Just to be clear, adding in supernatural events to the Deluge is probably a good idea or else it will alienate them from Siren's premise? Is it also alright if I used your text you put down for a Crossovers document perhaps? It sounds like perfect wording for one (at least for a section describing the Deluge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T20:58:07-07:00","id":993871,"title":"","content":"Feel free to use anything of mine for your Crossover appendix! I'm sure that's where a lot of my future commentary will go since Crossover as a use of compare/contrast for game themes is a favorite of mine, and a part for my own crossover heavy Princess game.<br /> <br /> The main thing when having another venue with your Siren game is the consideration of how other supernatural forces will play a part in the 'End of the World As We Know It.' How they compare to Sirens isn't the only focus, it's how the other Supernaturals might/do bring the world to its doom. How this occurs fits the importance of the mixed setting on your Chronicle. Other Supernaturals don't have to be at fault directly, a cataclysm could come from either Civilization (&quot;humanity's full uprising against their leaching from Vampires, or forced history by Geniuses&quot;) or Nature (&quot;out-evolving the need of Werewolves, or erasing the long geographies of Mummies or Leviathan&quot;).<br /> <br /> I'm sure how another kind of Supernatural views their mythos would shade their perspective of a passenger visit into the Celestial Sea. It brings a mix of potential interactions from Sirens trying to gain allies into incomprehensible matters, trying to convince big shakers and movers of the consequences of their folly, or as outright antagonists if a group is extremist/self-justified enough it causes catastrophic ripples in the Deluge.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the Crossover section (which may end up like a small-upcoming-Chronicles book) there could be a template of how another game's themes compare to Siren, suggestions for how their presence would influence the Deluge, and a reciprocal look as how that venue would view Sirens. This would be bridged with what kinds of Waters and Currents associate with both the good and the bad of that venue, although need not be as specific as direct faction to faction equation.<br /> <br /> There are game lines I haven't perused as greatly, so there will still be a need for various contributors. Those write ups could get lengthy so since I just found a scribbled list I wanted to switch to Opus crossover.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Much like Mage Arcana, the Opuses offer direct integration for Sirens into the abilities of various other venues. Ideally you would have 1 Opus represent each venue, although there is some overlap and some may require the joint of 2 Opuses, but no more. A few were already suggested in the Opus list and some come naturally:<ul><li>Opus of Blood for Vampire</li> <li>Opus of Spirit for Werewolf and Spirits</li> <li>Opus of Fate for Changeling</li> <li>Opus of Human for Hunter/Mortal+</li> <li>Opus of Death for Sin-Eaters and Ghosts</li> </ul><br /> Now these are some official game lines that are difficult to peg into one Opus:<ul><li>Mage is a bit of a sticking point. The Arcana and Opus have their counterparts easily enough, but what single Opus represents the 'identity' of a Mage, an awakened being and the perception of Supernal Truth?</li> <li>Promethean shares an aspect of Death but with 2E's broadened emphasis even never formerly living Created are available. The character struggles of Promethean suggest Growth or Humanity as well.</li> <li>Demons and Angels could play into the Technology of the God-Machine, to really play up the machine aspects, yet its occult matrixes and bizarre classification of infrastructure at times bleeds into other Opuses, although I can't put my finger on which.</li> <li>Mummy is quite tricky, although Death is a likely aspect for the Arisen's condition. The rites and legacies of the Nameless Empire, the timeless aspects of this early culture that persist to this day, do not readily identify amongst the current Opuses.</li> <li>For Beast I am split on a mix of Passion and Darkness, for the Hungers/Horrors and self explanatory reference to primordial nightmares. There isn't exactly a 'Dreaming' Opus which could have been another thread of rationale</li> <li>We don't know enough about Deviant to give it a good Opus range, as the types of suggested Renegades are quite varied. Deviants are caused, most consistently, by humans preying upon and experimenting on others, the Remade aspect fitting both Flenser and Echidna's themes to some degree.</li> </ul><br /> And these are some fan lines I favor, with some easy and some harder to place due to early development or broad aspects:<ul><li>Opus of Technology for Genius</li> <li>Opus of Light for Princess. Their opposite, the Outer Darkness, works with both Darkness and Taint</li> <li>Opus of Pressure for Leviathan. Runner up, Chaos.</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?585862-necro-nWoD-Janus-the-Persona\" target=\"_blank\">Janus: the Persona</a> is a favorite of mine from RPG.net, an alpha-build about people whose personalities become so broken they split into their Shadow, the psychological 'other you' that acts on worse impulses. Your own enemy is yourself. However it is a very insular focused game which doesn't suggest much on the Crossover crisis spectrum. Possible aspects include Human, Darkness and Chaos</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat\">Demigod: the Empyrean</a> shares a bit of the Mage problem, as its Domains as as counterpart varied as the Opuses that their single identity is hard to grasp. You could argue Light as well, since a 'Divine' Opus doesn't exist.</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\">Monarch: the Endless</a> has the PCs as (semi)reluctant leaders of an alien hive mind. It's current trend is towards an interesting nuance of both Nature and Civilization as the Endless are the epitome of the problems you get from evasive species. A possible unifying aspect could be Growth.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T23:07:37-07:00","id":993911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993871#post993871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel free to use anything of mine for your Crossover appendix! I'm sure that's where a lot of my future commentary will go since Crossover as a use of compare/contrast for game themes is a favorite of mine, and a part for my own crossover heavy Princess game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And now the Crossovers Section is born!<br /> <br /> <b>Crossovers with Siren: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_vK6C6vfoUa9HS9Uc0Uz0jRotgDjHXXvlLBp6fKS2h8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993871#post993871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing when having another venue with your Siren game is the consideration of how other supernatural forces will play a part in the 'End of the World As We Know It.' How they compare to Sirens isn't the only focus, it's how the other Supernaturals might/do bring the world to its doom. How this occurs fits the importance of the mixed setting on your Chronicle. Other Supernaturals don't have to be at fault directly, a cataclysm could come from either Civilization (&quot;humanity's full uprising against their leaching from Vampires, or forced history by Geniuses&quot;) or Nature (&quot;out-evolving the need of Werewolves, or erasing the long geographies of Mummies or Leviathan&quot;).<br /> <br /> I'm sure how another kind of Supernatural views their mythos would shade their perspective of a passenger visit into the Celestial Sea. It brings a mix of potential interactions from Sirens trying to gain allies into incomprehensible matters, trying to convince big shakers and movers of the consequences of their folly, or as outright antagonists if a group is extremist/self-justified enough it causes catastrophic ripples in the Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993871#post993871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Crossover section (which may end up like a small-upcoming-Chronicles book) there could be a template of how another game's themes compare to Siren, suggestions for how their presence would influence the Deluge, and a reciprocal look as how that venue would view Sirens. This would be bridged with what kinds of Waters and Currents associate with both the good and the bad of that venue, although need not be as specific as direct faction to faction equation.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I was going to use this as abit of a reference for at least tackling specific supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/Crossovers\" target=\"_blank\">http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/Crossovers</a><br /> <br /> Pretty much, a paragraph or two describing the relationship between the Siren and the specified other supernatural type, and a paragraph describing some special mechanics when it comes to certain things between the splats. Such as how would Pneuma feeding go when feeding from a Vampire's dead soul? Or from a Promethean's still forming one? How much more Glamour would Changelings get if they were feeding from a Siren's Love or a Fury's Hate? How would a Wasteland, a Taint and a Quagmire mash up together?<br /> <br /> Right off the top of my head, I imagine given the revised Refraction (that deprives Sirens of a Masquerade, meaning they have to enforce it themselves, I sorta revised the Culture bit in the Introduction without saying anything on it) rules, Celestial Sirens may find themselves allying with Vampires more than they like to when it comes to protecting the masquerade. I imagine Sirens and Vampires would actually have alot to bond over. Namely, long lives, a need for feeding from humans (feeding from their blood and soul respectively) and a co-dependent relationship with human society. Although at the same time, I imagine most Sirens wouldn't get along with Vampires. Vampires can create bonds of artificial love that they freely abuse, corrupt the society around them to serve themselves and feed off of it more for selfish reasons. Sirens (at least the Celestial Ones) wouldn't be able to stand mistreatment of love and the Vampires also just as easily could be enemies of the progression that Sirens try to do. The Abyssal Currents on the other hand have more cordial relations. Acheron would get along great with VII and the Strix, Cocytus would be interested in the lore of the factions (namely Ordo Dracul, Lancea Sanctum and Circle of the Crone), Lethe would most likely have investors from the Invictus, Phlegethon wouldn't care about how vampires do their things and Styx would most likely kill them as &quot;unholy abominations backing the Flensers&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993871#post993871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are game lines I haven't perused as greatly, so there will still be a need for various contributors. Those write ups could get lengthy so since I just found a scribbled list I wanted to switch to Opus crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I can help with that. I would like to note that it's possible to use more than one Opus to specify a Splat. The outstanding examples I can think of are Death + Blood for Vampires, Spirit+Human+Animal for Werewolves and the like.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=-metablender;n993871]Much like Mage Arcana, the Opuses offer direct integration for Sirens into the abilities of various other venues. Ideally you would have 1 Opus represent each venue, although there is some overlap and some may require the joint of 2 Opuses, but no more. A few were already suggested in the Opus list and some come naturally:<ul><li>Opus of Blood for Vampire</li> <li>Opus of Spirit for Werewolf and Spirits</li> <li>Opus of Fate for Changeling</li> <li>Opus of Human for Hunter/Mortal+</li> <li>Opus of Death for Sin-Eaters and Ghosts</li> </ul><br /> <br /> These are good. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993871#post993871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now these are some official game lines that are difficult to peg into one Opus:<ul><li>Mage is a bit of a sticking point. The Arcana and Opus have their counterparts easily enough, but what single Opus represents the 'identity' of a Mage, an awakened being and the perception of Supernal Truth?</li> <li>Promethean shares an aspect of Death but with 2E's broadened emphasis even never formerly living Created are available. The character struggles of Promethean suggest Growth or Humanity as well.</li> <li>Demons and Angels could play into the Technology of the God-Machine, to really play up the machine aspects, yet its occult matrixes and bizarre classification of infrastructure at times bleeds into other Opuses, although I can't put my finger on which.</li> <li>Mummy is quite tricky, although Death is a likely aspect for the Arisen's condition. The rites and legacies of the Nameless Empire, the timeless aspects of this early culture that persist to this day, do not readily identify amongst the current Opuses.</li> <li>For Beast I am split on a mix of Passion and Darkness, for the Hungers/Horrors and self explanatory reference to primordial nightmares. There isn't exactly a 'Dreaming' Opus which could have been another thread of rationale</li> <li>We don't know enough about Deviant to give it a good Opus range, as the types of suggested Renegades are quite varied. Deviants are caused, most consistently, by humans preying upon and experimenting on others, the Remade aspect fitting both Flenser and Echidna's themes to some degree.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand on the Dream Opus idea. I should prolly make more Opuses to account for this. Otherwise, I feel this opus is good for Mages and Beasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Dream</b><br /> Dreams are the enlightenment of the mind, the windows to the world entirely your own. Well, at least most of the time.<br /> <b>Physically:</b> Messing with the beings found in the Astral Space.<br /> <b>Conceptually: </b>The act of bringing enlightenment to others or renewing beliefs. May also introduce things impossible to bring to reality (such as making a four walled house with all sides pointing North on the North Pole).<br /> <br /> This way, Human+Dream can represent Mages, and Darkness+Dream+Passion can represent Beasts. I would put Spirit+Technology for Demons/Angels (They start off as Ephemeral Beings at least). As for Mummies, from what I've read on TvTropes they're actually tied pretty tightly to Fate (at least, the enemy splat of Mummies are), so Death+Fate comes to mind for them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993871#post993871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And these are some fan lines I favor, with some easy and some harder to place due to early development or broad aspects:<ul><li>Opus of Technology for Genius</li> <li>Opus of Light for Princess. Their opposite, the Outer Darkness, works with both Darkness and Taint</li> <li>Opus of Pressure for Leviathan. Runner up, Chaos.</li> <li><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?585862-necro-nWoD-Janus-the-Persona\" target=\"_blank\">Janus: the Persona</a> is a favorite of mine from RPG.net, an alpha-build about people whose personalities become so broken they split into their Shadow, the psychological 'other you' that acts on worse impulses. Your own enemy is yourself. However it is a very insular focused game which doesn't suggest much on the Crossover crisis spectrum. Possible aspects include Human, Darkness and Chaos</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat\">Demigod: the Empyrean</a> shares a bit of the Mage problem, as its Domains as as counterpart varied as the Opuses that their single identity is hard to grasp. You could argue Light as well, since a 'Divine' Opus doesn't exist.</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\">Monarch: the Endless</a> has the PCs as (semi)reluctant leaders of an alien hive mind. It's current trend is towards an interesting nuance of both Nature and Civilization as the Endless are the epitome of the problems you get from evasive species. A possible unifying aspect could be Growth.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest Technology+Chaos for Genius, mainly because they don't have much control on their Wonders and they fall apart from human eyes. That and Chaos accounts for their insanity too. I would suggest Light+Passion for Princesses, since they get their powers from their emotions and the Light. As for Darkness, what you said sounds good. I would say Water+Chaos+Pressure for Leviathans. Ironically, I imagine the same opuses would be used to create a <i>Tempest.</i>(Sorry, the pun was begging me to make it.)<br /> <br /> As for Demigods, given how Domains seem to be akin to Influences (I do remember some fluff text saying that Domains have as many areas of coverage as Influences do). Due to this, I would suggest Human+Light+Spirit for the Demigods. Or perhaps Temper in place of Spirit. Taint could work as a sort of &quot;damnation&quot;/&quot;infernal&quot; Opus due to it's Conceptualization of Corruption and Temper could work as a &quot;divine&quot;/&quot;Heavenly&quot; opus for it's Conceptualization as &quot;making things better&quot;. <br /> <br /> As for Monarch, I feel abit ashamed to say that I haven't been paying attention to it. My only complaint is that there isn't a sort of compilation for the ideas (like in a google docs or the like). But otherwise, from what little I do know, I like the general concept of it and I do feel that Growth as an Opus would fit for them. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T21:32:42-07:00","id":994398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=993911#post993911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand on the Dream Opus idea. I should prolly make more Opuses to account for this. Otherwise, I feel this opus is good for Mages and Beasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Dream</b><br /> Dreams are the enlightenment of the mind, the windows to the world entirely your own. Well, at least most of the time.<br /> <b>Physically:</b> Messing with the beings found in the Astral Space.<br /> <b>Conceptually: </b>The act of bringing enlightenment to others or renewing beliefs. May also introduce things impossible to bring to reality (such as making a four walled house with all sides pointing North on the North Pole).</div> </div> </div> </div>It pleases me greatly to see a Dream Opus included, I was about to ask which Opus or set of Opuses you would consider to use with Travel to traverse dreams or Control to shape them, amongst other Conclusions. The use of collective dreams is one of my favorite aspects for storytelling with my game, and can bridge titles like Changeling, Beast and Mage with fan splats like Princess, Leviathan and Janus. It also fits in that the Opus is not one normally in the the common Siren's expertise, as it isn't favored by any Waters. I believe the Deluge and Spirit Opuses share this 'category' as well.<br /> <br /> Given how creatively you can use Opuses, you can typically use more than the suggested ones to influence each other venue, although keeping a simple pairing helps in bookkeeping. I shared the thought of combining Spirit + Technology for D-M/Angels/Demons, given Essence is primarily used by the first two and the 'Ghost in the Machine' aspect of the G-M. Temper sounds very fitting for Demigod, as divine beings are known for the legendary 'temper tantrums' in various myths.<br /> <br /> What is the main benefit for using multiple Opuses in a Verse again? It's looking like a main pair of 2 Opuses would be the best for noting crossover mechanics with another venue, although as said plenty of others could be used creatively.<br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> For the Crossovers, here's my early draft for the Princess: the Hopeful article;<br /> <br /> <u><b>Princess: the Hopeful</b></u><br /> <br /> <u>Overview:</u> Perhaps no other Supernatural being resonates as strongly with Sirens as the Princesses and Princes of the Light (the Nobility) for there are many similarities between the two. Both experience a pivotal stress in their life that brings them awareness of a great universal conflict beyond themselves. Where Sirens must find balance amongst Nature and Civilization after their Drowning, Princesses find themselves on the side of the Light against the entropic Darkness that degrades humanity. Being the paragons of humanity's best qualities, Princesses can become staunch allies for matters relating to Civilization. Although followers of the Queen of Clubs are as attuned to Nature as many Sirens. Princesses draw their power from within and their relationships with others, much like Sirens.<br /> <br /> Yet for their common bonds this does not mean Princesses and Sirens are automatic BFF 'besties.' Their respective conflicts run perpendicular to each other. For the majority of Nature minded Sirens they can find gripes with the reciprocal lack of conservational minded Nobility. Sirens often intuit their way through issues with little concern for ancillary matters, for the Deluge is a sign of what little time remains to prevent a disaster. Although they can be just as impassioned Princesses are more social and nostalgic agents, needing to confer with their Queens, fellow Nobility and others to determine the best course of action. As Princesses naturally cling to their humanity this can cause discord with Sirens who have lessened this emphasis in their mission.<br /> <br /> <u>Princess Perspective:</u> For those that study the countries from before the Fall, Princess scholars wonder if Ceto is herself a former Queen who went on to embody the aspect of the Song. This simple theory is complicated by the twisty bends of Siren 'history.' Ceto is both an actor in the creation myth and the 'first' great cataclysm that brought the Deluge and the need to send Sirens to warn the world of impending doom.<br /> <br /> Regardless, a Princess who befriends a Siren finds a complimentary partner to tackle both of their campaigns. Although originally an Embassy for exploration and world travel, the Embassy to the Ocean makes a Princess as close to a Siren as possible. The signature 'mermaid form' that is added to the Princess's Magical Self is all but a Diluvian form in name. The Embassy offers no further synergy with Siren: the Drowning, although it's the easiest for helping the Princess keep up with a Siren in an aquatic environment.<br /> <br /> <u>Antagonists:</u> Sirens that learn of the differences between the Radiant and Twilight Queens see a mirror with the Celestial and Abyssal Currents. All are sides in the same conflict with very different methodologies. There is nothing that suggests Twilight Princesses and Abyssal Sirens will find common ground, same as other pairings, as the Fallen Nobility are set against the Darkness primarily. Uneasy alliances may crop up from time to time, likely brief, between the agents of the Twilight Queens and the Sirens foes.<br /> <br /> <u>Waters and Currents:</u> many Siren splats find their counterpart in Princess. Of note Sirens from Freshwater are the most attuned to humanity and are the first to note the Blossomings and activities of a Princess. Tropicana empathizes with the ruling energies of emotions and self belief Princesses draw from. For Currents, Healing and Harmony find common ground with many Princesses, while Buoyancy connects with the the freeing and inspired aspects of Light's Nobility.<br /> <br /> <u>Suggested Opuses:</u> Light, Passion, Dream<br /> <br /> <u>Mechanics:</u> When a Princess would gain a Wisp from a significant relationship, it can be offered to a Siren as a point of Pneuma if they are in the same scene. This requires the Princess's consent, otherwise the Siren would have to devise a Verse to leech off the emotive speck of power. Alternatively, Princesses in the Embassy to the Ocean may use the Mermaid's Kiss benefit to offer the spent Wisp as a Pneuma.<br /> <br /> <u>Cataclysm: The Outer Darkness</u><br /> <br /> The Darkness inflicts wounds on the world and its peoples just as any other Quagmire. Indeed a Tainted Place is much like a Quagmire, although it only connects to the Dark World and its abominations. As the Creatures of Darkness destroy both Nature and Civilization alike Sirens sometimes come into conflict with these areas.<br /> <br /> In the Deluge marked by the stain of the Outer Darkness it is the aftermath of the second Fall. The world has been devastated from the attack of dark forces, leaving lightless ruins and freezing void as large wounds on the Earth. Between flow that is more ink than water are survivors that are even more depraved that accustomed, given into vices and lashing out at each other as well as outsiders. The very light of the world, it's last hope, has been snuffed out.<br /> <br /> What's worse is the great roving storm, a radioactive cloud front of searing green fire from the heavens that will still blight the remains of the Darkness. Unlike the apotheosis Queen of Storms, her Princesses would find no sentience in this Deluge cataclysm, no swirl of ever fighting souls. Unlike Echidna, no sapience of the Queen's form appears to have survived entry into the drowned planet.<br /> <br /> In the Deluge, these environments pertain to Polaria and Discordia Waters respectively.<br /> <br /> <u>Suggested Opuses:</u> Darkness, Taint, Chaos<br /> <br /> <u>Antagonists:</u> Abyssal Currents may find poaching a Creature of Darkness for their particular goals to be a useful strategy. Echidna sometimes gains curiosity towards the Darkened, Darkspawn, Mnemosyne and Cataphractoi to transfer their Umbrae and Calignes as adaptations for her Vodinaoi. However, there is little human or natural about the latter three Creatures of Darkness. Flensers find the Darkness objectionable towards the progression of humanity.<br /> <br /> Most tellingly, Darkspawn and their Taint are some of the worse sins against Nature in the mind of a Quagmire, as much of the Darkness is formed from humanity's worst traits.<br /> <br /> <u>Mechanics:</u> When a Quagmire and a Tainted Place would butt boundaries, compare the Resentment and Severity of each. Roll these numbers as a dice pool and whichever side gets more successes begins eating away at the other, taking over its space. The transfer of Resentment or Severity occurs every 12 hours, this time is halved for each further transgression committed in the area. The dominating side gains access to the other's curses. Furies treat a source of Tainted Darkness as Pollution when crafting their Vessels. Otherwise Darkspawn and Furies do not gain access to each other's abilities.<br /> <br /> <u>Cataclysm: The Searing Light</u><br /> <br /> They say the road to hell is paved with good intentions. Within the chronicles of a world filled with darkness, aren't the paragons of the Light good for changing the course of this wretched world?<br /> <br /> That's what one would think. Although the Deluge filled to the brim with searing light raises many uncomfortable questions. It is a light that blinds. It is a light that burns. It is a light that has shown every ugly truth of the past world yet has not been able to better it. When not in a blinding patch the waters of the Deluge are crystal clear. Survivors are friendly and pleasant, not always for the benefits from lending a helping hand. There's a palpable fear, a sense of being judged. Anything deemed dark and wrong is eaten away, scorched from the inside out. In the battle of Light and Darkness the light has upended it's lifelong foe. Yet this has not brought peace, prosperity or contentment.<br /> <br /> For Sirens privy to this warning from the Deluge it paints a degree of questionableness to the Nobility. And the origin of this cataclysm is not obvious. Is this the true result of the Outer Darkness's final defeat? Has the hidden Queen of Mirrors unleashed her ultimate agenda with the True Heir? Or has something happened to the Radiant Queens, worse than their complacency that gave rise to the first Fall enacted by the Darkness? May-haps the Twilight Queens can count more amongst their Fallen number.<br /> <br /> In the Deluge, this searing environment pertains to the Tropicana Water. Clearer, more populated areas correspond with Freshwater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T06:55:45-07:00","id":994542,"title":"","content":"Question, what do sirens actually do? Are they just doing ecoterrorism 24/7?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:35:07-07:00","id":995018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=994398#post994398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It pleases me greatly to see a Dream Opus included, I was about to ask which Opus or set of Opuses you would consider to use with Travel to traverse dreams or Control to shape them, amongst other Conclusions. The use of collective dreams is one of my favorite aspects for storytelling with my game, and can bridge titles like Changeling, Beast and Mage with fan splats like Princess, Leviathan and Janus. It also fits in that the Opus is not one normally in the the common Siren's expertise, as it isn't favored by any Waters. I believe the Deluge and Spirit Opuses share this 'category' as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy it's pleasing. :3<br /> <br /> As for an Opus not in a common Siren's Expertise, there is techically 3 Opuses that are favored by all Sirens. Water, Sound and Beauty. I'm now wondering if I should put the Deluge amongst those Opuses, it feels weird to not be amongst the most favored ones. Speaking of which, I'm thinking of adding more Opuses that aren't favored. How do these sound?<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lighting</i></b><br /> Lightning is the light humanity has captured through technology to serve their purposes, as well as the element of enlightenment and madness.<br /> <b>Physically: </b>Manipulating lightning and electricity from any source.<br /> <b>Conceptually: </b>May entice revelations or enlightenment within people. (Isn't required to be good ones, and is also based on a Buddhist saying on Lightning being connected to enlightenment)<br /> <br /> <b><i>Metal</i></b><br /> Metal is the riches found in the earth's crust that man has turned to Civilization's foundations.<br /> <b>Physically:</b> Manipulating all kinds of metals.<br /> <b>Conceptually:</b> Making circumstances and events more resilient to change, even to the point of sterility.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Time</i></b><br /> Time is the element that only mankind cares to keep track of, that eternally runs out until the day of the Deluge.<br /> <b>Physically: </b>Manipulation of time. Freezing, slowing, or speeding up time are all possible. Going to alternate timelines however isn't possible.<br /> <b>Conceptually: </b>Manipulating the perception of time, such as time flying when having fun or going slower when being bored.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: Self-Time-Travel?</b><br /> It would be inevitable that a question would be asked along the lines of &quot;Can a Verse using the Time Opus and Travel Conclusion be able to travel through time?&quot;.<br /> The simple answer is &quot;No&quot;. Mostly to avoid the problems that come with Time Travel and that Sirens already can mess with temporal events without it through their Traces. Instead, Using a Time-Travel Conclusion allows for a Siren to achieve extra actions upon her rolls. For each dot in the Travel Conclusion in a Time-Travel Verse, the Siren may have a number of extra actions equals to the dots. For example, a Siren who uses Self-Time-Travel 3 can have three extra actions through a turn. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=994398#post994398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how creatively you can use Opuses, you can typically use more than the suggested ones to influence each other venue, although keeping a simple pairing helps in bookkeeping. I shared the thought of combining Spirit + Technology for D-M/Angels/Demons, given Essence is primarily used by the first two and the 'Ghost in the Machine' aspect of the G-M. Temper sounds very fitting for Demigod, as divine beings are known for the legendary 'temper tantrums' in various myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=994398#post994398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the main benefit for using multiple Opuses in a Verse again? It's looking like a main pair of 2 Opuses would be the best for noting crossover mechanics with another venue, although as said plenty of others could be used creatively.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main benefit for using more than one Opus in a verse is to be able to be more specific with the Verse's effect for what she wants it to do. For example, let's go with Location-Weather-Invoke. A Siren could call up clouds or make them go away, but that's all she can do with only Weather. If she adds in the Water Opus (Location-Weather-Water-Invoke), then the Siren can call up a rainstorm. If she added in one more Opus (Location-Weather-Water-Freeze-Invoke), then she can make it into Sleet or a Hailstorm. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=994398#post994398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Crossovers, here's my early draft for the Princess: the Hopeful article;<br /> <br /> *HUGE SNIP OH MY GOD YOU ARE A GOD METABLENDER <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />*</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe my words in the snip say how I feel on this. You did a perfect job on this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And if it's fine, I'll be using it as a reference of how to make the Crossover overviews. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=994542#post994542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, what do sirens actually do? Are they just doing ecoterrorism 24/7?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Siren's are not ecoterrorists (that archetype is mainly the Styx Abyssal Current who want to wipe out civilization for nature to thrive). They're meant to serve as guides for the world, keeping it alive and healthy. They've seen the end of the world first hand, and while they do not know what causes it, they do know that it could happen for multitudes of reasons (financial collapse leading to World War 3, extreme climate change, forces beyond human control that could ruin everything). <br /> <br /> So for this reason, I would say that Sirens do &quot;maintenence work for existence&quot;. They try to make sure things keep running as they should, or upgrade/downgrade things when it's called for. The themes of love also play into Siren as love is a huge motivator to keep things strong and alive. <br /> <br /> Celestial Sirens are perhaps the most involved in the &quot;maintenence work&quot; aspect. I should note that Sirens AREN'T required to take up jobs purely dealing with naturalism and the growth of civilization in ways that harm the environment less. I imagine some could play in politics as an attempt to maintain power in a region (be it city, country, or even nation) or make sure that chains of a food market stay afloat so millions of families could still maintain their jobs. And given the reworked Trace mechanics, Sirens don't even have to &quot;infiltrate&quot; the workplace to get changes done, they could get all the info they need on a problem, manipulate events with verses from afar and the like. <br /> <br /> Abyssal Sirens however have different takes on the &quot;maintenence work&quot; aspect, namely by disregarding one or many aspects. Acheron believes the &quot;machine&quot; (for anyone reading, do note I'm not referring to the God Machine here, just a metaphor for &quot;the function&quot;) of existence is broken and it's easier to break it apart and try to start anew. Cocytus believes that there can be improvement found, but that they may need to &quot;grease the gears&quot; with blood/pain to get anywhere (an extra oomph from their dark secrets). Lethe believes that nature is unnecessary and human life would be easier if they just reaped all the hidden treasures of nature and destroyed it. Oceanus believes that the &quot;machine&quot; is doomed to failure and that it's easier to simply upgrade the few parts that can work independently of it (humanity in this case). Phlegethon flatly disregards any thoughts towards maintenence work and would rather do whatever they pleased. Finally, Styx is kinda like you said, &quot;Ecoterrorism 24/7&quot;. They think that humanity's the problem of the earth and seek to annihilate all traces of their existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:17:06-07:00","id":995041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995018#post995018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Siren's are not ecoterrorists (that archetype is mainly the Styx Abyssal Current who want to wipe out civilization for nature to thrive). They're meant to serve as guides for the world, keeping it alive and healthy. They've seen the end of the world first hand, and while they do not know what causes it, they do know that it could happen for multitudes of reasons (financial collapse leading to World War 3, extreme climate change, forces beyond human control that could ruin everything).<br /> <br /> So for this reason, I would say that Sirens do &quot;maintenence work for existence&quot;. They try to make sure things keep running as they should, or upgrade/downgrade things when it's called for. The themes of love also play into Siren as love is a huge motivator to keep things strong and alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. So what do they actually do in a session though? Those sort of things don't really sound dramatic enough for a campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T21:55:43-07:00","id":995073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995041#post995041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So what do they actually do in a session though? Those sort of things don't really sound dramatic enough for a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see. For starters, there's the whole &quot;maintenence work&quot;, which involves keeping existence as we know it from taking more steps over the edge into the Deluge. This mainly takes the form of dealing with major events, or forseeing major events and taking steps to prevent, brace for it or to set them into motion. I would expect that a Siren game would involve messing with meaningful events, trying to ensure that there isn't a single step taken towards the Deluge or the like. I know it sounds bland stating them as in the general &quot;Events&quot; bit, but please stick with me on this. The reason I term them in a general format is because all events have their choices and consequences associate them, and Sirens (with their powers of Trace and Verses) can easily stick their foot into the door of many events if they use the right powers.<br /> <br /> For example, if a Siren foresaw that Caesar was about to be murdered, they may try looking through alternate routes, seeing who or what would play in the murder, how it would be like if he wasn't murdered, and making important decisions that could cost lives. What if she had to let Brutus and Cassius (or heck, what if she planted the seeds into their heads of) killing Caesar because she saw him becoming a ruthless dictator? To be honest, I think it's common for a Siren to come across problems where she'll have to make important decisions and weigh the consequences of her decisions. I also imagine Sirens fighting over how to tackle issues, such as the Current of Conflict's heart on sleeve attitudes would make the Current of Wisdom to try and stall them to implement their own solution. <br /> <br /> For another thing, there's the aspect of Love. All Sirens have to deal with humanity in some way, shape or fashion. If it's not the nature of their powers, then it's through the nature of the Song compelling them to. There's plenty of drama to be found in maintaining a social and/or love life. Of course, with most humans having an integrity system and that seeing something supernatural is a breaking point, think of how screwed up a Siren's life could become if those she interacted with knew she was a monster? How would the Siren react if those she loved shunned her? Will her ending be the same as the Little Mermaid? This attempt at keeping those they love alive, and keeping their dirty secrets is how I imagine a Siren could get drama in.<br /> <br /> And that's just some ideas off the top of my head; Siren is very flexible in what kind of scenarios they can get involved in, what goals to pursue and what methods to use to go about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T22:14:12-07:00","id":995077,"title":"","content":"When you described Siren to me in the past Saulot, I was stricken by the beauty of the premise: someone at the end of time gets swept up in the tsunami of the apocalypse and is set adrift in the sea of time--for time is not a river but a sea at storm.<br /> <br /> I was naturally drawn to the conclusion that the Siren are those who learn to swim in this sea and thus can travel from their present &quot;the end of days&quot; to the past in an effort to change the future. Perhaps a more active role in that regard is called for?<br /> Rather, I mean that perhaps a Siren must go to the apocalyptic future on a regular basis to research what went wrong (as events are already in play there) and then swim back to the past to attempt to avert those wrongs. Their own actions could wildly change the world they came from (and are no longer part of, having been dragged out by the tide) and perhaps cause them to become lost at sea, no longer able to perceive the apocalypse because they've averted it... in their lifetime, at least.<br /> <br /> In that regard, some of the torment your monsters might suffer could come from seeking relationships with humans only to learn those particular humans are key to averting the cataclysm and must instead be preserved... or worse, learning they are the cause and must be destroyed (Sing Odysseus's crew into the rocks, as it were).<br /> <br /> I dunno, it'd certainly be unique if each session of your game involved taking action both in the (Siren's) present [The apocalypse] and the past [Modern Chronicle Nights].<br /> <br /> EDIT: Essentially, Chrono Trigger + Dark Cloud 2, with a more sinister thematic coloration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T23:45:47-07:00","id":995099,"title":"","content":"As for the other new Opuses they are looking good. I remember that Sound, Beauty and Water are universally favored. My earlier comment was that it was good that there are some Opuses that aren't really favored by any Waters as they extend to concepts not inherent to the Sirens usual expertise. And with so many Opuses (24+3+?) there's a point where the concepts become esoteric enough that they are harder to learn although the Song ripples through each of them.<br /> <br /> Spirit is a prime example, as while Polaria reflects on Death as a passing none looked attuned to the amortal animistic spirit world. Dream would likely follow. My read on Deluge is that while its something all Sirens experience, it's not really their 'birthright' or domain that exists only because there are Sirens in the world. The Deluge is the end-stop of all futures however climatic. Plus there's more of an in character reasoning, as I imagine Verses done on Earth trying to use the Deluge would be difficult to bridge the future with the past. Although that really depends on the Introduction and Conclusion.<br /> <br /> Would there be favored Opuses swapped out with the newer ones? There's kind of a nice pattern with 3 universal Opuses, 3 favored per water and 3-ish or more that aren't. And making a new pattern would require upping things to 4 and finding many more Opuses. This extends to a clarification I wanted to ask about. At character creation, does a Siren only start with her Water's Opuses? Or could they be traded with the Universal ones, which are favored but are implied to only be available with post-creation experience.<br /> <br /> That being said, Time as an Opus sounds like a step backwards. In particular that it brings up the timey-whimey question again of how much time travel Sirens can or can't do outside of journeying the Deluge. And unlike other Opuses it has an immediate exception to how certain Verse components are used, like Self and Travel, ones that other Opuses do not have in these groupings. The criteria of Introductions and Conclusions are meant to apply consistent tiers of effects no matter the Opus. I think you could also get both aspects of Time from metaphorical application of Freeze and Temper (slow and haste, respectively). Let alone that Sirens already have a scouring of time with their Trace, and with the expanded Trace mechanics can retroactively use their Verses in situations where enough successes were applied that it allows for more controlled blatant time trickery. With all that a Time Opus seems redundant, even with the notion some Opuses have mild overlap.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head with the various Conclusions, Time is just too linear of a concept. All of the various Verses are only going to gain time or lose time with the only difference being how the same effect came about, leaving only the Introduction to alter target of effect in terms of Verse variability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T00:55:28-07:00","id":995109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995077#post995077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you described Siren to me in the past Saulot, I was stricken by the beauty of the premise: someone at the end of time gets swept up in the tsunami of the apocalypse and is set adrift in the sea of time--for time is not a river but a sea at storm.<br /> <br /> I was naturally drawn to the conclusion that the Siren are those who learn to swim in this sea and thus can travel from their present &quot;the end of days&quot; to the past in an effort to change the future. Perhaps a more active role in that regard is called for?<br /> Rather, I mean that perhaps a Siren must go to the apocalyptic future on a regular basis to research what went wrong (as events are already in play there) and then swim back to the past to attempt to avert those wrongs. Their own actions could wildly change the world they came from (and are no longer part of, having been dragged out by the tide) and perhaps cause them to become lost at sea, no longer able to perceive the apocalypse because they've averted it... in their lifetime, at least.<br /> <br /> In that regard, some of the torment your monsters might suffer could come from seeking relationships with humans only to learn those particular humans are key to averting the cataclysm and must instead be preserved... or worse, learning they are the cause and must be destroyed (Sing Odysseus's crew into the rocks, as it were).<br /> <br /> I dunno, it'd certainly be unique if each session of your game involved taking action both in the (Siren's) present [The apocalypse] and the past [Modern Chronicle Nights].<br /> <br /> EDIT: Essentially, Chrono Trigger + Dark Cloud 2, with a more sinister thematic coloration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, coming from the creator (or one of the most influential people) of Dragon the Embers, I feel really honored by your statement. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes, that is indeed one of the reasons for the Celestial Ocean. To be able to find ruins of old things and use Trace to read back into events that have &quot;already happened&quot; (in the purview of the Celestial Ocean but &quot;haven't happened yet&quot; for reality). And indeed, play within the Celestial Ocean is definitely something I'd like to encourage. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T01:02:22-07:00","id":995111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995099#post995099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the other new Opuses they are looking good. I remember that Sound, Beauty and Water are universally favored. My earlier comment was that it was good that there are some Opuses that aren't really favored by any Waters as they extend to concepts not inherent to the Sirens usual expertise. And with so many Opuses (24+3+?) there's a point where the concepts become esoteric enough that they are harder to learn although the Song ripples through each of them.<br /> <br /> Spirit is a prime example, as while Polaria reflects on Death as a passing none looked attuned to the amortal animistic spirit world. Dream would likely follow. My read on Deluge is that while its something all Sirens experience, it's not really their 'birthright' or domain that exists only because there are Sirens in the world. The Deluge is the end-stop of all futures however climatic. Plus there's more of an in character reasoning, as I imagine Verses done on Earth trying to use the Deluge would be difficult to bridge the future with the past. Although that really depends on the Introduction and Conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this reasoning. :3 Just to be clear, in your opinion it would be better if Deluge wasn't favored by all Sirens?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995099#post995099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would there be favored Opuses swapped out with the newer ones? There's kind of a nice pattern with 3 universal Opuses, 3 favored per water and 3-ish or more that aren't. And making a new pattern would require upping things to 4 and finding many more Opuses. This extends to a clarification I wanted to ask about. At character creation, does a Siren only start with her Water's Opuses? Or could they be traded with the Universal ones, which are favored but are implied to only be available with post-creation experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question! Indeed, I'll change it in character creation that a Siren can gain 3 Opuses for free, and they may be out of her water's favored or out of all Siren's Favored ones. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995099#post995099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, Time as an Opus sounds like a step backwards. In particular that it brings up the timey-whimey question again of how much time travel Sirens can or can't do outside of journeying the Deluge. And unlike other Opuses it has an immediate exception to how certain Verse components are used, like Self and Travel, ones that other Opuses do not have in these groupings. The criteria of Introductions and Conclusions are meant to apply consistent tiers of effects no matter the Opus. I think you could also get both aspects of Time from metaphorical application of Freeze and Temper (slow and haste, respectively). Let alone that Sirens already have a scouring of time with their Trace, and with the expanded Trace mechanics can retroactively use their Verses in situations where enough successes were applied that it allows for more controlled blatant time trickery. With all that a Time Opus seems redundant, even with the notion some Opuses have mild overlap.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head with the various Conclusions, Time is just too linear of a concept. All of the various Verses are only going to gain time or lose time with the only difference being how the same effect came about, leaving only the Introduction to alter target of effect in terms of Verse variability.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I think it would be simpler to just cut out the Time Opus then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:28:28-07:00","id":995647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995111#post995111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this reasoning. :3 Just to be clear, in your opinion it would be better if Deluge wasn't favored by all Sirens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that Deluge isn't part of the favored Opuses. It fits along the above thoughts of the Sirens being swept away in the apocalypses of the Deluge and being barely able to swim and avert the consequences of the Deluge from happening. That splinters into a few other ideas I've recently had for playing up the literal 'siren' definition as warning of future doom.<br /> <br /> The show Quantum Leap, although it sounds very much like a 'Demon' show with the Cover-like bodily occupation that Sam does, makes me think of how Sirens experience reemergence from the Deluge. They have limited time to avert disaster from happening and are likely in unfamiliar places with nary a clue or connection to the pending cataclysm in most cases. The major difference is that Sam has an ally from the future in the case of Al and the computer Ziggy to keep in touch with future events.<br /> <br /> Perhaps used sparingly, there could be a similar glimpse of the future without going to the full Deluge. At least in cases where a Siren is already dedicated towards preventing a set outcome. The use of the Sense Conclusion and Deluge Opus may fill this in regards to the Introduction setting the target of inquiry. Maybe when a Siren is experiencing a Malestrom it's like living out the disaster for her, having not only the evidence of her frenzy but a memory of the worsening outcome as well. Or an as of yet undetermined mechanic.<br /> <br /> Another idea is if the Siren had a Theron or Survivor companion that came to the present with them, said companion would 'update' their memories and maybe their abilities in regards to shifting cataclysms. All that has been said for certain is that Echidna is the only figure to live through the end of the Earth and remain in depths of the Celestial Sea regardless of its forms. There's no guarantee who else would survive the enacting of the Deluge but as lifeforms struggling after that time it's natural to think elements of their existence would change from a Siren's influence. This creates a new purpose for Theron/Survivor companions outside of the Deluge.<br /> <br /> <br /> Continuing from my question on favored Opuses, for the Double Dipping merit it grants the Siren the secondary Knowledges for Pneuma gain but doesn't count the Opuses as favored. Would a Siren with this merit count her second Water's Alterations as favored? I'd wager letting Alterations count if Opuses aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T18:43:32-07:00","id":995902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995647#post995647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that Deluge isn't part of the favored Opuses. It fits along the above thoughts of the Sirens being swept away in the apocalypses of the Deluge and being barely able to swim and avert the consequences of the Deluge from happening. That splinters into a few other ideas I've recently had for playing up the literal 'siren' definition as warning of future doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, listed and confirmed. :3 And recently I've been having the same thoughts on how Sirens also fit a tiny bit in the literal definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995647#post995647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The show Quantum Leap, although it sounds very much like a 'Demon' show with the Cover-like bodily occupation that Sam does, makes me think of how Sirens experience reemergence from the Deluge. They have limited time to avert disaster from happening and are likely in unfamiliar places with nary a clue or connection to the pending cataclysm in most cases. The major difference is that Sam has an ally from the future in the case of Al and the computer Ziggy to keep in touch with future events.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Which reminds me, we (speaking as in Reaper, Yads and I) had discussions on some Survivors in the Deluge actually being some people in the present day or descendents of those people. Perhaps this could help in that regard? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995647#post995647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps used sparingly, there could be a similar glimpse of the future without going to the full Deluge. At least in cases where a Siren is already dedicated towards preventing a set outcome. The use of the Sense Conclusion and Deluge Opus may fill this in regards to the Introduction setting the target of inquiry. Maybe when a Siren is experiencing a Malestrom it's like living out the disaster for her, having not only the evidence of her frenzy but a memory of the worsening outcome as well. Or an as of yet undetermined mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sirens don't need the Celestial Ocean in order to trace, but it does help. When it comes to Tracing in the Celestial Ocean, I've just made mechanics for it and fluff text in the Celestial Ocean document. :3 <br /> <br /> Along with an extra section I've put into the Celestial Ocean Document on uses for it. :3<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Clues of the Past</b><br /> As the Celestial Ocean holds the ruins of the past within it, it\u2019s simple for Sirens to sift through the wreckage to find pieces they can Trace on that lead back to the present reality. Perhaps they find a serial killer\u2019s knife, rusted with blood and covered in barnacles at his last crime scene, or a waterlogged safe containing the tax returns of a corrupt company. Either way, a Siren may make (Intelligence or Wits) + Investigation rolls to find a clue for a Trace. And depending on what event the clue is tied to, it\u2019s usually tied to a circumstance or purview of one of the six Waters. In which case, the Siren may add the Water\u2019s Prevalance as a bonus to her (Wits or Intelligence) + Investigation roll. For example events dealing with Freshwater\u2019s Purviews (Technology, Humanity, Fate and Civilization in general) would add bonuses to searching for clues dealing with Civilization\u2019s problems.<br /> <b>Uses of the Celestial Ocean</b><br /> Now with all of the dangers of the Celestial Ocean made clear, the Diasters, Survivors, Therons, Vodianoi, and even other Sirens, there\u2019s undoubtedly one question that crosses every Siren\u2019s mind at one point or another. \u201cWhy even go there in the first place?\u201d Like most treasures in the sea, it takes looking below the water\u2019s surface to find the answers to these questions.<br /> <i>Safety: </i>There\u2019s one thing that\u2019s hard to deny - The Celestial Ocean is a dangerous place and nobody in their right mind would think of casually setting up shop there. And yet that\u2019s what makes the Celestial Ocean so useful. It\u2019s someplace that nobody thinks of staying at for long, and is an ideal place for people who desire safety from the mortal world. Due to this factor, it\u2019s common for Sirens of all Currents to think of finding safety within the Celestial Ocean. It\u2019s the biggest reason why Grotto building is so popular, afterall.<br /> <i>Treasures and Trinkets:</i> The most obvious benefit of the Celestial Ocean is the ability to find Treasures and Trinkets as stated in their section above. No Siren knows why they only appear in the Deluge and not in normal reality, but for what it\u2019s worth, they truly are treasures amongst the ruins. No Siren can also assume where they may find any, but more than a few (namely those in Cocytus) are aware that they can be cultivated from major events in reality. More than a few Sirens make it their profession for Treasure Seeking.<br /> <i>Clues and Survivors: </i>As stated above, within the bad future of the Celestial Ocean may the Siren find clues of events and tragedies that she can enforce or prevent in the present. The case of Clues are simple to find and deal with, as they may be an object or place connected to events the Siren hopes to interfere with.<br /> However, the Survivors show a peculiar inclination when it comes to Clues. More than a few of them however can show surprising knowledge on events. Sirens are surprised that the Survivors can show such an affinity for the world before the apocalypse, but then again the existence of the Celestial Ocean relies on the existence of reality. These special kinds of Survivors tend to be descendents of those in important events (and yet they strangely appear like the people they\u2019re connected to), or even self-professed Flensers who\u2019ve survived the Deluge and regret it ever happening. Whatever the case is on these special Survivors, no Siren knows. However, for the right price, these survivors are willing to divulge all the information they can in hopes their future will be fixed. <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995647#post995647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea is if the Siren had a Theron or Survivor companion that came to the present with them, said companion would 'update' their memories and maybe their abilities in regards to shifting cataclysms. All that has been said for certain is that Echidna is the only figure to live through the end of the Earth and remain in depths of the Celestial Sea regardless of its forms. There's no guarantee who else would survive the enacting of the Deluge but as lifeforms struggling after that time it's natural to think elements of their existence would change from a Siren's influence. This creates a new purpose for Theron/Survivor companions outside of the Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, I feel like I need to make the Theron Companion Merit. I believe that social merits pertaining to other humans can apply equally to Survivors. As for survival outside the Deluge, I'm conflicted. On one hand, I wrote that Survivors cannot exit the Deluge (that is, unless they become Vodianoi). On another, I have been spitballing about ideas for how a Siren can bring out a Theron from the Deluge for the said merit above. Would they be in Twilight? Would they be in reality?<br /> <br /> And furthermore I still haven't thought of any satisfactory ways a Siren can enter or exit the Celestial Ocean or how independent beings can do such. If nothing else, I'm fine with the idea that it's a place that only Sirens can enter it (or drag people there to fit the whole &quot;dragging people to their deaths&quot; motif when it's actually entry into the Celestial Ocean) and limiting Independent beings to using Treasures or special magic to achieve entry. Ack, how does that sound? And also, I'm not doing the Sylphs idea if that's fine, I feel it was scatterbrained for me to pull that up and I don't feel very inspired at using it. <br /> <br /> <b>[1+] Theronic Companion</b><br /> Whereas the animals of the earth serve as man's best friend, a Siren's best friend lies within the Celestial Ocean and can be found within the Therons of the Celestial Ocean. A Theronic Companion is an animal loyal to the owning Siren, capable of carrying out her orders as she gives them. They can only understand commands like the smartest of dogs can understand, such as &quot;Go find food outside&quot; or &quot;Go find shelter&quot; is fine. &quot;Go get me the Clue at the bottom of the ruins 20 miles from here&quot; or other complex orders aren't. Each dot in Theronic Companion accounts for how many Alterations the Theron owns. Assume the dots in Theronic Companion also acts as the Theron's &quot;Akashic Record&quot; rating for Alterations that call as such.<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback: </i>Therons are animals, through and through. It may be hard to domesticate one, and the Siren needs to treat them right and train them in order to have one at her beck and call. The process of gaining a Theronic Companion should take a scene or be worth a session to gain and/or train. The Control Conclusion can be used to domesticate a Theron Companion.<br /> <br /> <b>[2] Potnia Theron</b><br /> Requirement: The Siren is of the Water Gardenia or membership in the Current of Primordial Darkness.<br /> <br /> Translated from greek, the name of this merit translates into &quot;Mistress of the Animals&quot;. Like this mythical figure, a Siren may be worthy of the same title as she calls her Therons to flock to her in her time of need. A Siren with this merit may buy the Theronic Companion Merit as many times as she desires it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=995647#post995647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Continuing from my question on favored Opuses, for the Double Dipping merit it grants the Siren the secondary Knowledges for Pneuma gain but doesn't count the Opuses as favored. Would a Siren with this merit count her second Water's Alterations as favored? I'd wager letting Alterations count if Opuses aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, let's go with that. :3 I'll add it in. Alterations in the second water being favored too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:06:56-07:00","id":997180,"title":"","content":"What I like about the Deluge as presented is that it is a real place. An ever shifting potential reality but real nonetheless. That it has no other supernatural realms of its own is a powerful feature as to how real and isolated the Deluge is.<br /> <br /> What is key is how the Waters bridge the Earth of the modern present with the Deluge, that they not only reflect biomes on the planet but the harsh waters of the Celestial Ocean as well. And from each Water's purview (the range of Opuses) you can link major cataclysms and hazards to a category of Water. When it comes to basic travel to the Deluge, especially for non-Sirens, it could occur during a similar disaster of a lesser scale.<br /> <br /> Those lost at sea, that disappear during violent storms, that were trapped under the ice. For a brief moment (from the perspective of the present) that person is gone, thrust into the raging Deluge where the disaster continues past their present area on arrival. Events that, even before the Dangers of the Deluge are faced, would constitute facing a Breaking Point just from the sheer trauma of being thrust through the Deluge. It's not easy and not pretty, for even to get back requires further strain to your Integrity.<br /> <br /> Taken to the full extreme, when present in a fitting disaster travel to or from the Deluge requires a loss of Integrity. On a dramatic failure from such a roll the travel is involuntary. It fits the tidbit that most are unable to survive exposure to the Deluge.<br /> <br /> The earlier idea of Quagmires connecting to the Deluge would work similarly. Along with their punishments, if they have no use for a victim they could be flung into the Deluge fitting the type of Quagmire. Sirens have an easier time with travel to the Deluge. For one, they can try to barter passage with the Quagmire/Fury, and would not risk their Lucidity in the above example. Let alone that with the Deluge Opus and the right Introductions and Conclusions, they can interact with the Deluge in various ways. Travel to it safely, Sense it while remaining in the present, Invoke some of its environmental tilts...<br /> <br /> As for Survivors and Therons, there are no exits from the Deluge. No Quagmires to appease, no departure points from a former 'present' because they did not come from the pre-Deluge earth. It is only with a Siren to guide them (or the Vodinaoi route) that they could leave the Deluge. They are real people so they do not emerge via Twilight, and as the Deluge has no Twilight state they'll have no advantage to use it. However, the 'present' would be as uncomfortable to them as we would be as modern people going back in time to the Neolithic era. Survivors and other Deluge residents are adapted to survive its cataclysms. It' like they're locked into their own Diluvian form, basically losing health where a Siren would lose Pneuma unless they dwell in waters fitting that of the Deluge equivalent.<br /> <br /> <br /> I fear I did a disservice comparing Furies and Slyphs to Qasmilim when the idea was just starting out. Non-Siren aspects of the Song sound like a novel idea and if their gatekeeper status is kept they could offer passage to a calm or at least benign section of the Deluge. Though like any late development addition, it requires a bit more effort to find the nessecary niche for Slyphs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:30:41-07:00","id":997453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=997180#post997180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I like about the Deluge as presented is that it is a real place. An ever shifting potential reality but real nonetheless. That it has no other supernatural realms of its own is a powerful feature as to how real and isolated the Deluge is.<br /> <br /> What is key is how the Waters bridge the Earth of the modern present with the Deluge, that they not only reflect biomes on the planet but the harsh waters of the Celestial Ocean as well. And from each Water's purview (the range of Opuses) you can link major cataclysms and hazards to a category of Water. When it comes to basic travel to the Deluge, especially for non-Sirens, it could occur during a similar disaster of a lesser scale.<br /> <br /> Those lost at sea, that disappear during violent storms, that were trapped under the ice. For a brief moment (from the perspective of the present) that person is gone, thrust into the raging Deluge where the disaster continues past their present area on arrival. Events that, even before the Dangers of the Deluge are faced, would constitute facing a Breaking Point just from the sheer trauma of being thrust through the Deluge. It's not easy and not pretty, for even to get back requires further strain to your Integrity.<br /> <br /> Taken to the full extreme, when present in a fitting disaster travel to or from the Deluge requires a loss of Integrity. On a dramatic failure from such a roll the travel is involuntary. It fits the tidbit that most are unable to survive exposure to the Deluge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. This feels like fitting ways to enter the Celestial Ocean. What's abit delicious about this is that if a disaster of enough intensity can drag individual people into the Celestial Ocean, imagine that a Quagmire's Flooding can do the same thing. C:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=997180#post997180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The earlier idea of Quagmires connecting to the Deluge would work similarly. Along with their punishments, if they have no use for a victim they could be flung into the Deluge fitting the type of Quagmire. Sirens have an easier time with travel to the Deluge. For one, they can try to barter passage with the Quagmire/Fury, and would not risk their Lucidity in the above example. Let alone that with the Deluge Opus and the right Introductions and Conclusions, they can interact with the Deluge in various ways. Travel to it safely, Sense it while remaining in the present, Invoke some of its environmental tilts...</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, I would still like to keep the ability to deliberately enter the Celestial Ocean when fully submerged in water, and even adding in modifiers for bringing other people or using a Quagmire to help them further. And yes, the Deluge Opus can be used for as you said. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=997180#post997180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Survivors and Therons, there are no exits from the Deluge. No Quagmires to appease, no departure points from a former 'present' because they did not come from the pre-Deluge earth. It is only with a Siren to guide them (or the Vodinaoi route) that they could leave the Deluge. They are real people so they do not emerge via Twilight, and as the Deluge has no Twilight state they'll have no advantage to use it. However, the 'present' would be as uncomfortable to them as we would be as modern people going back in time to the Neolithic era. Survivors and other Deluge residents are adapted to survive its cataclysms. It' like they're locked into their own Diluvian form, basically losing health where a Siren would lose Pneuma unless they dwell in waters fitting that of the Deluge equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, I'll add them in. I'll also add to the Vodianoi Section that they can exit the Celestial Ocean whenever they wish, but usually only do so on Echidnal orders to kidnap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=997180#post997180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear I did a disservice comparing Furies and Slyphs to Qasmilim when the idea was just starting out. Non-Siren aspects of the Song sound like a novel idea and if their gatekeeper status is kept they could offer passage to a calm or at least benign section of the Deluge. Though like any late development addition, it requires a bit more effort to find the nessecary niche for Slyphs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ok, I think a part of it is that we have loads of social splats and creatures in the game already. That and I don't wish to unintentionally make any reference to Princess the Hopeful mechanics or the like further than I already have (used with permission I shall note). The Quagmire Mechanics are outright based on Taint Mechanics and adding in a Sylph/Shrine ideas makes me fear of doing the same for Blessed Places in PtH.<br /> <br /> All of that said, I have some bits of development done and some news! For the development, I've wrote out the Siren crossovers for Vampires and Beasts, the Cataclysm for Hunter the Vigil, the Mechanics for Changeling, Demon, Promethean and Hunter and finally trying to begin the prologue on Werewolf. <br /> <br /> <b>Crossovers: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_vK6C6vfoUa9HS9Uc0Uz0jRotgDjHXXvlLBp6fKS2h8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I hope what I have so far is satisfactory. I admit, I fear I might've done a bad job on Beast. Reasons why are explained in the spoiler below, please do not take it as an entire reflection of my character.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm unread on it which is partially out of my personal distaste for the gameline, but I did skim the corebook (mainly kinship powers and the crossovers section in the book) and based it on other general gists I've read on it. I've tried to remain unbiased on it though, and I do believe that most Sirens would really dislike Beasts if because they can casually defile both Civilization and Nature, and for my ideas on how to redo Relationships, I've thought that if a Siren's Relationship got hurt they will fly into Maelstrom to kill whatever caused it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now for the news! I have mentioned that I desired to revamp Relationships, but I wanted to look around homebrew hubs to see if anyone had something I could use as a base, to which I would ask for permission if I could use the system. In particular, I looked at Pale_Crusader's Frality Chronicles and found his system of Supports and Atrocity. With the way a relationship with another person can get damaged, I felt these were the best systems that can be used as a basis for Relationships. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749\"> Homebrew of Pale_Crusader - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801749#post801749 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Frailty Chronicles Disclaimer* The follow Material is re-written homebrew adapting rules from Danse Macabre, Mirrors, and Walking Shadows (http://forum.theonyxpath. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So far, my ideas at the moment are as follows based on my ideas and the Supports System.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Relationships Merit will be like a modified version of the Touchstones Merit. Like the Touchstones merit, Relationships will go on a rating from one to five. Unlike a Touchstone though, Relationships are much more intimate to Sirens than other Supernaturals. As such, this Merit is much more personal and includes more Storytelling than normal Touchstones. As such, the Relationship merit doesn't keep track of the number of relationships, but rather the Strength of the Relationship the merit represents. <br /> <br /> The Relationship merit can be bought multiple times, and each Relationship represents a single person or being. Each dot in the Relationship as said is the Strength of connection. A Siren with a single dot in a Relationship may have that person as an aquaintence or a disconnected friend, but a Siren with five dots in a Relationship may have the person as a lover, a longtime and trusted friend or they're the Siren's parent(s), guardian(s) or even beloved pets. The type of Love can be any of the four types: Familial, Romantic, Platonic or Unconditional. But it must be listed underneath one of these types. <br /> <br /> For each Dot a Relationship has, it has one Health box. The Health Boxes are not representative of physical health like they normally denote, but the health of the Relationship. This health is still in the flavor of physical health, being committed in Bashing, Lethal and then Aggravated Damage. Bashing overdone can become Lethal, and Lethal overdone can become Aggravated.<br /> <br /> Relationships require upkeep and support, but they also face stress and times where it seems it may break off. When it comes to measuring Stress, roll the Siren's Lucidity. For each <b>Failure </b>on the roll, fill one box with Bashing damage. Stress is usually rolled at the beginning of each Story, but a Siren may spend a point of Willpower to roll 3 additional dice <i>separate </i>from the Stress roll. Each success on these dice negate one of the Failures on the original Stress roll.<br /> <br /> Stress can be rerolled throughout a story, but it's primarily caused from negative interaction between the Siren and her Relationship, or the lack of interaction. Examples of Stress rolls are primarily:<ul><li><b>Beaching: </b>When a Siren commits an action according to her Beaching, or a mortal does the same with their Vice, roll Stress.</li> <li><b>Kink: </b>Each Relationship has at least one Kink, one point of dysfunctionality present that can be annoying and attributed to one or both sides of a relationship. Afterall, perfect relationships only exist in fairy tales, and real ones need maintenence and upkeep to keep the flames going. When the Kink presents itself, roll Stress.</li> <li><b>Supernatural Nature: </b>Mortals are not conditioned to accept the supernatural, and many freak out over it. When a Relationship faces a breaking point from the Siren indirectly, roll Stress, the damage here is <i>Lethal. </i>If the Siren was intentionally revealing her nature to her beloved, then the damage is upgraded to <i>Aggravated</i>.</li> <li><b>Neglect: </b>Mostly done as a thematic approach, but neglect can kill relationships on one or both ends. If the mortal neglects the Siren or Vice versa, roll Stress. For a Siren to count as Neglecting her Relationship, the Siren has either not made any contact (no matter how brief) to the Relationship within three sessions, or doesn't interact with them during downtime.</li> </ul>If a Siren ever manages to fill the Relationship's Health Boxes with Aggravated, clear them all and have the Siren <i>lose </i>a dot in that Relationship. It represents losing the once higher amount of connection they once had, the pain of simply walking past someone you once talked all day every day with. Should the Siren lose the last dot in her Relationship, then the Relationship breaks off, lost to the Siren. The Siren can spend Experience to raise her Relationship score back up, to represent her getting back in touch with those she cares about.<br /> <br /> The Relationship can be healed of Damage. Spending time, trying to get problems (caused by Stress) to become water under the bridge. This is primarily done with spending time with the Relationship and showing why it's a meaningful relationship.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think I may have gone overboard with describing the Relationship ideas/conceptualization, but I hope this covers the general ideas I have for them. :3<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T00:22:45-07:00","id":997588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=997180#post997180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Survivors and Therons, there are no exits from the Deluge. No Quagmires to appease, no departure points from a former 'present' because they did not come from the pre-Deluge earth. It is only with a Siren to guide them (or the Vodinaoi route) that they could leave the Deluge. They are real people so they do not emerge via Twilight, and as the Deluge has no Twilight state they'll have no advantage to use it. However, the 'present' would be as uncomfortable to them as we would be as modern people going back in time to the Neolithic era. Survivors and other Deluge residents are adapted to survive its cataclysms. It' like they're locked into their own Diluvian form, basically losing health where a Siren would lose Pneuma unless they dwell in waters fitting that of the Deluge equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this up to the point of them taking damage if they don't stick around water. I would argue that's not necessary and think it's enough discomfort that they're placed in, according to their perception, society just before the end comes and as long as they're there they will have to weather out the ensuing shitstorm as well rather than the calm aftermaths.<br /> <br /> Imagine being put in Germany after WWI, you know what happens according to history, you can see how society is doing all the wrong things around you and you know the Nazi party responsible for the shitstorm that is WWII is right around the corner. But you can't tell anybody about it cuz few (if any) will believe you; you have no proof afterall. You're powerless to stop it, you've got no political power in a place where you shouldn't even exist, let alone to stop the strongest rising political party in the entire country; and what's more if you talk enough they're gonna come after you to put you down as a threat to their veil. And even others in your position aren't a safe bet, because a lot of them don't come from the exact same version of the world you're from and may argue with you over what's the greater threat, or even directly oppose your version of the incoming threat because in their view that's what's making things worse or they think they can control it or use it and then toss it aside to prevent their incoming horror from happening.<br /> <br /> Replace post-WWI with modern, Germany with Earth, and Nazis with whatever ails that ruins the planet, be it major corporations polluting rivers or the rising tensions between Russia and the US, as well as supernatural forces who will hunt you down for breaking the Masquerade if you go into details trying to warn people who probably won't believe you anyway. I think the addition then to cause damage because you're not close enough to a specific body of water kinda ruins the atmosphere of horror by tossing in something unnecessairly mechanical to the mix that takes away from the focus of &quot;the end can go down at any moment&quot; in favor of &quot;I gotta make sure I stay near X Lake&quot;. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T01:46:34-07:00","id":998654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=997588#post997588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *snip* What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but agree with this from a standpoint.<br /> <br /> Also, some news. I've finally reworked Relationships and made them into something that is fully customizable with! Special Credits to Pale_Crusader for allowing me to use his system of Supports, Comforts and Kinks! They're the first thing below Modified Merits!<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 3 - The Antediluvian Symphony: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Br5u6ylBDdzNDG6Q_r09pohkyGvgq3hSWVuJPDPrRXA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> As well, I would also like to thank Amechra! Awhile back, they made a merit that dealt with the nature of Soulmates, and I asked for permission to place it within Siren. I received it and as such it's in Siren. It's been tweaked a tiny bit in the Merits section to include factors on Relationships, but it's basically the same as it is here! It's underneath the Mundane Merits. :3<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813925-dialling-my-brain-back-down-true-friendship\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...rue-friendship<br /> <br /> I</a>'ve also edited Lucidity a tiny bit to take account of Relationships and Dissonances that can come from losing them and to be abit less &quot;moral&quot;, kind of like how Harmony or Synergy is for Werewolves/Sin-Eaters. I've also edited Maelstrom to be more viable to come up in a session. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 11-05-2016, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T17:52:41-07:00","id":998962,"title":"","content":"Looking back, mirroring the aspects of the Diluvian form are far too limiting I agree. My initial idea was that they required some connection to their home water, maybe once a day or another frequency would be better, like how we need food or sleep. The main question with the inclusion of ways for Survivors and Therons to accompany Sirens is how much connection they have to the Akashic Record. Do they require Pneuma? How much could they hold, if they don't have their own Akashic Record score. Yet many of the Alterations are structured to use Pnuema. And by that point when you look back at the level of comparing character sheets, the only criteria to differ Deluge residents and Sirens is access to the Song to weave Verses and choice of merits.<br /> <br /> Several game lines have the 'minor Supernatural' template which is just the lesser version of the main player characters, often with 0 for the Supernatural Tolerance. I think a good next question is how similar to Sirens Survivors and Therons are meant to be. And beyond companionship what else they bring to a Siren trying to prevent the Deluge they came from.<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> With the character creation questions out of the way, I've been having a few drafts for Siren characters in my head. I plan to share them once I can spare more time to writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:12:50-07:00","id":998969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=998962#post998962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back, mirroring the aspects of the Diluvian form are far too limiting I agree. My initial idea was that they required some connection to their home water, maybe once a day or another frequency would be better, like how we need food or sleep. The main question with the inclusion of ways for Survivors and Therons to accompany Sirens is how much connection they have to the Akashic Record. Do they require Pneuma? How much could they hold, if they don't have their own Akashic Record score. Yet many of the Alterations are structured to use Pnuema. And by that point when you look back at the level of comparing character sheets, the only criteria to differ Deluge residents and Sirens is access to the Song to weave Verses and choice of merits.<br /> <br /> Several game lines have the 'minor Supernatural' template which is just the lesser version of the main player characters, often with 0 for the Supernatural Tolerance. I think a good next question is how similar to Sirens Survivors and Therons are meant to be. And beyond companionship what else they bring to a Siren trying to prevent the Deluge they came from.<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> With the character creation questions out of the way, I've been having a few drafts for Siren characters in my head. I plan to share them once I can spare more time to writing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only thing I have to point out is how the Survivors actually lack Alterations. They were pretty much made to be inhabitants of the Celestial Ocean and possible points of interaction in there, aside from Echidna and her Vodianoi. Since Vodianoi and Survivors don't have any Pneuma or Akashic Record, I think I wrote for the former to always be treated as if they had at least Akashic Record 1 even though they aren't technically Sirens. It's for this bit of faulty reasoning that I made two of the Malformations pretty much be upgraded versions of the skill boosting Alterations.<br /> <br /> Given that Survivors cannot be fed on for Pneuma however, I imagine that would be the one thing anchoring them to the Antediluvian World.<br /> <br /> As for the subsplat, we actually did cover that, but we sadly haven't brought them up for awhile. We have the Breathless as the Siren Subsplat, the people who've experienced the Drowning but never Surfaced. In mundane terms, when the event that gave them despair in their lives came up, instead of fighting tooth and claw to survive it anyways (aka the Surfacing), the Breathless decided to walk away from it all. Because they didn't surface and become a Siren, their soul has been wounded/marked by the Song. It gives them a sort of aura that makes people notice them, in the same way that people notice a body barely clinging to life on the beach. It can make them prone to being helped by people, even if they never asked for it. Some Breathless know how to manipulate this aura and use it to their advantage. For Sirens, they're valuable sources of Pneuma, as they may feed off of the Breathless, who automatically drains willpower from others. It allows a Siren to feed from Pneuma without doing it in person.<br /> <br /> In case of TL;DR, the Breathless are at the bottom of this Document.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BixAH8CJOcG0z40bNmJ6psZha7r6a6WUFDbg-sBYdb4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":9750,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","user":"SaulottheGentle","date":". 11-05-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:42:18-07:00","id":998980,"title":"","content":"At this point it sounds like Survivors themselves have no mechanical benefits, so better to leave their interactions with Sirens as to the Storyteller's discretion. Like them being descendants of other characters, turned into Vodinaoi, and other plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Therons, as antediluvian animals, do have Alterations and mimic Akashic Record as per the outline in the merit. Any reason it's rated at 1+ instead of 1-5 dots? Other companion merits and really the majority of merits stick to a 5 dot rating maximum, which seems plenty for creating a strange creature with multiple Alterations. Also for clarity you'll want it outlined how much Pneuma a Theron can store, be it like the Siren's equivalent pool or 1 Pneuma per merit dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:08:28-07:00","id":999023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=998962#post998962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back, mirroring the aspects of the Diluvian form are far too limiting I agree. My initial idea was that they required some connection to their home water, maybe once a day or another frequency would be better, like how we need food or sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>For my part, I can at least see them taking solace in it and a tad more at ease when taking a bath in x water; I just don't think they should get bruised up if they don't. As for Survivor mechanics, I would personally put them as resilient towards Breathless appeal a l\u00e1 1E Wolf-Blooded towards Lunacy and make them able to use Treasures with Willpower instead of Pneuma. It's the classic &quot;minor template&quot; run. I'm slightly mushy from newly awokenness atm, but afaik the Survivors have some sort of connection to Pneuma even if they can't store it themselves: to this I have an idea of maybe they can go through the process of generating it, but it sorta &quot;drops and spreads&quot; rather than going into them; letting them create but not indulge it. That could be a useful thing to Sirens, especially if they don't want to draw attention to themselves. What do you think?<br /> On Therons I like how it sounds atm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:36:18-08:00","id":999462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=998980#post998980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point it sounds like Survivors themselves have no mechanical benefits, so better to leave their interactions with Sirens as to the Storyteller's discretion. Like them being descendants of other characters, turned into Vodinaoi, and other plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Therons, as antediluvian animals, do have Alterations and mimic Akashic Record as per the outline in the merit. Any reason it's rated at 1+ instead of 1-5 dots? Other companion merits and really the majority of merits stick to a 5 dot rating maximum, which seems plenty for creating a strange creature with multiple Alterations. Also for clarity you'll want it outlined how much Pneuma a Theron can store, be it like the Siren's equivalent pool or 1 Pneuma per merit dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties. How does it sound for a Theronic Companion to have an Akashic Record rating equal to the Merit's dot rating? As well as having one Pneuma per merit dot as you said? :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=999023#post999023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For my part, I can at least see them taking solace in it and a tad more at ease when taking a bath in x water; I just don't think they should get bruised up if they don't. As for Survivor mechanics, I would personally put them as resilient towards Breathless appeal a l\u00e1 1E Wolf-Blooded towards Lunacy and make them able to use Treasures with Willpower instead of Pneuma. It's the classic &quot;minor template&quot; run. I'm slightly mushy from newly awokenness atm, but afaik the Survivors have some sort of connection to Pneuma even if they can't store it themselves: to this I have an idea of maybe they can go through the process of generating it, but it sorta &quot;drops and spreads&quot; rather than going into them; letting them create but not indulge it. That could be a useful thing to Sirens, especially if they don't want to draw attention to themselves. What do you think?<br /> On Therons I like how it sounds atm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty, I will make it so that Survivors can use Treasures and don't cause Refraction. <br /> <br /> Given though that Survivors can't hold Pneuma, and Echidna, her Sirens and Vodianoi are prevalent in the Deluge, I have an idea for what to write in the mage section of the crossover document. What if Mages see the Celestial Ocean as a Lower Depth? And the thing it lacks is the &quot;Spark of Life&quot;. Not as in the Life Arcana, but more as in the drive to keep living, to keep surviving for another day in hopes everything will someday get better?<br /> <br /> Of course, do note what I'm saying here is how I'd imagine MAGES seeing it, not what it actually is. I'd imagine Sirens would detest it if Mages treated them like baser creatures leeching off of the world (like how most creatures from Lower Depths do and usually the lower depth itself) when in reality they're trying to save it. And I imagine Mages (perhaps sans the Guardians of the Veil who would agree with the Siren's analysis) would hate it when a Siren would begin messing with them because the Siren has forseen massive reality breaking consequences from a mage in question. What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:37:27-08:00","id":1003640,"title":"","content":"Pardon for my lack of posting as of late. I think I've hit another block, or at least I'm out of inspiration at the moment.<br /> <br /> And I would like to make note of a few things I've been thinking of. <b>First, </b>I'm thinking of not fully developing the Crossovers section, at least for now. As much fun as it has been making the sections for it, it's heavily draining on Inspiration. And given that a Crossover section isn't required to fully finish the corebook,<b> I will be holding off on Crossovers until Siren as a Corebook is complete.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Second, </b>given that thought, I was thinking on what parts of the Corebook need to be completed, which so far includes three sections: <b>Choruses, Ascension/Descension and Honolulu. </b>So far, Honolulu has at least ideas on how it should be written and Ascension/Descension was liked by the people who looked at it. All that's left is Choruses, the Z-Splat of Siren. But I'm having problems as it were with them or designing them.<br /> <br /> <b>Chorus Thoughts</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> My thoughts so far on Choruses remain as I said they were. Powers include powering up Verses better, making it easier to trace out other members or the like, etc. The only problem I'm having at the moment is what their general theme should be. Either focusing on Operas and Musical Productions, or basing off of Musical Genres. There's Pros and Cons to each of them. <br /> <br /> For Operas or Musical Productions, the pros are as follows: They grant a theme to the Sirens within them, making it easier to write about them, the general character of the Sirens who join them and the like, and maybe even including a special Verse or power that only the Sirens in the chorus can take up, and the possibility that Opera/Musical Choruses could belong to either Celestial or Abyssal Currents. The only con I can see with this is that it may be abit too limiting (in terms of Verse style and &quot;belongs to either Celestial or Abyssal) and the Opera schtick feels like something that should be in Changeling (given how the use of Story tropes and the like are used alot in Changeling).<br /> <br /> For Musical Genres, the pros are as follows: It makes it much more versatile in terms of powering up Verses (meaning if you're in a Chorus whose genre is Punk Rock, then performing a Verse to Punk Rock will grant a bigger bonus), and following a theme of music feels fitting for Sirens. Plus, it just feels right in Siren and gives something outside of Celestial and Abyssal duties to take part in. The cons I can see with this though is that it may be too open, not to mention it feels like writing on the various Genres would be painting with a wide brush and annoy people who like the Genre and go &quot;but *insert genre here* isn't just about *insert general theme the songs within the genre covers*&quot;. One way around that would be to insert subgenres as various powers or extra effects for Verses, which could be a pro.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyways, going up further, my <b>last thought</b>. When it comes to Survivors and Breathless, I was thinking. They both serve as special conditions that can be inflicted onto humans due to the Song's influence. Given Karavolo's thoughts on Survivors being able to make but not own Pneuma and how that sounds like Breathless, <b>what if Survivors and Breathless are the same kind of being? </b>Instead of being two separate splats, they're the same one with different living spaces? <br /> <br /> What do you guys think of these thoughts?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:29:45-08:00","id":1003746,"title":"","content":"I think making Survivors and Breathless the same thing is a good idea. Since the Breathless don't have the pull effect on each other, they can still come off as normal in the Celestial Ocean while showing a clear effect upon the world if they're brought into our Earth to showcase they don't belong and help separating them from regular people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T18:30:31-08:00","id":1008733,"title":"","content":"Alrighties then, the Survivors and Breathless have been merged into one Splat! :3<br /> <br /> As well, I've been also thinking. Almost all of the Siren Currents are based on dealing with the Deluge in a specific way...save for two Currents. Cocytus and Phlegethon. So far, it feels like they're only interested with their own things rather than with the Deluge, and I feel that sorta puts them off compared to the other currents, feeling abit bland if you will. <br /> <br /> So I was thinking, what if we did tiny modifications to make them abit more important? For example, Cocytus still has their themes of dark secrets, awe of the dark depths and the like, but they concern themselves with the Deluge in the way a scientist throws away their ethics to stop the plague. They're desperate and feel that ethics shouldn't stop them from achieving their end goals.<br /> <br /> As for Phlegethon, I imagine that upon seeing the Deluge happen, they decide it's too much work or it's insurmountable. In short, they decide that given the apocalypse is happening that it's better to spend the rest of your days happy and indulging in some good old &quot;End of the world debauchery&quot; than trying to fix what isn't fixable. It also gives them abit more sympathetic points than their current &quot;For the Evulz&quot; take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T21:18:31-08:00","id":1008798,"title":"","content":"I think that the Phlegethon should have a lesser mindset of &quot;but if they get the idea that they stand a chance, they will jump it&quot; by logic of &quot;why give up your nice life to an apocalypse when you can prevent it?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T10:54:38-08:00","id":1010265,"title":"","content":"<u>Minor Templates</u><br /> Making Survivors and Breathless the same is really brilliant. It shows that humanity is going to change from the Cataclysms that enact the Deluge, let alone the exposure to the Song that has not made them Sirens. It easily explains the difference of post-Deluge beings, as they won't have any benefits normally seen amongst Sirens that Therons will have but aren't too vulnerable to a Siren's verses either. It makes any modern day or far future flung Breathless/Survivors companions the same for ease of game mechanics.<br /> <br /> <u>Choruses</u><br /> So seeing that Choruses are the attempted prestige class or z-splat option for Sirens, the first question to ask is what is their THEME? What is it that binds them together and how does that provide them benefits not common amongst everyday Sirens?<br /> <br /> Each Chronicles system that has a z-splat option does so to provide new opportunities for the character, as any prestige option should. To generalize some examples: Changeling's Entitlements bring the Lost into new social groups, titles, new stories and roles and the power begotten from the Wyrd that fits the Entitlement. In Princess the Embassies give the Hopeful expertise in different avenues beyond the battle of Light vs the Darkness, a new motif to their Regalia and exclusive privileges or powers, and a focus towards different facets of the word both mundane and supernatural. And for Genius (ideally with 2E readdressing the structure) a Fellowship is a niche application, project or field of Mad Science. It is tiered towards one particular Wonder or theorem that is nigh-perfected and avoids the pitfalls lesser Wonders of the same type would have.<br /> <br /> So from how a Chorus should be outlined, they usually have a few prerequisites. Usually Supernatural Tolerance at a certain level, certain Attribute or Skill minimums and some require belonging to a certain faction. Although I would suggest only a minority of Chorus have a faction or Current based prerequisite.<br /> <br /> If the <b>Water</b> represents where the Siren comes from and what she embodies, and the <b>Current</b> is both her outlook, methodology and like mindedness with other Sirens, what niche does the <b>Chorus</b> expand or fulfill?<br /> <br /> From what is initially presented, teamwork looks to be a central point of Choruses. You cannot form a Chorus from an individual. Perhaps besides benefits for herself the Siren can provide a small boon to her fellows <i>(what is a group of Sirens called again, I've forgotten)</i>, and the boon is better when performed with more members of the same Chorus.<br /> <br /> As for the unifying themes of each Chorus several have been presented. One way is to allow the Siren more formats to enact the Song, the music and theatrical connotations. Another is a Chorus formed to deal with specific kinds of disasters, conflicts or other issues. The Chorus could even be the background of a certain kind of story, giving the Siren an 'in' with different facets of life while remaining inconspicuous. A Chorus is also a soft way of inducting Crossover themes (like the way Princess does it) to represent the Siren approach to material not found in the typical Siren game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T11:37:51-08:00","id":1010279,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the double post, I have been working on drafting some Siren NPC characters and wanted to share the first of these characters. I plan to use her to introduce Siren to my mega crossover game that is Princess centered, so the Crossover material is set aside in it's own tab. Nonetheless I wanted to provide basis for the character without Crossover in mind, as she would serve as a model for the type of Siren I would want to play as my first character in a Siren: the Drowning game.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Character Draft: Ixcuina</u><br /> </span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Concept: snarky ex-Echidnal filth eater</i></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Water:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Discordia (Gardenia)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Current:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Buoyancy</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Favored Opuses:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Beauty, Sound, Water, Taint, Blood, Chaos</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Favored Conclusion:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Travel</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Attributes:</b><br /> Intelligence </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">2, Wits 4, Resolve 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Strength 2, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mental Skills:</b> Computer 1, Crafts 1, Medicine 3, Occult 4, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Brawl 1, Drive 2, Larceny 3, Stealth 2, Survival 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 3, Empathy 4, Intimidation 2, Socialize 3, Streetwise 4, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Specialties:</b><br /> Crafts: Destruction<br /> Survival: Hazardous Areas<br /> Streetwise: Carnal Pleasures<br /> <br /> <b>Flow:</b> Disruptive<br /> <b>Beaching:</b> Dirty</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Size:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Perception:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 6</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Willpower:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 5</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Akashic Record:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Pneuma:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 13/4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Refraction:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> -4 (Song +1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Introductions:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Location, Sentient, Self</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Insensate</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Opuses:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Beauty, Sound, Water, Blood, Taint, Chaos, Earth, Growth, Darkness</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Conclusions:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Travel 4, Invoke 3, Disturb 5, Calm 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Trace:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Bonus for the Time aspect</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Diluvian Form:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> max 7 Alterations</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Common:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Boneless Imitation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Gardenia:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Fetid Touch</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Tropicana:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Poison Immunity</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Malformations:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Poisonous Blood, Slimy Physique, Acidic Excretion</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Knowledges:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">4 total from Double Dipping merit</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Gardenia:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> History Repeats Itself, You Get As Much As You Give</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Discordia:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Water Changes Land Does Not, Conflict Is Life</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mental Merits:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Tolerance for Biology, Language (English), Multilingual (Nahuatl, Korean)</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>; Spanish is her primary language</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Physical Merits:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Small Framed, Double Jointed, Demolisher (1 dot)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Social Merits:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Fixer, Fast Talking (Style; 3 dots), Striking Looks (Unseemly, 1 dot)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Siren Merits:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Double Dipping, Bel Canto</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Appearance:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Ixcuina has dark skin befitting south Mexican Aztec descended features. Short and quite petite, her body is quite flexible making her a natural contortionist. She has a scar from a cleft lip. She's been letting her hair out but doesn't style it much, having thick dreads as a mass of snarling strands.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Given her Malformations there's a sickly bruised choler to her skin and her skin's slime is glossy, like tanning lotion, so she has to avoid whites and light colors.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Her Diluvian form is as blue as window cleaner, with rubbery skin and wet clinging blue hair smoothed down the back of her neck. Her tail is long and sinuous, something like an eel\u2019s, with the skeletal frame of cartilage branching out with vestigial fins stretched between. Her green blood is more prevalent in areas like her hands and mouth, her eyes a green-yellow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Most noticeable in her Diluvian form is the smudge of questionable whatsit around her mouth and nose, a deep brown covering her cleft lip that forms a pattern of strands along the rest of her face and neck.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Personality:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Ixcuina is a women well accustomed to the worst the world has to offer, one who remains defiant in response to these troubles. While appearing to have a languid, resigned and almost slothful personality her signature brand of black comedy is the tip of a feisty avenger. She frequently thinks outside the box and relishes in using taboos to catch opponents off guard. A frequent trick of hers is to catch others at their most vulnerable in public bathrooms. Although quite driven as a Siren she enjoys meeting simple, basic desires and doing as she pleases.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Backstory:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Ixcuina, as she now calls herself, grew up in the region south of the Gulf of Mexico, a land of highs and lows. Lows included the mingling trade of Colombian drugs and Mexican cartels. As she grew older her hometown grew more corrupt with crime and pollution. The dregs of society have no hope when both neighboring sets of Civilization reject them, the very land itself refusing to aid as Nature worsens at maltreatment.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Her full despairing event was being in the midst of a shootout between two gangs, her travel through the Deluge sympathetic to another event far across the Gulf where oil corporations really screwed up just outside of American waters. The Deepwater Horizon oil spill.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">In the Deluge she saw an earth where such pollution had reached its penultimate turmoil. The flooded seas a mire of crude sludge, stricken wildlife dead in the oceans and flaming spills blocking out the skies with smoke.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Her survival instincts were ones of desperation, needing any way out of this cataclysmic destruction humanity had reeked on itself in pursuit of energy and greed. It brought Ixcuina into the depths of Echidna's domain, the dark mother welcome to new recruits that would agree to help her help humanity. Fixing Ixcuina with the means to survive this massive oil spill, Echidna joined her with another group of her Sirens and Vodianoi sent to punish those that failed to remedy their crimes against nature that threatened humanity so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">She was a capable agent amongst the Echidnal Sirens, going off to enact eco-terrorism and returning with more human resources for Vodianoi. Her resolve to follow Echidna's aims, enforced by the sheer number of malformations she had at one time, soon began to waver as her Akashic Record increased. First it was the fights amongst other Abyssal Currents, which drew attention of the Celestial Currents and other foes. And from each defeat or pyrrhic victory, Ixcuina had more questions brought on from the realization that there are more Sirens in the sea than she imagined, each with very different viewpoints.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Questions her fellow Echidnal Sirens didn\u2019t appreciate, especially the thought that Echidna\u2019s deprived mutilations would never produce the next stage of humanity that could survive the Deluge. After leaving anonymous tip offs to Sirens from the Celestial Currents about Echidna\u2019s recent aims, she effectively defected from the sea monster\u2019s faction in the midst of an ambush (more of a slaughter, really) of her former comrades.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Since then Ixcunia has been enjoying newfound freedom, her independent streak leading her along the Current of Buoyancy, rarely keeping close ties with other Sirens save for the original Sirens she developed rapport with as an Echidnal agent. Still, the oil spoiled Deluge she experienced strives her to prevent or punish widescale pollution, be it actual or thematic corruption of life.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Crossover:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> </span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">After distancing herself from Echidna, Ixcunia once came across the site of a Tainted Place that she mistook for a Quagmire. After some trial and error she found that the wounds left of the world from the Darkness could be impacted by similar Verses she used combating mundane pollution. Although Darkspawn were just mindless monsters and easily considered foes, she was more sympathetic towards Darkened humans if unsure what to do about them. From her spective the tainted Darkness was a potent stain not easily cleaned, the unfortunate Darkened could only be prevented from getting worse rather than better.<br /> <br /> Developing a specialty towards Tainted Areas, investigation of a location in the MidWest got Ixcuina in over her head. Low on Pneuma when she needed to escape, the Mnemosyne that tended the Taint managing to capture her and developing an ingenious way to imprison the Siren where she would be unable gain Pneuma or form a rhythm to enact even the most basic verse.<br /> <br /> Given that the Light forms the natural enemy of the Darkness, perhaps some Princesses will manage to discover her in time when dealing with the Mnemosyne foe.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T16:11:05-08:00","id":1010384,"title":"","content":"Sorry for not contributing to this thread for awhile. Anyway. how is progress on the Honolulu chapter? Also, would Ixcuina be familiar with Poseidon? Considering she was a Echidnal and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T17:01:04-08:00","id":1010407,"title":"","content":"Honolulu is a big focus being one of the final core chapters (as opposed to supplementary material) so I know the shift of effort is pointed there. I've only been to Maui myself so I can't think of anything to suggest outside of being watered down Hawaii 5-O. I imagine Tropicana is the most popular water along the islands in the Pacific, so my interest is what Sirens of the other waters would be like in Honolulu.<br /> <br /> If locations from other islands were ever wanted for adventure blurbs, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haleakal\u0101\" target=\"_blank\">Haleakala Crater</a>, the main volcano on Maui, would be an interesting spot. A potential Quagmire would tie heavily to the Earth aspect of Gardenia, as there are protected plants along the crest of the crater prevent access from other people. There is also a space observatory nearby.<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> As for Ixcuina, if Poseidon is largely controlled by Echidnal forces it would be a place she would want to avoid after cutting ties with the Oceanus Current. Exactly how this would come into play depends on the plot of the chronicle. If I was playing her as a PC where she wouldn't have this exact build I would like retain some knowledge of Poseidon in the form of a merit like Contacts for example and have the company factor more into her origin and her crossing into the Celestial Currents. Otherwise her main shtick and experiences in her Drowning is tied to combating crude oil and similar hazardous pollution, working her way in and disrupting companies as messily and nastily as possible.<br /> <br /> There's no tie to Poseidon here although her Multilingual inclusion of Korean comes from learning the basics of the language from a fellow Siren she worked with, likely an Echidnal one. The other goal of her draft was a degree of ambiguity for the unwritten aspects, making her adaptable for many kinds of Chronicles as an example character.<br /> <br /> As my Princess game has plenty of antagonists already (although no main villain) again I'm in no position to factor Poseidon into Ixcuina's NPC introduction in that game. Let alone my current plot to lead my players into 2017 involves a full conflict of Tears and Storms on the Twin Cities, in setting having little of a Hopeful population before this point. And Changelings and ghosts are also involved, so Siren is only tied to a tiny ancillary tangent should my players pick up on the plot thread, well after the battle dies down.<br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, really odd segue to jump back to another topic: if Cocytus and Phlegethon are being mildly revised and most of Abyssal Currents can count the antagonist teams in Pokemon for some of their inspiration, perhaps Team Skull of the new Sun and Moon games may provide some material. Course at this time many who don't have the game yet wouldn't want spoilers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","user":"-metablender","date":". 11-30-2016, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:36:43-08:00","id":1010441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010265#post1010265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Minor Templates</u><br /> Making Survivors and Breathless the same is really brilliant. It shows that humanity is going to change from the Cataclysms that enact the Deluge, let alone the exposure to the Song that has not made them Sirens. It easily explains the difference of post-Deluge beings, as they won't have any benefits normally seen amongst Sirens that Therons will have but aren't too vulnerable to a Siren's verses either. It makes any modern day or far future flung Breathless/Survivors companions the same for ease of game mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. :3 And welcome back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010265#post1010265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Choruses</u><br /> So seeing that Choruses are the attempted prestige class or z-splat option for Sirens, the first question to ask is what is their THEME? What is it that binds them together and how does that provide them benefits not common amongst everyday Sirens?<br /> <br /> Each Chronicles system that has a z-splat option does so to provide new opportunities for the character, as any prestige option should. To generalize some examples: Changeling's Entitlements bring the Lost into new social groups, titles, new stories and roles and the power begotten from the Wyrd that fits the Entitlement. In Princess the Embassies give the Hopeful expertise in different avenues beyond the battle of Light vs the Darkness, a new motif to their Regalia and exclusive privileges or powers, and a focus towards different facets of the word both mundane and supernatural. And for Genius (ideally with 2E readdressing the structure) a Fellowship is a niche application, project or field of Mad Science. It is tiered towards one particular Wonder or theorem that is nigh-perfected and avoids the pitfalls lesser Wonders of the same type would have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know a theme is required, although I see what you mean. The only ideas I have is social groups and special powers. To be more specific, the ideas I had at the moment for Choruses came mostly from the VtM Bloodline &quot;Daughters of Cacophony&quot;, abit in how they're all connected by a song together to the point it's kinda creepy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/VtM:Daughters_of_Cacophony\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/VtM:Daughters_of_Cacophony\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/VtM:Daughters_of_Cacophony\" target=\"_blank\"> http://reference.l2fury.com/index.php/VtM:Daughters_of_Cacophony </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I hope it's not minded being asked again, but I have had two ideas for Choruses when it comes to theme. One idea was to base them off of Operas and Musicals, which I imagine would have special powers or the like associated to them. For example, a Chorus known as the Freeshooters are capable of making deals with occult beings (or normal humans, if they're playing the supernatural being) for 7 favors that can be called in at any time. However, one of the favors can be twisted by the supernatural being to anything they desire, kind of like how in the play the devil gave seven magic bullets that hit whatever the target is aiming for, but one of them will be controlled by the devil and will hit whoever they designate it to hit.<br /> <br /> The other idea I had was basing it off of musical genres and different ways to carry out verses. This gives the idea of bands and being able to play out in the Siren's favored musical genre (afterall, it's not called &quot;The Song&quot; for nothing). The only problem is mainly OOC, that musical taste HIGHLY differs between people and it's easy to get into arguments over the genres, especially if we represent them wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010265#post1010265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from how a Chorus should be outlined, they usually have a few prerequisites. Usually Supernatural Tolerance at a certain level, certain Attribute or Skill minimums and some require belonging to a certain faction. Although I would suggest only a minority of Chorus have a faction or Current based prerequisite.<br /> <br /> If the <b>Water</b> represents where the Siren comes from and what she embodies, and the <b>Current</b> is both her outlook, methodology and like mindedness with other Sirens, what niche does the <b>Chorus</b> expand or fulfill?<br /> <br /> From what is initially presented, teamwork looks to be a central point of Choruses. You cannot form a Chorus from an individual. Perhaps besides benefits for herself the Siren can provide a small boon to her fellows <i>(what is a group of Sirens called again, I've forgotten)</i>, and the boon is better when performed with more members of the same Chorus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, that's what a Chorus is meant to be. Focus on teamwork and the like. Given that most gamelines have a prerequisite of at least Supernatural Tolerance 3 to join a Z-Splat, it'll most likely remain the same for Siren. I don't know if there'll be higher levels, I do like the ideas of there being three positions a Siren can ascend to. At Akashic Record 3, the Siren is simply a Chorus Initiate, a Soprano, Baritone, Alto, Tenor, Base, whatever is most fitting for his/her voice. At Akashic Record 5, the Siren ascends to be a Lead Singer of the Chorus. At Akashic Record 7, the Siren is the Conductor, the one who leads the Chorus and how it sounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010265#post1010265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the unifying themes of each Chorus several have been presented. One way is to allow the Siren more formats to enact the Song, the music and theatrical connotations. Another is a Chorus formed to deal with specific kinds of disasters, conflicts or other issues. The Chorus could even be the background of a certain kind of story, giving the Siren an 'in' with different facets of life while remaining inconspicuous. A Chorus is also a soft way of inducting Crossover themes (like the way Princess does it) to represent the Siren approach to material not found in the typical Siren game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Pardon, I didn't read this section when I posted the ideas for Themes I had above. But after reading up abit on TvTropes, I have to ask, would the idea of a Chorus being the background of a certain kind of story being somewhat like the trope linked below? :3<br /> <br /> Although, in somewhat the same vein as the Theatrical/play connotations, I fear this idea still steps abit on Changeling's toes due to the story tropes in play and whatnot. I'm sorry if I'm sounding too limiting and the like when I say these kinds of things.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GreekChorus\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GreekChorus</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010279#post1010279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the double post, I have been working on drafting some Siren NPC characters and wanted to share the first of these characters. I plan to use her to introduce Siren to my mega crossover game that is Princess centered, so the Crossover material is set aside in it's own tab. Nonetheless I wanted to provide basis for the character without Crossover in mind, as she would serve as a model for the type of Siren I would want to play as my first character in a Siren: the Drowning game.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Character Draft: Ixcuina</u><br /> </span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Concept: snarky ex-Echidnal filth eater</i></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Water:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Discordia (Gardenia)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Current:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Buoyancy</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Favored Opuses:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Beauty, Sound, Water, Taint, Blood, Chaos</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Favored Conclusion:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Travel</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Attributes:</b><br /> Intelligence </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">2, Wits 4, Resolve 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Strength 2, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3<br /> Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mental Skills:</b> Computer 1, Crafts 1, Medicine 3, Occult 4, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 1, Brawl 1, Drive 2, Larceny 3, Stealth 2, Survival 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 3, Empathy 4, Intimidation 2, Socialize 3, Streetwise 4, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <b>Specialties:</b><br /> Crafts: Destruction<br /> Survival: Hazardous Areas<br /> Streetwise: Carnal Pleasures<br /> <br /> <b>Flow:</b> Disruptive<br /> <b>Beaching:</b> Dirty</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Size:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Perception:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 6</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Willpower:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 5</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Akashic Record:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Pneuma:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> 13/4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Refraction:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> -4 (Song +1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Introductions:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Location, Sentient, Self</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Insensate</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Opuses:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Beauty, Sound, Water, Blood, Taint, Chaos, Earth, Growth, Darkness</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Conclusions:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Travel 4, Invoke 3, Disturb 5, Calm 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Trace:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Bonus for the Time aspect</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Diluvian Form:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> max 7 Alterations</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Common:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Boneless Imitation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Gardenia:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Fetid Touch</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Tropicana:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Poison Immunity</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Malformations:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Poisonous Blood, Slimy Physique, Acidic Excretion</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Knowledges:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">4 total from Double Dipping merit</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Gardenia:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> History Repeats Itself, You Get As Much As You Give</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Discordia:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Water Changes Land Does Not, Conflict Is Life</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mental Merits:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Tolerance for Biology, Language (English), Multilingual (Nahuatl, Korean)</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>; Spanish is her primary language</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Physical Merits:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Small Framed, Double Jointed, Demolisher (1 dot)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Social Merits:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Fixer, Fast Talking (Style; 3 dots), Striking Looks (Unseemly, 1 dot)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Siren Merits:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Double Dipping, Bel Canto</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Appearance:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Ixcuina has dark skin befitting south Mexican Aztec descended features. Short and quite petite, her body is quite flexible making her a natural contortionist. She has a scar from a cleft lip. She's been letting her hair out but doesn't style it much, having thick dreads as a mass of snarling strands.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Given her Malformations there's a sickly bruised choler to her skin and her skin's slime is glossy, like tanning lotion, so she has to avoid whites and light colors.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Her Diluvian form is as blue as window cleaner, with rubbery skin and wet clinging blue hair smoothed down the back of her neck. Her tail is long and sinuous, something like an eel\u2019s, with the skeletal frame of cartilage branching out with vestigial fins stretched between. Her green blood is more prevalent in areas like her hands and mouth, her eyes a green-yellow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Most noticeable in her Diluvian form is the smudge of questionable whatsit around her mouth and nose, a deep brown covering her cleft lip that forms a pattern of strands along the rest of her face and neck.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Personality:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Ixcuina is a women well accustomed to the worst the world has to offer, one who remains defiant in response to these troubles. While appearing to have a languid, resigned and almost slothful personality her signature brand of black comedy is the tip of a feisty avenger. She frequently thinks outside the box and relishes in using taboos to catch opponents off guard. A frequent trick of hers is to catch others at their most vulnerable in public bathrooms. Although quite driven as a Siren she enjoys meeting simple, basic desires and doing as she pleases.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Backstory:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Ixcuina, as she now calls herself, grew up in the region south of the Gulf of Mexico, a land of highs and lows. Lows included the mingling trade of Colombian drugs and Mexican cartels. As she grew older her hometown grew more corrupt with crime and pollution. The dregs of society have no hope when both neighboring sets of Civilization reject them, the very land itself refusing to aid as Nature worsens at maltreatment.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Her full despairing event was being in the midst of a shootout between two gangs, her travel through the Deluge sympathetic to another event far across the Gulf where oil corporations really screwed up just outside of American waters. The Deepwater Horizon oil spill.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">In the Deluge she saw an earth where such pollution had reached its penultimate turmoil. The flooded seas a mire of crude sludge, stricken wildlife dead in the oceans and flaming spills blocking out the skies with smoke.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Her survival instincts were ones of desperation, needing any way out of this cataclysmic destruction humanity had reeked on itself in pursuit of energy and greed. It brought Ixcuina into the depths of Echidna's domain, the dark mother welcome to new recruits that would agree to help her help humanity. Fixing Ixcuina with the means to survive this massive oil spill, Echidna joined her with another group of her Sirens and Vodianoi sent to punish those that failed to remedy their crimes against nature that threatened humanity so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">She was a capable agent amongst the Echidnal Sirens, going off to enact eco-terrorism and returning with more human resources for Vodianoi. Her resolve to follow Echidna's aims, enforced by the sheer number of malformations she had at one time, soon began to waver as her Akashic Record increased. First it was the fights amongst other Abyssal Currents, which drew attention of the Celestial Currents and other foes. And from each defeat or pyrrhic victory, Ixcuina had more questions brought on from the realization that there are more Sirens in the sea than she imagined, each with very different viewpoints.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Questions her fellow Echidnal Sirens didn\u2019t appreciate, especially the thought that Echidna\u2019s deprived mutilations would never produce the next stage of humanity that could survive the Deluge. After leaving anonymous tip offs to Sirens from the Celestial Currents about Echidna\u2019s recent aims, she effectively defected from the sea monster\u2019s faction in the midst of an ambush (more of a slaughter, really) of her former comrades.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Since then Ixcunia has been enjoying newfound freedom, her independent streak leading her along the Current of Buoyancy, rarely keeping close ties with other Sirens save for the original Sirens she developed rapport with as an Echidnal agent. Still, the oil spoiled Deluge she experienced strives her to prevent or punish widescale pollution, be it actual or thematic corruption of life.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Crossover:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> </span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">After distancing herself from Echidna, Ixcunia once came across the site of a Tainted Place that she mistook for a Quagmire. After some trial and error she found that the wounds left of the world from the Darkness could be impacted by similar Verses she used combating mundane pollution. Although Darkspawn were just mindless monsters and easily considered foes, she was more sympathetic towards Darkened humans if unsure what to do about them. From her spective the tainted Darkness was a potent stain not easily cleaned, the unfortunate Darkened could only be prevented from getting worse rather than better.<br /> <br /> Developing a specialty towards Tainted Areas, investigation of a location in the MidWest got Ixcuina in over her head. Low on Pneuma when she needed to escape, the Mnemosyne that tended the Taint managing to capture her and developing an ingenious way to imprison the Siren where she would be unable gain Pneuma or form a rhythm to enact even the most basic verse.<br /> <br /> Given that the Light forms the natural enemy of the Darkness, perhaps some Princesses will manage to discover her in time when dealing with the Mnemosyne foe.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about it, this is a good char. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010384#post1010384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for not contributing to this thread for awhile. Anyway. how is progress on the Honolulu chapter? Also, would Ixcuina be familiar with Poseidon? Considering she was a Echidnal and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I haven't actually done much of anything with Honolulu. Lack of inspiration. &gt;&lt;&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010407#post1010407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honolulu is a big focus being one of the final core chapters (as opposed to supplementary material) so I know the shift of effort is pointed there. I've only been to Maui myself so I can't think of anything to suggest outside of being watered down Hawaii 5-O. I imagine Tropicana is the most popular water along the islands in the Pacific, so my interest is what Sirens of the other waters would be like in Honolulu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, Tropicana is the most active water in Honolulu I imagine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010407#post1010407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If locations from other islands were ever wanted for adventure blurbs, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haleakal\u0101\" target=\"_blank\">Haleakala Crater</a>, the main volcano on Maui, would be an interesting spot. A potential Quagmire would tie heavily to the Earth aspect of Gardenia, as there are protected plants along the crest of the crater prevent access from other people. There is also a space observatory nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems fitting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010407#post1010407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: also, really odd segue to jump back to another topic: if Cocytus and Phlegethon are being mildly revised and most of Abyssal Currents can count the antagonist teams in Pokemon for some of their inspiration, perhaps Team Skull of the new Sun and Moon games may provide some material. Course at this time many who don't have the game yet wouldn't want spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which reminds me, they are done being revised. And I really need to get Pokemon Moon. &gt;w&gt;&quot; No spoilers please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:23:20-08:00","id":1010491,"title":"","content":"<u>Choruses</u><br /> When it comes to finding purpose for Choruses that finds ground between the themes, mechanics and various ways you can take it, there should be one foundation from which each Chorus is built.<br /> <br /> A Chorus is made in <b><i>support</i></b> of something.<br /> <br /> If Water is their origin and Current their motivation, the Chorus is what brings various Sirens together for the support of something greater. No matter how small or background their part, the Sirens within the Chorus are vital for dynamic and continued support of this ideal. Sometimes this requires joining together with others of the Chorus. Sometimes this requires knowing when to take center stage and when to stay in the wings so another can act. Sometimes it can be a grueling obligation, for the Chorus is also the refrain that occurs again and again in the Song. Some Sirens take comfort in this, knowing that even if the point of a Chorus disappears it will one day become important again.<br /> <br /> You could label the 'what' that a Chorus supports based on category although I think this is unnecessary. With a core of 'support' you can have Sirens dedicated to various goals and the enhanced abilities to match. This could be providing the support of a story or sequence to come to pass, much like the roles Changelings and Prometheans put themselves in. It could be support of a specific culture, genre or style for how it can be applied to the Siren's woven magic. Choruses can also be proactive or preventive towards various kinds of disasters, both social and natural, all the way up to insuring a specific version of the Deluge comes to pass for more ambiguously nefarious takes on Choruses.<br /> <br /> In this way Choruses are much like Embassies and Protectorates from Princess, with a side of Changeling Entitlements. I do like the Princess variety of z-splat where you have tiers of effects for that sense of achievement and progression, although that isn't to say it should carbon copy that method of a prestige option.<br /> <br /> I'm waffling about what else to cast as concrete for the origination of a Chorus. At the same time it provides new avenues and benefits you don't what it to replace other parts of the system. Perhaps a Siren can join and leave Choruses easily, or even have multiple in effect if she can manage it. Yet her advancement in multiple won't be as significant as a single or primary Chorus. I'm not sure what determines that limit. You also don't what the Chorus benefits to be redundant of Verse or Trace mechanics, as there is already a lot of freeform in those systems. On one hand using an Opus as a prerequisite for a Chorus would represent both the niche and variety of Sirens within it, although you <i>shouldn't</i> have to belong in a certain Chorus to use an Opus (&amp; Introduction/Conclusion) in any particular way.<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> I also ended up putting down another character draft to the page, one that I hadn't yet although he was bouncing in my head for some time. Yet not as long as Ixcuina, who was worked over for several days with her draft.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Character Draft: Roe Lannister</u></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>Concept: self sustaining acoustic musician</i><br /> <br /> <b>Water:</b> Freshwater<br /> <b>Current:</b> Harmony<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Opuses:</b> <i>Beauty, Sound, Water, Human, Technology, Fate</i><br /> <b>Favored Conclusion:</b> <i>Calm</i><br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b><br /> Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 4<br /> Strength 3, Dexterity 1, Stamina 2<br /> Presence 2, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 4, Computer 2, Investigation 2, Occult 2, Politics 3<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Survival 3<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 4, Empathy 2, Expression 4, Persuasion 2, Socialize 4<br /> <br /> <b>Specialties:</b> Computer (Sound-mixing, Digital Distribution), Expression (Folk Music), Socialize (Concerts)<br /> <br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Perception:</b> 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <br /> <b>Flow:</b> Spontaneity<br /> <b>Beaching:</b> Seclusion<br /> <br /> <b>Akashic Record:</b> 3<br /> <b>Pneuma:</b> 12/3<br /> <b>Refraction:</b> -2<br /> <br /> <b>Introductions:</b> Sentient, Location, Society<br /> <b>Opuses:</b> Beauty, Sound, Human, Technology, Fate, Animal, Growth, Dream, Passion<br /> <b>Conclusions:</b> Calm 4, Restore 3, Protect 2, Sense 4<br /> <br /> <b>Trace:</b> bonus to Audience<br /> <br /> <b>Diluvian Form:</b> max 6 Alterations<br /> <b>Common:</b> Whalesong<br /> <b>Polaria:</b> Ice Walker<br /> <b>Freshwater:</b> Anuran Breath, Amphibious Legs<br /> <b>Discordia:</b> The Living Fossil Coelacanth<br /> <br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> The Future is Now, Life is Always Changing<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Merits:</b> Common Sense, Direction Sense, Indomitable, Meditative Mind (4 dots)<br /> <b>Physical Merits:</b> Ambidextrous<br /> <b>Social Merits:</b> Fame (2 dots; musician), Barfly, Inspiring, Safe Place (2 dots; cabin)<br /> <b>Siren Merits:</b> Enchanting Voice (2 dots), Theronic Companion (3 dots)<br /> <br /> <b>Companion:</b> Matthias the \u201cMarsh Hound\u201d<br /> Taking the mundane appearance of a well trained husky and lab mix, the hound is more like an aquatic wolf with flipper appendages, a seal-like pelt and coloration matching the frozen marshlands. Friends know Matthias to accompany Roe most anywhere and for being notoriously thirsty.<br /> Size: 4; Alterations: Thalassic Movement, Lamian Senses, Amphibious Legs<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Roe is an aged looking man approaching his seventies. He has an angular face, long grey/white hair and an unshaven face. He favors casual yet durable wear including down jackets, pullovers and tan pants. He has a slim build with strong legs.<br /> <br /> In his Diluvian form Roe looks mostly the same, with wrinkly waterlogged skin and webbed digits. If anything his hair becomes extra shaggy, almost like thatch. His amphibus features and retained humanoid frame, along with hometown location, are indicative of legends about swamp or marsh men. Particularly like the character of \u2018Puddleglum, the Marshwiggle\u2019 from the Chronicles of Narnia.<br /> <br /> <b>Personality:</b> Roe is a friendly and outgoing man, very sensitive towards changes in society and the stretches of nature along his northwoods hometown along Lake Superior. He has earned some modest fame as a folk musician, developing a signature style where he \u2018records\u2019 his music live by layering vocal and guitar tracks with a pedal operated sound mixer.<br /> <br /> Although very comfortable onstage and other public areas, Roe remains a private man who favors stretches of solitude. People interest him, because his music is derived from the human condition. It is within nature, the deep forests and cold lakes bordering Minnesota and Canada, that he finds solace. Roe is very much a slow and steady type of guy, often eschewing contact entirely between tours when he is at work at new music. His love is to bring nature, technology and music together, a desire that has grown stronger since his Drowning.<br /> <br /> <b>Backstory:</b> Monroe Lannister, to use his full name, did not experience his Drowning until he was past middle age. For the first half of his life he was a curious and passionate if wayward individual, unsure of where he wanted to be in the world. Feeling that his hometown was small and too confining he had many false starts as an adult trying to find a new niche.<br /> <br /> He traveled extensively, tried his hands at the fast paced world of business, studied new technologies and rarely stayed in a career for long. He did hone his skills as a musician at this time but never did anything with it beyond busking at street corners. Roe had no ambitions, no direction and no family. Ultimately he had no ties of his own.<br /> <br /> Roe recounts his Drowning as a bitter soul wracking pang of nostalgia and homesickness. He remembered his hometown, the one that felt so confining when he was in his youth. He remembered exploring the woods behind his home, of endless gazing across the lapping waves of the great lake. He remembered the simple, rural people and the qualities of the small town that rooted them within family and community, along with others like him who had spurned their early life the first chance they got.<br /> <br /> He experienced the both widespread and personal horror of the Deluge. Of people who forgot their roots, of humanity forgetting what it owes to the geography and planet that sustains them. Of a world deaded, the lakes destroyed and the woods cut down from endless urban sprawl. Of the dangers when Civilization is left unchecked, not only is Nature destroyed but humanity and its descendants also get the raw end of the deal. Domed to futile lives under the trappings of Civilization, its concrete and metal and technology that is uncentered from the core of community, protection and love for one\u2019s home. A sorrow that says 'if only there was more that had been done.'<br /> <br /> Roe was reminded that change did not need to be big. Small changes, even as simple as a smile at the right time or a simple comfort for a troubled soul, can add up to make all the difference. Another man of his age might have languished that he had wasted his life for so long but for Roe it was a new beginning. If his only legacy was going to be the music that reminds people to find their family and community, bridging the needs of both Nature and Civilization, then that was enough for him.<br /> <br /> He returned to the hometown he left behind, taking home in a cabin that had no plumbing or modern comforts until he installed green technology only for his basic needs. The majority of the power was dedicated to his recording studio, his music all self produced. He became a prolific local musician in a relatively short time, reintegrating himself in his community and gaining a modicum of recognition across the MidWest. Alongside his career he invested in green technologies, joined or encouraged grassroots movements, and becoming a fixture in an annual festival along the shores of Superior. The great lake served as the testing ground to explore his new abilities. He is a musician of two musics, the sound of his guitar and the twisting tale of the great Song.<br /> <br /> Roe prefers to work indirectly as a Siren, not only encouraging humanity to rethink their place in the world but to inspire and support his fellow Sirens as well. If it is within his power he would travel to assist another Celestial Siren, especially in his own Current. Otherwise he remains in his semi-reclusive lifestyle in the heart of the northwoods. A life that is punctuated by sojourns into the Deluge, observing the flux of its cataclysms and the initial breakdowns that cause its ripples. From this he creates new music or fosters communication across Sirens continental and international that are striving for a positive change. It was from such a journey that he trained the Theron he named Matthias.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","user":"-metablender","date":".  forgot Conclusion ratings 12-01-2016, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T23:32:33-08:00","id":1010533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010491#post1010491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Choruses</u><br /> When it comes to finding purpose for Choruses that finds ground between the themes, mechanics and various ways you can take it, there should be one foundation from which each Chorus is built.<br /> <br /> A Chorus is made in <b><i>support</i></b> of something.<br /> <br /> If Water is their origin and Current their motivation, the Chorus is what brings various Sirens together for the support of something greater. No matter how small or background their part, the Sirens within the Chorus are vit