pecially in his own Current. Otherwise he remains in his semi-reclusive lifestyle in the heart of the northwoods. A life that is punctuated by sojourns into the Deluge, observing the flux of its cataclysms and the initial breakdowns that cause its ripples. From this he creates new music or fosters communication across Sirens continental and international that are striving for a positive change. It was from such a journey that he trained the Theron he named Matthias.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>This is good. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T15:27:42-08:00","id":1010844,"title":"","content":"Today at work (as I frequently let my mind percolate ideas in the background) I had more ideas about how a Chorus could be structured. I'm not sure if the mechanics 'sound' proper for Siren but it would be a unique z-splat option to expand upon Siren further.<br /> <br /> Continuing from the idea that a Chorus is formed in <i>support</i> of something, the tier of benefit the Siren receives from a Chorus is factored by how much effort she puts into it. There is also a timely aspect to the Chorus, membership 'renewing' every month which hereafter will be referred to as a Cycle. The length of a Cycle is the personal timeline the Siren experiences. For example, if she spent a day in the Deluge but returned to earth a week after she departed, her Cycle only would have advanced a day.<br /> <br /> Membership in a Chorus provides 3-4 benefits with permanency in the following categories: <b>Passive</b>, <b>Active</b> and <b>Invested</b>.<br /> <br /> A Siren receives the <b>Passive</b> benefit the moment she joins a Chorus she meets the prerequisites for. Prerequisites would be Akashic Record 3 and any Attribute/Skill etc ratings. The Siren always receives the Passive benefit from a Chorus she has joined until she decides to leave it. A Passive benefit should provide, at most, a +1 bonus, automatic Trace success or a simple effect normally conveyed by a Conclusion 1 Verse.<br /> <br /> The <b>Active</b> benefit shows the Siren is not passively sitting in her Chorus, that she communicates and helps others in her Chorus frequently. Each Cycle, the Siren can have only one Active Benefit from a single Chorus. For Sirens only in one Chorus they receive that Active benefit. For Sirens in two or more Choruses, they must select which Chorus they are Active in each Cycle, trading off one Active Benefit for another. To change Active Benefits early the Siren must invest Pneuma, covered below. The Active benefit is either an increased version of the Passive benefit or a new, slightly more widespread effect.<br /> <br /> A Siren receives the <b>Invested</b> benefit by dedicating her full capabilities and energy to supporting her Chorus, above and beyond the duty of Active membership. Being Invested means you have both the Passive and Active benefits, so the Siren needed to have selected the Active benefit in the Chorus for this Cycle. A Siren is Invested in her Chorus by giving most of her voice into the snippet of the Song her Chorus represents. This is done by spending a hefty cost of Pneuma, the precise tier of the Invested benefit being scalable for a gross amount of Pneuma for either a factored dice bonus or widespread and nuanced effect. The base Investment cost is also the price for the Siren to become Active in a Chorus before the end of her Cycle.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although this analogy has nothing to do with the themes of Siren: the Drowning, where a Siren sits in her Chorus(es) in this model is very much like a game of Monopoly. Initially joining a Chorus and being Passive is like owning one property in Monopoly. You get a little perk but don't receive much until you collect the whole set (become Active). Once a Siren is Active if she has the Pneuma to spend each Cycle she can become Invested, which in the Monopoly analogy is when you start putting down houses and hotels. Normally only Sirens with a high Akashic Record will be able to be Invested in the Choruses. A Siren could remain in a single Chorus and be able to use its benefits more consistently. Or the Siren could be a member of different Choruses, receiving all the Passive benefits but only a sole Active and chance for Invested benefits at one time each Cycle. Leaving a Chorus completely is when you no longer own any Monopoly properties in the set.<br /> <br /> While that's a draft for the general layout of a Chorus, I admit I don't have any full example Choruses with theme and mechanics to help demonstrate the idea at the time of this post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T19:43:56-08:00","id":1011316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1010844#post1010844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today at work (as I frequently let my mind percolate ideas in the background) I had more ideas about how a Chorus could be structured. I'm not sure if the mechanics 'sound' proper for Siren but it would be a unique z-splat option to expand upon Siren further.<br /> <br /> Continuing from the idea that a Chorus is formed in <i>support</i> of something, the tier of benefit the Siren receives from a Chorus is factored by how much effort she puts into it. There is also a timely aspect to the Chorus, membership 'renewing' every month which hereafter will be referred to as a Cycle. The length of a Cycle is the personal timeline the Siren experiences. For example, if she spent a day in the Deluge but returned to earth a week after she departed, her Cycle only would have advanced a day.<br /> <br /> Membership in a Chorus provides 3-4 benefits with permanency in the following categories: <b>Passive</b>, <b>Active</b> and <b>Invested</b>.<br /> <br /> A Siren receives the <b>Passive</b> benefit the moment she joins a Chorus she meets the prerequisites for. Prerequisites would be Akashic Record 3 and any Attribute/Skill etc ratings. The Siren always receives the Passive benefit from a Chorus she has joined until she decides to leave it. A Passive benefit should provide, at most, a +1 bonus, automatic Trace success or a simple effect normally conveyed by a Conclusion 1 Verse.<br /> <br /> The <b>Active</b> benefit shows the Siren is not passively sitting in her Chorus, that she communicates and helps others in her Chorus frequently. Each Cycle, the Siren can have only one Active Benefit from a single Chorus. For Sirens only in one Chorus they receive that Active benefit. For Sirens in two or more Choruses, they must select which Chorus they are Active in each Cycle, trading off one Active Benefit for another. To change Active Benefits early the Siren must invest Pneuma, covered below. The Active benefit is either an increased version of the Passive benefit or a new, slightly more widespread effect.<br /> <br /> A Siren receives the <b>Invested</b> benefit by dedicating her full capabilities and energy to supporting her Chorus, above and beyond the duty of Active membership. Being Invested means you have both the Passive and Active benefits, so the Siren needed to have selected the Active benefit in the Chorus for this Cycle. A Siren is Invested in her Chorus by giving most of her voice into the snippet of the Song her Chorus represents. This is done by spending a hefty cost of Pneuma, the precise tier of the Invested benefit being scalable for a gross amount of Pneuma for either a factored dice bonus or widespread and nuanced effect. The base Investment cost is also the price for the Siren to become Active in a Chorus before the end of her Cycle.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although this analogy has nothing to do with the themes of Siren: the Drowning, where a Siren sits in her Chorus(es) in this model is very much like a game of Monopoly. Initially joining a Chorus and being Passive is like owning one property in Monopoly. You get a little perk but don't receive much until you collect the whole set (become Active). Once a Siren is Active if she has the Pneuma to spend each Cycle she can become Invested, which in the Monopoly analogy is when you start putting down houses and hotels. Normally only Sirens with a high Akashic Record will be able to be Invested in the Choruses. A Siren could remain in a single Chorus and be able to use its benefits more consistently. Or the Siren could be a member of different Choruses, receiving all the Passive benefits but only a sole Active and chance for Invested benefits at one time each Cycle. Leaving a Chorus completely is when you no longer own any Monopoly properties in the set.<br /> <br /> While that's a draft for the general layout of a Chorus, I admit I don't have any full example Choruses with theme and mechanics to help demonstrate the idea at the time of this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely putting you in the Special Thanks for making the Chorus outline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really like how this looks, it's a good system for Siren and it fits the ideas presented above as well as one I haven't presented. Namely, the ideas of how Fellowships were in Genius and how Geniuses could temporarily join one and being called a &quot;Scholarship&quot;. The idea of having a passive Benefit and that Sirens could belong to one temporarily.<br /> <br /> I wonder at the possibility of Choruses (as a Passive Effect) also being able to favor Opuses or Conclusions, making it easy to gain experience in a Conclusion or to form up Stanzas for Opuses.<br /> <br /> Anyways, just as a thought, here's my first attempt at making a Chorus.<br /> <br /> <b>The Order of the Black Huntsmen</b><br /> <i>Now now, don't fret about our deal. It was clearly spelt out, and you put your name on the dotted line. Maybe next time you'll actually look over the fine print and know that I always get my due.</i><br /> <b>Aka: </b>The Order of Strangers, The Order of Old Scratch<br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Samiels, Dealers, Strangers, Freeshooters<br /> <br /> Throughout history, there have been many stories of people who have made deals with the supernatural for various boons. Sometimes it's to extend lives, sometimes it's to make a simple fortune, sometimes it's to win their beloved's heart. But in all cases, there's always a price, almost always equal to the boon gained. The Sirens have taken note of these events, forging a Chorus based on the simple support of the concept of equivalent exchange: gaining one thing and something of equal value must be lost. <br /> <br /> The Order of the Black Huntsmen are therefore happy to play the role as a mysterious benefactor that treats their targets to whatever their hearts desire, until the day comes that they eventually take something of equal value away. Sometimes it helps against the deluge, but those within this Chorus can sometimes care less and focus more on the present.<br /> <br /> <b>The Huntsmen and the Requirements: </b>The Huntsmen, or Huntswomen, are usually made up from the ranks of the Vaporia or Polaria Waters, given the formers knowledge of choice and consequence and the latter's knowledge that eventually everything must end. The Currents of Buoyancy and Cocytus are also enamored with this Chorus, as the Winding Current is usually good enough to carry out manipulations to grant boons and take them away, and Cocytus either has things of great power to offer to potential &quot;signatories&quot; or are willing to dig up dirty secrets to show the world of their target as their due. <br /> <br /> In order to join the Order, the Siren must not just display the prerequisite for her connection to the Song, but also through her ability to manipulate others and get them willing to sign for what they dream of. Their Persuasion Skill must be at 3 or above.<br /> <br /> <b>Passive: </b>The Samiel gains a +1 Bonus to all Traces and Verses that deal with affecting someone she currently has an outstanding deal with. <br /> <b>Active: </b>The Samiel may add their Akashic Record to all Traces and verses that deal with affecting someone she currently has an outstanding deal with.<br /> <b>Invested: </b>The Samiel can at any time make a deal with a mortal, in which the mortal is entitled to receive a number of boons equal to the Siren's Akashic Record. They may choose whether the boon is small (like using a verse for a Mortal's devices), medium (the mortal desires Resources 2 and above) or even large (the mortal wishes to start a new life elsewhere). The number of beginning boons are small boons, but a mortal can give up two small boons to gain a medium boon, or three small boons to get one large boon, or vice versa.<br /> <br /> Then, within the time agreed upon to grant the boons, the Huntsman must deliver upon them whenever the mortal calls upon them. One catch is that the Huntsman is free to twist any one of the boons to whatever they desire, usually equivalent to the boons already spent or used. A Hunstman can choose to do the twist at the first boon called in, meaning the mortal will not suffer from any further twists but also denying any equal exchange, turning the Huntsman's bonuses from this current into penalties (effectively, this means the Siren takes the bad luck on herself). <br /> <br /> However, a Huntsman may choose to hold back committing their twists until after doing a few boons already. Doing so in this manner grants a +1 for each small boon completed beforehand, +2 for each medium boon, and +3 for each large boon. This bonus stacks with the Passive and Active bonuses from this Chorus, and the bonuses apply towards any roll that would help set up or act out the Twist, so a Huntsmen who waits to twist a boon until it's the very last boon usually find that their efforts succeed without fail. Huntsmen who do not commit a Twist find that the boons are taken out of their own lives instead, which is a harsh warning to those in the Order to take it out on those who desire favors.<br /> <br /> <br /> How does this look for a Chorus? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:04:18-08:00","id":1012270,"title":"","content":"Holy crap. I can't believe I'm saying this but it seems like it's Siren's birthday today. Been a year since I began this project, and to be honest I thought I wouldn't be near done by now. I'm happy though that we're at least on the last two laps and a half: Choruses, Honolulu and Ascension/Descension. :3<br /> <br /> Anyways, I haven't been completely inactive or uninspired. I've made up a list of ideas for Choruses. I should note that I've expanded the definition of &quot;Support of&quot; when it comes to Choruses. Basically, &quot;Support of&quot; is defined here as &quot;The Siren cares for the core concept the Chorus is about, whether she is for the concept or against it, and Choruses mainly help in dealing with the concept no matter what&quot;. So for example, a Siren within a Chorus based on Drug Trade could be for or against the idea of Drug Trade, be it legalizing it or slapping on harder penalties or restrictions for it. <br /> <br /> Chorus Examples As Of Now: Support of Drug Trade<br /> Support of Equivalent Exchange<br /> Support of Governmental parties<br /> Support of Global Warming<br /> Support of Politics<br /> Support of Police/Navy/Army<br /> Support of Schooling/College<br /> Support of Ecological Politics or Environmentalism<br /> I feel that these could potentially show that Sirens don't have to just be doing Environmentalism (though it is a theme), that they can expand to other areas should the players or ST want to deal with different things. The biggest themes I can imagine for Choruses are &quot;current events&quot; or issues within the mortal world like rights and stuff. :3<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T17:11:35-08:00","id":1012272,"title":"","content":"Congrats. I am glad to have helped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T21:06:27-08:00","id":1014134,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, time for an update. Using Metablender's model, I've constructed the Choruses page! I've also added in the Chorus of the Black Huntsmen and changed their benefits abit to be different and more useful. I also have a few example Choruses depicted, ones that I plan on making. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> <b>Choruses: </b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14r45y-H3mweVul34mzTMMotZJ-MCG-1SgUDVUWw-H9I/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T19:03:03-08:00","id":1014571,"title":"","content":"I realized something. Poseidon would make a great Deviant organization","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T00:50:05-08:00","id":1015180,"title":"","content":"Let's stay on-topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T18:00:06-08:00","id":1015919,"title":"","content":"Sorry to drop off for a bit but it looks like there's been a lot happening (and belated b-day cake for the anniversary). And there's even a TvTropes page too, which is cool.<br /> <br /> I had some more refinements for the Chorus model. Passive and Active are as they are, stackable depending on where a Siren puts her focus. Invested, which requires a lot of Pneuma to upkeep a new permanent effect, has its own tier from the effects being scalable for Pneuma price.<br /> <br /> Comparing the Akashic Record table to possible costs, I thought of having Invested be tiered for 30, 50 and 75 Pneuma. Or for better modulation, perhaps, the basic Investment is 20 Pneuma per x effect. This doesn't mean that the Siren needs to have a Pneuma pool big enough to Invest all in one go, although high Akashic Record Sirens would have an easier time of achieving a certain level of Investment. For lesser Sirens, they achieve the Invested effect once they are able to encode enough Pneuma into the song, the duration starting once that has been achieved. A partial Investment can be kept indefinitely if the Siren is part of the Chorus, although doesn't take effect until effectively powered of course.<br /> <br /> So let's try applying this to some Chorus models.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Chorus of the Black Huntsman</u><br /> <br /> Invested: the Faustian Bargain</b><br /> The Siren can grant a robust supernatural deal with a mortal, encoded into the Song that binds the Siren and their target into an inescapable declaration. A deal is tracked by its Boons, which are usually weighted for the mortal. However, the Siren can force her partner to upkeep their end of the deal by receiving their own Boon representing the mortal's efforts, which is free but cannot be greater than the mortal's Boon. However the mortal agrees to more terms (Siren Boons) to increase the effectiveness of their Boon by one level.<br /> <br /> [30 or 20x Pneuma] Small Boon: a permanent minor effect, like a Conclusion 1-2 Verse or new Social/Mental Merits<br /> [50 or 40x Pneuma] Medium Boon: a permanent effect like a Conclusion 3 Verse, new Physical Merits, new Skill dots, or 2 Small Boon effects<br /> [75 or 60x Pneuma] Large Boon: a permanent effect like a Conclusion 4-5 Verse, new Attribute dots, 2 Medium Boon effects or 3-6 Small Boon effects<br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> <u>Commentary:</u> this is an interesting Chorus as much like the Embassy to Stories for Princess it grants the Siren in this case one of the main systems of another game line, the Changeling ability to craft and bind others to Pledges. Yet it isn't dependent on having Changeling present in the game for it to be used, unlike the Embassy to Stories privileges that grant Unseen Sense: Wyrd and use the talecrafting rules. Thematically, for the scope of your Chronicle, it could be the Wyrd upholding the bargain if you ran a crossover game, although it works on its own merits for being a pledge 'cast out into the Song' that will then recur to the benefit of both sides if the terms are upheld. Like an omega level Verse. There's a lot of shared terminology with Changeling, although that is only because both the game and the Chorus are drawing from similar folklore, and again a point for the Chorus side for not needing another venue to become required reading.<br /> <br /> This is really making me want to blend Sirens and Changelings together more. I am having plenty of plot ideas involving Siren flesh entering a Goblin Market.<br /> <br /> ((Future posts, a sweep on the other Choruses and posting my own Chorus draft))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","user":"-metablender","date":". 12-11-2016, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T18:23:18-08:00","id":1015924,"title":"","content":"Good job on making it to tvtropes. My only question is what trope would Poseidon fall under?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T19:36:20-08:00","id":1015943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1015919#post1015919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to drop off for a bit but it looks like there's been a lot happening (and belated b-day cake for the anniversary). And there's even a TvTropes page too, which is cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine. And I know of the TvTropes page. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1015919#post1015919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had some more refinements for the Chorus model. Passive and Active are as they are, stackable depending on where a Siren puts her focus. Invested, which requires a lot of Pneuma to upkeep a new permanent effect, has its own tier from the effects being scalable for Pneuma price.<br /> <br /> Comparing the Akashic Record table to possible costs, I thought of having Invested be tiered for 30, 50 and 75 Pneuma. Or for better modulation, perhaps, the basic Investment is 20 Pneuma per x effect. This doesn't mean that the Siren needs to have a Pneuma pool big enough to Invest all in one go, although high Akashic Record Sirens would have an easier time of achieving a certain level of Investment. For lesser Sirens, they achieve the Invested effect once they are able to encode enough Pneuma into the song, the duration starting once that has been achieved. A partial Investment can be kept indefinitely if the Siren is part of the Chorus, although doesn't take effect until effectively powered of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? I mean, I know that that you said the idea of spending loads of Pneuma would be a thing for Choruses, but I didn't imagine that much. If I may ask though, would Investing Pneuma be kinda the same thing as...let's say Binding Mania in Genius Foundations? Or does it just cover &quot;spending X amount of Pnuema for the Choruses needs no matter what it was spent for (Verses or Trace that were in line with the Chorus). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1015919#post1015919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's try applying this to some Chorus models.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Chorus of the Black Huntsman</u><br /> <br /> Invested: the Faustian Bargain</b><br /> The Siren can grant a robust supernatural deal with a mortal, encoded into the Song that binds the Siren and their target into an inescapable declaration. A deal is tracked by its Boons, which are usually weighted for the mortal. However, the Siren can force her partner to upkeep their end of the deal by receiving their own Boon representing the mortal's efforts, which is free but cannot be greater than the mortal's Boon. However the mortal agrees to more terms (Siren Boons) to increase the effectiveness of their Boon by one level.<br /> <br /> [30 or 20x Pneuma] Small Boon: a permanent minor effect, like a Conclusion 1-2 Verse or new Social/Mental Merits<br /> [50 or 40x Pneuma] Medium Boon: a permanent effect like a Conclusion 3 Verse, new Physical Merits, new Skill dots, or 2 Small Boon effects<br /> [75 or 60x Pneuma] Large Boon: a permanent effect like a Conclusion 4-5 Verse, new Attribute dots, 2 Medium Boon effects or 3-6 Small Boon effects</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's fine, I'm going to wait for an answer to the above question before I post ideas on this. ^^&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1015919#post1015919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Commentary:</u> this is an interesting Chorus as much like the Embassy to Stories for Princess it grants the Siren in this case one of the main systems of another game line, the Changeling ability to craft and bind others to Pledges. Yet it isn't dependent on having Changeling present in the game for it to be used, unlike the Embassy to Stories privileges that grant Unseen Sense: Wyrd and use the talecrafting rules. Thematically, for the scope of your Chronicle, it could be the Wyrd upholding the bargain if you ran a crossover game, although it works on its own merits for being a pledge 'cast out into the Song' that will then recur to the benefit of both sides if the terms are upheld. Like an omega level Verse. There's a lot of shared terminology with Changeling, although that is only because both the game and the Chorus are drawing from similar folklore, and again a point for the Chorus side for not needing another venue to become required reading.<br /> <br /> This is really making me want to blend Sirens and Changelings together more. I am having plenty of plot ideas involving Siren flesh entering a Goblin Market.<br /> <br /> ((Future posts, a sweep on the other Choruses and posting my own Chorus draft))</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I wasn't actually thinking of the Black Huntsmen being a crossover to Changeling. I mostly thought of it if we went with the Opera idea for Choruses with Rip Van Winkle from Hellsing (and Xigbar from Kingdom Hearts), the opera in question being Der Freisch\u00fctz (The Freeshooter). I just liked the idea too much to set it down. &gt;w&gt;&quot; <br /> <br /> That said, I'd say a comparison to Changeling is more a happy coincidence if it's fine. And feel free, I haven't exactly made up ideas on Siren-Changeling Crossovers just yet. &gt;w&gt;&quot; Although anyone's free to come up with ideas for it, I've personally put off the Crossovers until Choruses are finished.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FeyP70LP92Y\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FeyP70LP92Y\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FeyP70LP92Y\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FeyP70LP92Y </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T00:31:26-08:00","id":1016015,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Investment Costs</b></i><br /> One of the main ideas for the Investment affect, and how it ties into Choruses in general, is that it's of a lot of upfront effort and commitment to the Siren's part for the cause of her Chorus. Once Invested, it is a permanent effect available as is any other Chorus benefit. It needs no other costs by this point, at most an activation condition. If a small bit of Pneuma and a Verse can cause a change in the world, a great expenditure would cause an equally monumental change. And the Invested benefit should be scalable in that regard, better done with the 'X Pneuma per instance' ratio.<br /> <br /> It also serves as an alternative scale of the Chorus benefits. A Siren's advancement in a Chorus is not tied to her Akashic Record but by how much Pneuma she puts into it, investing herself. Which, when taking the upper bounds of Investment into account, would have no theoretical limit. Yet there's limits as to how this would realistically enter play, such as how you would get that much Pneuma to begin with.<br /> <br /> Another thought is that, for the purposes of becoming Invested in her Chorus, a Siren could take 1 resistant Aggravated damage to get their Akashic Record in Pneuma for the Investment only. Choruses would likely warn of Sirens so motivated to cause a grand scale effect that they undid themselves in the process.<br /> <br /> The current unit for determining tiers of Investment, as I presented above, is a block of Pneuma for each layer of the effect. 20 is closer to an ideal number, the lowest base unit I would suggest under this model is 15 Pneuma per instance of the effect. That is the max Pneuma pool for Akashic Record 6, creating an iconic Siren symmetry of the '3's compared to the Akashic Record prerequisite of 3 for any Chorus. Having a universal ratio for Chorus Investment is important because regardless of what the support, benefit or thematics of the Chorus is it will make the OOC budgeting of Pneuma very straightforward. It is also used as the cost to switch Active benefits if the Siren focuses on a different Chorus before the month concludes.<br /> <br /> A Siren Investing in her Chorus is not putting that Pneuma towards other purposes. Investment, in practice, is a '<i>Pneuma sink.'</i> Is she finding a regular tithe of Pneuma leaves her drained, or that the great investment leaves her without the Breath to power other abilities unrelated to the Chorus once she had that set up? <br /> <br /> This could also be represented with the 'binding Pneuma' you suggested, as it was in Genius or the Demigod venue being developed elsewhere on the site. In that model the Siren's max Pneuma pool is shrinking, she has already dedicated the Pneuma for a specific purpose in the Chorus so other use and storage becomes limited. If that where the case I would drop the ratio to 10 Pneuma per. Although this changes the mechanics and application of the Chorus benefits.<br /> <br /> Firstly, your rank of Akashic Record regains emphasis. While this creates a better defined cap a Siren literally could not impart certain tiers of Investment until she gained Akashic Record, gaining more of her Pneuma potential to dedicate. And while ending an Investment is easy (she removes the restriction on max Pneuma pool) it creates further punishment for changing Choruses. Pneuma would have to be dedicated for a cycle to get the Active benefit early before the restriction is removed, and the same amount further bound to become Invested at such a time.<br /> <br /> <br /> In short: Invested as a 'Pneuma sink' or 'Pneuma pool restriction' will have to be determined for the bounds of the top Chorus benefit are implemented.<br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> Also going to comment on the other Choruses for the points raised above.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Chorus of Gloriana's Satirists</u><br /> <br /> Invested: Sweet Nothings Will Get You Anywhere</b><br /> By becoming a Critic the Siren finds that the world of politics grants leeway only one way. Privileges unavailable to most come who you know. At any time, once a Session, the Siren may exchange her Politics dots of Social Merits into other Social Merits regarding political or business dealings for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback:</i> while this will adhere a new group to the Siren's beck and call, it does not help her with the group she left behind with the temporary exchange of Social Merit(s). Let alone how some in the new organization may react unkindly to sudden upstarts. Depending on how word of her affiliation change gets out or her abuse of this benefit affects a group, the Siren risks gaining the Notoriety Condition.<br /> <br /> [20 or 15 Pneuma] The Siren gains the benefit and drawback outlined above. For every additional [20 or 15] the Siren invests she may choose to increase the number of times a Session she may use this benefit, increase her effective Politics dots by half its original rating (round down) for the purposes of this benefit, or negate 1 incursion of the Notoriety Condition from the use of this benefit.<br /> <br /> <i>Commentary: I always like seeing more uses politically minded character perks, because at least in the games I've played they're ones overlooked. I'm reminded of the Embassy to the Economy in Princess to some extent, as they both cover similar spheres of influence but the Chorus is exclusively as to how the Siren positions herself with the organization in question, while the Embassy is more focused on the finance.<br /> <br /> This Chorus is also an example of a stackable Invested Benefit, as more cost increases the level of benefit. This is contrasted to the <b>Huntsmens</b> dealmaking, in which the tiers of possible Boons (normally) have separate costs to set up, although the Siren would only be limited by her Pneuma in the number of such deals she could keep active.</i><br /> <br /> <b><u>The Chorus of Turnadot</u><br /> <br /> Active: Gaze of True Love</b><br /> As a Matchmaker the Siren is premier on realizing the extent of others relationships. By touching a target, the Siren may ask the ST a question about the target's relations, which must be answered to the best of the ST's ability. For each target the Siren can only ask a number of these questions up to her Empathy dots. Once touching the target, she can ask any number of questions she is allowed.<br /> <br /> {example questions remain the same}<br /> <br /> <b>Invested: Love Conquers All</b><br /> The Matchmaker is able to prompt and shape her targets into new relationships, or bring nuances into already present ones. [Basic price is the Inspired Condition, while further investment likely gets into crafting Relationships between subjects]<br /> <br /> <i>Commentary: this expands on mechanics introduced in Siren, making it a decent vanilla type of Chorus. Although it is half complete on the draft, any further comments I have are for the use of Relationships in the system. I would suggest removing Relationships from being a 'merit' as they have more particulars and variation than other merits, letting it be an independent system.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T03:26:55-08:00","id":1016045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1016015#post1016015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Investment Costs</b></i><br /> One of the main ideas for the Investment affect, and how it ties into Choruses in general, is that it's of a lot of upfront effort and commitment to the Siren's part for the cause of her Chorus. Once Invested, it is a permanent effect available as is any other Chorus benefit. It needs no other costs by this point, at most an activation condition. If a small bit of Pneuma and a Verse can cause a change in the world, a great expenditure would cause an equally monumental change. And the Invested benefit should be scalable in that regard, better done with the 'X Pneuma per instance' ratio.<br /> <br /> It also serves as an alternative scale of the Chorus benefits. A Siren's advancement in a Chorus is not tied to her Akashic Record but by how much Pneuma she puts into it, investing herself. Which, when taking the upper bounds of Investment into account, would have no theoretical limit. Yet there's limits as to how this would realistically enter play, such as how you would get that much Pneuma to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, given that Pneuma can kind of be fed off of like how Vampires get vitae (save through actual kissing rather than neck biting), I imagine a Siren with enough time on her hands could pay it up in one-three days if she put effort into it. Although she still needs to worry on whether she drains permanent willpower or Drowns the person (unless she's in Phlegethon).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1016015#post1016015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thought is that, for the purposes of becoming Invested in her Chorus, a Siren could take 1 resistant Aggravated damage to get their Akashic Record in Pneuma for the Investment only. Choruses would likely warn of Sirens so motivated to cause a grand scale effect that they undid themselves in the process.<br /> <br /> The current unit for determining tiers of Investment, as I presented above, is a block of Pneuma for each layer of the effect. 20 is closer to an ideal number, the lowest base unit I would suggest under this model is 15 Pneuma per instance of the effect. That is the max Pneuma pool for Akashic Record 6, creating an iconic Siren symmetry of the '3's compared to the Akashic Record prerequisite of 3 for any Chorus. Having a universal ratio for Chorus Investment is important because regardless of what the support, benefit or thematics of the Chorus is it will make the OOC budgeting of Pneuma very straightforward. It is also used as the cost to switch Active benefits if the Siren focuses on a different Chorus before the month concludes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So wait, at the least there's 15 Pneuma for every time the Siren wants to use the effect? I mean, I know you said it would take alot of Pneuma but I can't help but feel like that's something way too costly, even if Pneuma can be kinda easily regained. Let's look at Mage Legacies or Princess Embassies. Their third Attainments and Ambassador Privileges are useful effects that the Mage/Princess can make use of in the right circumstances or at any time. I feel that either the Pneuma cost should be reduced or the Siren could simply invest the Pneuma as a one time payment in a Cycle (a month as you said) and then she's able to use the Invested Aria as an automatic power. For comparison, it's kind of like paying money to get a magazine. But instead of getting a page they're getting the whole magazine. <br /> <br /> There's only one other problem I have with Choruses and Investing Pneuma atm. Simply put, what happens to the invested Pneuma? Is there metaphysics at work? <br /> <br /> I was kinda musing on the question (pardon if I'm just answering my own question), and I was thinking. Investing Pneuma to a Chorus gives a Siren greater power and sway over it. She finds it easier to trace out her fellow chorus members and lead them (mainly through her Trace). I imagine a Siren who has the Invested Aria would be called a Chorus Master.<br /> <br /> Ack, pardon if I'm sounding bad. I'm just feeling so extreme a cost should have additional benefits than just being able to use the power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1016015#post1016015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Siren Investing in her Chorus is not putting that Pneuma towards other purposes. Investment, in practice, is a '<i>Pneuma sink.'</i> Is she finding a regular tithe of Pneuma leaves her drained, or that the great investment leaves her without the Breath to power other abilities unrelated to the Chorus once she had that set up?<br /> <br /> This could also be represented with the 'binding Pneuma' you suggested, as it was in Genius or the Demigod venue being developed elsewhere on the site. In that model the Siren's max Pneuma pool is shrinking, she has already dedicated the Pneuma for a specific purpose in the Chorus so other use and storage becomes limited. If that where the case I would drop the ratio to 10 Pneuma per. Although this changes the mechanics and application of the Chorus benefits.<br /> <br /> Firstly, your rank of Akashic Record regains emphasis. While this creates a better defined cap a Siren literally could not impart certain tiers of Investment until she gained Akashic Record, gaining more of her Pneuma potential to dedicate. And while ending an Investment is easy (she removes the restriction on max Pneuma pool) it creates further punishment for changing Choruses. Pneuma would have to be dedicated for a cycle to get the Active benefit early before the restriction is removed, and the same amount further bound to become Invested at such a time.<br /> <br /> In short: Invested as a 'Pneuma sink' or 'Pneuma pool restriction' will have to be determined for the bounds of the top Chorus benefit are implemented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I feel that &quot;Pneuma Sink&quot; is abit high of a cost. So I feel that the next best thing is Binding Pneuma to the Chorus (and as you said, lowering the cost of Pneuma that would be &quot;bound&quot;). If we also mash in the idea of it granting abit of influence over Trace (I suppose in metaphysics it would be like reviewing the notes in the Song) over other Chorus members. In a sense, it's more for the purposes of getting members of a chorus together, and further giving a feel of &quot;Prestige Class&quot; to Choruses (by making it easier for Choruses to get together).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1016015#post1016015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also going to comment on the other Choruses for the points raised above.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Chorus of Gloriana's Satirists</u><br /> <br /> Invested: Sweet Nothings Will Get You Anywhere</b><br /> By becoming a Critic the Siren finds that the world of politics grants leeway only one way. Privileges unavailable to most come who you know. At any time, once a Session, the Siren may exchange her Politics dots of Social Merits into other Social Merits regarding political or business dealings for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback:</i> while this will adhere a new group to the Siren's beck and call, it does not help her with the group she left behind with the temporary exchange of Social Merit(s). Let alone how some in the new organization may react unkindly to sudden upstarts. Depending on how word of her affiliation change gets out or her abuse of this benefit affects a group, the Siren risks gaining the Notoriety Condition.<br /> <br /> [20 or 15 Pneuma] The Siren gains the benefit and drawback outlined above. For every additional [20 or 15] the Siren invests she may choose to increase the number of times a Session she may use this benefit, increase her effective Politics dots by half its original rating (round down) for the purposes of this benefit, or negate 1 incursion of the Notoriety Condition from the use of this benefit.<br /> <br /> <i>Commentary: I always like seeing more uses politically minded character perks, because at least in the games I've played they're ones overlooked. I'm reminded of the Embassy to the Economy in Princess to some extent, as they both cover similar spheres of influence but the Chorus is exclusively as to how the Siren positions herself with the organization in question, while the Embassy is more focused on the finance.<br /> <br /> This Chorus is also an example of a stackable Invested Benefit, as more cost increases the level of benefit. This is contrasted to the <b>Huntsmens</b> dealmaking, in which the tiers of possible Boons (normally) have separate costs to set up, although the Siren would only be limited by her Pneuma in the number of such deals she could keep active.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This is good. I kind of had some inspiration from Princess when making this Invested Aria, mainly from Terra. There's so few other games that deal with using Politics (as in the Skill and mundane mortal structures compared to supernatural ones) or Social Merits, so the general idea I had behind this Chorus was to give some focus on that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1016015#post1016015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>The Chorus of Turnadot</u><br /> <br /> Active: Gaze of True Love</b><br /> As a Matchmaker the Siren is premier on realizing the extent of others relationships. By touching a target, the Siren may ask the ST a question about the target's relations, which must be answered to the best of the ST's ability. For each target the Siren can only ask a number of these questions up to her Empathy dots. Once touching the target, she can ask any number of questions she is allowed.<br /> <br /> {example questions remain the same}<br /> <br /> <b>Invested: Love Conquers All</b><br /> The Matchmaker is able to prompt and shape her targets into new relationships, or bring nuances into already present ones. [Basic price is the Inspired Condition, while further investment likely gets into crafting Relationships between subjects]<br /> <br /> <i>Commentary: this expands on mechanics introduced in Siren, making it a decent vanilla type of Chorus. Although it is half complete on the draft, any further comments I have are for the use of Relationships in the system. I would suggest removing Relationships from being a 'merit' as they have more particulars and variation than other merits, letting it be an independent system.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the stuff on the Invested Aria. I didn't have that many ideas and the only one I had was something having to do with causing the Inspired Condition. <br /> <br /> Although I would still rather keep Relationships as a Merit, abeit a really special one. I have an idea though for the Invested Aria. What if it grants the ability to introduce or remove Kinks and Comforts, or even adding/removing kinks and comforts where a Relationship already exists? Basically, it's like the Matchmakers are trying to enforce their idea of love or how they think two people will work together into a Relationship or trying to drive nails into a relationship? Let's say each additional/removed Kink/Support costs an extra five Pneuma per kink/support modified? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:36:20-08:00","id":1017450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1016045#post1016045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So wait, at the least there's 15 Pneuma for every time the Siren wants to use the effect? I mean, I know you said it would take alot of Pneuma but I can't help but feel like that's something way too costly, even if Pneuma can be kinda easily regained. Let's look at Mage Legacies or Princess Embassies. Their third Attainments and Ambassador Privileges are useful effects that the Mage/Princess can make use of in the right circumstances or at any time. I feel that either the Pneuma cost should be reduced or the Siren could simply invest the Pneuma as a one time payment in a Cycle (a month as you said) and then she's able to use the Invested Aria as an automatic power. For comparison, it's kind of like paying money to get a magazine. But instead of getting a page they're getting the whole magazine.<br /> <br /> There's only one other problem I have with Choruses and Investing Pneuma atm. Simply put, what happens to the invested Pneuma? Is there metaphysics at work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of my newer revisions are making the original details lost, sorry about that. To put my thoughts in order becoming Invested was only going to have a flat cost to begin it. As said, Chorus benefits are always permanent for the Cycle they are active. The exact timeframe of a Cycle, if not a month, would be whatever feels right for the Storyteller and players for their game.<br /> <br /> <b>Passive Benefit:</b> Always active while a Chorus member<br /> <b>Active Benefit:</b> Always active if selected each Cycle (only one)<br /> <b>Invested Benefit:</b> Always active after the Pneuma cost each Cycle (requires Active)<br /> <br /> <br /> Within the last tier, the Invested Benefit, I found it to be a novel concept if the benefit could be enhanced/layered further with more cost. To bring back the Monopoly analog, each purchased house further enhances the property. This is entirely optional on the Siren\u2019s part. Plus, the Invested cost is used to change Active Benefit early.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s less that the Invested cost is always needed but it must be paid each time the effect is enhanced. None of the previous effort the Siren put in is lost, only improved if more Pneuma is pumped into it. Putting this into practice, however, may or may not be suitable for all kinds of Choruses.<br /> <br /> As for the metaphysics of it, I see it as the Siren expending her voice back into the Song. If Ceto and/or the last cries of humanity was said to enact the Song from the initial cataclysm that begot the Deluge, the Sirens of a Chorus are enacting a similar shift to support their efforts. Additional basic Chorus benefits, such as being able to scout out fellow members with the Trace, makes sense. Wasn't there previously a means, whether associated with Akashic Record or not, for Sirens to connect with each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T10:19:19-08:00","id":1017699,"title":"","content":"So because I loves me some fan-lines, I've got a few question.<br /> <br /> 1: So basically, the biggest difference between Sirens and Leviathans is that the Sirens are trying to affect the future, while Leviathans are metaphorically trapped in the past?<br /> <br /> 2: The Furies, are they nature-beings that are trying to save the world by destroying humanity, or do they represent something else","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T12:07:11-08:00","id":1018540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1017450#post1017450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of my newer revisions are making the original details lost, sorry about that. To put my thoughts in order becoming Invested was only going to have a flat cost to begin it. As said, Chorus benefits are always permanent for the Cycle they are active. The exact timeframe of a Cycle, if not a month, would be whatever feels right for the Storyteller and players for their game.<br /> <br /> <b>Passive Benefit:</b> Always active while a Chorus member<br /> <b>Active Benefit:</b> Always active if selected each Cycle (only one)<br /> <b>Invested Benefit:</b> Always active after the Pneuma cost each Cycle (requires Active)<br /> <br /> Within the last tier, the Invested Benefit, I found it to be a novel concept if the benefit could be enhanced/layered further with more cost. To bring back the Monopoly analog, each purchased house further enhances the property. This is entirely optional on the Siren\u2019s part. Plus, the Invested cost is used to change Active Benefit early.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s less that the Invested cost is always needed but it must be paid each time the effect is enhanced. None of the previous effort the Siren put in is lost, only improved if more Pneuma is pumped into it. Putting this into practice, however, may or may not be suitable for all kinds of Choruses.<br /> <br /> As for the metaphysics of it, I see it as the Siren expending her voice back into the Song. If Ceto and/or the last cries of humanity was said to enact the Song from the initial cataclysm that begot the Deluge, the Sirens of a Chorus are enacting a similar shift to support their efforts. Additional basic Chorus benefits, such as being able to scout out fellow members with the Trace, makes sense. Wasn't there previously a means, whether associated with Akashic Record or not, for Sirens to connect with each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Alrighties then. :3 The metaphysics seem fine. If I may note, then all of the benefits will become passive ones instead of ones that can be activated? That conflicts with some of the powers currently made. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1017699#post1017699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So because I loves me some fan-lines, I've got a few question.<br /> <br /> 1: So basically, the biggest difference between Sirens and Leviathans is that the Sirens are trying to affect the future, while Leviathans are metaphorically trapped in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1017699#post1017699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: The Furies, are they nature-beings that are trying to save the world by destroying humanity, or do they represent something else</div> </div> </div> </div>I left it a tiny bit ambiguous on purpose. For the most part, they are created from disregard for nature, and they mostly seek to avenge themselves. They don't really have an overarching plan like &quot;destroy humanity&quot;, it's more singular like &quot;destroy the beings who defiled me&quot; and are more likely to harm those who fit the description of what made them which to them would be humanity in general. They pretty much remain this way until either the nature that makes up the quagmire is utterly destroyed, or the Quagmire's rage is appeased by killing the people responsible for making it pop up. Or healing the life present in the Quagmire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T18:19:56-08:00","id":1018634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1018540#post1018540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Alrighties then. :3 The metaphysics seem fine. If I may note, then all of the benefits will become passive ones instead of ones that can be activated? That conflicts with some of the powers currently made.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a confusion of terms in regards to the structure of a Chorus.<br /> <br /> <u>Passive</u>, <u>Active</u> and <u>Invested</u> indicate how much of herself and her song <b>the Siren</b> puts into the Chorus. Each level of involvement has its own benefit. The benefit takes effect whenever its <i>criteria</i> is met, which could make it a passive boost or an activated power depending on the Chorus. You do not require a dice roll to activate the benefit. The only time Pneuma is needed as a 'price' is to become Invested or to change Active benefit out of Cycle. After that point no Pneuma or Willpower costs are needed to operate the benefit.<br /> <br /> In my research of the other game lines, the &quot;Affinities&quot; of Mummy are much like this. They were subtle mystical effects always active for the character when the circumstances were right, and most did not require anything spent to activate them. In this case it is the relation of how a Siren is present in a Chorus that determines the scope of her benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","user":"-metablender","date":". 12-17-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T19:38:52-08:00","id":1020131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1018634#post1018634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a confusion of terms in regards to the structure of a Chorus.<br /> <br /> <u>Passive</u>, <u>Active</u> and <u>Invested</u> indicate how much of herself and her song <b>the Siren</b> puts into the Chorus. Each level of involvement has its own benefit. The benefit takes effect whenever its <i>criteria</i> is met, which could make it a passive boost or an activated power depending on the Chorus. You do not require a dice roll to activate the benefit. The only time Pneuma is needed as a 'price' is to become Invested or to change Active benefit out of Cycle. After that point no Pneuma or Willpower costs are needed to operate the benefit.<br /> <br /> In my research of the other game lines, the &quot;Affinities&quot; of Mummy are much like this. They were subtle mystical effects always active for the character when the circumstances were right, and most did not require anything spent to activate them. In this case it is the relation of how a Siren is present in a Chorus that determines the scope of her benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I see. It's mostly my fault then, I was kind of assuming that the Passive Aria would be...passive, basically a power that's &quot;always on&quot;, Active would need to be activated (kind of like verses) and finally Invested would be somewhere between the two. <br /> <br /> I'll get to revising them. Pardon my lack of inspiration and creating stuff as of late, christmas is coming up and all. ^^&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T08:23:38-08:00","id":1022769,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, I've finally edited the Choruses so that they don't rely on Pneuma expendature to activate Arias and I've created the Invested Aria for the Chorus of Turandot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Edit on Arias and explaining Cycles<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> There are usually three benefits associated to Choruses, known as Arias. Arias are gained by a Siren spending a prerequisite amount of Pneuma while she\u2019s within a Chorus within a Cycle, which covers a lunar month. When a Cycle is over, a Siren must repay a certain amount of Pneuma to regain the Arias she desires. Choruses are special however that a Siren may belong to any number of them so long as she has the Pneuma to pay within a Cycle. There is a limit to how many Arias she may own at once however. She may have as many Passive Arias as she can pay for, a number of Active Arias equal to her Akashic Record and a fiinally Siren may only ever have one Invested Aria at any Cycle in time. If a Siren cannot renew the Pneuma cost for any Aria she was within at the beginning of a new Cycle, then she isn\u2019t considered a part of the Chorus the Aria(s) belonged to. Passive Arias require around 10 Pneuma, Active Arias cost 25 Pneuma and Invested Arias cost 35 Pneuma to unlock respectively. Dice rolls are not required to activate an Aria. Most Choruses do have a Prerequisite skill and Akashic Record rating before one can gain an Aria or make use of it, which effectively means a Siren who wishes to first join a Chorus must have the bare minimum for the first Aria. To gain the Passive Aria, the Siren must have Akashic Record 3, the required Skill to be at 3 dots. The Active Aria requires Akashic Record 5 and the prerequisite Skill at 4 dots to gain. The Invested Aria demands the Siren to have Akashic Record 7 and the prerequisite Skill at five dots.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Invested Aria: Love Conquers All</b><br /> If love conquers all, then perfect love perfectly conquers all. At this level, the Matchmakers and Homewreckers can truly live up to their name, creating relationships where there is none or breaking them apart. The Siren may at any point choose two people in her line of sight and divide her Empathy dots to grant them the Relationship merit or a Social Merit that represents a connection between them (Allies, Contacts, Mentor, Retainer, Staff and True Friend is applicable) at an equivalent number of dots for a scene. The Siren may inversely use the same dots to deny a person the use of the same merits above, to which they remain supressed for a scene. If a person\u2019s Relationship or merit dots are destroyed, then Sanctity of Merits applies.<br /> A Matchmaker may also edit already existing Relationships, as well. She may use her unspent Empathy dots to add or subtract Kinks and Comforts at a rate of 1:1. A Matchmaker may take out all the Kinks from a Relationship or a Homewrecker may deprive a relationship of it\u2019s Comforts in this fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T18:03:17-08:00","id":1024590,"title":"","content":"So...I know this might not be much a surprise to note, but I feel the need to make another post on how I haven't made much progress. I feel like I've put so much into making Siren that I'm running out of creative steam for it. I have ideas on what I'd like for things, but I'm drained of the will to write them out. <br /> <br /> In light of this, there's two things that needs to happen to complete Siren. Either I go on hiatus and continue Siren when I have the inspiration for it back, or someone else writes for it.<br /> <br /> I want to thank the people who have helped in making it this far today, but I'm just too borked at the moment to continue and I feel the lack of progress is mainly my fault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:30:54-08:00","id":1026819,"title":"","content":"Sorry to not be as active over the holidays, hope everyone has been having a good year.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say there's a lack of progress, if you define progress as new material. Since 99% of Siren is ready this is the stage of revisions, such as making tweaks and adjustments to the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Such as the Chorus structure, which I apologize if my last posts have muddled the design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1020131#post1020131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. I see. It's mostly my fault then, I was kind of assuming that the Passive Aria would be...passive, basically a power that's &quot;always on&quot;, Active would need to be activated (kind of like verses) and finally Invested would be somewhere between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your assumption is correct, save Invested sits at the end. There's a bit of confusion versus HOW a Chorus is meant to work with WHAT benefit the Chorus provides. I was trying to write examples of possible benefits at each tier, yet how these Arias manifest is always consistent to allow for unique Choruses to be written.<br /> <br /> The Passive benefit is always available. It only requires Chorus membership, no activation or other costs.<br /> <br /> The Active benefit usually requires no cost. The Siren can benefit from a single Active Aria each Cycle. If she was to switch the Active Aria before that time ran out, it requires the base Pnuema cost to activate early.<br /> <br /> The Invested benefit has the most requirements. The Siren must be Active and pay a Pnuema price to keep the Invested Aria for the Cycle. Any use within that time has no further activation costs. Depending on the benefit in question, the potency of the effect can be scaled by increase payment of the same base Pnuema value. For this i've suggested either 15 or 20 Pneuma for the increment.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> Where Siren sits at this moment does require more input than just one author. There's little to add outside of the campaign prompts (such as the Honolulu chapter) so a designated proofreader would help with revisions. Having anyone willing to play test Siren will also help, providing critical feedback. The reminder of 'tasks' come down to layout and art, which is more optional should anyone have the talent to contribute there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T18:30:07-08:00","id":1029849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1026819#post1026819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to not be as active over the holidays, hope everyone has been having a good year.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say there's a lack of progress, if you define progress as new material. Since 99% of Siren is ready this is the stage of revisions, such as making tweaks and adjustments to the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Such as the Chorus structure, which I apologize if my last posts have muddled the design.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine. Everyone has lives. It's ok on that. It's the reason I haven't responded until now, sorry on that. &gt;&lt;&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1026819#post1026819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your assumption is correct, save Invested sits at the end. There's a bit of confusion versus HOW a Chorus is meant to work with WHAT benefit the Chorus provides. I was trying to write examples of possible benefits at each tier, yet how these Arias manifest is always consistent to allow for unique Choruses to be written.<br /> <br /> The Passive benefit is always available. It only requires Chorus membership, no activation or other costs.<br /> <br /> The Active benefit usually requires no cost. The Siren can benefit from a single Active Aria each Cycle. If she was to switch the Active Aria before that time ran out, it requires the base Pnuema cost to activate early.<br /> <br /> The Invested benefit has the most requirements. The Siren must be Active and pay a Pnuema price to keep the Invested Aria for the Cycle. Any use within that time has no further activation costs. Depending on the benefit in question, the potency of the effect can be scaled by increase payment of the same base Pnuema value. For this i've suggested either 15 or 20 Pneuma for the increment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I'll implement those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1026819#post1026819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where Siren sits at this moment does require more input than just one author. There's little to add outside of the campaign prompts (such as the Honolulu chapter) so a designated proofreader would help with revisions. Having anyone willing to play test Siren will also help, providing critical feedback. The reminder of 'tasks' come down to layout and art, which is more optional should anyone have the talent to contribute there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and Siren is open for playtesting for anyone who's interested. When it comes to layout and Art, we had Yads Dom who made the awesome logo and a few examples for Character sheets, but he's gotten a new job and it's really taking a chunk of his time. <br /> <br /> Also, there has been token bits of progress on Honolulu. Not very much mind you, but enough that we have a baseline on things. Also, I have something funny to share that has to do with Honolulu. Essentially, a weird law. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;In Honolulu, hawaii it is illegal to sing loudly outside after sunset.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given Honolulu IS the Siren sample city, and they have powers on Verses, I just imagine this weird law existing because:<br /> <br /> A: It makes it easier for Flensers to find Sirens from those arrested.<br /> B: The Celestial Currents set it up as part of the masquerade.<br /> C: Acheron made it to interfere with Siren's lives and make any caught &quot;breaking the law&quot; to be unable to do any actions.<br /> D: All of the above. <br /> <br /> Either way, it's a funny tidbit I wanted to share.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T15:41:54-07:00","id":1062032,"title":"","content":"I'm Always briefly back until I'm gone. But again, that's life. I wanted to, again, say how the game is incredible and how we all (mostly you Saul) did a great wprk on it. In this state it's almost finished and ready to play. I even have flirted with putting a few Siren characters and Trinkets and Treasures ia a few games of mine. But unfortunately I barely have time to play now, which means I couldnt go much further in testing the system. But alas, I have the archives all in my computer. and am Always around Reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9279-yads-dom","name":"Yads Dom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T21:29:07-07:00","id":1062162,"title":"","content":"It's been awhile but I've finally had some thoughts for some more Choruses. I always had trouble coming up with ones that weren't just Crossover bridges. By no means are these finished drafts but they might provide something interesting.<br /> <br /> Also, were the comments quoted on Choruses from the January 10th post above integrated into the document? Having just looked it says each membership and tier requires a full list of Akashic Record and Skill ratings with Pneuma dues each Cycle <i>per effect</i>, which is a lot of hoops to jump through for what is meant to be always available boons.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Chorus of the Parading Band</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Big Band, the Music Meisters, the College of Bards<br /> Nicknames: musicians, the orchestra, band geeks<br /> <br /> The Song takes many forms. While the majority of Sirens prefer to sing their Verses or tap a rhythm if they are denied their voice, it's easy to forget that the Song can convey through any medium of music. Sirens of this Chorus delight in learning instruments and performing in groups. The are, in some ways, the music industry of the Siren society. Although don't let their endless revisions, practice and jam sessions fool you. These Sirens are as serious about warning the world about the coming Deluge as much as any other. They find music performed on instruments, blending and redefining genres into new styles and having a full assembly of players to be one of the better ways to influence the world. Humanity is a species of romance and passion, and the Sirens of this chorus will learn whatever instrument from distant cultures to help adapt the flow of the Song for a new audience.<br /> <br /> No means of producing music is off limits. Everything from marching big brass, hand carved acoustic, the latest electronica remixes, raving metal and opera strings are only the tip of the hodgepodge of styles mixed together in this Chorus.<br /> <br /> Populace: Freshwater and Tropicana tend to be the most popular Waters in this Chorus, then Vaporiea and about equal amounts of the reminder. The Currents of Buoyancy, Harmony and Healing tend to stick out the most as well. Members of the Current of Wisdom are likely to become scholars of handcrafted musical libraries. Conflict isn't unheard of, as Sirens can weapons their music as well, although most of that Current stick to more straightforward approaches.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive Aria</i><br /> Each member of the Parading Band masters a particular instrument. Take a Specialty in Expression pertaining to this musical instrument or medium of performance. The Specialty in question also receives the benefits of the Area of Expertise and Interdisciplinary Merits for free.<br /> <br /> <i>Active Aria</i><br /> The Siren is never without her instrument. A treasured instrument becomes associated with her Diluvian form and it can also be drawn to her human form much like applying one of her Adaptations. It takes an instant action to retrieve it from anywhere it has been lost or taken.<br /> <br /> The band that performs together creates of symphony of music with increased effects. Members of the Chorus can perform together to weave their Verses together in dynamic ways. This requires the Chorus to use the same Introduction and at least one Opus, although individual Conclusions provided by each member. Furthermore, the band gets an automatic success (that doesn't count for an exceptional success) for each added instrument to apply towards any particular Verse. The same automatic successes may also be used for a shared Trace.<br /> <br /> <i>Invested Aria</i><br /> The Siren must composure, arrange or remix a new piece of music with her instrument. By sending her Investment into the Song she creates an imprint of the music she has just created. The Siren selects one of her Conclusions. That Conclusion is tied to the piece. When the Siren performs her piece she may activate any of her Verses with that Conclusion for free. Rather, her Invested Pneuma becomes a deposit that can be spent back to activate the Conclusion, in place of the Siren's current stores of Pneuma. Obviously, when the Siren uses the last of her allotted Invested Pneuma she is no longer able to use the Invested Aria until she writes a new piece and again seals the notation with the Invested price.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u><b>The Chorus of the Chthonic Mourners</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Avernian Avengers, Psychopomps of the Dead Rivers, the Underworld Sluagh<br /> Nicknames: Chthonian Daughters, Chthonian Sons, ferrymen, spelunkers, corpse fish<br /> <br /> The Deluge marks the death of the world. Sirens of this Chorus, in place of looking towards the future Cataclysm to destroy an entire planet, track down other incursions of death. And they have found their answers in the 'final' resting place of ghosts, the land of the dead in a great Underworld from which the traces of lost souls and past epidemics can be discovered. Even more distant in this autochtonous depths, perhaps the record of past cataclysms can be found. Maybe the knowledge of what the sweet relief of death may bring, as the great dooming change that will ravage the world at the Deluge.<br /> <br /> This that spend any time past the dark crevices and hell tunnels on the planet, down into that dead domain, find the Underworld to be fragmented by rivers. Rivers not always of water, rivers that include bone dust or congealed blood or lifeless seeds amongst other variations on death and decay. Each soon reaching an ocean of fragments, the edge of the dead realms where nothing that has passed beyond comes back. Sirens adapt to any body of water and the dead rivers of the Underworld are no exception, as Sirens study these rivers and the dead denizens that line their banks.<br /> <br /> Populace: it goes without saying that Polaria boasts quite the representation of members, Death being their favored Opus after all. Discordia and Freshwater follow next, with fewer numbers of the rest. As for Currents: Acheron, Cocytus, Lethe, Phlegethon, Styx. Did you know that these are also iconic rivers amongst the multitude that crisscross the Underworld? It is quite odd to consider that this Chorus is perhaps the one mutually trusting sorority of the Abyssal Currents, Only Oceanus lacks a signature river, although the agents of Echidna may lay claim to the boundless dead sea beyond. However the reasons for seeking out the realm of the dead are varied, as this very Chorus can be prompt with numerous strifes. Amongst the Celestial Currents you may find Conflict and Wisdom, perhaps Buoyancy, more readily than any others.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive Aria</i><br /> The Siren becomes attuned to the state of the dead. She adds her Lucidity to any roll to notice, identify or decipher a ghost or other deathly phenomena, which she can see out of Twilight if successful.<br /> <br /> <i>Active Aria</i><br /> Once she knows of a passageway to the Underworld (called an Avernian Gate) she may cross over to it from up to Akashic Record miles away using the same process used for entering the Celestial Ocean. From there she must survive the depths and may seek out the dead souls of others. The Siren may treat a Ghost as a Breathless for the purposes of drawing Pneuma, instead targeting the living that remember that Ghost.<br /> <br /> <i>Invested Aria</i><br /> The Siren attunes herself to one of the rivers in the Underworld, learning all of its properties. When entering the Underworld she may travel anywhere along her patron river in an instant, both for navigating the infernal depths and to use the Underworld as a conduit between areas that resonate with the river's themes of death. Additionally, the Siren selects one skill as receiving the benefits of her patron river. That skill has the rote quality. However, the Siren effectively stains herself as a member of the dead rather than the living. She takes an extra point of damage from Ghosts or necrotic energies and any healing she receives, mundane or magical, heals one less point of the worst damage that what it could have.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u><b>The Chorus of Cosmonauts</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Riders of the Etheric Waves, Travelers of the Spacial Oceans<br /> Nicknames: aliens, astronauts, lunar bounders, orbiters<br /> <br /> Survivors of the Deluge are few and far between, compared to the population of earth from pre-diluvian times. For some Sirens, with the knowledge that the death of an entire planet is coming they look to the stars. When one door closes surely another must open? Or in this instance, replace doors with planets. Those that study space theorize that further exploration and the possible colonization of other planets is possible. If little more than a distant fantasy outpacing current technology.<br /> <br /> No time like the present...<br /> <br /> Cosmonauts seek to guide humanity along mankind's next wayward leap. Some see the moon or Mars as likely candidates for future Civilizations, while others prefer such heavenly bodies to remain domains where Nature may change course drastically unbothered by human lives. Still others say that man will need to journey farther, the great Cataclysm could spell the end for our solar system as well as earth, with the next planet capable of sustaining life is an untold eons of lightyears away. And journeying space is a lonely trip.<br /> <br /> Yet still other Sirens of this Chorus, more mindful of immediate needs, may deduce that it's a failure of space travel or some wayward debris that could spell doom for planet Earth. The upper limits of the atmosphere are as much a border to safeguard. Didn't an asteroid exterminate all the dinosaurs?<br /> <br /> Populace: As the Waters are both a terrestrial and Celestial bridging of environs and cataclysms the outwards vastness of space suggests few correlations. With Vaporia and Freshwater as a possible uptick in representations any Water is otherwise valid for joining this Chorus.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive Aria</i><br /> When exposed to an airless, vacuum environment the Siren does not need to breath and is immune to the dangers such a void presents. She can eliminate her need to breath in any environment by drastically altering her physiology, although this requires a point of Aggravated damage that cannot be healed or degraded, or the Siren will need to breath once again.<br /> <br /> <i>Active Aria</i><br /> The Siren is able to control her own personal gravity. She may move up to twice her speed in any direction in reference to the gravity of another structure. Or she may dedicate herself to a plummet, a controlled orbit set by Dexterity + Science which sets her on an ever falling path until she makes another roll to slow her descent.<br /> <br /> I<i>nvested Aria</i><br /> Paying immense stores of Pneuma the Siren furthers the relativistic speed of her orbit, allowing her to circumnavigate the globe or head out towards local bodies within a short timeframe. Many cosmonauts warn of Sirens unable to control these extremes speeds that meet fatal ends to their orbits. Additionally, the Siren prepares her body further towards the hazardous on other planets. When Invested she defines the hazard of a planet, be it one in our solar system or another. She is immune to all Environmental Tilts and sources of damage fitting the biome of the selected planet.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T19:20:49-07:00","id":1063713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yads Dom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1062032#post1062032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm Always briefly back until I'm gone. But again, that's life. I wanted to, again, say how the game is incredible and how we all (mostly you Saul) did a great wprk on it. In this state it's almost finished and ready to play. I even have flirted with putting a few Siren characters and Trinkets and Treasures ia a few games of mine. But unfortunately I barely have time to play now, which means I couldnt go much further in testing the system. But alas, I have the archives all in my computer. and am Always around Reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine. Don't worry, life comes first. I'm sorry that there hasn't been any updates in the past few months.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1062162#post1062162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been awhile but I've finally had some thoughts for some more Choruses. I always had trouble coming up with ones that weren't just Crossover bridges. By no means are these finished drafts but they might provide something interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I'm sorry for the lack of updates as of now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1062162#post1062162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, were the comments quoted on Choruses from the January 10th post above integrated into the document? Having just looked it says each membership and tier requires a full list of Akashic Record and Skill ratings with Pneuma dues each Cycle <i>per effect</i>, which is a lot of hoops to jump through for what is meant to be always available boons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meta, I hope this idea doesn't come off as a bad one or condescending, but if you desire, I could add you to be able to edit the Choruses page. I'm sorry that I keep getting them wrong.<br /> <br /> I'm just gonna post this update here before anything else. I know my last post was in January and I know that there's been few changes to Siren (save grammatical ones). But as I've kinda said abit before, I feel my inspiration for Siren has hit an all time low. I feel that I've probably worked on it abit too much to the point that when I look at it, I see it more as &quot;What's left to be done&quot; and just seeing that there's still a pretty long final stretch (namely Honolulu and Choruses) just feels like it just burns me out and it shuts me down on any attempts to work on it. If it's alright, I think I'm gonna just say that Siren is on Hiatus right now. I don't mind if other people write, make ideas or bring them up, but I'm in no state to do anything myself for the time being. I'm so sorry about this. =m=&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection?p=1062162#post1062162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[spoiler]<br /> <u><b>The Chorus of the Parading Band</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Big Band, the Music Meisters, the College of Bards<br /> Nicknames: musicians, the orchestra, band geeks<br /> <br /> The Song takes many forms. While the majority of Sirens prefer to sing their Verses or tap a rhythm if they are denied their voice, it's easy to forget that the Song can convey through any medium of music. Sirens of this Chorus delight in learning instruments and performing in groups. The are, in some ways, the music industry of the Siren society. Although don't let their endless revisions, practice and jam sessions fool you. These Sirens are as serious about warning the world about the coming Deluge as much as any other. They find music performed on instruments, blending and redefining genres into new styles and having a full assembly of players to be one of the better ways to influence the world. Humanity is a species of romance and passion, and the Sirens of this chorus will learn whatever instrument from distant cultures to help adapt the flow of the Song for a new audience.<br /> <br /> No means of producing music is off limits. Everything from marching big brass, hand carved acoustic, the latest electronica remixes, raving metal and opera strings are only the tip of the hodgepodge of styles mixed together in this Chorus.<br /> <br /> Populace: Freshwater and Tropicana tend to be the most popular Waters in this Chorus, then Vaporiea and about equal amounts of the reminder. The Currents of Buoyancy, Harmony and Healing tend to stick out the most as well. Members of the Current of Wisdom are likely to become scholars of handcrafted musical libraries. Conflict isn't unheard of, as Sirens can weapons their music as well, although most of that Current stick to more straightforward approaches.<br /> <br /> <i>Passive Aria</i><br /> Each member of the Parading Band masters a particular instrument. Take a Specialty in Expression pertaining to this musical instrument or medium of performance. The Specialty in question also receives the benefits of the Area of Expertise and Interdisciplinary Merits for free.<br /> <br /> <i>Active Aria</i><br /> The Siren is never without her instrument. A treasured instrument becomes associated with her Diluvian form and it can also be drawn to her human form much like applying one of her Adaptations. It takes an instant action to retrieve it from anywhere it has been lost or taken.<br /> <br /> The band that performs together creates of symphony of music with increased effects. Members of the Chorus can perform together to weave their Verses together in dynamic ways. This requires the Chorus to use the same Introduction and at least one Opus, although individual Conclusions provided by each member. Furthermore, the band gets an automatic success (that doesn't count for an exceptional success) for each added instrument to apply towards any particular Verse. The same automatic successes may also be used for a shared Trace.<br /> <br /> <i>Invested Aria</i><br /> The Siren must composure, arrange or remix a new piece of music with her instrument. By sending her Investment into the Song she creates an imprint of the music she has just created. The Siren selects one of her Conclusions. That Conclusion is tied to the piece. When the Siren performs her piece she may activate any of her Verses with that Conclusion for free. Rather, her Invested Pneuma becomes a deposit that can be spent back to activate the Conclusion, in place of the Siren's current stores of Pneuma. Obviously, when the Siren uses the last of her allotted Invested Pneuma she is no longer able to use the Invested Aria until she writes a new piece and again seals the notation with the Invested price.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I freaking love this idea. Banding Sirens together and stuff like that and a minor focus on how Verses are done through music. I should note on the Active Aria that it's &quot;Alterations&quot;, not &quot;Adaptations&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>-metablender</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world